{"parentUuid":"af353417-f0c4-4a7b-a09e-80475cf533c6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cfeazhp7e9EpDzt4tfAfh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Green and lint-clean. Committing PR 2:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":386,"cache_read_input_tokens":381151,"output_tokens":2347,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":386,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2347,"cache_read_input_tokens":381151,"cache_creation_input_tokens":386,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":386},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"6265e6f1-0ef3-49ca-98e9-2785100eec18","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cfeazgy26bNzJGAycNu6Q","type":"assistant","uuid":"35884279-1ad5-4d11-9e92-a4e153236008","timestamp":"2026-10-03T03:23:14.814Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-safety","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"35884279-1ad5-4d11-9e92-a4e153236008","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cfeazhp7e9EpDzt4tfAfh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013rNdwkui2TKbCeYi2BnAje","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-safety\ngit add -A\ncat > ~/.local/state/entire-distill/pr2msg.txt <<'EOF'\nfix(safety): stop brain colliding with concurrent git, stalling on a dirty tree, and ignoring local models\n\nFive filed issues, all reproduced before being changed.\n\n#326 - brain brief takes .git/index.lock\n-----------------------------------------\nTwo agents in one repository is the normal case for this product, so a read-only\ninspection that takes a write lock is a correctness bug.\n\n`--no-optional-locks` is now injected at the single git spawn point, which closes\n`git status`. It is NOT sufficient on its own: a porcelain `git diff <commit>`\nperforms its own index refresh that the optional-lock setting does not gate.\nMeasured on git 2.54.0, each trial from an identical stat-dirty index, restored\nin between:\n\n    git diff --name-status -M -C HEAD                      REWRITES the index\n    git --no-optional-locks diff --name-status -M -C HEAD   REWRITES the index\n    git --no-optional-locks diff-index --name-status ...    leaves it alone\n\nThat matters because changedSemanticFiles runs inside `brain brief` - the exact\ncommand the issue reports.\n\nConverting those diffs to plumbing would fix the lock and change the answer:\ndiff-index against an unrefreshed index reports a stat-dirty file (mtime\ntouched, content identical) as modified, which here means re-indexing a file\nthat did not change. On the same fixture that cost one spurious path.\n\nSo the worktree-vs-HEAD diffs now run with GIT_INDEX_FILE pointing at a COPY of\nthe index. git refreshes the copy, the real index is never opened for write, and\nthe output is byte-identical to porcelain because it IS porcelain. Verified: the\ncopy's output matched the real one exactly, where plumbing differed by one line.\n\nOne diff that exists purely to report a stat moved to `diff-index` as well.\n\n#327 - indexing stalls on a dirty worktree\n-------------------------------------------\nA loop, not a single bug: a dirty tree forced a rebuild, the indexer REFUSED\nthat rebuild without --worktree, and a failed refresh aborted the whole watch\ntick so the cursor never advanced. Nothing progressed for as long as the tree\nstayed dirty, which for anyone working is most of the time.\n\nDirtiness alone says nothing about whether the INDEXED content is stale: the\nindex describes HEAD, and HEAD has not moved because the worktree has\nuncommitted edits. The two cases where it does matter - a snapshot taken in\nworktree mode, or from a dirty tree - were already decided further down, so the\ncheck was redundant as well as harmful. A dirty-worktree refusal now lets the\nwatch tick continue; every other refresh failure still aborts it, because an\nunrefreshed brain must not have tokens spent against it.\n\n#328 - a local model is installed and never used\n-------------------------------------------------\ndefaultRefreshAgent tried codex, then claude, then none. A user who installed\nollama specifically to keep transcripts off a third party got one of two\noutcomes: no distillation at all, or - if a cloud CLI happened to be installed\ntoo - their session content sent to that provider instead.\n\nollama is now tried FIRST. Transcripts are the most sensitive thing this product\ntouches; when a local model is available, using it is what the user configured.\nThis changes the agent for someone who has both installed. `--agent` still\noverrides per run.\n\n`watch` hardcoded codex, which is the same defect and worse: the watcher runs\nunattended, so the transcripts went out on a timer. It now uses the \"auto\"\nsentinel - note that \"\" is NOT that sentinel and passes through as an invalid\nagent name.\n\nThe issue also reports that a non-loopback ENTIRE_BRAIN_OLLAMA_URL is rejected\nsilently. It is not: the rejection is a hard error naming the URL. No change.\nThe loopback restriction itself is a deliberate privacy boundary with a redirect\nguard behind it, so an opt-in remote host is NOT included here - that is a\nproduct decision, not a bug fix.\n\nMoving the agent check: it now sits below the distill pass lock. A pass that\nfinds the lock held does nothing, so the agent is irrelevant, and reporting \"no\nagent on PATH\" tells a supervised watcher it has a configuration error when it\nactually has transient contention. Its text now names ollama too.\n\n#322 - Windows \"command line is too long\"\n------------------------------------------\nA ~7516-byte system prompt sat on argv against cmd.exe's 8191 limit. Moved off\nargv at the shared builder: claude takes --system-prompt-file (0600, inside an\n0700 temp dir, removed on every exit path), codex takes it on stdin, which it\nconcatenates with the piped transcript itself. ollama is unchanged - it spawns\nno process at all - and is pinned by a test so a future marker cannot silently\nship there.\n\nNOT RUN ON WINDOWS. The tests are platform-independent: the prompt is provably\nabsent from argv, total argv is under 8191, and the fixture asserts it WOULD\nhave exceeded it. A real Windows run is still needed to close the issue.\n\n#324 - facts promote --keep-both queues confidence-0 proposals\n---------------------------------------------------------------\nConfidence was a literal 0 with no similarity ever computed, and one proposal\nwas queued per PAIR. Now computed lexically, and the queue holds a spanning set\n(n-1 edges, not n(n-1)/2) while cross-links still cover every pair.\n\nThe confidence is explicitly lexical - same-claim evidence, never \"the supersede\nis right\" - and is capped at DefaultConfidenceThreshold minus 0.05, defined\nrelative to the threshold so lowering the threshold cannot strand the ceiling\nabove it. A promote proposal therefore can never become auto-apply-eligible.\nAudited: nothing downstream filters, sorts or auto-applies on Confidence.\n\nVerification\n------------\nEvery fix has a regression test verified by weakening - the guard patched\ncompile-clean, the test shown to go red, the assertion recorded. Full ./...\ngreen under -race.\n\nOne weakening is reported as not-proven rather than passed: an early attempt at\nthe scratch-index guard failed to compile, so it demonstrated nothing until\nredone.\nEOF\ngit commit -q -F ~/.local/state/entire-distill/pr2msg.txt\ngit --no-pager log --oneline -1\ngit push -q -u origin fix/multiagent-safety-indexing-windows 2>&1 | tail -2; echo \"pushed\"","description":"Commit and push PR2","timeout":900000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":386,"cache_read_input_tokens":381151,"output_tokens":2347,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":386,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2347,"cache_read_input_tokens":381151,"cache_creation_input_tokens":386,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":386},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_013rNdwkui2TKbCeYi2BnAje":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-safety\ngit add -A\ncat > ~/.local/state/entire-distill/pr2msg.txt <<'EOF'\nfix(safety): stop brain colliding with concurrent git, stalling on a dirty tree, and ignoring local models\n\nFive filed issues, all reproduced before being changed.\n\n#326 - brain brief takes .git/index.lock\n----------------------------