tent is stale: the\nindex describes HEAD, and HEAD has not moved because the worktree has\nuncommitted edits. The two cases where it does matter - a snapshot taken in\nworktree mode, or from a dirty tree - were already decided further down, so the\ncheck was redundant as well as harmful. A dirty-worktree refusal now lets the\nwatch tick continue; every other refresh failure still aborts it, because an\nunrefreshed brain must not have tokens spent against it.\n\n#328 - a local model is installed and never used\n-------------------------------------------------\ndefaultRefreshAgent tried codex, then claude, then none. A user who installed\nollama specifically to keep transcripts off a third party got one of two\noutcomes: no distillation at all, or - if a cloud CLI happened to be installed\ntoo - their session content sent to that provider instead.\n\nollama is now tried FIRST. Transcripts are the most sensitive thing this product\ntouches; when a local model is available, using it is what the user configured.\nThis changes the agent for someone who has both installed. `--agent` still\noverrides per run.\n\n`watch` hardcoded codex, which is the same defect and worse: the watcher runs\nunattended, so the transcripts went out on a timer. It now uses the \"auto\"\nsentinel - note that \"\" is NOT that sentinel and passes through as an invalid\nagent name.\n\nThe issue also reports that a non-loopback ENTIRE_BRAIN_OLLAMA_URL is rejected\nsilently. It is not: the rejection is a hard error naming the URL. No change.\nThe loopback restriction itself is a deliberate privacy boundary with a redirect\nguard behind it, so an opt-in remote host is NOT included here - that is a\nproduct decision, not a bug fix.\n\nMoving the agent check: it now sits below the distill pass lock. A pass that\nfinds the lock held does nothing, so the agent is irrelevant, and reporting \"no\nagent on PATH\" tells a supervised watcher it has a configuration error when it\nactually has transient contention. Its text now names ollama too.\n\n#322 - Windows \"command line is too long\"\n------------------------------------------\nA ~7516-byte system prompt sat on argv against cmd.exe's 8191 limit. Moved off\nargv at the shared builder: claude takes --system-prompt-file (0600, inside an\n0700 temp dir, removed on every exit path), codex takes it on stdin, which it\nconcatenates with the piped transcript itself. ollama is unchanged - it spawns\nno process at all - and is pinned by a test so a future marker cannot silently\nship there.\n\nNOT RUN ON WINDOWS. The tests are platform-independent: the prompt is provably\nabsent from argv, total argv is under 8191, and the fixture asserts it WOULD\nhave exceeded it. A real Windows run is still needed to close the issue.\n\n#324 - facts promote --keep-both queues confidence-0 proposals\n---------------------------------------------------------------\nConfidence was a literal 0 with no similarity ever computed, and one proposal\nwas queued per PAIR. Now computed lexically, and the queue holds a spanning set\n(n-1 edges, not n(n-1)/2) while cross-links still cover every pair.\n\nThe confidence is explicitly lexical - same-claim evidence, never \"the supersede\nis right\" - and is capped at DefaultConfidenceThreshold minus 0.05, defined\nrelative to the threshold so lowering the threshold cannot strand the ceiling\nabove it. A promote proposal therefore can never become auto-apply-eligible.\nAudited: nothing downstream filters, sorts or auto-applies on Confidence.\n\nVerification\n------------\nEvery fix has a regression test verified by weakening - the guard patched\ncompile-clean, the test shown to go red, the assertion recorded. Full ./...\ngreen under -race.\n\nOne weakening is reported as not-proven rather than passed: an early attempt at\nthe scratch-index guard failed to compile, so it demonstrated nothing until\nredone.\nEOF\ngit commit -q -F ~/.local/state/entire-distill/pr2msg.txt\ngit --no-pager log --oneline -1\ngit push -q -u origin fix/multiagent-safety-indexing-windows 2>&1 | tail -2; echo \"pushed\"","description":"Commit and push PR2","timeout":900000}},"serverClassifierRequest":"6265e6f1-0ef3-49ca-98e9-2785100eec18","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cfeazgy26bNzJGAycNu6Q","type":"assistant","uuid":"55015873-6768-4c34-bfeb-62a3be670db6","timestamp":"2026-10-03T03:23:41.917Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-safety","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
