remote":"entireio/entire-graph","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-safety","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"55015873-6768-4c34-bfeb-62a3be670db6","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-safety","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"3d9ee793-f931-494e-89e1-e193a120c551","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14462497 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"997a4d9e-ad7a-4c1b-a4b1-956faea42ec3","timestamp":"2026-10-03T03:23:44.591Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14462497 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-safety","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"997a4d9e-ad7a-4c1b-a4b1-956faea42ec3","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cfeb38FbZ8UP1v2WM8a9m","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016Sd7o5JAFnosJYbWKWE7Tm","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-safety\ngh pr create --repo entireio/entire-brain --base fix/retrieval-output-correctness --head fix/multiagent-safety-indexing-windows \\\n  --title \"fix(safety): stop brain colliding with concurrent git, stalling on a dirty tree, and ignoring local models\" \\\n  --body \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nSecond of three. Stacked on #329 — **base is `fix/retrieval-output-correctness`, not `main`.**\n\nFive filed issues, each reproduced before being changed. Two of the plan's premises turned out to be wrong and are corrected below.\n\n## #326 — `brain brief` takes `.git/index.lock`\n\n`--no-optional-locks` at the single spawn point closes `git status`. It is **not sufficient**: a porcelain `git diff <commit>` does its own index refresh that the flag does not gate. Measured on git 2.54.0, each trial from an identical stat-dirty index, restored in between:\n\n| command | index |\n|---|---|\n| `git diff --name-status -M -C HEAD` | **rewrites** |\n| `git --no-optional-locks diff --name-status -M -C HEAD` | **rewrites** |\n| `git --no-optional-locks diff-index --name-status …` | leaves it alone |\n\nThat matters because `changedSemanticFiles` runs inside `brain brief` — the exact command the issue reports.\n\nConverting to plumbing would fix the lock and **change the answer**: `diff-index` against an unrefreshed index reports a stat-dirty file (mtime touched, content identical) as modified, i.e. re-indexing a file that did not change. On the same fixture that cost one spurious path.\n\nSo those diffs now run with `GIT_INDEX_FILE` pointing at a **copy**. git refreshes the copy, the real index is never opened for write, and output is byte-identical to porcelain because it *is* porcelain. Verified: copy output matched real exactly; plumbing differed by one line.\n\n## #327 — indexing stalls on a dirty worktree\n\nA loop, not one bug: dirty → forced rebuild → indexer **refuses** it without `--worktree` → failed refresh aborts the whole watch tick → cursor never advances. Nothing progressed for as long as the tree stayed dirty.\n\nDirtiness alone says nothing about whether indexed content is stale — the index describes HEAD, and HEAD has not moved. The cases where it *does* matter were already decided further down, so the check was redundant as well as harmful. A dirty refusal now lets the tick continue; every other refresh failure still aborts, because an unrefreshed brain must not have tokens spent against it.\n\n## #328 — a local model is installed and never used\n\n`defaultRefreshAgent` tried codex → claude → none. Someone who installed ollama **to keep transcripts off a third party** got either no distillation, or — if a cloud CLI was also present — their sessions sent to that provider.\n\nollama is now tried **first**. This changes the agent for anyone with both installed; `--agent` still overrides. `watch` hardcoded codex, which is worse since it runs unattended — now the `\"auto\"` sentinel (`\"\"` is *not* that sentinel and passes through as an invalid agent name).\n\n**Premise corrected:** the issue says a non-loopback `ENTIRE_BRAIN_OLLAMA_URL` is rejected *silently*. It is not — the rejection is a hard error naming the URL. And the loopback restriction is a deliberate privacy boundary with a redirect guard, so **an opt-in remote host is not included here**: that is a product decision, not a bug fix. Say the word and I will add it.\n\nThe agent check also moved below the distill pass lock. A pass that finds the lock held does nothing, so the agent is irrelevant — reporting \"no agent on PATH\" tells a supervised watcher it has a config error when it has transient contention.\n\n## #322 — Windows \"command line is too long\"\n\nA ~7516-byte prompt on argv against cmd.exe's 8191 limit. Moved off argv at the shared builder: claude takes `--system-prompt-file` (0600 inside an 0700 temp dir, removed on every exit path), codex takes stdin, which it concatenates with the piped transcript itself. ollama unchanged — it spawns no process — and pinned so a marker cannot silently ship there.\n\n**Not run on Windows.** Tests are platform-independent: prompt provably absent from argv, argv under 8191, and the fixture asserts it *would* have exceeded it. A real Windows run is still needed to close the issue.\n\n## #324 — `facts promote --keep-both` queues confidence-0 proposals\n\nConfidence was a literal `0` with no similarity computed, one proposal per **pair**. Now computed lexically, with a spanning set (n−1 edges, not n(n−1)/2); cross-links still cover every pair.\n\nThe confidence is explicitly lexical — same-claim evidence, never \"the supersede is right\" — capped at `DefaultConfidenceThreshold - 0.05`, defined *relative* to the threshold so lowering it cannot strand the ceiling above. A promote proposal can therefore never become auto-apply-eligible. Audited: nothing downstream filters, sorts or auto-applies on `Confidence`.\n\n## Verification\n\nEvery fix has a regression test **verified by weakening** — guard patched compile-clean, test shown red, assertion recorded. Full `./...` green under `-race`, lint clean.\n\nOne weakening is reported as *not proven* rather than passed: an early scratch-index mutation failed to compile, so it demonstrated nothing until redone.\n\nNot merging without your approval.\nEOF\n)\" 2>&1 | tail -2","description":"Open PR 2","timeout":900000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2502,"cache_read_input_tokens":381537,"output_tokens":2008,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2502,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2008,"cache_read_input_tokens":381537,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2502,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2502},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_016Sd7o5JAFnosJYbWKWE7Tm":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-safety\ngh pr create --repo entireio/entire-brain --base fix/retrieval-output-correctness --head fix/multiagent-safety-indexing-windows \\\n  --title \"fix(safety): stop brain colliding with concurrent git, stalling on a dirty tree, and ignoring local models\" \\\n  --body \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nSecond of three. Stacked on #329 — **base is `fix/retrieval-output-correctness`, not `main`.**\n\nFive filed issues, each reproduced before being changed. Two of the plan's premises turned out to be wrong and are corrected below.\n\n## #326 — `brain brief` takes `.git/index.lock`\n\n`--no-optional-locks` at the single spawn point closes `git status`. It is **not sufficient**: a porcelain `git diff <commit>` does its own index refresh that the flag does not gate. Measured on git 2.54.0, each trial from an identical stat-dirty index, restored in between:\n\n| command | index |\n|---|---|\n| `git diff --name-status -M -C HEAD` | **rewrites** |\n| `git --no-optional-locks diff --name-status -M -C HEAD` | **rewrites** |\n| `git --no-optional-locks diff-index --name-status …` | leaves it alone |\n\nThat matters because `changedSemanticFiles` runs inside `brain brief` — the exact command the issue reports.\n\nConverting to plumbing would fix the lock and **change the answer**: `diff-index` against an unrefreshed index reports a stat-dirty file (mtime touched, content identical) as modified, i.e. re-indexing a file that did not change. On the same fixture that cost one spurious path.\n\nSo those diffs now run with `GIT_INDEX_FILE` pointing at a **copy**. git refreshes the copy, the real index is never opened for write, and output is byte-identical to porcelain because it *is* porcelain. Verified: copy output matched real exactly; plumbing differed by one line.\n\n## #327 — indexing stalls on a dirty worktree\n\nA loop, not one bug: dirty → forced rebuild → indexer **refuses** it without `--worktree` → failed refresh aborts the whole watch tick → cursor never advances. Nothing progressed for as long as the tree stayed dirty.\n\nDirtiness alone says nothing about whether indexed content is stale — the index describes HEAD, and HEAD has not moved. The cases where it *does* matter were already decided further down, so the check was redundant as well as harmful. A dirty refusal now lets the tick continue; every other refresh failure still aborts, because an unrefreshed brain must not have tokens spent against it.\n\n## #328 — a local model is installed and never used\n\n`defaultRefreshAgent` tried codex → claude → none. Someone who installed ollama **to keep transcripts off a third party** got either no distillation, or — if a cloud CLI was also present — their sessions sent to that provider.\n\nollama is now tried **first**. This changes the agent for anyone with both installed; `--agent` still overrides. `watch` hardcoded codex, which is worse since it runs unattended — now the `\"auto\"` sentinel (`\"\"` is *not* that sentinel and passes through as an invalid agent name).\n\n**Premise corrected:** the issue says a non-loopback `ENTIRE_BRAIN_OLLAMA_URL` is rejected *silently*. It is not — the rejection is a hard error naming the URL. And the loopback restriction is a deliberate privacy boundary with a redirect guard, so **an opt-in remote host is not included here**: that is a product decision, not a bug fix. Say the word and I will add it.\n\nThe agent check also moved below the distill pass lock. A pass that finds the lock held does nothing, so the agent is irrelevant — reporting \"no agent on PATH\" tells a supervised watcher it has a config error when it has transient contention.\n\n## #322 — Windows \"command line is too long\"\n\nA ~7516-byte prompt on argv against cmd.exe's 8191 limit. Moved off argv at the shared builder: claude takes `--system-prompt-file` (0600 inside an 0700 temp dir, removed on every exit path), codex takes stdin, which it concatenates with the piped transcript itself. ollama unchanged — it spawns no process — and pinned so a marker cannot silently ship there.\n\n**Not run on Windows.** Tests are platform-independent: prompt provably absent from argv, argv under 8191, and the fixture asserts it *would* have exceeded it. A real Windows run is still needed to close the issue.\n\n## #324 — `facts promote --keep-both` queues confidence-0 proposals\n\nConfidence was a literal `0` with no similarity computed, one proposal per **pair**. Now computed lexically, with a spanning set (n−1 edges, not n(n−1)/2); cross-links still cover every pair.\n\nThe confidence is explicitly lexical — same-claim evidence, never \"the supersede is right\" — capped at `DefaultConfidenceThreshold - 0.05`, defined *relative* to the threshold so lowering it cannot strand the ceiling above. A promote proposal can therefore never become auto-apply-eligible. Audited: nothing downstream filters, sorts or auto-applies on `Confidence`.\n\n## Verification\n\nEvery fix has a regression test **verified by weakening** — guard patched compile-clean, test shown red, assertion recorded. Full `./...` green under `-race`, lint clean.\n\nOne weakening is reported as *not proven* rather than passed: an early scratch-index mutation failed to compile, so it demonstrated nothing until redone.\n\nNot merging without your approval.\nEOF\n)\" 2>&1 | tail -2","description":"Open PR 2","timeout":900000}},"serverClassifierRequest":"a3a36a83-99ab-44ef-a6f1-b3942c514d13","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cfeb37G4ijKKCG4GBMhBs","type":"assistant","uuid":"1c43c923-612e-412a-b9fb-1927645f419b","timestamp":"2026-10-03T03:24:08.515Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-safety","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
