{"parentUuid":"7fc9bfb8-eacf-4e95-a4ae-798ea2b164d3","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14460027 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"a0f8bace-0f74-4322-ac54-7b0428e5c84a","timestamp":"2026-10-03T03:24:21.185Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14460027 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"a0f8bace-0f74-4322-ac54-7b0428e5c84a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cfeb5pdX2iYNWCzBiDzYs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XXQ7HsKa97EktYkdUCnFT2","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide\ngo test ./internal/agentsetup/ ./internal/cli/ -run 'TestNormalGuide|TestGuidesNameOnly|TestPreEditHook|TestCoordination|TestMCPToolDescriptions|TestAgentGuide|TestInitAgents' -count=1 -timeout 900s 2>&1 | tail -4\ngofmt -l internal/ | head -3\ngit add -A && git commit -q -m \"fix(guide): make shipped guidance directive, name only commands graph exposes, and wire the pre-edit hook\n\nThe guide told agents not to use the tools, and CI enforced that in both\ndirections: the test BANNED the directive strings \\\"FIRST action\\\" and\n\\\"SEARCH FIRST\\\", and separately REQUIRED \\\"sufficient locations\\\" to be present.\n\nThat wording came from benchmark arm-fairness doctrine, which forbids giving one\narm an instruction the other lacks. The requirement is correct for an A/B cell\nand fatal for shipped text: in a user's repo there is no second arm, only an\nagent deciding whether to bother. Measured afterwards: 332 graph calls against\n96,987 exploration calls (0.34%), graph-first rate 0 in every session sampled.\nA Claude session asked to explain itself said it had been told to start with\nbrain brief and skipped it. It was following the guide it was given.\n\nentire-graph diagnosed this, fixed its own copy and left the reasoning behind.\nThis is that fix, ported, plus three things its port did not cover.\n\nThe permissive wording was pinned in THREE places, not two: coordination_test.go,\nscripts/test-agent-coordination.py, and strict_test.go, which asserted that\nNORMAL mode contains \\\"Skip ceremonial queries\\\". Normal mode is distinguished\nfrom strict by its mode, not by offering the agent a way out.\n\ncombinedWorkflow - the guide most users get - carried no Graph obligation at\nall. It was brainWorkflow plus a capability list, so an agent reading it had\nnothing telling it to check the call graph before editing.\n\n#323: the guide named \\`entire graph query\\`, which does not exist in the\nreleased v0.4.0 dispatch. The binary installed here is a symlink to a dev\ncheckout where it does, which is how this survived. \\`search\\` is the only verb\ncorrect against every graph a user may have: it is the sole verb in 0.4.0 and\nremains an alias on 0.4.1+. Verified against the running build.\n\nhook pre-edit has shipped since PR #24 with nothing invoking it - the only push\npath in a product that is otherwise entirely pull, which is the measured\nproblem. Wiring it surfaced a scoping issue: brain does not own\n.claude/settings.json, \\`entire enable\\` writes it. So it MERGES - unrelated keys\npreserved, other products' entries untouched, idempotent by command match - and\nrefuses rather than overwrites anything it does not recognise. The matcher is\nEdit|Write|MultiEdit, not the Agent-only matcher \\`entire enable\\` writes, which\nnever fires at the moment a fact about the file would change the edit.\n\nMCP tool descriptions: 37 tools, none of which said when to use the tool instead\nof grep. The description is what an agent reads when choosing; the guide is a\nfile it may never open. 23 rewritten, each with a substitution cue and a limit;\nthe test iterates the live tool table with an explicit deny-list, so a new tool\nfails by default.\n\nREADME: the \\\"What to ask\\\" table moved from line 124 to the top, its command\ncolumn dropped, its verbs corrected, and branch-scoped facts stated.\n\nGuards added so none of this can regress: TestNormalGuideStaysDirective pins\nthe absence of every exit by its exact words AND the presence of the directive;\nTestGuidesNameOnlyCommandsGraphExposes pins #323. Both verified by weakening.\" 2>&1 | tail -2\ngit log --oneline -1","description":"Test and commit PR3","timeout":1200000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":490,"cache_read_input_tokens":386096,"output_tokens":1428,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":490,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1428,"cache_read_input_tokens":386096,"cache_creation_input_tokens":490,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":490},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01XXQ7HsKa97EktYkdUCnFT2":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide\ngo test ./internal/agentsetup/ ./internal/cli/ -run 'TestNormalGuide|TestGuidesNameOnly|TestPreEditHook|TestCoordination|TestMCPToolDescriptions|TestAgentGuide|TestInitAgents' -count=1 -timeout 900s 2>&1 | tail -4\ngofmt -l internal/ | head -3\ngit add -A && git commit -q -m \"fix(guide): make shipped guidance directive, name only commands graph exposes, and wire the pre-edit hook\n\nThe guide told agents not to use the tools, and CI enforced that in both\ndirections: the test BANNED the directive strings \\\"FIRST action\\\" and\n\\\"SEARCH FIRST\\\", and separately REQUIRED \\\"sufficient locations\\\" to be present.\n\nThat wording came from benchmark arm-fairness doctrine, which forbids giving one\narm an instruction the other lacks. The requirement is correct for an A/B cell\nand fatal for shipped text: in a user's repo there is no second arm, only an\nagent deciding whether to bother. Measured afterwards: 332 graph calls against\n96,987 exploration calls (0.34%), graph-first rate 0 in every session sampled.\nA Claude session asked to explain itself said it had been told to start with\nbrain brief and skipped it. It was following the guide it was given.\n\nentire-graph diagnosed this, fixed its own copy and left the reasoning behind.\nThis is that fix, ported, plus three things its port did not cover.\n\nThe permissive wording was pinned in THREE places, not two: coordination_test.go,\nscripts/test-agent-coordination.py, and strict_test.go, which asserted that\nNORMAL mode contains \\\"Skip ceremonial queries\\\". Normal mode is distinguished\nfrom strict by its mode, not by offering the agent a way out.\n\ncombinedWorkflow - the guide most users get - carried no Graph obligation at\nall. It was brainWorkflow plus a capability list, so an agent reading it had\nnothing telling it to check the call graph before editing.\n\n#323: the guide named \\`entire graph query\\`, which does not exist in the\nreleased v0.4.0 dispatch. The binary installed here is a symlink to a dev\ncheckout where it does, which is how this survived. \\`search\\` is the only verb\ncorrect against every graph a user may have: it is the sole verb in 0.4.0 and\nremains an alias on 0.4.1+. Verified against the running build.\n\nhook pre-edit has shipped since PR #24 with nothing invoking it - the only push\npath in a product that is otherwise entirely pull, which is the measured\nproblem. Wiring it surfaced a scoping issue: brain does not own\n.claude/settings.json, \\`entire enable\\` writes it. So it MERGES - unrelated keys\npreserved, other products' entries untouched, idempotent by command match - and\nrefuses rather than overwrites anything it does not recognise. The matcher is\nEdit|Write|MultiEdit, not the Agent-only matcher \\`entire enable\\` writes, which\nnever fires at the moment a fact about the file would change the edit.\n\nMCP tool descriptions: 37 tools, none of which said when to use the tool instead\nof grep. The description is what an agent reads when choosing; the guide is a\nfile it may never open. 23 rewritten, each with a substitution cue and a limit;\nthe test iterates the live tool table with an explicit deny-list, so a new tool\nfails by default.\n\nREADME: the \\\"What to ask\\\" table moved from line 124 to the top, its command\ncolumn dropped, its verbs corrected, and branch-scoped facts stated.\n\nGuards added so none of this can regress: TestNormalGuideStaysDirective pins\nthe absence of every exit by its exact words AND the presence of the directive;\nTestGuidesNameOnlyCommandsGraphExposes pins #323. Both verified by weakening.\" 2>&1 | tail -2\ngit log --oneline -1","description":"Test and commit PR3","timeout":1200000}},"serverClassifierRequest":"3454a384-fbed-4cba-979c-b02e1fd388a2","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cfeb5oMPLLWpLGz8fyeBF","type":"assistant","uuid":"3f0cfcb4-b508-4afa-84cb-a8a646852993","timestamp":"2026-10-03T03:24:40.872Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
