hich","+\t// takes `.git/index.lock` and makes a concurrent human or agent git command","+\t// fail (issue #326). --no-optional-locks does not suppress that particular","+\t// refresh -- measured, see gitHardenConfig -- so the only fix is to stop","+\t// calling the porcelain. `diff-index` is the plumbing `git diff <commit>`","+\t// is built on and never refreshes.","+\t//","+\t// -M is load-bearing. `git diff` gets rename detection from diff.renames,","+\t// whose default is true; plumbing reads only the basic diff config and so","+\t// gets none. Without -M a rename is counted as a whole-file delete plus a","+\t// whole-file add, changing BOTH the file count and the insertion/deletion","+\t// counts (measured: \" 3 files changed, 6 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)\"","+\t// against the porcelain's \" 2 files changed, 1 insertion(+)\" on the same","+\t// worktree). With -M the output is byte-identical to the porcelain on git","+\t// 2.54.0, including against a stat-dirty-but-identical file -- the","+\t// --shortstat path reads content, so such a file is dropped from both.","+\t// (The raw `diff-index --name-status` path does NOT read content and would","+\t// report it, which is why this swap is safe only for stat output.)","+\tif stat, err := gitScalar(ctx, runner, repoDir, \"diff-index\", \"-M\", \"--shortstat\", \"HEAD\"); err == nil {"," \t\tlive.DiffStat = stat"," \t} else {"," \t\tlive.Warnings = append(live.Warnings, \"diff stat unavailable: \"+err.Error())"]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/brain_brief_profile_test.go","hunks":[{"oldStart":65,"oldLines":7,"newStart":65,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," \trunner.responses[fakeCommandKey(\"git\", \"status\", \"--porcelain\")] = fakeCommandResponse{}"," \trunner.responses[fakeCommandKey(\"git\", \"status\", \"--porcelain\", \"--untracked-files=all\")] = fakeCommandResponse{}","-\trunner.responses[fakeCommandKey(\"git\", \"diff\", \"--shortstat\", \"HEAD\")] = fakeCommandResponse{}","+\tr