{"parentUuid":"9a41af4b-5374-46f3-963e-31f84aa965c9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfedLCYWn9GkdL27jyJod","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 14 packages green under `-race`, lint clean. Pushing PR 3:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":453,"cache_read_input_tokens":403360,"output_tokens":1652,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":453,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1652,"cache_read_input_tokens":403360,"cache_creation_input_tokens":453,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":453},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"848033cc-824b-476b-95be-541a27e43402","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfedLBS3XbkMYm6wSLnza","type":"assistant","uuid":"56e8da19-9005-43fd-b276-e22c31bae039","timestamp":"2026-10-03T03:53:53.124Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"56e8da19-9005-43fd-b276-e22c31bae039","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfedLCYWn9GkdL27jyJod","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Xcf1wkLMbQgQTbCzhsFQrq","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide\ngit add -A && git commit -q --amend --no-edit\ngit push -q -f -u origin fix/agent-guide-directive-and-discovery 2>&1 | tail -2\ngh pr create --repo entireio/entire-brain --base fix/multiagent-safety-indexing-windows --head fix/agent-guide-directive-and-discovery \\\n  --title \"fix(guide): make shipped guidance directive, name only commands graph exposes, and wire the pre-edit hook\" \\\n  --body \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nThird of three. Stacked on #330 — **base is `fix/multiagent-safety-indexing-windows`, not `main`.**\n\nThis is the root cause of \"agents don't use Brain or Graph.\" It is not that agents are habitual.\n\n## The guide told them not to, and CI enforced it both ways\n\n`coordination_test.go` **banned** the directive strings `\"FIRST action\"` and `\"SEARCH FIRST\"`, and separately **required** `\"sufficient locations\"` to be present. The permissive wording was pinned from both directions at once.\n\nIt came from benchmark arm-fairness doctrine, which forbids giving one arm an instruction the other lacks. Correct for an A/B cell; fatal for shipped text — in a user's repo there is no second arm, only an agent deciding whether to bother. Measured afterwards: **332 graph calls against 96,987 exploration calls (0.34%)**, graph-first rate **0** in every session sampled.\n\nA Claude session asked to explain itself said it had been told to start with `brain brief` and skipped it. It was following the guide it was given.\n\nentire-graph diagnosed this, fixed its own copy, and left the reasoning and a guard behind. **This is that fix, ported** — not a new product decision — plus three things its port did not cover.\n\n## Three things the port did not cover\n\n**It was pinned in three places, not two.** `strict_test.go` asserted that *normal* mode contains `\"Skip ceremonial queries\"`. Normal mode is distinguished from strict by its mode, not by offering the agent a way out.\n\n**`combinedWorkflow` carried no Graph obligation at all.** It was `brainWorkflow` plus a capability list — and it is the guide most users get. An agent reading it had nothing telling it to check the call graph before editing.\n\n**#323 — the guide named a command that does not exist.** `entire graph query` is absent from the released v0.4.0 dispatch. The binary installed here is a symlink to a dev checkout where it *does* exist, which is how this survived review. `search` is the only verb correct against every graph a user may have: the sole verb in 0.4.0, still an alias on 0.4.1+. Verified against the running build.\n\n## The hook that shipped and was never called\n\n`hook pre-edit` has existed since PR #24 with **nothing invoking it** — the only push path in a product that is otherwise entirely pull, which is precisely the measured problem.\n\nWiring it surfaced a scoping issue: **brain does not own `.claude/settings.json`** — `entire enable` writes it. So it **merges**: unrelated keys preserved, other products' entries untouched, idempotent by command match, and it *refuses and reports* on anything it does not recognise rather than overwriting. Matcher is `Edit|Write|MultiEdit`, not the `Agent`-only matcher `entire enable` writes, which never fires at the moment a fact about the file would change the edit.\n\n## Tool descriptions and README\n\n37 `brain_*` tools, **none** of which said when to use the tool instead of grep. The description is what an agent reads when choosing; the guide is a file it may never open. 23 rewritten with a substitution cue and a limit. The test iterates the live tool table with an explicit deny-list, so a new tool fails by default.\n\nTwo byte-budget pins moved (917→1090, 1167→1263) with the reasoning recorded in place: this is sent once per session in the tool list, not per call.\n\nREADME: the \"What to ask\" table moved from line 124 to the top, command column dropped, verbs corrected against commands actually run, and branch-scoped facts stated.\n\n## Verification\n\n`TestNormalGuideStaysDirective` pins the absence of every exit **by its exact words** and the presence of the directive. `TestGuidesNameOnlyCommandsGraphExposes` pins #323. Both verified by weakening, along with the four hook-merge guards.\n\nFull `./...` green under `-race` across the whole stack; lint clean.\n\nNot merging without your approval.\nEOF\n)\" 2>&1 | tail -2","description":"Push and open PR 3","timeout":900000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":453,"cache_read_input_tokens":403360,"output_tokens":1652,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":453,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1652,"cache_read_input_tokens":403360,"cache_creation_input_tokens":453,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":453},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Xcf1wkLMbQgQTbCzhsFQrq":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide\ngit add -A && git commit -q --amend --no-edit\ngit push -q -f -u origin fix/agent-guide-directive-and-discovery 2>&1 | tail -2\ngh pr create --repo entireio/entire-brain --base fix/multiagent-safety-indexing-windows --head fix/agent-guide-directive-and-discovery \\\n  --title \"fix(guide): make shipped guidance directive, name only commands graph exposes, and wire the pre-edit hook\" \\\n  --body \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nThird of three. Stacked on #330 — **base is `fix/multiagent-safety-indexing-windows`, not `main`.**\n\nThis is the root cause of \"agents don't use Brain or Graph.\" It is not that agents are habitual.\n\n## The guide told them not to, and CI enforced it both ways\n\n`coordination_test.go` **banned** the directive strings `\"FIRST action\"` and `\"SEARCH FIRST\"`, and separately **required** `\"sufficient locations\"` to be present. The permissive wording was pinned from both directions at once.\n\nIt came from benchmark arm-fairness doctrine, which forbids giving one arm an instruction the other lacks. Correct for an A/B cell; fatal for shipped text — in a user's repo there is no second arm, only an agent deciding whether to bother. Measured afterwards: **332 graph calls against 96,987 exploration calls (0.34%)**, graph-first rate **0** in every session sampled.\n\nA Claude session asked to explain itself said it had been told to start with `brain brief` and skipped it. It was following the guide it was given.\n\nentire-graph diagnosed this, fixed its own copy, and left the reasoning and a guard behind. **This is that fix, ported** — not a new product decision — plus three things its port did not cover.\n\n## Three things the port did not cover\n\n**It was pinned in three places, not two.** `strict_test.go` asserted that *normal* mode contains `\"Skip ceremonial queries\"`. Normal mode is distinguished from strict by its mode, not by offering the agent a way out.\n\n**`combinedWorkflow` carried no Graph obligation at all.** It was `brainWorkflow` plus a capability list — and it is the guide most users get. An agent reading it had nothing telling it to check the call graph before editing.\n\n**#323 — the guide named a command that does not exist.** `entire graph query` is absent from the released v0.4.0 dispatch. The binary installed here is a symlink to a dev checkout where it *does* exist, which is how this survived review. `search` is the only verb correct against every graph a user may have: the sole verb in 0.4.0, still an alias on 0.4.1+. Verified against the running build.\n\n## The hook that shipped and was never called\n\n`hook pre-edit` has existed since PR #24 with **nothing invoking it** — the only push path in a product that is otherwise entirely pull, which is precisely the measured problem.\n\nWiring it surfaced a scoping issue: **brain does not own `.claude/settings.json`** — `entire enable` writes it. So it **merges**: unrelated keys preserved, other products' entries untouched, idempotent by command match, and it *refuses and reports* on anything it does not recognise rather than overwriting. Matcher is `Edit|Write|MultiEdit`, not the `Agent`-only matcher `entire enable` writes, which never fires at the moment a fact about the file would change the edit.\n\n## Tool descriptions and README\n\n37 `brain_*` tools, **none** of which said when to use the tool instead of grep. The description is what an agent reads when choosing; the guide is a file it may never open. 23 rewritten with a substitution cue and a limit. The test iterates the live tool table with an explicit deny-list, so a new tool fails by default.\n\nTwo byte-budget pins moved (917→1090, 1167→1263) with the reasoning recorded in place: this is sent once per session in the tool list, not per call.\n\nREADME: the \"What to ask\" table moved from line 124 to the top, command column dropped, verbs corrected against commands actually run, and branch-scoped facts stated.\n\n## Verification\n\n`TestNormalGuideStaysDirective` pins the absence of every exit **by its exact words** and the presence of the directive. `TestGuidesNameOnlyCommandsGraphExposes` pins #323. Both verified by weakening, along with the four hook-merge guards.\n\nFull `./...` green under `-race` across the whole stack; lint clean.\n\nNot merging without your approval.\nEOF\n)\" 2>&1 | tail -2","description":"Push and open PR 3","timeout":900000}},"serverClassifierRequest":"848033cc-824b-476b-95be-541a27e43402","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfedLBS3XbkMYm6wSLnza","type":"assistant","uuid":"593b1d17-22e7-4ab7-a69b-0f0f3fff1624","timestamp":"2026-10-03T03:54:11.039Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
