{"parentUuid":"01df9b4b-bcfc-471c-9413-943b201770fc","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfedY6rYmvUjAHN39TbSM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WbmqBtFq4rdFn2qosNzN4p","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Locate task arm OLD 1","prompt":"SETUP (do this first, exactly): run `export PATH=\"/Users/suhaan/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp/usage-exp/bin:$PATH\"; export EXP_ARM=\"old-1\"` and keep every later shell command in that same session so the variables persist. Work read-only in /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide. Do not edit any file.\n\nYour repository's agent guide (.entire/agent-guide.md) reads:\n\n---\nUse Brain for task context and retained knowledge. Begin substantive tasks needing orientation with:\n\n    entire brain brief \"<task>\" --json\n\nSkip this when equivalent task context is already available. Reuse useful code locations from the brief. Use Brain retrieval for previous decisions, attempts, documentation, and durable facts - Brain's episodic memory of what was decided, what went wrong before, and what must stay true.\n\nUse Brain entities history to connect code changes to earlier checkpoints and sessions. Use Brain memory-informed review and workspace capabilities when relevant. Brain semantic answers refer to a stored index, which may differ from current working-tree source.\n\nUse Graph query, def, neighbors, and impact for additional code discovery and structural analysis. Useful locations from the brief do not require a redundant Graph query. Do not ask both tools the same question without an identified gap. Use Graph diff, commit, and checkpoint for semantic comparisons of code revisions.\n\n    entire graph query --repo . --profile full --query \"<task>\"\n\nDirectly inspect source when the task already provides sufficient locations.\nSkip ceremonial queries for small edits and follow-up work with sufficient context.\nRead focused source around useful locations before editing. Check related contracts and make the smallest complete change. VERIFY before stopping. Prefer precise queries and line ranges, but never trade resolution for fewer turns.\n\nIf an ordinary task query fails, continue with useful remaining tools or direct source inspection. Do not automatically install, configure, or repair tools.\n---\n\nTASK: Explain how this codebase decides whether the semantic index needs rebuilding, and what happens downstream when it decides yes. Name the function that makes the decision (file:line), every caller of it, and the one condition that was recently changed. Answer in your own words with file:line citations.\n\nThen, separately, report honestly:\n1. What was your FIRST action after reading the task? Name the exact command or tool call.\n2. Did you use `entire graph` or `entire brain` at any point? If not, why not — what made the alternative more attractive?\n3. How many shell/search/read tool calls did you make in total (your best count)?\n\nBe honest in that report even if the answer is \"I did not use them\". An inaccurate self-report is worse than a negative result. Output caveman-ultra compressed, max 250 words.","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"sonnet"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":708,"cache_read_input_tokens":414848,"output_tokens":4451,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":708,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4451,"cache_read_input_tokens":414848,"cache_creation_input_tokens":708,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":708},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"