{"parentUuid":"144a435e-0614-42df-b77c-8fbbcad6ddf1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfeeFXmt56NLGskFRiHKX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"CI is still running. While it does, let me save the two findings from this session that will matter again:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":483,"cache_read_input_tokens":444710,"output_tokens":1346,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":556},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":483,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1346,"cache_read_input_tokens":444710,"cache_creation_input_tokens":483,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":483},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"7d238e1c-9e1c-44f3-b6f0-fb16ec3ab291","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfeeFWD8dodCz8CEe6wfa","type":"assistant","uuid":"b8b33d80-9fad-4124-81ef-9417ed071b2c","timestamp":"2026-10-03T04:06:04.993Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"b8b33d80-9fad-4124-81ef-9417ed071b2c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfeeFXmt56NLGskFRiHKX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0187uZKKkoQ5wpMXuNrrh7r5","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/verification-harness-false-pass.md","content":"---\nname: verification-harness-false-pass\ndescription: My own verification commands silently no-opped three times in one session, each producing a comfortable false PASS, never a false failure\nmetadata:\n  type: feedback\n---\n\nA check that cannot fail reports success. This happened three times in one\nsession, by three different mechanisms, and every time the bogus answer was the\none that let me stop looking:\n\n1. **`timeout` does not exist on macOS.** `timeout 60 <cmd>` failed with\n   \"command not found\", which did not match the error pattern I was grepping\n   for, so ten broken doc commands were recorded as `ok`. Three of them were\n   genuinely broken.\n2. **`.git` is a FILE in a worktree, not a directory.** `md5sum .git/index`\n   failed identically before and after, the hashes \"matched\", and I reported a\n   subagent's correct measurement as wrong.\n3. **Trials that mutate the thing they measure.** Running `git diff` to test\n   whether it refreshes the index refreshes the index, so trial 2 saw a clean\n   state and passed. Only snapshot-restore between trials gave a stable answer.\n\n**Why:** a false failure is loud and gets investigated; a false pass is silent\nand ends the investigation. The asymmetry means an unreliable harness\nsystematically moves me toward \"no problem here\".\n\n**How to apply:** before trusting any verification loop, run the\nNEGATIVE control first — prove the harness reports failure when the defect is\npresent. If the unflagged/broken case does not fail, nothing after it means\nanything. Assert the fixture is in the state the test needs (file exists, is\nnon-empty, is actually stat-dirty) and fail loudly when it is not. Isolate\ntrials that mutate shared state. See [[mutation-didnt-fire-suspect-the-test]]\nand [[green-suite-is-not-evidence]] — same family, but those are about guards\nnot firing; this is about the measuring instrument reading zero because it is\nunplugged.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":483,"cache_read_input_tokens":444710,"output_tokens":1346,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":556},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":483,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1346,"cache_read_input_tokens":444710,"cache_creation_input_tokens":483,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":483},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_0187uZKKkoQ5wpMXuNrrh7r5":{"file_path":"/Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/verification-harness-false-pass.md","content":"---\nname: verification-harness-false-pass\ndescription: My own verification commands silently no-opped three times in one session, each producing a comfortable false PASS, never a false failure\nmetadata:\n  type: feedback\n---\n\nA check that cannot fail reports success. This happened three times in one\nsession, by three different mechanisms, and every time the bogus answer was the\none that let me stop looking:\n\n1. **`timeout` does not exist on macOS.** `timeout 60 <cmd>` failed with\n   \"command not found\", which did not match the error pattern I was grepping\n   for, so ten broken doc commands were recorded as `ok`. Three of them were\n   genuinely broken.\n2. **`.git` is a FILE in a worktree, not a directory.** `md5sum .git/index`\n   failed identically before and after, the hashes \"matched\", and I reported a\n   subagent's correct measurement as wrong.\n3. **Trials that mutate the thing they measure.** Running `git diff` to test\n   whether it refreshes the index refreshes the index, so trial 2 saw a clean\n   state and passed. Only snapshot-restore between trials gave a stable answer.\n\n**Why:** a false failure is loud and gets investigated; a false pass is silent\nand ends the investigation. The asymmetry means an unreliable harness\nsystematically moves me toward \"no problem here\".\n\n**How to apply:** before trusting any verification loop, run the\nNEGATIVE control first — prove the harness reports failure when the defect is\npresent. If the unflagged/broken case does not fail, nothing after it means\nanything. Assert the fixture is in the state the test needs (file exists, is\nnon-empty, is actually stat-dirty) and fail loudly when it is not. Isolate\ntrials that mutate shared state. See [[mutation-didnt-fire-suspect-the-test]]\nand [[green-suite-is-not-evidence]] — same family, but those are about guards\nnot firing; this is about the measuring instrument reading zero because it is\nunplugged.\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"7d238e1c-9e1c-44f3-b6f0-fb16ec3ab291","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CfeeFWD8dodCz8CEe6wfa","type":"assistant","uuid":"fa12ec1a-84df-4838-9dcb-22e243ecca4f","timestamp":"2026-10-03T04:06:15.946Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
