arness\nsystematically moves me toward \"no problem here\".\n\n**How to apply:** before trusting any verification loop, run the\nNEGATIVE control first — prove the harness reports failure when the defect is\npresent. If the unflagged/broken case does not fail, nothing after it means\nanything. Assert the fixture is in the state the test needs (file exists, is\nnon-empty, is actually stat-dirty) and fail loudly when it is not. Isolate\ntrials that mutate shared state. See [[mutation-didnt-fire-suspect-the-test]]\nand [[green-suite-is-not-evidence]] — same family, but those are about guards\nnot firing; this is about the measuring instrument reading zero because it is\nunplugged.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false,"memdirStamped":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"fa12ec1a-84df-4838-9dcb-22e243ecca4f","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
