{"type":"pr-link","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","prNumber":331,"prUrl":"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/331","prRepository":"entireio/entire-brain","timestamp":"2026-10-03T04:06:27.299Z"}
{"parentUuid":"e4291b8f-0b0c-476a-bd5e-eca9b1e987ae","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfeeHE84V1vBpqLw6siAb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01A6BsrgennVY9yCdGAVBS5y","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/git-no-optional-locks-insufficient.md","content":"---\nname: git-no-optional-locks-insufficient\ndescription: --no-optional-locks stops git status taking index.lock but NOT git diff <commit>; only plumbing or GIT_INDEX_FILE does\nmetadata:\n  type: reference\n---\n\nMeasured on git 2.54.0, each trial from an identical stat-dirty index with the\nindex restored between trials:\n\n    git diff --name-status -M -C HEAD                      REWRITES .git/index\n    git --no-optional-locks diff --name-status -M -C HEAD   REWRITES .git/index\n    git --no-optional-locks diff-index --name-status …      leaves it alone\n\nA porcelain `git diff <commit>` performs its own index refresh that the\noptional-lock setting does not gate. So `--no-optional-locks` closes\n`git status` and leaves every worktree-vs-HEAD diff taking the lock.\n\n**Switching to plumbing changes the answer**, so it is not a free swap:\n`diff-index` against an unrefreshed index reports a stat-dirty file (mtime\ntouched, content identical) as modified.\n\n**The fix that keeps both:** point `GIT_INDEX_FILE` at a COPY of the index.\ngit refreshes the copy, the real index is never opened for write, and the\noutput is byte-identical to porcelain because it IS porcelain. Verified: copy\noutput matched real exactly where plumbing differed by one line.\n\nIn entire-brain this is `runGitWithScratchIndex` (git_harden.go); it mattered\nbecause `changedSemanticFiles` runs inside `brain brief`, which is what\nissue #326 reports colliding with a concurrent git.\n\nCaveat found by CI, not locally: path handling around this must not assume\nUnix. `strings.HasPrefix(path, \"/\")` is true for every absolute path a\nmacOS/Linux test can build and false for every absolute path on Windows —\nsee [[verification-harness-false-pass]].\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1426,"cache_read_input_tokens":445193,"output_tokens":753,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1426,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":753,"cache_read_input_tokens":445193,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1426,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1426},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01A6BsrgennVY9yCdGAVBS5y":{"file_path":"/Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/git-no-optional-locks-insufficient.md","content":"---\nname: git-no-optional-locks-insufficient\ndescription: --no-optional-locks stops git status taking index.lock but NOT git diff <commit>; only plumbing or GIT_INDEX_FILE does\nmetadata:\n  type: reference\n---\n\nMeasured on git 2.54.0, each trial from an identical stat-dirty index with the\nindex restored between trials:\n\n    git diff --name-status -M -C HEAD                      REWRITES .git/index\n    git --no-optional-locks diff --name-status -M -C HEAD   REWRITES .git/index\n    git --no-optional-locks diff-index --name-status …      leaves it alone\n\nA porcelain `git diff <commit>` performs its own index refresh that the\noptional-lock setting does not gate. So `--no-optional-locks` closes\n`git status` and leaves every worktree-vs-HEAD diff taking the lock.\n\n**Switching to plumbing changes the answer**, so it is not a free swap:\n`diff-index` against an unrefreshed index reports a stat-dirty file (mtime\ntouched, content identical) as modified.\n\n**The fix that keeps both:** point `GIT_INDEX_FILE` at a COPY of the index.\ngit refreshes the copy, the real index is never opened for write, and the\noutput is byte-identical to porcelain because it IS porcelain. Verified: copy\noutput matched real exactly where plumbing differed by one line.\n\nIn entire-brain this is `runGitWithScratchIndex` (git_harden.go); it mattered\nbecause `changedSemanticFiles` runs inside `brain brief`, which is what\nissue #326 reports colliding with a concurrent git.\n\nCaveat found by CI, not locally: path handling around this must not assume\nUnix. `strings.HasPrefix(path, \"/\")` is true for every absolute path a\nmacOS/Linux test can build and false for every absolute path on Windows —\nsee [[verification-harness-false-pass]].\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"d84f3a97-69b7-4953-8b69-4e8deab55f80","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfeeHDNQhZW5vQMdNbaso","type":"assistant","uuid":"6b428fb8-e0b8-49c8-8a78-06d28307bc92","timestamp":"2026-10-03T04:06:27.187Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"6b428fb8-e0b8-49c8-8a78-06d28307bc92","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"0c238ab7-1a98-4faa-92ae-19f5662f7ef2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01A6BsrgennVY9yCdGAVBS5y","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/git-no-optional-locks-insufficient.md"}]},"uuid":"01baa7a6-dbdf-4a9d-b743-2da8e0512e9b","timestamp":"2026-10-03T04:06:27.200Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"/Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/git-no-optional-locks-insufficient.md","content":"---\nname: git-no-optional-locks-insufficient\ndescription: \"--no-optional-locks stops git status taking index.lock but NOT git diff <commit>; only plumbing or GIT_INDEX_FILE does\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: reference\n  originSessionId: 6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2\n  modified: 2026-10-03T04:06:27.198Z\n---\n\nMeasured on git 2.54.0, each trial from an identical stat-dirty index with the\nindex restored between trials:\n\n    git diff --name-status -M -C HEAD                      REWRITES .git/index\n    git --no-optional-locks diff --name-status -M -C HEAD   REWRITES .git/index\n    git --no-optional-locks diff-index --name-status …      leaves it alone\n\nA porcelain `git diff <commit>` performs its own index refresh that the\noptional-lock setting does not gate. So `--no-optional-locks` closes\n`git status` and leaves every worktree-vs-HEAD diff taking the lock.\n\n**Switching to plumbing changes the answer**, so it is not a free swap:\n`diff-index` against an unrefreshed index reports a stat-dirty file (mtime\ntouched, content identical) as modified.\n\n**The fix that keeps both:** point `GIT_INDEX_FILE` at a COPY of the index.\ngit refreshes the copy, the real index is never opened for write, and the\noutput is byte-identical to porcelain because it IS porcelain. Verified: copy\noutput matched real exactly where plumbing differed by one line.\n\nIn entire-brain this is `runGitWithScratchIndex` (git_harden.go); it mattered\nbecause `changedSemanticFiles` runs inside `brain brief`, which is what\nissue #326 reports colliding with a concurrent git.\n\nCaveat found by CI, not locally: path handling around this must not assume\nUnix. `strings.HasPrefix(path, \"/\")` is true for every absolute path a\nmacOS/Linux test can build and false for every absolute path on Windows —\nsee [[verification-harness-false-pass]].\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false,"memdirStamped":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6b428fb8-e0b8-49c8-8a78-06d28307bc92","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
