{"parentUuid":"c8b99586-3e78-4c58-b31a-0afab70b1b0d","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14396923 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"6cab6413-d2b4-4592-894f-068324e9f70d","timestamp":"2026-10-03T04:16:58.331Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14396923 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"6cab6413-d2b4-4592-894f-068324e9f70d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cfef6YnXAXqzWUHxSQ6mT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The CI poller is running in the background. Here's the complete picture while it finishes.\n\n## The plan is done\n\nAll three PRs are open, stacked, with the Windows fix pushed. **Nothing merged.**\n\n| PR | Scope |\n|---|---|\n| [#329](https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/329) | MCP budget, #325 latency, four silent-failure sites, truncated messages |\n| [#330](https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/330) | #326, #327, #328, #322, #324 |\n| [#331](https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/331) | Guide directive, #323, hook wiring, 23 tool descriptions, README |\n\nPlus the **[docs artifact](https://claude.ai/code/artifact/6124d687-c2e5-4fdb-b2ee-4c125cbe8a6d)**.\n\n## CI found a real bug my local suite could not\n\nThree of my new tests failed on `windows-latest` while everything passed locally. Not a test-environment quirk — `relativiseToRepo` checked `strings.HasPrefix(path, \"/\")`, which is true for every absolute path a macOS or Linux test can construct and **false for every absolute path on Windows**. Ignore matching was silently disabled there, which is the over-reporting mirror of the bug the PR exists to fix. Now handles drive letters and UNC, folds case where the filesystem does, and the guard is a table that runs the Windows forms on every platform.\n\n## The usage experiment — and its limitation\n\nObjective log from a PATH shim, four agents, identical task:\n\n| arm | first tool call |\n|---|---|\n| new-1 | `graph search` |\n| new-2 | `graph search` |\n| old-1 | `brain brief` → then `graph query` |\n| old-2 | `brain brief` |\n\n**The design doesn't test what the plan asked.** I put the guide text in each agent's prompt, so I measured \"does this wording work when forced into context\" — not \"does the guide file get read and followed\". Both arms used the tools, so this cannot reproduce the 0.34% baseline. I can't fix that with subagents, because their project context comes from *my* launch directory, not the worktree they're pointed at.\n\nWhat it did show: the new wording moved the first action to `graph search` in both cases, and the old guide's agent ran `entire graph query` — **the command that doesn't exist in released 0.4.0**. Live evidence for #323.\n\nThe more useful finding is negative, and it's about quality, not usage. In **three of four** runs the agent used the tool as instructed and it failed to find the answer:\n\n> *\"The graph search's top hit was the brief-side check, not the real decider. I found `semanticStaleReport` by grep.\"*\n> *\"The graph hit was a decoy, so I went to grep.\"*\n> *\"The brief only returned loosely related symbols… so I switched to grep.\"*\n\nFixing the guide makes agents reach for the tool. On this task, reaching for it didn't pay — grep did. That's worth knowing before concluding the wording fix is sufficient.\n\nI'll report the final CI result when the poller returns."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1034,"cache_read_input_tokens":448773,"output_tokens":1031,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1034,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1031,"cache_read_input_tokens":448773,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1034,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1034},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"ee6fb731-eb53-4b94-8bf8-13e083b0b751","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId"