{"parentUuid":"e1a52128-f547-4c99-9d6e-f39eff323442","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfegNxd3YC1swkeAcJTpK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013tGUjkUTWL8efhhrQ1ct5o","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-safety\ngit add -A && git commit -q -m \"fix(scratch-index): copy the index's mtime, not just its bytes\n\ngit decides whether a cached stat entry is trustworthy by comparing the file's\nrecorded mtime against THE INDEX FILE'S OWN mtime. An entry whose file changed\nin the same moment the index was written is racily clean, and git re-reads its\ncontent rather than believing the cache.\n\nA freshly written copy has a newer mtime than every tracked file, so every\nentry looks safely older than the index, git trusts the stat cache, and a\nsame-moment edit -- especially one that does not change the file's size -- is\nreported as UNCHANGED. Silently losing a worktree edit is worse than the lock\ncontention the scratch index exists to avoid.\n\nCaught by TestWorktreeFingerprintDoesNotRunRepoLocalDiffExternal on CI after\nthe full suite passed locally: its fixture overwrites a 12-byte file with 12\ndifferent bytes immediately after committing it, which is exactly the racy\nwindow.\n\nThe new guard asserts the MECHANISM (the copy carries the original's mtime)\nrather than the symptom. A first attempt at a symptom test passed with AND\nwithout the fix on this machine -- the race needs a file whose mtime equals the\none git add recorded, which is not portably forceable -- so it was replaced\nrather than shipped as protection that does not protect. The symptom stays\ncovered by the hardening test that caught it.\"\ngit push -q -f 2>&1|tail -2; echo \"PR2: $(git rev-parse --short HEAD)\"\ncd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide && git fetch -q origin && git rebase origin/fix/multiagent-safety-indexing-windows 2>&1|tail -2 && go build ./... 2>&1|head -2 && git push -q -f