{"parentUuid":"21002551-0ef1-4962-8973-6870e73157da","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14371207 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"aac5a985-1843-4b99-8b79-5e3aa5c54e09","timestamp":"2026-10-03T04:44:15.266Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14371207 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"aac5a985-1843-4b99-8b79-5e3aa5c54e09","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfehBDhgRqrWSXMa8cJnv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"CI is re-running in the background. The second CI round found a bug worth reporting on its own.\n\n## CI caught something my local suite structurally could not\n\nThe `test-cgo` failure was **not** a flake. `gitDiffBinary` returned empty — my scratch-index fix was silently losing worktree edits.\n\nThe cause is subtle: git decides whether a cached stat entry is trustworthy by comparing a file's recorded mtime against **the index file's own mtime**. A file changed in the same moment the index was written is \"racily clean\", and git re-reads it rather than trusting the cache. My copy had a *fresh* mtime, so every tracked file looked safely older, git trusted the stale cache, and a same-size edit came back as unchanged.\n\nThat's worse than the lock contention the change exists to fix. Now the copy carries the original's mtime.\n\nWhat caught it was a **pre-existing hardening test** whose fixture overwrites a 12-byte file with 12 different bytes immediately after committing — exactly the racy window. My own tests sailed past it.\n\n## I wrote a test that wasn't a guard, and threw it away\n\nMy first attempt reproduced the scenario directly. It passed. Then I weakened the fix and **it still passed** — it protected nothing. I tried forcing the race by setting mtimes; still didn't fire, because the stat cache invalidates on any mtime mismatch, and the true racy state needs the file's mtime to equal the one `git add` recorded, which isn't portably forceable.\n\nSo I deleted it rather than ship protection that doesn't protect, and replaced it with a guard on the **mechanism** — the copy carries the original's mtime — which does fail when the fix is removed:\n\n> `scratch index mtime is 2026-10-03 00:29:24…, want the original's 2026-10-02 22:29:24…; git would trust a stale stat cache`\n\nThe symptom stays covered by the hardening test that actually caught it, and the comment says so.\n\n## Earlier in the same round\n\nThe Windows failures were also real, not environmental: `relativiseToRepo` tested `HasPrefix(path, \"/\")` — true for every absolute path a macOS or Linux test can build, false for every absolute path on Windows. Ignore matching was silently off there.\n\nBoth bugs share a shape worth noting: **a local suite that cannot construct the failing input will always be green.** I've saved that as a memory alongside the three times my own verification harness false-passed this session.\n\nI'll report the final CI state when the poller returns. Nothing is merged."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":659,"cache_read_input_tokens":474736,"output_tokens":821,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":659,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":821,"cache_read_input_tokens":474736,"cache_creation_input_tokens":659,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":659},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"f19a9672-ca83-4df3-9029-ee9dc1ab08f9","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfehBCGMm4EqDh9GR5UUc","type":"assistant","uuid":"eca33cfb-b1ea-4920-83cb-bc5ddfb898f2","timestamp":"2026-10-03T04:44:31.000Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0