{"parentUuid":"8c695465-c98e-4337-a633-f84c8daa062a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfehGv2UeJTpT7mSruknM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016tMEFK6u6J7VPzeZQ6JQ6o","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv\ncat >> GRAPH-FEEDBACK.md <<'EOF'\n\n---\n\n## Measured 2026-10-03: the tool got used and returned a decoy\n\nFour Claude subagents, same read-only locate task against entire-brain, same prompt;\nthe only difference was the agent-guide wording. Tool calls logged by a PATH shim,\nnot self-reported.\n\nTask: \"how does this codebase decide whether the semantic index needs rebuilding,\nwhat calls that, and which condition changed recently\".\n\n| arm | first tool call |\n|---|---|\n| directive guide x2 | `entire graph search` (both) |\n| permissive guide x2 | `entire brain brief` (both); one then ran `entire graph query` |\n\nUsage is not the interesting part — the guide text moves it, as expected. **The quality is.**\nIn three of the four runs the agent used the tool as instructed and then abandoned it:\n\n- \"The graph search's top hit was the brief-side check, not the real decider.\n  I found `semanticStaleReport` by grep.\"\n- \"The graph hit was a decoy, so I went to grep, `sed` and `git log -L`.\"\n- (brain) \"the brief only returned loosely related symbols\n  (`distillCommandOptions`, `semanticSourceManifest`, `selectedSession`), so I switched to grep.\"\n\nThe decoy is the same one twice: `brainBriefSemanticNeedsCurrentBoundary`\n(brain_brief_semantic_freshness.go:19). It ranks first for \"decide whether the semantic\nindex needs rebuilding\" and is not that decision — it gates overfetch inside the brief.\nThe real answers (`semanticStaleReport` semantic.go:3007, `semanticIndexAlreadyCurrent`\nsemantic.go:408) were found by grep in every case.\n\nBoth plausible answers sit in the same file as the decoy's caller, so this is not a\nrecall failure — the symbols were indexed. It is a ranking failure on a question phrased\nas intent rather than as a name. That is exactly the query shape the `--profile full`\npitch is aimed at.\n\n**The useful signal for graph:** winning the first call is now the easy half. An agent that\ncomplies once, gets a decoy, and falls back to grep has learned the tool does not pay —\nand it will not comply twice. Ranking on intent-phrased queries is worth more than any\nfurther wording change.\n\nCaveat on the usage half, stated plainly: the guide text was injected into each agent's\nPROMPT, not read from `.entire/agent-guide.md`. So this measures whether the wording works\nonce in context, not whether the file gets read. It cannot reproduce the 0.34% baseline and\nshould not be quoted as if it did. n=2 per arm.\nEOF\necho \"appended; still untracked:\"; git status --short GRAPH-FEEDBACK.md","description":"Record the experiment finding for graph","timeout":600000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1635,"cache_read_input_tokens":484660,"output_tokens":1044,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1635,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1044,"cache_read_input_tokens":484660,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1635,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1635},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_016tMEFK6u6J7VPzeZQ6JQ6o":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv\ncat >> GRAPH-FEEDBACK.md <<'EOF'\n\n---\n\n## Measured 2026-10-03: the tool got used and returned a decoy\n\nFour Claude subagents, same read-only locat