{"parentUuid":"60d5483b-5bc1-4834-80a3-72cd7649c9c6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfehLkpCbXsJW3juT4xrT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Progressing cleanly. Meanwhile — I amended both PRs *after* writing their descriptions, so the Windows and mtime fixes aren't mentioned. Let me correct that:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":552,"cache_read_input_tokens":488562,"output_tokens":998,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":264},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":552,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":998,"cache_read_input_tokens":488562,"cache_creation_input_tokens":552,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":552},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"2c3a639c-acc4-4027-8d8c-d007ad494055","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfehLkKvb8dBTh29MPxn6","type":"assistant","uuid":"08795173-856e-4cfa-ba32-2eb55ec721ed","timestamp":"2026-10-03T04:46:32.678Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-retrieval","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"08795173-856e-4cfa-ba32-2eb55ec721ed","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfehLkpCbXsJW3juT4xrT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PHFBqiWEKfr1GS8ngNsVB4","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-retrieval\ngh pr view 329 --repo entireio/entire-brain --json body --jq .body > /Users/suhaan/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp/pr329.md 2>/dev/null\ncat >> /Users/suhaan/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp/pr329.md <<'EOF'\n\n---\n\n## Added after the first CI run: a Windows bug my local suite could not catch\n\nThree of the new brainignore tests failed on `windows-latest` while everything passed locally. Not an environment quirk — `relativiseToRepo` tested `strings.HasPrefix(token, \"/\")`, which is true for every absolute path a macOS or Linux test can construct and **false for every absolute path on Windows**. Ignore matching was silently disabled there, so provider warnings naming ignored files were never withheld: the over-reporting mirror of the bug this PR fixes.\n\nNow recognises drive letters and UNC paths, and folds case on Windows and macOS where the filesystem does — staying case-sensitive elsewhere, since folding on Linux would match a different file.\n\nThe replacement guard is a table over the Windows forms that runs on **every** platform, so a Unix-only test can no longer miss it. Verified by weakening: restoring the `\"/\"`-only check fails it with `absolutePathToken(\"C:/Users/dev/repo/x.go\") = false, want true`.\nEOF\ngh pr edit 329 --repo entireio/entire-brain --body-file /Users/suhaan/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp/pr329.md 2>&1 | tail -1","description":"Update PR1 description with the Windows fix","timeout":900000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":552,"cache_read_input_tokens":488562,"output_tokens":998,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":264},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":552,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":998,"cache_read_input_tokens":488562,"cache_creation_input_tokens":552,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":552},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01PHFBqiWEKfr1GS8ngNsVB4":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-retrieval\ngh pr view 329 --repo entireio/entire-brain --json body --jq .body > /Users/suhaan/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp/pr329.md 2>/dev/null\ncat >> /Users/suhaan/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp/pr329.md <<'EOF'\n\n---\n\n## Added after the first CI run: a Windows bug my local suite could not catch\n\nThree of the new brainignore tests failed on `windows-latest` while everything passed locally. Not an environment quirk — `relativiseToRepo` tested `strings.HasPrefix(token, \"/\")`, which is true for every absolute path a macOS or Linux test can construct and **false for every absolute path on Windows**. Ignore matching was silently disabled there, so provider warnings naming ignored files were never withheld: the over-reporting mirror of the bug this PR fixes.\n\nNow recognises drive letters and UNC paths, and folds case on Windows and macOS where the filesystem does — staying case-sensitive elsewhere, since folding on Linux would match a different file.\n\nThe replacement guard is a table over the Windows forms that runs on **every** platform, so a Unix-only test can no longer miss it. Verified by weakening: restoring the `\"/\"`-only check fails it with `absolutePathToken(\"C:/Users/dev/repo/x.go\") = false, want true`.\nEOF\ngh pr edit 329 --repo entireio/entire-brain --body-file /Users/suhaan/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp/pr329.md 2>&1 | tail -1","description":"Update PR1 description with the Windows fix","timeout":900000}},"serverClassifierRequest":"2c3a639c-acc4-4027-8d8c-d007ad494055","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CfehLkKvb8dBTh29MPxn6","type":"assistant","uuid":"5dbeaaaf-8a03-49ee-8429-4ad225e667d5","timestamp":"2026-10-03T04:46:39.582Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-retrieval","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
