{"parentUuid":"f393962c-0889-46f0-9e7d-399aa1552829","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14989691 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"4a3b96e9-6414-4c9a-b2b6-44ee0469f4e0","timestamp":"2026-10-03T13:17:08.411Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14989691 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"4a3b96e9-6414-4c9a-b2b6-44ee0469f4e0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CffNHdqDe9HQ8R8ztaVKU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Measured against `origin/main`'s README (362 lines, 15,730 chars). The README shows **34 command forms**; the binary exposes **126**.\n\n## Coverage\n\n| | total | in README | missing |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Top-level commands | 42 | 27 | **15** |\n| Subcommands | 84 | 11 | **73** |\n| MCP tools (`brain_*`) | 37 | 0 named | **37** |\n\n## Top-level commands with zero mentions\n\n`distill` · `doctor` · `watch` · `stats` · `bundle` · `config` · `gc` · `reset` · `repair` · `patterns` · `entities` · `show` · `multi-get` · `bench` · `version`\n\nFour of those matter more than the rest:\n\n- **`distill`** — the command that extracts durable facts from sessions. It needs an agent, sends transcripts to a model provider, costs money, and can run for hours. It is the mechanism behind \"durable facts\" and appears nowhere.\n- **`doctor`** — the diagnostic you'd want when any of this misbehaves.\n- **`watch`** — the README describes \"a watcher\" five times as a thing setup installs, but never shows the command, so you can't run, inspect, or tune it.\n- **`reset` / `gc`** — the only ways to undo or prune. A user whose brain goes wrong has no documented recovery.\n\n## Subcommand families, entirely undocumented\n\n| parent | missing | notable |\n|---|---|---|\n| `facts` | 14 of 16 | `sync`, `promote`, `review`, `proposals`, `tree`, `map`, `outline`, `files`, `eval*` |\n| `inspect` | 11 | `blame`, `regressions`, `boundaries`, `tests`, `trace-path`, `search-graph`, `snippet` |\n| `memory` | 11 | `configure`, `jobs`, `rebuild`, `reconcile`, `abstract`, `retry` |\n| `workspace` | 10 of 11 | `create`, `add`, `review`, `patterns`, `watch` |\n| `privacy` | 6 | `exclude`, `include`, `retention`, `purge`, `verify` — the whole retention-control surface |\n| `refresh` | 5 | `index`, `seed`, `sessions`, `history`, `delta` |\n| `patterns` | 4 | `refresh`, `skills`, `verify`, `status` |\n| `entities` | 4 | `history`, `show`, `backfill`, `migrate` |\n| `config` | 3 | `init`, `show`, `path` |\n| `bundle` | 2 | `import`, `export` |\n\n`privacy` is the one I'd raise first on principle: six subcommands governing what the brain retains from your sessions, none documented.\n\n## Non-command surface also absent\n\n- **All 37 MCP tools.** The README mentions MCP generically eight times and shows `entire brain mcp --print-config`, but never names a single tool — so a reader can't tell what an agent actually gets.\n- **`hook pre-edit` / `hook post-failure`** — zero mentions. (These are the ones PR [#331](https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/331) wires up; they've shipped since PR #24 with nothing invoking them.)\n- **`--strict` guidance mode** — zero mentions, though it changes the agent guide substantially.\n- **No-egress mode** — zero mentions, despite being the control that keeps content local.\n\n## One caveat on the method\n\nThis counts *mentions*, not quality of documentation — a command named once in a code block counts as present. And `config` is mentioned seven times as a word but never as a command, which my regex scored as \"missing\"; I'd call that correct, but it's a judgement call. PR #331 moves the \"What to ask\" table and fixes its verbs but does **not** add any of the above, so this gap survives the stack as it stands."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1315,"cache_read_input_tokens":507105,"output_tokens":1288,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1315,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1288,"cache_read_input_tokens":507105,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1315,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1315},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"8285fd39-b12a-44df-a261-482c8002b9b4","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CffNHcMfCjFCwK6HY8Re1","type":"assistant","uuid":"5ba268ab-c682-4a86-aacb-98227b377d59","timestamp":"2026-10-03T13:17:25.906Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
