{"parentUuid":"9dbd1209-7574-4470-8627-2aade58b2167","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CffNRA9J9cGeygKw48wQk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Checked and up to date. Three things confirmed:\n\n1. **`origin/main` hasn't moved** — still `f423963d`, README byte-identical to what I diffed. My earlier numbers were already against current main.\n2. **The latest README is PR #331's**, at 378 lines (+16 over main).\n3. **Rebuilt the binary from the stack tip** (`4f4e4bf6`) — command surface is byte-identical to my earlier enumeration: 42 top-level, 84 subcommands, 126 paths.\n\n## The coverage numbers are unchanged\n\n| README | documented | missing |\n|---|---|---|\n| `origin/main` (362 ln) | 38 / 126 | 15 top-level + 73 subcommands |\n| **PR #331 tip (378 ln)** | **38 / 126** | **15 top-level + 73 subcommands** |\n\nNewly documented by #331: **none**. Newly missing: **none**.\n\nSo every command in the list I gave you is still absent from the newest README — `distill`, `doctor`, `watch`, `stats`, `bundle`, `config`, `gc`, `reset`, `repair`, `patterns`, `entities`, `show`, `multi-get`, `bench`, `version`, plus all 37 MCP tools, `hook pre-edit`/`post-failure`, `--strict`, and no-egress mode.\n\n## Worth saying plainly about my own PR\n\nPR #331's README work added 16 lines and **closed zero of the gap**. What it actually did:\n\n- moved the \"What to ask\" table from line 145 to line 11\n- dropped its Brain-command column (per the reviewer feedback)\n- added the branch-scoping warning for `recall`\n- added a paragraph distinguishing `query`/`search`/`vsearch` (prose) from `recall` (facts)\n- fixed the decision example, which had been pointing at `query`\n\nAll useful, all about *correctness* of what was already there. None of it documents a new command. I checked specifically whether dropping the command column removed any unique reference — it didn't, so coverage held flat rather than regressing.\n\nIf you want that gap closed, it's a separate piece of work, and the honest framing is a reference section rather than more prose: 88 of 126 command paths have no documentation anywhere in the README. I'd start with `privacy` (six subcommands governing session retention), `distill` (costs money, sends transcripts to a provider), and `reset`/`gc` (the only recovery paths) — those three are the ones where absence has consequences rather than just inconvenience."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2495,"cache_read_input_tokens":513150,"output_tokens":831,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2495,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":831,"cache_read_input_tokens":513150,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2495,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2495},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"cfcc6706-b066-46b2-9187-0dd6d57418a7","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CffNR9AGnuDQVK9dbbWpD","type":"assistant","uuid":"004babe6-47fc-4155-b568-fce155009ac4","timestamp":"2026-10-03T13:19:03.473Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
