{"parentUuid":"317e29ff-7c39-465d-98ff-4d521353a45b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CffPTUy4fe5uHKT43YpLt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1384,"cache_read_input_tokens":517449,"output_tokens":2954,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":514},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1384,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2954,"cache_read_input_tokens":517449,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1384,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1384},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":6659,"serverClassifierRequest":"28e72153-82a8-40c2-9773-a4f93364a47f","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CffPTUGPGZRr5DwMbj5Lu","type":"assistant","uuid":"86cfc74b-a726-40af-bd08-25bf4ebc9880","timestamp":"2026-10-03T13:32:38.975Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"86cfc74b-a726-40af-bd08-25bf4ebc9880","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CffPTUy4fe5uHKT43YpLt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here's the full accounting. Two of the seven filed issues are **partial**, and their titles ask for more than I delivered — that's the most important thing to know before you review.\n\n## The seven filed issues\n\n| # | Reporter | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| 325 | leine4550 | ✅ fixed, measured |\n| 326 | peyton-alt | ✅ fixed |\n| 323 | leine4550 | ✅ fixed |\n| 324 | leine4550 | ✅ fixed |\n| 322 | leine4550 | ✅ fixed — **not run on Windows** |\n| 327 | peyton-alt | ⚠️ **partial** |\n| 328 | peyton-alt | ⚠️ **partial** |\n\n### ⚠️ #327 — \"keeps indexing new commits while the worktree has uncommitted changes\"\n\n**What I fixed:** a self-inflicted stall. A dirty tree forced a rebuild, the indexer *refused* that rebuild, and a failed refresh aborted the whole watch tick so the cursor never advanced. Nothing progressed at all while the tree stayed dirty. Dirtiness now doesn't force a rebuild it can't perform, and the refusal no longer aborts the tick.\n\n**What I did not fix:** `semantic.go:575` still reads\n\n```go\nif dirty && !indexOpts.worktree {\n    return errors.New(dirtyWorktreeErrorCode + \": refusing to index uncommitted content without --worktree\")\n}\n```\n\nSo when you make a **new commit** with a dirty worktree, the semantic index still refuses to advance to it. The title's literal ask — keep indexing new commits while uncommitted changes exist — needs indexing HEAD via a temp tree, which I didn't build. The watcher no longer wedges, but the index stays behind.\n\n### ⚠️ #328 — \"can use Ollama on another machine **and** picks Ollama automatically\"\n\nTwo asks. I did the second, not the first.\n\n**Fixed:** `defaultRefreshAgent` tried codex → claude → none, with ollama absent entirely. Someone who installed a local model to keep transcripts off a third party got no distillation, or — if a cloud CLI happened to be present — their sessions sent to that provider. ollama is now tried first. `watch` hardcoded `codex`, worse because it runs unattended; now auto-detects.\n\n**Not done:** a non-loopback `ENTIRE_BRAIN_OLLAMA_URL` is still rejected. The loopback restriction is a deliberate privacy boundary with a redirect guard behind it, so opening it is a product decision rather than a bug fix. Say the word and I'll add an opt-in flag.\n\nAlso worth flagging: the issue says the rejection is *silent*. It isn't — it's a hard error naming the URL. That premise was wrong.\n\n### The four clean ones\n\n**#325** — `status --json` ran `git for-each-ref --contains` per anchor commit, a full history walk, on every call once facts existed. Gated behind the existing `--details`. **24.19s → 2.42s** on the real 961-fact brain.\n\n**#326** — `brain brief` took `.git/index.lock`. `--no-optional-locks` turned out *not* to be enough: a porcelain `git diff <commit>` does its own index refresh the flag doesn't gate. The fix points `GIT_INDEX_FILE` at a copy — lock-free and byte-identical to porcelain, where switching to plumbing would have changed the answer.\n\n**#323** — the generated guide recommended `entire graph query`, absent from released v0.4.0. It worked here only because the installed binary is a symlink to a dev checkout. Now emits `search`, correct on both.\n\n**#324** — `facts promote --keep-both` emitted `Confidence: 0` as a literal with no similarity ever computed, one proposal per *pair*. Now computed, with a spanning set (n−1 edges, not n(n−1)/2), capped relative to the auto-apply threshold so it can never become auto-applyable.\n\n**#322** — a 7,516-byte system prompt on argv against cmd.exe's 8,191 limit. Moved off argv at the shared builder. Tests are platform-independent, but **a real Windows run is still needed** to close it.\n\n## Problems fixed that nobody filed\n\nThese came from the transcripts and a sweep, not the issue tracker:\n\n| Problem | Why it mattered |\n|---|---|\n| **MCP tools returned results no client accepts** | `brain_status`, `brain_brief`, `brain_impact` all errored. The budget was sized to the 4 MiB transport frame, not the context window — 128 KiB of this JSON is ~52k tokens, double a client's ceiling. A context-saving tool that overflows context is worse than no tool. |\n| **`FilterWarnings` discarded every index warning** | It matched `.brainignore` patterns against free prose by substring. This repo's line 1 is `entire-brain`, a substring of every absolute path under it — so status reported a clean index that had silently missed files. |\n| **Guide told agents not to use the tools** | And CI enforced it: the test *banned* `\"FIRST action\"`/`\"SEARCH FIRST\"` and *required* `\"sufficient locations\"`. Measured cost: 332 graph calls against 96,987 exploration calls. |\n| **`hook pre-edit` shipped and was never called** | Since PR #24. The only push path in an otherwise pull-only product. |\n| **37 MCP tools, none saying when to use them instead of grep** | The description is what an agent reads when choosing. |\n| **regression / export / distill dropped work silently** | A capped scan printed \"No suspected regressions\"; export counted the *filtered* warning set; distill's 50-entry cap ran *before* persisting, so warning 51 existed nowhere. |\n| **Three status messages cut mid-word** | A 140-**byte** width on a rune string. One was reported as a typo. |\n\n## Two bugs I introduced, and CI caught\n\nWorth knowing because they say something about the test suite:\n\n- **Unix-only path check** — `HasPrefix(path, \"/\")` is true for every absolute path a macOS or Linux test can build and false for every absolute path on Windows. Ignore matching was silently off there.\n- **Scratch index lost worktree edits** — copying the index gave it a fresh mtime, which breaks git's racily-clean detection, so a same-size edit read as unchanged. Worse than the lock problem it fixed. Caught by a *pre-existing* hardening test; all of mine sailed past.\n\n## Which PR holds what\n\n- **[#329](https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/329)** — MCP budget, #325, the four silent-failure sites, truncated messages, Windows path fix\n- **[#330](https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/330)** — #326, #327 (partial), #328 (partial), #322, #324, scratch-index mtime fix\n- **[#331](https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/331)** — guide directive, #323, hook wiring, tool descriptions, README\n\nAll three: 30 checks green, agent review found nothing blocking, only Approvals red. Every fix has a regression test verified by weakening — guard patched compile-clean, test shown red, assertion recorded."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1384,"cache_read_input_tokens":517449,"output_tokens":2954,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":514},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1384,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2954,"cache_read_input_tokens":517449,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1384,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1384},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"28e72153-82a8-40c2-9773-a4f93364a47f","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CffPTUGPGZRr5DwMbj5Lu","type":"assistant","uuid":"7a566ae1-b56e-442b-a41a-90f6c7dc553f","timestamp":"2026-10-03T13:33:08.141Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
