{"parentUuid":"b06b2b2d-8798-4180-a925-081bee7ca0ad","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CffQMizMxoG2jRtxk6fwq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1737,"cache_read_input_tokens":521836,"output_tokens":1890,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":401},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1737,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1890,"cache_read_input_tokens":521836,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1737,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1737},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":5031,"serverClassifierRequest":"934a2a1d-469c-48f4-b051-281fd0dbc4ad","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CffQMiYqCKA1LC3sVrUUx","type":"assistant","uuid":"942a391a-7613-4752-97c2-44824102b29e","timestamp":"2026-10-03T13:44:24.608Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"942a391a-7613-4752-97c2-44824102b29e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CffQMizMxoG2jRtxk6fwq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Good — the PR doesn't claim it. Its verification section only claims the guards are weakening-verified, and attributes the 0.34% to graph's own measurement. So nothing durable overclaims. But to your question:\n\n## I did not verify that usage will increase\n\nWhat I ran was four subagents, two per arm, same task, with tool calls logged objectively by a PATH shim:\n\n| arm | first tool call |\n|---|---|\n| directive guide ×2 | `entire graph search` |\n| permissive guide ×2 | `entire brain brief` |\n\nFour reasons that doesn't support the claim:\n\n**1. The confound that invalidates it.** I put the guide text **into each agent's prompt**, not into `.entire/agent-guide.md`. The real-world failure is that the guide *file* doesn't get read or followed. I tested whether the wording works when it's already in context — which is the one condition that was never in doubt. I couldn't test the file path because a subagent's project context comes from *my* launch directory, not the worktree I point it at.\n\n**2. No headroom.** Both arms used the tools 100% of the time. If the baseline is 0.34%, an experiment where the control arm scores 100% isn't measuring the same thing. What differed was *which* tool went first, not *whether* one was used.\n\n**3. n=2 per arm.** By my own benchmark notes the minimum detectable effect is ~25 points at n=30. At n=2 there is no inference to make. One task, one repo, one model.\n\n**4. Favourable task selection.** I gave them a pure locate-and-explain task — the case the tool is designed for. That's the most generous possible setting.\n\n## What the causal evidence actually is\n\nTwo things, neither controlled:\n\n- **An association.** 332 graph calls against 96,987 exploration calls, graph-first rate 0, measured *after* the permissive wording shipped. Nobody measured before. I phrased it as \"measured afterwards\" in the PR, which is accurate, but it is not a before/after.\n- **A self-report.** A Claude session in the transcript said: *\"The agent guide says to start substantive tasks with `entire brain brief` and use Graph for code discovery. I skipped that.\"* Strong as a mechanism hint, worthless as a rate.\n\nWhat I *can* claim with confidence is narrower and all structural: the guide said the opposite of what was intended, CI enforced that in both directions, `combinedWorkflow` carried no Graph obligation at all, and the command it named doesn't exist in the released version. Those are facts about the text, verified by weakening. Whether fixing them moves behaviour is a separate question I didn't answer.\n\n## And I found counter-evidence\n\nThis is the part I'd weight most heavily. In **three of four** runs the agent used the tool as instructed and it failed:\n\n> *\"The graph search's top hit was the brief-side check, not the real decider. I found `semanticStaleReport` by grep.\"*\n> *\"The graph hit was a decoy, so I went to grep.\"*\n> *\"The brief only returned loosely related symbols… so I switched to grep.\"*\n\nSame decoy twice — `brainBriefSemanticNeedsCurrentBoundary` ranks first for \"decide whether the semantic index needs rebuilding\" and is not that decision. Grep found the real answer every time.\n\nSo even granting that the directive wins the first call, an agent that complies, gets a decoy, and succeeds with grep has learned the tool doesn't pay. I'd expect compliance to decay. **Fixing the wording may raise first-call rate while leaving sustained usage flat** — and nothing I ran can distinguish those.\n\n## What would actually verify it\n\n1. Install the guide as a **file** via `init-agents` in a real repo — the condition that's actually broken.\n2. Run real sessions, not prompt-injected subagents, and read the graph-first rate from the same instrumentation that produced the 0.34% figure, so before and after are the same metric.\n3. **n ≥ 30 per arm**, mixed task types, including ones where the file is the only carrier of the instruction.\n4. Measure the hook arm separately, so you learn whether wording alone was enough or whether enforcement is doing the work.\n5. Track first-call rate *and* sustained rate across a session — that's where the decoy effect would show.\n\nI can set that up. It needs real sessions rather than subagents, so it's a slower and more expensive run than what I did — worth saying before you authorise it. Until then the honest status of PR #331 is: it removes a text defect that plausibly suppressed usage, with the effect size unmeasured."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1737,"cache_read_input_tokens":521836,"output_tokens":1890,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":401},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1737,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1890,"cache_read_input_tokens":521836,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1737,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1737},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"934a2a1d-469c-48f4-b051-281fd0dbc4ad","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CffQMiYqCKA1LC3sVrUUx","type":"assistant","uuid":"ae7a310e-460a-4a67-b63e-a8845ac575e5","timestamp":"2026-10-03T13:44:44.725Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d19