{"parentUuid":"3eccce8e-de6f-44e9-8f32-5f342370ae75","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PreToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_018rgVnqGzVqLwX2JhBHncbR","hookEvent":"PreToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"hookSpecificOutput\":{\"hookEventName\":\"PreToolUse\",\"permissionDecisionReason\":\"RTK auto-rewrite\",\"updatedInput\":{\"command\":\"sed -n '1,20p' /Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/dynamic-petting-globe.md; echo \\\"...\\\"; rtk wc -l /Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/dynamic-petting-globe.md\",\"timeout\":600000,\"description\":\"Read the existing plan's framing\"}}}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"rtk hook claude","durationMs":16},"type":"attachment","uuid":"4145a25b-5eb9-4a12-a74c-ab2a918e06f2","timestamp":"2026-10-03T13:48:13.882Z","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"3eccce8e-de6f-44e9-8f32-5f342370ae75","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"fc0e85dc-8585-4b18-a360-2e0091ce935d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018rgVnqGzVqLwX2JhBHncbR","type":"tool_result","content":"# Brain + Graph v1 readiness\n\n## Context\n\nThree streams of evidence converged this week:\n\n1. **A user install report (Joseph)** — distill stalled at 75/237; `AGENTS.md`/`CLAUDE.md` never\n   appeared at repo level; doc ambiguity about where to run setup.\n2. **Seven issues filed 2026-10-02** by two external testers (leine4550, peyton-alt).\n3. **Two full agent transcripts** (Claude Code and Codex, same prompts, same repo) showing agents\n   not using Brain or Graph.\n\nInvestigation of all three found that the headline problem is **not** that agents are habitual.\nThree distinct, verified causes sit underneath it, and all are fixable.\n\n**Already fixed and merged:** #316 (semantic memo on the wrong path, unbounded, unlinearized),\n#317 (ollama envelope cap measuring the prompt, silent truncation, probe on an exhausted budget,\nusage-accounting bypass, misleading flag help). **Open and green:** #306, #318, #320, #321.\n\nThis plan covers what is *not* taken care of.\n...\n299","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"38c361be-297a-4e7f-82bc-cc31fd3f2d76","timestamp":"2026-10-03T13:48:16.416Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"# Brain + Graph v1 readiness\n\n## Context\n\nThree streams of evidence converged this week:\n\n1. **A user install report (Joseph)** — distill stalled at 75/237; `AGENTS.md`/`CLAUDE.md` never\n   appeared at repo level; doc ambiguity about where to run setup.\n2. **Seven issues filed 2026-10-02** by two external testers (leine4550, peyton-alt).\n3. **Two full agent transcripts** (Claude Code and Codex, same prompts, same repo) showing agents\n   not using Brain or Graph.\n\nInvestigation of all three found that the headline problem is **not** that agents are habitual.\nThree distinct, verified causes sit underneath it, and all are fixable.\n\n**Already fixed and merged:** #316 (semantic memo on the wrong path, unbounded, unlinearized),\n#317 (ollama envelope cap measuring the prompt, silent truncation, probe on an exhausted budget,\nusage-accounting bypass, misleading flag help). **Open and green:** #306, #318, #320, #321.\n\nThis plan covers what is *not* taken care of.\n...\n299","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"classifierBoundary":true,"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"c073ba73-354e-44da-960e-4795c377aa05","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","root":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","branch":"fix/agent-guide-directive-and-discovery","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"entireio","host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"},{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-graph","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3eccce8e-de6f-44e9-8f32-5f342370ae75","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"38c361be-297a-4e7f-82bc-cc31fd3f2d76","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14990371 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"9882a9a4-a629-4d33-97db-51c34f8cb45e","timestamp":"2026-10-03T13:48:16.430Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14990371 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"9882a9a4-a629-4d33-97db-51c34f8cb45e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CffQfMnuqqJpHxzVQoyw9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012GML4vShesDRHtqHJ6LzWF","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Explore guide delivery mechanics","prompt":"Read-only exploration in /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide (entire-brain, branch fix/agent-guide-directive-and-discovery). Do NOT edit anything.\n\nQUESTION: in a CLEAN repository, what exactly has to happen for a coding agent to actually RECEIVE the Entire agent guide, and what can silently prevent it?\n\nTrace and report precisely:\n1. `entire brain init-agents` — every file it writes, the exact path of each, and the exact markers/wrappers it uses. Does it write AGENTS.md and CLAUDE.md at repo ROOT, or elsewhere? Does it create them if absent, or only patch existing ones?\n2. `entire brain setup` — does it write ANY of those files? (A user reported AGENTS.md/CLAUDE.md never appearing after setup. Confirm or refute from code.)\n3. What gates guide installation: does it require a built brain, a git repo, `.entire/settings.json` with enabled:true, a TTY, network, or an installed graph plugin? Name each gate and its file:line, and what happens when each fails (silent skip vs error).\n4. `agentsetup.Context`/`Preview`/`Install` — how is the repo root resolved, and what happens in a NESTED repo (a clone inside another repo)?\n5. Normal vs strict mode: where is the mode persisted, what is the DEFAULT when nothing is saved, and which guide text ships by default?\n6. Does anything write `.claude/settings.json`, and does `init-agents` emit any PreToolUse hook wiring? (Check internal/agentsetup/claudehooks.go if present.)\n\nThen answer the key empirical question: if someone runs `claude` (Claude Code CLI) with its working directory set to that clean repo, which of the written files would Claude Code load as project instructions, and would the guide text reach the model? Say what you can establish from the repo's own docs/tests and what you CANNOT establish from source alone.\n\nUse `entire graph search --repo . --profile full --query \"...\"` FIRST for locating code (this repo has a graph index), then read focused ranges. Use `rtk` for git.\n\nOUTPUT: caveman-ultra compressed. file:line for every claim. Separate \"ESTABLISHED\" from \"CANNOT ESTABLISH FROM SOURCE\". Max 400 words.","subagent_type":"Explore","model":"sonnet"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1838,"cache_read_input_tokens":529984,"output_tokens":2674,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1838,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2674,"cache_read_input_tokens":529984,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1838,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1838},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_012GML4vShesDRHtqHJ6LzWF":{"description":"Explore guide delivery mechanics","prompt":"Read-only exploration in /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide (entire-brain, branch fix/agent-guide-directive-and-discovery). Do NOT edit anything.\n\nQUESTION: in a CLEAN repository, what exactly has to happen for a coding agent to actually RECEIVE the Entire agent guide, and what can silently prevent it?\n\nTrace and report precisely:\n1. `entire brain init-agents` — every file it writes, the exact path of each, and the exact markers/wrappers it uses. Does it write AGENTS.md and CLAUDE.md at repo ROOT, or elsewhere? Does it create them if absent, or only patch existing ones?\n2. `entire brain setup` — does it write ANY of those files? (A user reported AGENTS.md/CLAUDE.md never appearing after setup. Confirm or refute from code.)\n3. What gates guide installation: does it require a built brain, a git repo, `.entire/settings.json` with enabled:true, a TTY, network, or an installed graph plugin? Name each gate and its file:line, and what happens when each fails (silent skip vs error).\n4. `agentsetup.Context`/`Preview`/`Install` — how is the repo root resolved, and what happens in a NESTED repo (a clone inside another repo)?\n5. Normal vs strict mode: where is the mode persisted, what is the DEFAULT when nothing is saved, and which guide text ships by default?\n6. Does anything write `.claude/settings.json`, and does `init-agents` emit any PreToolUse hook wiring? (Check internal/agentsetup/claudehooks.go if present.)\n\nThen answer the key empirical question: if someone runs `claude` (Claude Code CLI) with its working directory set to that clean repo, which of the written files would Claude Code load as project instructions, and would the guide text reach the model? Say what you can establish from the repo's own docs/tests and what you CANNOT establish from source alone.\n\nUse `entire graph search --repo . --profile full --query \"...\"` FIRST for locating code (this repo has a graph index), then read focused ranges. Use `rtk` for git.\n\nOUTPUT: caveman-ultra compressed. file:line for every claim. Separate \"ESTABLISHED\" from \"CANNOT ESTABLISH FROM SOURCE\". Max 400 words.","subagent_type":"Explore","model":"sonnet"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"ef1717a7-ef7c-44e4-9271-52f0313c5403","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CffQfJoKrWQJWVBHeFjoY","type":"assistant","uuid":"370501cd-f964-4393-b750-4b97d195274f","timestamp":"2026-10-03T13:48:31.528Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/User