{"parentUuid":"370501cd-f964-4393-b750-4b97d195274f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CffQfMnuqqJpHxzVQoyw9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BdAWayz87ZVRDAEEUrXcoW","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Explore graph MCP and ranking","prompt":"Read-only exploration. Do NOT edit anything. Two repos: /Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph (entire-graph) and /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide (entire-brain).\n\nAnswer two questions that decide whether agent tool-usage can be fixed at all.\n\n**Q1 — Does entire-graph ship an MCP server?**\nentire-brain exposes 37 `brain_*` MCP tools (internal/cli/mcp.go). Does entire-graph expose ANY MCP tools? Search its cmd/ and internal/ for an mcp server, stdio transport, tools/list handler. If none: confirm it by naming where such a server WOULD live and showing it is absent. This matters because a guide that says \"your FIRST action MUST be ONE Graph search\" names a shell command, and in an MCP-first harness the agent may only reach for MCP tools.\n\n**Q2 — Why did graph search rank a decoy first?**\nMeasured: for the query \"decide whether semantic index needs rebuilding\" against entire-brain, `entire graph search --repo . --profile full` returned `brainBriefSemanticNeedsCurrentBoundary` (internal/cli/brain_brief_semantic_freshness.go:19) as rank 1. That function is NOT the rebuild decision — it gates overfetch inside the brief. The real deciders are `semanticStaleReport` (internal/cli/semantic.go:3007) and `semanticIndexAlreadyCurrent` (internal/cli/semantic.go:408). Grep found both; graph did not rank either first.\n\nInvestigate the ranking path in entire-graph: internal/sem/search*.go and internal/cli/search*.go. Report:\n- how candidates are scored (the signal list and weights)\n- whether name/identifier matching dominates body/semantic matching\n- whether there is any known idf-over-preselected-sample problem (check comments and recent commits for \"idf\")\n- what `--profile full` changes versus the default\n- whether intent-phrased queries (a sentence describing behaviour) are handled differently from name-phrased queries\n\nDo NOT propose fixes. Just establish the mechanism with file:line evidence.\n\nUse `entire graph search` itself where helpful, plus focused reads. `rtk` for git/gh.\n\nOUTPUT: caveman-ultra compressed. file:line per claim. Clearly separate Q1 and Q2. State anything you could not determine. Max 400 words.","subagent_type":"Explore","model":"sonnet"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1838,"cache_read_input_tokens":529984,"output_tokens":2674,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1838,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2674,"cache_read_input_tokens":529984,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1838,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1838},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01BdAWayz87ZVRDAEEUrXcoW":{"description":"Explore graph MCP and ranking","prompt":"Read-only exploration. Do NOT edit anything. Two repos: /Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph (entire-graph) and /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide (entire-brain).\n\nAnswer two questions that decide whether agent tool-usage can be fixed at all.\n\n**Q1 — Does entire-graph ship an MCP server?**\nentire-brain exposes 37 `brain_*` MCP tools (internal/cli/mcp.go). Does entire-graph expose ANY MCP tools? Search its cmd/ and internal/ for an mcp server, stdio transport, tools/list handler. If none: confirm it by naming where such a server WOULD live and showing it is absent. This matters because a guide that says \"your FIRST action MUST be ONE Graph search\" names a shell command, and in an MCP-first harness the agent may only reach for MCP tools.\n\n**Q2 — Why did graph search rank a decoy first?**\nMeasured: for the query \"decide whether semantic index needs rebuilding\" against entire-brain, `entire graph search --repo . --profile full` returned `brainBriefSemanticNeedsCurrentBoundary` (internal/cli/brain_brief_semantic_freshness.go:19) as rank 1. That function is NOT the rebuild decision — it gates overfetch inside the brief. The real deciders are `semanticStaleReport` (internal/cli/semantic.go:3007) and `semanticIndexAlreadyCurrent` (internal/cli/semantic.go:408). Grep found both; graph did not rank either first.\n\nInvestigate the ranking path in entire-graph: internal/sem/search*.go and internal/cli/search*.go. Report:\n- how candidates are scored (the signal list and weights)\n- whether name/identifier matching dominates body/semantic matching\n- whether there is any known idf-over-preselected-sample problem (check comments and recent commits for \"idf\")\n- what `--profile full` changes versus the default\n- whether intent-phrased queries (a sentence describing behaviour) are handled differently from name-phrased queries\n\nDo NOT propose fixes. Just establish the mechanism with file:line evidence.\n\nUse `entire graph search` itself where helpful, plus focused reads. `rtk` for git/gh.\n\nOUTPUT: caveman-ultra compressed. file:line per claim. Clearly separate Q1 and Q2. State anything you could not determine. Max 400 words.","subagent_type":"Explore","model":"sonnet"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"ef1717a7-ef7c-44e4-9271-52f0313c5403","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CffQfJoKrWQJWVBHeFjoY","type":"assistant","uuid":"9762ffac-849b-4522-9043-2a6decf67745","timestamp":"2026-10-03T13:48:43.065Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c