{"parentUuid":"9762ffac-849b-4522-9043-2a6decf67745","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CffQfMnuqqJpHxzVQoyw9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LL7frYBPvEh7N6dCsKR9G6","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Explore usage measurement surface","prompt":"Read-only exploration. Do NOT edit anything. Repos: /Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph and /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide.\n\nQUESTION: what instrumentation already exists for measuring whether an agent USES these tools, so a before/after experiment can report the same metric the project already quotes?\n\nThe project quotes a figure: \"332 graph calls against 96,987 exploration calls (0.34%), and the graph-first rate was 0 in every session sampled\" (entire-graph internal/agentsetup/guide.go header comment). Find what produced it.\n\nReport precisely:\n1. Where is \"graph-first rate\" computed? `entire graph stats` is a candidate (internal/cli/stats*.go). Name the file:line, the exact definition of the metric, and what data source it reads (session transcripts? a local log? checkpoints?).\n2. What counts as an \"exploration call\" in that denominator? Is it read from captured Entire sessions, or from Claude Code transcripts on disk, or something else? Name the path it reads.\n3. Does the figure require Entire capture to be enabled in the repo, or does it work from local agent transcripts alone?\n4. Is there anything in entire-brain that records tool usage — e.g. does `hookRecordServed` (internal/cli/hook_cmd.go) or the MCP server write a usage log? Where does it land on disk?\n5. CAVEAT CHECK: there is a known note that `entire graph stats` reported 82.9M tokens saved where an honest figure was ~46k. Find the comment/commit behind that and say whether the graph-first-rate metric shares the same defect or is independent.\n\nThis is for designing a measurement, so accuracy about WHAT each number counts matters more than breadth.\n\nUse `entire graph search --repo . --profile full --query \"...\"` first, then focused reads. `rtk` for git/gh.\n\nOUTPUT: caveman-ultra compressed. file:line per claim. Say explicitly which metrics are trustworthy for a before/after and which are not. Max 400 words.","subagent_type":"Explore","model":"sonnet"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1838,"cache_read_input_tokens":529984,"output_tokens":2674,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1838,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2674,"cache_read_input_tokens":529984,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1838,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1838},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01LL7frYBPvEh7N6dCsKR9G6":{"description":"Explore usage measurement surface","prompt":"Read-only exploration. Do NOT edit anything. Repos: /Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph and /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide.\n\nQUESTION: what instrumentation already exists for measuring whether an agent USES these tools, so a before/after experiment can report the same metric the project already quotes?\n\nThe project quotes a figure: \"332 graph calls against 96,987 exploration calls (0.34%), and the graph-first rate was 0 in every session sampled\" (entire-graph internal/agentsetup/guide.go header comment). Find what produced it.\n\nReport precisely:\n1. Where is \"graph-first rate\" computed? `entire graph stats` is a candidate (internal/cli/stats*.go). Name the file:line, the exact definition of the metric, and what data source it reads (session