{"parentUuid":"6a35b030-7137-40bd-a9ad-f8e833efeb97","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CffQzRzh43fPBGyM5g8mb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Message delivered to the graph session. Now let me write the plan."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1097,"cache_read_input_tokens":551704,"output_tokens":6381,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2231},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1097,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":6381,"cache_read_input_tokens":551704,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1097,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1097},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"5b26772b-97f8-412d-a8c1-043bc5af733d","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CffQzPMCoetiEdtevmmsP","type":"assistant","uuid":"db6709e9-fe66-407d-8536-124beab8ec93","timestamp":"2026-10-03T13:53:08.914Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"db6709e9-fe66-407d-8536-124beab8ec93","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CffQzRzh43fPBGyM5g8mb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GCVdHdyngQNv3bbzjnCg6a","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/dynamic-petting-globe.md","content":"# Fix agent usage of Brain + Graph, and verify it in a clean environment\n\n## Context\n\nPRs #329–#331 (unmerged) fixed a text defect that plausibly suppressed tool usage: brain's\nshipped agent guide told agents they could skip the tools, and CI enforced that wording in both\ndirections. **Whether fixing it actually raises usage is unmeasured.**\n\nThe one experiment run so far is invalid, and it is worth being precise about why: the guide text\nwas injected into each agent's *prompt*. That tests whether the wording works once it is already\nin context — the thing nobody doubted. The real-world failure is that the guide *file* never\nchanges behaviour. Both arms used the tools 100% of the time, so there was no headroom to detect\nan increase, and n was 2 per arm.\n\nThis plan replaces that with a clean-environment measurement using real `claude -p` sessions, a\npre-registered success bar, and a fix/re-measure loop. Three exploration passes established the\nmechanics below; everything cited is `file:line` from source.\n\n### What is now established\n\n**Guide delivery (entire-brain).** `init-agents` writes `.entire/agent-guide.md`, root `AGENTS.md`,\nroot `CLAUDE.md` (carrying `@.entire/agent-guide.md`), and — new in #331 — a `PreToolUse` entry in\n`.claude/settings.json` (`internal/agentsetup/files.go:19,221,249`; `claudehooks.go:46`). `setup`\nwrites **none** of them (`setup.go` has no reference to any of those names), which confirms the\nreported \"AGENTS.md never appeared\" as intended behaviour, not a bug. There are almost no gates;\nthe only hard one is root resolution (`agent_setup.go:47`).\n\n**Two hazards in that path.** `ENTIRE_REPO_ROOT` outranks cwd (`env.go:23,73`), so a host that sets\nit can silently install into the outer repo; and the walk-up stops at the *innermost* `.git`\n(`migration.go:94-131`), so a nested clone captures the files. Also: the combined guide carrying\nthe Graph directive ships **only when both products are enabled** (`guide.go:128`) — a brain-only\ninstall gets `BrainGuide()` with no Graph instruction at all (`guide.go:130`).\n\n**Graph has no MCP server, by design.** No MCP/JSON-RPC dependency in `go.mod`, no server under\n`cmd/` or `internal/cli`, and `README.md:268` states it will not expose one. So Bash is the only\nroute to Graph, and the guide is correct to name a shell command — but an MCP-first harness has no\nGraph tool at all. This is a constraint to measure around, not a bug to fix.\n\n**The measurement already exists and is usable.** `entire graph stats` computes\n`graph_first_rate = GraphFirstSessions / SessionsWithLocate`\n(`entire-graph/internal/cli/stats.go:1183-1189,1236`) from local Claude Code JSONL transcripts in\n`~/.claude/projects/<repo-slug>/` (`:374-386`), and `--sessions-dir` / `--transcript` override that\npath — which is what makes a clean-env arm measurable. Two caveats that change the design:\n\n- **MCP calls are invisible to it.** Only Bash `entire graph <verb>` / `entire-graph <verb>` count\n  as graph calls (`:1048-1055`); `mcp__entire-brain__*` matches neither bucket. Brain usage\n  therefore needs its own measure.\n- **Pin the binary.** The withdrawn \"82.9M tokens saved\" figure was binary-version drift\n  (`scripts/entire-graph-statusline.sh:115`), and the graph-first rate runs in the same binary.\n\nThe exploration could not find the provenance of the quoted `332 / 96,987 (0.34%)` baseline — it is\nonly ever quoted, never derived. Treat it as context, not as this experiment's control.\n\n### The two unknowns that decide everything\n\nNeither is answerable from source, and both are cheap to settle:\n\n1. **Does the model actually receive the guide** through `CLAUDE.md`'s `@.entire/agent-guide.md`\n   import? If not, every wording fix in #331 is inert.\n2. **Is `$CLAUDE_FILE_PATH` populated** in a `PreToolUse` hook? #331's wiring passes\n   `--file \"$CLAUDE_FILE_PATH\"`; if that variable is not set, the hook runs with an empty path and\n   **my own hook is a no-op.**\n\nThese run first, as two single sessions, before any arm.\n\n---\n\n## Scope note: entire-graph is on hold\n\nThe decoy/ranking problem is the half that makes usage *persist* — 3 of 4 sessions used the tool\nexactly as instructed, got a decoy, and succeeded with grep instead. Two mechanisms are located:\nidf is computed over the preselected sample rather than the repo\n(`internal/sem/search.go:1376-1411,1495,3889`; one run indexed 384 of 1855 files,\n`preselection_confidence 0.0027`), and the stopword list (`:1027`) lacks \"decide\", \"whether\",\n\"needs\", \"rebuilding\" so they score against *names*, where signals dominate (`:4355`, `:4422`).\n\nA message has been sent to the `redesign-graph-cost-reduction` session asking whether this is\nalready fixed or in flight, and who should own it. **No entire-graph file will be touched until it\nreplies.** If it owns the fix, this plan measures against its branch; if it declines, adding a\ngraph PR is a separate decision to bring back to you.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 1 — Harness (no model cost)\n\nBuild under `~/.claude/jobs/<job>/tmp/cleanenv/`, nothing inside `devenv/`.\n\n- **Pinned binaries.** Build `entire-brain` from the stack tip (`fix/agent-guide-directive-and-discovery`)\n  and record the commit; use the installed `entire-graph` and record its version. Every arm uses\n  the same two binaries.\n- **One fresh clone per arm**, each with no `.entire/`, no `CLAUDE.md`, no `AGENTS.md`, so arms\n  cannot contaminate each other. `ENTIRE_REPO_ROOT` explicitly unset in every arm (it outranks cwd).\n- **Instrumentation, three independent channels** — because no single one sees everything:\n  | channel | catches | why needed |\n  |---|---|---|\n  | PATH shim logging every `entire` call with a run id | all Brain + Graph **CLI** calls, in order | the only ordered record of what the agent actually ran |\n  | `entire graph stats --sessions-dir <arm>` | `graph_first_rate`, graph calls, exploration calls | the project's own metric, so before/after is comparable |\n  | transcript grep for `mcp__entire-brain__` | Brain **MCP** usage | invisible to `graph stats` |\n- **Isolated transcript dir per arm** so `--sessions-dir` reads only that arm's sessions.\n- A fixed task set (6–8 locate/explain/change tasks) written once and reused verbatim across arms.\n\n## Phase 2 — Settle the two unknowns (2 sessions)\n\n- **Probe A:** `claude -p \"quote the sentence in your instructions about your FIRST action\"` with cwd\n  in an `init-agents`-installed clone. Establishes whether the `@` import reaches the model.\n- **Probe B:** a session told to edit one file; check the shim log for a `hook pre-edit --file <path>`\n  call with a **non-empty** path. Establishes whether `$CLAUDE_FILE_PATH` works.\n\nIf Probe A fails, the fix is to inline the directive into `CLAUDE.md` rather than import it, and\neverything downstream re-runs. If Probe B fails, #331's hook wiring is corrected before the arms run.\n\n## Phase 3 — Arms, pre-registered\n\nThree arms, **n ≥ 10 sessions each**, same tasks, same binaries, fresh clone per arm:\n\n- **A0 — no guide.** `setup` only, no `init-agents`. The true baseline.\n- **A1 — guide only.** `init-agents`, hook entry removed from `.claude/settings.json`.\n- **A2 — guide + hook.** Full `init-agents`. Isolates whether wording alone sufficed.\n\n**Pre-registered bar, fixed before the first session runs:**\n\n| metric | A0 expectation | pass condition for A1 |\n|---|---|---|\n| sessions with ≥1 Graph or Brain call | low | **≥ 9/10** |\n| `graph_first_rate` | ~0 | **≥ 0.7** |\n| sessions that used a tool then abandoned it for grep | — | **≤ 3/10** |\n\nn=10 per arm is adequate *for an effect this large* — 0/10 vs 7/10 is Fisher exact p < 0.001 — and\nis not adequate for a small one. If the observed effect is small, the honest outcome is \"not\nestablished at this n\", not a wider search for a subgroup that worked.\n\nThe third row is the one that matters most and the one the earlier run exposed: first-call\ncompliance can rise while sustained usage stays flat.\n\n## Phase 4 — Ask every session what went wrong\n\nAfter each task, a follow-up turn in the same session: what was your first action, did you reach\nfor Brain or Graph, if not why not, what did the tool return, was it useful, what would have made\nyou use it. Collected verbatim.\n\nThis is the highest-yield channel available — it is what exposed the root cause in the first place\n(\"The agent guide says to start substantive tasks with `entire brain brief`… I skipped that\"). It is\nalso self-report, so it is used to *find* mechanisms, never to score the arms; scoring comes from\nthe three instrumented channels only.\n\n## Phase 5 — Loop\n\nEach round: read the feedback, find the top blocker, fix it in the stack (brain side) or hand it to\nthe graph session, re-run the affected arm, re-check against the same pre-registered bar. Stop when\nA1 or A2 clears the bar on a round where no new blocker class appeared, or when a round produces a\nblocker that is a product decision rather than a defect — which comes back to you rather than\ngetting guessed.\n\n**Candidate blockers already identified**, to check rather than assume: the `@`-import path (Probe A);\n`$CLAUDE_FILE_PATH` (Probe B); brain-only installs getting no Graph directive (`guide.go:128,130`);\n`ENTIRE_REPO_ROOT` mis-targeting; and MCP-first sessions having no Graph route at all, which no\nwording can fix.\n\n---\n\n## Cost, stated up front\n\nRoughly 32+ real `claude -p` sessions (2 probes + 3 arms × 10) plus a feedback turn each, at a\nlocate task's typical size. Order of a few million tokens per full round, and the loop may need more\nthan one round. Sonnet, small tasks, and arms re-run individually rather than all three each time.\nSay the word if you want a smaller first round — 5 per arm would still separate 0 from 0.7.\n\n## Verification\n\nThe deliverable is not \"the tests pass\" — it is a number against a bar fixed in advance:\n\n1. Phase 2 probes answered yes/no with the evidence inline.\n2. A table of A0 / A1 / A2 on all three metrics, with counts beside every rate and the exact\n   commands and binary versions that produced them.\n3. Every fix made during the loop carries a regression test verified by weakening — guard patched\n   compile-clean, test shown red, assertion quoted.\n4. The verbatim feedback, including anything that contradicts the result.\n5. If the bar is not cleared, that is reported as the finding, with what remains unfixed. A result\n   that says \"usage did not improve\" is a successful execution of this plan.\n\nNothing merges without your approval; PRs #329–#331 stay unmerged and this work stacks on #331.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1097,"cache_read_input_tokens":551704,"output_tokens":6381,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2231},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1097,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":6381,"cache_read_input_tokens":551704,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1097,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1097},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01GCVdHdyngQNv3bbzjnCg6a":{"file_path":"/Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/dynamic-petting-globe.md","content":"# Fix agent usage of Brain + Graph, and verify it in a clean environment\n\n## Context\n\nPRs #329–#331 (unmerged) fixed a text defect that plausibly suppressed tool usage: brain's\nshipped agent guide told agents they could skip the tools, and CI enforced that wording in both\ndirections. **Whether fixing it actually raises usage is unmeasured.**\n\nThe one experiment run so far is invalid, and it is worth being precise about why: the guide text\nwas injected into each agent's *prompt*. That tests whether the wording works once it is already\nin context — the thing nobody doubted. The real-world failure is that the guide *file* never\nchanges behaviour. Both arms used the tools 100% of the time, so there was no headroom to detect\nan increase, and n was 2 per arm.\n\nThis plan replaces that with a clean-environment measurement using real `claude -p` sessions, a\npre-registered success bar, and a fix/re-measure loop. Three exploration passes established the\nmechanics below; everything cited is `file:line` from source.\n\n### What is now established\n\n**Guide delivery (entire-brain).** `init-agents` writes `.entire/agent-guide.md`, root `AGENTS.md`,\nroot `CLAUDE.md` (carrying `@.entire/agent-guide.md`), and — new in #331 — a `PreToolUse` entry in\n`.claude/settings.json` (`internal/agentsetup/files.go:19,221,249`; `claudehooks.go:46`). `setup`\nwrites **none** of them (`setup.go` has no reference to any of those names), which confirms the\nreported \"AGENTS.md never appeared\" as intended behaviour, not a bug. There are almost no gates;\nthe only hard one is root resolution (`agent_setup.go:47`).\n\n**Two hazards in that path.** `ENTIRE_REPO_ROOT` outranks cwd (`env.go:23,73`), so a host that sets\nit can silently install into the outer repo; and the walk-up stops at the *innermost* `.git`\n(`migration.go:94-131`), so a nested clone captures the files. Also: the combined guide carrying\nthe Graph directive ships **only when both products are enabled** (`guide.go:128`) — a brain-only\ninstall gets `BrainGuide()` with no Graph instruction at all (`guide.go:130`).\n\n**Graph has no MCP server, by design.** No MCP/JSON-RPC dependency in `go.mod`, no server under\n`cmd/` or `internal/cli`, and `README.md:268` states it will not expose one. So Bash is the only\nroute to Graph, and the guide is correct to name a shell command — but an MCP-first harness has no\nGraph tool at all. This is a constraint to measure around, not a bug to fix.\n\n**The measurement already exists and is usable.** `entire graph stats` computes\n`graph_first_rate = GraphFirstSessions / SessionsWithLocate`\n(`entire-graph/internal/cli/stats.go:1183-1189,1236`) from local Claude Code JSONL transcripts in\n`~/.claude/projects/<repo-slug>/` (`:374-386`), and `--sessions-dir` / `--transcript` override that\npath — which is what makes a clean-env arm measurable. Two caveats that change the design:\n\n- **MCP calls are invisible to it.** Only Bash `entire graph <verb>` / `entire-graph <verb>` count\n  as graph calls (`:1048-1055`); `mcp__entire-brain__*` matches neither bucket. Brain usage\n  therefore needs its own measure.\n- **Pin the binary.** The withdrawn \"82.9M tokens saved\" figure was binary-version drift\n  (`scripts/entire-graph-statusline.sh:115`), and the graph-first rate runs in the same binary.\n\nThe exploration could not find the provenance of the quoted `332 / 96,987 (0.34%)` baseline — it is\nonly ever quoted, never derived. Treat it as context, not as this experiment's control.\n\n### The two unknowns that decide everything\n\nNeither is answerable from source, and both are cheap to settle:\n\n1. **Does the model actually receive the guide** through `CLAUDE.md`'s `@.entire/agent-guide.md`\n   import? If not, every wording fix in #331 is inert.\n2. **Is `$CLAUDE_FILE_PATH` populated** in a `PreToolUse` hook? #331's wiring passes\n   `--file \"$CLAUDE_FILE_PATH\"`; if that variable is not set, the hook runs with an empty path and\n   **my own hook is a no-op.**\n\nThese run first, as two single sessions, before any arm.\n\n---\n\n## Scope note: entire-graph is on hold\n\nThe decoy/ranking problem is the half that makes usage *persist* — 3 of 4 sessions used the tool\nexactly as instructed, got a decoy, and succeeded with grep instead. Two mechanisms are located:\nidf is computed over the preselected sample rather than the repo\n(`internal/sem/search.go:1376-1411,1495,3889`; one run indexed 384 of 1855 files,\n`preselection_confidence 0.0027`), and the stopword list (`:1027`) lacks \"decide\", \"whether\",\n\"needs\", \"rebuilding\" so they score against *names*, where signals dominate (`:4355`, `:4422`).\n\nA message has been sent to the `redesign-graph-cost-reduction` session asking whether this is\nalready fixed or in flight, and who should own it. **No entire-graph file will be touched until it\nreplies.** If it owns the fix, this plan measures against its branch; if it declines, adding a\ngraph PR is a separate decision to bring back to you.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 1 — Harness (no model cost)\n\nBuild under `~/.claude/jobs/<job>/tmp/cleanenv/`, nothing inside `devenv/`.\n\n- **Pinned binaries.** Build `entire-brain` from the stack tip (`fix/agent-guide-directive-and-discovery`)\n  and record the commit; use the installed `entire-graph` and record its version. Every arm uses\n  the same two binaries.\n- **One fresh clone per arm**, each with no `.entire/`, no `CLAUDE.md`, no `AGENTS.md`, so arms\n  cannot contaminate each other. `ENTIRE_REPO_ROOT` explicitly unset in every arm (it outranks cwd).\n- **Instrumentation, three independent channels** — because no single one sees everything:\n  | channel | catches | why needed |\n  |---|---|---|\n  | PATH shim logging every `entire` call with a run id | all Brain + Graph **CLI** calls, in order | the only ordered record of what the agent actually ran |\n  | `entire graph stats --sessions-dir <arm>` | `graph_first_rate`, graph calls, exploration calls | the project's own metric, so before/after is comparable |\n  | transcript grep for `mcp__entire-brain__` | Brain **MCP** usage | invisible to `graph stats` |\n- **Isolated transcript dir per arm** so `--sessions-dir` reads only that arm's sessions.\n- A fixed task set (6–8 locate/explain/change tasks) written once and reused verbatim across arms.\n\n## Phase 2 — Settle the two unknowns (2 sessions)\n\n- **Probe A:** `claude -p \"quote the sentence in your instructions about your FIRST action\"` with cwd\n  in an `init-agents`-installed clone. Establishes whether the `@` import reaches the model.\n- **Probe B:** a session told to edit one file; check the shim log for a `hook pre-edit --file <path>`\n  call with a **non-empty** path. Establishes whether `$CLAUDE_FILE_PATH` works.\n\nIf Probe A fails, the fix is to inline the directive into `CLAUDE.md` rather than import it, and\neverything downstream re-runs. If Probe B fails, #331's hook wiring is corrected before the arms run.\n\n## Phase 3 — Arms, pre-registered\n\nThree arms, **n ≥ 10 sessions each**, same tasks, same binaries, fresh clone per arm:\n\n- **A0 — no guide.** `setup` only, no `init-agents`. The true baseline.\n- **A1 — guide only.** `init-agents`, hook entry removed from `.claude/settings.json`.\n- **A2 — guide + hook.** Full `init-agents`. Isolates whether wording alone sufficed.\n\n**Pre-registered bar, fixed before the first session runs:**\n\n| metric | A0 expectation | pass condition for A1 |\n|---|---|---|\n| sessions with ≥1 Graph or Brain call | low | **≥ 9/10** |\n| `graph_first_rate` | ~0 | **≥ 0.7** |\n| sessions that used a tool then abandoned it for grep | — | **≤ 3/10** |\n\nn=10 per arm is adequate *for an effect this large* — 0/10 vs 7/10 is Fisher exact p < 0.001 — and\nis not adequate for a small one. If the observed effect is small, the honest outcome is \"not\nestablished at this n\", not a wider search for a subgroup that worked.\n\nThe third row is the one that matters most and the one the earlier run exposed: first-call\ncompliance can rise while sustained usage stays flat.\n\n## Phase 4 — Ask every session what went wrong\n\nAfter each task, a follow-up turn in the same session: what was your first action, did you reach\nfor Brain or Graph, if not why not, what did the tool return, was it useful, what would have made\nyou use it. Collected verbatim.\n\nThis is the highest-yield channel available — it is what exposed the root cause in the first place\n(\"The agent guide says to start substantive tasks with `entire brain brief`… I skipped that\"). It is\nalso self-report, so it is used to *find* mechanisms, never to score the arms; scoring comes from\nthe three instrumented channels only.\n\n## Phase 5 — Loop\n\nEach round: read the feedback, find the top blocker, fix it in the stack (brain side) or hand it to\nthe graph session, re-run the affected arm, re-check against the same pre-registered bar. Stop when\nA1 or A2 clears the bar on a round where no new blocker class appeared, or when a round produces a\nblocker that is a product decision rather than a defect — which comes back to you rather than\ngetting guessed.\n\n**Candidate blockers already identified**, to check rather than assume: the `@`-import path (Probe A);\n`$CLAUDE_FILE_PATH` (Probe B); brain-only installs getting no Graph directive (`guide.go:128,130`);\n`ENTIRE_REPO_ROOT` mis-targeting; and MCP-first sessions having no Graph route at all, which no\nwording can fix.\n\n---\n\n## Cost, stated up front\n\nRoughly 32+ real `claude -p` sessions (2 probes + 3 arms × 10) plus a feedback turn each, at a\nlocate task's typical size. Order of a few million tokens per full round, and the loop may need more\nthan one round. Sonnet, small tasks, and arms re-run individually rather than all three each time.\nSay the word if you want a smaller first round — 5 per arm would still separate 0 from 0.7.\n\n## Verification\n\nThe deliverable is not \"the tests pass\" — it is a number against a bar fixed in advance:\n\n1. Phase 2 probes answered yes/no with the evidence inline.\n2. A table of A0 / A1 / A2 on all three metrics, with counts beside every rate and the exact\n   commands and binary versions that produced them.\n3. Every fix made during the loop carries a regression test verified by weakening — guard patched\n   compile-clean, test shown red, assertion quoted.\n4. The verbatim feedback, including anything that contradicts the result.\n5. If the bar is not cleared, that is reported as the finding, with what remains unfixed. A result\n   that says \"usage did not improve\" is a successful execution of this plan.\n\nNothing merges without your approval; PRs #329–#331 stay unmerged and this work stacks on #331.\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"5b26772b-97f8-412d-a8c1-043bc5af733d","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CffQzPMCoetiEdtevmmsP","type":"assistant","uuid":"6d99bd86-04c0-41df-917f-abac0b533ddf","timestamp":"2026-10-03T13:54:03.839Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"6d99bd86-04c0-41df-917f-abac0b533ddf","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"fc0e85dc-8585-4b18-a360-2e0091ce935d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GCVdHdyngQNv3bbzjnCg6a","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/dynamic-petting-globe.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"9f834e96-0d0b-4a36-bc93-e1926425c141","timestamp":"2026-10-03T13:54:03.883Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"update","filePath":"/Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/dynamic-petting-globe.md","content":"# Fix agent usage of Brain + Graph, and verify it in a clean environment\n\n## Context\n\nPRs #329–#331 (unmerged) fixed a text defect that plausibly suppressed tool usage: brain's\nshipped agent guide told agents they could skip the tools, and CI enforced that wording in both\ndirections. **Whether fixing it actually raises usage is unmeasured.**\n\nThe one experiment run so far is invalid, and it is worth being precise about why: the guide text\nwas injected into each agent's *prompt*. That tests whether the wording works once it is already\nin context — the thing nobody doubted. The real-world failure is that the guide *file* never\nchanges behaviour. Both arms used the tools 100% of the time, so there was no headroom to detect\nan increase, and n was 2 per arm.\n\nThis plan replaces that with a clean-environment measurement using real `claude -p` sessions, a\npre-registered success bar, and a fix/re-measure loop. Three exploration passes established the\nmechanics below; everything cited is `file:line` from source.\n\n### What is now established\n\n**Guide delivery (entire-brain).** `init-agents` writes `.entire/agent-guide.md`, root `AGENTS.md`,\nroot `CLAUDE.md` (carrying `@.entire/agent-guide.md`), and — new in #331 — a `PreToolUse` entry in\n`.claude/settings.json` (`internal/agentsetup/files.go:19,221,249`; `claudehooks.go:46`). `setup`\nwrites **none** of them (`setup.go` has no reference to any of those names), which confirms the\nreported \"AGENTS.md never appeared\" as intended behaviour, not a bug. There are almost no gates;\nthe only hard one is root resolution (`agent_setup.go:47`).\n\n**Two hazards in that path.** `ENTIRE_REPO_ROOT` outranks cwd (`env.go:23,73`), so a host that sets\nit can silently install into the outer repo; and the walk-up stops at the *innermost* `.git`\n(`migration.go:94-131`), so a nested clone captures the files. Also: the combined guide carrying\nthe Graph directive ships **only when both products are enabled** (`guide.go:128`) — a brain-only\ninstall gets `BrainGuide()` with no Graph instruction at all (`guide.go:130`).\n\n**Graph has no MCP server, by design.** No MCP/JSON-RPC dependency in `go.mod`, no server under\n`cmd/` or `internal/cli`, and `README.md:268` states it will not expose one. So Bash is the only\nroute to Graph, and the guide is correct to name a shell command — but an MCP-first harness has no\nGraph tool at all. This is a constraint to measure around, not a bug to fix.\n\n**The measurement already exists and is usable.** `entire graph stats` computes\n`graph_first_rate = GraphFirstSessions / SessionsWithLocate`\n(`entire-graph/internal/cli/stats.go:1183-1189,1236`) from local Claude Code JSONL transcripts in\n`~/.claude/projects/<repo-slug>/` (`:374-386`), and `--sessions-dir` / `--transcript` override that\npath — which is what makes a clean-env arm measurable. Two caveats that change the design:\n\n- **MCP calls are invisible to it.** Only Bash `entire graph <verb>` / `entire-graph <verb>` count\n  as graph calls (`:1048-1055`); `mcp__entire-brain__*` matches neither bucket. Brain usage\n  therefore needs its own measure.\n- **Pin the binary.** The withdrawn \"82.9M tokens saved\" figure was binary-version drift\n  (`scripts/entire-graph-statusline.sh:115`), and the graph-first rate runs in the same binary.\n\nThe exploration could not find the provenance of the quoted `332 / 96,987 (0.34%)` baseline — it is\nonly ever quoted, never derived. Treat it as context, not as this experiment's control.\n\n### The two unknowns that decide everything\n\nNeither is answerable from source, and both are cheap to settle:\n\n1. **Does the model actually receive the guide** through `CLAUDE.md`'s `@.entire/agent-guide.md`\n   import? If not, every wording fix in #331 is inert.\n2. **Is `$CLAUDE_FILE_PATH` populated** in a `PreToolUse` hook? #331's wiring passes\n   `--file \"$CLAUDE_FILE_PATH\"`; if that variable is not set, the hook runs with an empty path and\n   **my own hook is a no-op.**\n\nThese run first, as two single sessions, before any arm.\n\n---\n\n## Scope note: entire-graph is on hold\n\nThe decoy/ranking problem is the half that makes usage *persist* — 3 of 4 sessions used the tool\nexactly as instructed, got a decoy, and succeeded with grep instead. Two mechanisms are located:\nidf is computed over the preselected sample rather than the repo\n(`internal/sem/search.go:1376-1411,1495,3889`; one run indexed 384 of 1855 files,\n`preselection_confidence 0.0027`), and the stopword list (`:1027`) lacks \"decide\", \"whether\",\n\"needs\", \"rebuilding\" so they score against *names*, where signals dominate (`:4355`, `:4422`).\n\nA message has been sent to the `redesign-graph-cost-reduction` session asking whether this is\nalready fixed or in flight, and who should own it. **No entire-graph file will be touched until it\nreplies.** If it owns the fix, this plan measures against its branch; if it declines, adding a\ngraph PR is a separate decision to bring back to you.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 1 — Harness (no model cost)\n\nBuild under `~/.claude/jobs/<job>/tmp/cleanenv/`, nothing inside `devenv/`.\n\n- **Pinned binaries.** Build `entire-brain` from the stack tip (`fix/agent-guide-directive-and-discovery`)\n  and record the commit; use the installed `entire-graph` and record its version. Every arm uses\n  the same two binaries.\n- **One fresh clone per arm**, each with no `.entire/`, no `CLAUDE.md`, no `AGENTS.md`, so arms\n  cannot contaminate each other. `ENTIRE_REPO_ROOT` explicitly unset in every arm (it outranks cwd).\n- **Instrumentation, three independent channels** — because no single one sees everything:\n  | channel | catches | why needed |\n  |---|---|---|\n  | PATH shim logging every `entire` call with a run id | all Brain + Graph **CLI** calls, in order | the only ordered record of what the agent actually ran |\n  | `entire graph stats --sessions-dir <arm>` | `graph_first_rate`, graph calls, exploration calls | the project's own metric, so before/after is comparable |\n  | transcript grep for `mcp__entire-brain__` | Brain **MCP** usage | invisible to `graph stats` |\n- **Isolated transcript dir per arm** so `--sessions-dir` reads only that arm's sessions.\n- A fixed task set (6–8 locate/explain/change tasks) written once and reused verbatim across arms.\n\n## Phase 2 — Settle the two unknowns (2 sessions)\n\n- **Probe A:** `claude -p \"quote the sentence in your instructions about your FIRST action\"` with cwd\n  in an `init-agents`-installed clone. Establishes whether the `@` import reaches the model.\n- **Probe B:** a session told to edit one file; check the shim log for a `hook pre-edit --file <path>`\n  call with a **non-empty** path. Establishes whether `$CLAUDE_FILE_PATH` works.\n\nIf Probe A fails, the fix is to inline the directive into `CLAUDE.md` rather than import it, and\neverything downstream re-runs. If Probe B fails, #331's hook wiring is corrected before the arms run.\n\n## Phase 3 — Arms, pre-registered\n\nThree arms, **n ≥ 10 sessions each**, same tasks, same binaries, fresh clone per arm:\n\n- **A0 — no guide.** `setup` only, no `init-agents`. The true baseline.\n- **A1 — guide only.** `init-agents`, hook entry removed from `.claude/settings.json`.\n- **A2 — guide + hook.** Full `init-agents`. Isolates whether wording alone sufficed.\n\n**Pre-registered bar, fixed before the first session runs:**\n\n| metric | A0 expectation | pass condition for A1 |\n|---|---|---|\n| sessions with ≥1 Graph or Brain call | low | **≥ 9/10** |\n| `graph_first_rate` | ~0 | **≥ 0.7** |\n| sessions that used a tool then abandoned it for grep | — | **≤ 3/10** |\n\nn=10 per arm is adequate *for an effect this large* — 0/10 vs 7/10 is Fisher exact p < 0.001 — and\nis not adequate for a small one. If the observed effect is small, the honest outcome is \"not\nestablished at this n\", not a wider search for a subgroup that worked.\n\nThe third row is the one that matters most and the one the earlier run exposed: first-call\ncompliance can rise while sustained usage stays flat.\n\n## Phase 4 — Ask every session what went wrong\n\nAfter each task, a follow-up turn in the same session: what was your first action, did you reach\nfor Brain or Graph, if not why not, what did the tool return, was it useful, what would have made\nyou use it. Collected verbatim.\n\nThis is the highest-yield channel available — it is what exposed the root cause in the first place\n(\"The agent guide says to start substantive tasks with `entire brain brief`… I skipped that\"). It is\nalso self-report, so it is used to *find* mechanisms, never to score the arms; scoring comes from\nthe three instrumented channels only.\n\n## Phase 5 — Loop\n\nEach round: read the feedback, find the top blocker, fix it in the stack (brain side) or hand it to\nthe graph session, re-run the affected arm, re-check against the same pre-registered bar. Stop when\nA1 or A2 clears the bar on a round where no new blocker class appeared, or when a round produces a\nblocker that is a product decision rather than a defect — which comes back to you rather than\ngetting guessed.\n\n**Candidate blockers already identified**, to check rather than assume: the `@`-import path (Probe A);\n`$CLAUDE_FILE_PATH` (Probe B); brain-only installs getting no Graph directive (`guide.go:128,130`);\n`ENTIRE_REPO_ROOT` mis-targeting; and MCP-first sessions having no Graph route at all, which no\nwording can fix.\n\n---\n\n## Cost, stated up front\n\nRoughly 32+ real `claude -p` sessions (2 probes + 3 arms × 10) plus a feedback turn each, at a\nlocate task's typical size. Order of a few million tokens per full round, and the loop may need more\nthan one round. Sonnet, small tasks, and arms re-run individually rather than all three each time.\nSay the word if you want a smaller first round — 5 per arm would still separate 0 from 0.7.\n\n## Verification\n\nThe deliverable is not \"the tests pass\" — it is a number against a bar fixed in advance:\n\n1. Phase 2 probes answered yes/no with the evidence inline.\n2. A table of A0 / A1 / A2 on all three metrics, with counts beside every rate and the exact\n   commands and binary versions that produced them.\n3. Every fix made during the loop carries a regression test verified by weakening — guard patched\n   compile-clean, test shown red, assertion quoted.\n4. The verbatim feedback, including anything that contradicts the result.\n5. If the bar is not cleared, that is reported as the finding, with what remains unfixed. A result\n   that says \"usage did not improve\" is a successful execution of this plan.\n\nNothing merges without your approval; PRs #329–#331 stay unmerged and this work stacks on #331.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":299,"newStart":1,"newLines":181,"lines":["-# Brain + Graph v1 readiness","+# Fix agent usage of Brain + Graph, and verify it in a clean environment"," "," ## Context"," ","-Three streams of evidence converged this week:","+PRs #329–#331 (unmerged) fixed a text defect that plausibly suppressed tool usage: brain's","+shipped agent guide told agents they could skip the tools, and CI enforced that wording in both","+directions. **Whether fixing it actually raises usage is unmeasured.**"," ","-1. **A user install report (Joseph)** — distill stalled at 75/237; `AGENTS.md`/`CLAUDE.md` never","-   appeared at repo level; doc ambiguity about where to run setup.","-2. **Seven issues filed 2026-10-02** by two external testers (leine4550, peyton-alt).","-3. **Two full agent transcripts** (Claude Code and Codex, same prompts, same repo) showing agents","-   not using Brain or Graph.","+The one experiment run so far is invalid, and it is worth being precise about why: the guide text","+was injected into each agent's *prompt*. That tests whether the wording works once it is already","+in context — the thing nobody doubted. The real-world failure is that the guide *file* never","+changes behaviour. Both arms used the tools 100% of the time, so there was no headroom to detect","+an increase, and n was 2 per arm."," ","-Investigation of all three found that the headline problem is **not** that agents are habitual.","-Three distinct, verified causes sit underneath it, and all are fixable.","+This plan replaces that with a clean-environment measurement using real `claude -p` sessions, a","+pre-registered success bar, and a fix/re-measure loop. Three exploration passes established the","+mechanics below; everything cited is `file:line` from source."," ","-**Already fixed and merged:** #316 (semantic memo on the wrong path, unbounded, unlinearized),","-#317 (ollama envelope cap measuring the prompt, silent truncation, probe on an exhausted budget,","-usage-accounting bypass, misleading flag help). **Open and green:** #306, #318, #320, #321.","+### What is now established"," ","-This plan covers what is *not* taken care of.","+**Guide delivery (entire-brain).** `init-agents` writes `.entire/agent-guide.md`, root `AGENTS.md`,","+root `CLAUDE.md` (carrying `@.entire/agent-guide.md`), and — new in #331 — a `PreToolUse` entry in","+`.claude/settings.json` (`internal/agentsetup/files.go:19,221,249`; `claudehooks.go:46`). `setup`","+writes **none** of them (`setup.go` has no reference to any of those names), which confirms the","+reported \"AGENTS.md never appeared\" as intended behaviour, not a bug. There are almost no gates;","+the only hard one is root resolution (`agent_setup.go:47`)."," ","----","+**Two hazards in that path.** `ENTIRE_REPO_ROOT` outranks cwd (`env.go:23,73`), so a host that sets","+it can silently install into the outer repo; and the walk-up stops at the *innermost* `.git`","+(`migration.go:94-131`), so a nested clone captures the files. Also: the combined guide carrying","+the Graph directive ships **only when both products are enabled** (`guide.go:128`) — a brain-only","+install gets `BrainGuide()` with no Graph instruction at all (`guide.go:130`)."," ","-## The three root causes","+**Graph has no MCP server, by design.** No MCP/JSON-RPC dependency in `go.mod`, no server under","+`cmd/` or `internal/cli`, and `README.md:268` states it will not expose one. So Bash is the only","+route to Graph, and the guide is correct to name a shell command — but an MCP-first harness has no","+Graph tool at all. This is a constraint to measure around, not a bug to fix."," ","-### 1. Brain's guide instructs agents to skip the tools","+**The measurement already exists and is usable.** `entire graph stats` computes","+`graph_first_rate = GraphFirstSessions / SessionsWithLocate`","+(`entire-graph/internal/cli/stats.go:1183-1189,1236`) from local Claude Code JSONL transcripts in","+`~/.claude/projects/<repo-slug>/` (`:374-386`), and `--sessions-dir` / `--transcript` override that","+path — which is what makes a clean-env arm measurable. Two caveats that change the design:"," ","-`internal/agentsetup/files.go:1-3` claims the package is \"mirrored byte-for-byte in both","-repositories\". It is not. entire-graph carries directive text; entire-brain still carries a","-permissive regression from 2026-09-14.","+- **MCP calls are invisible to it.** Only Bash `entire graph <verb>` / `entire-graph <verb>` count","+  as graph calls (`:1048-1055`); `mcp__entire-brain__*` matches neither bucket. Brain usage","+  therefore needs its own measure.","+- **Pin the binary.** The withdrawn \"82.9M tokens saved\" figure was binary-version drift","+  (`scripts/entire-graph-statusline.sh:115`), and the graph-first rate runs in the same binary."," ","-| entire-graph `guide.go:78-81` | entire-brain `guide.go:8-9`, `:31`, `:68` |","-|---|---|","-| \"Your FIRST action … **MUST** be ONE Graph query\" | \"**Directly inspect source** when the task already provides sufficient locations\" |","-| \"Do not skip the query on the grounds that the available context feels sufficient\" | \"**Skip ceremonial queries** for small edits and follow-up work\" |","-| | \"Useful locations from the brief do not require a redundant Graph query\" |","+The exploration could not find the provenance of the quoted `332 / 96,987 (0.34%)` baseline — it is","+only ever quoted, never derived. Treat it as context, not as this experiment's control."," ","-Claude's own transcript: *\"The agent guide says to start substantive tasks with `entire brain","-brief` and use Graph for code discovery. I skipped that.\"* It was following the guide it was given.","+### The two unknowns that decide everything"," ","-**`internal/agentsetup/coordination_test.go:137` and `scripts/test-agent-coordination.py:69`","-actively ban the strings `\"FIRST action\"` and `\"SEARCH FIRST\"`** — and the same test *requires*","-`\"sufficient locations\"` to be present. The permissive wording is enforced by CI in both","-directions. Verified directly, not taken from a report.","+Neither is answerable from source, and both are cheap to settle:"," ","-**Graph has already diagnosed and fixed this.** Its `coordination_test.go:142-145` says:","+1. **Does the model actually receive the guide** through `CLAUDE.md`'s `@.entire/agent-guide.md`","+   import? If not, every wording fix in #331 is inert.","+2. **Is `$CLAUDE_FILE_PATH` populated** in a `PreToolUse` hook? #331's wiring passes","+   `--file \"$CLAUDE_FILE_PATH\"`; if that variable is not set, the hook runs with an empty path and","+   **my own hook is a no-op.**"," ","-> *\"'FIRST action' and 'SEARCH FIRST' used to be banned here alongside those probes. They are not","-> probes; they are the directive that makes the product get used, and **banning them was benchmark","-> arm-fairness doctrine applied to shipped text.**\"*","+These run first, as two single sessions, before any arm."," ","-That is the root cause, and it is a good mistake: arm-fairness is correct for benchmarks — you","-cannot give one arm instructions the other lacks — and was then applied to the guide that ships to","-users, where there is no other arm. Graph's `guide.go:8` now reads \"TWO KINDS OF WORDING LIVE IN","-THIS PACKAGE, AND THEY MUST NOT BE UNIFIED\", and it added `TestNormalGuideStaysDirective`.","-","-So PR 3 is not reversing a deliberate product decision. It is **porting a fix graph already made","-and documented**, for a cause graph already named. Brain never caught up.","-","-Graph's guide (`guide.go:9-27`) states the measured cost: *\"332 graph calls against 96,987","-exploration calls (0.34%), and the graph-first rate was 0 in every session sampled.\"*","-","-### 2. The tools punish the agent that does comply","-","-From the Claude transcript, when finally instructed to run them:","-","-| tool | result |","-|---|---|","-| `brain_status` | Error: 124,295 chars — exceeds maximum allowed tokens |","-| `brain_brief` | Error: 125,822 chars — exceeds maximum allowed tokens |","-| `brain_impact` | Error: 61,580 chars — exceeds maximum allowed tokens |","-| `brain_entity_history` | `\"matches\": []` |","-| `brain_regressions` | `\"no code identifiers found\"`, `scanned_files: 0` |","-","-A context-saving tool that overflows context is worse than no tool. `mcp_response_budget.go:54`","-exists but is only a byte-budget *notice*.","-","-### 3. Warnings and failures are silently dropped","-","-A sweep found four HIGH instances of the class that has already cost this project repeatedly.","-Worst: `internal/cli/semantic.go:2380` — `FilterWarnings` drops any warning whose Detail merely","-*contains* a `.brainignore` pattern, by substring with no path parse. This repo's `.brainignore`","-line 1 is `entire-brain`, a substring of every absolute path in it, so **every index warning is","-discarded** and status reports a clean index that silently missed files.","-","-### Also confirmed","-","-- **Codex could not use Brain at all** — `entire` does not expose `brain`; it found the local","-  executable by accident. Packaging/discovery gap, separate from compliance.","-- **entire-graph ships no MCP server.** In an MCP-first harness the \"MUST run a Graph query\"","-  instruction names a tool the agent does not have. 37 `brain_*` tools exist; **zero** tool","-  descriptions mention grep, \"first\", \"instead of\" or \"before\".","-- **`hook pre-edit` already exists** (`internal/cli/hook_cmd.go`, shipped in merged PR #24) and","-  **nothing wires it**. Not in any settings template, not emitted by `init-agents`.","-- The nested `entire-brain/` clone degrades Graph's index:","-  `W_GIT_WORKTREE_FALLBACK: nested .git marker at \"entire-brain/.git\"`.","-"," ---"," ","-## Decisions, and why","+## Scope note: entire-graph is on hold"," ","-**Three stacked PRs, not one.** PR1 and PR2 both touch `semantic.go` and `distill_cmd.go`, so they","-genuinely conflict — stacking is correct here rather than cosmetic. Risk to accept: a stall in PR1","-blocks 2 and 3. Mitigation: PR1 is the smallest and most obviously correct.","+The decoy/ranking problem is the half that makes usage *persist* — 3 of 4 sessions used the tool","+exactly as instructed, got a decoy, and succeeded with grep instead. Two mechanisms are located:","+idf is computed over the preselected sample rather than the repo","+(`internal/sem/search.go:1376-1411,1495,3889`; one run indexed 384 of 1855 files,","+`preselection_confidence 0.0027`), and the stopword list (`:1027`) lacks \"decide\", \"whether\",","+\"needs\", \"rebuilding\" so they score against *names*, where signals dominate (`:4355`, `:4422`)."," ","-**Guide text before enforcement hook.** The guide currently says the opposite of what we want;","-changing text is free and addresses the cause. The hook is belt-and-braces and goes in the same","-PR, but we measure the guide change on its own first so we learn which one worked.","+A message has been sent to the `redesign-graph-cost-reduction` session asking whether this is","+already fixed or in flight, and who should own it. **No entire-graph file will be touched until it","+replies.** If it owns the fix, this plan measures against its branch; if it declines, adding a","+graph PR is a separate decision to bring back to you."," ","-**Port graph's fix rather than invent one.** I was ready to flag the directive-wording ban as","-needing the author's sign-off. Checking graph first showed it had already diagnosed the cause","-(arm-fairness doctrine applied to shipped text), fixed it, and left both the reasoning and a","-guard test behind. Copying a documented in-house fix beats re-deciding it.","-","-**Not in scope, recommended separately:** an MCP server for entire-graph. It is the structural","-reason the Graph instruction is unenforceable in Claude Code, but it is a build, not a fix.","-"," ---"," ","-## PR 1 — Retrieval returns usable output and reports what it dropped","+## Phase 1 — Harness (no model cost)"," ","-Bottom of the stack. Nothing above matters if the tools error or lie.","+Build under `~/.claude/jobs/<job>/tmp/cleanenv/`, nothing inside `devenv/`."," ","-**MCP response budget**","-- `internal/cli/mcp.go`, `internal/cli/mcp_response_budget.go` — enforce a real byte/token ceiling","-  on every `brain_*` response, not a notice. Truncate with an explicit, machine-readable marker","-  naming what was dropped and how to get it (`--json`, a path, a narrower query).","-- Worst offenders to verify: `brain_status`, `brain_brief`, `brain_impact`.","+- **Pinned binaries.** Build `entire-brain` from the stack tip (`fix/agent-guide-directive-and-discovery`)","+  and record the commit; use the installed `entire-graph` and record its version. Every arm uses","+  the same two binaries.","+- **One fresh clone per arm**, each with no `.entire/`, no `CLAUDE.md`, no `AGENTS.md`, so arms","+  cannot contaminate each other. `ENTIRE_REPO_ROOT` explicitly unset in every arm (it outranks cwd).","+- **Instrumentation, three independent channels** — because no single one sees everything:","+  | channel | catches | why needed |","+  |---|---|---|","+  | PATH shim logging every `entire` call with a run id | all Brain + Graph **CLI** calls, in order | the only ordered record of what the agent actually ran |","+  | `entire graph stats --sessions-dir <arm>` | `graph_first_rate`, graph calls, exploration calls | the project's own metric, so before/after is comparable |","+  | transcript grep for `mcp__entire-brain__` | Brain **MCP** usage | invisible to `graph stats` |","+- **Isolated transcript dir per arm** so `--sessions-dir` reads only that arm's sessions.","+- A fixed task set (6–8 locate/explain/change tasks) written once and reused verbatim across arms."," ","-**Status latency (#325)**","-- `internal/cli/verify_cmd.go:833` → `:424`, `internal/cli/agent_surface.go:1053` —","-  `populateBrainStatusVerification` runs `git for-each-ref --contains <commit>` per distinct anchor","-  commit, a full reachability walk. Gate verification behind `--details`; keep the summary cheap.","+## Phase 2 — Settle the two unknowns (2 sessions)"," ","-**The four HIGH silent-failure sites**","-- `semantic.go:2380`/`:2518` — `FilterWarnings` substring match against `.brainignore`. Parse paths;","-  never match on Detail text. Report a dropped-count.","-- `regression.go:316`/`:1224` — `SkipAll` at 20000 scanned / 400 seen with no warning, then prints","-  \"No suspected regressions (scanned N files)\". Emit a cap warning; correct the claim.","-- `export.go:3588`,`:3619`/`:382` — `usefulExportWarnings` drops `checkpoint snapshot unavailable:`","-  unless `--debug`, and the reported `warnings: %d` counts the filtered set.","-- `distill_cmd.go:79` `capWarnings` — cap of 50 applied *before* persisting to the manifest, so the","-  dropped text exists nowhere. Persist all; cap only the display.","+- **Probe A:** `claude -p \"quote the sentence in your instructions about your FIRST action\"` with cwd","+  in an `init-agents`-installed clone. Establishes whether the `@` import reaches the model.","+- **Probe B:** a session told to edit one file; check the shim log for a `hook pre-edit --file <path>`","+  call with a **non-empty** path. Establishes whether `$CLAUDE_FILE_PATH` works."," ","-**Truncated user-facing messages** (`status_render.go:264`, `statusCauseWidth=140`, byte-based)","-- `semantic_stream.go:518` (182 chars), `semantic.go:1783` (173, still unfixed on main),","-  `semantic.go:6720` (147). Shorten the strings; make truncation rune-aware.","+If Probe A fails, the fix is to inline the directive into `CLAUDE.md` rather than import it, and","+everything downstream re-runs. If Probe B fails, #331's hook wiring is corrected before the arms run."," ","-## PR 2 — Multi-agent safety, indexing, and Windows","+## Phase 3 — Arms, pre-registered"," ","-**#326 — `brain brief` takes `.git/index.lock`**","-- `internal/cli/git_harden.go:78-81` is the single git spawn point and injects no","-  `--no-optional-locks`. Add it there; swap `git diff --shortstat HEAD` → `diff-index`.","-  Call sites: `semantic.go:2613`,`:2617`,`:5022`, `agent_surface.go:4768`.","+Three arms, **n ≥ 10 sessions each**, same tasks, same binaries, fresh clone per arm:"," ","-**#327 — indexing stalls on a dirty worktree**","-- `semantic.go:575` + `refresh.go:795-796`: dirty && !`--worktree` → `dirty_worktree` error, and","-  needs-rebuild returns true unconditionally on dirty, so every refresh hits the refusal.","-  `watch.go:305-309` aborts the whole tick, so the cursor never advances. Index HEAD via a temp","-  tree; let watch skip only the semantic step. Same shape at `seed.go:276`.","+- **A0 — no guide.** `setup` only, no `init-agents`. The true baseline.","+- **A1 — guide only.** `init-agents`, hook entry removed from `.claude/settings.json`.","+- **A2 — guide + hook.** Full `init-agents`. Isolates whether wording alone sufficed."," ","-**#328 — Ollama is loopback-only and never auto-selected**","-- `refresh.go:829-840` `defaultRefreshAgent` tries codex→claude→none with ollama absent;","-  `distill_cmd.go:2349` rejects a non-loopback `ENTIRE_BRAIN_OLLAMA_URL` **silently**;","-  `watch.go:110` hardcodes `\"codex\"`; `embed.go:300` repeats the pattern.","-  Add an opt-in remote host, add ollama to the auto order, and **warn loudly when a configured URL","-  is ignored** — silent fallback to a cloud agent is the privacy bug in the report.","+**Pre-registered bar, fixed before the first session runs:**"," ","-**#322 — Windows \"command line is too long\"**","-- `distill.go:137`, exec at `distill_cmd.go:2237`: argv ends `\"--system-prompt\", <7516-byte","-  prompt>`, blowing cmd.exe's 8191 limit. The chunk is already on stdin. Move the prompt to stdin","-  or a temp file. ~15 callers share `distillAgentCommandArgs` (`seed.go:1830`, `facts_eval`,","-  `facts_write_cmd`, `pattern_*`) — fix at the shared builder.","-- **Verification limit, stated up front:** I cannot run Windows here. The test asserts the prompt","-  is not on argv and that total argv stays under 8191, which is deterministic on any platform.","+| metric | A0 expectation | pass condition for A1 |","+|---|---|---|","+| sessions with ≥1 Graph or Brain call | low | **≥ 9/10** |","+| `graph_first_rate` | ~0 | **≥ 0.7** |","+| sessions that used a tool then abandoned it for grep | — | **≤ 3/10** |"," ","-**#324 — `facts promote --keep-both` queues confidence-0 proposals**","-- `internal/factmerge/admin.go:128` emits `Proposal{Action: ActionSupersede, Confidence: 0}` as a","-  literal, with no similarity ever computed, once per same-path target — quadratic fanout.","-  Compute similarity, or do not queue when confidence is 0. Callers: `factsync/sync.go:118`,","-  `facts_sync_cmd.go`, `facts_admin_cmd.go`.","+n=10 per arm is adequate *for an effect this large* — 0/10 vs 7/10 is Fisher exact p < 0.001 — and","+is not adequate for a small one. If the observed effect is small, the honest outcome is \"not","+established at this n\", not a wider search for a subgroup that worked."," ","-## PR 3 — The guide, the hook, and discovery","+The third row is the one that matters most and the one the earlier run exposed: first-call","+compliance can rise while sustained usage stays flat."," ","-**Restore directive wording in brain's guide — port graph's fix**","-- `internal/agentsetup/guide.go:8-9`,`:31`,`:68`,`:11-12` — align with entire-graph's text,","-  including its `guide.go:8` header comment explaining why the two wordings must not be unified.","-- `coordination_test.go:137` — remove `\"FIRST action\"`/`\"SEARCH FIRST\"` from the `bad` list and","-  `\"sufficient locations\"` from the `want` list, keeping the genuine runtime-probe bans","-  (`entire plugin list`, `command -v`, `setup.json`). Carry over graph's explanatory comment.","-- Add brain's equivalent of `TestNormalGuideStaysDirective` so the regression cannot recur.","-- `scripts/test-agent-coordination.py:69` — same ban, same change.","+## Phase 4 — Ask every session what went wrong"," ","-**#323 — the guide names a command that does not exist**","-- `guide.go:33`,`:74`, `strict.go:66` hardcode `entire graph query`; entire-graph v0.4.0 dispatch","-  has only `case \"search\"` (`query` lands in unreleased 0.5.0). Emit `search`, or probe","-  `graph capabilities --json`. Same stale text at `docs/agent-coordination.md:107`.","+After each task, a follow-up turn in the same session: what was your first action, did you reach","+for Brain or Graph, if not why not, what did the tool return, was it useful, what would have made","+you use it. Collected verbatim."," ","-**Wire the hook that already exists**","-- `internal/cli/hook_cmd.go` (`hook pre-edit`, `hook post-failure`) is registered hidden at","-  `root.go:169` and wired nowhere. Emit the `PreToolUse` wiring from `init-agents` so it lands in","-  `.claude/settings.json` alongside the guide. Existing `PreToolUse` entries use","-  `\"matcher\": \"Agent\"` only; this needs a Bash/Grep/Read matcher.","+This is the highest-yield channel available — it is what exposed the root cause in the first place","+(\"The agent guide says to start substantive tasks with `entire brain brief`… I skipped that\"). It is","+also self-report, so it is used to *find* mechanisms, never to score the arms; scoring comes from","+the three instrumented channels only."," ","-**MCP tool descriptions**","-- `mcp.go:805-1030`, 37 tools. None say when to use the tool *instead of* grep. The description is","-  what an agent reads when choosing; the guide is a file it may never open.","+## Phase 5 — Loop"," ","-**In-repo docs**","-- `README.md` — move the \"What to ask\" table (currently line 124 of 362) near the top and drop the","-  Brain-command column, per Joseph's feedback. Fix its `query`→`recall` verbs for decision","-  questions.","-- `docs/agent-coordination.md:107` — stale `entire graph query`.","+Each round: read the feedback, find the top blocker, fix it in the stack (brain side) or hand it to","+the graph session, re-run the affected arm, re-check against the same pre-registered bar. Stop when","+A1 or A2 clears the bar on a round where no new blocker class appeared, or when a round produces a","+blocker that is a product decision rather than a defect — which comes back to you rather than","+getting guessed."," ","+**Candidate blockers already identified**, to check rather than assume: the `@`-import path (Probe A);","+`$CLAUDE_FILE_PATH` (Probe B); brain-only installs getting no Graph directive (`guide.go:128,130`);","+`ENTIRE_REPO_ROOT` mis-targeting; and MCP-first sessions having no Graph route at all, which no","+wording can fix.","+"," ---"," ","-## Docs that are NOT in this repo","+## Cost, stated up front"," ","-These live on the docs site, so they cannot be part of these PRs. They ship as a change list plus","-an artifact (below), for whoever owns the site.","+Roughly 32+ real `claude -p` sessions (2 probes + 3 arms × 10) plus a feedback turn each, at a","+locate task's typical size. Order of a few million tokens per full round, and the loop may need more","+than one round. Sonnet, small tasks, and arms re-run individually rather than all three each time.","+Say the word if you want a smaller first round — 5 per arm would still separate 0 from 0.7."," ","-| Page | Fix |","-|---|---|","-| Continuous Agent Memory | **\"up to 71%\" is a retracted figure** — that instance had the graph arm silently falling back to grep on a zero-byte payload and a 452-word stripped baseline. Replace with cost +2.49% (CI [−6.83, +11.18]) or drop the number. |","-| Continuous Agent Memory | `entire/agent-guide.md` → `.entire/agent-guide.md` (leading dot) |","-| Continuous Agent Memory | `entire graph stats --repo` errors without a value — drop the flag |","-| Continuous Agent Memory | Remove the `entire graph stats` recommendation (reported 82.9M saved vs an honest ~46k) |","-| Continuous Agent Memory | The rerun instruction is prose; make it a code block |","-| Overview | **Add `entire brain init-agents` to the setup section** — `setup` never writes AGENTS.md/CLAUDE.md, which is why Joseph saw nothing even from the repo root |","-| Overview | \"From your repository's root\" → \"…not from a cloned `entire-brain` directory\" |","-| Overview | `query` → `recall` for the decision example; document that facts are branch-scoped |","-| Overview + Use Cases | Copy fixes: \"For example,you can move\"; \"lessons that **has**\"; the run-on \"…and make sure to commit…\" |","-| Use Cases | `inspect impact --symbol X` **errors** (`unknown flag: --symbol`) — it is positional |","-| All | Confirm the \"CLI 0.10.0 or later\" floor; no version gate exists in brain's source |","-","-**Deliverable:** a two-tab artifact — tab 1 every problem with evidence and severity, tab 2 the","-corrected pages as they should read.","-","----","-"," ## Verification"," ","-Each fix gets a reproduction that fails before and passes after. Mutation-verified: patch the","-guard, prove the test goes red (`verified-by-weakening`).","+The deliverable is not \"the tests pass\" — it is a number against a bar fixed in advance:"," ","-| Fix | Reproduction |","-|---|---|","-| MCP budget | Call `brain_status`/`brain_brief`/`brain_impact` against a large repo; assert every response is under the cap and carries a dropped-marker |","-| #325 | Brain with ~250 facts; assert `status --json` under a wall-clock threshold; assert `--details` still verifies |","-| FilterWarnings | `.brainignore` containing a string that is a substring of an absolute path; assert warnings survive |","-| regression cap | Corpus over 20000 files; assert a cap warning appears and the \"no regressions\" claim is qualified |","-| export/capWarnings | Assert dropped warnings are persisted and recoverable |","-| #326 | Hold a `brain brief` while running `git status` concurrently; assert no lock error. Deterministic form: assert `--no-optional-locks` in the spawn args |","-| #327 | Dirty worktree + commit + refresh; assert the index advances rather than refusing |","-| #328 | Non-loopback `ENTIRE_BRAIN_OLLAMA_URL`; assert a loud warning, and that opt-in remote works |","-| #322 | Assert the prompt is not on argv and total argv < 8191 (platform-independent) |","-| #324 | `promote --keep-both` over same-path facts; assert no confidence-0 proposals and no quadratic fanout |","-| Guide | Assert the generated guide contains the directive sentence and names only commands the installed graph exposes |","+1. Phase 2 probes answered yes/no with the evidence inline.","+2. A table of A0 / A1 / A2 on all three metrics, with counts beside every rate and the exact","+   commands and binary versions that produced them.","+3. Every fix made during the loop carries a regression test verified by weakening — guard patched","+   compile-clean, test shown red, assertion quoted.","+4. The verbatim feedback, including anything that contradicts the result.","+5. If the bar is not cleared, that is reported as the finding, with what remains unfixed. A result","+   that says \"usage did not improve\" is a successful execution of this plan."," ","-**Loop:** run the full `internal/...` suite under `-race` (CI runs `-race`; local darwin does not),","-re-run each reproduction, repeat until two consecutive passes find nothing new. One suite at a","-time — concurrent runs contend over the global brain data dir and produce false failures.","-","-### The usage experiment (the deeper ask)","-","-`entire graph stats` already computes a **graph-first rate**, and graph's guide records the","-baseline: 0.34% of calls, graph-first rate 0 in every session sampled.","-","-1. Measure the baseline on a repo with the current permissive guide.","-2. Install the corrected guide. Run a fleet of subagents on real tasks (locate, impact, \"why did","-   we\"), each in its own worktree.","-3. Re-measure graph-first rate.","-4. Then enable the hook and measure again — so we learn whether wording alone was enough.","-5. Collect each agent's own account of why it did or did not reach for the tool. That self-report","-   is what exposed cause #1; it is the highest-yield signal we have.","-","----","-","-## Sequencing","-","-1. PR 1 — retrieval correctness (smallest, most obviously right, unblocks the stack)","-2. PR 2 — multi-agent safety, indexing, Windows","-3. PR 3 — guide, hook, discovery, in-repo docs","-4. Docs artifact for the off-repo pages","-5. Usage experiment, reported with before/after graph-first rate","-","-Nothing merges without approval.","-","-## Recommended, but not in these PRs","-","-**An MCP server for entire-graph.** Brain ships 37 `brain_*` MCP tools; graph ships none. In","-Claude Code the guide's \"MUST run a Graph query\" names a tool the agent does not have, so the","-directive is unenforceable in the harness most users are in. This is the structural half of the","-usage problem and the guide fix will only partly land without it. It is a build, not a fix, and","-wants its own decision.","-","-**Deferred with reasons, say the word to include:** nothing — all seven filed issues are in scope.","-The only stated verification limit is #322, which cannot be executed on macOS; its test is","-platform-independent but a real Windows run should confirm before closing the issue.","+Nothing merges without your approval; PRs #329–#331 stay unmerged and this work stacks on #331."]}],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6d99bd86-04c0-41df-917f-abac0b533ddf","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"9f834e96-0d0b-4a36-bc93-e1926425c141","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"queued_command","prompt":"<cross-session-message from=\"uds:/tmp/cc-socks/12017.sock\" from-name=\"redesign-graph-cost-reduction\" from-mode=\"prompting\">\nRanking answer: mechanism 1 (sample idf) is fixed but unmerged; mechanism 2 (name dominance) is diagnosed, not fixed. Please don't take either into entire-graph yet.\n\n(1) idf over the preselected sample: FIXED on an unmerged branch.\n- Fix: PR #291 (repo-wide idf). It is also inside the launch-candidate stack: #315 at dd76b8fe, and 0d92152d (#315 plus #316), via the 8-patch port chain 7a372859..873896b0. range-diff is 8/8 '='.\n- Behaviour: searchChooseIDFStatistics (sem/search.go:~4012 at 0d92) uses exact repo-wide DF when an exact corpus is known: small repo, warm git-tree-grep, or a complete cold content pass with no read failures. Otherwise it falls back to the sample.\n- Your line numbers (:1376-1411, :1495, :3889) look like an older build without it.\n- Please re-measure your exact query with the frozen launch binary before concluding anything: /Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/pilot8-artifacts/static/bin/entire-graph-0d92152d (sha256 09f393fe…, vcs.revision 0d92152d). Use the same flags, plus --format json so you can see which idf source and stats it used.\n\n(2) Stopwords and name-signal dominance: DIAGNOSED, NOT FIXED, and deliberately not being patched ad hoc.\n- searchNameCoverageWeight=10 (search.go:4531 at 0d92) is intentionally not idf-weighted (comment cites hugo#12171).\n- Our post-hoc study-6 analysis found the name gap in 25/66 ranking misses vs 16/123 hits.\n- In a scoring emulator, weight 0 rescued 6 misses and lost 0 hits. That is emulator evidence only.\n- The planned test is \"study 7\": a free offline prereg with arms F2Z (weight 0) and F2I (idf-weighted name coverage), on 12 fresh repos with a paraphrase stratum. The paper is closed by Codex review but not yet run.\n- I haven't looked at expanding the stopword list. Note, though, that \"decide/whether/needs\" are not universally inert in code, so it needs the same eval treatment.\n\nOwnership: Codex holds the Go lease on entire-graph, and ranking changes go through the study-7 prereg so they're measured on held-out repos rather than tuned to single cases. So please don't take (2) as a code change.\n\nWhat would help most:\n- Re-run with 0d92 and send me the top-5 with scores.\n- Keep your decoy query OUT of any tuning set. It is a perfect example of the paraphrase failure, and it should go into an evaluation set only if it's held out.\n- If you want, file it on GitHub as an issue on entireio/entire-graph with the repro (repo, commit, query, expected deciders). That's safe and doesn't collide with anything.\n\nI'm currently busy with the pilot8 token A/B harness (graphmark), not ranking.\n</cross-session-message>","source_uuid":"2bfe8214-0496-449c-a413-2151dbe764db","delivery_id":"16a6dd96-b1ff-41fa-9f2e-2f1c8ee2dc94","commandMode":"prompt","origin":{"kind":"peer","from":"uds:/tmp/cc-socks/12017.sock","verifiedPeerPid":12017,"msg_id":"f951c66d-a5f7-4208-8e22-eafd3f3c7216","name":"redesign-graph-cost-reduction","hopChain":["70e3193bf23ede08d799538f"],"fromMode":"prompting","body":"Ranking answer: mechanism 1 (sample idf) is fixed but unmerged; mechanism 2 (name dominance) is diagnosed, not fixed. Please don't take either into entire-graph yet.\n\n(1) idf over the preselected sample: FIXED on an unmerged branch.\n- Fix: PR #291 (repo-wide idf). It is also inside the launch-candidate stack: #315 at dd76b8fe, and 0d92152d (#315 plus #316), via the 8-patch port chain 7a372859..873896b0. range-diff is 8/8 '='.\n- Behaviour: searchChooseIDFStatistics (sem/search.go:~4012 at 0d92) uses exact repo-wide DF when an exact corpus is known: small repo, warm git-tree-grep, or a complete cold content pass with no read failures. Otherwise it falls back to the sample.\n- Your line numbers (:1376-1411, :1495, :3889) look like