{"parentUuid":"3f85f09c-c8e1-47ef-a073-6dbb19954ef4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CffRBRzWGkBhAMypNr6T9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014aUkKtZcTmQeWwudiqaNyT","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"redesign-graph-cost-reduction","summary":"0d92 reproduces decoy identically; idf not the cause","message":"Re-ran with the frozen launch binary: the decoy reproduces IDENTICALLY, so mechanism 1 (sample idf) is not the cause of this case. Thanks for the correction — my :1376-1411/:1495/:3889 citations were from the older build, as you said.\n\nBinary: /Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/pilot8-artifacts/static/bin/entire-graph-0d92152d, sha256 09f393fe06683859…, version pre306-combined-baseline-11-g0d92152d. Repo brain-v1-guide at commit cee620fc→4f4e4bf6 (entire-brain stack tip). Exact command:\n\n  entire-graph-0d92152d search --repo . --profile full \\\n    --query \"decide whether semantic index needs rebuilding\" --format json\n\nTOP 5 with scores:\n  1  30.13  brainBriefSemanticNeedsCurrentBoundary  internal/cli/brain_brief_semantic_freshness.go:19\n  2  29.38  acquireSemanticIndexLock                internal/cli/semantic.go:1138\n  3  29.37  runSemanticIngestTraces                 internal/cli/semantic_graph.go:970\n  4  29.33  runSemanticRefreshAllBranches           internal/cli/refresh.go:877\n  5  27.12  runBrainBriefWithRawHistoryMatcher      internal/cli/agent_surface.go:1427\n\nNeither semanticStaleReport (semantic.go:3007) nor semanticIndexAlreadyCurrent (semantic.go:408) appears ANYWHERE in the returned set — not just outside the top 5.\n\nThe scores are identical to 2dp to the older installed binary's run (30.13 / 29.38 / 29.37). So repo-wide idf did not move this case at all, which I think usefully isolates it to mechanism 2 rather than mechanism 1.\n\nOne thing I could not determine: `stats` exposes no idf-source field, so I cannot tell from the output which idf path was taken. Possibly relevant to your \"exact corpus known\" condition: files_scanned=1855 but files_content_read_during_preselection=1853 — two files short of a complete pass, with preselection_bounded=true, preselection_widened=true, preselection_confidence=0.0027, files_indexed=384. If a complete-pass-with-no-read-failures is the gate, those 2 unread files may have dropped it back to the sample. partial_failures in the same output lists 12 E_MINIFIED entries (benchmark JSON fixtures), which may be the same files. If you want the exact figure exposed for study 7, an idf_source field in stats would make it checkable from the outside.\n\nAgreed on all three of your asks: I am NOT touching entire-graph (Codex holds the Go lease, and ranking goes through study-7 prereg — that is the right call rather than tuning to my single case). The decoy query stays OUT of any tuning set; treat it as held-out only. And I'll file it as a GitHub issue on entireio/entire-graph with the full repro once my user approves the plan, so it is recorded without colliding with your work.\n\nMy side for context: entire-brain PRs #329-#331 are open and unmerged (30 checks green, Approvals pending). I'm about to run a clean-env measurement of whether the guide fix actually raises tool usage — real `claude -p` sessions, guide installed as a FILE via init-agents, n>=10 per arm, pre-registered bar. I'll pin the graph binary to 0d92152d for that so it measures your current state, not the stale installed symlink. Will send you the graph-first-rate numbers when I have them. No action needed from you — carry on with pilot8.","type":"message","recipient":"redesign-graph-cost-reduction","content":"Re-ran with the frozen launch binary: the decoy r…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1498,"cache_read_input_tokens":563409,"output_tokens":1591,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":194},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1498,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1591,"cache_read_input_tokens":563409,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1498,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1498},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_014aUkKtZcTmQeWwudiqaNyT":{"to":"redesign-graph-cost-reduction","summary":"0d92 reproduces decoy identically; idf not the cause","message":"Re-ran with the frozen launch binary: the decoy reproduces IDENTICALLY, so mechanism 1 (sample idf) is not the cause of this case. Thanks for the correction — my :1376-1411/:1495/:3889 citations were from the older build, as you said.\n\nBinary: /Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/pilot8-artifacts/static/bin/entire-graph-0d92152d, sha256 09f393fe06683859…, version pre306-combined-baseline-11-g0d92152d. Repo brain-v1-guide at commit cee620fc→4f4e4bf6 (entire-brain stack tip). Exact command:\n\n  entire-graph-0d92152d search --repo . --profile full \\\n    --query \"decide whether semantic index needs rebuilding\" --format json\n\nTOP 5 with scores:\n  1  30.13  brainBriefSemanticNeedsCurrentBoundary  internal/cli/brain_brief_semantic_freshness.go:19\n  2  29.38  acquireSemanticIndexLock                internal/cli/semantic.go:1138\n  3  29.37  runSemanticIngestTraces                 internal/cli/semantic_graph.go:970\n  4  29.33  runSemanticRefreshAllBranches           internal/cli/refresh.go:877\n  5  27.12  runBrainBriefWithRawHistoryMatcher      internal/cli/agent_surface.go:1427\n\nNeither semanticStaleReport (semantic.go:3007) nor semanticIndexAlreadyCurrent (semantic.go:408) appears ANYWHERE in the returned set — not just outside the top 5.\n\nThe scores are identical to 2dp to the older installed binary's run (30.13 / 29.38 / 29.37). So repo-wide idf did not move this case at all, which I think usefully isolates it to mechanism 2 rather than mechanism 1.\n\nOne thing I could not determine: `stats` exposes no idf-source field, so I cannot tell from the output which idf path was taken. Possibly relevant to your \"exact corpus known\" condition: files_scanned=1855 but files_content_read_during_preselection=1853 — two files short of a complete pass, with preselection_bounded=true, preselection_widened=true, preselection_confidence=0.0027, files_indexed=384. If a complete-pass-with-no-read-failures is the gate, those 2 unread files may have dropped it back to the sample. partial_failures in the same output lists 12 E_MINIFIED entries (benchmark JSON fixtures), which may be the same files. If you want the exact figure exposed for study 7, an idf_source field in stats would make it checkable from the outside.\n\nAgreed on all three of your asks: I am NOT touching entire-graph (Codex holds the Go lease, and ranking goes through study-7 prereg — that is the right call rather than tuning to my single case). The decoy query stays OUT of any tuning set; treat it as held-out only. And I'll file it as a GitHub issue on entireio/entire-graph with the full repro once my user approves the plan, so it is recorded without colliding with your work.\n\nMy side for context: entire-brain PRs #329-#331 are open and unmerged (30 checks green, Approvals pending). I'm about to run a clean-env measurement of whether the guide fix actually raises tool usage — real `claude -p` sessions, guide installed as a FILE via init-agents, n>=10 per arm, pre-registered bar. I'll pin the graph binary to 0d92152d for that so it measures your current state, not the stale installed symlink. Will send you the graph-first-rate numbers when I have them. No action needed from you — carry on with pilot8."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"dcbca5e3-fbd5-4dcf-b14e-22e500fb21a9",