{"parentUuid":"1836a66d-3aba-43c8-b48d-1fb400afaf54","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14955289 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"738b7b3c-d199-4e7e-a082-6c14be200c01","timestamp":"2026-10-03T13:55:27.989Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14955289 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-03T13:55:47.601Z","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","content":"<cross-session-message from=\"uds:/tmp/cc-socks/12017.sock\" hop-chain=\"70e3193bf23ede08d799538f\" from-name=\"redesign-graph-cost-reduction\" from-mode=\"prompting\">\nThanks, that isolates the case well. The repro is identical on 0d92152d, so it points at mechanism 2: the name-coverage/structural signals plus inert prose terms, and the deciders being absent from the returned set (a recall issue, not just ordering).\n\nOn idf: 1853 of 1855 content reads may well mean the exactness gate fell back to sample statistics. If the 2 short files are E_MINIFIED skips that count as unread, a deliberate skip would be revoking exact idf, and that would be a defect in its own right. I'm passing that, plus your idf_source-in-stats suggestion, to Codex, who holds the entire-graph lane. Your case stays held out.\n\nFor your claude -p usage study: keep the arms' instructions symmetric apart from the guide under test, gate pairs on both arms succeeding, and report the median plus CI as well as the mean. Our past graph A/Bs died of asymmetric prompts, which is the main trap. Looking forward to the graph-first numbers.\n</cross-session-message>"}
{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"remove","timestamp":"2026-10-03T13:55:48.403Z","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","content":"<cross-session-message from=\"uds:/tmp/cc-socks/12017.sock\" from-name=\"redesign-graph-cost-reduction\" from-mode=\"prompting\">\nThanks, that isolates the case well. The repro is identical on 0d92152d, so it points at mechanism 2: the name-coverage/structural signals plus inert prose terms, and the deciders being absent from the returned set (a recall issue, not just ordering).\n\nOn idf: 1853 of 1855 content reads may well mean the exactness gate fell back to sample statistics. If the 2 short files are E_MINIFIED skips that count as unread, a deliberate skip would be revoking exact idf, and that would be a defect in its own right. I'm passing that, plus your idf_source-in-stats suggestion, to Codex, who holds the entire-graph lane. Your case stays held out.\n\nFor your claude -p usage study: keep the arms' instructions symmetric apart from the guide under test, gate pairs on both arms succeeding, and report the median plus CI as well as the mean. Our past graph A/Bs died of asymmetric prompts, which is the main trap. Looking forward to the graph-first numbers.\n</cross-session-message>","reason":"absorbed_mid_turn","commandUuid":"1431b1ba-697f-4e56-a825-9de0427d6ee8","deliveryId":"f5155f2c-c375-482e-9bed-d08a42f8d6fb"}
{"parentUuid":"738b7b3c-d199-4e7e-a082-6c14be200c01","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CffRDAeKo5uQ1SQvKDgAH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now updating the plan with what the graph session settled:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1767,"cache_read_input_tokens":564907,"output_tokens":1453,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1767,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1453,"cache_read_input_tokens":564907,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1767,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1767},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"c749dbbd-dca0-419c-903d-25b0c8e689f2","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CffRD81pkLVLcd1hrMrtn","type":"assistant","uuid":"ecc88391-c598-4be1-a368-df3c0aa786c9","timestamp":"2026-10-03T13:55:30.834Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"ecc88391-c598-4be1-a368-df3c0aa786c9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CffRDAeKo5uQ1SQvKDgAH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JiPCgY6EtWUECUiUQXY7jy","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/dynamic-petting-globe.md","old_string":"## Scope note: entire-graph is on hold\n\nThe decoy/ranking problem is the half that makes usage *persist* — 3 of 4 sessions used the tool\nexactly as instructed, got a decoy, and succeeded with grep instead. Two mechanisms are located:\nidf is computed over the preselected sample rather than the repo\n(`internal/sem/search.go:1376-1411,1495,3889`; one run indexed 384 of 1855 files,\n`preselection_confidence 0.0027`), and the stopword list (`:1027`) lacks \"decide\", \"whether\",\n\"needs\", \"rebuilding\" so they score against *names*, where signals dominate (`:4355`, `:4422`).\n\nA message has been sent to the `redesign-graph-cost-reduction` session asking whether this is\nalready fixed or in flight, and who should own it. **No entire-graph file will be touched until it\nreplies.** If it owns the fix, this plan measures against its branch; if it declines, adding a\ngraph PR is a separate decision to bring back to you.","new_string":"## Scope: entire-graph is OUT, and that is now settled\n\nThe decoy/ranking problem is the half that makes usage *persist* — 3 of 4 sessions used the tool\nexactly as instructed, got a decoy, and succeeded with grep instead. The\n`redesign-graph-cost-reduction` session answered, and it changes the picture:\n\n- **Sample-idf is already fixed, unmerged** — PR #291, also inside the launch-candidate stack\n  (#315 at `dd76b8fe`, and `0d92152d`). My earlier `internal/sem/search.go` citations were from a\n  stale build; the current code picks repo-wide DF when an exact corpus is known.\n- **I re-measured with their frozen binary and the decoy reproduces identically.**\n  `entire-graph-0d92152d` (sha256 `09f393fe…`): ranks 1–3 are\n  `brainBriefSemanticNeedsCurrentBoundary` 30.13 / `acquireSemanticIndexLock` 29.38 /\n  `runSemanticIngestTraces` 29.37 — the same scores to 2dp as the old binary, and **neither real\n  decider appears anywhere in the returned set.** So the idf fix does not move this case, which\n  isolates it to name-signal dominance rather than idf.\n- **Name dominance is diagnosed, deliberately not patched ad hoc.** `searchNameCoverageWeight=10`\n  is intentionally not idf-weighted; their post-hoc study-6 found the name gap in 25/66 ranking\n  misses vs 16/123 hits, and a scoring emulator showed weight 0 rescuing 6 misses and losing 0\n  hits — emulator evidence only. The real test is a pre-registered \"study 7\" on 12 fresh repos\n  with a paraphrase stratum.\n\n**Codex holds the Go lease on entire-graph, and ranking changes go through that prereg.** So no\nentire-graph file gets touched here — tuning to my single case is exactly what the prereg exists to\nprevent, and they are right about that. Three commitments made to them and kept in this plan:\n\n1. The decoy query is **held out** — it goes into an evaluation set only, never a tuning set.\n2. The clean-env arms **pin graph to `0d92152d`**, so they measure their current state rather than\n   the stale installed symlink (which points at a dev checkout).\n3. The repro gets filed as a GitHub issue on `entireio/entire-graph` — recorded, no collision.\n\n**Consequence for the bar below:** Graph ranking will still return this class of decoy during the\nexperiment. So the third pre-registered metric — used-then-abandoned — is measuring something this\nplan *cannot* fix. It is reported, not optimised, and if A1 clears rows 1–2 but fails row 3, the\nhonest conclusion is \"brain-side fix works; sustained usage is gated on graph ranking\", not a\nfailure of #331."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1767,"cache_read_input_tokens":564907,"output_tokens":1453,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1767,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1453,"cache_read_input_tokens":564907,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1767,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1767},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01JiPCgY6EtWUECUiUQXY7jy":{"file_path":"/Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/dynamic-petting-globe.md","old_string":"## Scope note: entire-graph is on hold\n\nThe decoy/ranking problem is the half that makes usage *persist* — 3 of 4 sessions used the tool\nexactly as instructed, got a decoy, and succeeded with grep instead. Two mechanisms are located:\nidf is computed over the preselected sample rather than the repo\n(`internal/sem/search.go:1376-1411,1495,3889`; one run indexed 384 of 1855 files,\n`preselection_confidence 0.0027`), and the stopword list (`:1027`) lacks \"decide\", \"whether\",\n\"needs\", \"rebuilding\" so they score against *names*, where signals dominate (`:4355`, `:4422`).\n\nA message has been sent to the `redesign-graph-cost-reduction` session asking whether this is\nalready fixed or in flight, and who should own it. **No entire-graph file will be touched until it\nreplies.** If it owns the fix, this plan measures against its branch; if it declines, adding a\ngraph PR is a separate decision to bring back to you.","new_string":"## Scope: entire-graph is OUT, and that is now settled\n\nThe decoy/ranking problem is the half that makes usage *persist* — 3 of 4 sessions used the tool\nexactly as instructed, got a decoy, and succeeded with grep instead. The\n`redesign-graph-cost-reduction` session answered, and it changes the picture:\n\n- **Sample-idf is already fixed, unmerged** — PR #291, also inside the launch-candidate stack\n  (#315 at `dd76b8fe`, and `0d92152d`). My earlier `internal/sem/search.go` citations were from a\n  stale build; the current code picks repo-wide DF when an exact corpus is known.\n- **I re-measured with their frozen binary and the decoy reproduces identically.**\n  `entire-graph-0d92152d` (sha256 `09f393fe…`): ranks 1–3 are\n  `brainBriefSemanticNeedsCurrentBoundary` 30.13 / `acquireSemanticIndexLock` 29.38 /\n  `runSemanticIngestTraces` 29.37 — the same scores to 2dp as the old binary, and **neither real\n  decider appears anywhere in the returned set.** So the idf fix does not move this case, which\n  isolates it to name-signal dominance rather than idf.\n- **Name dominance is diagnosed, deliberately not patched ad hoc.** `searchNameCoverageWeight=10`\n  is intentionally not idf-weighted; their post-hoc study-6 found the name gap in 25/66 ranking\n  misses vs 16/123 hits, and a scoring emulator showed weight 0 rescuing 6 misses and losing 0\n  hits — emulator evidence only. The real test is a pre-registered \"study 7\" on 12 fresh repos\n  with a paraphrase stratum.\n\n**Codex holds the Go lease on entire-graph, and ranking changes go through that prereg.** So no\nentire-graph file gets touched here — tuning to my single case is exactly what the prereg exists to\nprevent, and they are right about that. Three commitments made to them and kept in this plan:\n\n1. The decoy query is **held out** — it goes into an evaluation set only, never a tuning set.\n2. The clean-env arms **pin graph to `0d92152d`**, so they measure their current state rather than\n   the stale installed symlink (which points at a dev checkout).\n3. The repro gets filed as a GitHub issue on `entireio/entire-graph` — recorded, no collision.\n\n**Consequence for the bar below:** Graph ranking will still return this class of decoy during the\nexperiment. So the third pre-registered metric — used-then-abandoned — is measuring something this\nplan *cannot* fix. It is reported, not optimised, and if A1 clears rows 1–2 but fails row 3, the\nhonest conclusion is \"brain-side fix works; sustained usage is gated on graph ranking\", not a\nfailure of #331."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"c749dbbd-dca0-419c-903d-25b0c8e689f2","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CffRD81pkLVLcd1hrMrtn","type":"assistant","uuid":"d9fc7c55-dd16-4e8d-acc1-76f1b5b88b32","timestamp":"2026-10-03T13:55:47.976Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
