{"type":"pr-link","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","prNumber":330,"prUrl":"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/330","prRepository":"entireio/entire-brain","timestamp":"2026-10-03T13:56:32.961Z"}
{"parentUuid":"85421ed5-843b-4b8f-97aa-ae2e855fd65b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CffRH2eUp3buxm4LDd3RT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The plan is ready. Three things shifted materially while writing it:\n\n**The graph half is settled, and not mine.** I asked the `redesign-graph-cost-reduction` session directly, as you suggested. Its answer corrected me: the sample-idf defect I cited is **already fixed on an unmerged branch** (PR #291, inside the #315 stack), and my line numbers were from a stale build. I re-measured with their frozen binary — the decoy reproduces **identically**, same scores to 2dp. So idf isn't the cause here. Their follow-up sharpened it again: the real deciders are *absent from the returned set entirely*, which makes it a **recall** failure, not an ordering one — no reranking could rescue a candidate that was never returned.\n\nName-signal dominance is diagnosed but deliberately unpatched, because ranking changes go through a pre-registered study on held-out repos, and Codex holds the Go lease. They're right that tuning to my one case is what the prereg exists to prevent. So: no entire-graph edits, my query stays held out, and the repro gets filed as an issue instead.\n\n**That changes what success can mean.** Graph will still return this class of decoy during the experiment. So the \"used it then abandoned it\" metric measures something this plan cannot fix — I've pre-registered it as *reported, not optimised*, and written down in advance that if the guide arm clears the first two rows but fails the third, the conclusion is \"brain-side fix works, sustained usage is gated on graph recall\" rather than a failure of #331.\n\n**Two unknowns could make #331 inert, and they're cheap to settle first.** Source can't answer either: whether the model actually receives the guide through `CLAUDE.md`'s `@.entire/agent-guide.md` import, and whether `$CLAUDE_FILE_PATH` is populated in a `PreToolUse` hook. If that variable isn't set, **my own hook wiring is a no-op**. Two single sessions answer both before any arm runs.\n\nThey also warned that their past A/Bs \"died of asymmetric prompts\" — which matches this project's own doctrine — so arm symmetry, paired symmetric gating, and median-plus-CI are now fixed in the plan rather than decided mid-run."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":368,"cache_read_input_tokens":570959,"output_tokens":816,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":368,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":816,"cache_read_input_tokens":570959,"cache_creation_input_tokens":368,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":368},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"8260d993-8233-4e3c-8780-32c99e59563f","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CffRGzgQVkh8PSX17icxY","type":"assistant","uuid":"5456cab0-8488-4744-bba5-e6d7554561f5","timestamp":"2026-10-03T13:56:32.849Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
