{"parentUuid":"84a3f780-1ccc-417d-8ccf-338427a8e93e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CffRa4QdEPPDLkgeBHzrY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've found something that changes the picture before spending a token on the arms. Three findings, all from the clean env, all reproducible:\n\n## 1. Brain's documented setup never delivers the Graph directive\n\nA clean repo + `entire brain init-agents` — exactly what brain's README line 112 says to run — produces:\n\n```\n# Entire repository agent guide — Brain\n<!-- entire-agent-activation: {\"schema_version\":1,\"enabled\":[\"brain\"]} -->\n```\n\n**Zero** Graph instruction. `Preview` doesn't detect plugins at all (`preview.go:7` — *\"activation does not depend on plugin inventory\"*); products accumulate only as each one's own `init-agents` is run. So the Graph directive I restored in #331 is **unreachable** for anyone following brain's README, even with graph installed. The README never mentions `entire graph init-agents`.\n\n## 2. Last writer wins, and the two copies disagree\n\nRunning `entire graph init-agents` after brain's flipped the header to `Graph and Brain` — but the directive I fixed is still absent, because **graph's binary rewrote the file with graph's own copy of the text**:\n\n```\nYour FIRST action on any task that requires finding code MUST be ONE Graph query:\n    entire graph query --repo . --profile full --format agent --query \"<task>\"\n```\n\nThat's graph's wording, and it names **`query`** — the verb that doesn't exist in released v0.4.0, which is issue #323, the thing I fixed on brain's side. `files.go:1-3` claims this package is \"mirrored byte-for-byte in both repositories\". It isn't, and the mismatch is now demonstrated rather than inferred: whichever product runs `init-agents` last silently overwrites the other's guide.\n\nSo #331's fix survives only if brain runs last. Install order decides which bugs you get.\n\n## 3. The fixture had to change\n\nentire-brain commits its own `.entire/agent-guide.md`, so a fresh clone arrives pre-seeded — that would have poisoned the no-guide baseline. I switched to `graphmark` (0 committed instruction files, 179 code files). Worth noting the trap: **the obvious fixture would have silently invalidated the A0 arm.**\n\n## Where this leaves the experiment\n\nRunning the arms right now would measure a guide that, in the documented install path, contains no Graph instruction at all — so a null result would be uninformative. Two of these are brain-side defects I can fix in the stack first:\n\n- README/`init-agents` never tells you to activate graph\n- a cross-product overwrite that reintroduces the `query` bug #323 fixed\n\nBoth are small, both are in files I already own in #331, and both are prerequisites for the measurement meaning anything.\n\nPinned binaries recorded in `PINS.txt` (brain `4f4e4bf6`, graph `0d92152d` / `sha256 09f393fe…`, fixture `graphmark 623b2c6`). Probe A and B — does the `@` import reach the model, and is `$CLAUDE_FILE_PATH` populated — are next; those are the two that decide whether any of this is inert."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1049,"cache_read_input_tokens":589035,"output_tokens":1028,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1049,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1028,"cache_read_input_tokens":589035,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1049,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1049},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"1b7c3108-e494-4223-