ote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-graph","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/entiredb","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ad8d204c-1230-4f0e-8a1e-693aed3e0f4f","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"d24e8ab6-334c-4cf6-a14a-8140ef12b7d0","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14897863 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"506d4f9c-1bc7-4fa2-8138-51dfe6f01c66","timestamp":"2026-10-03T14:07:27.802Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14897863 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"506d4f9c-1bc7-4fa2-8138-51dfe6f01c66","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CffS8D3B2Ei9dcqsWmEE7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The call site is now covered. Let me report this round before continuing — it's the most consequential finding so far.\n\n## Probe A: PASS — the guide does reach the model\n\nA real `claude -p` session in a clean clone quoted the directive verbatim:\n\n> `Your FIRST action on any task that requires finding code MUST be ONE Graph query:`\n\nSo the `CLAUDE.md` → `@.entire/agent-guide.md` delivery path works. #331's wording fix is **not** inert.\n\n## Probe B: FAIL — and the bug was mine\n\nMy #331 hook wiring passed `--file \"$CLAUDE_FILE_PATH\"`. The shim log showed `brain hook pre-edit --file` with **nothing after it**.\n\nRather than guess the right mechanism, I installed a hook that dumped its own stdin and environment. Claude Code 2.1.288 sends:\n\n```\nstdin: {\"hook_event_name\":\"PreToolUse\",\"tool_name\":\"Write\",\n        \"tool_input\":{\"file_path\":\"/abs/path\",\"content\":\"…\"}, …}\nenv:   CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR, CLAUDE_PID, CLAUDE_EFFORT,\n       CLAUDE_TRANSCRIPT_PATH, CLAUDE_CODE_ENTRYPOINT …\n```\n\n**There is no `CLAUDE_FILE_PATH`.** It expanded to empty on every edit, the hook errored every time, and no fact ever reached an agent. `init-agents` reported success — installed and inert, which is the worst combination and exactly the class of defect this whole stack is about.\n\nFixed: `hook pre-edit` now reads the harness payload from stdin (`file_path`, and `notebook_path` for NotebookEdit, which the matcher includes), `--file` stays for hand-testing and wins when both are given, and the wiring no longer names a variable that doesn't exist.\n\n**I also caught a flaw in my own fix.** My first version exited 1 on unparseable stdin — an error on *every* edit, when the hook's own contract says noise gets it deleted within a day. Now: a payload with bytes we can't read is silence and exit 0; only genuinely nothing (no stdin, no `--file`) errors, so hand-testing stays debuggable.\n\n```\nvalid payload        exit=0\nunrecognised payload exit=0   <- harness never sees an error\npayload, no path     exit=0\nnothing at all       exit=1   <- hand-test misuse is told\nexplicit --file      exit=0\n```\n\n**And my tests weren't guarding the thing that broke.** Neutering the call site left every helper test green — logic living in the wiring between two correct functions. The replacement drives the real command over a real brain with a real fact, delivered only via stdin, and it now fails on that mutation:\n\n> `hook pre-edit with a stdin payload and no --file: --file is required…`\n\n## Still open from this round\n\nTwo blockers found earlier are not yet fixed: brain's README never tells you to run `entire graph init-agents` (so the documented path yields a Brain-only guide with no Graph directive at all), and whichever product runs `init-agents` last silently overwrites the other's guide — which reintroduced the `query` verb that #323 fixed. Those are next, then the arms."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":709,"cache_read_input_tokens":623414,"output_tokens":1084,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":709,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1084,"cache_read_input_tokens":623414,"cache_creation_input_tokens":709,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":709},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"07021ace-d3ce-41b0-9748-59bf50e9624d","api