{"parentUuid":"873757d9-c5c8-4ba6-a675-9278cc3d3850","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CffSmnfXnS9mF1v9rzYGU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The scorer works and the early signal is stark. Let me commit the fixes while the rest run:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2729,"cache_read_input_tokens":640933,"output_tokens":1643,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":312},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2729,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1643,"cache_read_input_tokens":640933,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2729,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2729},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"6f10eefd-4e98-4ba4-b32d-0255914defb6","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CffSmm3ncLaTNyFWjUR22","type":"assistant","uuid":"88628d20-7386-4e13-b78b-e04a51cdab90","timestamp":"2026-10-03T14:16:04.650Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"88628d20-7386-4e13-b78b-e04a51cdab90","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CffSmnfXnS9mF1v9rzYGU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KUXgUd8JMBEaZpnggXYWxY","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide\ngofmt -l internal/ | head -3\ngo test ./internal/cli/ -run 'TestHook|TestPreEdit|TestInstalledWiring' -count=1 -timeout 900s 2>&1|tail -2\ngo test ./internal/agentsetup/ -count=1 -timeout 600s 2>&1|tail -2\ngit add -A\ngit commit -q -m \"fix(hook): read the harness payload from stdin; document both activations\n\nTHE HOOK WAS INSTALLED AND INERT.\n\nThe wiring added in this branch passed --file \\\"\\$CLAUDE_FILE_PATH\\\". No such\nvariable exists. Measured against Claude Code 2.1.288 by installing a hook that\ndumped its own stdin and environment: the payload arrives as JSON on STDIN\ncarrying tool_input.file_path, and the CLAUDE_* environment holds\nCLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR, CLAUDE_PID, CLAUDE_EFFORT, CLAUDE_TRANSCRIPT_PATH and\nCLAUDE_CODE_ENTRYPOINT -- nothing naming the edited file.\n\nSo the flag expanded to the empty string on every edit, the verb errored every\ntime, and no fact ever reached an agent while init-agents reported success.\nInstalled and inert is the worst of the two, and it is the same defect class\nthis branch exists to remove.\n\npre-edit now reads the payload from stdin (file_path, plus notebook_path, since\nthe installed matcher includes NotebookEdit). --file stays for hand testing and\nwins when both are present.\n\nA correction to the first version of this fix: it exited 1 on unreadable stdin,\nwhich is an error on EVERY edit, and the verb's own contract says a hook that\nemits noise is removed from the harness within a day. A payload we cannot read\nis now silence and exit 0; only genuinely nothing -- no stdin and no --file --\nerrors, so hand testing stays debuggable.\n\nThe tests did not guard what broke. Neutering the call site left every helper\ntest green, because the defect lived in the wiring between two correct\nfunctions. The end-to-end test added here drives the real command over a real\nbrain holding a real fact, delivered only as a stdin payload, and it fails on\nthat mutation.\n\nBRAIN'S DOCUMENTED INSTALL NEVER DELIVERED THE GRAPH DIRECTIVE.\n\nActivation is recorded in the guide, not probed from installed plugins\n(preview.go: \\\"activation does not depend on plugin inventory\\\"). So\n\\`entire brain init-agents\\` alone writes enabled:[\\\"brain\\\"] and a guide with\nzero Graph instructions, however many plugins are installed. Verified in a\nclean clone. The directive restored earlier in this branch was therefore\nunreachable for anyone following the README.\n\nAnd each product rewrites the shared guide from ITS OWN copy of the text, so\nwhichever runs last decides the wording -- graph's init-agents was overwriting\nbrain's fixed text with graph's, which reintroduces the \\`entire graph query\\`\nverb that does not exist in released v0.4.0 (#323).\n\nREADME now names both commands and states that Brain runs last. It also loses a\nsentence claiming the guide covers Graph \\\"when Graph is installed\\\", which is\nfalse unless Graph was activated.\n\nBoth facts are pinned by tests: a Brain-only guide must name no Graph command,\nthe combined guide must keep the directive, and the README must document both\nactivations and the order.\" 2>&1|tail -2\ngit log --oneline -1","description":"Commit the hook and README fixes","timeout":1200000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2729,"cache_read_input_tokens":640933,"output_tokens":1643,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":312},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2729,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1643,"cache_read_input_tokens":640933,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2729,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2729},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01KUXgUd8JMBEaZpnggXYWxY":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide\ngofmt -l internal/ | head -3\ngo test ./internal/cli/ -run 'TestHook|TestPreEdit|TestInstalledWiring' -count=1 -timeout 900s 2>&1|tail -2\ngo test ./internal/agentsetup/ -count=1 -timeout 600s 2>&1|tail -2\ngit add -A\ngit commit -q -m \"fix(hook): read the harness payload from stdin; document both activations\n\nTHE HOOK WAS INSTALLED AND INERT.\n\nThe wiring added in this branch passed --file \\\"\\$CLAUDE_FILE_PATH\\\". No such\nvariable exists. Measured against Claude Code 2.1.288 by installing a hook that\ndumped its own stdin and environment: the payload arrives as JSON on STDIN\ncarrying tool_input.file_path, and the CLAUDE_* environment holds\nCLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR, CLAUDE_PID, CLAUDE_EFFORT, CLAUDE_TRANSCRIPT_PATH and\nCLAUDE_CODE_ENTRYPOINT -- nothing naming the edited file.\n\nSo the flag expanded to the empty string on every edit, the verb errored every\ntime, and no fact ever reached an agent while init-agents reported success.\nInstalled and inert is the worst of the two, and it is the same defect class\nthis branch exists to remove.\n\npre-edit now reads the payload from stdin (file_path, plus notebook_path, since\nthe installed matcher includes NotebookEdit). --file stays for hand testing and\nwins when both are present.\n\nA correction to the first version of this fix: it exited 1 on unreadable stdin,\nwhich is an error on EVERY edit, and the verb's own contract says a hook that\nemits noise is removed from the harness within a day. A payload we cannot read\nis now silence and exit 0; only genuinely nothing -- no stdin and no --file --\nerrors, so hand testing stays debuggable.\n\nThe tests did not guard what broke. Neutering the call site left every helper\ntest green, because the defect lived in the wiring between two correct\nfunctions. The end-to-end test added here drives the real command over a real\nbrain holding a real fact, delivered only as a stdin payload, and it fails on\nthat mutation.\n\nBRAIN'S DOCUMENTED INSTALL NEVER DELIVERED THE GRAPH DIRECTIVE.\n\nActivation is recorded in the guide, not probed from installed plugins\n(preview.go: \\\"activation does not depend on plugin inventory\\\"). So\n\\`entire brain init-agents\\` alone writes enabled:[\\\"brain\\\"] and a guide with\nzero Graph instructions, however many plugins are installed. Verified in a\nclean clone. The directive restored earlier in this branch was therefore\nunreachable for anyone following the README.\n\nAnd each product rewrites the shared guide from ITS OWN copy of the text, so\nwhichever runs last decides the wording -- graph's init-agents was overwriting\nbrain's fixed text with graph's, which reintroduces the \\`entire graph query\\`\nverb that does not exist in released v0.4.0 (#323).\n\nREADME now names both commands and states that Brain runs last. It also loses a\nsentence claiming the guide covers Graph \\\"when Graph is installed\\\", which is\nfalse unless Graph was activated.\n\nBoth facts are pinned by tests: a Brain-only guide must name no Graph command,\nthe combined guide must keep the directive, and the README must document both\nactivations and the order.\" 2>&1|tail -2\ngit log --oneline -1","description":"Commit the hook and README fixes","timeout":1200000}},"serverClassifierRequest":"6f10eefd-4e98-4ba4-b32d-0255914defb6","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CffSmm3ncLaTNyFWjUR22","type":"assistant","uuid":"49569dcb-5470-4e68-907b-390fa4398817","timestamp":"2026-10-03T14:16:19.340Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","per