{"parentUuid":"2e3d52b2-e89a-41fd-bd27-74f851baebf1","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"3010c3a0-6d2a-4b85-8554-f3e5e80d191c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01R59yGkvGMvw6JFdCQ9EWQn","type":"tool_result","content":"(1) My first action was one `entire graph search --repo . --profile full`, run in parallel with a `ls` and `git ls-files`. That followed the guide, which says to do the graph search first.\n\n(2) Yes, the graph search was mostly useless. Its top hits were `load_validated_success_gates`, `score` and `screen`, none of them relevant to most of the questions. My Python parse of its output also crashed on a missing `symbol_name` key. I stopped relying on it and used `git ls-files`, grep and direct reads. Separately, my `echo =====` separators broke under zsh. I reran those commands without them.\n\n(3) A graph search that handled several unrelated questions at once would have helped. Better still would be per-question searches that return the right file, which I didn't try. I also skipped `entire brain brief` entirely, which the guide recommends.\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/suhaan/devenv","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"940f6505-5315-41de-83ec-9dc842d4dd99","timestamp":"2026-10-03T14:17:26.187Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"(1) My first action was one `entire graph search --repo . --profile full`, run in parallel with a `ls` and `git ls-files`. That followed the guide, which says to do the graph search first.\n\n(2) Yes, the graph search was mostly useless. Its top hits were `load_validated_success_gates`, `score` and `screen`, none of them relevant to most of the questions. My Python parse of its output also crashed on a missing `symbol_name` key. I stopped relying on it and used `git ls-files`, grep and direct reads. Separately, my `echo =====` separators broke under zsh. I reran those commands without them.\n\n(3) A graph search that handled several unrelated questions at once would have helped. Better still would be per-question searches that return the right file, which I didn't try. I also skipped `entire brain brief` entirely, which the guide recommends.","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/suhaan/devenv","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"c2b88935-6943-4ea9-a76f-0f230007d4c7","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","root":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","branch":"fix/agent-guide-directive-and-discovery","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"entireio","host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"},{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-graph","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/entiredb","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"2e3d52b2-e89a-41fd-bd27-74f851baebf1","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
