{"parentUuid":"a8926ef3-bbfa-4020-ab2a-4ac65ff9bd54","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CffStLMgqKXrjJih9j2Ak","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The feedback mechanism works, and the very first response is the most actionable thing yet. Three findings, recorded — I won't touch the guide mid-run or I'd invalidate the arms:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1251,"cache_read_input_tokens":647583,"output_tokens":1925,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":898},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1251,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1925,"cache_read_input_tokens":647583,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1251,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1251},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"c91f1766-e0a1-4a14-a036-060cbe8629c5","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CffStK5nHrsuq2Wb5BD54","type":"assistant","uuid":"5fa52151-c46e-467d-a1e2-b115f84abffa","timestamp":"2026-10-03T14:17:42.595Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"5fa52151-c46e-467d-a1e2-b115f84abffa","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CffStLMgqKXrjJih9j2Ak","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01M4zjoDc2Ak3M8A2CoTqDpN","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"E=/Users/suhaan/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp/cleanenv\ncat > \"$E/FINDINGS-round1.md\" <<'EOF'\n# Round 1 findings (clean env, guide installed as a FILE)\n\n## Instrumented result at 9/30 sessions\nA0 (no guide):    0/3 used a tool, 0/3 tool-first\nA1 (guide):       3/3 used,        3/3 tool-first\nA2 (guide+hook):  2/2 used,        2/2 tool-first\nA1 used-then-abandoned: 1/3\n\n## From agent self-report (A1 task1, verbatim)\n\nF1. COMPETING \"FIRST ACTION\" DIRECTIVES -- brain-side, mine, actionable.\n\"I also skipped `entire brain brief` entirely, which the guide recommends.\"\nThe combined guide now carries TWO first-action instructions:\n  brainWorkflow: begin substantive tasks with `entire brain brief`, and\n                 \"Run it before deciding the task does not need it\"\n  graphWorkflow: \"Your FIRST action ... MUST be ONE Graph search\"\nAn agent can only do one thing first, so it picks one and drops the other --\nand it dropped Brain. I introduced this conflict when restoring the Graph\ndirective. The guide must state a definite SEQUENCE rather than two absolutes.\n\nF2. GRAPH JSON CAN OMIT symbol_name -- graph-side, report only.\n\"My Python parse of its output also crashed on a missing `symbol_name` key.\"\nIndependently hit by my own scorer, which needed\n`r.get('symbol_name') or r.get('qualified_name')`. A documented result schema\nwith an always-present identifier would stop consumers crashing.\n\nF3. RECALL FAILURE GENERALISES TO A SECOND REPO -- graph-side, held out.\n\"the graph search was mostly useless. Its top hits were\n`load_validated_success_gates`, `score` and `screen`, none of them relevant\"\nPreviously measured on entire-brain; this is graphmark, a different repo and\nlanguage (Python). Not a one-repo artifact.\n\n## Not acted on during the run\nChanging the guide mid-experiment would invalidate the arms. F1 is fixed in\nround 2 and the affected arms re-run. F2/F3 go to the graph session and an issue.\nEOF\necho \"recorded. findings:\"; grep -c \"^F[0-9]\" \"$E/FINDINGS-round1.md\" | xargs echo \" \"\ncat \"$E/logs/progress.txt\" | tail -3","description":"Record round-1 findings durably","timeout":600000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1251,"cache_read_input_tokens":647583,"output_tokens":1925,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":898},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1251,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1925,"cache_read_input_tokens":647583,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1251,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1251},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01M4zjoDc2Ak3M8A2CoTqDpN":{"command":"E=/Users/suhaan/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp/cleanenv\ncat > \"$E/FINDINGS-round1.md\" <<'EOF'\n# Round 1 findings (clean env, guide installed as a FILE)\n\n## Instrumented result at 9/30 sessions\nA0 (no guide):    0/3 used a tool, 0/3 tool-first\nA1 (guide):       3/3 used,        3/3 tool-first\nA2 (guide+hook):  2/2 used,        2/2 tool-first\nA1 used-then-abandoned: 1/3\n\n## From agent self-report (A1 task1, verbatim)\n\nF1. COMPETING \"FIRST ACTION\" DIRECTIVES -- brain-side, mine, actionable.\n\"I also skipped `entire brain brief` entirely, which the guide recommends.\"\nThe combined guide now carries TWO first-action instructions:\n  brainWorkflow: begin substantive tasks with `entire brain brief`, and\n                 \"Run it before deciding the task does not need it\"\n  graphWorkflow: \"Your FIRST action ... MUST be ONE Graph search\"\nAn agent can only do one thing first, so it picks one and drops the other --\nand it dropped Brain. I introduced this conflict when restoring the Graph\ndirective. The guide must state a definite SEQUENCE rather than two absolutes.\n\nF2. GRAPH JSON CAN OMIT symbol_name -- graph-side, report only.\n\"My Python parse of its output also crashed on a missing `symbol_name` key.\"\nIndependently hit by my own scorer, which needed\n`r.get('symbol_name') or r.get('qualified_name')`. A documented result schema\nwith an always-present identifier would stop consumers crashing.\n\nF3. RECALL FAILURE GENERALISES TO A SECOND REPO -- graph-side, held out.\n\"the graph search was mostly useless. Its top hits were\n`load_validated_success_gates`, `score` and `screen`, none of them relevant\"\nPreviously measured on entire-brain; this is graphmark, a different repo and\nlanguage (Python). Not a one-repo artifact.\n\n## Not acted on during the run\nChanging the guide mid-experiment would invalidate the arms. F1 is fixed in\nround 2 and the affected arms re-run. F2/F3 go to the graph session and an issue.\nEOF\necho \"recorded. findings:\"; grep -c \"^F[0-9]\" \"$E/FINDINGS-round1.md\" | xargs echo \" \"\ncat \"$E/logs/progress.txt\" | tail -3","description":"Record round-1 findings durably","timeout":600000}},"serverClassifierRequest":"c91f1766-e0a1-4a14-a036-060cbe8629c5","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CffStK5nHrsuq2Wb5BD54","type":"assistant","uuid":"d34d08ca-746b-4a30-aa9a-0da305b2d5a2","timestamp":"2026-10-03T14:17:54.017Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e