{"parentUuid":"3454ef58-c239-49b0-9b8b-a07cdbfa90d4","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14870574 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"8cea30d9-6dbf-4a25-9496-4520b5eff9c6","timestamp":"2026-10-03T14:18:00.783Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14870574 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"8cea30d9-6dbf-4a25-9496-4520b5eff9c6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CffSvtBRLeyHndRBy7xAp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The loop is producing exactly what it was supposed to. The first feedback turn found a defect I introduced and couldn't have found by reading code.\n\n## The finding that matters\n\nThe agent complied with the Graph directive — and **silently dropped Brain**:\n\n> *\"I also skipped `entire brain brief` entirely, which the guide recommends.\"*\n\nThe combined guide now carries **two** first-action absolutes:\n\n- `brainWorkflow`: begin substantive tasks with `entire brain brief`, *\"run it before deciding the task does not need it\"*\n- `graphWorkflow`: *\"Your FIRST action … MUST be ONE Graph search\"*\n\nAn agent can only do one thing first, so it picks one and drops the other. **I created that conflict** when I restored the Graph directive in #331. The fix is to state a definite sequence rather than two competing absolutes — brief for prior decisions, then search for code.\n\nThis is the one class of defect that only a real session in a real clean env could surface: the text reads fine, each sentence is individually correct, and the conflict only exists at execution time.\n\n## Two more, both graph-side\n\n- **Its JSON can omit `symbol_name`** — *\"My Python parse of its output also crashed on a missing `symbol_name` key.\"* I hit this independently; my own scorer needed a `qualified_name` fallback. Real consumer-breaking schema gap.\n- **The recall failure generalises.** *\"the graph search was mostly useless. Its top hits were `load_validated_success_gates`, `score` and `screen`, none of them relevant.\"* That's graphmark — a different repo and language from where I first measured it. Not a one-repo artifact.\n\nBoth go to the graph session and an issue, per the lease. I'm not touching that repo.\n\n## Why I'm not fixing F1 yet\n\nChanging the guide mid-run would invalidate the arms. It's recorded in `FINDINGS-round1.md`, gets fixed in round 2, and the affected arms re-run against the same pre-registered bar.\n\nInstrumented standing at 9/30 — A0 at **0/3** on both metrics, A1 **3/3**, A2 **2/2**."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":510,"cache_read_input_tokens":650831,"output_tokens":702,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":510,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":702,"cache_read_input_tokens":650831,"cache_creation_input_tokens":510,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":510},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"b7dbaf97-7835-4cdf-9d97-7d8b82a4509a","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CffSvqnYb3jvU943PFm1v","type":"assistant","uuid":"620973ca-8f73-442f-88b1-e9f36eb3bfff","timestamp":"2026-10-03T14:18:11.426Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
