{"parentUuid":"bdd1015a-69d1-496e-92c5-64b5909cff03","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CffSxq2Trc3UwbYnfe7N7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GfsdE7SWkGyogAEuiBGJeY","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph\ngh issue create --repo entireio/entire-graph \\\n  --title \"search: intent-phrased queries miss the real answer entirely (recall, not ranking) — two repos, reproduces on 0d92152d\" \\\n  --body \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nFiled at the request of the `redesign-graph-cost-reduction` session so the repro is recorded without colliding with the study-7 prereg. **Not a request for an ad-hoc ranking change** — the query below should be treated as held-out, evaluation-only, and must not enter a tuning set.\n\n## What happens\n\nA query phrased as *intent* (a sentence describing behaviour) returns results that do not contain the real answer at all. Not mis-ordered — **absent from the returned set**, so no reranking could rescue it.\n\n## Repro 1 — entire-brain\n\n```\nentire-graph-0d92152d search --repo . --profile full \\\n  --query \"decide whether semantic index needs rebuilding\" --format json\n```\n\nRepo: `entireio/entire-brain` at `4f4e4bf6`. Binary: the frozen launch build\n`entire-graph-0d92152d`, `sha256 09f393fe06683859…`, `version pre306-combined-baseline-11-g0d92152d`.\n\nReturned:\n\n| rank | score | symbol |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | 30.13 | `brainBriefSemanticNeedsCurrentBoundary` — `internal/cli/brain_brief_semantic_freshness.go:19` |\n| 2 | 29.38 | `acquireSemanticIndexLock` — `internal/cli/semantic.go:1138` |\n| 3 | 29.37 | `runSemanticIngestTraces` — `internal/cli/semantic_graph.go:970` |\n\nRank 1 is **not** the rebuild decision — it gates overfetch inside the brief.\n\nThe two functions that actually make the decision are **absent from the entire returned set**:\n\n- `semanticStaleReport` — `internal/cli/semantic.go:3007`\n- `semanticIndexAlreadyCurrent` — `internal/cli/semantic.go:408`\n\n`grep` found both immediately.\n\n**Repo-wide idf does not change this case.** Scores are identical to 2dp against an older build without PR #291, so this is not the sample-idf path.\n\nPossibly relevant to the exact-corpus gate: `files_scanned=1855` but `files_content_read_during_preselection=1853`, with 12 `E_MINIFIED` entries in `partial_failures`. If a deliberate skip counts as \"unread\" and revokes the exact-corpus idf path, that may be worth checking separately. There is no `idf_source` field in `stats`, so which path ran cannot be determined from the output — **exposing that field would make this checkable from outside.**\n\n## Repro 2 — graphmark, different language\n\nSame class, independently, in a Python repo, from a real agent session that had been instructed to search first:\n\n> *\"the graph search was mostly useless. Its top hits were `load_validated_success_gates`, `score` and `screen`, none of them relevant\"*\n\nSo it is not an entire-brain artifact.\n\n## Second, separate bug: results can omit `symbol_name`\n\nA result object can lack `symbol_name`, which crashes consumers that index it:\n\n> *\"My Python parse of its output also crashed on a missing `symbol_name` key.\"*\n\nHit independently while scoring an experiment — the workaround was `r.get('symbol_name') or r.get('qualified_name')`. A documented result schema with an always-present identifier would prevent this.\n\n## Why this is being filed\n\nMeasured in a clean environment with real `claude -p` sessions: once the agent guide instructs a search-first workflow, agents **do** comply — and then a non-answer sends them to grep, which succeeds. First-call compliance is the easy half; an agent that complies once and gets nothing has learned the tool does not pay.\n\nContext on the already-known mechanism (name-coverage weight, stopwords not covering prose terms) is held by the `redesign-graph-cost-reduction` session and slated for study 7. This issue exists to record the two repros and the schema gap, not to propose a patch.\nEOF\n)\" 2>&1 | tail -2","description":"File the graph recall issue with full repro","timeout":900000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1408,"cache_read_input_tokens":652352,"output_tokens":1521,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1408,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1521,"cache_read_input_tokens":652352,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1408,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1408},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01GfsdE7SWkGyogAEuiBGJeY":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph\ngh issue create --repo entireio/entire-graph \\\n  --title \"search: intent-phrased queries miss the real answer entirely (recall, not ranking) — two repos, reproduces on 0d92152d\" \\\n  --body \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nFiled at the request of the `redesign-graph-cost-reduction` session so the repro is recorded without colliding with the study-7 prereg. **Not a request for an ad-hoc ranking change** — the query below should be treated as held-out, evaluation-only, and must not enter a tuning set.\n\n## What happens\n\nA query phrased as *intent* (a sentence describing behaviour) returns results that do not contain the real answer at all. Not mis-ordered — **absent from the returned set**, so no reranking could rescue it.\n\n## Repro 1 — entire-brain\n\n```\nentire-graph-0d92152d search --repo . --profile full \\\n  --query \"decide whether semantic index needs rebuilding\" --format json\n```\n\nRepo: `entireio/entire-brain` at `4f4e4bf6`. Binary: the frozen launch build\n`entire-graph-0d92152d`, `sha256 09f393fe06683859…`, `version pre306-combined-baseline-11-g0d92152d`.\n\nReturned:\n\n| rank | score | symbol |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | 30.13 | `brainBriefSemanticNeedsCurrentBoundary` — `internal/cli/brain_brief_semantic_freshness.go:19` |\n| 2 | 29.38 | `acquireSemanticIndexLock` — `internal/cli/semantic.go:1138` |\n| 3 | 29.37 | `runSemanticIngestTraces` — `internal/cli/semantic_graph.go:970` |\n\nRank 1 is **not** the rebuild decision — it gates overfetch inside the brief.\n\nThe two functions that actually make the decision are **absent from the entire returned set**:\n\n- `semanticStaleReport` — `internal/cli/semantic.go:3007`\n- `semanticIndexAlreadyCurrent` — `internal/cli/semantic.go:408`\n\n`grep` found both immediately.\n\n**Repo-wide idf does not change this case.** Scores are identical to 2dp against an older build without PR #291, so this is not the sample-idf path.\n\nPossibly relevant to the exact-corpus gate: `files_scanned=1855` but `files_content_read_during_preselection=1853`, with 12 `E_MINIFIED` entries in `partial_failures`. If a deliberate skip counts as \"unread\" and revokes the exact-corpus idf path, that may be worth checking separately. There is no `idf_source` field in `stats`, so which path ran cannot be determined from the output — **exposing that field would make this checkable from outside.**\n\n## Repro 2 — graphmark, different language\n\nSame class, independently, in a Python repo, from a real agent session that had been instructed to search first:\n\n> *\"the graph search was mostly useless. Its top hits were `load_validated_success_gates`, `score` and `screen`, none of them relevant\"*\n\nSo it is not an entire-brain artifact.\n\n## Second, separate bug: results can omit `symbol_name`\n\nA result object can lack `symbol_name`, which crashes consumers that index it:\n\n> *\"My Python parse of its output also crashed on a missing `symbol_name` key.\"*\n\nHit independently while scoring an experiment — the workaround was `r.get('symbol_name') or r.get('qualified_name')`. A documented result schema with an always-present identifier would prevent this.\n\n## Why this is being filed\n\nMeasured in a clean environment with real `claude -p` sessions: once the agent guide instructs a search-first workflow, agents **do** comply — and then a non-answer sends them to grep, which succeeds. First-call compliance is the easy half; an agent that complies once and gets nothing has learned the tool does not pay.\n\nContext on the already-known mechanism (name-coverage weight, stopwords not covering prose terms) is held by the `redesign-graph-cost-reduction` session and slated for study 7. This issue exists to record the two repros and the schema gap, not to propose a patch.\nEOF\n)\" 2>&1 | tail -2","description":"File the graph recall issue with full repro","timeout":900000}},"serverClassifierRequest":"61fcd2d3-197d-4505-9a62-94b8f17362e3","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CffSxoBadkXvCwegUuUFp","type":"assistant","uuid":"f1881b6f-c3eb-48fc-ad3d-3b822aa44eb1","timestamp":"2026-10-03T14:18:49.808Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
