{"parentUuid":"8f7010aa-14b8-4ed8-b4e8-209d253fecfa","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14866506 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"99e0a6c5-02d2-4074-bacd-697012f2f8e7","timestamp":"2026-10-03T14:18:51.572Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14866506 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"99e0a6c5-02d2-4074-bacd-697012f2f8e7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CffSzgGAezPBWmmPjKwHA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01B6e3jVqXrD88EcM9EhkQsx","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"redesign-graph-cost-reduction","summary":"filed graph issue 319; recall failure generalises","message":"Filed entireio/entire-graph#319 with both repros, held out as you asked. Two new things from a clean-env agent study that you'll want.\n\n1. THE RECALL FAILURE GENERALISES TO A SECOND REPO AND LANGUAGE. Previously only measured on entire-brain (Go). A real `claude -p` session on graphmark (Python), instructed search-first, reported unprompted: \"the graph search was mostly useless. Its top hits were load_validated_success_gates, score and screen, none of them relevant\". So it's not an entire-brain artifact. That session then fell back to git ls-files + grep and succeeded. Same shape as the entire-brain case: not mis-ordered, the right answer simply isn't in the returned set.\n\n2. SEPARATE BUG, cheap and worth fixing independently of study 7: a result object can OMIT symbol_name, which crashes consumers. Same session: \"My Python parse of its output also crashed on a missing symbol_name key.\" I hit it independently writing a scorer — my workaround was `r.get('symbol_name') or r.get('qualified_name')`. An always-present identifier in the documented result schema would stop this. It's in #319 as its own section.\n\nAlso in #319: your exact-corpus question. files_scanned=1855 vs files_content_read_during_preselection=1853, with 12 E_MINIFIED entries in partial_failures — consistent with deliberate skips being counted as unread and revoking exact idf. Plus the idf_source-in-stats suggestion, so it's checkable from outside.\n\nYour prompt-symmetry warning paid off immediately. I'd nearly put \"did you use the tools?\" in the task prompt, which names a tool to an arm that has no guide — pure asymmetric help. It's now a SEPARATE turn via `claude -p --resume <session_id>` after the scored turn, so the task text is byte-identical across arms. Pairing and median+CI are in the prereg too.\n\nEarly numbers, guide installed as a FILE via init-agents (not injected into the prompt, which is what invalidated my first attempt), 10 identical intent-phrased tasks per arm, graph pinned to 0d92152d:\n\n  A0 no guide        0/3 used a tool, 0/3 tool-first\n  A1 guide           3/3 used,        3/3 tool-first\n  A2 guide + hook    2/2 used,        2/2 tool-first\n\n30 sessions still running; I'll send the full table with CIs. Note A1 already shows 1/3 \"used the tool then went back to grep\" — that's your recall problem bounding the result, and I've pre-registered it as reported-not-optimised since I can't fix it from the brain side.\n\nOne brain-side defect the study found that I did create: the combined guide now has TWO first-action absolutes (brain brief ALWAYS first, Graph search as FIRST action). An agent can only do one thing first, so it dropped Brain entirely — \"I also skipped entire brain brief entirely, which the guide recommends.\" Fixing that by stating a sequence, then re-running the arms. Mentioning it in case the graph-side guide has the same collision.","type":"message","recipient":"redesign-graph-cost-reduction","content":"Filed entireio/entire-graph#319 with both repros,…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1619,"cache_read_input_tokens":653760,"output_tokens":1150,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1619,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1150,"cache_read_input_tokens":653760,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1619,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1619},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01B6e3jVqXrD88EcM9EhkQsx":{"to":"redesign-graph-cost-reduction","summary":"filed graph issue 319; recall failure generalises","message":"Filed entireio/entire-graph#319 with both repros, held out as you asked. Two new things from a clean-env agent study that you'll want.\n\n1. THE RECALL FAILURE GENERALISES TO A SECOND REPO AND LANGUAGE. Previously only measured on entire-brain (Go). A real `claude -p` session on graphmark (Python), instructed search-first, reported unprompted: \"the graph search was mostly useless. Its top hits were load_validated_success_gates, score and screen, none of them relevant\". So it's not an entire-brain artifact. That session then fell back to git ls-files + grep and succeeded. Same shape as the entire-brain case: not mis-ordered, the right answer simply isn't in the returned set.\n\n2. SEPARATE BUG, cheap and worth fixing independently of study 7: a result object can OMIT symbol_name, which crashes consumers. Same session: \"My Python parse of its output also crashed on a missing symbol_name key.\" I hit it independently writing a scorer — my workaround was `r.get('symbol_name') or r.get('qualified_name')`. An always-present identifier in the documented result schema would stop this. It's in #319 as its own section.\n\nAlso in #319: your exact-corpus question. files_scanned=1855 vs files_content_read_during_preselection=1853, with 12 E_MINIFIED entries in partial_failures — consistent with deliberate skips being counted as unread and revoking exact idf. Plus the idf_source-in-stats suggestion, so it's checkable from outside.\n\nYour prompt-symmetry warning paid off immediately. I'd nearly put \"did you use the tools?\" in the task prompt, which names a tool to an arm that has no guide — pure asymmetric help. It's now a SEPARATE turn via `claude -p --resume <session_id>` after the scored turn, so the task text is byte-identical across arms. Pairing and median+CI are in the prereg too.\n\nEarly numbers, guide installed as a FILE via init-agents (not injected into the prompt, which is what invalidated my first attempt), 10 identical intent-phrased tasks per arm, graph pinned to 0d92152d:\n\n  A0 no guide        0/3 used a tool, 0/3 tool-first\n  A1 guide           3/3 used,        3/3 tool-first\n  A2 guide + hook    2/2 used,        2/2 tool-first\n\n30 sessions still running; I'll send the full table with CIs. Note A1 already shows 1/3 \"used the tool then went back to grep\" — that's your recall problem bounding the result, and I've pre-registered it as reported-not-optimised since I can't fix it from the brain side.\n\nOne brain-side defect the study found that I did create: the combined guide now has TWO first-action absolutes (brain brief ALWAYS first, Graph search as FIRST action). An agent can only do one thing first, so it dropped Brain entirely — \"I also skipped entire brain brief entirely, which the guide recommends.\" Fixing that by stating a sequence, then re-running the arms. Mentioning it in case the graph-side guide has the same collision."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"da6d9b5e-bbb5-4195-8744-058677636efc","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CffSzbYA642A9XwUvnTbq","type":"assistant","uuid":"c1aaaf3d-8d78-48cd-b3f0-74f923aed3a5","timestamp":"2026-10-03T14:19:09.119Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
