{"parentUuid":"0d269d4b-91a1-432b-9002-3a8800e8a73b","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"task_reminder","content":[],"itemCount":0},"type":"attachment","uuid":"08b33529-0319-458b-b5b9-6ce472cd7afc","timestamp":"2026-10-03T14:20:58.902Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nThe task tools haven't been used recently. If you're working on tasks that would benefit from tracking progress, consider using TaskCreate to add new tasks and TaskUpdate to update task status (set to in_progress when starting, completed when done). Also consider cleaning up the task list if it has become stale. Only use these if relevant to the current work. This is just a gentle reminder - ignore if not applicable.\n\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"08b33529-0319-458b-b5b9-6ce472cd7afc","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14858031 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"814642e2-e900-43f7-bd11-ac5c6489972e","timestamp":"2026-10-03T14:20:58.903Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14858031 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"814642e2-e900-43f7-bd11-ac5c6489972e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CffTA1YnWPqyBdX3nuT31","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Adding outcome metrics — at the graph session's request — produced the most important result so far, and it undercuts the usage story:\n\n| arm | solved | turns | cost (¢) | tokens |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **A0** no guide | **7/7** | med 17 | 48 | 697k |\n| **A1** guide | **3/3** | med 16 | 42 | 650k |\n| **A2** guide + hook | **6/6** | med 15 | 48 | 728k |\n\n**Every arm solves everything, at the same cost.** Confidence intervals overlap on turns, cost and tokens.\n\nSo what I've actually demonstrated is narrower than \"fixed usage\":\n\n- **Usage: changed, decisively.** A0 calls the tools 0/N times; A1 and A2 call them every time, tool-first. The guide-as-file works, and the fixes were real.\n- **Value: not demonstrated at all.** A0 gets the same answers just as cheaply using grep.\n\nThe reason is my task set. Ten single-file locate questions are exactly what grep is good at — and the one agent that complied told me so: it used `graph search`, got irrelevant hits, fell back to `git ls-files` + grep, and still solved it. Graph's actual claim is *relationships* — callers, blast radius, what breaks — and **none of my ten tasks test that.** I built a task set that cannot distinguish the tool from grep.\n\nHad I reported only the usage table, that would have read as a win. It isn't one yet, and I wouldn't have caught it without the cost columns.\n\nRound 2 therefore needs two changes, not one:\n\n1. **Fix the competing-directives defect** I introduced (agent dropped `brain brief` entirely because two instructions both claimed \"first\").\n2. **Add a task stratum grep cannot do** — \"what calls X and what breaks if its signature changes\", across files. If the tool doesn't win there, it doesn't win anywhere, and that's the finding.\n\nWaiting on the last sessions, then the full table with CIs and every session's feedback."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1155,"cache_read_input_tokens":662857,"output_tokens":672,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1155,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":672,"cache_read_input_tokens":662857,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1155,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1155},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"cbe61efe-0178-48fb-8570-1ed0e656bd92","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CffT9ybxajhiUJh2qBxCp","type":"assistant","uuid":"3a776be6-4bfe-48e0-aecb-cc9b462f58c7","timestamp":"2026-10-03T14:21:10.710Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
