{"parentUuid":"963d9b91-3552-450c-8121-374429c54c23","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CffTFWePu9ENYoHJaDgYE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Duplicate stopped. Now the F1 fix — the competing-directives defect I introduced. Editing source is safe since the arms run off the already-built binary and already-written guides:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1415,"cache_read_input_tokens":664979,"output_tokens":1241,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1415,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1241,"cache_read_input_tokens":664979,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1415,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1415},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"ec66c4a8-3805-4291-8a0f-666fda615771","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CffTFUMV9tJQJahXzm1Bc","type":"assistant","uuid":"a16c2b5c-9ef8-4918-a152-3a96007e7a2c","timestamp":"2026-10-03T14:22:16.459Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"a16c2b5c-9ef8-4918-a152-3a96007e7a2c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CffTFWePu9ENYoHJaDgYE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FagmeMo7hjknPncJj8Aw5v","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide\npython3 - <<'PY'\np='internal/agentsetup/guide.go'; s=open(p).read()\nold='''// combinedWorkflow is the guide most users get, and it carried NO Graph\n// obligation at all: it was brainWorkflow plus a capability list. The brief is\n// about prior decisions, so an agent reading only this had nothing telling it to\n// look at the call graph before editing.\nconst combinedWorkflow = brainWorkflow + `\nYour FIRST action on any task that requires finding code MUST be ONE Graph search:\n\n    entire graph search --repo . --profile full --query \"<task>\"\n\nThis holds for small edits, follow-up work, and tasks that already name the file.\nA named file answers where code is; it does not answer what else depends on it.\nDo not skip the search on the grounds that the available context feels sufficient.\nUse Graph search, def, neighbors, and impact for code discovery and structural\nanalysis.'''\nnew='''// combinedWorkflow is the guide most users get, and it carried NO Graph\n// obligation at all: it was brainWorkflow plus a capability list. The brief is\n// about prior decisions, so an agent reading only this had nothing telling it to\n// look at the call graph before editing.\n//\n// IT MUST STATE AN ORDER, NOT TWO ABSOLUTES. The first version of this fix put\n// \"your FIRST action MUST be ONE Graph search\" after brainWorkflow's \"begin\n// substantive tasks with brain brief\". Both claimed to be first, an agent can\n// only do one thing first, and in a measured clean-environment session it\n// resolved the conflict by dropping Brain entirely: \"I also skipped\n// `entire brain brief` entirely, which the guide recommends.\" Two competing\n// absolutes are weaker than one sequence, because the agent picks.\nconst combinedWorkflow = brainWorkflow + `\nBoth tools run, in this order, and neither replaces the other:\n\n    1. entire brain brief \"<task>\" --json                      (why, and what was decided)\n    2. entire graph search --repo . --profile full --query \"<task>\"   (where, and what depends on it)\n\nStep 2 holds for small edits, follow-up work, and tasks that already name the\nfile: a named file answers where code is, not what else depends on it. Do not\nskip either step on the grounds that the available context feels sufficient, and\ndo not treat having done one as having done the other.\nUse Graph search, def, neighbors, and impact for code discovery and structural\nanalysis.'''\nassert s.count(old)==1\nopen(p,'w').write(s.replace(old,new)); print(\"combined guide now states a sequence\")\nPY\ngofmt -w internal/agentsetup/guide.go && go build ./... 2>&1|head -3\necho \"=== both steps present, exactly once each, in the combined guide? ===\"\n\"$PWD/../../.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp/cleanenv/bin/entire-brain-pinned\" version >/dev/null 2>&1\ngo run ./cmd/entire-brain agent-guide --normal --repo . 2>/dev/null | grep -nE \"entire brain brief|entire graph search|MUST be ONE\" | head -5","description":"Fix the competing first-action directives","timeout":1200000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1415,"cache_read_input_tokens":664979,"output_tokens":1241,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1415,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1241,"cache_read_input_tokens":664979,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1415,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_