{"parentUuid":"1cb89377-dc4e-4064-9db3-b7969fa43be0","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"task_reminder","content":[],"itemCount":0},"type":"attachment","uuid":"cf7cd78c-a5ba-4247-a34a-143b890a79eb","timestamp":"2026-10-03T14:23:40.430Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nThe task tools haven't been used recently. If you're working on tasks that would benefit from tracking progress, consider using TaskCreate to add new tasks and TaskUpdate to update task status (set to in_progress when starting, completed when done). Also consider cleaning up the task list if it has become stale. Only use these if relevant to the current work. This is just a gentle reminder - ignore if not applicable.\n\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"cf7cd78c-a5ba-4247-a34a-143b890a79eb","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14849259 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"09ccc959-fa11-4da7-bb80-65a2729f5c58","timestamp":"2026-10-03T14:23:40.431Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14849259 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"09ccc959-fa11-4da7-bb80-65a2729f5c58","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CffTMvAfmaQzJ8a9Yy4Wv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"F1 is fixed and the guard fires on the exact collision that caused it. Round 2 is prepared while round 1 finishes.\n\n## The fix\n\nThe combined guide had **two** first-action absolutes. It now states one ordered sequence:\n\n```\n1. entire brain brief \"<task>\" --json                    (why, and what was decided)\n2. entire graph search --repo . --profile full --query   (where, and what depends on it)\n\n...do not treat having done one as having done the other.\n```\n\nThe Graph-**only** guide keeps `MUST be ONE Graph search` — with one tool there's no ambiguity. The distinction is deliberate and now written down, because the failure mode is specifically *two* absolutes.\n\nI had to reconcile three of my own guards, which is itself the evidence they were pinning the wrong thing: they asserted the word `MUST` where the intent was \"the obligation is unambiguous\". They now assert the sequence, and a new one **forbids** a second absolute:\n\n> `the combined guide carries a second first-action absolute beside the ordered sequence; two absolutes let the agent pick one and drop the other`\n\n## What this round of the loop actually produced\n\nThree defects, each found a different way, none findable by reading code:\n\n| found by | defect |\n|---|---|\n| clean-env probe | hook wiring named a nonexistent env var — **installed and inert** |\n| clean-env install | brain's documented setup delivers **no Graph directive at all** |\n| **agent self-report** | two competing absolutes → agent **silently dropped Brain** |\n\nAnd the cost columns the graph session asked for turned a would-be win into an honest null: **all arms solve everything at the same cost**, because ten single-file locate tasks are what grep is best at. My task set can't distinguish the tool from grep — that's a flaw in my design, not a property of the tool.\n\nRound 2 adds a relationship stratum (callers, blast radius) where grep should genuinely lose. If the tool doesn't win there, that's the finding."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1262,"cache_read_input_tokens":671615,"output_tokens":645,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1262,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":645,"cache_read_input_tokens":671615,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1262,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1262},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"dbe6df47-bfad-4f40-971f-2151e2662838","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CffTMtRk3MXnUABqECiZB","type":"assistant","uuid":"c3d18506-82ad-41d5-a821-78f968b7796b","timestamp":"2026-10-03T14:23:52.086Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
