{"parentUuid":"559fdb80-925a-42a9-8d69-20012927cc8f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CffTbvHkayvsT5neq8ZjP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`cli` is the right fixture — **10 of 40** sampled exported functions have 4+ cross-file referencing files, versus graphmark's one. Let me record the round-2 design:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1572,"cache_read_input_tokens":675689,"output_tokens":1550,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":293},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1572,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1550,"cache_read_input_tokens":675689,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1572,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1572},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"ccf3e9d9-45bf-4775-93ca-bbfca16b6671","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CffTbu3qiER7d1U8ikYwA","type":"assistant","uuid":"45c1fb6e-4d2e-4e1e-9d90-c911d30161aa","timestamp":"2026-10-03T14:26:57.096Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/cli","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"45c1fb6e-4d2e-4e1e-9d90-c911d30161aa","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CffTbvHkayvsT5neq8ZjP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HHGY3Q4eZBNXCpaDDR6WnL","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/cli\necho \"=== what instruction files does cli commit (must be stripped, identically, per arm)? ===\"\ngit ls-tree -r --name-only HEAD | grep -iE \"^(CLAUDE|AGENTS)\\.md$|^\\.entire/\" | head -6\nE=/Users/suhaan/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp/cleanenv\ncat > \"$E/ROUND2-DESIGN.md\" <<'EOF'\n# Round 2 design\n\n## Why round 1 could not have shown tool VALUE (fixture defect, mine)\n\ngraphmark has 178 Python files and exactly ONE function with >=3 cross-file\ncallers. It is a collection of standalone scripts, not an interconnected\ncodebase. So there were no relationships to discover, and grep was always going\nto be sufficient -- every arm solved 100% at identical cost. That is a property\nof the fixture I chose, not evidence about the tool.\n\nMeasured density, 40 sampled exported funcs with >=4 cross-file referencing files:\n  graphmark    1 (of all functions sampled)\n  entire-api   5 of 40\n  cli         10 of 40   <- round 2 fixture\n\n## Changes from round 1\n\n1. FIXTURE: entireio/cli (1390 Go files, dense internal calls). Go is Graph's\n   best-supported language. cli commits instruction files, so each arm clone\n   gets ONE prep commit removing them -- identical in every arm, and stated.\n2. TASK STRATUM: relationship questions grep is genuinely bad at, on symbols\n   verified to have >=4 cross-file referencing files:\n     - \"what calls X, and what breaks if its signature changes\"\n     - \"what does X depend on that would need updating\"\n   Paired with a locate stratum carried over from round 1, so the comparison\n   shows WHERE the tool helps rather than only whether it is used.\n3. GUIDE: the competing-absolutes fix (ordered sequence) is in. Round 1's A1/A2\n   ran the two-absolutes guide, which is why they dropped `brain brief`.\n\n## Carried over unchanged\nPinned binaries, one fresh clone per arm, prompt byte-identical across arms and\nnever naming a tool, feedback as a SEPARATE --resume turn after the scored turn,\npaired symmetric gating, median + bootstrap CI beside every rate, and outcome\nmetrics (solved / turns / cost / tokens) reported beside usage.\n\n## Pre-registered, unchanged from round 1\n  sessions with >=1 Graph or Brain call   A1 >= 9/10\n  tool-first rate                        A1 >= 0.7\n  used-then-abandoned                    A1 <= 3/10   (reported, not optimised:\n                                         bounded by graph recall, see #319)\nNEW, and the one that matters for value:\n  solved on the RELATIONSHIP stratum     A1 > A0, or the tool is not pulling\n                                         its weight on the question class it\n                                         exists for.\nEOF\necho \"recorded\"\necho \"sessions: $(grep -c 'exit=' \"$E/logs/progress.txt\")/30  arms: $(grep -c DONE \"$E/logs/progress.txt\")/3\"","description":"Record the round-2 design and check progress","timeout":900000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1572,"cache_read_input_tokens":675689,"output_tokens":1550,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":293},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1572,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1550,"cache_read_input_tokens":675689,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1572,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1572},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_man