{"parentUuid":"62e6230f-fe54-476b-a795-787f03de4f36","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"task_reminder","content":[],"itemCount":0},"type":"attachment","uuid":"819487d4-d4ed-4ada-8817-49a8176c6249","timestamp":"2026-10-03T14:28:46.249Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nThe task tools haven't been used recently. If you're working on tasks that would benefit from tracking progress, consider using TaskCreate to add new tasks and TaskUpdate to update task status (set to in_progress when starting, completed when done). Also consider cleaning up the task list if it has become stale. Only use these if relevant to the current work. This is just a gentle reminder - ignore if not applicable.\n\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/cli","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"819487d4-d4ed-4ada-8817-49a8176c6249","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14841618 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"d54cf1b0-9da1-4cd3-ac8a-cee07b424c5e","timestamp":"2026-10-03T14:28:46.250Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14841618 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/cli","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"d54cf1b0-9da1-4cd3-ac8a-cee07b424c5e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CffTkTWSA1W2T21Maspwb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Round 1 complete, n=10 per arm, all 10 tasks paired across all three arms.\n\n## Usage — the fixes work, decisively\n\n| arm | used a tool | tool-first |\n|---|---|---|\n| **A0** no guide | **0/10** = 0.00 [0.00, 0.00] | **0/10** = 0.00 |\n| **A1** guide | **10/10** = 1.00 [1.00, 1.00] | **10/10** = 1.00 |\n| **A2** guide + hook | **10/10** = 1.00 [1.00, 1.00] | **10/10** = 1.00 |\n\n0/10 vs 10/10 is Fisher exact **p = 1.1 × 10⁻⁵**. Both pre-registered usage bars cleared (≥9/10 and ≥0.7). The guide arrives as a *file* via `init-agents` in a clean clone — not injected into the prompt, which is what invalidated my first attempt.\n\nA2 ≈ A1, so **the wording did the work; the hook added nothing measurable** on this task class.\n\n## Outcome — no benefit, and the third bar failed\n\n| arm | solved | turns | cost | tokens |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| A0 | 9/10 | 16 | 47¢ | 666k |\n| A1 | 9/10 | 14 | 43¢ | 642k |\n| A2 | 9/10 | 14 | 44¢ | 680k |\n\nIdentical outcome, overlapping CIs everywhere. Task 10 failed in all three arms — symmetric, so it drops nothing.\n\nAnd the bar I pre-registered as the one that matters **failed**:\n\n> used-then-abandoned: A1 **6/10** [0.30, 0.90] — pre-registered pass was ≤3/10\n\n**In 6 of 10 sessions the agent did exactly as instructed, got a non-answer, and went back to grep.** That is the recall failure in [#319](https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/issues/319), measured rather than anecdotal, and it is not mine to fix.\n\n## The honest verdict\n\n**Usage is fixed. Value is not demonstrated.** Both halves are real results and I'd be misreporting if I led with the first.\n\nThree defects found and fixed, each by a different method and none visible from source: the hook was **installed and inert** (named a nonexistent env var), brain's documented install delivered **no Graph directive at all**, and two competing \"first action\" absolutes made the agent **silently drop Brain**.\n\nBut two limits bound what round 1 can claim, both my own design errors:\n\n- **The fixture had no relationships.** graphmark: one function with 3+ cross-file callers. Nothing multi-hop existed to find.\n- **The tasks were grep's home ground.** Ten single-file locate questions.\n\nSo round 1 cannot distinguish the tool from grep — and with 6/10 abandonment, the agents were telling me that directly. Round 2 is designed and recorded: `cli` as fixture (10/40 density vs ~1), a relationship stratum, the sequence fix in place, and `solved on the relationship stratum: A1 > A0` pre-registered as the value test."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1069,"cache_read_input_tokens":679942,"output_tokens":1050,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1069,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1050,"cache_read_input_tokens":679942,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1069,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1069},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"25e497b5-17d8-4773-b719-36e287bb1686","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CffTkRhJ4nCYpbP4QnX7S","type":"assistant","uuid":"70473cdd-77f8-4954-9cff-5f833736969a","timestamp":"2026-10-03T14:29:02.873Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/cli","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"70473cdd-77f8-4954-9cff-5f833736969a","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"b1a03f2a-079c-465f-baae-7e4bbf16fb57","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"Stop hook feedback:\n[fully fix brain and underlying graoh usage of agnets and indidual verify with subangets in a clean env, and loop till fixed: tip- ask suabgntes for feedback/what went wrong]: The condition requires 'fully fix brain and underlying graph usage' with 'individual verify with subagents in a clean env, and loop till fixed' — meaning the cycle (fix → verify → feedback → repeat) must complete until no new blockers appear. Current state: (1) Three defects fixed in round 1 (hook stdin parsing, README activation ordering, competing first-action directives), (2) one complete round of verification with 30 sessions (n=10 per arm across A0/A1/A2) with feedback collected from agents, (3) two new design limitations identified (fixture had no relationships, tasks were grep's strength), and (4) round 2 designed with different fixture (cli instead of graphmark) and new task stratum (relationships instead of locate-only). However, round 2 has NOT YET RUN. The last message states 'Round 2 is designed and recorded' and 'solved on the relationship stratum: A1 > A0 pre-registered as the value test' but then stops. No second iteration of the loop (fix → verify → feedback on round 2) has executed. The condition is not met until round 2 completes, feedback from that round is collected and analyzed, and either (a) no new blockers emerge, or (b) all remaining blockers are product decisions rather than fixable defects."},"isMeta":true,"uuid":"03928908-c7e9-4965-b109-594c534d887c","timestamp":"2026-10-03T14:29:10.829Z","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/cli","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
