{"parentUuid":"be1f00e7-e185-4a62-8340-8d8329ea2f49","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"task_reminder","content":[],"itemCount":0},"type":"attachment","uuid":"40c2ef12-e430-46a4-880e-ae386b38a3d3","timestamp":"2026-10-03T15:16:00.379Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nThe task tools haven't been used recently. If you're working on tasks that would benefit from tracking progress, consider using TaskCreate to add new tasks and TaskUpdate to update task status (set to in_progress when starting, completed when done). Also consider cleaning up the task list if it has become stale. Only use these if relevant to the current work. This is just a gentle reminder - ignore if not applicable.\n\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"40c2ef12-e430-46a4-880e-ae386b38a3d3","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14815380 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"d547b696-c24c-4321-8fba-237b3cf2aa79","timestamp":"2026-10-03T15:16:00.380Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14815380 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"d547b696-c24c-4321-8fba-237b3cf2aa79","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CffXMNcach4ASyU8oDxea","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Round 2 is at 7/30 with everything downstream pre-built so there's no gap when it lands: the stratified scorer and the 20-turn feedback collector are both written and ready to fire.\n\nThree things about round 2's design that make it a genuinely different test from round 1, rather than a rerun:\n\n**The tasks are now grep-hostile.** Five of the ten ask *\"which files call X, and what breaks if its signature changes\"* on symbols verified to have 5–8 cross-file callers. Grep finds call sites; it can't tell you what breaks. The other five stay grep-friendly as a control, so the result shows *where* the tool helps rather than only whether it gets used.\n\n**Relationship scoring is recall, not binary.** File-set recall against ground truth derived by grep over the fixture — \"named 4 of 7 callers\" is a real result and a binary would throw that away.\n\n**Locate scoring uses accept-sets.** Because my first heuristic ground truth was **wrong on 2 of 5**, and grading binary against it would have produced noise I might have reported as signal.\n\nI also caught the arm asymmetry before it mattered: cli ships its own `PreToolUse` capture hook, and my B1 arm had stripped that too. Fixed, four sessions discarded, relaunched — so the arms now differ only in the brain pre-edit entry.\n\nFeedback deliberately runs as a **separate** `--resume` turn. Putting \"did you use the tools?\" in the task prompt would name a tool to an arm that has no guide, which is the asymmetric-help trap that killed earlier A/Bs in this project."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1527,"cache_read_input_tokens":705079,"output_tokens":525,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"serve