{"parentUuid":"6f481f5f-4f5b-468e-ad6a-d5b34ffb8162","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CffXwfVnN58cbX8kpT6Pm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HJm39sUBPoVd1Cn37Bpr12","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"E=/Users/suhaan/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp/cleanenv; R2=\"$E/r2\"\ncat > \"$R2/FINDINGS-round2.md\" <<'EOF'\n# Round 2 result, and two methodological errors of mine\n\n## Numbers (n=9-10 per arm, cli fixture, sequence-fix guide)\n            used a tool   tool-first   REL file-recall   LOC solved\nB0 no guide     0/9          0/9          1.00             3/5\nB1 guide        2/9          2/9          1.00             4/5\nB2 guide+hook   8/9          8/9          1.00             2/5\nShim log agrees: B1 made 2 locate calls, B2 made 9.\n\n## ERROR 1: the B1/B2 split has no mechanism, so I do not believe it\nB1 and B2 have byte-identical guides and settings that differ ONLY by the\npre-edit hook group -- verified by diff. That hook matches Edit|Write|MultiEdit\nand CANNOT fire on a read-only locate task. So there is no causal path from the\nonly configured difference to a 2/9 vs 8/9 gap.\nFisher exact p ~ 0.015, which is exactly why a p-value without a mechanism is\nnot evidence. This project has measured 100% run-level variance before\n(same instance twice, r = -0.022). Treat as variance until replicated.\n\n## ERROR 2: round 2 cannot be compared to round 1\nI changed THREE things at once: fixture (graphmark -> cli), task stratum\n(locate-only -> relationship+locate), and guide wording (MUST -> ordered\nsequence). So the A1=10/10 vs B1=2/9 drop cannot be attributed to the guide\nchange, the fixture, or the tasks. That is a confounded design and the fault is\nmine.\n\n## ERROR 3: the \"grep-hostile\" stratum was not grep-hostile\nREL file-set recall is 1.00 in EVERY arm, including the arm with no guide at\nall. Listing the files that call a symbol is exactly what grep does well. The\npart grep cannot do -- \"what breaks if the signature changes\" -- is not captured\nby file-set recall, so my own metric measured the greppable half of the question.\nThird task-design failure in a row, same root cause: I keep choosing tasks whose\nanswer a text search can reach.\n\n## Decisive next test\nReplicate B1 vs B2 at the same config. If the hook has no effect, a rerun should\nscramble which arm is high. If B2 is high again, the hook is doing something and\nthe mechanism needs finding.\nEOF\necho \"recorded\"\n# replication: same config, fresh sessions\nfor arm in B1 B2; do\n  d=$(ls -d /Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/*cleanenv-r2-$arm 2>/dev/null | head -1)\n  [ -n \"$d\" ] && mkdir -p \"${d:?}/../r2keep-$arm\" && cp \"$d\"/*.jsonl \"${d:?}/../r2keep-$arm/\" 2>/dev/null\ndone\necho \"round-2 transcripts backed up before replication\"","description":"Record round-2 errors and back up transcripts","timeout":900000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1400,"cache_read_input_tokens":717617,"output_tokens":2365,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1098},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1400,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2365,"cache_read_input_tokens":717617,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1400,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1400},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01HJm39sUBPoVd1Cn37Bpr12":{"command":"E=/Users/suhaan/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp/cleanenv; R2=\"$E/r2\"\ncat > \"$R2/FINDINGS-round2.md\" <<'EOF'\n# Round 2 result, and two methodological errors of mine\n\n## Numbers (n=9-10 per arm, cli fixture, sequence-fix guide)\n            used a tool   tool-first   REL file-recall   LOC solved\nB0 no guide     0/9          0/9          1.00             3/5\nB1 guide        2/9          2/9          1.00             4/5\nB2 guide+hook   8/9          8/9          1.00             2/5\nShim log agrees: B1 made 2 locate calls, B2 made 9.\n\n## ERROR 1: the B1/B2 split has no mechanism, so I do not believe it\nB1 and B2 have byte-identical guides and settings that differ ONLY by the\npre-edit hook group -- verified by diff. That hook matches Edit|Write|MultiEdit\nand CANNOT fire on a read-only locate task. So there is no causal path from the\nonly configured difference to a 2/9 vs 8/9 gap.\nFisher exact p ~ 0.015, which is exactly why a p-value without a mechanism is\nnot evidence. This project has measured 100% run-level variance before\n(same instance twice, r = -0.022). Treat as variance until replicated.\n\n## ERROR 2: round 2 cannot be compared to round 1\nI changed THREE things at once: fixture (graphmark -> cli), task stratum\n(locate-only -> relationship+locate), and guide wording (MUST -> ordered\nsequence). So the A1=10/10 vs B1=2/9 drop cannot be attributed to the guide\nchange, the fixture, or the tasks. That is a confounded design and the fault is\nmine.\n\n## ERROR 3: the \"grep-hostile\" stratum was not grep-hostile\nREL file-set recall is 1.00 in EVERY arm, including the arm with no guide at\nall. Listing the files that call a symbol is exactly what grep does well. The\npart grep cannot do -- \"what breaks if the signature changes\" -- is not captured\nby file-set recall, so my own metric measured the greppable half of the question.\nThird task-design failure in a row, same root cause: I keep choosing tasks whose\nanswer a text search can reach.\n\n## Decisive next test\nReplicate B1 vs B2 at the same config. If the hook has no effect, a rerun should\nscramble which arm is high. If B2 is high again, the hook is doing something and\nthe mechanism needs finding.\nEOF\necho \"recorded\"\n# replication: same config, fresh sessions\nfor arm in B1 B2; do\n  d=$(ls -d /Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/*cleanenv-r2-$arm 2>/dev/null | head -1)\n  [ -n \"$d\" ] && mkdir -p \"${d:?}/../r2keep-$arm\" && cp \"$d\"/*.jsonl \"${d:?}/../r2keep-$arm/\" 2>/dev/null\ndone\necho \"round-2 transcripts backed up before replication\"","description":"Record round-2 errors and back up transcripts","timeout":900000}},"serverClassifierRequest":"b4dfce3b-52ea-43d6-95fc-ed34405628c6","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CffXweUXGnW1CJUAD9U1P","type":"assistant","uuid":"8747754f-8603-4c6c-8967-b13953732b7d","timestamp":"2026-10-03T15:24:18.051Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
