{"parentUuid":"5e9681e6-3e8d-4439-8d45-711aee6244ea","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14800405 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"02b14f01-2110-4546-96ab-9db50ee4a377","timestamp":"2026-10-03T15:24:18.614Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14800405 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"02b14f01-2110-4546-96ab-9db50ee4a377","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CffXz7PL3kFQbis471b9c","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Round 2 is complete, and it mostly taught me about my own methodology. I'm reporting it straight rather than picking the flattering reading.\n\n## The numbers\n\n| arm | used a tool | tool-first | REL file-recall | LOC solved |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| B0 no guide | 0/9 | 0/9 | **1.00** | 3/5 |\n| B1 guide | **2/9** | 2/9 | **1.00** | 4/5 |\n| B2 guide + hook | **8/9** | 8/9 | **1.00** | 2/5 |\n\n## Three errors, all mine\n\n**1. The B1/B2 split has no mechanism, so I don't believe it.** Their guides are byte-identical and their settings differ *only* by the pre-edit hook group — I diffed them. That hook matches `Edit|Write|MultiEdit` and **cannot fire on a read-only locate task**. There is no causal path from the one configured difference to a 2/9 vs 8/9 gap. Fisher exact gives p ≈ 0.015, which is precisely why a p-value without a mechanism isn't evidence. This project has already measured 100% run-level variance.\n\n**2. Round 2 can't be compared to round 1.** I changed three things at once — fixture, task stratum, *and* guide wording. So A1's 10/10 vs B1's 2/9 is uninterpretable. Confounded design, my fault.\n\n**3. My \"grep-hostile\" tasks weren't.** REL file-recall is **1.00 in every arm, including the one with no guide**. Listing a symbol's callers is exactly what grep is good at. The part grep genuinely can't do — *what breaks if the signature changes* — isn't captured by file-set recall, so my metric scored the greppable half of the question I'd designed to be ungreppable.\n\nThat's the third task-design failure in a row with the same root cause: I keep picking tasks a text search can reach.\n\n## What's established despite that\n\n**No-guide arms used the tools 0/9 and 0/10 across two fixtures and two task sets.** That replicates. And the three defects fixed are real regardless: the hook was installed-and-inert, brain's documented install shipped no Graph directive, and two competing absolutes made an agent drop Brain.\n\nWhat is *not* established is that usage improves outcomes — and after two rounds I now think my task design can't test that, which is a more useful conclusion than another null.\n\nRunning the decisive test now: replicate B1 vs B2 at identical config. If the hook does nothing, a rerun should scramble which arm is high."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2412,"cache_read_input_tokens":719017,"output_tokens":846,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2412,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":846,"cache_read_input_tokens":719017,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2412,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2412},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"34af94a3-82c2-48a2-a0f9-b48097372087","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CffXz5oKyoGt1jACgxZme","type":"assistant","uuid":"26532e7a-033a-4f9d-a11a-2483d251217d","timestamp":"2026-10-03T15:24:30.782Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"26532e7a-033a-4f9d-a11a-2483d251217d","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"beb7d680-d128-4b3b-b527-ab394af4b8e1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"Stop hook feedback:\n[fully fix brain and underlying graoh usage of agnets and indidual verify with subangets in a clean env, and loop till fixed: tip- ask suabgntes for feedback/what went wrong]: The condition requires 'fully fix brain and underlying graph usage' with 'individual verify with subagents in a clean env, and loop till fixed' — meaning the fix→verify→feedback→repeat cycle must complete until no new blockers appear. Current state: (1) Three defects were fixed in round 1 (hook stdin parsing, README activation ordering, competing first-action directives), (2) Round 1 was fully verified with 30 sessions and feedback collected from agents, (3) Round 2 was designed and run (30 sessions, n=10 per arm), but (4) Round 2 itself revealed THREE NEW METHODOLOGICAL ERRORS of the session's own design ('the B1/B2 split has no mechanism', 'round 2 cannot be compared to round 1 [confounded design]', 'the grep-hostile tasks weren't'). The transcript explicitly states 'Running the decisive test now: replicate B1 vs B2 at identical config' — indicating a third loop iteration has begun but not completed. The loop is not yet 'till fixed': the session identified that its own task design cannot test the outcome question it set out to answer ('I now think my task design can't test that'), has acknowledged three successive task-design failures, and is about to run a replication that has not yet executed or been scored. No iteration of the loop has ended with 'no new blockers appear' — each round has surfaced new defects or design limitations requiring further iteration."},"isMeta":true,"uuid":"e843893e-d8e6-491b-bd23-bdd6060d1843","timestamp":"2026-10-03T15:24:38.008Z","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","s