{"parentUuid":"028b6530-a1a7-4d7a-9319-1ecc24f11c7f","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14796346 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"3a8ed62d-7157-4273-b5ad-6943f7d2c4b2","timestamp":"2026-10-03T15:26:59.616Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14796346 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"3a8ed62d-7157-4273-b5ad-6943f7d2c4b2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CffYByg4sxdi7jgCKCgbn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Y6vzPzSZCYvkJHq1d27GXa","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"E=/Users/suhaan/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp/cleanenv; R2=\"$E/r2\"\ncat > \"$R2/ROUND3-DESIGN.md\" <<'EOF'\n# Round 3: a task whose outcome grep cannot fake\n\n## The problem with rounds 1 and 2\nThree task sets in a row were answerable by text search, so every arm scored\nthe same and the outcome question stayed open. The root cause was constant: I\ngraded on whether the answer NAMED the right thing, and naming is exactly what\ngrep delivers.\n\n## The fix: grade on a COMPILE, not on prose\nTask: \"Add a parameter to <symbol>, update every call site, and leave\n`go build ./...` passing.\"\n\nWhy this cannot be faked by a text search:\n  - An incomplete caller set does not produce a worse-sounding answer, it\n    produces a BUILD FAILURE. The grade is objective and binary.\n  - `go build` is the ground truth, so there is no ground-truth derivation of\n    mine to get wrong -- which I did twice (2 of 5 locate answers, and the\n    file-recall metric that scored the greppable half).\n  - It is precisely what `entire graph impact` claims to answer, so if the tool\n    has value on relationships, it shows up here or nowhere.\n\n## Targets (verified 5-8 cross-file callers, Go, cli fixture)\n  AlreadyRedacted (7), AsTextGenerator (8), AbsPath (5),\n  AllProtectedDirs (5), AppendReviewEnv (5)\nInterface-returning symbols like AsTextGenerator are the hardest: callers can\nsatisfy an interface without naming the function, so grep under-counts.\n\n## Metrics\n  PRIMARY   build passes after the change        (objective, binary)\n  SECONDARY turns and cost to get there\n  USAGE     used a tool / tool-first             (as before)\n  MECHANISM the agent's own account of what the tool returned\n\n## Arms\nSame three as before, same guide, same pinned binaries. Each arm gets a FRESH\nclone per task, because a task mutates the repo and a failed attempt would\ncontaminate the next one.\n\n## Pre-registered, before any session runs\n  build-pass rate: B1 > B0 on the same tasks, or the tool does not help on the\n  question class it exists for -- and that is the finding, not a prompt to try\n  a fourth task design.\nEOF\necho \"round 3 designed\"\necho \"replication: $(grep -c 'exit=' \"$R2/rep1/progress.txt\" 2>/dev/null)/20\"","description":"Design round 3 around a compile-verified outcome","timeout":900000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1061,"cache_read_input_tokens":724508,"output_tokens":975,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1061,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":975,"cache_read_input_tokens":724508,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1061,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1061},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Y6vzPzSZCYvkJHq1d27GXa":{"command":"E=/Users/suhaan/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp/cleanenv; R2=\"$E/r2\"\ncat > \"$R2/ROUND3-DESIGN.md\" <<'EOF'\n# Round 3: a task whose outcome grep cannot fake\n\n## The problem with rounds 1 and 2\nThree task sets in a row were answerable by text search, so every arm scored\nthe same and the outcome question stayed open. The root cause was constant: I\ngraded on whether the answer NAMED the right thing, and naming is exactly what\ngrep delivers.\n\n## The fix: grade on a COMPILE, not on prose\nTask: \"Add a parameter to <symbol>, update every call site, and leave\n`go build ./...` passing.\"\n\nWhy this cannot be faked by a text search:\n  - An incomplete caller set does not produce a worse-sounding answer, it\n    produces a BUILD FAILURE. The grade is objective and binary.\n  - `go build` is the ground truth, so there is no ground-truth derivation of\n    mine to get wrong -- which I did twice (2 of 5 locate answers, and the\n    file-recall metric that scored the greppable half).\n  - It is precisely what `entire graph impact` claims to answer, so if the tool\n    has value on relationships, it shows up here or nowhere.\n\n## Targets (verified 5-8 cross-file callers, Go, cli fixture)\n  AlreadyRedacted (7), AsTextGenerator (8), AbsPath (5),\n  AllProtectedDirs (5), AppendReviewEnv (5)\nInterface-returning symbols like AsTextGenerator are the hardest: callers can\nsatisfy an interface without naming the function, so grep under-counts.\n\n## Metrics\n  PRIMARY   build passes after the change        (objective, binary)\n  SECONDARY turns and cost to get there\n  USAGE     used a tool / tool-first             (as before)\n  MECHANISM the agent's own account of what the tool returned\n\n## Arms\nSame three as before, same guide, same pinned binaries. Each arm gets a FRESH\nclone per task, because a task mutates the repo and a failed attempt would\ncontaminate the next one.\n\n## Pre-registered, before any session runs\n  build-pass rate: B1 > B0 on the same tasks, or the tool does not help on the\n  question class it exists for -- and that is the finding, not a prompt to try\n  a fourth task design.\nEOF\necho \"round 3 designed\"\necho \"replication: $(grep -c 'exit=' \"$R2/rep1/progress.txt\" 2>/dev/null)/20\"","description":"Design round 3 around a compile-verified outcome","timeout":900000}},"serverClassifierRequest":"50434a45-4b06-4fc6-9025-ee0e5fced0b9","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CffYBwtQdn33WaGNfXCeA","type":"assistant","uuid":"4aabdadd-188f-44a8-89ca-6