{"parentUuid":"dce7f745-de08-4ef6-b592-918975c94e1d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CffYf9n2RBGpyYRZ7NF9c","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The replication is decisive, so I'll stop here and report.\n\n## The anomaly was variance, confirmed\n\n| | round 2 | replication |\n|---|---|---|\n| B1 locate calls | 2 | **19** |\n| B2 locate calls | 9 | **11** |\n| higher arm | B2 | **B1** — reversed |\n\nIdentical config both times. The ordering flipped and the gap closed, which is exactly what I predicted from the *absence* of a mechanism — an `Edit|Write` hook cannot affect read-only tasks. **Round 2's p ≈ 0.015 was noise**, and I'm glad I didn't report it as the hook working.\n\nOne caveat on the table above: the shim log is complete and ordered (B1=19, B2=11), but the transcript scorer only resolved 4 sessions per arm this pass, so I'm quoting the shim log and flagging that the per-session rates in that output are under-read.\n\n## What's established\n\n**Usage is fixed.** No-guide arms used the tools **0/9 and 0/10** across two fixtures and two task sets. Guide arms always used them. That replicates and is the thing I was asked to fix.\n\n**Three real defects fixed**, each found a different way — none visible from source:\n- the pre-edit hook named a nonexistent env var: **installed and inert**\n- brain's documented install shipped **no Graph directive at all**\n- two competing \"first action\" absolutes made an agent **silently drop Brain**\n\nAll three are committed on `fix/agent-guide-directive-and-discovery` (PR #331's branch), weakening-verified. PRs #329–#331 remain **unmerged**.\n\n**Value is not established**, and after three rounds I know why: I kept grading on whether the answer *named* the right thing, and naming is what grep does. That's a grading flaw, not a task-wording one.\n\n## What's left\n\n1. **Round 3 is designed, not run** (`ROUND3-DESIGN.md`): grade on `go build ./...` passing after a signature change. An incomplete caller set becomes a build failure, which grep can't fake and I can't mis-derive. Pre-registered: build-pass B1 > B0, or the tool doesn't help on its own question class.\n2. **Round 2's feedback turns** were still running in background when I stopped — transcripts are on disk at `cleanenv/r2/logs/fb-*.txt` if you want them.\n3. [entire-graph#319](https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/issues/319) is filed; ranking/recall stays with Codex under the study-7 prereg.\n\n**Your usage limit was reached** — that's why I'm stopping rather than running round 3. Background feedback sessions may still be finishing; `pkill -f feedback.sh` stops them if you'd rather they didn't."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1312,"cache_read_input_tokens":728168,"output_tokens":1200,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":285},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1312,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1200,"cache_read_input_tokens":728168,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1312,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1312},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"c834c200-5494-4ae4-92d4-c48120ba54d9","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CffYf8FG41mu1bU7e9VPg","type":"assistant","uuid":"064fed8a-f17b-4496-83ef-91427be68b0e","timestamp":"2026-10-03T15:33:27.213Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1