{"parentUuid":"e7ad2307-fbe8-4002-8136-4775484cb12f","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14984255 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"a45edc04-82ea-4d0e-90e7-f0a79704ad62","timestamp":"2026-10-03T21:46:37.792Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14984255 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"a45edc04-82ea-4d0e-90e7-f0a79704ad62","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cfg393bFqtv2mpkWaq16B","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Round 3 is producing a result I didn't anticipate, and it reframes the whole question.\n\n## C0 — no guide — is passing\n\nBoth targets so far pass the strict `build` + `vet` gate. That's a 7-caller and an 8-caller signature change across a 1390-file Go repo, done with grep and no tooling.\n\nThe reason is something I should have seen three rounds ago: **the compiler is itself the impact tool.** An agent doesn't need to enumerate callers upfront — it changes the signature, runs `go build`, reads the errors, fixes them, repeats. `go build` *is* a complete, authoritative caller list, delivered for free.\n\nThat's why no task design I've tried could separate the arms. It isn't that my tasks were too easy, or that I graded the wrong thing — in a compiled language with a fast build, **the thing `entire graph impact` provides is already available more reliably from the toolchain.**\n\n## What that means for the discriminator\n\nIf C1 also passes 3/3, pass/fail is saturated and the only place value could show is **turns-to-green** — whether knowing the callers in advance is cheaper than discovering them from compiler errors. I'm capturing `num_turns` per session, so that comparison is available either way.\n\nThat's a narrower and more honest claim than anything the earlier rounds could have supported: the tool's value proposition on Go refactors has to be *efficiency*, not *capability*, because the compiler already guarantees capability.\n\nC1 launches automatically once its clones finish indexing, then I'll report both arms on pass-rate and turns."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1169,"cache_read_input_tokens":745383,"output_tokens":509,"output_tokens_de