{"parentUuid":"2b143150-d114-4d79-8d76-00b045bc56bc","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14982049 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"3c834187-3087-45e8-ac25-08af3f9953c8","timestamp":"2026-10-03T21:47:12.445Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14982049 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"3c834187-3087-45e8-ac25-08af3f9953c8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cfg3Bc1wpCXx4EPoS7rju","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here's where it stands.\n\n## C0 — the control — finished 3/3 PASS\n\n| target | callers | strict gate |\n|---|---|---|\n| `AlreadyRedacted` | 7 | **PASS** |\n| `AsTextGenerator` | 8 | **PASS** |\n| `AppendReviewEnv` | 5 | **PASS** |\n\nNo guide, no tooling. Grep plus the compiler did multi-file signature changes across a 1390-file Go repo, and passed `go build` *and* `go vet`.\n\n## C1 prep is genuinely slow, not hung\n\nIt's alive and working — `entire brain setup` is running on C1-t1 right now, plus two `memory worker` processes. But the prep log hasn't advanced in **7+ minutes**, and 3 clones have taken ~30 min, so `setup` on cli is costing roughly 6–10 min each. Three more to go, so ~20–30 min before C1's sessions can even start.\n\nNot stuck, just expensive. I'll let it run.\n\n## The result is already fairly clear, and it isn't what I expected\n\nC0 passing 3/3 means **pass/fail is saturated** — so even if C1 goes 3/3, the metric can't separate them. The reason is one I should have spotted three rounds back: **`go build` *is* an impact tool**, and a better one than any index. The agent changes a signature, compiles, reads the exact list of broken call sites, fixes them, repeats. It never needs to know the callers in advance.\n\nThat's why no task design I tried could discriminate. Not too-easy tasks, not wrong grading — in a compiled language with a fast build, the capability `entire graph impact` sells is already guaranteed by the toolchain.\n\nSo the only place value can show is **turns-to-green**: is knowing the callers upfront cheaper than discovering them from compiler errors? I'm capturing `num_turns`, so I'll have that comparison when C1 lands.\n\nNet so far: **usage is fixed and replicated** (0/9 and 0/10 in no-guide arms, p = 1.1 × 10⁻⁵ in round 1), three real defects fixed, and the round-2 anomaly shown to be noise. What's still open is whether the usage buys anything — and the honest answer is trending toward \"not on Go refactors, because the compiler already does it.\""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1060,"cache_read_input_tokens":747884,"output_tokens":765,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1060,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":765,"cache_read_input_tokens":747884,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1060,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1060},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"d7dc87e8-e3e2-42fa-b707-2e4270254efa","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cfg3BZzuRCVoorcKzgTyx","type":"assistant","uuid":"ad562302-30aa-40c7-a717-efad32b53346","timestamp":"2026-10-03T21:47:25.447Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
