{"parentUuid":"ae5f883e-3fd6-4f13-9a1f-dd319e5ffcef","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14979038 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"7ddc0a45-34c5-443c-b059-6e6e3580c7d6","timestamp":"2026-10-03T21:51:56.292Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14979038 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"7ddc0a45-34c5-443c-b059-6e6e3580c7d6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cfg3Ya3i9a8CHv4N7SQCK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Monitor armed to launch C1 the moment prep finishes, then signal completion.\n\n**Where it's looking, honestly:**\n\nThe usage question is answered and replicated — **that part is fixed.** Three real defects came out of it, each found by a different method, and one of them (the inert hook) was my own bug that only a clean-environment probe could expose.\n\nThe value question is converging on a negative, for a reason that's more interesting than the number: **`go build` is a better impact tool than any index.** It returns the exact, complete, authoritative list of broken call sites for free. C0 proved it — 3/3 on 5-to-8-caller signature changes, grep only.\n\nSo if C1 also goes 3/3, the finding is that on Go refactors the tool can only compete on *efficiency*, not *capability* — and with C0 at a median of 13 turns, there isn't much headroom to win.\n\nThat would make the overall verdict: the guide fixes get agents to use the tools, and on this question class the tools don't yet earn the call. Which, combined with the 6/10 abandonment in round 1 and the recall failures in [#319](https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/issues/319), points at the same conclusion from three directions — **the bottleneck is what the tool returns, not whether agents reach for it.**\n\nI'll report C1's pass-rate and turns against the 13-turn bar when it lands."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":694,"cache_read_input_tokens":751076,"output_tokens":447,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":694,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inferen