{"parentUuid":"29a25e1c-4408-451d-b21c-1e109cda412f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cfg5jfqkz3Jv8Ve3er7P3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"C1 is running with its first result matching C0 (PASS on the 7-caller target). Two sessions to go, then I'll have the full comparison against C0's bar of 3/3 at a median of 13 turns.\n\nThe loop has now run three full rounds, and the picture is consistent across all of them:\n\n**Fixed and verified.** Agents use the tools. No-guide arms: 0/9, 0/10, and 0/3 across three rounds, two fixtures, three task designs. Guide arms: used them, tool-first. Three real defects fixed along the way, each caught by a different method — the inert hook by a clean-env probe, the missing Graph directive by a clean install, and the dropped-Brain collision by **asking the agent what went wrong**, which was your tip and the only thing that could have surfaced it.\n\n**Not fixed, and not mine.** What the tool returns. Round 1 measured 6/10 abandonment; #319 shows the right answer absent from the result set on two repos and two languages; round 3 shows `go build` already supplying a complete caller list for free. Three independent routes to the same conclusion.\n\n**Four of my own errors caught mid-loop**, which I'd rather flag than bury: a scoring/feedback race, an arm asymmetry where I'd stripped cli's own capture hook, ground truth wrong on 2 of 5 answers, and three successive task designs that graded the greppable half of the question.\n\nI'll post C1's final pass-rate and turns when the last two sessions land."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":539,"cache_read_input_tokens":757151,"output_tokens":486,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_inp