{"type":"pr-link","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","prNumber":330,"prUrl":"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/330","prRepository":"entireio/entire-brain","timestamp":"2026-10-03T22:51:07.876Z"}
{"parentUuid":"20a49abe-d48f-4303-9c98-76722b8bce6a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cfg82zZ7AKANdpTvTYUkZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Short answer: not from the benchmark evidence, but round 3 is the first thing I've seen that argues otherwise — and the reason is specific.**\n\n## What the benchmark says (and it's not good)\n\nThe honest, out-of-sample figure from the paired SWE-bench work is **cost +2.49%, CI [−6.83, +11.18], median negative**. The interval crosses zero and the median goes the wrong way. The exhaustive analysis put the *fair ceiling* at ~+15%, and a perfect difficulty oracle at +8.3% — so even best-case isn't transformative.\n\nTwo things from that work matter here:\n\n- **Graph is a ~1:1 substitute** — it displaces 0.980 exploration calls per call made. To get 10% you'd need 3.28 displaced per call.\n- **The savings were causally the frugality prompt, not graph.** Unclamped, −25.8% collapsed to −0.9%.\n\nAlso: don't quote any published *token* number from that work. The harness read `usage.*` instead of `modelUsage`, which is arm-dependent and wrong by up to 36×. The cost numbers stand.\n\n## What round 3 measured\n\n| task | C0 tokens | C1 tokens | delta |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| t1 (7 callers) | 1,277,601 | 930,540 | **−27.2%** |\n| t2 (8 callers) | 1,110,344 | 958,820 | **−13.6%** |\n| t3 (5 callers) | 696,496 | 612,704 | **−12.0%** |\n\n**Mean −17.6%, all three the same sign**, turns 13/14/9 → 9/10/7. Summed from `modelUsage`, the canonical source.\n\nn=3, so that's a signal, not a result. But the mechanism is coherent: **graph saves by deleting locate turns**, so savings scale with how much of a session is exploration. SWE-bench instances are mostly *reasoning* about a known bug; a multi-file refactor is mostly *finding call sites*. Round 3 is the task shape where the mechanism should pay, and it did.\n\n## The thing blocking real savings\n\nRight now, in **6 of 10** sessions, the agent calls the tool, gets a non-answer, and *then* greps. It pays for both. That's not a saving — it's a tax.\n\nSo the arithmetic is:\n\n- today: 4/10 save, 6/10 pay double → near zero, which is exactly the +2.49%\n- fix recall: those 6 convert from tax to saving\n\n**Retrieval recall is the whole lever.** Not wording, not the hook — those are done and verified. Which is why [#319](https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/issues/319) and study 7 matter more for token economics than everything in my seven PRs combined.\n\n## My honest estimate, post-merge\n\n**On refactor/locate-heavy work: plausibly 10–20%**, if round 3 holds at larger n. **On SWE-bench-shaped reasoning work: ~0%**, and that's measured, not guessed.\n\nI would not put a single blended number in a launch. The defensible claim is conditional: *\"saves tokens on exploration-heavy tasks, in proportion to how much exploration the task needs\"* — with round 3 as the evidence and n=3 stated.\n\nThe cheap next step is replicating round 3 at n=10–15 on a second repo. If −17.6% survives, you have a real, mechanism-backed number for a specific task class. That's worth more than a bigger number nobody can defend."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2307,"cache_read_input_tokens":780491,"output_tokens":1157,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2307,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1157,"cache_read_input_tokens":780491,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2307,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2307},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"a29b3758-0f20-4052-83d1-48dd714c19e1","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cfg82xaYD1p8NUWKdXGP6","type":"assistant","uuid":"209b4fb0-1bf8-493e-b642-515e2afca6f9","timestamp":"2026-10-03T22:51:07.765Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
