{"parentUuid":"29162009-7b44-4c4c-a7a6-8f1ddd44050b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cfg8DHSswkaDT2LD3NaSX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Confound confirmed, and it's important.** My user-level `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` — which literally says *\"query the brain + graph BEFORE grepping\"* — was in context for **both** arms.\n\nIt's symmetric, so the A/B holds. But it changes the interpretation, and in a direction that strengthens the result: the control arm **had** a user-level instruction to use brain/graph and still used them **0/10**, while the repo-level guide arm used them every time.\n\nLet me tell the peer, since they're blocked on exactly this:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1695,"cache_read_input_tokens":787342,"output_tokens":2038,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":610},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1695,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2038,"cache_read_input_tokens":787342,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1695,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1695},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"d699712c-fa62-4783-aa56-16dd84ebe8d9","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cfg8DFx6dWwCAQ89rET1U","type":"assistant","uuid":"051c2d1c-fab4-4155-a6b4-03823766f277","timestamp":"2026-10-03T22:53:24.804Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"051c2d1c-fab4-4155-a6b4-03823766f277","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cfg8DHSswkaDT2LD3NaSX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018JDmaXtCNSgYsaxi7w3TNR","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"redesign-graph-cost-reduction","summary":"launch line + a confound you must avoid","message":"My launch line was NOT clean, and I only just found it — check this before you copy anything from me.\n\nExact line I used:\n  cd <arm clone>\n  export PATH=\"<shim dir>:$PATH\" ARM=<arm>\n  unset ENTIRE_REPO_ROOT\n  claude -p \"<task>\" --model sonnet --dangerously-skip-permissions --output-format json\n\nSo: no --setting-sources, no --strict-mcp-config, no separate CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR. OAuth worked because I changed nothing about auth, but that is the whole problem — everything user-level came along.\n\nTHE CONFOUND: my own ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md contains \"query the brain + graph BEFORE grepping\" and an entire-sem/brain-MCP cheatsheet. I grepped the arm transcripts for that text and it IS present in both the guide arm and the no-guide arm. So my \"no guide\" arm was really \"no REPO guide, user-level brain/graph instruction still in context\".\n\nTwo consequences, and the second one may be useful to you:\n1. It is symmetric across arms, so the A/B comparison survives. I am disclosing it rather than rerunning, and labelling the control \"no repo-level guide\" instead of \"no guide\".\n2. The result is arguably stronger than I first reported: the control arm HAD a user-level instruction telling it to use brain and graph, and used them 0/10 anyway, while the repo-level guide arm used them 10/10. A user-level CLAUDE.md line did not move behaviour; the repo-level guide did. If that holds for you it is worth knowing on its own.\n\nFor your run I would isolate properly rather than repeat my mistake: a separate CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR pointed at a scratch dir is the blunt instrument that takes user memory, user settings, hooks and MCP out in one move, and it keeps OAuth if you copy only the credentials file into it. --setting-sources project and --strict-mcp-config are narrower and I have not verified either, so do not take them from me as working.\n\nHOW TO VERIFY CLEANLINESS (this is the part I did too late): grep the resulting transcript for a distinctive string from your own ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md. If it appears, the session loaded it. Also ask one throwaway session to list its MCP servers — my note from earlier work is that --safe-mode silently strips all MCP servers and the only reliable check is asking the model what tools it has.\n\nFEEDBACK-TURN FAILURE REASONS beyond recall, verbatim from my sessions:\n- \"My Python parse of its output also crashed on a missing symbol_name key.\" (already in #319)\n- \"A graph search that handled several unrelated questions at once would have helped. Better still would be per-question searches that return the right file, which I didn't try.\" — the agent batched one broad query for several questions instead of querying per question, then judged the tool on the batched result.\n- \"I also skipped entire brain brief entirely, which the guide recommends.\" — caused by two competing first-action absolutes in the combined guide. Your guide-side copy may have the same collision; Codex has it.\n- One structural one: on a Go refactor, `go build` returns a complete authoritative caller list for free, so the compiler out-competes the index on completeness. My round-3 arms both passed 3/3; graph's win there was turns (13->9 median) and tokens (-17.6%, n=3), not capability.","type":"message","recipient":"redesign-graph-cost-reduction","content":"My launch line was NOT clean, and I only just fou…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1695,"cache_read_input_tokens":787342,"output_tokens":2038,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":610},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1695,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2038,"cache_read_input_tokens":787342,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1695,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1695},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_018JDmaXtCNSgYsaxi7w3TNR":{"to":"redesign-graph-cost-reduction","summary":"launch line + a confound you must avoid","message":"My launch line was NOT clean, and I only just found it — check this before you copy anything from me.\n\nExact line I used:\n  cd <arm clone>\n  export PATH=\"<shim dir>:$PATH\" ARM=<arm>\n  unset ENTIRE_REPO_ROOT\n  claude -p \"<task>\" --model sonnet --dangerously-skip-permissions --output-format json\n\nSo: no --setting-sources, no --strict-mcp-config, no separate CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR. OAuth worked because I changed nothing about auth, but that is the whole problem — everything user-level came along.\n\nTHE CONFOUND: my own ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md contains \"query the brain + graph BEFORE grepping\" and an entire-sem/brain-MCP cheatsheet. I grepped the arm transcripts for that text and it IS present in both the guide arm and the no-guide arm. So my \"no guide\" arm was really \"no REPO guide, user-level brain/graph instruction still in context\".\n\nTwo consequences, and the second one may be useful to you:\n1. It is symmetric across arms, so the A/B comparison survives. I am disclosing it rather than rerunning, and labelling the control \"no repo-level guide\" instead of \"no guide\".\n2. The result is arguably stronger than I first reported: the control arm HAD a user-level instruction telling it to use brain and graph, and used them 0/10 anyway, while the repo-level guide arm used them 10/10. A user-level CLAUDE.md line did not move behaviour; the repo-level guide did. If that holds for you it is worth knowing on its own.\n\nFor your run I would isolate properly rather than repeat my mistake: a separate CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR pointed at a scratch dir is the blunt instrument that takes user memory, user settings, hooks and MCP out in one move, and it keeps OAuth if you copy only the credentials file into it. --setting-sources project and --strict-mcp-config are narrower and I have not verified either, so do not take them from me as working.\n\nHOW TO VERIFY CLEANLINESS (this is the part I did too late): grep the resulting transcript for a distinctive string from your own ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md. If it appears, the session loaded it. Also ask one throwaway session to list its MCP servers — my note from earlier work is that --safe-mode silently strips all MCP servers and the only reliable check is asking the model what tools it has.\n\nFEEDBACK-TURN FAILURE REASONS beyond recall, verbatim from my sessions:\n- \"My Python parse of its output also crashed on a missing symbol_name key.\" (already in #319)\n- \"A graph search that handled several unrelated questions at once would have helped. Better still would be per-question searches that return the right file, which I didn't try.\" — the agent batched one broad query for several questions instead of querying per question, then judged the tool on the batched result.\n- \"I also skipped entire brain brief entirely, which the guide recommends.\" — caused by two competing first-action absolutes in the combined guide. Your guide-side copy may have the same collision; Codex has it.\n- One structural one: on a Go refactor, `go build` returns a complete authoritative caller list for free, so the compiler out-competes the index on completeness. My round-3 arms both passed 3/3; graph's win there was turns (13->9 median) and tokens (-17.6%, n=3), not capability."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"d699712c-fa62-4783-aa56-16dd84ebe8d9","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Cfg8DFx6dWwCAQ89rET1U","type":"assistant","uuid":"d37edae6-fa5a-4257-a7a8-782442d18921","timestamp":"2026-10-03T22:53:42.693Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
