{"parentUuid":"4bf523dd-ed99-4501-b4e5-b42597fefde1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfgA3GTZRFbALUs1MGofy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I need to correct myself clearly: **brain's symbol search works, and the bug was in my probe.** I read a JSON key that doesn't exist (`symbols` instead of `results`), got zeros, and built a diagnosis on them. Everything downstream of that — \"entirely dead\", the schema-gate theory — was wrong.\n\nThe actual behaviour, measured correctly:\n\n| query | results | top hit |\n|---|---|---|\n| `runDistill` | 20 | `runDistill @ internal/cli/distill_cmd.go:666` ✅ |\n| `briefBranchBlindSpot` | 1 | `blind_spot.go:114` ✅ — the function I wrote today |\n| `brainBriefReport` | 20 | `agent_surface.go:217` ✅ |\n| `defaultDistillTimeout` | **0** | — |\n\nRank 1 is exact in every case it finds anything. **Brain's own symbol search is good** — notably better than the graph-search decoys I measured earlier.\n\nThe one real finding that survives: **`defaultDistillTimeout` returns nothing because package-level constants aren't indexed as symbols.** That's a genuine, narrow coverage gap, not a broken search.\n\nThat's the fourth false-pass I've caught in this session from suppressed or mis-keyed output, and the costliest — I was three steps into an incorrect root-cause story. The pattern is always the same shape: a probe that returns \"nothing\" when it should return an error.\n\nLet me verify the const gap is real before claiming it:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1133,"cache_read_input_tokens":839835,"output_tokens":835,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1133,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_availabl