{"parentUuid":"ba5774da-bf67-4dcb-a175-be3a91a5940f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfgA5hQnaGkwFHxsEhGCZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Finishing the two concrete items."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":852,"cache_read_input_tokens":842070,"output_tokens":1138,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":161},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":852,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1138,"cache_read_input_tokens":842070,"cache_creation_input_tokens":852,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":852},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"a0ff0c01-326e-4d57-b4ec-051d0a072afb","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfgA5dpjz4r62vBYrQf3s","type":"assistant","uuid":"89cf162b-bdef-4828-b9d8-9d9650deff80","timestamp":"2026-10-03T23:17:48.531Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"89cf162b-bdef-4828-b9d8-9d9650deff80","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfgA5hQnaGkwFHxsEhGCZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01F91MQRycTg5McPcy6tSCRK","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph 2>/dev/null || cd /Users/suhaan/devenv\ngh issue comment 319 --repo entireio/entire-graph --body \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nSecond, separate coverage gap found while measuring brain's retrieval: **Go package-level constants and vars are not indexed as symbols at all.**\n\nMeasured against the snapshot graph produced for `entireio/entire-brain` at `ae9e2f0b` (51,131 symbols, provider `v0.4.1-nightly.202609180615.5637039f`, schema 1.3):\n\n```sql\nsqlite> select kind, count(*) from symbols group by kind order by 2 desc;\nsection|31083\nfunction|10366\nfield|4633\nmethod|2773\ntype|978\ncode_fence|728\nclass|335\ndocument|123\ntool|55\nsetting|30\n```\n\nNo `const` and no `var` kind exists. Concretely:\n\n```\nentire brain inspect search-graph \"defaultDistillTimeout\"  -> 0 results\nsqlite> select name from symbols where name like '%DistillTimeout%';  -> (empty)\n```\n\n`defaultDistillTimeout = 10 * time.Minute` is a package-level const at `internal/cli/distill_cmd.go:37`, and it is consumed at `:631`. It is simply absent from the index.\n\nWhy it matters beyond the one symbol: tuning constants, default timeouts, size caps and feature-flag names are a common class of \"where is this configured\" question, and they are exactly the questions an agent would otherwise answer with grep. An index that silently lacks them trains the agent that the tool is unreliable for configuration questions — the same abandonment dynamic as the recall issue above, from a different cause.\n\n**Correction to something I implied in my earlier message:** I briefly believed brain's symbol search was broken entirely. It is not, and the fault was in my measurement — I read a `symbols` key from the JSON where the field is `results`, and treated the resulting zeros as data. Measured correctly, brain's symbol search returns exact rank-1 hits:\n\n| query | rank 1 |\n|---|---|\n| `runDistill` | `internal/cli/distill_cmd.go:666` |\n| `brainBriefReport` | `internal/cli/agent_surface.go:217` |\n| `briefBranchBlindSpot` | `internal/cli/blind_spot.go:114` |\n\nSo the name-based path is healthy. The two open gaps are the intent-phrased recall failure in the issue body and the missing const/var kinds here.\nEOF\n)\" 2>&1 | tail -1","description":"Add the const gap to issue 319","timeout":900000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":852,"cache_read_input_tokens":842070,"output_tokens":1138,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":161},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":852,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1138,"cache_read_input_tokens":842070,"cache_creation_input_tokens":852,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":852},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01F91MQRycTg5McPcy6tSCRK":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph 2>/dev/null || cd /Users/suhaan/devenv\ngh issue comment 319 --repo entireio/entire-graph --body \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nSecond, separate coverage gap found while measuring brain's retrieval: **Go package-level constants and vars are not indexed as symbols at all.**\n\nMeasured against the snapshot graph produced for `entireio/entire-brain` at `ae9e2f0b` (51,131 symbols, provider `v0.4.1-nightly.202609180615.5637039f`, schema 1.3):\n\n```sql\nsqlite> select kind, count(*) from symbols group by kind order by 2 desc;\nsection|31083\nfunction|10366\nfield|4633\nmethod|2773\ntype|978\ncode_fence|728\nclass|335\ndocument|123\ntool|55\nsetting|30\n```\n\nNo `const` and no `var` kind exists. Concretely:\n\n```\nentire brain inspect search-graph \"defaultDistillTimeout\"  -> 0 results\nsqlite> select name from symbols where name like '%DistillTimeout%';  -> (empty)\n```\n\n`defaultDistillTimeout = 10 * time.Minute` is a package-level const at `internal/cli/distill_cmd.go:37`, and it is consumed at `:631`. It is simply absent from the index.\n\nWhy it matters beyond the one symbol: tuning constants, default timeouts, size caps and feature-flag names are a common class of \"where is this configured\" question, and they are exactly the questions an agent would otherwise answer with grep. An index that silently lacks them trains the agent that the tool is unreliable for configuration questions — the same abandonment dynamic as the recall issue above, from a different cause.\n\n**Correction to something I implied in my earlier message:** I briefly believed brain's symbol search was broken entirely. It is not, and the fault was in my measurement — I read a `symbols` key from the JSON where the field is `results`, and treated the resulting zeros as data. Measured correctly, brain's symbol search returns exact rank-1 hits:\n\n| query | rank 1 |\n|---|---|\n| `runDistill` | `internal/cli/distill_cmd.go:666` |\n| `brainBriefReport` | `internal/cli/agent_surface.go:217` |\n| `briefBranchBlindSpot` | `internal/cli/blind_spot.go:114` |\n\nSo the name-based path is healthy. The two open gaps are the intent-phrased recall failure in the issue body and the missing const/var kinds here.\nEOF\n)\" 2>&1 | tail -1","description":"Add the const gap to issue 319","timeout":900000}},"serverClassifierRequest":"a0ff0c01-326e-4d57-b4ec-051d0a072afb","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CfgA5dpjz4r62vBYrQf3s","type":"assistant","uuid":"3a9441f9-f84a-4202-80b1-3bf00e4964f1","ti