{"parentUuid":"9d66da76-90e3-4772-8378-70d90353e1e2","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14939895 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"95ee788f-6513-4289-941f-fa156f25e487","timestamp":"2026-10-03T23:18:03.192Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14939895 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"95ee788f-6513-4289-941f-fa156f25e487","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfgA7SCJCHby9aGbtHz58","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GCkHunwnYNvxgRjZoEcVUh","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"redesign-graph-cost-reduction","summary":"const/var kinds missing from the index; plus a correction","message":"Second graph-side gap, added to #319: Go package-level consts and vars are not indexed as symbols at all.\n\nFrom the snapshot graph produced for entire-brain at ae9e2f0b (51,131 symbols, provider v0.4.1-nightly, schema 1.3):\n\n  select kind, count(*) from symbols group by kind order by 2 desc;\n  section 31083 | function 10366 | field 4633 | method 2773 | type 978\n  code_fence 728 | class 335 | document 123 | tool 55 | setting 30\n\nNo const kind, no var kind. Concretely `defaultDistillTimeout = 10 * time.Minute` at internal/cli/distill_cmd.go:37 (consumed at :631) is absent from the store entirely, so `inspect search-graph \"defaultDistillTimeout\"` returns 0 and grep is the only route.\n\nWhy I think it is worth more than its size: \"where is this timeout / cap / flag / default configured\" is a common question class, and it is precisely the one an agent would otherwise grep. An index that silently lacks it produces the same abandonment dynamic as the recall failure, from a different cause. It may also be cheap to fix relative to ranking work, since it is extraction coverage rather than scoring.\n\nA CORRECTION you should have, because I told you something adjacent earlier: I briefly concluded brain's symbol search was broken entirely. It is not. My probe read a `symbols` key from the JSON where the field is actually `results`, I read the zeros as data, and I got three steps into a schema-gate root-cause story before catching it. Measured properly, brain's name-based search is healthy and returns exact rank-1 hits: runDistill -> distill_cmd.go:666, brainBriefReport -> agent_surface.go:217, briefBranchBlindSpot -> blind_spot.go:114. Nothing I said about a schema-version gate was real; please discard it.\n\nSo from my side the standing graph-side items are exactly two, both in #319: intent-phrased recall (the deciders absent from the returned set, reproduced on two repos and two languages) and the missing const/var kinds. Brain-side I am not holding a known unfixed defect.\n\nSeparately, in case it saves you a cycle: my round-3 arms both passed 3/3 on compile-verified Go refactors, so pass/fail saturated and the only separation was efficiency — median turns 13 -> 9 and tokens -17.6% (n=3, all three pairs same sign). The reason is that `go build` already returns a complete authoritative caller list, so on compiled-language refactors the toolchain bounds how much capability an index can add. If your study measures value rather than usage, picking a task class where no compiler closes the loop will matter.","type":"message","recipient":"redesign-graph-cost-reduction","content":"Second graph-side gap, added to #319: Go package-…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1275,"cache_read_input_tokens":842922,"output_tokens":1013,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1275,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1013,"cache_read_input_tokens":842922,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1275,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1275},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01GCkHunwnYNvxgRjZoEcVUh":{"to":"redesign-graph-cost-reduction","summary":"const/var kinds missing from the index; plus a correction","message":"Second graph-side gap, added to #319: Go package-level consts and vars are not indexed as symbols at all.\n\nFrom the snapshot graph produced for entire-brain at ae9e2f0b (51,131 symbols, provider v0.4.1-nightly, schema 1.3):\n\n  select kind, count(*) from symbols group by kind order by 2 desc;\n  section 31083 | function 10366 | field 4633 | method 2773 | type 978\n  code_fence 728 | class 335 | document 123 | tool 55 | setting 30\n\nNo const kind, no var kind. Concretely `defaultDistillTimeout = 10 * time.Minute` at internal/cli/distill_cmd.go:37 (consumed at :631) is absent from the store entirely, so `inspect search-graph \"defaultDistillTimeout\"` returns 0 and grep is the only route.\n\nWhy I think it is worth more than its size: \"where is this timeout / cap / flag / default configured\" is a common question class, and it is precisely the one an agent would otherwise grep. An index that silently lacks it produces the same abandonment dynamic as the recall failure, from a different cause. It may also be cheap to fix relative to ranking work, since it is extraction coverage rather than scoring.\n\nA CORRECTION you should have, because I told you something adjacent earlier: I briefly concluded brain's symbol search was broken entirely. It is not. My probe read a `symbols` key from the JSON where the field is actually `results`, I read the zeros as data, and I got three steps into a schema-gate root-cause story before catching it. Measured properly, brain's name-based search is healthy and returns exact rank-1 hits: runDistill -> distill_cmd.go:666, brainBriefReport -> agent_surface.go:217, briefBranchBlindSpot -> blind_spot.go:114. Nothing I said about a schema-version gate was real; please discard it.\n\nSo from my side the standing graph-side items are exactly two, both in #319: intent-phrased recall (the deciders absent from the returned set, reproduced on two repos and two languages) and the missing const/var kinds. Brain-side I am not holding a known unfixed defect.\n\nSeparately, in case it saves you a cycle: my round-3 arms both passed 3/3 on compile-verified Go refactors, so pass/fail saturated and the only separation was efficiency — median turns 13 -> 9 and tokens -17.6% (n=3, all three pairs same sign). The reason is that `go build` already returns a complete authoritative caller list, so on compiled-language refactors the toolchain bounds how much capability an index can add. If your study measures value rather than usage, picking a task class where no compiler closes the loop will matter."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"01a29f32-f1ed-40be-9c91-caaaf0864354","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfgA7NbWD3pe6KFwZJT4R","type":"assistant","uuid":"13503d9a-96f1-439a-857d-320994ecc4a0","timestamp":"2026-10-03T23:18:20.394Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
