{"parentUuid":"4a0f74fb-b84b-42e6-b017-462e3e368b63","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfgAuj5qcrW7yTmCBSatj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014kAGs8GTA3xnqMSi2dw4ct","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Review brain PR 306","prompt":"Adversarial review of an UNMERGED PR in /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide (entire-brain). READ-ONLY: do not edit, commit, or push anything. Fetch the diff with `gh pr diff 306 --repo entireio/entire-brain`.\n\nPR #306 \"feat(facts): import memory from another tool\", +1744/-0 across 8 files including internal/cli/facts_import.go. It is queued to merge and has never been reviewed.\n\nHunt these SEVEN defect classes specifically. Every one has been found live in this codebase in the last day, so treat each as likely, not hypothetical:\n\n1. SILENT FAILURE — work is dropped, capped, skipped or filtered and the user is told nothing, or is told a number computed differently from how it is described. Real instances found here: a warning cap applied BEFORE persisting so the text existed nowhere; a reported count that counted the FILTERED set; a scan that stopped at a cap then printed \"no results found\".\n2. LOGIC IN THE CALL SITE — a correct helper that nothing calls, or is called on only one of several paths. Found 3x here: every unit test stayed green while the call site was neutered.\n3. INERT WIRING — something installed that cannot work. Found here: a hook passing \"$CLAUDE_FILE_PATH\", a variable the harness does not define, so it ran with an empty arg on every edit and served nothing while reporting success.\n4. UNFALSIFIABLE TEST — a test that passes with the behaviour removed. For any test in this PR, ask: if I deleted the line it guards, would it go red? Name the ones that would not.\n5. CONTAINMENT FOR EXACTNESS — a substring/shape assertion standing in for the exact check its name claims (strings.Contains where equality is meant; matching free prose where a parsed path is meant). A real bug here matched .brainignore patterns against prose and discarded every warning in the repo.\n6. PLATFORM ASSUMPTION — strings.HasPrefix(p,\"/\"), filepath assumptions, case-sensitivity. One shipped here: true for every absolute path a macOS/Linux test can build, false for every Windows one.\n7. EMPTY THAT DOES NOT EXPLAIN ITSELF — a result of zero that is indistinguishable from \"never built\", \"wrong branch\", \"unsupported kind\" or \"broken\".\n\nAlso check: does the import path validate or sanitise what it ingests from the foreign tool, and what happens on a partial/corrupt import — is the brain left in a half-imported state with no record?\n\nFor EVERY finding: file:line, the concrete input or state that triggers it, and what the user sees versus what is true. Default to REFUTED — if you cannot construct the failing case, say so and drop it. A review that confirms everything is suspicious; state your refutation rate.\n\nUse `rtk` for git/gh. Do not run the full test suite (it contends over a global data dir); narrow `go test -run` only if you need it.\n\nOUTPUT: caveman-ultra compressed. Findings ranked by severity, file:line each. Then refutation rate and anything you could not check. Max 400 words.","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"opus"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1266,"cache_read_input_tokens":863191,"output_tokens":2589,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":328},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1266,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2589,"cache_read_input_tokens":863191,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1266,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens"