md.go, retrieve_cmd.go\n#320 \"fix(remember): return the persisted merged fact in JSON\" (+56/-0): facts_write_cmd.go, facts_remember_revive_test.go\n\nBoth are queued to merge and unreviewed.\n\nHunt these defect classes, each found live in this codebase in the last day:\n1. UNFALSIFIABLE TEST — would the test go red if the behaviour it guards were removed? Check each added test by actually reasoning through the mutation. Name any that would stay green.\n2. LOGIC IN THE CALL SITE — a correct helper nothing calls, or called on only SOME paths. Found 3x here. For #318 specifically: it adds branch-naming to recall/retrieve — check whether EVERY surface that can return an empty fact set reaches it, or only some. `brain brief` was recently found to be missing from exactly this choke point.\n3. EMPTY THAT DOES NOT EXPLAIN ITSELF, or explains itself WRONGLY — e.g. a note that fires when the current branch IS the one holding facts, telling the user to retry where they already are. Construct that case for #318 and say whether it fires.\n4. SILENT FAILURE / MISREPORTED COUNT — a number described one way and computed another.\n5. CONTAINMENT FOR EXACTNESS — substring matching standing in for an exact or parsed comparison.\n6. For #320: does the returned JSON actually reflect what was PERSISTED, or what was computed in memory before the write? If a merge or supersede changed the record on disk, does the JSON match disk or the pre-write value? Construct the divergent case.\n\nFor EVERY finding: file:line, the triggering input/state, and user-visible symptom vs truth. Default to REFUTED — if you cannot construct the failing case, drop it and say so. Confirming everything is a red flag; report your refutation rate.\n\n`rtk` for git/gh. Do NOT run the full suite (global data dir contention); narrow `go test -run` only if needed.\n\nOUTPUT: caveman-ultra compressed. Per PR: findings with file:line, ranked by severity. Then refutation rate and what you could not check. Max 400 words.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2/tasks/a357e156f411e6ce9.output","canReadOutputFile":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"d7175d3b-5a7e-4f0b-9113-142438ac0f2d","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","root":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","branch":"fix/agent-guide-directive-and-discovery","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"entireio","host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"},{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-graph","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/entiredb","visibility":"private"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/cli","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b5bfe6f5-05ea-405c-9400-6cb7cfb5b836","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
