{"parentUuid":"4ef4795d-3952-432d-aff7-4917e073cc9d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfgAxYXAgpRBSQmoMF2Gq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Two adversarial reviewers are on the three unreviewed PRs, hunting the seven defect classes this session has found live — each told to default to *refuted* and report its refutation rate, since a review that confirms everything is a review that found nothing.\n\nThat's the last thing I can genuinely reach. To be concrete about where the boundary is:\n\n**Done and verified (brain side):** ten defects fixed, all weakening-verified, 14 packages green, lint clean. The newest — `inspect search-graph` now distinguishing *\"no such symbol\"* from *\"that kind isn't indexed\"* — came from a sweep I ran because I'd been misled by that exact message myself.\n\n**Owned elsewhere (graph side):** two gaps in [#319](https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/issues/319), both independently reproduced by the graph session and handed to Codex under the study-7 prereg. Taking them myself would mean crossing a lease I was explicitly asked not to cross.\n\n**Yours:** the seven merges.\n\nI'm not going to keep looping on that last one — it isn't an oversight I can engineer around. Two things would unblock it:\n\n- **approve the stack** (#329 → #330 → #331 in order, plus #306/#318/#320/#321 on main), or\n- **tell me to merge**, which overrides your standing instruction and I'll do it\n\nOnce the reviewers report, I'll either fix what they find or tell you the PRs are clean — and that's the last substantive brain-side work in front of me. After that, the benchmark pilot you asked about is ready to draft, built around round 3's finding since that's the only task class where the arms actually separated."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3418,"cache_read_input_tokens":864457,"