{"parentUuid":"96d68432-6e10-488d-a9e7-ba0eb15dd595","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfgC4NDamJd3Q6Z4xNAhk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Confirmed: `sanitizeDistilledFactText` exists, is called from `distill.go` only, and the import path doesn't use it. Let me record the full review on the PR — this is the kind of finding that should block a merge:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":977,"cache_read_input_tokens":891152,"output_tokens":2274,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":527},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":977,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2274,"cache_read_input_tokens":891152,"cache_creation_input_tokens":977,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":977},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"22fa912d-3a8e-4c33-9ef4-cf349c6c1a58","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfgC4KhHJU4hpnBS7YuWG","type":"assistant","uuid":"50bc135e-6666-4ea8-95b8-80cd03053e49","timestamp":"2026-10-03T23:43:48.540Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"50bc135e-6666-4ea8-95b8-80cd03053e49","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfgC4NDamJd3Q6Z4xNAhk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VTuUME8AsFCXiLmbSNDEhG","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide\ngh pr comment 306 --repo entireio/entire-brain --body \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nAdversarial pre-merge review. **13 confirmed, 12 refuted (48% refutation).** Flagging two as merge-blocking; the rest are recorded so they can be triaged rather than rediscovered.\n\n## Blocking\n\n**1. Imported fact text is never sanitised.** `facts_import.go:95`/`:286` store `m.Memory` verbatim. `sanitizeDistilledFactText` (`distill.go:483`) exists for exactly this and is called only from `distill.go:295`/`:512` — the import path skips it.\n\nAn export containing `{\"memory\":\"deploy ‮yadirF no reven\\u001b[31m\"}` is stored raw, and `printFactLine` (`facts_read_cmd.go:605`) plus the compact brief print `f.Text` unescaped. So ANSI, bidi overrides and zero-width characters from a foreign tool reach both the terminal and **the agent's prompt**. The PR bounds the input file's *size* as untrusted; it does not bound its *content*.\n\nFix is a call to the existing sanitiser on the import path.\n\n**2. `--path-prefix` bypasses the taxonomy.** `:199` validates the regex only; `:504` never calls `filterFactPathsByTaxonomy`/`loadFactTaxonomy`. The sibling surface treats this as a hard error — `facts_write_cmd.go:239-250`: *\"otherwise --path can mint immediately-orphaned facts the rest of the system treats as invalid\"*. So `--path-prefix notes.inbox` can import 400 facts that `factmerge.GC` (`admin.go:218`) reports as orphans while the command prints **\"imported 400 of 400\"**.\n\n## Worth fixing before or soon after\n\n**3.** The new `imported` origin bucket is added at `facts.go:407` and `facts_status_cmd.go:224` but not at the agent surface: `brainStatusFacts` (`agent_surface.go:96`, populated `:4559-4566`) and `brain_brief_compact.go:98-105` still carry distilled/authored only. Import 400 → `brain status --json` and the brief show `facts=400 distilled=0 authored=0`. That is the \"origins do not sum and nothing explains it\" defect `facts.go:409` exists to prevent.\n\n**4.** Asymmetric refusal: `{\"nope\":true}` errors, but `[{\"nope\":true}]` decodes to len 1 → \"imported 0 of 1 / 1 skipped\", exit 0. A bare-array export with no `memory` key imports nothing and reports success.\n\n**5.** `:78` discards `err`, so a type error anywhere (`\"id\":1`, `\"categories\":\"travel\"`) is reported as \"not a mem0 export\" — false — and the field-naming error is lost.\n\n**6.** `verify_cmd.go:310` returns before the anchor loop for `origin:\"imported\"`, so a self-declared origin plus a bogus commit anchor reads \"unverifiable here\" rather than orphaned. `identity.go:79` notes records are not authenticated by transport.\n\n**7.** Importing text that collides with a **retracted** local fact counts as imported: `upsertFact` (`dedup.go:32`) moves neither Status nor Text, so \"imported 1 of 1\" lands nothing and says nothing.\n\n**8–13 (lower).** Categories 2..n dropped at `:157-166` though `MaxPaths=2` could hold a second; unparseable timestamps silently re-dated to now (`:106`→`:149`→`:270`); `report.Superseded` counts memories while `Imported` counts facts (`:281` vs `:439`); manifest-refresh failure at `:555` aborts after `writeFacts` succeeded, so the store has the facts and the user is told it failed; neither report nor stdout names the branch (`:240`, `:577`) though facts are branch-scoped; three conditional `t.Skipf` guards turn fixture drift into a pass.\n\n## Checked and found sound\n\nNo half-written store (parse is all-or-nothing, `writeFacts` atomic). No platform assumptions. Wiring is live (`root.go:124`). The verify/oversize/FIFO/manifest guards are falsifiable — each goes red when the line it guards is deleted. Twelve further hypotheses were constructed and refuted; details on request.\n\n**Not checked:** no package tests run; whether real mem0 exports emit the numeric/epoch types finding 5 needs (mechanism confirmed, likelihood not).\nEOF\n)\" 2>&1 | tail -1","description":"Post the 306 review to the PR","timeout":900000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":977,"cache_read_input_tokens":891152,"output_tokens":2274,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":527},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":977,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2274,"cache_read_input_tokens":891152,"cache_creation_input_tokens":977,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":977},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01VTuUME8AsFCXiLmbSNDEhG":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide\ngh pr comment 306 --repo entireio/entire-brain --body \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nAdversarial pre-merge review. **13 confirmed, 12 refuted (48% refutation).** Flagging two as merge-blocking; the rest are recorded so they can be triaged rather than rediscovered.\n\n## Blocking\n\n**1. Imported fact text is never sanitised.** `facts_import.go:95`/`:286` store `m.Memory` verbatim. `sanitizeDistilledFactText` (`distill.go:483`) exists for exactly this and is called only from `distill.go:295`/`:512` — the import path skips it.\n\nAn export containing `{\"memory\":\"deploy ‮yadirF no reven\\u001b[31m\"}` is stored raw, and `printFactLine` (`facts_read_cmd.go:605`) plus the compact brief print `f.Text` unescaped. So ANSI, bidi overrides and zero-width characters from a foreign tool reach both the terminal and **the agent's prompt**. The PR bounds the input file's *size* as untrusted; it does not bound its *content*.\n\nFix is a call to the existing sanitiser on the import path.\n\n**2. `--path-prefix` bypasses the taxonomy.** `:199` validates the regex only; `:504` never calls `filterFactPathsByTaxonomy`/`loadFactTaxonomy`. The sibling surface treats this as a hard error — `facts_write_cmd.go:239-250`: *\"otherwise --path can mint immediately-orphaned facts the rest of the system treats as invalid\"*. So `--path-prefix notes.inbox` can import 400 facts that `factmerge.GC` (`admin.go:218`) reports as orphans while the command prints **\"imported 400 of 400\"**.\n\n## Worth fixing before or soon after\n\n**3.** The new `imported` origin bucket is added at `facts.go:407` and `facts_status_cmd.go:224` but not at the agent surface: `brainStatusFacts` (`agent_surface.go:96`, populated `:4559-4566`) and `brain_brief_compact.go:98-105` still carry distilled/authored only. Import 400 → `brain status --json` and the brief show `facts=400 distilled=0 authored=0`. That is the \"origins do not sum and nothing explains it\" defect `facts.go:409` exists to prevent.\n\n**4.** Asymmetric refusal: `{\"nope\":true}` errors, but `[{\"nope\":true}]` decodes to len 1 → \"imported 0 of 1 / 1 skipped\", exit 0. A bare-array export with no `memory` key imports nothing and reports success.\n\n**5.** `:78` discards `err`, so a type error anywhere (`\"id\":1`, `\"categories\":\"travel\"`) is reported as \"not a mem0 export\" — false — and the field-naming error is lost.\n\n**6.** `verify_cmd.go:310` returns before the anchor loop for `origin:\"imported\"`, so a self-declared origin plus a bogus commit anchor reads \"unverifiable here\" rather than orphaned. `identity.go:79` notes records are not authenticated by transport.\n\n**7.** Importing text that collides with a **retracted** local fact counts as imported: `upsertFact` (`dedup.go:32`) moves neither Status nor Text, so \"imported 1 of 1\" lands nothing and says nothing.\n\n**8–13 (lower).** Categories 2..n dropped at `:157-166` though `MaxPaths=2` could hold a second; unparseable timestamps silently re-dated to now (`:106`→`:149`→`:270`); `report.Superseded` counts memories while `Imported` counts facts (`:281` vs `:439`); manifest-refresh failure at `:555` aborts after `writeFacts` succeeded, so the store has the facts and the user is told it failed; neither report nor stdout names the branch (`:240`, `:577`) though facts are branch-scoped; three conditional `t.Skipf` guards turn fixture drift into a pass.\n\n## Checked and found sound\n\nNo half-written store (parse is all-or-nothing, `writeFacts` atomic). No platform assumptions. Wiring is live (`root.go:124`). The verify/oversize/FIFO/manifest guards are falsifiable — each goes red when the line it guards is deleted. Twelve further hypotheses were constructed and refuted; details on request.\n\n**Not checked:** no package tests run; whether real mem0 exports emit the numeric/epoch types finding 5 needs (mechanism confirmed, likelihood not).\nEOF\n)\" 2>&1 | tail -1","description":"Post the 306 review to the PR","timeout":900000}},"serverClassifierRequest":"22fa912d-3a8e-4c33-9ef4-cf349c6c1a58","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CfgC4KhHJU4hpnBS7YuWG","type":"assistant","uuid":"2094b589-7bd6-480a-a613-bb6d2255890c","timestamp":"2026-10-03T23:44:07.747Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
