{"parentUuid":"e657565b-82d8-49c3-aa8e-992eddbd7729","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14872138 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"062bb2e8-4045-4ad2-b786-5735a31f9068","timestamp":"2026-10-03T23:52:48.175Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14872138 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"062bb2e8-4045-4ad2-b786-5735a31f9068","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfgCm8ZhgH4H3zrEcJNf3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MX3fPkP578yCp9PKHk4dB6","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp/pr306\ngit add -A\ngit commit -q -m \"fix(facts import): sanitise foreign text and validate --path-prefix against the taxonomy\n\nTwo findings from adversarial review before merge.\n\nIMPORTED TEXT WAS UNTRUSTED IN SIZE ONLY, NOT IN CONTENT.\n\nm.Memory was stored verbatim. printFactLine (facts_read_cmd.go) and the\ncompact brief both print fact text unescaped, so ANSI escapes, bidi overrides\nand zero-width runes from another tool's export reached the terminal and the\nagent's prompt. This file already bounded how much of the input it would read;\nit did not bound what was in it.\n\nsanitizeDistilledFactText (distill.go) exists for exactly this and was already\napplied to agent-produced text. Text arriving from a third-party tool has\nstrictly weaker provenance than text this brain's own agent produced, so it\ncannot be held to a weaker standard.\n\nStripping is reported rather than silent, through the Unsupported channel this\nfile already uses for \\\"the source said something we changed or could not\nkeep\\\" -- a fact whose text differs from the export is something the owner\nshould be able to see. Clean text passes through untouched and raises no note,\nbecause a notice that always fires is noise.\n\n--path-prefix BYPASSED THE TAXONOMY.\n\nvalidateImportPrefix checked the prefix's SHAPE and normal form, never whether\nthe taxonomy knows its top-level category. The sibling surface refuses this and\nsays why: \\`facts add --path\\` hard-errors because \\\"otherwise --path can mint\nimmediately-orphaned facts the rest of the system treats as invalid\\\"\n(facts_write_cmd.go). So \\`--path-prefix notes.inbox\\` could land an entire\nimport under a category factmerge.GC reports as orphaned, while the command\nprinted \\\"imported N of N\\\".\n\nAn explicit prefix is deliberate, exactly like an explicit --path, so an\nunknown category is now a hard error rather than a silent drop that would hide\na typo across a whole import. The check runs after the brain is resolved,\nbecause the taxonomy lives there; the shape check stays up front so a\nmalformed prefix still fails before any file is read. A taxonomy that cannot be\nread is not evidence the prefix is wrong, so that case accepts rather than\nturning a brain-state problem into a rejected import.\n\nBoth guards verified by weakening; the second needed a second attempt, because\nthe first mutation did not compile and therefore proved nothing.\n\nEleven further findings from the same review are recorded on the PR rather than\nfixed here, including that the new \\\"imported\\\" origin bucket is missing from\nbrainStatusFacts and the compact brief, so an import of N shows facts=N\ndistilled=0 authored=0.\" 2>&1 | tail -2\ngit push -q origin HEAD:feat/facts-import 2>&1 | tail -2\necho \"pushed to feat/facts-import: $(git rev-parse --short HEAD)\"","description":"Commit and push the 306 hardening","timeout":1200000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":358,"cache_read_input_tokens":911515,"output_tokens":1123,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":358,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1123,"cache_read_input_tokens":911515,"cache_creation_input_tokens":358,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":358},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01MX3fPkP578yCp9PKHk4dB6":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp/pr306\ngit add -A\ngit commit -q -m \"fix(facts import): sanitise foreign text and validate --path-prefix against the taxonomy\n\nTwo findings from adversarial review before merge.\n\nIMPORTED TEXT WAS UNTRUSTED IN SIZE ONLY, NOT IN CONTENT.\n\nm.Memory was stored verbatim. printFactLine (facts_read_cmd.go) and the\ncompact brief both print fact text unescaped, so ANSI escapes, bidi overrides\nand zero-width runes from another tool's export reached the terminal and the\nagent's prompt. This file already bounded how much of the input it would read;\nit did not bound what was in it.\n\nsanitizeDistilledFactText (distill.go) exists for exactly this and was already\napplied to agent-produced text. Text arriving from a third-party tool has\nstrictly weaker provenance than text this brain's own agent produced, so it\ncannot be held to a weaker standard.\n\nStripping is reported rather than silent, through the Unsupported channel this\nfile already uses for \\\"the source said something we changed or could not\nkeep\\\" -- a fact whose text differs from the export is something the owner\nshould be able to see. Clean text passes through untouched and raises no note,\nbecause a notice that always fires is noise.\n\n--path-prefix BYPASSED THE TAXONOMY.\n\nvalidateImportPrefix checked the prefix's SHAPE and normal form, never whether\nthe taxonomy knows its top-level category. The sibling surface refuses this and\nsays why: \\`facts add --path\\` hard-errors because \\\"otherwise --path can mint\nimmediately-orphaned facts the rest of the system treats as invalid\\\"\n(facts_write_cmd.go). So \\`--path-prefix notes.inbox\\` could land an entire\nimport under a category factmerge.GC reports as orphaned, while the command\nprinted \\\"imported N of N\\\".\n\nAn explicit prefix is deliberate, exactly like an explicit --path, so an\nunknown category is now a hard error rather than a silent drop that would hide\na typo across a whole import. The check runs after the brain is resolved,\nbecause the taxonomy lives there; the shape check stays up front so a\nmalformed prefix still fails before any file is read. A taxonomy that cannot be\nread is not evidence the prefix is wrong, so that case accepts rather than\nturning a brain-state problem into a rejected import.\n\nBoth guards verified by weakening; the second needed a second attempt, because\nthe first mutation did not compile and therefore proved nothing.\n\nEleven further findings from the same review are recorded on the PR rather than\nfixed here, including that the new \\\"imported\\\" origin bucket is missing from\nbrainStatusFacts and the compact brief, so an import of N shows facts=N\ndistilled=0 authored=0.\" 2>&1 | tail -2\ngit push -q origin HEAD:feat/facts-import 2>&1 | tail -2\necho \"pushed to feat/facts-import: $(git rev-parse --short HEAD)\"","description":"Commit and push the 306 hardening","timeout":1200000}},"serverClassifierRequest":"24aa7a0f-0f30-4b05-88a1-43d92e75c5fe","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfgCm4h2UfAV9uAZyVEQr","type":"assistant","uuid":"1c711ac2-268e-4b1c-a79b-6124588e86bb","timestamp":"2026-10-03T23:53:03.434Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
