{"parentUuid":"c5742c84-9474-4d7f-893c-fa511ba5a27c","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"9c898549-e91b-4dd8-b6b2-c59581d2857f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"[Usage limit reached; a short grace allowance remains, then this turn is cut off without warning. Judge what's left: if it's genuinely only a few steps, finish it properly, then stop and say so without extra polishing. Otherwise don't attempt it all: finish the piece in hand and at most two more like it, then stop. The allowance also pays for any subagents you have running: they don't get this message and will keep going, so it's up to you how to handle them. Either way, end by telling the user their usage limit was reached, what's done and what's left.]"},"isMeta":true,"turnCompanion":true,"usageLimitNote":"wrap_up","uuid":"9cc15278-ce4f-4064-9441-7c11c16a3543","timestamp":"2026-10-03T23:53:06.421Z","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"type":"pr-link","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","prNumber":306,"prUrl":"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/306","prRepository":"entireio/entire-brain","timestamp":"2026-10-03T23:53:06.873Z"}
{"parentUuid":"9cc15278-ce4f-4064-9441-7c11c16a3543","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfgCnS5vwFBpQfPwibuWP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both #306 blockers are fixed and pushed. Stopping here.\n\n## What I did this round\n\n**Reviewed the three unreviewed PRs queued to merge**, with two adversarial reviewers told to default to *refuted*. They came back at **47% and 48% refutation** — the range that means they were testing rather than agreeing.\n\n**#318 — fixed and pushed** (`74a65b53`). The branch-naming feature was **unreachable in the case it was built for**: the branch note was checked *after* the coverage notes, and `undigested > 0` holds in every repo someone is actively working in — which is exactly when you're on a feature branch. A remember-only brain dead-ended too. One reorder fixes both. The PR's own fixtures couldn't catch it, because `declareFacts` pins `LastDistilledAt = now` while sessions are two hours old, so `undigested` was always 0.\n\n**#306 — both blockers fixed and pushed** (`c809b9ea`):\n- **Imported text was untrusted in size only, not content.** `m.Memory` was stored verbatim while `printFactLine` and the compact brief print it unescaped — so ANSI, bidi overrides and zero-width runes from a foreign export reached the terminal *and the agent's prompt*. `sanitizeDistilledFactText` already guarded agent-produced text; third-party text has weaker provenance and can't be held to a weaker standard. Stripping now reports itself through the file's existing `Unsupported` channel.\n- **`--path-prefix` bypassed the taxonomy.** `facts add --path` hard-errors on this and says why — \"can mint immediately-orphaned facts\". Import had only a shape check, so `--path-prefix notes.inbox` could land a whole import under a category GC calls orphaned while printing \"imported N of N\".\n\nBoth weakening-verified; the second needed a retry because the first mutation didn't compile and so proved nothing. Eleven further findings are recorded on PR #306 rather than silently fixed.\n\n## State\n\n**Brain side: no known unfixed blocking defect.** Twelve fixed across the session, all weakening-verified, suites green.\n\n**Graph side: two, owned by Codex** under the study-7 prereg — intent-phrased recall and missing const/var extraction, both in [#319](https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/issues/319), the second independently reproduced by the graph session on a different repo.\n\n**Left for you: the merges.** #306, #318, #320, #321 on `main`; #329 → #330 → #331 stacked and order-dependent. #306 and #318 now carry the review fixes and will need a fresh CI run.\n\n**Your usage limit was reached** — that's why I'm stopping rather than continuing to the benchmark pilot, which is designed in `ROUND3-DESIGN.md` but unrun. No subagents are still running."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1397,"cache_read_input_tokens":911873,"output_tokens":943,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1397,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":943,"cache_read_input_tokens":911873,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1397,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1397},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"f89e5cae-5be8-49f4-8fbf-a6b6d43d7a88","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfgCnQ9qacR6ENG6mgctY","type":"assistant","uuid":"e1927678-2d1a-4c15-998e-dbd00b23614a","timestamp":"2026-10-03T23:53:20.215Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf