{"parentUuid":"9fb8f2f8-62c7-4094-9a99-1acde6e0ca2b","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14982754 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"5287c73e-2714-4180-91d1-bbaef559384c","timestamp":"2026-10-04T03:24:42.148Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14982754 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"5287c73e-2714-4180-91d1-bbaef559384c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfgUvJdYiSvtmUA8vPCJ6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Ryc2ksLrZMi8xittRbMoNo","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp/pr306\ngofmt -l internal/ | head -2\ngit add -A\ngit commit -q -m \"fix(facts import): name the bad field, and refuse an import that found nothing\n\nTwo more findings from the pre-merge review, both the same class: a true\nstatement that misleads.\n\nTHE DECODER'S ERROR WAS DISCARDED AND REPLACED WITH A FALSE ONE.\n\nparseMem0 threw away both unmarshal errors and returned \\\"not a mem0 export\\\".\nFor {\\\"results\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":1}]} that is simply wrong -- the file is\nunmistakably a mem0 export -- and the decoder already knew the offending field\nwas \\`id\\`. The user was told their file was the wrong kind of file and given\nnothing to look for.\n\nA type error that NAMES A FIELD is now surfaced instead. The field is the whole\npoint, and getting there needed one correction: trying the bare-array shape\nfirst produces its own UnmarshalTypeError for any JSON object (\\\"cannot\nunmarshal object into []mem0Memory\\\"), which names nothing. My first version\npreferred that one, and the test caught it. Only a field-naming error beats the\nformat message; a syntax error still falls through to it, because a truncated\nfile genuinely is not an export.\n\nAN IMPORT THAT SKIPPED EVERY RECORD REPORTED SUCCESS.\n\nA bare JSON array parses as mem0, so an export from another tool (Letta, Zep)\nwhose records carry no \\`memory\\` key reached the report as \\\"imported 0 of N /\nN skipped: no memory text\\\" and exited 0. This file's own doctrine is that a\nfile which is not an export \\\"is an error naming both, not a silent\nzero-record import\\\"; a file where not one record has text is that same case,\ndiscovered one layer later.\n\nAll-skipped is now an error naming the missing field and the count. SOME\nrecords skipped stays a warning, because a real export can carry an empty\nmemory.\n\nBoth guards verified by weakening. Running total on this PR: five findings\nfixed, eight recorded on it for triage.\" 2>&1 | tail -2\ngit push -q origin HEAD:feat/facts-import 2>&1|tail -2\necho \"pushed: $(git rev-parse --short HEAD)\"","description":"Commit and push findings 4 and 5","timeout":1200000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1188,"cache_read_input_tokens":930607,"output_tokens":876,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1188,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":876,"cache_read_input_tokens":930607,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1188,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1188},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Ryc2ksLrZMi8xittRbMoNo":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp/pr306\ngofmt -l internal/ | head -2\ngit add -A\ngit commit -q -m \"fix(facts import): name the bad field, and refuse an import that found nothing\n\nTwo more findings from the pre-merge review, both the same class: a true\nstatement that misleads.\n\nTHE DECODER'S ERROR WAS DISCARDED AND REPLACED WITH A FALSE ONE.\n\nparseMem0 threw away both unmarshal errors and returned \\\"not a mem0 export\\\".\nFor {\\\"results\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":1}]} that is simply wrong -- the file is\nunmistakably a mem0 export -- and the decoder already knew the offending field\nwas \\`id\\`. The user was told their file was the wrong kind of file and given\nnothing to look for.\n\nA type error that NAMES A FIELD is now surfaced instead. The field is the whole\npoint, and getting there needed one correction: trying the bare-array shape\nfirst produces its own UnmarshalTypeError for any JSON object (\\\"cannot\nunmarshal object into []mem0Memory\\\"), which names nothing. My first version\npreferred that one, and the test caught it. Only a field-naming error beats the\nformat message; a syntax error still falls through to it, because a truncated\nfile genuinely is not an export.\n\nAN IMPORT THAT SKIPPED EVERY RECORD REPORTED SUCCESS.\n\nA bare JSON array parses as mem0, so an export from another tool (Letta, Zep)\nwhose records carry no \\`memory\\` key reached the report as \\\"imported 0 of N /\nN skipped: no memory text\\\" and exited 0. This file's own doctrine is that a\nfile which is not an export \\\"is an error naming both, not a silent\nzero-record import\\\"; a file where not one record has text is that same case,\ndiscovered one layer later.\n\nAll-skipped is now an error naming the missing field and the count. SOME\nrecords skipped stays a warning, because a real export can carry an empty\nmemory.\n\nBoth guards verified by weakening. Running total on this PR: five findings\nfixed, eight recorded on it for triage.\" 2>&1 | tail -2\ngit push -q origin HEAD:feat/facts-import 2>&1|tail -2\necho \"pushed: $(git rev-parse --short HEAD)\"","description":"Commit and push findings 4 and 5","timeout":1200000}},"serverClassifierRequest":"3e883ef7-8841-4d6d-8883-a1ec5a31d8b1","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfgUvGEvmGRFB18Tq9t6x","type":"assistant","uuid":"a3d4889e-0dbe-4c86-9acc-07a81c444d42","timestamp":"2026-10-04T03:24:54.377Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"