{"parentUuid":"5322bcd8-aa13-4696-ac9b-33d6f6d9baa2","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14970814 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"695b2ce5-f5ad-415a-be54-395628651f87","timestamp":"2026-10-04T03:31:28.378Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14970814 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"695b2ce5-f5ad-415a-be54-395628651f87","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfgVSGV9MtyWX6WRZgczv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Six of #306's findings fixed, pushed at `f902f5c0`.\n\n## This one was the most interesting\n\n`verify` skipped its anchor checks for anything claiming `origin: \"imported\"`. The reasoning in the code was genuinely good: an imported fact's anchor names a session in the *source* system, so running the session checks would report it \"orphaned\" — \"its evidence is gone\" — when the truth is it was never here. Wrong answer, and a more alarming one.\n\nBut the origin field is **self-declared**, and `factmerge/identity.go` is explicit that records aren't authenticated by transport. A fact reaches the store from a shared fact-set head or a hand-written file as easily as from `facts import`.\n\nAnd the premise fails precisely when the anchor claims repository evidence. I checked what a real import writes: **one anchor, carrying only `SessionID: \"<tool>:<foreignID>\"`** — never a commit, checkpoint, transcript, or verified flag. So `imported` + a commit anchor is internally inconsistent, and trusting it meant a fabricated anchor into this repo was never checked and read as benign.\n\nIt now reports the contradiction, which beats both alternatives: checking the commit would print \"orphaned\" and blame the wrong thing; skipping hides a record that shouldn't exist. Genuine imports are untouched.\n\n## Tally\n\n**Sixteen defects fixed this session.** On #306 specifically: **six fixed, seven recorded** for triage.\n\n| fixed on #306 | |\n|---|---|\n| HIGH | unsanitised foreign text reaching the agent prompt |\n| HIGH | `--path-prefix` minting orphaned facts |\n| MED-HIGH | `imported` origin missing from status and brief |\n| MED | decoder error discarded, reported as wrong file type |\n| MED | all-records-skipped import reporting success |\n| MED | `verify` trusting a self-declared origin |\n\nRemaining on #306 are the lower-severity ones: a retracted-fact collision counted as imported, categories 2..n dropped, timestamps silently re-dated, a memories-vs-facts count mismatch, a manifest-refresh failure after a successful write, no branch named in the report, and three conditional `t.Skipf` guards.\n\nTwo of my own weakenings failed to compile this round and I redid both — a mutation that doesn't build proves nothing, and I'd rather say that than count it.\n\nBranches: #306 `f902f5c0`, #318 `74a65b53`, #331 `ae6df5b2`. The merges remain yours."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":879,"cache_read_input_tokens":942613,"output_tokens":842,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":879,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":842,"cache_read_input_tokens":942613,"cache_creation_input_tokens":879,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":879},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"825b7493-26f2-4297-9ccf-a66dbe1cf068","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfgVSDCCxChScAr4wbv2m","type":"assistant","uuid":"6080e55a-dc2f-4c50-b15a-049164c3b3e9","timestamp":"2026-10-04T03:31:41.101Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
