{"parentUuid":"6c456be2-09aa-471d-ba6c-798432c599ec","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14955647 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"d8e341e2-1efb-421b-aace-8927cce5b3b8","timestamp":"2026-10-04T03:42:55.372Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14955647 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"d8e341e2-1efb-421b-aace-8927cce5b3b8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfgWJvS5747sknGHjiv6n","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Eight of #306's findings now fixed, pushed at `67b58d7c`.\n\n## This round\n\n**A manifest refresh failing *after* the write reported a failed import.** `writeFacts` had already succeeded, so the facts were on disk — but the refresh error was returned from inside the lock, aborting before any report. The user was told it failed while their brain held every imported fact, and would reasonably re-run it. Now a warning beside the successful report, naming the remedy.\n\n**Importing text matching a retracted fact counted as an import.** `Upsert` never moves `Status` or `Text` — correct for a re-distill, since a retracted fact mustn't spring back because it got distilled again. But for an import it means the anchor attaches to the retracted record, nothing retrievable lands, and it still counts toward \"imported N of N\". `countKeptActiveFacts` already covered the opposite direction; this mirror was simply missing.\n\n**One thing worth flagging about my own work:** the manifest fix initially had **no guard at all** — I only discovered that because a weakening compiled and no test complained. The guard I added is source-level and weaker than the others, because forcing that refresh to fail needs write-failure injection the import path doesn't expose. It's labelled as such in the test and the commit rather than presented as behavioural.\n\n## Tally\n\n**Eighteen defects fixed this session.** On #306: **eight fixed, five recorded**.\n\nRemaining on #306 are the lowest-severity items: categories 2..n dropped (`MaxPaths=2` could hold a second), timestamps silently re-dated to now, `Superseded` counting memories while `Imported` counts facts, no branch named in the report, and three conditional `t.Skipf` guards that turn fixture drift into a pass.\n\nBranches: #306 `67b58d7c`, #318 `74a65b53`, #331 `ae6df5b2`. All suites green.\n\nI'll keep going down the list — the `t.Skipf` guards are next, since a test that silently skips is the same defect class as everything else here."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1006,"cache_read_input_tokens":957654,"output_tokens":666,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1006,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":666,"cache_read_input_tokens":957654,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1006,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1006},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"9b180b75-c536-422d-8372-10b11e32f0ba","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfgWJsTDzMmtMXd8toso8","type":"assistant","uuid":"86f5ffaf-ebfa-4e84-a54b-9e338cd90566","timestamp":"2026-10-04T03:43:06.297Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
