{"parentUuid":"98b4cd09-d95d-4732-b470-69d71e5142e5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfgXkv93Eacf6BEaNTHdx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DnHeuA34ZWTj7VKqdyBLtM","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp/pr306\ngit add -A\ngit commit -q -m \"fix(facts import): carry a second category, align the counts, name the branch\n\nThe last three findings from the pre-merge review of this PR.\n\nA SECOND CATEGORY WAS DROPPED WHILE THE CAPACITY FOR IT EXISTED.\n\nimportTaxonomyPath takes the FIRST usable category and breaks, so a memory\ntagged [\\\"deployment\\\",\\\"security\\\"] was filed under project.imported.deployment\nwith \\\"security\\\" gone and nothing said -- while factmerge.MaxPaths is 2, so the\nroom for a second path was already there.\n\nUp to MaxPaths categories are now carried, deduplicated after sanitising so one\ncategory spelled two ways is still one path. Categories past the cap ARE\ngenuinely lost -- the cap is an identity invariant, not a formatting choice --\nso they are named in the report instead of vanishing. Note that this changes\nderived fact ids for multi-category memories, which is free only because this\nPR is unmerged.\n\nSUPERSEDED AND IMPORTED WERE COUNTED IN DIFFERENT UNITS.\n\nSuperseded was incremented once per MEMORY while Imported counts distinct\nFACTS. Two memories that dedupe into one fact, both superseded at the source,\nreported \\\"2 already superseded at the source\\\" out of \\\"1 imported\\\" -- two\nnumbers in different units presented as comparable, which is the whole defect\nclass this report exists to avoid. It is now counted by distinct id.\n\nTHE REPORT DID NOT SAY WHICH BRANCH THE FACTS LANDED ON.\n\nFacts are branch-scoped. An import that resolved to a different branch than the\nuser had in mind is invisible: recall on another branch reports an empty corpus,\nwhich reads as a failed import rather than a misplaced one. The branch is now\nin the report and printed under the summary line.\n\nThree weakenings, each turning a test red: one category only, per-memory\nsuperseded counting, and an unnamed branch.\n\nThis closes every finding raised on this PR: thirteen in total, all with\nregression tests verified by weakening.\" 2>&1 | tail -2\ngit push -q origin HEAD:feat/facts-import 2>&1|tail -1\necho \"pushed: $(git rev-parse --short HEAD)\"\ngit log --oneline origin/main..HEAD | wc -l | xargs echo \"commits on the branch:\"","description":"Commit the final three #306 findings","timeout":1200000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1506,"cache_read_input_tokens":180445,"output_tokens":953,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1506,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":953,"cache_read_input_tokens":180445,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1506,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1506},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01DnHeuA34ZWTj7VKqdyBLtM":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp/pr306\ngit add -A\ngit commit -q -m \"fix(facts import): carry a second category, align the counts, name the branch\n\nThe last three findings from the pre-merge review of this PR.\n\nA SECOND CATEGORY WAS DROPPED WHILE THE CAPACITY FOR IT EXISTED.\n\nimportTaxonomyPath takes the FIRST usable category and breaks, so a memory\ntagged [\\\"deployment\\\",\\\"security\\\"] was filed under project.imported.deployment\nwith \\\"security\\\" gone and nothing said -- while factmerge.MaxPaths is 2, so the\nroom for a second path was already there.\n\nUp to MaxPaths categories are now carried, deduplicated after sanitising so one\ncategory spelled two ways is still one path. Categories past the cap ARE\ngenuinely lost -- the cap is an identity invariant, not a formatting choice --\nso they are named in the report instead of vanishing. Note that this changes\nderived fact ids for multi-category memories, which is free only because this\nPR is unmerged.\n\nSUPERSEDED AND IMPORTED WERE COUNTED IN DIFFERENT UNITS.\n\nSuperseded was incremented once per MEMORY while Imported counts distinct\nFACTS. Two memories that dedupe into one fact, both superseded at the source,\nreported \\\"2 already superseded at the source\\\" out of \\\"1 imported\\\" -- two\nnumbers in different units presented as comparable, which is the whole defect\nclass this report exists to avoid. It is now counted by distinct id.\n\nTHE REPORT DID NOT SAY WHICH BRANCH THE FACTS LANDED ON.\n\nFacts are branch-scoped. An import that resolved to a different branch than the\nuser had in mind is invisible: recall on another branch reports an empty corpus,\nwhich reads as a failed import rather than a misplaced one. The branch is now\nin the report and printed under the summary line.\n\nThree weakenings, each turning a test red: one category only, per-memory\nsuperseded counting, and an unnamed branch.\n\nThis closes every finding raised on this PR: thirteen in total, all with\nregression tests verified by weakening.\" 2>&1 | tail -2\ngit push -q origin HEAD:feat/facts-import 2>&1|tail -1\necho \"pushed: $(git rev-parse --short HEAD)\"\ngit log --oneline origin/main..HEAD | wc -l | xargs echo \"commits on the branch:\"","description":"Commit the final three #306 findings","timeout":1200000}},"serverClassifierRequest":"cb81ec0f-a15e-41ee-9e78-10a262acf818","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfgXktse91CKa8q8qcFia","type":"assistant","uuid":"44c3e765-54fb-4b49-8256-e6393709c565","