{"parentUuid":"b470566b-42dd-441d-a9f7-cfaca84868d0","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"environment","snapshot":{"workingDirectory":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","isWorktree":true,"isGitRepo":true,"additionalWorkingDirectories":[],"platform":"darwin","shell":"zsh","osVersion":"Darwin 25.5.0"},"changes":[{"field":"workingDirectory","from":"/Users/suhaan/devenv"},{"field":"isWorktree"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"bfdcb1e3-f061-42f3-b292-b13e86c49e1a","timestamp":"2026-10-04T04:17:02.762Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n# Environment update\n - Primary working directory: /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide (was /Users/suhaan/devenv)\n - This is a git worktree — an isolated copy of the repository. Run all commands from this directory. Do NOT `cd` to the original repository root.\n - The git stash stack is shared with the main checkout and all other worktrees, and other Claude sessions may push or pop it concurrently. Never use bare `git stash` / `git stash pop` — you could pop another session's changes. Prefer a temporary WIP commit to set work aside; if you must stash, use `git stash push -u -m \"<unique-tag>\"`, immediately capture your entry's SHA via `git stash list --format='%H %gs'`, restore with `git stash apply <sha>` (not pop), and afterwards drop the entry, re-finding its current `stash@{n}` by tag first.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"bfdcb1e3-f061-42f3-b292-b13e86c49e1a","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14727115 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"9cf316d5-5be7-42a3-85fc-c21e601f93fd","timestamp":"2026-10-04T04:17:02.763Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14727115 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"9cf316d5-5be7-42a3-85fc-c21e601f93fd","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfgYunG8tfZk4TMp6LDK4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both review sets are now fully closed. Where brain stands:\n\n## #306 and #318: every review finding fixed\n\n| | findings | state |\n|---|---|---|\n| **#306** `feat/facts-import` | 13 of 13 | `75aba5ae` — build + vet clean |\n| **#318** `fix/blind-spot-other-branches` | 4 of 4 | `5472ef08` — build + vet clean |\n| **#331** `fix/agent-guide-directive-and-discovery` | — | `ae6df5b2` — build clean |\n\n**Twenty-six defects fixed this session**, each with a regression test shown to go red on a compile-clean revert.\n\n## Two things worth your attention\n\n**I was wrong in a commit message and corrected it in the next one.** I claimed `recall` already routed through the blind-spot check, citing two call sites. It doesn't — `facts_read_cmd.go:259` returns to `runRecallEvidence` *before* both of them. The reviewer was right. The correction is in the commit, not buried.\n\n**A weakening found nothing, and that was the finding.** When I removed the `recall --evidence` call site entirely, all three of my tests stayed green — they called the helper directly, so a perfect helper and a silent surface look identical to them. That is the exact bug I was fixing, reproduced inside my own test suite. The end-to-end test I added afterwards does go red, and asserts the fixture produced an empty result first so it can't pass vacuously.\n\nOn the `recall --evidence` fix specifically: I did **not** reuse the fact-branch note there. Evidence recall returns session spans, so \"N active fact(s) on M other branch(es)\" would have attached a claim about facts to a result holding none — the shape mismatch the reviewer flagged on the unified surfaces. The new note counts sessions, and stays silent when the queried branch has its own, because then an empty result is about the query.\n\n## What remains\n\nOne recorded, not fixed: a **divergent twin** — my `briefBranchBlindSpot` on #331 and `otherBranchBlindSpot` on #318 do similar work in different functions. That's a merge-order hazard rather than a defect, and it's worth collapsing into one when these land. I'd rather flag it than silently pick a winner across two unmerged branches.\n\nAnd the merges themselves, which stay yours — seven PRs: #306, #318, #320, #321 standalone, then #329 → #330 → #331 in order."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":841,"cache_read_input_tokens":220017,"output_tokens":802,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":841,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":802,"cache_read_input_tokens":220017,"cache_creation_input_tokens":841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":841},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"b0787818-4ab6-489d-b03c-d135d9e9f023","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfgYumkPV5rj1owGyE9zH","type":"assistant","uuid":"520bb023-8d14-44e9-af8a-b02a2ab278ef","timestamp":"2026-10-04T04:17:15.612Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"520bb023-8d14-44e9-af8a-b02a2ab278ef","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"e7885167-dc2d-44de-bb8f-d1c797ad583a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"Stop hook feedback:\n[make brain fully solid]: The assistant states 'What remains' explicitly: 'One recorded, not fixed: a divergent twin' and 'the merges themselves, which stay yours — seven PRs: #306, #318, #320, #321 standalone, then #329 → #330 → #331 in order.' The assistant has fixed 26 defects across two PR reviews (#306: 13 of 13, #318: 4 of 4) and achieved full closure on those reviews with all tests green. However, the condition 'make brain fully solid' encompasses the complete system stability, which requires merging these PRs and resolving the remaining items: the divergent-twin consolidation and the seven PR merges. The assistant explicitly reserves the merge decisions ('which stay yours') and does not complete the full solidification."},"isMeta":true,"uuid":"0c01d68b-4e07-4b28-a791-270dda6f46a4","timestamp":"2026-10-04T04:17:20.118Z","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
