{"parentUuid":"15ecfee5-c744-4e98-bf7f-f487debf23ee","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfgZPcGug1VYTnaVG2xpL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018JahPmeovr8c9k8zexmbS5","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide\ngit add -A\ngit commit -q -m \"fix(blind-spot): brief's branch note must count only ACTIVE facts\n\nThe divergent twin recorded against this stack turned out to carry a real\ndefect, not just duplication.\n\nbriefBranchBlindSpot named any branch whose fact file was non-empty, while\notherBranchBlindSpot (PR #318) counted ACTIVE facts from the start. So a branch\nholding nothing but retracted or superseded facts was offered as the remedy:\n\n  no facts on branch \\\"main\\\", but 1 branch(es) hold facts: feat/dead\n  — retry with \\`--branch feat/dead\\`\n\nRetrying there also comes back empty, because retracted and superseded facts\nare not retrievable. A false lead dressed as a remedy is worse than the silence\nthis note replaces -- the reader follows it, gets nothing, and concludes the\nbrain is empty rather than that they are on the wrong branch, which is the\nprecise misreading this feature exists to prevent.\n\nNow active-only, matching #318. That also removes the merge hazard rather than\nonly documenting it: the two functions are now behaviourally IDENTICAL in what\nthey count and differ only in phrasing for their surface, so whichever of #318\nand #331 lands second can collapse this into a call to that function as a pure\nrefactor. Divergence on this exact check is what would have made the collapse\ndangerous, and a MERGE NOTE in the code says so at the site.\n\nTwo guards, both verified by weakening: restoring the any-fact check makes the\nfalse-lead test red and makes the nothing-live-anywhere test emit the bad note\nverbatim.\" 2>&1 | tail -2\ngit push -q origin HEAD:fix/agent-guide-directive-and-discovery 2>&1|tail -1\necho \"pushed: $(git rev-parse --short HEAD)\"","description":"Commit the twin alignment","timeout":1200000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":945,"cache_read_input_tokens":230694,"output_tokens":750,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":945,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":750,"cache_read_input_tokens":230694,"cache_creation_input_tokens":945,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":945},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_018JahPmeovr8c9k8zexmbS5":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide\ngit add -A\ngit commit -q -m \"fix(blind-spot): brief's branch note must count only ACTIVE facts\n\nThe divergent twin recorded against this stack turned out to carry a real\ndefect, not just duplication.\n\nbriefBranchBlindSpot named any branch whose fact file was non-empty, while\notherBranchBlindSpot (PR #318) counted ACTIVE facts from the start. So a branch\nholding nothing but retracted or superseded facts was offered as the remedy:\n\n  no facts on branch \\\"main\\\", but 1 branch(es) hold facts: feat/dead\n  — retry with \\`--branch feat/dead\\`\n\nRetrying there also comes back empty, because retracted and superseded facts\nare not retrievable. A false lead dressed as a remedy is worse than the silence\nthis note replaces -- the reader follows it, gets nothing, and concludes the\nbrain is empty rather than that they are on the wrong branch, which is the\nprecise misreading this feature exists to prevent.\n\nNow active-only, matching #318. That also removes the merge hazar