{"parentUuid":"bde4811c-e008-443a-9787-3b6a625be114","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfgZQeCXBnBAo8xFjzRiw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The divergent twin is resolved — and it wasn't just duplication:\n\n## It was hiding a real defect\n\n`briefBranchBlindSpot` named any branch with a non-empty fact file, while #318's version counted **active** facts. So a branch holding nothing but retracted or superseded facts was offered as the fix:\n\n```\nno facts on branch \"main\", but 1 branch(es) hold facts: feat/dead\n— retry with `--branch feat/dead`\n```\n\nRetrying there also comes back empty. The reader follows the advice, gets nothing, and concludes the brain is empty — which is the precise misreading this feature exists to prevent. A false lead dressed as a remedy is worse than the silence it replaced.\n\nNow active-only, matching #318. That **removes** the merge hazard rather than documenting it: the two functions are now behaviourally identical in what they count and differ only in phrasing, so whichever lands second can collapse them as a pure refactor. Divergence on exactly that check is what would have made the collapse dangerous, and a `MERGE NOTE` at the site says so.\n\nBoth guards weakening-verified — restoring the any-fact check makes the test emit the bad note verbatim.\n\n## Where brain stands\n\n| branch | head | review findings | suite |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| #306 `feat/facts-import` | `75aba5ae` | 13 of 13 closed | green |\n| #318 `fix/blind-spot-other-branches` | `5472ef08` | 4 of 4 closed | green |\n| #331 `fix/agent-guide-directive-and-discovery` | `db0658ee` | twin resolved | green |\n\n**Twenty-seven defects fixed this session**, each with a regression test shown to go red on a compile-clean revert.\n\nEvery item I had recorded as \"not fixed\" is now fixed. Nothing is left on my side of the line.\n\nWhat's left is yours and only yours: the seven merges — #306, #318, #320, #321 standalone, then #329 → #330 → #331 in order. #306, #318 and #331 all carry new commits and need fresh CI before you look at them. I won't merge them without you saying so."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":819,"cache_read_input_tokens":231639,"output_tokens":702,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":819,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":702,"cache_read_input_tokens":231639,"cache_creation_input_tokens":819,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":819},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"f87d03d0-7fc5-4b37-b5d9-df25d637429e","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfgZQdjVDRxRTfXt5TzgY","type":"assistant","uuid":"a1c0d19c-90d0-4b7a-b73d-505cc1478f90","timestamp":"2026-10-04T04:23:44.765Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
