{"parentUuid":"f109385c-165d-4d65-9d85-4f6516d72c4c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfgZVV9gvyuB2KrbHjscF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Y5EnReCipN5ZUkQjoVmunE","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide\nfor t in 226 238 247; do\n  printf \"\\n########## TRAIL %s ##########\\n\" \"$t\"\n  entire trail finding list \"$t\" --repo gh/entireio/entire-brain --freshness any --status open --json 2>/dev/null \\\n  | python3 -c '\nimport json,sys\nd=json.load(sys.stdin)\nfor f in d.get(\"findings\",[]):\n    loc=f.get(\"location\") or {}\n    print(\"\\n--- ID:\",f[\"id\"],\"| sev:\",f.get(\"severity\"),\"|\",loc.get(\"path\"),loc.get(\"startLine\"))\n    print((f.get(\"body\") or \"\").strip()[:1100])\n'\ndone","description":"Read all eight finding bodies","timeout":1200000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1287,"cache_read_input_tokens":237258,"output_tokens":479,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":108},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1287,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":479,"cache_read_input_tokens":237258,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1287,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1287},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Y5EnReCipN5ZUkQjoVmunE":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide\nfor t in 226 238 247; do\n  printf \"\\n########## TRAIL %s ##########\\n\" \"$t\"\n  entire trail finding list \"$t\" --repo gh/entireio/entire-brain --freshness any --status open --json 2>/dev/null \\\n  | python3 -c '\nimport json,sys\nd=json.load(sys.stdin)\nfor f in d.get(\"findings\",[]):\n    loc=f.get(\"location\") or {}\n    print(\"\\n--- ID:\",f[\"id\"],\"| sev:\",f.get(\"severity\"),\"|\",loc.get(\"path\"),loc.get(\"startLine\"))\n    print((f.get(\"body\") or \"\").strip()[:1100])\n'\ndone","description":"Read all eight finding bodies","timeout":1200000}},"serverClassifierRequest":"9e17989f-5547-4fb2-8827-76288ff962e0","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CfgZVUMpNV1sMEU8uJKgd","type":"assistant","uuid":"dc7ca48d-aa5c-403c-b16b-374b62553f5a","timestamp":"2026-10-04T04:24:48.432Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"dc7ca48d-aa5c-403c-b16b-374b62553f5a","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"e7885167-dc2d-44de-bb8f-d1c797ad583a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Y5EnReCipN5ZUkQjoVmunE","type":"tool_result","content":"########## TRAIL 226 ##########\n\n--- ID: 01M42H2JD5GC9SM5QQ963MG2KV | sev: medium | None None\nThe `report.Read > 0 && report.Imported == 0 && report.SkippedText == report.Read` guard fires only after the `withBrainWriteLock` block above has already run `writeFacts` and `updateFactSourceManifestLocked`. So a non-dry-run import where every record lacks `memory` text still takes the write lock, rewrites the facts file, and refreshes the manifest's generation metadata before this function returns a hard error telling the user the import effectively didn't happen. It also means a `manifestErr` recorded during that lock is appended to `report.Warnings` but never surfaced, since the function returns via `fmt.Errorf` here without ever printing the report — silently dropping a manifest-refresh failure, contrary to the stated intent that such failures must not be lost. Move this validation before the `withBrainWriteLock` call so a doomed import can't mutate brain state first.\n\n--- ID: 01M42GGG7H7XPXESYBDDTJ5WS5 | sev: medium | None None\nWhen `conflictingRetirement` clears `SupersededBy` on line 471, it does not reset `Status` to `factStatusActive`. This creates an inconsistent state where a fact has `Status = factStatusSuperseded` but `SupersededBy = \"\"`, violating the invariant that superseded facts must point to their successor. Line 482 sets both fields together, but line 471 only clears the successor reference.\n\n--- ID: 01M42F8N9J5W4FNKV6NVE2GVM3 | sev: high | None None\nWhen every record in the export lacks memory text, `facts` is empty but the non-dry-run branch above (lines 605-634) still runs `writeFacts` and `updateFactSourceManifestLocked` under the write lock *before* this check fires and the command returns an error. The manifest's generation/count/freshness fields get bumped as if a real import happened, even though the command ultimately fails and reports nothing was imported — a command that errors out should not mutate brain state (facts file rewrite + manifest generation bump) first. Move this all-skipped check before the `if !dryRun { withBrainWriteLock(...) }` block so a doomed import never touches disk.\n\n########## TRAIL 238 ##########\n\n--- ID: 01M42J6JYAMBSB9HGN4SGAMREJ | sev: high | None None\nThe new branch-note logic (`otherBranchBlindSpot` via `missingFactIDs`) only runs inside the plain-text branch of `runGet`. The `jsonOut` branch at lines 759-770 builds `{\"branch\",\"results\",\"missing\"}` and returns before this code ever executes, so `get --json`/`multi-get --json` never emit the note. Since `mcp.go` calls `runGet(..., true, ...)` for `brain_get`/`brain_multi_get` (the primary MCP/agent surface this fix targets), the feature is effectively unreachable for exactly the consumers most likely to act on a `--branch` retry hint. The note should also be added to the JSON payload before line 760.\n\n--- ID: 01M42HRFVSJ9H3GW9AH634C2PB | sev: high | None None\n`loadAllFactBranches` at blind_spot.go:111 lacks symlink validation, while similar functions like `loadAllFactBranchesForPrivacy` explicitly check for and reject symlinks. An attacker with write access to `.entire/brain/facts/` could create a symlink pointing outside the repository, potentially exposing sensitive files when `otherBranchBlindSpot` is triggered on empty query results. The privacy variant checks `entry.Type()&os.ModeSymlink != 0` at session_privacy.go:1140 and single-branch `loadFacts` uses `rejectExistingSymlinkPathComponents` at facts.go:146, but this new code path bypasses both protections.\n\n########## TRAIL 247 ##########\n\n--- ID: 01M421MP2QH04VT7H2XQ9GXR4G | sev: medium | None None\nBroken markdown code fence: line 134 opens a code fence with ``` (no language), then prose appears inside the fence (lines 136-141), then `sh` appears on line 143 as if it's a language specifier but it's actually inside the previous code block. Either close the fence on line 134 and reopen with ````sh` on line 143, or replace the ``` on line 134 with ````sh` and remove line 143's `sh`.\n\n--- ID: 01M420K6PZ7324PDZ1GEJVDNCE | sev: high | None None\n`MergePreEditHook` is called with the literal string `\"entire brain\"` instead of the resolved prefix from `setupCommandPrefix(os.LookupEnv)` (used everywhere else in this package, see `internal/cli/setup_invocation.go`). For a standalone-binary install (no `ENTIRE_CLI_VERSION`, i.e. no `entire` host CLI on PATH), the correct invocation is `entire-brain`, not `entire brain`. The hook written into `.claude/settings.json` will therefore be `entire brain hook pre-edit`, a command that does not exist on that user's PATH — silently defeating the only push-path feature this PR adds, for exactly the install mode `setupCommandPrefix`'s own doc comment calls out as the common fallback case.\n\n--- ID: 01M3ZYEYYSNFAQRBH3NM7VXKT3 | sev: high | None None\nMergePreEditHook bypasses repository containment safeguards by using raw `os.WriteFile` instead of `os.OpenRoot()`. The existing codebase (see `internal/agentsetup/files.go:74`) uses `os.OpenRoot()` for all repository writes to prevent symlink-based path traversal attacks. If `root/.claude` is a symlink to a directory outside the repository, this writes to an arbitrary location. Should use the existing `os.OpenRoot()` + `resolveContainedName` pattern like other file writes in this package.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"0f9afc41-4585-4a41-9f51-82b6e4c05c1b","timestamp":"2026-10-04T04:24:53.739Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"########## TRAIL 226 ##########\n\n--- ID: 01M42H2JD5GC9SM5QQ963MG2KV | sev: medium | None None\nThe `report.Read > 0 && report.Imported == 0 && report.SkippedText == report.Read` guard fires only after the `withBrainWriteLock` block above has already run `writeFacts` and `updateFactSourceManifestLocked`. So a non-dry-run import where every record lacks `memory` text still takes the write lock, rewrites the facts file, and refreshes the manifest's generation metadata before this function returns a hard error telling the user the import effectively didn't happen. It also means a `manifestErr` recorded during that lock is appended to `report.Warnings` but never surfaced, since the function returns via `fmt.Errorf` here without ever printing the report — silently dropping a manifest-refresh failure, contrary to the stated intent that such failures must not be lost. Move this validation before the `withBrainWriteLock` call so a doomed import can't mutate brain state first.\n\n--- ID: 01M42GGG7H7XPXESYBDDTJ5WS5 | sev: medium | None None\nWhen `conflictingRetirement` clears `SupersededBy` on line 471, it does not reset `Status` to `factStatusActive`. This creates an inconsistent state where a fact has `Status = factStatusSuperseded` but `SupersededBy = \"\"`, violating the invariant that superseded facts must point to their successor. Line 482 sets both fields together, but line 471 only clears the successor reference.\n\n--- ID: 01M42F8N9J5W4FNKV6NVE2GVM3 | sev: high | None None\nWhen every record in the export lacks memory text, `facts` is empty but the non-dry-run branch above (lines 605-634) still runs `writeFacts` and `updateFactSourceManifestLocked` under the write lock *before* this check fires and the command returns an error. The manifest's generation/count/freshness fields get bumped as if a real import happened, even though the command ultimately fails and reports nothing was imported — a command that errors out should not mutate brain state (facts file rewrite + manifest generation bump) first. Move this all-skipped check before the `if !dryRun { withBrainWriteLock(...) }` block so a doomed import never touches disk.\n\n########## TRAIL 238 ##########\n\n--- ID: 01M42J6JYAMBSB9HGN4SGAMREJ | sev: high | None None\nThe new branch-note logic (`otherBranchBlindSpot` via `missingFactIDs`) only runs inside the plain-text branch of `runGet`. The `jsonOut` branch at lines 759-770 builds `{\"branch\",\"results\",\"missing\"}` and returns before this code ever executes, so `get --json`/`multi-get --json` never emit the note. Since `mcp.go` calls `runGet(..., true, ...)` for `brain_get`/`brain_multi_get` (the primary MCP/agent surface this fix targets), the feature is effectively unreachable for exactly the consumers most likely to act on a `--branch` retry hint. The note should also be added to the JSON payload before line 760.\n\n--- ID: 01M42HRFVSJ9H3GW9AH634C2PB | sev: high | None None\n`loadAllFactBranches` at blind_spot.go:111 lacks symlink validation, while similar functions like `loadAllFactBranchesForPrivacy` explicitly check for and reject symlinks. An attacker with write access to `.entire/brain/facts/` could create a symlink pointing outside the repository, potentially exposing sensitive files when `otherBranchBlindSpot` is triggered on empty query results. The privacy variant checks `entry.Type()&os.ModeSymlink != 0` at session_privacy.go:1140 and single-branch `loadFacts` uses `rejectExistingSymlinkPathComponents` at facts.go:146, but this new code path bypasses both protections.\n\n########## TRAIL 247 ##########\n\n--- ID: 01M421MP2QH04VT7H2XQ9GXR4G | sev: medium | None None\nBroken markdown code fence: line 134 opens a code fence with ``` (no language), then prose appears inside the fence (lines 136-141), then `sh` appears on line 143 as if it's a language specifier but it's actually inside the previous code block. Either close the fence on line 134 and reopen with ````sh` on line 143, or replace the ``` on line 134 with ````sh` and remove line 143's `sh`.\n\n--- ID: 01M420K6PZ7324PDZ1GEJVDNCE | sev: high | None None\n`MergePreEditHook` is called with the literal string `\"entire brain\"` instead of the resolved prefix from `setupCommandPrefix(os.LookupEnv)` (used everywhere else in this package, see `internal/cli/setup_invocation.go`). For a standalone-binary install (no `ENTIRE_CLI_VERSION`, i.e. no `entire` host CLI on PATH), the correct invocation is `entire-brain`, not `entire brain`. The hook written into `.claude/settings.json` will therefore be `entire brain hook pre-edit`, a command that does not exist on that user's PATH — silently defeating the only push-path feature this PR adds, for exactly the install mode `setupCommandPrefix`'s own doc comment calls out as the common fallback case.\n\n--- ID: 01M3ZYEYYSNFAQRBH3NM7VXKT3 | sev: high | None None\nMergePreEditHook bypasses repository containment safeguards by using raw `os.WriteFile` instead of `os.OpenRoot()`. The existing codebase (see `internal/agentsetup/files.go:74`) uses `os.OpenRoot()` for all repository writes to prevent symlink-based path traversal attacks. If `root/.claude` is a symlink to a directory outside the repository, this writes to an arbitrary location. Should use the existing `os.OpenRoot()` + `resolveContainedName` pattern like other file writes in this package.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"9e17989f-5547-4fb2-8827-76288ff962e0","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","root":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","branch":"fix/agent-guide-directive-and-discovery","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"entireio","host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"},{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"},{"host":"github.