{"parentUuid":"f816f5c6-c814-4264-9317-67fb683e0854","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfgaNWr4GcTuJxvTDUWmo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Each guard is now individually justified by the vector only it catches. Full suite and commit:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1254,"cache_read_input_tokens":272297,"output_tokens":1163,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1254,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1163,"cache_read_input_tokens":272297,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1254,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1254},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"3ea78e4c-05f9-4514-8e2b-37a4c707c3ea","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfgaNVK2y8BdFKoKmc8uJ","type":"assistant","uuid":"628b9677-b955-4617-b150-449ddf3d9e03","timestamp":"2026-10-04T04:36:14.351Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"628b9677-b955-4617-b150-449ddf3d9e03","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfgaNWr4GcTuJxvTDUWmo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UHAvkjpra8uUD7Awhvzczp","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp/pr318\ngofmt -l internal/ | head -2\ngo test ./internal/cli/ -count=1 -timeout 2400s > ~/.local/state/entire-distill/pr318e.log 2>&1; echo \"suite exit=$?\"\ngrep -E \"^FAIL|\\[FAIL\\]\" ~/.local/state/entire-distill/pr318e.log | head -4\ngit add -A\ngit commit -q -m \"fix(blind-spot): emit the miss note on the JSON surface, and contain the fact inventory\n\nTwo findings from the agent review of this branch. Both were right that\nsomething was wrong; one was wrong about why.\n\nTHE JSON SURFACE NEVER CARRIED THE NOTE.\n\nThe branch note and the integrity warning lived inside runGet's text block, and\nthe jsonOut branch returns before it. mcp.go:1323,1333 call runGet with\njsonOut=true for brain_get and brain_multi_get, so the AGENT surface -- the\nconsumer most likely to act on a \\\"--branch\\\" hint -- was the one that could not\nsee it. The integrity note had this gap before any of this work and inherits\nthe fix.\n\nBoth notes now come from getMissNote, computed once above the format split and\ncarried as blind_spot in JSON. My own end-to-end test missed this because it\nused text output: the same call-site class I had already hit twice on this\nstack.\n\nTHE FACT INVENTORY READ WHATEVER A SYMLINK POINTED AT.\n\nloadAllFactBranches parsed each branch's facts file with no containment guards,\nwhile the single-branch loadFacts applies two (facts.go:146,150). Measured: a\nsymlinked facts.ndjson inside a real branch directory made loadFacts refuse\nwith \\\"path component must not be a symlink\\\" while the inventory returned the\noutside content. Now guarded the same way.\n\nThe finding's stated mechanism is REFUTED: it named a symlinked branch\nDIRECTORY, and os.ReadDir reports entry types without dereferencing, so\nIsDir() is false and the walk already skipped it -- measured, and pinned by a\ntest so the distinction survives. It also called the function new on this\nbranch; it is on main. The gap was the file one level down, and a new caller\nhere (otherBranchBlindSpot, on every empty result) is what widened the exposure.\n\nEach guard is justified by the vector only IT catches, because a single\nsymlinked-file test left both individually removable: the component guard\ncatches the facts DIRECTORY being a symlink, which os.ReadDir does follow, and\nthe Lstat check catches a non-regular store, which is not a symlink at all.\nBoth verified compile-clean -- and the first run of that isolation reported\nneither as necessary because the grep required leading spaces that top-level\n--- FAIL lines do not have. The harness was broken, not the guards.\" 2>&1 | tail -2\ngit push -q origin HEAD:fix/blind-spot-other-branches 2>&1|tail -1\necho \"pushed: $(git rev-parse --short HEAD)\"","description":"Commit both 318 review fixes","timeout":3000000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1254,"cache_read_input_tokens":272297,"output_tokens":1163,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1254,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1163,"cache_read_input_tokens":272297,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1254,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1254},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01UHAvkjpra8uUD7Awhvzczp":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp/pr318\ngofmt -l internal/ | head -2\ngo test ./internal/cli/ -count=1 -timeout 2400s > ~/.local/state/entire-distill/pr318e.log 2>&1; echo \"suite exit=$?\"\ngrep -E \"^FAIL|\\[FAIL\\]\" ~/.local/state/entire-distill/pr318e.log | head -4\ngit add -A\ngit commit -q -m \"fix(blind-spot): emit the miss note on the JSON surface, and contain the fact inventory\n\nTwo findings from the agent review of this branch. Both were right that\nsomething was wrong; one was wrong about why.\n\nTHE JSON SURFACE NEVER CARRIED THE NOTE.\n\nThe branch note and the integrity warning lived inside runGet's text block, and\nthe jsonOut branch returns before it. mcp.go:1323,1333 call runGet with\njsonOut=true for brain_get and brain_multi_get, so the AGENT surface -- the\nconsumer most likely to act on a \\\"--branch\\\" hint -- was the one that could not\nsee it. The integrity note had this gap before any of this work and inherits\nthe fix.\n\nBoth notes now come from getMissNote, computed once above the format split and\ncarried as blind_spot in JSON. My own end-to-end test missed this because it\nused text output: the same call-site class I had already hit twice on this\nstack.\n\nTHE FACT INVENTORY READ WHATEVER A SYMLINK POINTED AT.\n\nloadAllFactBranches parsed each branch's facts file with no containment guards,\nwhile the single-branch loadFacts applies two (facts.go:146,150). Measured: a\nsymlinked facts.ndjson inside a real branch directory made loadFacts refuse\nwith \\\"path component must not be a symlink\\\" while the inventory returned the\noutside content. Now guarded the same way.\n\nThe finding's stated mechanism is REFUTED: it named a symlinked branch\nDIRECTORY, and os.ReadDir reports entry types without dereferencing, so\nIsDir() is false and the walk already skipped it -- measured, and pinned by a\ntest so the distinction survives. It also called the function new on this\nbranch; it is on main. The gap was the file one level down, and a new caller\nhere (otherBranchBlindSpot, on every empty result) is what widened the exposure.\n\nEach guard is justified by the vector only IT catches, because a single\nsymlinked-file test left both individually removable: the component guard\ncatches the facts DIRECTORY being a symlink, which os.ReadDir does follow, and\nthe Lstat check catches a non-regular store, which is not a symlink at all.\nBoth verified compile-clean -- and the first run of that isolation reported\nneither as necessary because the grep required leading spaces that top-level\n--- FAIL lines do not have. The harness was broken, not the guards.\" 2>&1 | tail -2\ngit push -q origin HEAD:fix/blind-spot-other-branches 2>&1|tail -1\necho \"pushed: $(git rev-parse --short HEAD)\"","description":"Commit both 318 review fixes","timeout":3000000}},"serverClassifierRequest":"3ea78e4c-05f9-4514-8e2b-37a4c707c3ea","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfgaNVK2y8BdFKoKmc8uJ","type":"assistant","uuid":"a96f190e-b9f5-481c-babd-0506ffa386fa","timestamp":"2026-10-04T04:36:28.126Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
