{"parentUuid":"fff0d765-f0c4-4f1e-8e1d-44499b6df3ea","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfgcRTE6n9T5qGGW3kLYE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JuhU1Xv93G7MRmfNsUqXBQ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide\npython3 - <<'PY'\np='internal/agentsetup/claudehooks_test.go'; s=open(p).read()\nold='''// ATTRIBUTION, measured rather than assumed: it is the contained READ that\n// refuses this fixture, because it runs first and resolveContainedName rejects\n// the symlinked component before the write is reached. Reverting the write\n// alone leaves this test green. The contained write and MkdirAll are pinned by\n// the pre-existing merge tests above (clobber, idempotent, hand-written\n// equivalent), which do go red when either is reverted. Three guards, all\n// held, just not all by this test -- worth saying, because a test that passes\n// for a different reason than its name claims is how an unheld guard survives\n// a mutation sweep.'''\nnew='''// ATTRIBUTION, measured rather than assumed. There are three contained calls\n// here -- the read, the MkdirAll and the write -- and the measured result is:\n//\n//   all three reverted  -> this test and the read test both go RED\n//   any ONE kept        -> still refused, both tests green\n//\n// So no single call is NECESSARY for this fixture and each is SUFFICIENT. That\n// is defence in depth rather than three independent guards, and it is worth\n// stating plainly: a sweep that mutates one call at a time will report all\n// three as unheld, which is how a real escape could later be introduced by\n// removing them together. The decisive check is reverting all three.'''\nassert s.count(old)==1\nopen(p,'w').write(s.replace(old,new)); print(\"attribution set to the measured result\")\nPY\ngofmt -w internal/agentsetup/claudehooks_test.go\necho \"=== the markdown fence finding: which file has a fence at line 134? ===\"\nfor f in $(git diff --name-only origin/main...HEAD | grep -E '\\.(md|go)$'); do\n  n=$(sed -n '130,145p' \"$f\" 2>/dev/null | grep -c '```' || true)\n  [ \"${n:-0}\" -gt 0 ] && echo \"$f  (fences near 130-145: $n)\"\ndone | head -5","description":"Fix attribution and locate the markdown fence","timeout":1200000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1376,"cache_read_input_tokens":314964,"output_tokens":1185,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":288},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1376,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1185,"cache_read_input_tokens":314964,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1376,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1376},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01JuhU1Xv93G7MRmfNsUqXBQ":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide\npython3 - <<'PY'\np='internal/agentsetup/claudehooks_test.go'; s=open(p).read()\nold='''// ATTRIBUTION, measured rather than assumed: it is the contained READ that\n// refuses this fixture, because it runs first and resolveContainedName rejects\n// the symlinked component before the write is reached. Reverting the write\n// alone leaves this test green. The contained write and MkdirAll are pinned by\n// the pre-existing merge tests above (clobber, idempotent, hand-written\n// equivalent), which do go red when either is reverted. Three guards, all\n// held, just not all by this test -- worth saying, because a test that passes\n// for a different reason than its name claims is how an unheld guard survives\n// a mutation sweep.'''\nnew='''// ATTRIBUTION,