{"parentUuid":"a6f14b49-f8b0-4aea-9af0-58820400448c","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"e7885167-dc2d-44de-bb8f-d1c797ad583a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NxW3D7ckKyE9Eamp28Q9y8","type":"tool_result","content":"     1\tentire graph init-agents   # only if Graph is installed; see the note below\n     2\tentire brain init-agents\n     3\t```\n     4\t\n     5\tThe command creates or updates these files:\n     6\t\n     7\t- `.entire/agent-guide.md`: the agent instructions. Rerunning the command replaces this file.\n     8\t- `AGENTS.md` and `CLAUDE.md`: references to the guide inside managed blocks. Your text outside those blocks is preserved.\n     9\t\n    10\tThe guide is assembled from whichever products have been **activated**, and each\n    11\tproduct activates itself. `entire brain init-agents` on its own writes a\n    12\tBrain-only guide containing no Graph instructions at all — installing Graph does\n    13\tnot change that, because activation is recorded in the guide rather than probed.\n    14\tRun Graph's `init-agents` too if you want both.\n    15\t\n    16\tRun Brain's **last**. Each product rewrites the shared guide file from its own\n    17\tcopy of the text, so whichever you run last decides the wording.\n    18\t\n    19\tReview the generated files and commit them together when the instructions should apply to your team. Restart your agent or reload its repository instructions so it picks up the guide.\n    20\t\n    21\tFor an MCP client, print this repository's configuration:\n    22\t\n    23\t```\n    24\t\n    25\tThe agent guide is assembled from whichever products have been activated, and\n    26\teach product activates itself. `entire brain init-agents` alone writes a\n    27\tBrain-only guide with no Graph instructions in it, even when Graph is installed\n    28\t— so run Graph's `init-agents` too if you want both. Run Brain's **last**: each\n    29\tproduct rewrites the shared guide file from its 