{"parentUuid":"78288238-9668-4865-a780-070ad64c63ef","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfgcqKY9ddvzSRPQqykLc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":366,"cache_read_input_tokens":320601,"output_tokens":1210,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":104},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":366,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1210,"cache_read_input_tokens":320601,"cache_creation_input_tokens":366,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":366},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":952,"serverClassifierRequest":"7eeb556f-3ff9-4fe5-8eb1-2a9f0273b7c7","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfgcqJiJ4JxmnHNRBYHdn","type":"assistant","uuid":"9a0f95bd-75ee-405e-9eff-acdad0832dfd","timestamp":"2026-10-04T05:08:32.418Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"9a0f95bd-75ee-405e-9eff-acdad0832dfd","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfgcqKY9ddvzSRPQqykLc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VoY1cP1r9JcAJvjATgj89r","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide\ngit add -A\ngit commit -q -m \"fix(guide): resolve the hook invocation, contain its write, repair the README fence\n\nThree findings from the agent review of this branch. All three were real; one\nprescribed a remedy that breaks the feature.\n\nTHE HOOK NAMED A COMMAND THAT MAY NOT EXIST.\n\nagent_setup.go hardcoded \\\"entire brain\\\". That is correct only when a host\nentire CLI is on PATH; for a standalone install -- no ENTIRE_CLI_VERSION, which\nsetupCommandPrefix's own doc comment calls the common fallback -- the\ninvocation is \\`entire-brain\\`. The hook written into .claude/settings.json\nwould have been a command that does not exist, failing silently on every edit:\nthe same installed-and-inert failure this PR exists to fix. Now resolved with\nsetupCommandPrefix(os.LookupEnv), as every other caller in the package does.\n\nTHE HOOK WRITE COULD LEAVE THE REPOSITORY.\n\nMeasured before the fix: with \\`.claude\\` a symlink to another directory,\nMergePreEditHook wrote 255 bytes outside the repository. The read, the MkdirAll\nand the write now all go through an os.Root, which resolves each component with\nopenat so a link that stays inside is still followed and one that escapes is\nrefused. The read is included deliberately -- reading through an escaping\nsymlink would merge a settings file from outside and write the result back.\n\nThe prescribed remedy was \\\"os.OpenRoot() + resolveContainedName like other\nfile writes in this package\\\". The containment is right and is applied;\nresolveContainedName is NOT, and adopting it breaks the feature outright: it\nenforces an agent-instruction-file allowlist (AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, the guide)\nand refuses everything else. .claude/settings.json is not one. Three\npre-existing merge tests went red on exactly that error, which is how this was\ncaught rather than shipped.\n\nMeasured attribution, recorded in the test: all three contained calls reverted\nturns both escape tests red; keeping ANY ONE still refuses. So this is defence\nin depth, not three independent guards, and a sweep mutating one call at a time\nwill report all three as unheld. The decisive check is reverting all three.\n\nREADME FENCE.\n\nLine 134 opened a bare fence, trapped six lines of prose inside it, and left\n\\`sh\\` on line 143 reading as a language specifier when it was code-block\ncontent. The trapped paragraph was a worse duplicate of the activation note\ntwelve lines above, so it is removed rather than relocated, and the fence is\nnow \\`\\`\\`sh around the command alone. Fence parity across the file checked, and\nno stranded language line remains.\" 2>&1 | tail -2\ngit push -q origin HEAD:fix/agent-guide-directive-and-discovery 2>&1|tail -1\necho \"pushed: $(git rev-parse --short HEAD)\"","description":"Commit all three 331 review fixes","timeout":1200000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":366,"cache_read_input_tokens":320601,"output_tokens":1210,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":104},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":366,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1210,"cache_read_input_tokens":320601,"cache_creation_input_tokens":366,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":366},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01VoY1cP1r9JcAJvjATgj89r":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide\ngit add -A\ngit commit -q -m \"fix(guide): resolve the hook invocation, contain its write, repair the README fence\n\nThree findings from the agent review of this branch. All three were real; one\nprescribed a remedy that breaks the feature.\n\nTHE HOOK NAMED A COMMAND THAT MAY NOT EXIST.\n\nagent_setup.go hardcoded \\\"entire brain\\\". That is correct only when a host\nentire CLI is on PATH; for a standalone install -- no ENTIRE_CLI_VERSION, which\nsetupCommandPrefix's own doc comment calls the common fallback -- the\ninvocation is \\`entire-brain\\`. The hook written into .claude/settings.json\nwould have been a command that does not exist, failing silently on every edit:\nthe same installed-and-inert failure this PR exists to fix. Now resolved with\nsetupCommandPrefix(os.LookupEnv), as every other caller in the package does.\n\nTHE HOOK WRITE COULD LEAVE THE REPOSITORY.\n\nMeasured before the fix: with \\`.claude\\` a symlink to another directory,\nMergePreEditHook wrote 255 bytes outside the repository. The read, the MkdirAll\nand the write now all go through an os.Root, which resolves each component with\nopenat so a link that stays inside is still followed and one that escapes is\nrefused. The read is included deliberately -- reading through an escaping\nsymlink would merge a settings file from outside and write the result back.\n\nThe prescribed remedy was \\\"os.OpenRoot() + resolveContainedName like other\nfile writes in this package\\\". The containment is right and is applied;\nresolveContainedName is NOT, and adopting it breaks the feature outright: it\nenforces an agent-instruction-file allowlist (AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, the guide)\nand refuses everything else. .claude/settings.json is not one. Three\npre-existing merge tests went red on exactly that error, which is how this was\ncaught rather than shipped.\n\nMeasured attribution, recorded in the test: all three contained calls reverted\nturns both escape tests red; keeping ANY ONE still refuses. So this is defence\nin depth, not three independent guards, and a sweep mutating one call at a time\nwill report all three as unheld. The decisive check is reverting all three.\n\nREADME FENCE.\n\nLine 134 opened a bare fence, trapped six lines of prose inside it, and left\n\\`sh\\` on line 143 reading as a language specifier when it was code-block\ncontent. The trapped paragraph was a worse duplicate of the activation note\ntwelve lines above, so it is removed rather than relocated, and the fence is\nnow \\`\\`\\`sh around the command alone. Fence parity across the file checked, and\nno stranded language line remains.\" 2>&1 | tail -2\ngit push -q origin HEAD:fix/agent-guide-directive-and-discovery 2>&1|tail -1\necho \"pushed: $(git rev-parse --short HEAD)\"","description":"Commit all three 331 review fixes","timeout":1200000}},"serverClassifierRequest":"7eeb556f-3ff9-4fe5-8eb1-2a9f0273b7c7","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfgcqJiJ4JxmnHNRBYHdn","type":"assistant","uuid":"8fdd88bd-1e47-462c-bf0a-d24ae4e43822","timestamp":"2026-10-04T05:08:45.059Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
