{"parentUuid":"f65f7baf-11a7-446d-bf63-80e0779550db","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14608551 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"a55271e1-ebde-4253-a12a-c9bce0468129","timestamp":"2026-10-04T05:11:52.350Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14608551 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"a55271e1-ebde-4253-a12a-c9bce0468129","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cfgd6GjQH3Zhmn7iXn1ce","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01L5rSc6ZR6q8s1sbHJnL3hT","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv\nEB=/Users/suhaan/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp/entire-main\n$EB trail finding resolve 238 01M42J6JYAMBSB9HGN4SGAMREJ --repo gh/entireio/entire-brain -m \"FIXED in b32dbf32 — confirmed exactly as described, including the part that matters most: mcp.go:1323,1333 call runGet with jsonOut=true for brain_get and brain_multi_get, so the agent surface was the one consumer that could not see the hint it is most likely to act on.\n\nIt was worse than reported. The PRE-EXISTING integrity warning (\\\"not found is NOT evidence of absence\\\") lived in the same text block, so get --json never carried that either. Both now come from getMissNote, computed once above the format split and emitted as blind_spot in the JSON payload.\n\nMy own end-to-end test missed this because it used text output — the same call-site class I had already hit twice on this stack.\n\nGuards: TestGetJSONCarriesTheMissNote asserts a miss was actually produced before checking the note, and TestGetJSONMissNoteFollowsTheSameGates pins that integrity still wins over the branch note on the JSON surface. Dropping blind_spot from the payload turns the first red:\n\n    get_branch_note_test.go:158: get --json must carry the branch note; it is the surface MCP uses. got \\\"\\\"\" 2>&1 | tail -1\n\n$EB trail finding resolve 238 01M42HRFVSJ9H3GW9AH634C2PB --repo gh/entireio/entire-brain -m \"FIXED in b32dbf32 — a real gap, but the stated mechanism is REFUTED and the ownership claim is wrong. Both corrections are measured.\n\nREFUTED: a symlinked branch DIRECTORY is not a vector. os.ReadDir reports entry types without dereferencing, so a symlink-to-directory has IsDir()==false and Type()&os.ModeSymlink!=0 — measured — and the existing \\`if !entry.IsDir() { continue }\\` already skips it. Pinned now by TestFactInventorySkipsASymlinkedBranchDirectory so the distinction survives.\n\nALSO WRONG: loadAllFactBranches is not new on this branch; it is on main (facts_manifest.go:13). What this branch adds is a new CALLER, otherBranchBlindSpot, which runs on every empty retrieval result — that is what widened the exposure and justifies fixing it here.\n\nTHE REAL GAP, one level down: a symlinked facts.ndjson INSIDE a real branch directory was read. Measured, same fixture, both functions:\n\n    loadFacts(brainDir, \\\"main\\\")  -> refused: path component must not be a symlink\n    loadAllFactBranches(brainDir) -> returned: evil:CONTENT FROM OUTSIDE\n\nNow guarded with the same two checks loadFacts applies (facts.go:146,150).\n\nEach guard is justified by the vector only IT catches, because a single symlinked-file test left both individually removable — measured. Without the component guard, TestFactInventoryRefusesASymlinkedFactsDirectory goes red (os.ReadDir DOES follow the path it is given, so a symlinked facts/ directory reads the whole tree from outside while every inner file looks regular). Without the Lstat check, TestFactInventoryRefusesANonRegularFactStore goes red. Both verified compile-clean.\" 2>&1 | tail -1","description":"Resolve the two 318 findings","timeout":1200000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":952,"cache_read_input_tokens":338185,"output_tokens":1289,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":952,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1289,"cache_read_input_tokens":338185,"cache_creation_input_tokens":952,"cache_creation":{