f !entry.IsDir() { continue }\\` already skips it. Pinned now by TestFactInventorySkipsASymlinkedBranchDirectory so the distinction survives.\n\nALSO WRONG: loadAllFactBranches is not new on this branch; it is on main (facts_manifest.go:13). What this branch adds is a new CALLER, otherBranchBlindSpot, which runs on every empty retrieval result — that is what widened the exposure and justifies fixing it here.\n\nTHE REAL GAP, one level down: a symlinked facts.ndjson INSIDE a real branch directory was read. Measured, same fixture, both functions:\n\n    loadFacts(brainDir, \\\"main\\\")  -> refused: path component must not be a symlink\n    loadAllFactBranches(brainDir) -> returned: evil:CONTENT FROM OUTSIDE\n\nNow guarded with the same two checks loadFacts applies (facts.go:146,150).\n\nEach guard is justified by the vector only IT catches, because a single symlinked-file test left both individually removable — measured. Without the component guard, TestFactInventoryRefusesASymlinkedFactsDirectory goes red (os.ReadDir DOES follow the path it is given, so a symlinked facts/ directory reads the whole tree from outside while every inner file looks regular). Without the Lstat check, TestFactInventoryRefusesANonRegularFactStore goes red. Both verified compile-clean.\" 2>&1 | tail -1","description":"Resolve the two 318 findings","timeout":1200000}},"serverClassifierRequest":"49d7762a-3369-499d-9378-f515644f8382","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cfgd6FrpB6bL6VSqtLUeU","type":"assistant","uuid":"a0726962-69dc-4f84-930f-a3e3713d6a1e","timestamp":"2026-10-04T05:12:09.458Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
