{"parentUuid":"288a134d-aa2f-4ec4-bcbd-d56c57a84af0","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14607161 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"e513110b-5b54-4b22-8b19-c82ee58aa41e","timestamp":"2026-10-04T05:12:13.060Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14607161 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"e513110b-5b54-4b22-8b19-c82ee58aa41e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cfgd7opi7deHZpkJYM8rt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019GTdMU4vhvCiedpwmMvKL4","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv\nEB=/Users/suhaan/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp/entire-main\n$EB trail finding resolve 247 01M420K6PZ7324PDZ1GEJVDNCE --repo gh/entireio/entire-brain -m \"FIXED in 32e5b664 — correct in full, and this was the finding that would have silently defeated the only push-path feature this PR adds.\n\nagent_setup.go hardcoded \\\"entire brain\\\". That is right only when a host entire CLI is on PATH; for a standalone install — no ENTIRE_CLI_VERSION, which setupCommandPrefix's own doc comment calls the common fallback — the invocation is \\`entire-brain\\`. The hook written into .claude/settings.json would have been a command that does not exist, failing on every edit without ever saying so: the same installed-and-inert failure this PR exists to fix, reintroduced by the fix.\n\nNow setupCommandPrefix(os.LookupEnv), matching agent_surface.go:1190, env.go:173, path.go:166.\n\nGuard: TestPreEditHookUsesTheGivenInvocation writes settings for both \\\"entire-brain\\\" and \\\"entire brain\\\" and asserts the file carries the invocation it was given.\" 2>&1 | tail -1\n\n$EB trail finding resolve 247 01M3ZYEYYSNFAQRBH3NM7VXKT3 --repo gh/entireio/entire-brain -m \"FIXED in 32e5b664 — the defect is real and reproduced. The prescribed remedy was rejected because adopting it breaks the feature outright, which is worth stating in full.\n\nREPRODUCED: with \\`.claude\\` a symlink to another directory, MergePreEditHook wrote 255 bytes outside the repository.\n\nFIXED: the read, the MkdirAll and the write now all go through an os.Root. The read is included deliberately — reading through an escaping symlink would merge a settings file from outside the repository and write the result back, so containment has to cover both ends.\n\nREMEDY REJECTED, with evidence: the suggestion was \\\"os.OpenRoot() + resolveContainedName like other file writes in this package\\\". The containment is right and is applied. resolveContainedName is not: it enforces an agent-instruction-file allowlist (AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, the guide) and refuses everything else with \\\"not an agent-instruction file\\\". .claude/settings.json is not one. Three pre-existing merge tests went red on exactly that error when I tried it — which is how this was caught rather than shipped. os.Root's own methods give the openat component resolution with no allowlist.\n\nMEASURED ATTRIBUTION, recorded in the test rather than assumed: all three contained calls reverted turns both escape tests red; keeping ANY ONE still refuses. So this is defence in depth, not three independent guards, and a sweep mutating one call at a time will report all three as unheld. The decisive check is reverting all three.\" 2>&1 | tail -1\n\n$EB trail finding resolve 247 01M421MP2QH04VT7H2XQ9GXR4G --repo gh/entireio/entire-brain -m \"FIXED in 32e5b664 — correct, and the diagnosis was precise: line 134 opened a bare fence, six lines of prose sat inside it, and \\`sh\\` on line 143 read as a language specifier while actually being code-block content.\n\nTaking the second of the two suggested repairs, with one addition: the trapped paragraph was a near-duplicate of the activation note twelve lines above (README.md:121-128), so it is removed rather than relocated. The fence is now \\`\\`\\`sh around the command alone.\n\nChecked after the edit: fence lines across the file total 40 (balanced), and no stranded bare language line remains outside a fence.\" 2>&1 | tail -1","description":"Resolve the three 331 findings","timeout":1200000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1390,"cache_read_input_tokens":3