{"parentUuid":"5e2e672a-b8e2-4551-813b-24b213fa626b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfgdAKf8PPiVCUKwVv5Sy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014n6vqSBgUvHEM9RZJvgVpD","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv\nEB=/Users/suhaan/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp/entire-main\nfor t in 226 247; do\n  printf \"\\n########## TRAIL %s ##########\\n\" \"$t\"\n  $EB trail finding list \"$t\" --repo gh/entireio/entire-brain --freshness any --status open --json 2>/dev/null \\\n  | sed '/^Using context/d' | python3 -c '\nimport json,sys\nd=json.load(sys.stdin)\nfor f in d.get(\"findings\",[]):\n    print(\"\\n--- \"+f[\"id\"])\n    print((f.get(\"body\") or \"\").strip()[:1000])\n'\ndone","description":"Read the four new findings in full","timeout":1200000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1092,"cache_read_input_tokens":342060,"output_tokens":364,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1092,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":364,"cache_read_input_tokens":342060,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1092,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1092},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_014n6vqSBgUvHEM9RZJvgVpD":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv\nEB=/Users/suhaan/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp/entire-main\nfor t in 226 247; do\n  printf \"\\n########## TRAIL %s ##########\\n\" \"$t\"\n  $EB trail finding list \"$t\" --repo gh/entireio/entire-brain --freshness any --status open --json 2>/dev/null \\\n  | sed '/^Using context/d' | python3 -c '\nimport json,sys\nd=json.load(sys.stdin)\nfor f in d.get(\"findings\",[]):\n    print(\"\\n--- \"+f[\"id\"])\n    print((f.get(\"body\") or \"\").strip()[:1000])\n'\ndone","description":"Read the four new findings in full","timeout":1200000}},"serverClassifierRequest":"74f13638-9dc1-4efe-9021-06e7dc1c82d1","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfgdAJPjAEHfMzvJ9GMUD","type":"assistant","uuid":"39ae8edb-1852-4b44-810f-e6979ec97a72","timestamp":"2026-10-04T05:12:52.170Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"39ae8edb-1852-4b44-810f-e6979ec97a72","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"e7885167-dc2d-44de-bb8f-d1c797ad583a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014n6vqSBgUvHEM9RZJvgVpD","type":"tool_result","content":"########## TRAIL 226 ##########\n\n--- 01M42MCX9Q6Z6W9ENBD2PG6YN5\n`upsertFact`/`factmerge.Upsert` keys purely on content-addressed `ID` (text+paths) and unions provenance while keeping the *existing* record's `Origin` unchanged. If an imported memory's text+paths normalise to the same ID as a pre-existing non-imported fact (e.g. importing under `--path-prefix` set to an existing real taxonomy category, which `validateImportPrefixAgainstTaxonomy` explicitly permits), the merged record keeps `Origin` != `\"imported\"` but now carries the foreign `source:foreignID` anchor. `verifyFact`'s new imported-origin short-circuit (lines 310-343) never triggers for this record, so `verifyAnchor` tries to resolve the foreign `SessionID` as a real local session, fails, and reports the fact `orphaned` (\"its evidence is gone\") — exactly the false/alarming diagnosis this PR's own comments say importing must avoid, just reached through a different path than the one explicitly guarded against.\n\n--- 01M42MCX9CAMPMTQYAERT9N6SQ\nThe foreign `id` field (`mem.ForeignID`, raw from the untrusted export) is embedded unsanitised into the fact's anchor as `SessionID: source + \":\" + mem.ForeignID`. This file explicitly treats `m.Memory` as untrusted and runs it through `sanitizeDistilledFactText` because unescaped foreign text reaches the terminal (see the comment at line ~116 and `TestImportedMemoryTextIsSanitised`), but the same raw-text-to-terminal path exists for `SessionID`: `facts show <id>` (`facts_read_cmd.go`) prints `a.SessionID` directly via `%s` with no quoting. An export with ANSI escapes, bidi overrides or zero-width runes in `id` reaches the terminal unsanitised, contradicting this file's own stated threat model for foreign text.\n\n########## TRAIL 247 ##########\n\n--- 01M42N6V3PRADWNXEK1A4EB1R8\n`hookFileFromStdin` is now invoked whenever `--file` is empty, including when the command is run by hand in a terminal with no `--file` and no piped stdin. `io.ReadAll(io.LimitReader(in, 1<<20))` blocks until EOF or 1MB is read, so on a real TTY (not an empty `strings.Reader` as in the tests) the command hangs indefinitely instead of hitting the old immediate `--file is required` error. The codebase already has a `stdinIsTerminal()` helper (`internal/cli/seed.go:1810`) for exactly this situation; consider checking it before reading stdin here so manual/hand-testing invocations fail fast instead of hanging.\n\n--- 01M42N6V3D38AG3ZH7MQB30N39\n`semanticIndexKindInventory` sums `c` only over the rows returned by `SELECT kind, count(*) c FROM symbols GROUP BY kind ORDER BY c DESC LIMIT 6` (`internal/cli/semantic.go:3528`), so `total` undercounts whenever the store has more than 6 distinct kinds — it's a partial sum of the top 6 groups, not the real total. The note this feeds (`\"the index holds %d symbols of kinds %s\"`) is specifically meant to give an agent an accurate picture after the empty-result confusion described in the surrounding comment; reporting a wrong, too-low total risks the exact same false-root-cause problem this fix was written to prevent. Use a separate `SELECT count(*) FROM symbols` for `total` and keep the `LIMIT 6` only for the displayed `kinds` list.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"ffe0909d-57fc-4b28-906d-b3834b6b564b","timestamp":"2026-10-04T05:12:56.513Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"########## TRAIL 226 ##########\n\n--- 01M42MCX9Q6Z6W9ENBD2PG6YN5\n`upsertFact`/`factmerge.Upsert` keys purely on content-addressed `ID` (text+paths) and unions provenance while keeping the *existing* record's `Origin` unchanged. If an imported memory's text+paths normalise to the same ID as a pre-existing non-imported fact (e.g. importing under `--path-prefix` set to an existing real taxonomy category, which `validateImportPrefixAgainstTaxonomy` explicitly permits), the merged record keeps `Origin` != `\"imported\"` but now carries the foreign `source:foreignID` anchor. `verifyFact`'s new imported-origin short-circuit (lines 310-343) never triggers for this record, so `verifyAnchor` tries to resolve the foreign `SessionID` as a real local session, fails, and reports the fact `orphaned` (\"its evidence is gone\") — exactly the false/alarming diagnosis this PR's own comments say importing must avoid, just reached through a different path than the one explicitly guarded against.\n\n--- 01M42MCX9CAMPMTQYAERT9N6SQ\nThe foreign `id` field (`mem.ForeignID`, raw from the untrusted export) is embedded unsanitised into the fact's anchor as `SessionID: source + \":\" + mem.ForeignID`. This file explicitly treats `m.Memory` as untrusted and runs it through `sanitizeDistilledFactText` because unescaped foreign text reaches the terminal (see the comment at line ~116 and `TestImportedMemoryTextIsSanitised`), but the same raw-text-to-terminal path exists for `SessionID`: `facts show <id>` (`facts_read_cmd.go`) prints `a.SessionID` directly via `%s` with no quoting. An export with ANSI escapes, bidi overrides or zero-width runes in `id` reaches the terminal unsanitised, contradicting this file's own stated threat model for foreign text.\n\n########## TRAIL 247 ##########\n\n--- 01M42N6V3PRADWNXEK1A4EB1R8\n`hookFileFromStdin` is now invoked whenever `--file` is empty, including when the command is run by hand in a terminal with no `--file` and no piped stdin. `io.ReadAll(io.LimitReader(in, 1<<20))` blocks until EOF or 1MB is read, so on a real TTY (not an empty `strings.Reader` as in the tests) the command hangs indefinitely instead of hitting the old immediate `--file is required` error. The codebase already has a `stdinIsTerminal()` helper (`internal/cli/seed.go:1810`) for exactly this situation; consider checking it before reading stdin here so manual/hand-testing invocations fail fast instead of hanging.\n\n--- 01M42N6V3D38AG3ZH7MQB30N39\n`semanticIndexKindInventory` sums `c` only over the rows returned by `SELECT kind, count(*) c FROM symbols GROUP BY kind ORDER BY c DESC LIMIT 6` (`internal/cli/semantic.go:3528`), so `total` undercounts whenever the store has more than 6 distinct kinds — it's a partial sum of the top 6 groups, not the real total. The note this feeds (`\"the index holds %d symbols of kinds %s\"`) is specifically meant to give an agent an accurate picture after the empty-result confusion described in the surrounding comment; reporting a wrong, too-low total risks the exact same false-root-cause problem this fix was written to prevent. Use a separate `SELECT count(*) FROM symbols` for `total` and keep the `LIMIT 6` only for the displayed `kinds` list.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"74f13638-9dc1-4efe-9021-06e7dc1c82d1","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","root":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":1,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":242},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-graph","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/entiredb","visibility":"private"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/cli","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"39ae8edb-1852-4b44-810f-e6979ec97a72","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2