{"parentUuid":"c55a514c-1ca1-4292-9f24-df3b6100b67a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfgdmvjVKscPi5oFRLQCe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The call-site test reproduces the exact `orphaned` verdict the finding predicted. Committing:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":824,"cache_read_input_tokens":363132,"output_tokens":1201,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":824,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1201,"cache_read_input_tokens":363132,"cache_creation_input_tokens":824,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":824},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"928c7001-a0ac-4a92-ab7a-26ac877ae266","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfgdmuseSwfGPHZNcrAzY","type":"assistant","uuid":"420243c0-4e90-4a55-86fd-3add99ea8486","timestamp":"2026-10-04T05:20:52.449Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"420243c0-4e90-4a55-86fd-3add99ea8486","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfgdmvjVKscPi5oFRLQCe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RZnsupubM2pda8LAv3furM","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp/pr306\ngit add -A\ngit commit -q -m \"fix(facts import): classify foreign anchors per-anchor, and sanitise the foreign ids\n\nTwo more findings from the agent review. Both correct, both mine.\n\nA COLLISION GAVE AN AUTHORED FACT A FOREIGN ANCHOR, AND VERIFY CALLED IT ORPHANED.\n\nfactmerge.Upsert keys on the content-addressed id and keeps the EXISTING\nrecord's Origin while unioning provenance. So an imported memory whose text and\npaths normalise onto a pre-existing authored fact -- which importing under an\nexisting taxonomy prefix explicitly permits -- yields a fact with Origin !=\n\\\"imported\\\" that nonetheless carries a foreign anchor. Neither record-level\norigin gate fires, so verify tried to resolve \\\"mem0:abc\\\" as a local session\nand reported the fact ORPHANED: \\\"its evidence is gone\\\", about evidence that\nwas never here. The same false and alarming diagnosis those gates exist to\nprevent, reached by another route.\n\nThe gate is now PER-ANCHOR, which is the correct granularity: that record holds\nits original local anchor AND the foreign one, so the local one is still\nchecked normally while the foreign one returns unverifiable-here, and\nworseVerifyVerdict aggregates without masking a genuine local failure.\n\nDetection needs both the source prefix and the anchor shape. The prefix alone\nwould misread a local session id containing a colon; the shape alone would\nmisread a sparse local anchor. The accepted sources are now one shared list, so\nverify's detection cannot drift from what import writes -- and a test asserts\nevery declared source is detectable, so adding one without teaching verify\nabout it cannot slip through.\n\nTHE FOREIGN IDS WERE NOT SANITISED.\n\nm.Memory goes through sanitizeDistilledFactText because unescaped foreign text\nreaches the terminal. The ids take the same path and I left them raw:\nForeignID is embedded in the anchor as \\\"<tool>:<id>\\\", and \\`facts show\\`\nprints anchor.SessionID straight through valueOrUnset with %s\n(facts_read_cmd.go:540), which neither quotes nor strips.\n\nBoth ids are sanitised, and that is not optional: ReplacedBy is matched against\nForeignID through byForeignID, so cleaning one and not the other would silently\nbreak every supersession whose id contained a stripped character. Stripping is\ndisclosed through the same channel as the text case.\n\nThree guards verified by weakening. The first attempt on the per-anchor gate\nfound nothing: all the detector tests stayed green with the gate removed,\nbecause a perfect detector nothing consults looks identical to them. The\ncall-site test added afterwards reproduces the exact verdict the finding\npredicted -- anchor verdict \\\"orphaned\\\" (session is missing from exported\nsessions on branch main).\" 2>&1 | tail -2\ngit push -q origin HEAD:feat/facts-import 2>&1|tail -1\necho \"pushed: $(git rev-parse --short HEAD)\"","description":"Commit the two new 306 fixes","timeout":1200000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":824,"cache_read_input_tokens":363132,"output_tokens":1201,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":824,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1201,"cache_read_input_tokens":363132,"cache_creation_input_tokens":824,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":824},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01RZnsupubM2pda8LAv3furM":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp/pr306\ngit add -A\ngit commit -q -m \"fix(facts import): classify foreign anchors per-anchor, and sanitise the foreign ids\n\nTwo more findings from the agent review. Both correct, both mine.\n\nA COLLISION GAVE AN AUTHORED FACT A FOREIGN ANCHOR, AND VERIFY CALLED IT ORPHANED.\n\nfactmerge.Upsert keys on the content-addressed id and keeps the EXISTING\nrecord's Origin while unioning provenance. So an imported memory whose text and\npaths normalise onto a pre-existing authored fact -- which importing under an\nexisting taxonomy prefix explicitly permits -- yields a fact with Origin !=\n\\\"imported\\\" that nonetheless carries a foreign anchor. Neither record-level\norigin gate fires, so verify tried to resolve \\\"mem0:abc\\\" as a local session\nand reported the fact ORPHANED: \\\"its evidence is gone\\\", about evidence that\nwas never here. The same false and alarming diagnosis those gates exist to\nprevent, reached by another route.\n\nThe gate is now PER-ANCHOR, which is the correct granularity: that record holds\nits original local anchor AND the foreign one, so the local one is still\nchecked normally while the foreign one returns unverifiable-here, and\nworseVerifyVerdict aggregates without masking a genuine local failure.\n\nDetection needs both the source prefix and the anchor shape. The prefix alone\nwould misread a local session id containing a colon; the shape alone would\nmisread a sparse local anchor. The accepted sources are now one shared list, so\nverify's detection cannot drift from what import writes -- and a test asserts\nevery declared source is detectable, so adding one without teaching verify\nabout it cannot slip through.\n\nTHE FOREIGN IDS WERE NOT SANITISED.\n\nm.Memory goes through sanitizeDistilledFactText because unescaped foreign text\nreaches the terminal. The ids take the same path and I left them raw:\nForeignID is embedded in the anchor as \\\"<tool>:<id>\\\", and \\`facts show\\`\nprints anchor.SessionID straight through valueOrUnset with %s\n(facts_read_cmd.go:540), which neither quotes nor strips.\n\nBoth ids are sanitised, and that is not optional: ReplacedBy is matched against\nForeignID through byForeignID, so cleaning one and not the other would silently\nbreak every supersession whose id contained a stripped character. Stripping is\ndisclosed through the same channel as the text case.\n\nThree guards verified by weakening. The first attempt on the per-anchor gate\nfound nothing: all the detector tests stayed green with the gate removed,\nbecause a perfect detector nothing consults looks identical to them. The\ncall-site test added afterwards reproduces the exact verdict the finding\npredicted -- anchor verdict \\\"orphaned\\\" (session is missing from exported\nsessions on branch main).\" 2>&1 | tail -2\ngit push -q origin HEAD:feat/facts-import 2>&1|tail -1\necho \"pushed: $(git rev-parse --short HEAD)\"","description":"Commit the two new 306 fixes","timeout":1200000}},"serverClassifierRequest":"928c7001-a0ac-4a92-ab7a-26ac877ae266","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfgdmuseSwfGPHZNcrAzY","type":"assistant","uuid":"58c804a9-d1e9-45fb-8923-6d7146db23a6","timestamp":"2026-10-04T05:21:04.522Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
