{"parentUuid":"662b19c0-923c-4c76-81c8-fef3854e0603","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cfge3H7GGZbvuZPMFQe9y","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BY8wUrDSxuX8rXYKG8RSWS","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide\ngofmt -l internal/ | head -2\ngo test ./internal/cli/ ./internal/agentsetup/ -count=1 -timeout 2400s > ~/.local/state/entire-distill/pr331e.log 2>&1; echo \"suites exit=$?\"\ngrep -E \"^--- FAIL: \" ~/.local/state/entire-distill/pr331e.log | head -4\ngit add -A\ngit commit -q -m \"fix: do not read stdin on a terminal, and count every symbol kind\n\nTwo more findings from the agent review. Both correct, both mine.\n\nREADING STDIN HUNG WHEN RUN BY HAND.\n\nhookFileFromStdin does io.ReadAll, which on a real TTY waits for EOF. So\n\\`hook pre-edit\\` with no --file hung indefinitely where it previously failed\nfast with \\\"--file is required\\\" -- my fix traded a clear error for a hang. The\ntests missed it because they supply a strings.Reader, which EOFs at once.\n\nThe read is now gated on hookStdinWouldBlock, which is true only when the\nreader IS the process's stdin and that stdin is a character device. The check\nis on the READER, not just the process: a harness always redirects stdin and is\nread, a test with its own reader is read regardless of what the runner did with\nos.Stdin, and only a person at a terminal gets the error.\n\nTHE HANG ITSELF IS NOT REPRODUCIBLE IN-PROCESS -- it needs a real character\ndevice on stdin, which \\`go test\\` does not provide. So the guards are the\npredicate (every non-stdin reader is read; os.Stdin tracks stdinIsTerminal)\nplus a call-site assertion, and the test says plainly that this is weaker than\na behavioural one rather than implying otherwise.\n\nTHE SYMBOL TOTAL WAS A PARTIAL SUM.\n\nsemanticIndexKindInventory summed c over the rows returned by \\`... GROUP BY\nkind ORDER BY c DESC LIMIT 6\\`, so with more than six distinct kinds the total\nunder-reported. That note exists to give an agent an accurate picture after an\nempty result, and a too-low total risks the same false root cause the note was\nwritten to prevent -- which is the mistake that prompted writing it.\n\nThe total is now its own count(*), and the distinct-kind count its own query,\nso a truncated list says \\\"(6 of 9 kinds)\\\" instead of presenting six of nine\nas the whole set. Six or fewer kinds reads exactly as before, pinned by a test\nso the fix cannot pass by inflating every count.\n\nFour guards verified by weakening; summing the displayed rows again turns two\nred at once.\" 2>&1 | tail -2\ngit push -q origin HEAD:fix/agent-guide-directive-and-discovery 2>&1|tail -1\necho \"pushed: $(git rev-parse --short HEAD)\"","description":"Commit the two new 331 fixes","timeout":3000000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2223,"cache_read_input_tokens":378743,"output_tokens":1085,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2223,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1085,"cache_read_input_tokens":378743,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2223,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2223},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01BY8wUrDSxuX8rXYKG8RSWS":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide\ngofmt -l internal/ | head -2\ngo test ./internal/cli/ ./internal/agentsetup/ -count=1 -timeout 2400s > ~/.local/state/entire-distill/pr331e.log 2>&1; echo \"suites exit=$?\"\ngrep -E \"^--- FAIL: \" ~/.local/state/entire-distill/pr331e.log | head -4\ngit add -A\ngit commit -q -m \"fix: do not read stdin on a terminal, and count every symbol kind\n\nTwo more findings from the agent review. Both correct, both mine.\n\nREADING STDIN HUNG WHEN RUN BY HAND.\n\nhookFileFromStdin does io.ReadAll, which on a real TTY waits for EOF. So\n\\`hook pre-edit\\` with no --file hung indefinitely where it previously failed\nfast with \\\"--file is required\\\" -- my fix traded a clear error for a hang. The\ntests missed it because they supply a strings.Reader, which EOFs at once.\n\nThe read is now gated on hookStdinWouldBlock, which is true only when the\nreader IS the process's stdin and that stdin is a character device. The check\nis on the READER, not just the process: a harness always redirects stdin and is\nread, a test with its own reader is read regardless of what the runner did with\nos.Stdin, and only a person at a terminal gets the error.\n\nTHE HANG ITSELF IS NOT REPRODUCIBLE IN-PROCESS -- it needs a real character\ndevice on stdin, which \\`go test\\` does not provide. So the guards are the\npredicate (every non-stdin reader is read; os.Stdin tracks stdinIsTerminal)\nplus a call-site assertion, and the test says plainly that this is weaker than\na behavioural one rather than implying otherwise.\n\nTHE SYMBOL TOTAL WAS A PARTIAL SUM.\n\nsemanticIndexKindInventory summed c over the rows returned by \\`... GROUP BY\nkind ORDER BY c DESC LIMIT 6\\`, so with more than six distinct kinds the total\nunder-reported. That note exists to give an agent an accurate picture after an\nempty result, and a too-low total risks the same false root cause the note was\nwritten to prevent -- which is the mistake that prompted writing it.\n\nThe total is now its own count(*), and the distinct-kind count its own query,\nso a truncated list says \\\"(6 of 9 kinds)\\\" instead of presenting six of nine\nas the whole set. Six or fewer kinds reads exactly as before, pinned by a test\nso the fix cannot pass by inflating every count.\n\nFour guards verified by weakening; summing the displayed rows again turns two\nred at once.\" 2>&1 | tail -2\ngit push -q origin HEAD:fix/agent-guide-directive-and-discovery 2>&1|tail -1\necho \"pushed: $(git rev-parse --short HEAD)\"","description":"Commit the two new 331 fixes","timeout":3000000}},"serverClassifierRequest":"da3a16fb-eee0-4da6-8a04-5dd4d77d2584","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cfge3Fr7SeVWvfD6HxTRk","type":"assistant","uuid":"72339c77-e30e-4cf0-83d9-28a2f18f3a0c","timestamp":"2026-10-04T05:24:31.813Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
