{"parentUuid":"736baa2a-570f-4250-8b3a-63619b3095d3","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfgeTRYgc48L4dHBR3wzh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This is the same finding I already refuted, re-raised with a new id against the new code version. Let me dismiss it with the same evidence and flag the repeat:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":491,"cache_read_input_tokens":385044,"output_tokens":1318,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":180},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":491,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1318,"cache_read_input_tokens":385044,"cache_creation_input_tokens":491,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":491},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"33dbfbdd-9944-4d1c-8d9d-d7694f3ba594","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfgeTQdcRMuxsY2tLMWn5","type":"assistant","uuid":"a8e8f360-61bd-436b-a113-d0002892faa4","timestamp":"2026-10-04T05:29:51.732Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"a8e8f360-61bd-436b-a113-d0002892faa4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfgeTRYgc48L4dHBR3wzh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JPnq8XaCb97YW9fN7d94UE","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv\nEB=/Users/suhaan/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp/entire-main\n$EB trail finding dismiss 226 01M42NWVTQM277EP4Z8MEQS0C3 --repo gh/entireio/entire-brain -m \"REFUTED — and this is a RE-RAISE of 01M42GGG7H7XPXESYBDDTJ5WS5, dismissed earlier on this trail with the same evidence. Recording that explicitly, because a refuted finding returning under a new id against a new code version is how a loop manufactures work.\n\nThe claimed invariant does not exist in this codebase. I grepped for a validating check and found none; the claim is asserted, not sourced.\n\nThe behaviour is already deliberate, tested and documented. TestConflictingRetirementStaysRetiredWithoutASuccessor (facts_import_test.go:793) asserts exactly this state and FAILS if Status comes back as anything other than superseded. Its comment explains why: both halves are true — the source DID retire the memory, and which memory replaced it cannot be determined.\n\nThe prescribed repair is the harmful one. memoriesToFacts marks these superseded because \\\"importing it as active would resurrect something its owner retired\\\" (facts_import.go:463). An ambiguous successor is not evidence that the retirement did not happen, so setting Status = factStatusActive would discard what IS known because what is not known is contested. That is a data-losing change dressed as a consistency fix.\n\nConsumers handle an empty successor correctly: brain_brief_compact.go:246 omits it via compactV1String, and facts_sync_cmd.go:384,387,409 match on equality, so they simply match no proposal — right when no successor is known.\n\nThe contrast with facts_write_cmd.go:186, which does move Status and SupersededBy together, is real but not applicable: there a human has explicitly re-asserted the fact, a deliberate revival. A foreign export naming two different successors is not.\n\nThe ambiguity is disclosed rather than hidden: the report carries \\\"supersession target disagrees between duplicates (N fact(s) are named with more than one replacement and are left with no successor)\\\".\n\nIf the invariant is genuinely wanted, it needs to be introduced deliberately — a validator, a decision about what to do with a retirement whose successor is unknowable, and an answer for the imported case that is not resurrection. That is a design change, not a line edit at 604.\" 2>&1 | tail -1\necho \"=== final counts ===\"\nfor t in 226 238 247; do\n  printf \"trail %s: \" \"$t\"\n  $EB trail finding list \"$t\" --repo gh/entireio/entire-brain --freshness any --status open --json 2>/dev/null \\\n  | sed '/^Using context/d' | python3 -c 'import json,sys;c=json.load(sys.stdin).get(\"counts\",{});print(\"open=%s\" % c.get(\"Open\"))'\ndone","description":"Dismiss the re-raised finding and recount","timeout":1800000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":491,"cache_read_input_tokens":385044,"output_tokens":1318,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":180},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":491,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1318,"cache_read_input_tokens":385044,"cache_creation_input_tokens":491,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":491},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01JPnq8XaCb97YW9fN7d94UE":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv\nEB=/Users/suhaa