{"parentUuid":"eb9d0b8a-4554-42b1-99dd-30d34f896511","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"e7885167-dc2d-44de-bb8f-d1c797ad583a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019za26w4mzTgV93nTamm4wc","type":"tool_result","content":"########## TRAIL 241 ##########\n\n--- 01M3WJ9080G1DJPWYFQD4WXM7P  sev=medium  None:56\nThe `outer` path is interpolated directly into a suggested shell command without quoting. If the repository path contains spaces, shell metacharacters, or is otherwise adversarial, copying and executing the suggested command could fail or have unintended behavior. Consider using shell-quoted format: `entire brain init-agents --repo %q` or wrapping in quotes in the suggestion.\n\n########## TRAIL 242 ##########\n\n--- 01M3ZZ7G70PG8FVFJ8RSAPXAWK  sev=medium  None:450\nThis wrapper discards `regressionScanCaps` via `_`, which drops the \"history scan stopped early\" signal for every caller except `runRegressionDetect` (which was updated to call `detectRegressionAnomaliesCapped` directly). `runBrainReview` (`brain review`) and `scanWorkspaceRepoRegressions`/`runWorkspaceRegressionsManifest`/`runWorkspaceReviewManifest` (workspace regressions/review) still call this uncapped wrapper, so `reviewSummary`/`workspaceReviewSummary`/the workspace \"No suspected regressions\" headline can still print an unqualified clean-bill-of-health sentence (and `reviewReport.Checked=true`) over a raw-history scan that hit the file/signal cap and never finished — exactly the bug class this change set is meant to eliminate, just not propagated to these call sites.\n\n--- 01M3ZQDWHAVYPX6YT5F8ZE0C3M  sev=low  None:191\nInconsistent rune vs byte counting for ellipsis length. The function counts runes for the input but uses `len(statusCauseEllipsis)` (byte count) to reserve space. This works for ASCII `\"...\"` but would break if the ellipsis is changed to a multi-byte Unicode character like `\"…\"`. Use `len([]rune(statusCauseEllipsis))` or `utf8.RuneCountInString(statusCauseEllipsis)` for consistency.\n\n--- 01M3ZQDWGVP5VYJTG47HPNA1MP  sev=medium  None:2632\nWindows absolute paths won't be relativized to match brainignore patterns. After `filepath.ToSlash`, Windows paths like `C:/repo/secret/file.go` don't start with `/`, so the check at line 2632 returns them unchanged. These absolute paths then fail to match repo-relative patterns like `secret/`. Fix by checking `filepath.IsAbs(token)` instead, or explicitly handle `looksLikeWindowsDrivePath(token)`.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"8f1bcdd5-90c6-44e9-90c9-b9ee6ab413ce","timestamp":"2026-10-04T05:31:19.822Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"########## TRAIL 241 ##########\n\n--- 01M3WJ9080G1DJPWYFQD4WXM7P  sev=medium  None:56\nThe `outer` path is interpolated directly into a suggested shell command without quoting. If the repository path contains spaces, shell metacharacters, or is otherwise adversarial, copying and executing the suggested command could fail or have unintended behavior. Consider using shell-quoted format: `entire brain init-agents --repo %q` or wrapping in quotes in the suggestion.\n\n########## TRAIL 242 ##########\n\n--- 01M3ZZ7G70PG8FVFJ8RSAPXAWK  sev=medium  None:450\nThis wrapper discards `regressionScanCaps` via `_`, which drops the \"history scan stopped early\" signal for every caller except `runRegressionDetect` (which was updated to call `detectRegressionAnomaliesCapped` directly). `runBrainReview` (`brain review`) and `scanWorkspaceRepoRegressions`/`runWorkspaceRegressionsManifest`/`runWorkspaceReviewManifest` (workspace regressions/review) still call this uncapped wrapper, so `reviewSummary`/`workspaceReviewSummary`/the workspace \"No suspected regressions\" headline can still print an unqualified clean-bill-of-health sentence (and `reviewReport.Checked=true`) over a raw-history scan that hit the file/signal cap and never finished — exactly the bug class this change set is meant to eliminate, just not propagated to these call sites.\n\n--- 01M3ZQDWHAVYPX6YT5F8ZE0C3M  sev=low  None:191\nInconsistent rune vs byte counting for ellipsis length. The function counts runes for the input but uses `len(statusCauseEllipsis)` (byte count) to reserve space. This works for ASCII `\"...\"` but would break if the ellipsis is changed to a multi-byte Unicode character like `\"…\"`. Use `len([]rune(statusCauseEllipsis))` or `utf8.RuneCountInString(statusCauseEllipsis)` for consistency.\n\n--- 01M3ZQDWGVP5VYJTG47HPNA1MP  sev=medium  None:2632\nWindows absolute paths won't be relativized to match brainignore patterns. After `filepath.ToSlash`, Windows paths like `C:/repo/secret/file.go` don't start with `/`, so the check at line 2632 returns them unchanged. These absolute paths then fail to match repo-relative patterns like `secret/`. Fix by checking `filepath.IsAbs(token)` instead, or explicitly handle `looksLikeWindowsDrivePath(token)`.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"f07dee4c-704d-4bf9-b4aa-150f2a638c3b","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","root":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":1,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":242},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-graph","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/entiredb","visibility":"private"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/cli","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"eb9d0b8a-455