{"parentUuid":"1902c619-1538-4d9c-a33e-862705eb99ea","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfgfBs7yyRYBnTs7myZTL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WDAuDqAif9USdisbJGxzKt","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp/pr321\ngofmt -l internal/ | head -2\ngo test ./internal/cli/ -count=1 -timeout 2400s > ~/.local/state/entire-distill/pr321.log 2>&1; echo \"321 suite exit=$?\"\ngrep -E \"^--- FAIL: \" ~/.local/state/entire-distill/pr321.log | head -3\ngit add -A\ngit commit -q -m \"fix(init-agents): shell-quote the path in the suggested remedy\n\nThe nested-repo warning interpolated the outer path into a copy-pasteable\ncommand unquoted. A path with a space -- ordinary on macOS -- made the remedy\nsilently do the wrong thing when copied.\n\nThe review suggested %q. That is better than nothing and not sufficient: Go's\n%q produces a Go literal, so \\$ and a backtick survive into what a shell reads\nas a double-quoted string and EXPAND there. Single quotes suppress all of it,\nwith '\\\\'' carrying an embedded single quote through, and this package already\nhad shellQuotedRepoDir doing exactly that -- so the fix is to use it rather\nthan invent a second convention.\n\nIts own trigger set was too narrow, though: space, tab and quotes only, so a\npath holding \\$, a backtick, ;, |, & or a glob passed through bare. Widened,\nwhich cannot break an existing caller because a single-quoted token is valid\nwherever a bare one was. Quoting more than strictly necessary is free; quoting\nless is the bug.\n\nOnly the path in the COMMAND is quoted. The two in the surrounding prose are\nleft alone, because they are prose.\n\nGuards verified by weakening: unquoting the call site turns the end-to-end\ntest red, narrowing the character set turns the table red. The end-to-end test\nneeded fixing first -- its initial version passed --repo, which is precisely\nthe flag that suppresses this warning, so it skipped itself and reported\nsuccess. It now fails loudly if the warning does not fire.\" 2>&1 | tail -2\ngit push -q origin HEAD:fix/setup-traps 2>&1|tail -1\necho \"pushed 321: $(git rev-parse --short HEAD)\"","description":"Commit the 321 quoting fix","timeout":3000000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1081,"cache_read_input_tokens":439896,"output_tokens":865,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1081,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":865,"cache_read_input_tokens":439896,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1081,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1081},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01WDAuDqAif9USdisbJGxzKt":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp/pr321\ngofmt -l internal/ | head -2\ngo test ./internal/cli/ -count=1 -timeout 2400s > ~/.local/state/entire-distill/pr321.log 2>&1; echo \"321 suite exit=$?\"\ngrep -E \"^--- FAIL: \" ~/.local/state/entire-distill/pr321.log | head -3\ngit add -A\ngit commit -q -m \"fix(init-agents): shell-quote the path in the suggested remedy\n\nThe nested-repo warning interpolated the outer path into a copy-pasteable\ncommand unquoted. A path with a space -- ordinary on macOS -- made the remedy\nsilently do the wrong thing when copied.\n\nThe review suggested %q. That is better than nothing and not sufficient: Go's\n%q produces a Go literal, so \\$ and a backtick survive into what a shell reads\nas a double-quoted string and EXPAND there. Single quotes suppress all of it,\nwith '\\\\'' carrying an embedded single quote through, and this package already\nhad shellQuotedRepoDir doing exactly that -- so the fix is to use it rather\nthan invent a second convention.\n\nIts own trigger set was too narrow, though: space, tab and quotes only, so a\npath holding \\$, a backtick, ;, |, & or a glob passed through bare. Widened,\nwhich cannot break an existing caller because a single-quoted token is valid\nwherever a bare one was. Quoting more than strictly necessary is free; quoting\nless is the bug.\n\nOnly the path in the COMMAND is quoted. The two in the surrounding prose are\nleft alone, because they are prose.\n\nGuards verified by weakening: unquoting the call site turns the end-to-end\ntest red, narrowing the character set turns the table red. The end-to-end test\nneeded fixing first -- its initial version passed --repo, which is precisely\nthe flag that suppresses this warning, so it skipped itself and reported\nsuccess. It now fails loudly if the warning does not fire.\" 2>&1 | tail -2\ngit push -q origin HEAD:fix/setup-traps 2>&1|tail -1\necho \"pushed 321: $(git rev-parse --short HEAD)\"","description":"Commit the 321 quoting fix","timeout":3000000}},"serverClassifierRequest":"1715d8bb-9aba-4e44-93f2-fdc926770c63","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfgfBqC9T3WwoxZcQsvvE","type":"assistant","uuid":"3fe6a291-a557-46cd-8425-4bb211af43e5","timestamp":"2026-10-04T05:39:32.961Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
