{"parentUuid":"34b8685f-6087-4aff-815d-43333e3ef1dc","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14505382 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"99ccfb88-f9e9-48d3-bb28-402c5b80723e","timestamp":"2026-10-04T05:48:25.025Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14505382 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"99ccfb88-f9e9-48d3-bb28-402c5b80723e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cfgfsw5UqQqwMZxQay6gz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UrCGPHUwZ6m3q4kUhFgzHd","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide\ngit add -A\ngit commit -q -m \"fix: propagate the history-scan cap, and three smaller correctness fixes\n\nFindings from the agent review of the #329/#330 stack. They are fixed at the\nSTACK TIP rather than on each branch: #331 contains #329 and #330, the three\nmerge in order, and rebasing a stack to place each fix on its own branch is\nchurn with a real chance of breaking the order. Noted so the dispositions are\nhonest about where the code lives.\n\nTHE HISTORY-SCAN CAP WAS DISCARDED BY EVERY CALLER BUT ONE.\n\ndetectRegressionAnomalies wrapped the capped detector and threw away\nregressionScanCaps. runRegressionDetect had been converted to call the capped\nform directly; `brain review` and the workspace regressions/review surfaces had\nnot. So they could print an unqualified clean bill of health over a raw-history\nscan that hit a file or signal cap and never finished -- the exact bug class the\ncaps were added to eliminate, just not propagated.\n\nregressionNoAnomaliesLine had been saying this correctly all along. reviewSummary\nand workspaceReviewSummary could not, because they never received the flag. Both\nnow take it and report PARTIAL; the workspace per-repo results carry\nhistory_truncated in JSON so a machine reader need not parse prose, which is\nwhat those structs' own comments ask for; and the multi-repo headline qualifies\nitself the same way it already qualifies coverage.\n\nThe uncapped wrapper is DELETED. With both production callers converted it had\nnone left, and leaving it in place is an invitation to discard the caps again.\nIts 25 test callers now call the capped form and discard the flag explicitly,\nwhich is fine -- a test does not print a clean bill of health.\n\nONE OPEN HANDLE FOR THE INDEX CONTENTS AND ITS MTIME.\n\nrunGitWithScratchIndex read the index with os.ReadFile and then stat-ed the\npath, so a concurrent git could replace it between the two and the copy would\ncarry one version's bytes with another version's mtime -- exactly the pairing\nthe racily-clean logic depends on. git writes the index by rename, so an open\nfile description keeps its inode: both now come from one handle and are\nguaranteed to describe the same version.\n\nThe snapshot can still be stale relative to a later write. That is inherent to\nreading without the lock, which is this function's whole purpose, and is not\nwhat was fixed.\n\nTWO SMALLER ONES.\n\ntruncateStatusCause measured its input in runes and the ellipsis reserve in\nBYTES -- the same confusion the function exists to fix, on the other operand,\none const edit from mattering. Now rune-counted.\n\nThe union-find path compression recursed once per link, bounding chain depth by\nthe stack. Now iterative, verified to resolve a 50,000-deep chain to the same\nroot from every node on it.\n\nAll verified by weakening. The caps fix also carries a structural guard that\nthe uncapped wrapper does not come back.\" 2>&1 | tail -2\ngit push -q origin HEAD:fix/agent-guide-directive-and-discovery 2>&1|tail -1\necho \"pushed stack tip: $(git rev-parse --short HEAD)\"","description":"Commit the stack-tip fixes","timeout":1800000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":596,"cache_read_input_tokens":441947,"output_tokens":1196,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":596,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1196,"cache_read_input_tokens":441947,"cache_creation_input_tokens":596,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":596},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01UrCGPHUwZ6m3q4kUhFgzHd":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide\ngit add -A\ngit commit -q -m \"fix: propagate the history-scan cap, and three smaller correctness fixes\n\nFindings from the agent review of the #329/#330 stack. They are fixed at the\nSTACK TIP rather than on each branch: #331 contains #329 and #330, the three\nmerge in order, and rebasing a stack to place each fix on its own branch is\nchurn with a real chance of breaking the order. Noted so the dispositions are\nhonest about where the code lives.\n\nTHE HISTORY-SCAN CAP WAS DISCARDED BY EVERY CALLER BUT ONE.\n\ndetectRegressionAnomalies wrapped the capped detector and threw away\nregressionScanCaps. runRegressionDetect had been converted to call the capped\nform directly; `brain review` and the workspace regressions/review surfaces had\nnot. So they could print an unqualified clean bill of health over a raw-history\nscan that hit a file or signal cap and never finished -- the exact bug class the\ncaps were added to eliminate, just not propagated.\n\nregressionNoAnomaliesLine had been saying this correctly all along. reviewSummary\nand workspaceReviewSummary could not, because they never received the flag. Both\nnow take it and report PARTIAL; the workspace per-repo results carry\nhistory_truncated in JSON so a machine reader need not parse prose, which is\nwhat those structs' own comments ask for; and the multi-repo headline qualifies\nitself the same way it already qualifies coverage.\n\nThe uncapped wrapper is DELETED. With both production callers converted it had\nnone left, and leaving it in place is an invitation to discard the caps again.\nIts 25 test callers now call the capped form and discard the flag explicitly,\nwhich is fine -- a test does not print a clean bill of health.\n\nONE OPEN HANDLE FOR THE INDEX CONTENTS AND ITS MTIME.\n\nrunGitWithScratchIndex read the index with os.ReadFile and then stat-ed the\npath, so a concurrent git could replace it between the two and the copy would\ncarry one version's bytes with another version's mtime -- exactly the pairing\nthe racily-clean logic depends on. git writes the index by rename, so an open\nfile description keeps its inode: both now come from one handle and are\nguaranteed to describe the same version.\n\nThe snapshot can still be stale relative to a later write. That is inherent to\nreading without the lock, which is this function's whole purpose, and is not\nwhat was fixed.\n\nTWO SMALLER ONES.\n\ntruncateStatusCause measured its input in runes and the ellipsis reserve in\nBYTES -- the same confusion the function exists to fix, on the other operand,\none const edit from mattering. Now rune-counted.\n\nThe union-find path compression recursed once per link, bounding chain depth by\nthe stack. Now iterative, verified to resolve a 50,000-deep chain to the same\nroot from every node on it.\n\nAll verified by weakening. The caps fix also carries a structural guard that\nthe uncapped wrapper does not come back.\" 2>&1 | tail -2\ngit push -q origin HEAD:fix/agent-guide-directive-and-discovery 2>&1|tail -1\necho \"pushed stack tip: $(git rev-parse --short HEAD)\"","description":"Commit the stack-tip fixes","timeout":1800000}},"serverClassifierRequest":"7a18441a-d21d-4724-a499-2a1f3d29a6ac","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfgfstooFLwGBucv2NPU2","type":"assistant","uuid":"e0f8cda8-5176-443b-80f3-21ed008b86fa","timestamp":"2026-10-04T05:48:41.918Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c