{"parentUuid":"77a518ca-6f22-4663-9463-e5cfcdee0fff","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cfgfx5b4XkrRHvDNcgHwS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011RZdh68SawrTpiJLBsY8vG","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv\nEB=/Users/suhaan/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp/entire-main\nR=\"gh/entireio/entire-brain\"\n\n$EB trail finding resolve 241 01M3WJ9080G1DJPWYFQD4WXM7P --repo $R -m \"FIXED in fec9dc1a — correct. The nested-repo warning interpolated the outer path into a copy-pasteable command unquoted, so a path with a space (ordinary on macOS) made the remedy silently do the wrong thing.\n\nThe %q suggestion was not taken, for a reason worth recording: Go's %q produces a Go literal, so a dollar sign or a backtick survives into what a shell reads as a double-quoted string and EXPANDS there. Single quotes suppress all of it, and this package already had shellQuotedRepoDir (semantic_repokey.go:190) doing exactly that with the correct embedded-quote escape — so the fix uses it rather than introducing a second convention.\n\nIts own trigger set was too narrow to be relied on here: space, tab and quotes only, so a path holding a dollar sign, backtick, semicolon, pipe, ampersand or a glob passed through bare. Widened. That cannot break an existing caller, because a single-quoted token is valid wherever a bare one was — quoting more than necessary is free, quoting less is the bug.\n\nOnly the path in the COMMAND is quoted; the two in the surrounding prose are left alone, because they are prose.\n\nGuards: a table over space, dollar, backtick, semicolon, embedded single quote and glob, plus an end-to-end test driving init-agents in a nested repo under a path with a space. Unquoting the call site turns the end-to-end red; narrowing the character set turns the table red.\n\nThe end-to-end test needed fixing first: its initial version passed --repo, which is precisely the flag that suppresses this warning, so it skipped itself and reported success. It now fails loudly if the warning does not fire.\" 2>&1 | tail -1\n\n$EB trail finding resolve 242 01M3ZQDWGVP5VYJTG47HPNA1MP --repo $R -m \"STALE — already fixed on this branch's own head.\n\nCommit 3cd705d2 (\\\"fix(brainignore): match absolute paths on Windows, not just Unix\\\") IS the head of fix/retrieval-output-correctness, and it replaced the Unix-only prefix test the finding describes. Verified in the current source rather than inferred from the commit title: semantic.go:2633 now calls absolutePathToken(token), and absolutePathToken (semantic.go:2657) accepts a drive-letter path — a letter, a colon, then a slash — as well as a leading slash. A UNC path is handled by the leading-slash branch.\n\nSo \\\"the check at line 2632 returns them unchanged [because they do not start with /]\\\" is no longer what the code does. Resolving as superseded rather than dismissing, since the underlying defect was real and is simply already closed.\n\nThe companion change cutPathPrefix (semantic.go:2672) folds case on Windows and macOS, so C:/Repo/secret/x.go still matches a root recorded as C:/repo.\" 2>&1 | tail -1","description":"Resolve the quoting and stale Windows findings","timeout":1800000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":610,"cache_read_input_tokens":446349,"output_tokens":1203,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":610,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1203,"cache_read_input_tokens":446349,"cache_creation_input_tokens":610,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":610},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":nu