resolve 242 01M3ZQDWGVP5VYJTG47HPNA1MP --repo $R -m \"STALE — already fixed on this branch's own head.\n\nCommit 3cd705d2 (\\\"fix(brainignore): match absolute paths on Windows, not just Unix\\\") IS the head of fix/retrieval-output-correctness, and it replaced the Unix-only prefix test the finding describes. Verified in the current source rather than inferred from the commit title: semantic.go:2633 now calls absolutePathToken(token), and absolutePathToken (semantic.go:2657) accepts a drive-letter path — a letter, a colon, then a slash — as well as a leading slash. A UNC path is handled by the leading-slash branch.\n\nSo \\\"the check at line 2632 returns them unchanged [because they do not start with /]\\\" is no longer what the code does. Resolving as superseded rather than dismissing, since the underlying defect was real and is simply already closed.\n\nThe companion change cutPathPrefix (semantic.go:2672) folds case on Windows and macOS, so C:/Repo/secret/x.go still matches a root recorded as C:/repo.\" 2>&1 | tail -1","description":"Resolve the quoting and stale Windows findings","timeout":1800000}},"serverClassifierRequest":"77e99179-93b6-4f9f-9fc7-cdce3beb35dd","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cfgfx4pvX37jTFJFKyxVB","type":"assistant","uuid":"6874b943-a36b-4273-a983-8a83fadff306","timestamp":"2026-10-04T05:49:39.191Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
