{"parentUuid":"2e017f13-468c-469a-b414-ff17dad08c57","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cfgg7cNyMuN491uJCwPSN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01ATYxDtnBy3xuLVSkLWfM3m","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv\nEB=/Users/suhaan/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp/entire-main\nfor t in 241 247; do\n  printf \"\\n=== trail %s ===\\n\" \"$t\"\n  $EB trail finding list \"$t\" --repo gh/entireio/entire-brain --freshness any --status open --json 2>/dev/null \\\n  | sed '/^Using context/d' | python3 -c '\nimport json,sys\nfor f in json.load(sys.stdin).get(\"findings\",[]):\n    print(f[\"id\"], \"sev=\"+str(f.get(\"severity\")))\n    print((f.get(\"body\") or \"\").strip()[:800])\n'\ndone","description":"Read the two newly-appeared findings","timeout":1800000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":671,"cache_read_input_tokens":456143,"output_tokens":333,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":671,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":333,"cache_read_input_tokens":456143,"cache_creation_input_tokens":671,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":671},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01ATYxDtnBy3xuLVSkLWfM3m":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv\nEB=/Users/suhaan/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp/entire-main\nfor t in 241 247; do\n  printf \"\\n=== trail %s ===\\n\" \"$t\"\n  $EB trail finding list \"$t\" --repo gh/entireio/entire-brain --freshness any --status open --json 2>/dev/null \\\n  | sed '/^Using context/d' | python3 -c '\nimport json,sys\nfor f in json.load(sys.stdin).get(\"findings\",[]):\n    print(f[\"id\"], \"sev=\"+str(f.get(\"severity\")))\n    print((f.get(\"body\") or \"\").strip()[:800])\n'\ndone","description":"Read the two newly-appeared findings","timeout":1800000}},"serverClassifierRequest":"1905dc3b-1845-4443-8fd8-80d8ac813f86","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cfgg7a8XxcCQ8zpFu8EdJ","type":"assistant","uuid":"4713c835-1913-48f9-8efe-1fa99fe66d3d","timestamp":"2026-10-04T05:51:35.328Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"4713c835-1913-48f9-8efe-1fa99fe66d3d","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"e7885167-dc2d-44de-bb8f-d1c797ad583a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ATYxDtnBy3xuLVSkLWfM3m","type":"tool_result","content":"=== trail 241 ===\n01M42Q6F3962QMXJHDZPP60S90 sev=medium\nThe nested-repo guard only exempts explicit roots supplied via `--repo` or a positional arg, but `agentsetup.Context` also accepts an explicit root from `opts.Env.RepoRoot` (`ENTIRE_REPO_ROOT`), which is the normal path when this binary is dispatched by a parent Entire CLI (see `EntireEnv`'s doc comment). In that case `root` is never checked for a `.git` of its own, yet `OuterRepo` is still invoked and, if any ancestor happens to contain `.git` (e.g. a monorepo or a dotfiles-tracked home directory), prints \"%s is a git repository inside %s\" even though `root` itself may not be a repository at all — a misleading warning on every host-dispatched run in that layout, suggesting a remedy (`--repo <outer>`) that doesn't address anything. Consider also exempting `opts.Env.RepoRoot != \"\"` (or veri\n\n=== trail 247 ===\n01M42PBSX02H6DQBZ47D4SEKC4 sev=medium\n`pre, _ := hooks[\"PreToolUse\"].([]any)` silently discards the existing value and defaults `pre` to `nil` when `PreToolUse` exists but isn't a JSON array (e.g. an object or string from a hand-edited or legacy `settings.json`). The function's own doc comment promises \"any shape it does not recognise is left strictly alone and reported, rather than overwritten\" (mirrored by `claudeHooksSection`'s explicit type check on `hooks`), but `PreToolUse` itself gets no such check: the subsequent `hooks[\"PreToolUse\"] = append(pre, ...)` then replaces the unrecognised value with a brand-new one-element array, silently destroying the user's original `PreToolUse` configuration instead of refusing like the `hooks`-not-an-object case does.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"bdacc2bc-66f1-495d-b431-338fe19bcdd6","timestamp":"2026-10-04T05:51:38.124Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"=== trail 241 ===\n01M42Q6F3962QMXJHDZPP60S90 sev=medium\nThe nested-repo guard only exempts explicit roots supplied via `--repo` or a positional arg, but `agentsetup.Context` also accepts an explicit root from `opts.Env.RepoRoot` (`ENTIRE_REPO_ROOT`), which is the normal path when this binary is dispatched by a parent Entire CLI (see `EntireEnv`'s doc comment). In that case `root` is never checked for a `.git` of its own, yet `OuterRepo` is still invoked and, if any ancestor happens to contain `.git` (e.g. a monorepo or a dotfiles-tracked home directory), prints \"%s is a git repository inside %s\" even though `root` itself may not be a repository at all — a misleading warning on every host-dispatched run in that layout, suggesting a remedy (`--repo <outer>`) that doesn't address anything. Consider also exempting `opts.Env.RepoRoot != \"\"` (or veri\n\n=== trail 247 ===\n01M42PBSX02H6DQBZ47D4SEKC4 sev=medium\n`pre, _ := hooks[\"PreToolUse\"].([]any)` silently discards the existing value and defaults `pre` to `nil` when `PreToolUse` exists but isn't a JSON array (e.g. an object or string from a hand-edited or legacy `settings.json`). The function's own doc comment promises \"any shape it does not recognise is left strictly alone and reported, rather than overwritten\" (mirrored by `claudeHooksSection`'s explicit type check on `hooks`), but `PreToolUse` itself gets no such check: the subsequent `hooks[\"PreToolUse\"] = append(pre, ...)` then replaces the unrecognised value with a brand-new one-element array, silently destroying the user's original `PreToolUse` configuration instead of refusing like the `hooks`-not-an-object case does.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"1905dc3b-1845-4443-8fd8-80d8ac813f86","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","root":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean