{"parentUuid":"088a1787-8b31-4f96-91b9-ebe293c9e9ae","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfggE34hCfouBPzeD3jTU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DX9Ly8ypFQhWaw8r7iCRo2","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp/pr321\ncat >> internal/agentsetup/nested_test.go <<'EOF'\n\n// OuterRepo walks UP for an ancestor .git and never checked the starting\n// point, so a plain directory inside a repository came back with that ancestor\n// and the caller announced \"<root> is a git repository inside <outer>\" about a\n// path that is not a repository at all -- suggesting a remedy that addresses\n// nothing.\n//\n// This fires on an ordinary layout, not a contrived one: a monorepo\n// subdirectory, or anything under a dotfiles-tracked home directory.\nfunc TestOuterRepoRequiresAnInnerRepository(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\touter := t.TempDir()\n\tif err := os.MkdirAll(filepath.Join(outer, \".git\"), 0o755); err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n\t}\n\n\t// A PLAIN directory inside the repo: there is no nesting to report.\n\tplain := filepath.Join(outer, \"packages\", \"web\")\n\tif err := os.MkdirAll(plain, 0o755); err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n\t}\n\tif got := OuterRepo(plain); got != \"\" {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"a plain subdirectory is not a nested repository, but OuterRepo returned %q\", got)\n\t}\n\n\t// A real nested clone still reports, or the fix would disable the feature.\n\tinner := filepath.Join(outer, \"entire-brain\")\n\tif err := os.MkdirAll(filepath.Join(inner, \".git\"), 0o755); err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n\t}\n\tif got := OuterRepo(inner); got != outer {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"a genuine nested clone must still be reported: got %q, want %q\", got, outer)\n\t}\n\n\t// A .git FILE is how a worktree marks its root, so it counts too.\n\twt := filepath.Join(outer, \"wt\")\n\tif err := os.MkdirAll(wt, 0o755); err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n\t}\n\tif err := os.WriteFile(filepath.Join(wt, \".git\"), []byte(\"gitdir: /elsewhere\\n\"), 0o644); err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n\t}\n\tif got := OuterRepo(wt); got != outer {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"a worktree root carries .git as a FILE and must still be reported: got %q\", got)\n\t}\n\n\t// And a repository with no outer repository reports nothing.\n\tlone := t.TempDir()\n\tif err := os.MkdirAll(filepath.Join(lone, \".git\"), 0o755); err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n\t}\n\tif got := OuterRepo(lone); got != \"\" {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"a top-level repository has no outer repository, got %q\", got)\n\t}\n}\nEOF\ngofmt -w internal/agentsetup/nested_test.go 2>/dev/null || { python3 -c \"\nimport os\np='internal/agentsetup/nested_test.go'\nif not os.path.exists(p) or 'package ' not in open(p).read()[:200]:\n    s=open(p).read(); open(p,'w').write('package agentsetup\\n\\nimport (\\n\\t\\\"os\\\"\\n\\t\\\"path/filepath\\\"\\n\\t\\\"testing\\\"\\n)\\n'+s)\n\"; gofmt -w internal/agentsetup/nested_test.go; }\nhead -8 internal/agentsetup/nested_test.go\ngo test ./internal/agentsetup/ -run 'TestOuterRepoRequiresAnInnerRepository' -count=1 -timeout 900s 2>&1|tail -4","description":"Test the inner-repo requirement","timeout":1200000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2073,"cache_read_input_tokens":463242,"output_tokens":1369,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2073,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1369,"cache_read_input_tokens":463242,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2073,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2073},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null