{"parentUuid":"a08594ae-8da1-4f29-8ada-599898d69cdf","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14480206 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"4b0bb326-e32f-4c0d-81d9-686a88e14536","timestamp":"2026-10-04T05:57:48.087Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14480206 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"4b0bb326-e32f-4c0d-81d9-686a88e14536","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfggbTE6RTiwmYm27wacz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HkWFXe7HZuGb4kKzaZXoJD","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp/pr321\ncat > /Users/suhaan/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp/m321.txt <<'MSGEOF'\nfix(init-agents): only warn about nesting when there is an inner repository\n\nOuterRepo walks UP looking for an ancestor .git and never checked its starting\npoint. So a plain directory inside a repository came back with that ancestor,\nand the caller announced \"<root> is a git repository inside <outer>\" about a\npath that is not a repository at all -- then suggested a remedy addressing\nnothing.\n\nThat is not a contrived layout. A monorepo subdirectory hits it, and so does\nanything under a dotfiles-tracked home directory, which makes it a misleading\nwarning on every run in those trees.\n\nThe review offered two fixes: exempt an explicit ENTIRE_REPO_ROOT, or verify\nthe root. Verifying is the better one and is what this does. Exempting the env\nroot would also suppress the warning in the case where it is TRUE and useful --\na host dispatching into a genuine nested clone -- whereas requiring an inner\nrepository makes the message correct however the root was chosen, which\nsubsumes the env-root complaint without losing a real warning.\n\nThe check lives in OuterRepo rather than at the call site, so the guarantee\nsits with the function that makes the claim: it returns an outer repository\nonly when there is genuinely an inner one. A .git FILE counts, because that is\nhow a worktree marks its root, and Lstat matches how the walk already tests\neach ancestor.\n\nGuard verified by weakening: without the requirement, the plain-subdirectory\ncase returns the ancestor and the test goes red. The test also pins that a\ngenuine nested clone and a worktree root still report, so the fix cannot pass\nby disabling the feature.\nMSGEOF\ngit add -A\ngit commit -q -F /Users/suhaan/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp/m321.txt 2>&1 | tail -2\ngit push -q origin HEAD:fix/setup-traps 2>&1|tail -1\necho \"pushed 321: $(git rev-parse --short HEAD)\"","description":"Commit the nested-warning fix from a file","timeout":1800000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":807,"cache_read_input_tokens":466799,"output_tokens":842,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":807,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":842,"cache_read_input_tokens":466799,"cache_creation_input_tokens":807,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":807},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01HkWFXe7HZuGb4kKzaZXoJD":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp/pr321\ncat > /Users/suhaan/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp/m321.txt <<'MSGEOF'\nfix(init-agents): only warn about nesting when there is an inner repository\n\nOuterRepo walks UP looking for an ancestor .git and never checked its starting\npoint. So a plain directory inside a repository came back with that ancestor,\nand the caller announced \"<root> is a git repository inside <outer>\" about a\npath that is not a repository at all -- then suggested a remedy addressing\nnothing.\n\nThat is not a contrived layout. A monorepo subdirectory hits it, and so does\nanything under a dotfiles-tracked home directory, which makes it a misleading\nwarning on every run in those trees.\n\nThe review offered two fixes: exempt an explicit ENTIRE_REPO_ROOT, or verify\nthe root. Verifying is the better one and is what this does. Exempting the env\nroot would also suppress the warning in the case where it is TRUE and useful --\na host dispatching into a genuine nested clone -- whereas requiring an inner\nrepository makes the message correct however the root was chosen, which\nsubsumes the env-root complaint without losing a real warning.\n\nThe check lives in OuterRepo rather than at the call site, so the guarantee\nsits with the function that makes the claim: it returns an outer repository\nonly when there is genuinely an inner one. A .git FILE counts, because that is\nhow a worktree marks its root, and Lstat matches how the walk already tests\neach ancestor.\n\nGuard verified by weakening: without the requirement, the plain-subdirectory\ncase returns the ancestor and the test goes red. The test also pins that a\ngenuine nested clone and a worktree root still report, so the fix cannot pass\nby disabling the feature.\nMSGEOF\ngit add -A\ngit commit -q -F /Users/suhaan/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp/m321.txt 2>&1 | tail -2\ngit push -q origin HEAD:fix/setup-traps 2>&1|tail -1\necho \"pushed 321: $(git rev-parse --short HEAD)\"","description":"Commit the nested-warning fix from a file","timeout":1800000}},"serverClassifierRequest":"f97baa38-2919-4a29-845d-2d846ae1817b","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfggbQRB29WatgQmoEnYk","type":"assistant","uuid":"1a0683e9-fcd6-4305-b239-f7c3458e3a02","timestamp":"2026-10-04T05:58:01.178Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
