{"parentUuid":"324aa18a-9cf8-422e-851a-99258a48e36c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfggcZRBEkHt4U2VdK4Fw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01M4SiaD1h8N8nYHz7pDRdWz","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide\ngofmt -l internal/ | head -2\ngo test ./internal/agentsetup/ ./internal/cli/ -count=1 -timeout 2400s > ~/.local/state/entire-distill/pr331g.log 2>&1; echo \"331 suites exit=$?\"\ngrep -E \"^--- FAIL: \" ~/.local/state/entire-distill/pr331g.log | head -3\ncat > /Users/suhaan/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp/m331.txt <<'MSGEOF'\nfix(hooks): refuse an unrecognised PreToolUse instead of overwriting it\n\npre, _ := hooks[\"PreToolUse\"].([]any) discarded the assertion's second value,\nso a PreToolUse that existed but was not an array -- an object or a string\nfrom a hand-edited or legacy settings.json -- became nil, and the append then\nwrote a brand-new one-element array over it. The user's configuration was\ndestroyed silently.\n\nMergePreEditHook's own doc comment promises the opposite: any shape it does\nnot recognise is left strictly alone and reported, rather than overwritten.\nclaudeHooksSection already makes exactly this check one level up for \"hooks\".\nSo the promise held for the container and not for the key being modified.\n\nAbsent or null is not an unrecognised shape -- there is nothing to preserve\nand the key is created as before, which the tests pin so the refusal cannot\nblock a fresh install.\n\nGuards: four unrecognised shapes, each asserting the file is BYTE-IDENTICAL\nafterwards rather than merely that an error came back, plus five\nabsent/empty/sibling cases asserting the hook still installs and a neighbouring\nPostToolUse survives.\nMSGEOF\ngit add -A\ngit commit -q -F /Users/suhaan/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp/m331.txt 2>&1 | tail -2\ngit push -q origin HEAD:fix/agent-guide-directive-and-discovery 2>&1|tail -1\necho \"pushed 331: $(git rev