{"parentUuid":"a8badf02-8cf9-4f31-bf54-c0ca40faa8dc","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cfggy65UZoNvritEQreg5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016CShG7P7cqLrBAzN1BExip","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv\nEB=/Users/suhaan/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp/entire-main\n$EB trail finding resolve 247 01M42PBSX02H6DQBZ47D4SEKC4 --repo gh/entireio/entire-brain -m \"FIXED in d36dd869 — correct, and it is an internal contradiction in code I wrote: the function's own doc comment promises the opposite of what it did.\n\nThe discarded second return value defaulted pre to nil whenever PreToolUse was present but not an array, and the append then wrote a brand-new one-element array over it. The user's configuration was destroyed silently. claudeHooksSection already makes exactly this check one level up for the hooks object, so the promise held for the container and not for the key being modified.\n\nNow routed through claudePreToolUseEntries, which refuses any non-array shape with the same message style as the hooks check. Absent or null is deliberately NOT an unrecognised shape: there is nothing to preserve, so the key is created as before.\n\nGuards: four unrecognised shapes (object, string, number, bool), each asserting the file is BYTE-IDENTICAL afterwards rather than merely that an error came back — the point is the data survives, not that a call failed. Plus five absent/empty/sibling cases asserting the hook still installs and a neighbouring PostToolUse survives the merge, so the refusal cannot pass by blocking every fresh install.\" 2>&1 | tail -1\n\n$EB trail finding resolve 241 01M42Q6F3962QMXJHDZPP60S90 --repo gh/entireio/entire-brain -m \"FIXED in 101d2643 — correct on both halves, and it fires on ordinary layouts rather than contrived ones: a monorepo subdirectory, or anything under a dotfiles-tracked home directory.\n\nThe root cause is the one named second: OuterRepo walks UP for an ancestor .git and never checked its starting point, so a plain directory inside a repository came back with that ancestor and the caller announced that the path is a git repository inside another when it is not a repository at all.\n\nOf the two remedies offered, verifying the root is the better one and is what was applied. Exempting an explicit ENTIRE_REPO_ROOT would also suppress the warning where it is TRUE and useful — a host dispatching into a genuine nested clone — whereas requiring an inner repository makes the message correct however the root was chosen, which subsumes the env-root complaint without losing a real warning.\n\nThe check sits in OuterRepo rather than at the call site, so the guarantee lives with the function making the claim. A .git FILE counts, because that is how a worktree marks its root, and Lstat matches how the walk already tests each ancestor.\n\nGuard: without the requirement the plain-subdirectory case returns the ancestor and the test goes red. The same test pins that a genuine nested clone and a worktree root still report, so the fix cannot pass by disabling the feature.\" 2>&1 | tail -1\necho\nprintf \"%-6s %s\\n\" PR OPEN\nfor pair in 306:226 318:238 320:240 321:241 329:242 330:246 331:247; do\n  PR=${pair%%:*}; T=${pair##*:}\n  printf \"#%-5s \" \"$PR\"\n  $EB trail finding list \"$T\" --repo gh/entireio/entire-brain --freshness any --status open --json 2>/dev/null \\\n  | sed '/^Using context/d' | python3 -c 'import json,sys;print(json.load(sys.stdin).get(\"counts\",{}).get(\"Open\"))'\ndone","description":"Resolve the last two and recount all seven","timeout":1800000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1205,"cache_read_input_tokens":468542,"output_tokens":1301,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1205,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1301,"cache_read_input_tokens":468542,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1205,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1205},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_016CShG7P7cqLrBAzN1BExip":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv\nEB=/Users/suhaan/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp/entire-main\n$EB trail finding resolve 247 01M42PBSX02H6DQBZ47D4SEKC4 --repo gh/entireio/entire-brain -m \"FIXED in d36dd869 — correct, and it is an internal contradiction in code I wrote: the function's own doc comment promises the opposite of what it did.\n\nThe discarded second return value defaulted pre to nil whenever PreToolUse was present but not an array, and the append then wrote a brand-new one-element array over it. The user's configuration was destroyed silently. claudeHooksSection already makes exactly this check one level up for the hooks object, so the promise held for the container and not for the key being modified.\n\nNow routed through claudePreToolUseEntries, which refuses any non-array shape with the same message style as the hooks check. Absent or null is deliberately NOT an unrecognised shape: there is nothing to preserve, so the key is created as before.\n\nGuards: four unrecognised shapes (object, string, number, bool), each asserting the file is BYTE-IDENTICAL afterwards rather than merely that an error came back — the point is the data survives, not that a call failed. Plus five absent/empty/sibling cases asserting the hook still installs and a neighbouring PostToolUse survives the merge, so the refusal cannot pass by blocking every fresh install.\" 2>&1 | tail -1\n\n$EB trail finding resolve 241 01M42Q6F3962QMXJHDZPP60S90 --repo gh/entireio/entire-brain -m \"FIXED in 101d2643 — correct on both halves, and it fires on ordinary layouts rather than contrived ones: a monorepo subdirectory, or anything under a dotfiles-tracked home directory.\n\nThe root cause is the one named second: OuterRepo walks UP for an ancestor .git and never checked its starting point, so a plain directory inside a repository came back with that ancestor and the caller announced that the path is a git repository inside another when it is not a repository at all.\n\nOf the two remedies offered, verifying the root is the better one and is what was applied. Exempting an explicit ENTIRE_REPO_ROOT would also suppress the warning where it is TRUE and useful — a host dispatching into a genuine nested clone — whereas requiring an inner repository makes the message correct however the root was chosen, which subsumes the env-root complaint without losing a real warning.\n\nThe check sits in OuterRepo rather than at the call site, so the guarantee lives with the function making the claim. A .git FILE counts, because that is how a worktree marks its root, and Lstat matches how the walk already tests each ancestor.\n\nGuard: without the requirement the plain-subdirectory case returns the ancestor and the test goes red. The same test pins that a genuine nested clone and a worktree root still report, so the fix cannot pass by disabling the feature.\" 2>&1 | tail -1\necho\nprintf \"%-6s %s\\n\" PR OPEN\nfor pair in 306:226 318:238 320:240 321:241 329:242 330:246 331:247; do\n  PR=${pair%%:*}; T=${pair##*:}\n  printf \"#%-5s \" \"$PR\"\n  $EB trail finding list \"$T\" --repo gh/entireio/entire-brain --freshness any --status open --json 2>/dev/null \\\n  | sed '/^Using context/d' | python3 -c 'import json,sys;print(json.load(sys.stdin).get(\"counts\",{}).get(\"Open\"))'\ndone","description":"Resolve the last two and recount all seven","timeout":1800000}},"serverClassifierRequest":"d0c2f2fc-b585-4b0c-a804-125e4af609ad","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cfggy3PEz