{"parentUuid":"bdb58744-b028-4347-858d-f512cdc5ed59","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cfgio2D1ZC77vpdTCpm4S","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RvTB5Mv7xCAwLZHWQEQfXj","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp/pr306\ngofmt -l internal/ | head -2\ngo test ./internal/cli/ -count=1 -timeout 2400s > ~/.local/state/entire-distill/pr306q.log 2>&1; echo \"suite exit=$?\"\ngrep -E \"^--- FAIL: \" ~/.local/state/entire-distill/pr306q.log | head -3\ncat > /Users/suhaan/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp/m306.txt <<'MSGEOF'\nfix(verify): decide per anchor, not per record\n\nThe record-level origin gates I added earlier were the wrong granularity, and\nthe review caught the mirror of the bug they were written to fix.\n\nfactmerge.Upsert keys on the content id independent of Origin and keeps the\nexisting record's Origin while unioning anchors. So a record can hold anchors\nof BOTH kinds: an \"imported\" fact that later gains a genuine local anchor from\na distill of colliding text, or an authored fact that gains a foreign one.\nBailing on the whole record meant that for the first case the real commit,\ncheckpoint and transcript were never checked at all -- the same\nwrong-granularity defect the per-anchor check was introduced to fix, on the\nother side of the same merge.\n\nBoth record-level gates are gone. The per-anchor check handles every case, and\nbetter:\n\n  foreign-shaped anchor -> unverifiable-here, naming the tool\n  genuine local anchor  -> checked normally\n  repo-shaped anchor on an \"imported\" record -> CHECKED, so a fabricated\n    commit is reported missing instead of being described as an origin\n    contradiction and left unexamined\n\nNothing is lost by dropping the contradiction message: resolving the anchor is\na stronger answer than declaring it inconsistent.\n\nOne regression came with that and is fixed here too. The fact-level reason fell\nback to reasonForFactVerdict, which describes a VERDICT rather than a cause --\n\"one or more anchors need finer local evidence\" is equally true of an imported\nfact, a turn-signature limitation and a sparse authored anchor. The fact now\ntakes the reason its anchors give when they agree on one, and falls back when\nthey do not, because one of two causes stated as the cause is a wrong answer.\n\nAn existing assertion had to move with it: it tested that the reason contains\nthe literal word \"imported\", a containment check standing in for the real one.\nThe new reason answers the same question better by naming the tool, so the\nassertion now checks the substance -- which system the evidence lives in, and\nthat it is not this one.\n\nGuards verified by weakening: reinstating a record-level bail turns both new\nper-anchor tests red; forcing the generic fallback turns the imported-fact test\nred; and dropping the agreement check turns the new reason test red. That last\nguard was added only after a mutation found nothing to protect it.\nMSGEOF\ngit add -A\ngit commit -q -F /Users/suhaan/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp/m306.txt 2>&1|tail -2\ngit push -q origin HEAD:feat/facts-import 2>&1|tail -1\necho \"pushed: $(git rev-parse --short HEAD)\"","description":"Commit the per-anchor restructure","timeout":3000000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1797,"cache_read_input_tokens":493161,"output_tokens":1190,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1797,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1190,"cache_read_input_tokens":493161,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1797,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1797},"t