nchors need finer local evidence\" is equally true of an imported\nfact, a turn-signature limitation and a sparse authored anchor. The fact now\ntakes the reason its anchors give when they agree on one, and falls back when\nthey do not, because one of two causes stated as the cause is a wrong answer.\n\nAn existing assertion had to move with it: it tested that the reason contains\nthe literal word \"imported\", a containment check standing in for the real one.\nThe new reason answers the same question better by naming the tool, so the\nassertion now checks the substance -- which system the evidence lives in, and\nthat it is not this one.\n\nGuards verified by weakening: reinstating a record-level bail turns both new\nper-anchor tests red; forcing the generic fallback turns the imported-fact test\nred; and dropping the agreement check turns the new reason test red. That last\nguard was added only after a mutation found nothing to protect it.\nMSGEOF\ngit add -A\ngit commit -q -F /Users/suhaan/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp/m306.txt 2>&1|tail -2\ngit push -q origin HEAD:feat/facts-import 2>&1|tail -1\necho \"pushed: $(git rev-parse --short HEAD)\"","description":"Commit the per-anchor restructure","timeout":3000000}},"serverClassifierRequest":"3085f44d-45d3-4efb-9ec2-6df398d4fc16","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cfginzu8DU4eS54Fonaap","type":"assistant","uuid":"ef3d5df2-9316-41a3-a317-4ad82ee8cca8","timestamp":"2026-10-04T06:26:54.431Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
