{"parentUuid":"26607067-d478-4107-bf5a-aa5272298f6d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfgjEDWc64SnETQcRq6Ni","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019bgdjgJq7xjQK1jExwFV12","name":"AskUserQuestion","input":{"questions":[{"question":"All 7 PRs are at zero findings, CI-green and current with main, but 3 of 4 have no approval and I'm blocked on both approving and merging. How do you want to proceed?","header":"Merge/approve","multiSelect":false,"options":[{"label":"You approve + merge (Recommended)","description":"I stop here. You approve #318/#321/#331 and merge in order: #306, #318, #320, #321, then #329 → #330 → #331. This keeps the 'no merge without approval' rule and the never-self-approve doctrine intact, and a human looks at the diffs before they land."},{"label":"Authorize me to merge approved PRs only","description":"I merge any PR that already carries a human approval — today that's #306 once its CI finishes. I still never approve anything myself, so #318/#321/#331 wait for your review. Lifts the merge rule narrowly, keeps the review gate."},{"label":"Authorize me to merge all seven","description":"I merge the full set in dependency order, re-checking findings/CI/conflicts before each and stopping on the first failure. Fastest path to a merged main, but #318/#321/#331 would land without any human having reviewed them."},{"label":"Stop — park the stack as-is","description":"Leave all seven branches pushed and review-closed. Nothing merges now; you pick it up whenever. I write up the state so it's resumable."}]}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":575,"cache_read_input_tokens":499255,"output_tokens":1199,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":404},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creati