{"parentUuid":"374101f9-3e54-43b4-873f-7618622f5e9b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfhYWwd5AKXENRvnC37YR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TpvpHDSHLE9wCM9uzSy91Z","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide\ncat > /Users/suhaan/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp/mpc.txt <<'MSGEOF'\nfix(semantic): name the partial clone when the provider cannot stamp a header\n\nFound by running brain against a real repository instead of a fixture: the\nsemantic index failed on entiredb with \"semantic snapshot header missing\ncommit\", which names a symptom and leaves the cause to guesswork. It cost\nseveral wrong hypotheses -- worktree form, root symlink, cross-tree gitdir,\ntraversal budget -- before instrumenting the provider gave the answer.\n\nentire-graph refuses to run git metadata subprocesses in a PARTIAL CLONE. That\nrefusal is correct: a promisor remote means an ordinary git command can fetch\nover the network, and the provider runs --no-network. What it produces is not.\nIt emits an empty commit and tree with warnings[] and partial_failures[] both\nEMPTY, so nothing on the wire says why, and brain then discards a snapshot it\nhad already parsed -- 2,526 files, 35,510 symbols, 196,448 relations on this\nrepository -- with a message that mentions none of it.\n\nProven causal by toggling one config section on a single repository and\nchanging nothing else: with promisor=true and partialclonefilter set the commit\ncomes back \"\", without them it resolves, and it resolves again when they are\nremoved.\n\nThis is not an exotic state. `git clone --filter=blob:none` is ordinary on a\nlarge repository, and brain is used on large repositories -- so the repos most\nlikely to need a code index are the ones silently losing it.\n\nBrain now names the cause and the remedy. The annotation is best-effort: an\nunrelated error, a full clone, or a failed git probe each return the original\nerror untouched, because a diagnostic must never replace a real error with a\nworse one, and a wrong cause is worse than none.\n\nThe message is deliberately short. A repo guard\n(TestStatusCauseStringsFitStatusCauseWidth) caught the first version at 402\ncharacters against a 140 limit -- these errors are recorded as a freshness axis\ndetail, so an overlong cause is truncated in the very report it exists to\nexplain. The reasoning lives in the code comment, where length is free.\n\nGuards verified by weakening: dropping the annotation turns the behaviour test\nred, and removing the CALL SITE turns the call-site test red. The second guard\nexists only because the first weakening found nothing -- a correct diagnostic\nnothing invokes is indistinguishable from no diagnostic.\n\nThe provider-side half is not fixed here and belongs in entire-graph: a refusal\nthat produces an unusable snapshot should say so in warnings or\npartial_failures rather than emitting an empty header silently.\nMSGEOF\ngit add -A\ngit commit -q -F /Users/suhaan/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp/mpc.txt 2>&1|tail -2\ngit push -q origin HEAD:fix/agent-guide-directive-and-discovery 2>&1|tail -1\necho \"pushed: $(git rev-parse --short HEAD)\"","description":"Commit and push the partial-clone diagnostic","timeout":1800000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":323,"cache_read_input_tokens":670695,"output_tokens":1164,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":323},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1164,"cache_read_input_tokens":670695,"cache_creation_input_tokens":323,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":323,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01TpvpHDSHLE9wCM9uzSy91Z":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide\ncat > /Users/suhaan/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp/mpc.txt <<'MSGEOF'\nfix(semantic): name the partial clone when the provider cannot stamp a header\n\nFound by running brain against a real repository instead of a fixture: the\nsemantic index failed on entiredb with \"semantic snapshot header missing\ncommit\", which names a symptom and leaves the cause to guesswork. It cost\nseveral wrong hypotheses -- worktree form, root symlink, cross-tree gitdir,\ntraversal budget -- before instrumenting the provider gave the answer.\n\nentire-graph refuses to run git metadata subprocesses in a PARTIAL CLONE. That\nrefusal is correct: a promisor remote means an ordinary git command can fetch\nover the network, and the provider runs --no-network. What it produces is not.\nIt emits an empty commit and tree with warnings[] and partial_failures[] both\nEMPTY, so nothing on the wire says why, and brain then discards a snapshot it\nhad already parsed -- 2,526 files, 35,510 symbols, 196,448 relations on this\nrepository -- with a message that mentions none of it.\n\nProven causal by toggling one config section on a single repository and\nchanging nothing else: with promisor=true and partialclonefilter set the commit\ncomes back \"\", without them it resolves, and it resolves again when they are\nremoved.\n\nThis is not an exotic state. `git clone --filter=blob:none` is ordinary on a\nlarge repository, and brain is used on large repositories -- so the repos most\nlikely to need a code index are the ones silently losing it.\n\nBrain now names the cause and the remedy. The annotation is best-effort: an\nunrelated error, a full clone, or a failed git probe each return the original\nerror untouched, because a diagnostic must never replace a real error with a\nworse one, and a wrong cause is worse than none.\n\nThe message is deliberately short. A repo guard\n(TestStatusCauseStringsFitStatusCauseWidth) caught the first version at 402\ncharacters against a 140 limit -- these errors are recorded as a freshness axis\ndetail, so an overlong cause is truncated in the very report it exists to\nexplain. The reasoning lives in the code comment, where length is free.\n\nGuards verified by weakening: dropping the annotation turns the behaviour test\nred, and removing the CALL SITE turns the call-site test red. The second guard\nexists only because the first weakening found nothing -- a correct diagnostic\nnothing invokes is indistinguishable from no diagnostic.\n\nThe provider-side half is not fixed here and belongs in entire-graph: a refusal\nthat produces an unusable snapshot should say so in warnings or\npartial_failures rather than emitting an empty header silently.\nMSGEOF\ngit add -A\ngit commit -q -F /Users/suhaan/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp/mpc.txt 2>&1|tail -2\ngit push -q origin HEAD:fix/agent-guide-directive-and-discovery 2>&1|tail -1\necho \"pushed: $(git rev-parse --short HEAD)\"","description":"Commit and push the partial-clone diagnostic","timeout":1800000}},"serverClassifierRequest":"2e62d5b3-b108-4fbb-9823-a28ecd519229","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfhYWvQehotCVE8x4TQ1k","type":"assistant","uuid":"c7e998c2-a9ed-47ec-8924-3cf438cf45a4","timestamp":"2026-10-04T16:52:46.616Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
