{"parentUuid":"c295f74a-48b3-4ddb-8399-30383300daae","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14935383 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"3d2c8377-7ca2-4cf9-a97d-597b2f23a5cf","timestamp":"2026-10-04T16:53:03.771Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14935383 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"3d2c8377-7ca2-4cf9-a97d-597b2f23a5cf","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfhYZXjxeKFGYLGqeuLcy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Clean. Asking \"is it solid?\" and running it against a **real** repo found the biggest defect of the session.\n\n## What running it found\n\nBrain's semantic index **silently dies on any partially-cloned repository.**\n\n`entiredb` has `promisor = true` / `partialclonefilter = blob:none`. entire-graph correctly refuses git-metadata subprocesses there — a promisor remote means git can fetch over the network, and the provider runs `--no-network`. But it emits an **empty commit and tree with `warnings[]` and `partial_failures[]` both empty**, so nothing says why. Brain then throws away a snapshot it had already parsed — **2,526 files, 35,510 symbols, 196,448 relations** — behind the message *\"semantic snapshot header missing commit\"*.\n\nProven causal by toggling one config section and nothing else:\n\n| state | `commit` |\n|---|---|\n| no promisor | `a080ef23…` |\n| `promisor=true` + `partialclonefilter` | `''` |\n| removed again | `a080ef23…` |\n\n`git clone --filter=blob:none` is ordinary on large repos — so **the repos most likely to need a code index are the ones silently losing it.** That also compounds the scale story I'd been treating as separate.\n\n## Fixed and pushed (`f3680102`)\n\nBrain now names the cause and the remedy. Best-effort: unrelated error, full clone, or failed probe each return the original untouched.\n\nTwo things caught me, both worth recording:\n\n- A **repo guard caught my fix** — `TestStatusCauseStringsFitStatusCauseWidth` rejected my 402-character message against a 140 limit, because these errors are recorded as a freshness-axis detail and would be truncated in the very report they explain. Shortened; reasoning moved to the comment.\n- My first weakening **found nothing** — the test exercised the helper, so deleting the call site left it green. Added a call-site guard; that one goes red.\n\nI also chased four wrong hypotheses (worktree form, root symlink, cross-tree gitdir, traversal budget) before instrumenting the provider. Guessing cost more than measuring would have.\n\n## Status\n\nBrain is solid on everything I can test, with one genuine product gap now diagnosed rather than silent. The provider-side half — graph should report the refusal instead of emitting an empty header — belongs in entire-graph and isn't fixed here.\n\nSeven PRs, zero findings, merge order clean. Yours when you want them."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":825,"cache_read_input_tokens":672250,"output_tokens":819,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":825},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":819,"cache_read_input_tokens":672250,"cache_creation_input_tokens":825,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":825,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"9e408d5c-e577-4aaf-bae4-d1edc567ca7a","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfhYZX7mBVUxmcEExi15X","type":"assistant","uuid":"57de2dcf-204a-4b8f-8a62-2e22df803426","timestamp":"2026-10-04T16:53:14.517Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
