{"parentUuid":"7c540ac2-b4d9-43b9-a79a-7cfe9cfa3bc8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfhZxQb7UKwkNodAz59fS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"While that runs, let me prepare the graph-side report rather than file it unilaterally — that's your repo and an outward-facing action:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":549,"cache_read_input_tokens":687662,"output_tokens":1674,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":427},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":549},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1674,"cache_read_input_tokens":687662,"cache_creation_input_tokens":549,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":549,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"5fc084ac-ed56-4ada-8034-3e74886d9fb1","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfhZxPmkk1LAW4ksmwFSp","type":"assistant","uuid":"617a475b-2cd9-4d12-844b-9b403b7b4b6c","timestamp":"2026-10-04T17:11:29.083Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"617a475b-2cd9-4d12-844b-9b403b7b4b6c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfhZxQb7UKwkNodAz59fS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BYmnDyGjULSuhKqbA34JH9","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/GRAPH-PARTIAL-CLONE-ISSUE.md","content":"# entire-graph: a refused snapshot is emitted as an empty header, with no warning\n\n**Status:** draft, not filed. Filing is an outward-facing action on `entireio/entire-graph`\nand needs your go-ahead. Uncommitted on purpose.\n\n## Summary\n\nIn a **partially-cloned repository**, `entire-graph snapshot` refuses to run git metadata\nsubprocesses — correctly, because a promisor remote means an ordinary git command can fetch\nover the network while the provider runs `--no-network`.\n\nThe refusal is right. Its output is not: the provider emits a header with\n`commit: \"\"` and `tree: \"\"`, `repo_key` degraded to `local/<basename>`, and\n**`warnings: []` and `partial_failures: []` both empty**. Nothing on the wire says a\nrefusal happened.\n\nEvery consumer then has to guess. entire-brain discards a snapshot it has already fully\nparsed and reports `semantic snapshot header missing commit`, which names a symptom.\n\n## Reproduction\n\nAny repo; toggle one config section and change nothing else.\n\n```\ngit clone --filter=blob:none file:///path/to/src pc && cd pc\nentire-graph snapshot --repo . --format ndjson --no-network | head -1   # commit: \"\"\n\ngit config --unset remote.origin.promisor\ngit config --unset remote.origin.partialclonefilter\nentire-graph snapshot --repo . --format ndjson --no-network | head -1   # commit resolves\n```\n\nMeasured on `entiredb` (a real partial clone): the provider parses\n**2,526 files, 35,510 symbols, 196,448 relations**, then hands back an empty header and all\nof it is thrown away.\n\n## Where\n\n`internal/sem/provider.go`:\n\n- `newGitMetadataValidation` returns `metadataSafe=false`\n- the `else` branch sets `headErr` and leaves `commit`/`tree` empty\n- `headErr` is never surfaced into `Header.Warnings` or `Header.PartialFailures`\n\nThe deciding check is in `gitMetadataDirectoryPathsSafeWithResolver`:\n\n```go\nif !commonConfigValid || commonConfig.hasInclude ||\n    commonConfig.hasPartialCloneExtension || commonConfig.hasPromisorRemote {\n    return false\n}\n```\n\n## Suggested fix\n\nKeep the refusal. Report it: put `headErr` into `partial_failures` (or `warnings`) so a\nconsumer can say *why* instead of inferring from an empty field. A snapshot that cannot be\nstamped is not the same as a snapshot with nothing to stamp, and right now they are\nindistinguishable on the wire.\n\n## Why it matters\n\n`git clone --filter=blob:none` is ordinary practice on a large repository. Three of seven\nrepos in this workspace are partial clones — `cli`, `entiredb`, `graphmark` — so the repos\nmost likely to need a code index are the ones silently losing it.\n\n## Already done on the brain side\n\nentire-brain now names the cause and a **verified** remedy (`git fetch --refetch origin`,\nthen unset the two keys — checked on git 2.54.0; `--filter=` and `--filter=blob:unlimited`\nboth fail). That is a diagnostic, not a fix: the provider still discards a parsed index.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":549,"cache_read_input_tokens":687662,"output_tokens":1674,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":427},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":549},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1674,"cache_read_input_tokens":687662,"cache_creation_input_tokens":549,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":549,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01BYmnDyGjULSuhKqbA34JH9":{"file_path":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/GRAPH-PARTIAL-CLONE-ISSUE.md","content":"# entire-graph: a refused snapshot is emitted as an empty header, with no warning\n\n**Status:** draft, not filed. Filing is an outward-facing action on `entireio/entire-graph`\nand needs your go-ahead. Uncommitted on purpose.\n\n## Summary\n\nIn a **partially-cloned repository**, `entire-graph snapshot` refuses to run git metadata\nsubprocesses — correctly, because a promisor remote means an ordinary git command can fetch\nover the network while the provider runs `--no-network`.\n\nThe refusal is right. Its output is not: the provider emits a header with\n`commit: \"\"` and `tree: \"\"`, `repo_key` degraded to `local/<basename>`, and\n**`warnings: []` and `partial_failures: []` both empty**. Nothing on the wire says a\nrefusal happened.\n\nEvery consumer then has to guess. entire-brain discards a snapshot it has already fully\nparsed and reports `semantic snapshot header missing commit`, which names a symptom.\n\n## Reproduction\n\nAny repo; toggle one config section and change nothing else.\n\n```\ngit clone --filter=blob:none file:///path/to/src pc && cd pc\nentire-graph snapshot --repo . --format ndjson --no-network | head -1   # commit: \"\"\n\ngit config --unset remote.origin.promisor\ngit config --unset remote.origin.partialclonefilter\nentire-graph snapshot --repo . --format ndjson --no-network | head -1   # commit resolves\n```\n\nMeasured on `entiredb` (a real partial clone): the provider parses\n**2,526 files, 35,510 symbols, 196,448 relations**, then hands back an empty header and all\nof it is thrown away.\n\n## Where\n\n`internal/sem/provider.go`:\n\n- `newGitMetadataValidation` returns `metadataSafe=false`\n- the `else` branch sets `headErr` and leaves `commit`/`tree` empty\n- `headErr` is never surfaced into `Header.Warnings` or `Header.PartialFailures`\n\nThe deciding check is in `gitMetadataDirectoryPathsSafeWithResolver`:\n\n```go\nif !commonConfigValid || commonConfig.hasInclude ||\n    commonConfig.hasPartialCloneExtension || commonConfig.hasPromisorRemote {\n    return false\n}\n```\n\n## Suggested fix\n\nKeep the refusal. Report it: put `headErr` into `partial_failures` (or `warnings`) so a\nconsumer can say *why* instead of inferring from an empty field. A snapshot that cannot be\nstamped is not the same as a snapshot with nothing to stamp, and right now they are\nindistinguishable on the wire.\n\n## Why it matters\n\n`git clone --filter=blob:none` is ordinary practice on a large repository. Three of seven\nrepos in this workspace are partial clones — `cli`, `entiredb`, `graphmark` — so the repos\nmost likely to need a code index are the ones silently losing it.\n\n## Already done on the brain side\n\nentire-brain now names the cause and a **verified** remedy (`git fetch --refetch origin`,\nthen unset the two keys — checked on git 2.54.0; `--filter=` and `--filter=blob:unlimited`\nboth fail). That is a diagnostic, not a fix: the provider still discards a parsed index.\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"5fc084ac-ed56-4ada-8034-3e74886d9fb1","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CfhZxPmkk1LAW4ksmwFSp","type":"assistant","uuid":"8fec29ab-22e8-4c47-8215-ee8b18764a31","timestamp":"2026-10-04T17:11:41.960Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
