{"parentUuid":"da8ebf60-c6d7-4290-bfd2-2e3385a9d4f4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfhfDWkCZAwKo9aLMcRw6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Reviewed all seven and merged what I'm permitted to. Here's where it stopped and why.\n\n## Review\n\nClean across all seven — no debug prints, secrets, stray backup files, `TODO`s, or unconditional `t.Skip`s. Every PR ships tests roughly 1:1 with code:\n\n| PR | files | diff | tests |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| #306 | 12 | +3060/−4 | 5 |\n| #318 | 9 | +940/−11 | 4 |\n| #320 | 2 | +56/−0 | 1 |\n| #321 | 6 | +293/−2 | 2 |\n| #329 | 20 | +1758/−116 | 10 |\n| #330 | 26 | +1457/−57 | 26 |\n| #331 | 56 | +3704/−180 | 50 |\n\n## Merged: #306 ✅\n\n`6c8ebdab`. Verified after landing: **main builds, all `./internal/...` suites pass, 0 failures.**\n\n## Blocked: the other six\n\nThe sandbox refused with **\"Merge Without Review.\"** #306 went through because it carries `ashtom`'s approval; **#318, #320, #321, #329, #330 and #331 have zero approvals**, and the environment enforces that.\n\nI'm not going to route around it — that guard is doing exactly what the repo's own doctrine says (\"never self-approve\"), and it's the one check standing between 55 of my own fixes and your main branch.\n\n## To finish\n\nEither approve the six in GitHub and tell me to continue, or add a Bash permission rule for `gh pr merge` if you want me merging unapproved PRs.\n\nOrder from here: **#318, #320, #321, #329, #330, #331** — #331 last, since it carries #318 and #321 forward."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":667,"cache_read_input_tokens":712218,"output_tokens":585,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":667},