{"type":"pr-link","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","prNumber":331,"prUrl":"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/331","prRepository":"entireio/entire-brain","timestamp":"2026-10-04T19:32:43.879Z"}
{"parentUuid":"6272cc2d-6826-4f4a-8ef8-0f0f0d3c25ce","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"e65bf186-280e-44e7-9d82-2e29be8ae4f3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01S7iaWFKtgH6pHi8iYBitdH","type":"tool_result","content":"===== #306 =====\nfeat(facts): import memory from another tool\n  <!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\n  https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/226\n  <!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\n  \n  Gap 4 of 12. Brain could export (`bundle`) and could not import — the exact\n  friction a switcher hits, since everything they already recorded stays where it\n  is and Brain starts empty. cognee ships importers for mem0, Letta, Zep and\n  Graphiti for this reason.\n\n===== #318 =====\nfeat(facts): name the branches holding facts when a query finds none\n  <!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\n  https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/238\n  <!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\n  \n  ## Why\n  \n  Facts are recorded against the branch the **session** ran on. Sessions run on feature branches; queries run from `main`. So an empty result is the ordinary case, not a signal about the corpus — and the note explaining it is the line most callers actually read.\n  \n\n===== #320 =====\nfix(remember): return the persisted merged fact in JSON\n  ## Summary\n  \n  Supersedes #319 on current main without rewriting the original branch. The\n  product/test change is identical; the earlier branch started from stale local\n  main and failed the up-to-date review gate.\n  \n  - Make `remember --json` return the merged fact that was actually persisted, rather than the incoming record before upsert.\n  - Preserve retained provenance, original creation time/origin, confidence and related IDs while reporting reactivation and explicit-kind changes.\n\n===== #321 =====\nfix(setup): make the distill timeout configurable and name the nested-repo trap\n  <!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\n  https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/241\n  <!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\n  \n  Two traps from a real install report. Both fail silently, which is what makes them expensive.\n  \n  ## 1. The distill crawl\n  \n\n===== #329 =====\nfix(retrieval): return output an agent can accept, and disclose what was dropped\n  <!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\n  https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/242\n  <!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\n  \n  Bottom of a three-PR stack. Nothing above it matters if the tools error or lie.\n  \n  Two problems, both reproduced from a recorded session and from the filed issues.\n  \n\n===== #330 =====\nfix(safety): stop brain colliding with concurrent git, stalling on a dirty tree, and ignoring local models\n  <!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\n  https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/246\n  <!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\n  \n  Second of three. Stacked on #329 — **base is `fix/retrieval-output-correctness`, not `main`.**\n  \n  Five filed issues, each reproduced before being changed. Two of the plan's premises turned out to be wrong and are corrected below.\n  \n\n===== #331 =====\nfix(guide): make shipped guidance directive, name only commands graph exposes, and wire the pre-edit hook\n  <!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\n  https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/247\n  <!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\n  \n  Third of three. Stacked on #330 — **base is `fix/multiagent-safety-indexing-windows`, not `main`.**\n  \n  This is the root cause of \"agents don't use Brain or Graph.\" It is not that agents are habitual.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"cbf3a7b2-8e6e-4e96-9456-45ea30d3fefc","timestamp":"2026-10-04T19:32:49.097Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"===== #306 =====\nfeat(facts): import memory from another tool\n  <!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\n  https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/226\n  <!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\n  \n  Gap 4 of 12. Brain could export (`bundle`) and could not import — the exact\n  friction a switcher hits, since everything they already recorded stays where it\n  is and Brain starts empty. cognee ships importers for mem0, Letta, Zep and\n  Graphiti for this reason.\n\n===== #318 =====\nfeat(facts): name the branches holding facts when a query finds none\n  <!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\n  https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/238\n  <!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\n  \n  ## Why\n  \n  Facts are recorded against the branch the **session** ran on. Sessions run on feature branches; queries run from `main`. So an empty result is the ordinary case, not a signal about the corpus — and the note explaining it is the line most callers actually read.\n  \n\n===== #320 =====\nfix(remember): return the persisted merged fact in JSON\n  ## Summary\n  \n  Supersedes #319 on current main without rewriting the original branch. The\n  product/test change is identical; the earlier branch started from stale local\n  main and failed the up-to-date review gate.\n  \n  - Make `remember --json` return the merged fact that was actually persisted, rather than the incoming record before upsert.\n  - Preserve retained provenance, original creation time/origin, confidence and related IDs while reporting reactivation and explicit-kind changes.\n\n===== #321 =====\nfix(setup): make the distill timeout configurable and name the nested-repo trap\n  <!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\n  https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/241\n  <!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\n  \n  Two traps from a real install report. Both fail silently, which is what makes them expensive.\n  \n  ## 1. The distill crawl\n  \n\n===== #329 =====\nfix(retrieval): return output an agent can accept, and disclose what was dropped\n  <!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\n  https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/242\n  <!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\n  \n  Bottom of a three-PR stack. Nothing above it matters if the tools error or lie.\n  \n  Two problems, both reproduced from a recorded session and from the filed issues.\n  \n\n===== #330 =====\nfix(safety): stop brain colliding with concurrent git, stalling on a dirty tree, and ignoring local models\n  <!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\n  https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/246\n  <!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\n  \n  Second of three. Stacked on #329 — **base is `fix/retrieval-output-correctness`, not `main`.**\n  \n  Five filed issues, each reproduced before being changed. Two of the plan's premises turned out to be wrong and are corrected below.\n  \n\n===== #331 =====\nfix(guide): make shipped guidance directive, name only commands graph exposes, and wire the pre-edit hook\n  <!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\n  https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/247\n  <!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\n  \n  Third of three. Stacked on #330 — **base is `fix/multiagent-safety-indexing-windows`, not `main`.**\n  \n  This is the root cause of \"agents don't use Brain or Graph.\" It is not that agents are habitual.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"5924a55f-e13b-4d93-8293-163e632472eb","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","root":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","branch":"fix/agent-guide-directive-and-discovery","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"entireio","host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"},{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-graph","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/entiredb","visibility":"private"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/cli","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6272cc2d-6826-4f4a-8ef8-0f0f0d3c25ce","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"cbf3a7b2-8e6e-4e96-9456-45ea30d3fefc","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"environment","snapshot":{"workingDirectory":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","isWorktree":false,"isGitRepo":true,"additionalWorkingDirectories":[],"platform":"darwin","shell":"zsh","osVersion":"Darwin 25.5.0"},"changes":[{"field":"workingDirectory","from":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide"},{"field":"isWorktree"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"d83b4202-158d-4f55-bc04-849a09db0080","timestamp":"2026-10-04T19:32:49.109Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n# Environment update\n - Primary working directory: /Users/suhaan/devenv (was /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide)\n - The primary working directory is no longer a git worktree.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"d83b4202-158d-4f55-bc04-849a09db0080","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14998890 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"ec6bd216-45cd-4ec1-9d05-bbfbc2b4238f","timestamp":"2026-10-04T19:32:49.110Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14998890 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"ec6bd216-45cd-4ec1-9d05-bbfbc2b4238f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cfhkk9R12XYDfhDj2YuFe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here's what actually changes, grouped by what someone using brain would notice.\n\n## 1. Agents start using it (#331 — the big one)\n\nThis is the root cause of \"agents don't use Brain or Graph,\" and it wasn't habit. **The shipped guide told agents they could skip the tools**, and CI enforced that wording in both directions. It's now directive, and it names only commands graph actually exposes — it had been telling agents to run `graph query`, which isn't a verb.\n\nThe **pre-edit hook was completely inert**. It passed `--file \"$CLAUDE_FILE_PATH\"`, a variable Claude Code doesn't define, so it expanded to `\"\"` and errored on every edit while `init-agents` reported success. It now reads the harness payload from stdin and serves relevant facts before an edit — and names the right binary (`entire-brain` vs `entire brain`), which was a second silent killer for standalone installs.\n\n**Measured:** no-guide arms used the tools 0/10, 0/9, 0/3 across three rounds; guide arms went tool-first. p = 1.1e-5.\n\n## 2. Empty answers explain themselves (#318)\n\nFacts are recorded against the branch the *session* ran on; queries run from `main`. So an empty result was the ordinary case, and nothing said so. Now:\n\n```\nno facts for \"...\" on release-1.0\nnote: no matching facts on release-1.0, but 1 active fact(s)\n      on 1 other branch(es): feature — retry with --branch\n```\n\nAlso reaches `brain_get` over MCP, and a repo with no brain at all now says that instead of returning a bare empty array.\n\n## 3. The tools return usable output (#329)\n\nMCP responses were sized to the 4 MiB transport frame rather than an agent's context, so retrieval could return output the agent simply couldn't accept. Now budgeted to context, and it discloses what was dropped instead of truncating silently.\n\n## 4. Brain stops fighting your git (#330)\n\nIt collided with concurrent git operations, stalled on a dirty tree, and ignored local models. Five filed issues, each reproduced before being changed — and two of the plan's own premises turned out wrong and were corrected.\n\n## 5. You can migrate into it (#306)\n\nNew capability: `facts import --source mem0`. Brain could export and not import — the exact friction a switcher hits.\n\n## 6. Smaller but real\n\n- **#320** — `remember --json` returned the record you sent, not the fact actually persisted after merge.\n- **#321** — the distill timeout is configurable, and the nested-repo trap is named instead of silently writing the guide into a nested clone.\n\n## Plus, from this session\n\n**`cli`, `entiredb` and `graphmark` have had no semantic index at all** — they're partial clones, and graph refuses git metadata there while reporting nothing. Brain now names the cause and a remedy I verified by running it.\n\n---\n\n**Net:** before these, an agent was told it could skip brain, the push-path hook did nothing, empty answers looked like an empty brain, and on three of your repos the code index silently didn't exist. After, each of those either works or says why not.\n\nSix still need approvals — the sandbox blocks merging unapproved PRs, and I'd rather it did."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":689466,"cache_read_input_tokens":26450,"output_tokens":1059,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":689466,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1059,"cache_read_input_tokens":26450,"cache_creation_input_tokens":689466,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":689466},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"5b2934e3-9675-4790-80b5-7da1c8869bf8","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cfhkk6xfVwCGR4Fa3BAf5","type":"assistant","uuid":"d852cbd8-53dd-4f5a-8acc-a517bf804af6","timestamp":"2026-10-04T19:33:05.068Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
