{"parentUuid":"60ca8abc-1811-4464-a8c4-029654d17065","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfhmLCpLg7jdfi7qvUYNR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":31,"cache_read_input_tokens":716975,"output_tokens":2156,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1093},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":31,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2156,"cache_read_input_tokens":716975,"cache_creation_input_tokens":31,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":31},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":13627,"serverClassifierRequest":"b52a3c18-5ec3-47c5-910d-f94b757cc547","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfhmLA1fXQLXuhrxgmB87","type":"assistant","uuid":"92090020-322f-4a66-bada-15878320f0aa","timestamp":"2026-10-04T19:40:47.686Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"92090020-322f-4a66-bada-15878320f0aa","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfhmLCpLg7jdfi7qvUYNR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**#306 — `entire brain facts import`**\n\nBrain could export (`bundle`) but not import. That's the exact friction a switcher hits: everything they've already recorded stays in the old tool and brain starts empty. cognee ships importers for mem0, Letta, Zep and Graphiti for this reason.\n\n## What it does\n\n```\nentire brain facts import --source mem0 --file export.json\n```\n\nFlags: `--source` (mem0 today), `--file` (or `-` for stdin), `--path-prefix` (default `project.imported`), `--branch`, `--dry-run`, `--json`.\n\nReal output from my live test:\n\n```\nimported 2 of 3 memories from mem0\n  on branch feature\n  1 skipped: no memory text\n  not carried over: control, bidi or zero-width characters in a source id\n```\n\n## The interesting part is what it refuses to do quietly\n\nMost of the work wasn't the import — it was making it honest. Fifteen review findings, all variants of *a true statement that misleads*:\n\n**Foreign text is untrusted.** A memory's body *and its ids* go through the sanitiser. An id ends up inside the fact's anchor and gets printed by `facts show` through `%s` with no quoting — so an ANSI escape in `id` reached your terminal. Both ids are cleaned, and it says so, because cleaning one and not the other would silently break every `replaced_by` link.\n\n**Timestamps aren't guessed.** Epoch seconds, `2024-07-01 12:00:00`, python isoformat all parse. One that genuinely can't is **reported** rather than silently restamped with today's date — otherwise every imported fact claims to be from the import date and recency ordering is quietly destroyed. Verified: `created=2024-07-01`, not today.\n\n**The counts add up.** `facts=3 distilled=0 authored=1 imported=2`. Before, `imported` didn't exist at the agent surface, so importing 400 facts showed `facts=400 distilled=0 authored=0` — which reads as a corrupt brain.\n\n**Categories aren't dropped.** A memory tagged `[\"deployment\",\"security\"]` lands under both paths; a fact may hold two, and only the first was being kept.\n\n**`verify` doesn't cry wolf.** An imported fact's anchor names a session in mem0. Run through the normal checks it comes back *orphaned* — \"its evidence is gone\" — when the truth is it was never here. Now: `0 orphaned`, reason *\"anchor names a session in mem0, not this repository\"*.\n\n**A doomed import touches nothing.** An export where no record has a `memory` field used to take the write lock, rewrite the facts file, bump the manifest, *then* error. Now it refuses before touching disk.\n\n## What it deliberately won't do\n\nA memory whose text matches a fact you **retracted** doesn't come back to life — it's reported, not resurrected. A decision you made here isn't reversed by a foreign export. Same for a supersession whose target is ambiguous: it stays retired with no successor, and the report says so, rather than inventing a lineage from file order.\n\n---\n\nThe honest summary: the feature is small, the care is in refusing to look like it worked when it didn't. That's where fifteen of my 55 fixes went."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":31,"cache_read_input_tokens":716975,"output_tokens":2156,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1093},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":31,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2156,"cache_read_input_tokens":716975,"cache_creation_input_tokens":31,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":31},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"b52a3c18-5ec3-47c5-910d-f94b757cc547","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfhmLA1fXQLXuhrxgmB87","type":"assistant","uuid":"3fd644e2-9232-429a-8352-bb9e5acfc334","timestamp":"2026-10-04T19:41:01.192Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
