{"parentUuid":"03fb7560-c445-4558-9e4b-d0a3a18615f1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfhncHoXWHtJW7dhBLgsq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01L8MY4ctrwbZiRXf8e5giBc","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"T=/Users/suhaan/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp\necho \"########## doc-overview.md ##########\"\ncat $T/doc-overview.md 2>/dev/null | head -80","description":"Read the Overview page","timeout":1800000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1271,"cache_read_input_tokens":727293,"output_tokens":390,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":182},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1271,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":390,"cache_read_input_tokens":727293,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1271,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1271},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01L8MY4ctrwbZiRXf8e5giBc":{"command":"T=/Users/suhaan/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp\necho \"########## doc-overview.md ##########\"\ncat $T/doc-overview.md 2>/dev/null | head -80","description":"Read the Overview page","timeout":1800000}},"serverClassifierRequest":"b650b836-3ae9-4a8e-95d9-d3ffda6631ff","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CfhncHC4jmq7d4QeJa5SW","type":"assistant","uuid":"ea92c488-8966-42f1-89fe-f28d5ee66511","timestamp":"2026-10-04T19:57:23.018Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"ea92c488-8966-42f1-89fe-f28d5ee66511","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"3570d256-96d1-454b-9f16-9dbd4168da13","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01L8MY4ctrwbZiRXf8e5giBc","type":"tool_result","content":"########## doc-overview.md ##########\n---\ntitle: Overview\ndescription: Give your coding agents shared memory of your project, past decisions, and lessons learned.\n---\n\n## What Is Brain?\n\nEntire Brain is a memory layer for your Git repository. It brings together saved agent sessions, checkpoints, project facts, documentation, and code structure from [Entire Graph](/guides/graph/overview).\n\nGraph maps how your code connects while Brain adds the context behind it: why a decision was made, what was tried before, and what your team learned.\n\nThat memory belongs to the project and different coding agents can use it. For example,you can move from Claude Code to Codex and give the next agent context from earlier work.\n\n## How Does It Help?\n\nBrain is great for team collaboration and individual work when you are context switching across tasks and agents. It helps you spend less time explaining your project and repeating earlier research. A new agent session can start with the decisions, rules, and lessons that has already been recorded.\n\nFor example, before changing how failed requests are retried, you can ask Brain for earlier decisions about retries. Your agent can use that context to understand the current approach before editing the code.\n\n## What Can You Do with Brain?\n\n- Understand a project to get an overview of its structure and how it works.\n- Prepare for a task and find relevant decisions, code locations, and possible tests.\n- Find earlier work by searching through saved facts, history, and documentation.\n- Record a project rule or decision for future sessions.\n- Use memory to browse what Brain knows in a local UI.\n\n\n## Before You Start\n\nUse a local Git repository with at least one commit. Install the [Entire CLI](/installation) and Git 2.36 or later.\n\nTo give Brain access to future agent sessions, [enable Entire in your repository](/quickstart). Brain can also work from code, docs, and Git history when no saved sessions are available and make sure to commit your intended changes before setup.\n\n### Install Brain\n\nRun this once on your machine:\n\n```bash\ncurl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/entireio/entire-brain/main/scripts/get-brain.sh | bash\n```\n\nThe installer downloads a prebuilt binary, checks its checksum, and registers the `entire brain` command.\n\nInstall Graph for code analysis:\n\n```bash\nentire plugin install graph\n```\n\nWithout Graph, Brain can still use sessions, docs, and facts, but its code index is unavailable.\n\n### Set Up Your Repository\n\nFrom your repository's root, run:\n\n```bash\nentire brain setup\nentire brain status\n```\n\nSetup builds the repository's memory. Status shows what is ready and what needs attention.\n\n<Note>\n  By default, setup also extracts facts from past sessions and installs a background\n  watcher on supported macOS and Linux systems. Fact extraction uses an available\n  coding agent, can send session content to its model provider, and can incur token\n  charges. The watcher can continue extracting facts over time.\n\n  To skip the initial fact extraction and watcher installation, use\n  `entire brain setup --no-backfill --no-daemon` instead.\n</Note>\n\n\n## How to Use Brain\n\nFor a guided walkthrough, follow the [Brain Quickstart](/guides/brain/quickstart).\n\nUse Brain from the CLI or UI after setup, or use the agent prompt to have your agent set it up for you.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"cc2949b2-c403-46b9-9422-9f32279e57df","timestamp":"2026-10-04T19:57:23.512Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"########## doc-overview.md ##########\n---\ntitle: Overview\ndescription: Give your coding agents shared memory of your project, past decisions, and lessons learned.\n---\n\n## What Is Brain?\n\nEntire Brain is a memory layer for your Git repository. It brings together saved agent sessions, checkpoints, project facts, documentation, and code structure from [Entire Graph](/guides/graph/overview).\n\nGraph maps how your code connects while Brain adds the context behind it: why a decision was made, what was tried before, and what your team learned.\n\nThat memory belongs to the project and different coding agents can use it. For example,you can move from Claude Code to Codex and give the next agent context from earlier work.\n\n## How Does It Help?\n\nBrain is great for team collaboration and individual work when you are context switching across tasks and agents. It helps you spend less time explaining your project and repeating earlier research. A new agent session can start with the decisions, rules, and lessons that has already been recorded.\n\nFor example, before changing how failed requests are retried, you can ask Brain for earlier decisions about retries. Your agent can use that context to understand the current approach before editing the code.\n\n## What Can You Do with Brain?\n\n- Understand a project to get an overview of its structure and how it works.\n- Prepare for a task and find relevant decisions, code locations, and possible tests.\n- Find earlier work by searching through saved facts, history, and documentation.\n- Record a project rule or decision for future sessions.\n- Use memory to browse what Brain knows in a local UI.\n\n\n## Before You Start\n\nUse a local Git repository with at least one commit. Install the [Entire CLI](/installation) and Git 2.36 or later.\n\nTo give Brain access to future agent sessions, [enable Entire in your repository](/quickstart). Brain can also work from code, docs, and Git history when no saved sessions are available and make sure to commit your intended changes before setup.\n\n### Install Brain\n\nRun this once on your machine:\n\n```bash\ncurl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/entireio/entire-brain/main/scripts/get-brain.sh | bash\n```\n\nThe installer downloads a prebuilt binary, checks its checksum, and registers the `entire brain` command.\n\nInstall Graph for code analysis:\n\n```bash\nentire plugin install graph\n```\n\nWithout Graph, Brain can still use sessions, docs, and facts, but its code index is unavailable.\n\n### Set Up Your Repository\n\nFrom your repository's root, run:\n\n```bash\nentire brain setup\nentire brain status\n```\n\nSetup builds the repository's memory. Status shows what is ready and what needs attention.\n\n<Note>\n  By default, setup also extracts facts from past sessions and installs a background\n  watcher on supported macOS and Linux systems. Fact extraction uses an available\n  coding agent, can send session content to its model provider, and can incur token\n  charges. The watcher can continue extracting facts over time.\n\n  To skip the initial fact extraction and watcher installation, use\n  `entire brain setup --no-backfill --no-daemon` instead.\n</Note>\n\n\n## How to Use Brain\n\nFor a guided walkthrough, follow the [Brain Quickstart](/guides/brain/quickstart).\n\nUse Brain from the CLI or UI after setup, or use the agent prompt to have your agent set it up for you.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"b650b836-3ae9-4a8e-95d9-d3ffda6631ff","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","root":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":1,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":243},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-graph","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/entiredb","visibility":"private"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/cli","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ea92c488-8966-42f1-89fe-f28d5ee66511","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
