{"parentUuid":"50772d17-9e9c-4ad3-83cb-139508419587","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"3570d256-96d1-454b-9f16-9dbd4168da13","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BMvVCCd8TdovN8JEmmKHya","type":"tool_result","content":"<Tabs>\n  <Tab title=\"CLI\" icon=\"terminal\">\n    Run these commands from your repository.\n\n    Get a project overview:\n\n    ```bash\n    entire brain overview\n    ```\n\n    Get context for a task:\n\n    ```bash\n    entire brain brief \"update the retry policy\"\n    ```\n\n    Search earlier decisions:\n\n    ```bash\n    entire brain query \"why did we choose this retry policy\"\n    ```\n\n    Save a fact, then find it again. Replace the example with a rule that is true for your project:\n\n    ```bash\n    entire brain remember \"Retry failed requests at most three times.\" --path constraints.retry.policy\n    entire brain recall \"retry policy\"\n    ```\n\n    Check whether memory is current:\n\n    ```bash\n    entire brain status\n    ```\n\n    See the [command reference](https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/blob/main/docs/reference.md) for more options.\n  </Tab>\n\n  <Tab title=\"UI\" icon=\"browser\">\n    Open Brain's local browser view from your repository:\n\n    ```bash\n    entire brain viz\n    ```\n\n    Explore the graph to see code relationships, saved facts, sessions, history, and docs. This view runs on your machine and is read-only.\n\n    <div style={{ position: \"relative\", paddingTop: \"56.25%\" }}>\n      <iframe\n        src=\"https://customer-0x5hsk8lh27fm00g.cloudflarestream.com/988f4fb499040d1c5b3cc2417046e720/iframe\"\n        title=\"Explore Brain in the UI\"\n        loading=\"lazy\"\n        style={{\n          border: \"none\",\n          position: \"absolute\",\n          top: 0,\n          left: 0,\n          height: \"100%\",\n          width: \"100%\",\n        }}\n        allow=\"accelerometer; gyroscope; autoplay; encrypted-media; picture-in-picture;\"\n        allowFullScreen\n      />\n    </div>\n\n    If you prefer to stay in your terminal, open the dashboard:\n\n    ```bash\n    entire brain dash\n    ```\n\n    ![Brain terminal dashboard showing memory sources, session counts, saved facts, and working tree status.](/images/brain-terminal-dashboard.png)\n\n    Use it to browse status, facts, sessions, history, and code records. Both views let you explore existing memory without making model calls.\n\n  </Tab>\n\n  <Tab title=\"Agent Prompt\" icon=\"robot\">\n    To have your agent set up Brain for you, open it in your repository and send this prompt:\n\n    ```text\n    Set up Entire Brain in this repository and start using it for our work.\n\n    Check that the Entire CLI, Git 2.36 or later, and Entire Graph are\n    installed. Install any missing tools using the official instructions\n    at https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain#install.\n\n    Make sure this is a Git repository with at least one commit. If there\n    are uncommitted changes that block setup, tell me what needs attention.\n\n    Run `entire brain setup` to build the project's memory, then run\n    `entire brain init-agents` to add the agent instructions. Preserve my\n    existing instructions outside the managed blocks.\n\n    Run `entire brain status --verbose` and explain anything missing or\n    out of date. Read `.entire/agent-guide.md`, then run\n    `entire brain overview` and summarize what Brain knows about this project.\n\n    For my next task, use `entire brain brief` to gather relevant context\n    before making changes. Check the supporting sources and use Entire\n    Graph to find and inspect the code.\n    ```\n\n  </Tab>\n</Tabs>\n\n | docs\n\nThis is how Claude Code surfaces messages the user sends mid-turn — within the running turn, often alongside the next tool result, rather than as a separate conversation turn. Address the message above as you continue this turn.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"5a05810a-df03-4929-a68d-92f81fc53ece","timestamp":"2026-10-04T19:57:27.096Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"<Tabs>\n  <Tab title=\"CLI\" icon=\"terminal\">\n    Run these commands from your repository.\n\n    Get a project overview:\n\n    ```bash\n    entire brain overview\n    ```\n\n    Get context for a task:\n\n    ```bash\n    entire brain brief \"update the retry policy\"\n    ```\n\n    Search earlier decisions:\n\n    ```bash\n    entire brain query \"why did we choose this retry policy\"\n    ```\n\n    Save a fact, then find it again. Replace the example with a rule that is true for your project:\n\n    ```bash\n    entire brain remember \"Retry failed requests at most three times.\" --path constraints.retry.policy\n    entire brain recall \"retry policy\"\n    ```\n\n    Check whether memory is current:\n\n    ```bash\n    entire brain status\n    ```\n\n    See the [command reference](https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/blob/main/docs/reference.md) for more options.\n  </Tab>\n\n  <Tab title=\"UI\" icon=\"browser\">\n    Open Brain's local browser view from your repository:\n\n    ```bash\n    entire brain viz\n    ```\n\n    Explore the graph to see code relationships, saved facts, sessions, history, and docs. This view runs on your machine and is read-only.\n\n    <div style={{ position: \"relative\", paddingTop: \"56.25%\" }}>\n      <iframe\n        src=\"https://customer-0x5hsk8lh27fm00g.cloudflarestream.com/988f4fb499040d1c5b3cc2417046e720/iframe\"\n        title=\"Explore Brain in the UI\"\n        loading=\"lazy\"\n        style={{\n          border: \"none\",\n          position: \"absolute\",\n          top: 0,\n          left: 0,\n          height: \"100%\",\n          width: \"100%\",\n        }}\n        allow=\"accelerometer; gyroscope; autoplay; encrypted-media; picture-in-picture;\"\n        allowFullScreen\n      />\n    </div>\n\n    If you prefer to stay in your terminal, open the dashboard:\n\n    ```bash\n    entire brain dash\n    ```\n\n    ![Brain terminal dashboard showing memory sources, session counts, saved facts, and working tree status.](/images/brain-terminal-dashboard.png)\n\n    Use it to browse status, facts, sessions, history, and code records. Both views let you explore existing memory without making model calls.\n\n  </Tab>\n\n  <Tab title=\"Agent Prompt\" icon=\"robot\">\n    To have your agent set up Brain for you, open it in your repository and send this prompt:\n\n    ```text\n    Set up Entire Brain in this repository and start using it for our work.\n\n    Check that the Entire CLI, Git 2.36 or later, and Entire Graph are\n    installed. Install any missing tools using the official instructions\n    at https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain#install.\n\n    Make sure this is a Git repository with at least one commit. If there\n    are uncommitted changes that block setup, tell me what needs attention.\n\n    Run `entire brain setup` to build the project's memory, then run\n    `entire brain init-agents` to add the agent instructions. Preserve my\n    existing instructions outside the managed blocks.\n\n    Run `entire brain status --verbose` and explain anything missing or\n    out of date. Read `.entire/agent-guide.md`, then run\n    `entire brain overview` and summarize what Brain knows about this project.\n\n    For my next task, use `entire brain brief` to gather relevant context\n    before making changes. Check the supporting sources and use Entire\n    Graph to find and inspect the code.\n    ```\n\n  </Tab>\n</Tabs>\n\n | docs\n\nThis is how Claude Code surfaces messages the user sends mid-turn — within the running turn, often alongside the next tool result, rather than as a separate conversation turn. Address the message above as you continue this turn.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"10f1ab55-01ee-491e-a162-e64ac1e1b238","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","root":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","branch":"