{"parentUuid":"5d986731-901d-4c67-881a-bee947f1e430","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PreToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_01MhzWXz6z17R8cb5pGJvGEf","hookEvent":"PreToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"hookSpecificOutput\":{\"hookEventName\":\"PreToolUse\",\"permissionDecisionReason\":\"RTK auto-rewrite\",\"updatedInput\":{\"command\":\"T=/Users/suhaan/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp\\nrtk read $T/doc-usecases.md 2>/dev/null | head -70\",\"timeout\":1800000,\"description\":\"Read the use-cases page\"}}}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"rtk hook claude","durationMs":10},"type":"attachment","uuid":"05185a92-743c-4a00-97b8-5c6168616bc3","timestamp":"2026-10-04T19:57:35.513Z","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"5d986731-901d-4c67-881a-bee947f1e430","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"3570d256-96d1-454b-9f16-9dbd4168da13","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MhzWXz6z17R8cb5pGJvGEf","type":"tool_result","content":"---\ntitle: Getting started with Brain\nsidebarTitle: Brain Use Cases\ndescription: Learn what you can do with Brain and find the right command for each task.\n---\n\nYou can use Brain to find earlier decisions, save lessons, and give your agent context before it starts work. Below are some ways to use Brain in your project.\n\n[Install Brain and set up your repository](/guides/brain/overview#before-you-start) first. Run these commands from the repository, and replace the example questions and rules with your own.\n\n## Get to Know a Project\n\nIf you are joining a project or returning after a break, you can ask Brain for an overview of its structure, tools, and conventions.\n\n```bash\nentire brain overview\n```\n\n## Get Context Before Starting a Task\n\nDescribe what you want to build or change. Brain gathers relevant facts, earlier work, code locations, and possible tests into a brief.\n\n```bash\nentire brain brief \"add rate limiting to the upload endpoint\"\n```\n\nYou can now use the brief to plan your work or give your coding agent a starting point.\n\n## Find Out Why a Decision Was Made\n\nSearch earlier work before reopening a decision or trying an approach your team has already explored.\n\n```bash\nentire brain query \"why did we remove the queue abstraction\"\n```\n\nThis helps you read the supporting sources to understand the decision and whether it still applies.\n\n## Search for a Topic\n\nIf you are searching for a topic and know the keyword, you can use it with the command below:\n\n```bash\nentire brain query --keyword \"rate limiter\"\n```\n\nAnd if you know the problem but not the exact words, you can search by meaning:\n\n```bash\nentire brain query --semantic \"handling temporary request failures\"\n```\n\nWithout either flag, `query` combines keyword and meaning-based search. Make sure to use only one of these flags at a time.\n\n## Save a Rule for Future Work\n\nYou can also record a decision or lesson so another session can find it. It is advisable to only save rules that are true for your project.\n\n```bash\nentire brain remember \"Retry failed requests at most three times.\" --path constraints.retry.policy\n```\n\nThe path flag groups the fact under a topic. This lets you save the fact without asking an agent to choose a category.\n\n## Look Up Saved Rules\n\nBefore changing behavior, you can check what your project has already recorded about it.\n\n```bash\nentire brain recall \"retry policy\"","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"7c911dd0-8321-4ac5-b347-b5208ddad648","timestamp":"2026-10-04T19:57:40.624Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"---\ntitle: Getting started with Brain\nsidebarTitle: Brain Use Cases\ndescription: Learn what you can do with Brain and find the right command for each task.\n---\n\nYou can use Brain to find earlier decisions, save lessons, and give your agent context before it starts work. Below are some ways to use Brain in your project.\n\n[Install Brain and set up your repository](/guides/brain/overview#before-you-start) first. Run these commands from the repository, and replace the example questions and rules with your own.\n\n## Get to Know a Project\n\nIf you are joining a project or returning after a break, you can ask Brain for an overview of its structure, tools, and conventions.\n\n```bash\nentire brain overview\n```\n\n## Get Context Before Starting a Task\n\nDescribe what you want to build or change. Brain gathers relevant facts, earlier work, code locations, and possible tests into a brief.\n\n```bash\nentire brain brief \"add rate limiting to the upload endpoint\"\n```\n\nYou can now use the brief to plan your work or give your coding agent a starting point.\n\n## Find Out Why a Decision Was Made\n\nSearch earlier work before reopening a decision or trying an approach your team has already explored.\n\n```bash\nentire brain query \"why did we remove the queue abstraction\"\n```\n\nThis helps you read the supporting sources to understand the decision and whether it still applies.\n\n## Search for a Topic\n\nIf you are searching for a topic and know the keyword, you can use it with the command below:\n\n```bash\nentire brain query --keyword \"rate limiter\"\n```\n\nAnd if you know the problem but not the exact words, you can search by meaning:\n\n```bash\nentire brain query --semantic \"handling temporary request failures\"\n```\n\nWithout either flag, `query` combines keyword and meaning-based search. Make sure to use only one of these flags at a time.\n\n## Save a Rule for Future Work\n\nYou can also record a decision or lesson so another session can find it. It is advisable to only save rules that are true for your project.\n\n```bash\nentire brain remember \"Retry failed requests at most three times.\" --path constraints.retry.policy\n```\n\nThe path flag groups the fact under a topic. This lets you save the fact without asking an agent to choose a category.\n\n## Look Up Saved Rules\n\nBefore changing behavior, you can check what your project has already recorded about it.\n\n```bash\nentire brain recall \"retry policy\"","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"classifierBoundary":true,"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"fa37c52d-4cef-404f-bc67-ee83c43da8e7","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","root":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":1,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":243},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-graph","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/entiredb","visibility":"private"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/cli","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"5d986731-901d-4c67-881a-bee947f1e430","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
