{"parentUuid":"6a38cdfa-a4e0-4427-87be-3d8b3f8e5f50","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfhomDbtJGQoWsLATCQNb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YFsw2QBPh5GjZ83v51suHw","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide\ncat > /Users/suhaan/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp/mblock.txt <<'MSGEOF'\nfix: close a secret-leak path and an agent default that cannot run\n\nTwo blocking defects found by adversarial pre-merge review, both reproduced\nindependently before being changed. The two reviewers disagreed about the\nfirst; the probe settled it.\n\nAN IGNORED FILE'S CONTENTS COULD REACH `brain status`.\n\nbrainIgnorePathTokens trimmed only a TRAILING colon, so a compiler or parser\nlocation -- \"<path>:<line>:<col>\", the dominant shape of the warnings this\nfilter exists to withhold -- survived as one token and matched no exact-file\npattern: Ignored() compares against \".env\", and \".env:3:5\" is not equal to it,\ndoes not contain \"/.env\" and does not end in \".env\".\n\nSuch an error routinely quotes the offending SOURCE LINE. Measured before the\nfix, with patterns [\"secrets.yaml\",\"vault/\"]:\n\n    /repo/.env                  withheld\n    /repo/.env:3:5              NOT withheld\n    /repo/secrets.yaml:7:2      NOT withheld\n    /repo/config/prod.key:12:1  NOT withheld\n\nand a realistic warning quoting AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=... was not withheld\neither. Directory patterns were unaffected, which is why this survived.\n\nThe tokenizer now also offers the position-trimmed path, as an ADDITIONAL\ntoken rather than a replacement, so a filename that genuinely ends in a colon\nand digits still matches its own pattern. Only trailing digit groups are\nstripped.\n\nAUTO SELECTED AN AGENT THAT CANNOT RUN.\n\ndefaultRefreshAgent preferred ollama whenever the binary was on PATH, but\nexecOllamaDistillAgent hard-errors \"--agent ollama requires --model\" and auto\nhas no model to give: the distill path reads it from the flag alone, and\nENTIRE_BRAIN_OLLAMA_MODEL belongs to the EMBEDDING path. `ollama --version`\nsucceeds with no server and no models pulled, so merely installing ollama broke\ndistill, refresh, watch --distill, remember without --path, and recall\n--expand.\n\nThis amends Issue #328 rather than reverting it. That fix's premise does not\nhold: \"auto -> ollama\" never kept transcripts local, it returned an error, so\nnobody got distillation at all. Auto now selects an agent that can run, and\n#328's real concern -- sessions reaching a cloud provider SILENTLY -- is\ncovered by ollamaModelMissingWarning, which names the fallback and how to get\nthe local path back. Explicit `--agent ollama --model <name>` is unchanged.\n\nA model is NOT auto-picked. `ollama list` routinely offers an embedding model\nsuch as nomic-embed-text, which would return nonsense for distillation;\nchoosing one is a product decision, not a default worth guessing.\n\nTestLocalModelIsPreferredOverACloudAgent is amended, not deleted, with the\nreasoning recorded in it -- its premise was false, and the cases it now pins\nare what is actually achievable.\n\nBoth guards verified by weakening.\nMSGEOF\ngit add -A\ngit commit -q -F /Users/suhaan/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp/mblock.txt 2>&1|tail -2\ngit push -q origin HEAD:fix/agent-guide-directive-and-discovery 2>&1|tail -1\necho \"pushed: $(git rev-parse --short HEAD)\"","description":"Commit both blocking fixes","timeout":1800000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":287,"cache_read_input_tokens":779675,"output_tokens":1354,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":287,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[