H, but\nexecOllamaDistillAgent hard-errors \"--agent ollama requires --model\" and auto\nhas no model to give: the distill path reads it from the flag alone, and\nENTIRE_BRAIN_OLLAMA_MODEL belongs to the EMBEDDING path. `ollama --version`\nsucceeds with no server and no models pulled, so merely installing ollama broke\ndistill, refresh, watch --distill, remember without --path, and recall\n--expand.\n\nThis amends Issue #328 rather than reverting it. That fix's premise does not\nhold: \"auto -> ollama\" never kept transcripts local, it returned an error, so\nnobody got distillation at all. Auto now selects an agent that can run, and\n#328's real concern -- sessions reaching a cloud provider SILENTLY -- is\ncovered by ollamaModelMissingWarning, which names the fallback and how to get\nthe local path back. Explicit `--agent ollama --model <name>` is unchanged.\n\nA model is NOT auto-picked. `ollama list` routinely offers an embedding model\nsuch as nomic-embed-text, which would return nonsense for distillation;\nchoosing one is a product decision, not a default worth guessing.\n\nTestLocalModelIsPreferredOverACloudAgent is amended, not deleted, with the\nreasoning recorded in it -- its premise was false, and the cases it now pins\nare what is actually achievable.\n\nBoth guards verified by weakening.\nMSGEOF\ngit add -A\ngit commit -q -F /Users/suhaan/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp/mblock.txt 2>&1|tail -2\ngit push -q origin HEAD:fix/agent-guide-directive-and-discovery 2>&1|tail -1\necho \"pushed: $(git rev-parse --short HEAD)\"","description":"Commit both blocking fixes","timeout":1800000}},"serverClassifierRequest":"8e80d57e-45fc-4124-b45a-a88af04710a1","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfhomCa8cQcnjBtSE2fRt","type":"assistant","uuid":"76a79472-7dcc-4c8a-83e1-e43866efcbeb","timestamp":"2026-10-04T20:12:39.897Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"exte