nfor f in json.load(sys.stdin).get(\"findings\",[]):\n    loc=f.get(\"location\") or {}\n    print(\"\\n--- \"+f[\"id\"]+\"  sev=\"+str(f.get(\"severity\"))+\"  \"+str(loc.get(\"path\"))+\":\"+str(loc.get(\"startLine\")))\n    print((f.get(\"body\") or \"\").strip()[:850])\n'","description":"Read the three new findings","timeout":1800000}},"serverClassifierRequest":"a76980f3-a423-4846-8d73-3ac6e84fc554","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cfhpv9iqpA2KqhwSU4Ln3","type":"assistant","uuid":"cb06b6f9-4281-4715-b22a-b6af3e517d94","timestamp":"2026-10-04T20:27:37.679Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"cb06b6f9-4281-4715-b22a-b6af3e517d94","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"8b65ad49-bf96-4a34-9c99-2e67571b7f4d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GXBj2uXGzEkUw8EhLWFCcj","type":"tool_result","content":"--- 01M448V4WNMD0D88GCFB3AK5CA  sev=low  None:1506\nIn `detectRegressionAnomaliesCapped` and `runBrainReview`, the call to `detectRegressionAnomaliesCapped` now returns 4 values including `caps`, but the workspace functions `scanWorkspaceRepoRegressions` at workspace.go:3644 also call this function and must consistently handle the truncation flag. Verify all call sites properly handle the 4-tuple return to avoid silent truncation being reported as complete.\n\n--- 01M448V4WH9627FP0PS6YHM78Y  sev=medium  None:310\nThe `git_harden.go` change reads the index file twice from the same file descriptor - once with `Stat()` and once with `ReadAll()` - but only checks `readErr` and not `infoErr` before proceeding. If `Stat()` fails but `ReadAll()` succeeds, `indexInfo` will be nil and `indexInfo.ModTime()` on line 310 will panic. Check both errors or use the combined `readErr` check.\n\n--- 01M43XZE6KGC3WSBGGN09NRR4B  sev=medium  None:168\n`repoRoot.WriteFile` (Go 1.25+) truncates and writes `.claude/settings.json` in place rather than writing to a temp file and renaming, unlike every other managed write in this package (`replaceContainedFile`). A crash, kill, or disk-full partway through leaves the user's merged hook/settings file truncated or corrupted — losing not just the new pre-edit hook entry but any pre-existing settings the merge was supposed to preserve. It also skips `refuseSharedInode`'s hard-link check, so if `.claude/settings.json` is a hard link to another file (the same attack class this package's own comments describe being exploited against `.git/config` via `CLAUDE.md`), this write corrupts that other file too. Consider writing via a temp file + rename within `repoRoot` instead of a direct truncating write.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"50fee0f0-8d6d-408e-878e-4eaf37fac844","timestamp":"2026-10-04T20:27:39.444Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"--- 01M448V4WNMD0D88GCFB3AK5CA  sev=low  None:1506\nIn `detectRegressionAnomaliesCapped` and `runBrainReview`, the call to `detectRegressionAnomaliesCapped` now returns 4 values including `caps`, but the workspace functions `scanWorkspaceRepoRegressions` at workspace.go:3644 also call this function and must consistently handle the truncation flag. Verify all call sites properly handle the 4-tuple return to avoid silent truncation being reported as complete.\n\n--- 01M448V4WH9627FP0PS6YHM78Y  sev=medium  None:310\nThe `git_harden.go` change reads the index file twice from the same file descriptor - once with `Stat()` and once with `ReadAll()` - but only checks `readErr` and not `infoErr` before proceeding. If `Stat()` fails but `ReadAll()` succeeds, `indexInfo` will be nil and `indexInfo.ModTime()` on line 310 will panic. Check both errors or use the combined `readErr` check.\n\n--- 01M43XZE6KGC3WSBGGN09NRR4B  sev=medium  None:168\n`repoRoot.WriteFile` (Go 1.25+) truncates and writes `.claude/settings.json` in place rather than writing to a temp file and renaming, unlike every other managed write in this package (`replaceContainedFile`). A crash, kill, or disk-full partway through leaves the user's merged hook/settings file truncated or corrupted — losing not just the new pre-edit hook entry but any pre-existing settings the merge was supposed to preserve. It also skips `refuseSharedInode`'s hard-link check, so if `.claude/settings.json` is a hard link to another file (the same attack class this package's own comments describe being exploited against `.git/config` via `CLAUDE.md`), this write corrupts that other file too. Consider writing via a temp file + rename within `repoRoot` instead of a direct truncating write.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"a76980f