{"parentUuid":"372d4b0c-6c82-438e-9a65-5f8c5b7a559c","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14988355 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"6b99a9c1-c55b-48d8-a056-1289253b7631","timestamp":"2026-10-04T20:33:23.918Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14988355 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"6b99a9c1-c55b-48d8-a056-1289253b7631","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfhqN3wobsJeEsVtq8jJM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018s8tSkz96btnATf1Qh8nKJ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide\ncat > /Users/suhaan/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp/matomic.txt <<'MSGEOF'\nfix(hooks): write the merged settings atomically, and refuse a hard link\n\nrepoRoot.WriteFile TRUNCATES IN PLACE. This function MERGES, so a crash, a\nkill or a full disk partway through would destroy the user's own pre-existing\nsettings, not merely the hook entry being added -- the same class of loss the\nunrecognised-shape refusal was written to prevent, arriving by another route.\n\nIt also skipped the hard-link check. If .claude/settings.json is a hard link to\nanother file, an in-place write corrupts that other name too: the attack shape\nthis package's own comments describe against .git/config.\n\nreplaceContainedFile already does all of this and still cannot be reused -- it\nruns resolveContainedName, which admits only agent-instruction files and\nrefuses .claude/settings.json outright, as three pre-existing tests showed when\nthat was tried. So the sequence is repeated here against the plain name: probe\nfor write permission and shared inodes WITHOUT truncating, keep the original's\npermissions, stage beside the target, sync, then rename. A rename replaces a\ndirectory entry rather than following a link swapped in underneath it.\n\nGuards: a merge over an existing settings.json keeps the user's own keys and\nits 0600 mode and leaves no staging file behind; a hard-linked settings.json is\nrefused and its other name is byte-identical afterwards. Reverting to the\nin-place write turns the hard-link test red.\n\nTwo further findings from the same review round are REFUTED, with evidence:\n\n- \"git_harden.go dereferences indexInfo when Stat() fails\" -- it does not.\n  ModTime() is inside `if infoErr == nil` (git_harden.go:310-311), so the nil\n  case cannot reach it.\n\n- \"verify all callers handle the 4-tuple\" -- they do. All three production\n  callers of detectRegressionAnomaliesCapped bind caps (regression.go:1261,\n  regression.go:1506, workspace.go:3668), scanWorkspaceRepoRegressions returns\n  caps.Truncated(), and the uncapped wrapper no longer exists to be called.\nMSGEOF\ngit add -A\ngit commit -q -F /Users/suhaan/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp/matomic.txt 2>&1|tail -2\ngit push -q origin HEAD:fix/agent-guide-directive-and-discovery 2>&1|tail -1\necho \"pushed: $(git rev-parse --short HEAD)\"","description":"Commit the atomic write fix","timeout":1800000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":763,"cache_read_input_tokens":800157,"output_tokens":999,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":763,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":999,"cache_read_input_tokens":800157,"cache_creation_input_tokens":763,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":763},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_018s8tSkz96btnATf1Qh8nKJ":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide\ncat > /Users/suhaan/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp/matomic.txt <<'MSGEOF'\nfix(hooks): write the merged settings atomically, and refuse a hard link\n\nrepoRoot.WriteFile TRUNCATES IN PLACE. This function MERGES, so a crash, a\nkill or a full disk partway through would destroy the user's own pre-existing\nsettings, not merely the hook entry being added -- the same class of loss the\nunrecognised-shape refusal was written to prevent, arriving by another route.\n\nIt also skipped the hard-link check. If .claude/settings.json is a hard link to\nanother file, an in-place write corrupts that other name too: the attack shape\nthis package's own comments describe against .git/config.\n\nreplaceContainedFile already does all of this and still cannot be reused -- it\nruns resolveContainedName, which admits only agent-instruction files and\nrefuses .claude/settings.json outright, as three pre-existing tests showed when\nthat was tried. So the sequence is repeated here against the plain name: probe\nfor write permission and shared inodes WITHOUT truncating, keep the original's\npermissions, stage beside the target, sync, then rename. A rename replaces a\ndirectory entry rather than following a link swapped in underneath it.\n\nGuards: a merge over an existing settings.json keeps the user's own keys and\nits 0600 mode and leaves no staging file behind; a hard-linked settings.json is\nrefused and its other name is byte-identical afterwards. Reverting to the\nin-place write turns the hard-link test red.\n\nTwo further findings from the same review round are REFUTED, with evidence:\n\n- \"git_harden.go dereferences indexInfo when Stat() fails\" -- it does not.\n  ModTime() is inside `if infoErr == nil` (git_harden.go:310-311), so the nil\n  case cannot reach it.\n\n- \"verify all callers handle the 4-tuple\" -- they do. All three production\n  callers of detectRegressionAnomaliesCapped bind caps (regression.go:1261,\n  regression.go:1506, workspace.go:3668), scanWorkspaceRepoRegressions returns\n  caps.Truncated(), and the uncapped wrapper no longer exists to be called.\nMSGEOF\ngit add -A\ngit commit -q -F /Users/suhaan/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp/matomic.txt 2>&1|tail -2\ngit push -q origin HEAD:fix/agent-guide-directive-and-discovery 2>&1|tail -1\necho \"pushed: $(git rev-parse --short HEAD)\"","description":"Commit the atomic write fix","timeout":1800000}},"ser