{"parentUuid":"2987449b-9d09-4f50-a051-33d181f6df76","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14987258 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"9d58129a-d65b-4b64-8c7f-ea44b78d3bf6","timestamp":"2026-10-04T20:33:43.916Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14987258 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"9d58129a-d65b-4b64-8c7f-ea44b78d3bf6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfhqPXUJ88DvKDvnxkWEE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AwAi12usWvnoh7QLFTKCQx","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv\nEB=/Users/suhaan/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp/entire-main\n$EB trail finding resolve 247 01M43XZE6KGC3WSBGGN09NRR4B --repo gh/entireio/entire-brain -m \"FIXED in 05cbb55f — correct on both halves, and the merge framing is what makes it matter: repoRoot.WriteFile truncates in place, and this function MERGES, so a crash or full disk partway through destroys the user's pre-existing settings rather than just the hook entry being added.\n\nThe hard-link half is real too, and is the attack shape this package's own comments describe against .git/config.\n\nreplaceContainedFile cannot be reused, as suggested: it runs resolveContainedName, which admits only agent-instruction files and refuses .claude/settings.json outright — three pre-existing merge tests went red when that was tried earlier on this branch. So its sequence is repeated against the plain name: probe for write permission and shared inodes without truncating, preserve the original's permissions, stage beside the target, sync, rename.\n\nGuards: a merge over an existing file keeps the user's own keys and its 0600 mode and leaves no staging file; a hard-linked settings.json is refused and its other name is byte-identical afterwards. Reverting to the in-place write turns the hard-link test red.\" 2>&1 | tail -1\n\n$EB trail finding dismiss 247 01M448V4WH9627FP0PS6YHM78Y --repo gh/entireio/entire-brain -m \"REFUTED — the nil dereference cannot occur; ModTime() is already inside the infoErr guard.\n\ninternal/cli/git_harden.go:\n\n  275  indexInfo, infoErr := indexFile.Stat()\n  276  contents, readErr := io.ReadAll(indexFile)\n  278  if readErr != nil { ... }\n  310  if infoErr == nil {\n  311      mtime := indexInfo.ModTime()\n\nLine 311 is reachable only when infoErr == nil, which is exactly when indexInfo is non-nil. The finding reads the readErr check at 278 as the only guard, but it is not the one protecting indexInfo — 310 is.\n\nThe behaviour when Stat() fails is deliberate and already stated in the comment above it: the mtime is simply not copied onto the scratch index. Without the original's mtime the copy is not a faithful stand-in, so the surrounding code falls back to the unmodified git command rather than risking a wrong answer.\" 2>&1 | tail -1\n\n$EB trail finding dismiss 247 01M448V4WNMD0D88GCFB3AK5CA --repo gh/entireio/entire-brain -m \"REFUTED — every call site already binds the 4-tuple, and the uncapped wrapper no longer exists to be called.\n\nProduction callers of detectRegressionAnomaliesCapped, all binding caps:\n\n  internal/cli/regression.go:1261   runRegressionDetect\n  internal/cli/regression.go:1506   runBrainReview\n  internal/cli/workspace.go:3668    scanWorkspaceRepoRegressions\n\nscanWorkspaceRepoRegressions returns caps.Truncated() (workspace.go:3679), both workspace result structs carry history_truncated, and reviewSummary / workspaceReviewSummary / regressionNoAnomaliesLine and the multi-repo headline all take the flag.\n\nThe specific risk named — silent truncation reported as complete — is what this change set removed, and it is guarded: TestNoUncappedRegressionDetectorRemains asserts the uncapped wrapper is absent and that both summaries receive a real flag rather than a literal false. grep confirms func detectRegressionAnomalies( appears nowhere outside that test's own assertion string.\" 2>&1 | tail -1\necho \"--- recount ---\"\n$EB trail finding list 247 --repo gh/entireio/entire-brain --freshness any --status open --json 2>/dev/null | sed '/^Using context/d' | python3 -c 'import json,sys;print(\"#331 open:\",json.load(sys.stdin).get(\"counts\",{}).get(\"Open\"))'","description":"Disposition all three findings","timeout":1800000},"caller":