{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-04T20:58:03.353Z","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>amake-a-smth-20625e6e4d058074</task-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2/tasks/amake-a-smth-20625e6e4d058074.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"make a smth cladu e/ command to have a roflow two…\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Built `/court` at `/Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/skills/court/SKILL.md` (202 lines, uncommitted).\n\n**How it runs:** `/court &lt;idea&gt;` → Workflow with 15 agents per round, max 3 rounds (45 worst case).\n\n- **Two advocates, forced positions.** Prosecution may only argue it fails, defense only that it succeeds. Neither may hedge. A model asked \"is this good?\" agrees with whatever you hand it; one *assigned* a side argues.\n- **12 jurors, independent, one lens each** — unit economics, timing, execution, demand, competition, distribution, operations, regulation, technical debt, team, second-order harm, and the null hypothesis (what if the boring alternative wins). They never see each other's votes, or it's one opinion counted twelve times.\n- **A judge that rules on substance,** not vote-averaging: names the strongest surviving objection and rewrites the idea to beat it.\n- **Loop:** rewritten idea gets retried. Acquittal needs 9/12 *and* round &gt; 1.\n\n**The parts that make it not theatre:**\n\nA unanimous acquittal in round 1 is treated as **suspicious** — either the idea is trivial or the prosecution was lazy — and the judge must say so rather than celebrate. The surviving objection is always reported even on a win, since \"passes with a known fatal assumption\" is a lie by omission. Fabricated supporting facts lose the case. And `isDifferentIdea` flags when survival required becoming something else — if your idea died and a cousin lived, you're told that plainly.\n\nThe vote trend is the real output: 4/12 → 7/12 → 10/12 means it's being fixed; flat at 5/12 across rounds means it isn't, and the skill says to report that rather than keep grinding.\n\n**Verification:** script body syntax-checked inside the async context the runtime actually uses, `meta` confirmed a pure literal, 12 lenses confirmed present. My first check reported a false `SYNTAX_OK` — `&amp;&amp; echo` fired on `head`'s exit code, and top-level `return` is illegal in a bare module but valid in a workflow. Re-checked both properly.\n\nOne scope note: Claude Code also supports `.claude/commands/court.md` for a literal slash command. I used `.claude/skills/` to match the existing `trail-findings` convention in this repo; it's invocable as `/court` either way.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>821795</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>6</tool_uses><duration_ms>114968</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
