is a lie by omission. Fabricated supporting facts lose the case. And `isDifferentIdea` flags when survival required becoming something else — if your idea died and a cousin lived, you're told that plainly.\n\nThe vote trend is the real output: 4/12 → 7/12 → 10/12 means it's being fixed; flat at 5/12 across rounds means it isn't, and the skill says to report that rather than keep grinding.\n\n**Verification:** script body syntax-checked inside the async context the runtime actually uses, `meta` confirmed a pure literal, 12 lenses confirmed present. My first check reported a false `SYNTAX_OK` — `&amp;&amp; echo` fired on `head`'s exit code, and top-level `return` is illegal in a bare module but valid in a workflow. Re-checked both properly.\n\nOne scope note: Claude Code also supports `.claude/commands/court.md` for a literal slash command. I used `.claude/skills/` to match the existing `trail-findings` convention in this repo; it's invocable as `/court` either way.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>821795</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>6</tool_uses><duration_ms>114968</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>","reason":"absorbed_mid_turn","commandUuid":"1b778c62-45f2-4a7a-80bc-fdc31e3e74de","deliveryId":"0ed20ffc-8a92-4c5c-adbd-cfc3d101ee0d"}
