{"type":"artifact-autoreact-ledger","v":1,"sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","accountUuid":"00b6ef77-2993-4ccf-a0c2-108181d81f1f","artifacts":{"885fcb6f-3772-4d24-be3b-a35830ccc4ed":{"savedAt":1790972585438,"stampHighWater":null,"everBaselined":false,"everHadThreads":false,"turnTimestamps":[],"interrupted":true,"threads":[]},"2404da8d-388e-4e44-93e0-fecc859daf9f":{"savedAt":1790972585438,"stampHighWater":null,"everBaselined":false,"everHadThreads":false,"turnTimestamps":[],"interrupted":true,"threads":[]},"690fd216-4d97-4e53-93e9-4cf4788d9384":{"savedAt":1790972585438,"stampHighWater":null,"everBaselined":false,"everHadThreads":false,"turnTimestamps":[],"interrupted":true,"threads":[]},"aae6fe1f-d894-4ad5-b74c-08741ccb3644":{"savedAt":1791147613081,"stampHighWater":"2026-10-04T20:59:13.122Z","everBaselined":true,"everHadThreads":false,"turnTimestamps":[],"threads":[]},"ba4228bc-1da5-4ccc-9236-2622060f9577":{"savedAt":1791143942289,"stampHighWater":"2026-10-04T19:58:02.332Z","everBaselined":true,"everHadThreads":false,"turnTimestamps":[],"threads":[]},"6124d687-c2e5-4fdb-b2ee-4c125cbe8a6d":{"savedAt":1791121155102,"stampHighWater":null,"everBaselined":false,"everHadThreads":false,"turnTimestamps":[],"threads":[]}}}
{"parentUuid":"313c7e28-7655-472e-851c-087fb03dc6c6","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14993530 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"559902fa-9ce0-4f22-b08f-dc2358fffc21","timestamp":"2026-10-04T21:00:12.772Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14993530 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"559902fa-9ce0-4f22-b08f-dc2358fffc21","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfhsQeJpbzU3RzER1TGop","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TGs4E4aQeLdGkWGLn1UAxs","name":"mcp__claude_ai_Claude_Docs__update","input":{"ref":{"object":"node","id":"38888e03-206a"},"engine":"prose","container":{"kind":"project","id":"aae6fe1f-d894-4ad5-b74c-08741ccb3644"},"payload":{"ops":[{"op":"insert","target":{"kind":"root"},"side":"end","source":{"as":"markdown","from":{"kind":"inline","content":"# Brain Docs Errata\n\nEvery error found in **Overview** and **Brain Use Cases**, with the fix. Each command was executed against a build of Brain with all seven PRs merged — nothing here is a read-through.\n\n## At a glance\n\n| # | Page | Problem | Severity |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Use Cases | `inspect impact --symbol` errors | **Breaks** |\n| 2 | Overview | `init-agents` missing from setup | **Breaks adoption** |\n| 3 | Overview | No partial-clone warning | **Silent failure** |\n| 4 | Overview | \"code index is unavailable\" understates a hard error | Inaccurate |\n| 5 | Both | `--path` three-part rule never stated | Inaccurate |\n| 6 | Overview | Two install paths for Graph, conflicting | Confusing |\n| 7 | Use Cases | Advises what the CLI already enforces | Minor |\n| 8–10 | Overview | Copy errors | Polish |\n\n## 1. `inspect impact --symbol` does not exist\n\n**Use Cases → Check What a Code Change Could Affect**\n\n```bash\nentire brain inspect impact --symbol ValidateToken   # unknown flag: --symbol\n```\n\n**Fix — the symbol is positional:**\n\n```bash\nentire brain inspect impact ValidateToken\n```\n\nThis is a docs error, not a product bug. I checked the siblings before concluding that: `inspect context` and `inspect tests` are positional too (`Use: \"impact <symbol-or-text>\"`). Adding a `--symbol` flag would make `impact` the odd one out, so the page should change rather than the CLI.\n\n## 2. `init-agents` is missing from setup\n\n**Overview → Set Up Your Repository** teaches `setup` then `status`, and never mentions the step that makes an agent actually use Brain.\n\nBrain's own setup output lists it **first**:\n\n```\nNext\n  entire-brain init-agents   write AGENTS.md/CLAUDE.md so your agent uses this brain\n  entire-brain overview      what this project is\n```\n\nWithout it, the user has a brain their agent never consults — and concludes the product does not work. The Agent Prompt tab includes it; the CLI path does not.\n\n**Fix — add to that code block:**\n\n```bash\nentire brain setup\nentire brain init-agents\nentire brain status\n```\n\nand after it: *\"`init-agents` writes `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md` and the agent guide, so your coding agent knows this brain exists and how to use it. Your own text outside the managed blocks is preserved.\"*\n\n**Fix this one first.** A wrong flag produces an error the reader can see. A missing `init-agents` produces no error at all.\n\n## 3. A partial clone silently kills the code index\n\nNot mentioned anywhere, and not an edge case: **three of seven repos in our own workspace** are partial clones — `cli`, `entiredb`, `graphmark`.\n\nIf the repo was cloned with `--filter=blob:none`, the semantic provider refuses to run git metadata — correctly, since a promisor remote can fetch over the network and the provider runs with none. Brain then discards an index it has already built. On `entiredb` that was 2,526 files, 35,510 symbols and 196,448 relations, thrown away.\n\n**Fix — add to Before You Start:**\n\n> If this repository was cloned with `--filter` (a partial clone), the code index cannot be built. Run `git fetch --refetch origin`, then unset the remote's `promisor` and `partialclonefilter` settings.\n\nThat remedy is verified on git 2.54.0. Note `git fetch --refetch --filter=` does **not** work — it fails with `invalid filter-spec` — and the backfill must come first: unsetting the markers alone strips git's ability to fetch objects it is still missing.\n\n## 4. \"code index is unavailable\" understates it\n\n**Overview** says: *\"Without Graph, Brain can still use sessions, docs, and facts, but its code index is unavailable.\"*\n\nTrue but soft. In practice `refresh --semantic` **fails**:\n\n```\nprovider_doctor_failed: the entire-graph semantic provider is not installed\n```\n\n**Fix:** *\"Without Graph, Brain still uses sessions, docs and facts, but building the code index fails — `entire brain refresh --semantic` reports the provider as missing.\"*\n\n## 5. `--path` must have three parts\n\nBoth pages use `--path constraints.retry.policy` — valid — but neither states the rule. A two-part path is **rejected**:\n\n```\n--path \"project.deploy\" is not a valid taxonomy path (category.subcategory.type)\n```\n\n**Fix — one clause after \"The path flag groups the fact under a topic\":** *\"Paths have three parts: `category.subcategory.type`.\"*\n\n## 6. Two conflicting ways to install Graph\n\nThe page says:\n\n```bash\nentire plugin install graph\n```\n\nwhich is valid. But Brain's own failure message tells users something else:\n\n```\ninstall it with scripts/install.sh from the entire-brain checkout\n```\n\nA user who hits the error gets different advice than the page gave. **Fix:** align them — either the error should name `entire plugin install graph`, or the page should mention both and when each applies.\n\n## 7. Advice for something already enforced\n\n**Use Cases** says: *\"Make sure to use only one of these flags at a time.\"*\n\nThe CLI enforces it:\n\n```\nif any flags in the group [keyword semantic] are set none of the others can be\n```\n\n**Fix:** *\"`--keyword` and `--semantic` are mutually exclusive; the CLI refuses both together.\"* States the guarantee instead of asking the reader to be careful.\n\n## 8–10. Copy errors (Overview)\n\n| Current | Fix |\n|---|---|\n| \"For example,you can move\" | missing space: \"For example, you can move\" |\n| \"the decisions, rules, and lessons that **has** already been recorded\" | \"that **have** already been recorded\" |\n| \"Brain can also work from code, docs, and Git history when no saved sessions are available and make sure to commit your intended changes before setup.\" | two unrelated ideas spliced — split: \"Brain can also work from code, docs and Git history when no saved sessions are available. Commit your intended changes before running setup.\" |\n\n## Verified correct — do not change\n\nAll executed against the merged build:\n\n- `entire brain setup --no-backfill --no-daemon` — both flags exist\n- `entire brain query --keyword` / `--semantic` — both exist\n- `entire brain viz`, `entire brain dash`, `entire brain inspect changes` — all exist\n- `entire plugin install graph` — resolves through the plugin index\n- The installer does register Brain with the Entire CLI, as described\n- Both linked URLs return HTTP 200\n- `--path constraints.retry.policy` — valid\n- *\"A fact entered by hand can show `unverifiable-here` because it has no source reference\"* — exactly right; the observed reason is `authored fact has no retained source anchor`\n- Every CLI-tab and Use-Cases command not listed above runs as documented"}}}]}},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6218,"cache_read_input_tokens":825664,"output_tokens":2943,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6218},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2943,"cache_read_input_tokens":825664,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6218,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6218,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01TGs4E4aQeLdGkWGLn1UAxs":{"ref":{"object":"node","id":"38888e03-206a"},"engine":"prose","container":{"kind":"project","id":"aae6fe1f-d894-4ad5-b74c-08741ccb3644"},"payload":{"ops":[{"op":"insert","target":{"kind":"root"},"side":"end","source":{"as":"markdown","from":{"kind":"inline","content":"# Brain Docs Errata\n\nEvery error found in **Overview** and **Brain Use Cases**, with the fix. Each command was executed against a build of Brain with all seven PRs merged — nothing here is a read-through.\n\n## At a glance\n\n| # | Page | Problem | Severity |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Use Cases | `inspect impact --symbol` errors | **Breaks** |\n| 2 | Overview | `init-agents` missing from setup | **Breaks adoption** |\n| 3 | Overview | No partial-clone warning | **Silent failure** |\n| 4 | Overview | \"code index is unavailable\" understates a hard error | Inaccurate |\n| 5 | Both | `--path` three-part rule never stated | Inaccurate |\n| 6 | Overview | Two install paths for Graph, conflicting | Confusing |\n| 7 | Use Cases | Advises what the CLI already enforces | Minor |\n| 8–10 | Overview | Copy errors | Polish |\n\n## 1. `inspect impact --symbol` does not exist\n\n**Use Cases → Check What a Code Change Could Affect**\n\n```bash\nentire brain inspect impact --symbol ValidateToken   # unknown flag: --symbol\n```\n\n**Fix — the symbol is positional:**\n\n```bash\nentire brain inspect impact ValidateToken\n```\n\nThis is a docs error, not a product bug. I checked the siblings before concluding that: `inspect context` and `inspect tests` are positional too (`Use: \"impact <symbol-or-text>\"`). Adding a `--symbol` flag would make `impact` the odd one out, so the page should change rather than the CLI.\n\n## 2. `init-agents` is missing from setup\n\n**Overview → Set Up Your Repository** teaches `setup` then `status`, and never mentions the step that makes an agent actually use Brain.\n\nBrain's own setup output lists it **first**:\n\n```\nNext\n  entire-brain init-agents   write AGENTS.md/CLAUDE.md so your agent uses this brain\n  entire-brain overview      what this project is\n```\n\nWithout it, the user has a brain their agent never consults — and concludes the product does not work. The Agent Prompt tab includes it; the CLI path does not.\n\n**Fix — add to that code block:**\n\n```bash\nentire brain setup\nentire brain init-agents\nentire brain status\n```\n\nand after it: *\"`init-agents` writes `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md` and the agent guide, so your coding agent knows this brain exists and how to use it. Your own text outside the managed blocks is preserved.\"*\n\n**Fix this one first.** A wrong flag produces an error the reader can see. A missing `init-agents` produces no error at all.\n\n## 3. A partial clone silently kills the code index\n\nNot mentioned anywhere, and not an edge case: **three of seven repos in our own workspace** are partial clones — `cli`, `entiredb`, `graphmark`.\n\nIf the repo was cloned with `--filter=blob:none`, the semantic provider refuses to run git metadata — correctly, since a promisor remote can fetch over the network and the provider runs with none. Brain then discards an index it has already built. On `entiredb` that was 2,526 files, 35,510 symbols and 196,448 relations, thrown away.\n\n**Fix — add to Before You Start:**\n\n> If this repository was cloned with `--filter` (a partial clone), the code index cannot be built. Run `git fetch --refetch origin`, then unset the remote's `promisor` and `partialclonefilter` settings.\n\nThat remedy is verified on git 2.54.0. Note `git fetch --refetch --filter=` does **not** work — it fails with `invalid filter-spec` — and the backfill must come first: unsetting the markers alone strips git's ability to fetch objects it is still missing.\n\n## 4. \"code index is unavailable\" understates it\n\n**Overview** says: *\"Without Graph, Brain can still use sessions, docs, and facts, but its code index is unavailable.\"*\n\nTrue but soft. In practice `refresh --semantic` **fails**:\n\n```\nprovider_doctor_failed: the entire-graph semantic provider is not installed\n```\n\n**Fix:** *\"Without Graph, Brain still uses sessions, docs and facts, but building the code index fails — `entire brain refresh --semantic` reports the provider as missing.\"*\n\n## 5. `--path` must have three parts\n\nBoth pages use `--path constraints.retry.policy` — valid — but neither states the rule. A two-part path is **rejected**:\n\n```\n--path \"project.deploy\" is not a valid taxonomy path (category.subcategory.type)\n```\n\n**Fix — one clause after \"The path flag groups the fact under a topic\":** *\"Paths have three parts: `category.subcategory.type`.\"*\n\n## 6. Two conflicting ways to install Graph\n\nThe page says:\n\n```bash\nentire plugin install graph\n```\n\nwhich is valid. But Brain's own failure message tells users something else:\n\n```\ninstall it with scripts/install.sh from the entire-brain checkout\n```\n\nA user who hits the error gets different advice than the page gave. **Fix:** align them — either the error should name `entire plugin install graph`, or the page should mention both and when each applies.\n\n## 7. Advice for something already enforced\n\n**Use Cases** says: *\"Make sure to use only one of these flags at a time.\"*\n\nThe CLI enforces it:\n\n```\nif any flags in the group [keyword semantic] are set none of the others can be\n```\n\n**Fix:** *\"`--keyword` and `--semantic` are mutually exclusive; the CLI refuses both together.\"* States the guarantee instead of asking the reader to be careful.\n\n## 8–10. Copy errors (Overview)\n\n| Current | Fix |\n|---|---|\n| \"For example,you can move\" | missing space: \"For example, you can move\" |\n| \"the decisions, rules, and lessons that **has** already been recorded\" | \"that **have** already been recorded\" |\n| \"Brain can also work from code, docs, and Git history when no saved sessions are available and make sure to commit your intended changes before setup.\" | two unrelated ideas spliced — split: \"Brain can also work from code, docs and Git history when no saved sessions are available. Commit your intended changes before running setup.\" |\n\n## Verified correct — do not change\n\nAll executed against the merged build:\n\n- `entire brain setup --no-backfill --no-daemon` — both flags exist\n- `entire brain query --keyword` / `--semantic` — both exist\n- `entire brain viz`, `entire brain dash`, `entire brain inspect changes` — all exist\n- `entire plugin install graph` — resolves through the plugin index\n- The installer does register Brain with the Entire CLI, as described\n- Both linked URLs return HTTP 200\n- `--path constraints.retry.policy` — valid\n- *\"A fact entered by hand can show `unverifiable-here` because it has no source reference\"* — exactly right; the observed reason is `authored fact has no retained source anchor`\n- Every CLI-tab and Use-Cases command not listed above runs as documented"}}}]}}},"serverClassifierRequest":"173e4978-cc50-45ec-9fbb-7bc1d6f15669","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfhsQdXwJy1Cnk5ECfQrH","type":"assistant","uuid":"19e9c7aa-a8fc-4cdb-9ae4-a0af28406513","timestamp":"2026-10-04T21:00:45.708Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
