{"parentUuid":"a4deec15-2089-4784-abc4-72b4ce44d924","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfhtTSR9aKyfWsuoo6hnX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XaaUGStsP4kkcGwHqMUQ1k","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide\ncat > /Users/suhaan/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp/mprod.txt <<'MSGEOF'\nfix(semantic): index a partial clone, and answer the questions the docs raise\n\nThree fixes that move problems out of the documentation and into the product.\n\nA PARTIAL CLONE NOW INDEXES.\n\nentire-graph refuses git metadata subprocesses in a partial clone -- rightly,\nsince a promisor remote means an ordinary git command can fetch over the\nnetwork and the provider runs --no-network. It returns an empty commit and\ntree, and brain DISCARDED an index it had already parsed in full: 2,526 files\nand 35,510 symbols on one real repository here. `git clone --filter=blob:none`\nis ordinary on a large repo, so the repos that most need an index were the ones\nsilently losing it -- three of seven in this workspace.\n\nBrain never needed the provider for that answer. head and tree come from its\nown `git rev-parse HEAD` and `HEAD^{tree}`, which succeed in a partial clone.\nWhat makes stamping sound rather than a guess is verifySemanticWorktreeStable,\nwhich has already confirmed the tree did not move while the provider ran, so\nthe snapshot describes exactly that commit. The stamp is disclosed as a warning\nrather than applied silently.\n\nVerified end to end on a real `--filter=blob:none` clone: the index builds and\nresolves symbols. Two mistakes on the way, both pinned by tests:\n\n  - stamping only the in-memory header left the persisted snapshot blank, and\n    the two then disagreed (\"commit ... does not match snapshot \\\"\\\"\"). The\n    stamp belongs in the stream scanner, beside the repo_key normalisation that\n    exists for the same reason.\n  - the assignment first landed inside the already-current branch, which only\n    runs when a semantic source exists -- so a FIRST index, exactly the failing\n    case, left it empty. A test now asserts it precedes that guard.\n\nTHE INSTALL MESSAGE CONTRADICTED THE DOCS.\n\nIt named only `scripts/install.sh` from the entire-brain checkout -- the\ncontributor's path, assuming a sibling clone. The published guide says\n`entire plugin install graph`, so a user who followed the docs and hit this\nerror was handed a different, harder instruction they usually could not follow.\nBoth are kept, documented path first.\n\nAN UNKNOWN FLAG NOW ANSWERS ITSELF.\n\nThe guide documents `inspect impact --symbol`, which does not exist. The flag\nis deliberately not added -- `inspect context` and `inspect tests` take their\nsymbol positionally too, so accepting it on one would bend a consistent\ninterface around a typo. The error now names the right form.\n\nThat hint first vanished without a trace: wrapJSONErrorRendering walks every\nchild and REPLACED each one's flag-error handler. It now chains, so any command\nmay improve its own flag error. That was a latent trap for the next person as\nmuch as a bug for this one.\nMSGEOF\ngit add -A\ngit commit -q -F /Users/suhaan/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp/mprod.txt 2>&1|tail -2\ngit push -q origin HEAD:fix/agent-guide-directive-and-discovery 2>&1|tail -1\necho \"pushed: $(git rev-parse --short HEAD)\"","description":"Commit the three proactive fixes","timeout":1800000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":340,"cache_read_input_tokens":889617,"output_tokens":1259,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":340},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1259,"cache_read_input_tokens":889617,"cache_creation_input_tokens":340,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":340,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01XaaUGStsP4kkcGwHqMUQ1k":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide\ncat > /Users/suhaan/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp/mprod.txt <<'MSGEOF'\nfix(semantic): index a partial clone, and answer the questions the docs raise\n\nThree fixes that move problems out of the documentation and into the product.\n\nA PARTIAL CLONE NOW INDEXES.\n\nentire-graph refuses git metadata subprocesses in a partial clone -- rightly,\nsince a promisor remote means an ordinary git command can fetch over the\nnetwork and the provider runs --no-network. It returns an empty commit and\ntree, and brain DISCARDED an index it had already parsed in full: 2,526 files\nand 35,510 symbols on one real repository here. `git clone --filter=blob:none`\nis ordinary on a large repo, so the repos that most need an index were the ones\nsilently losing it -- three of seven in this workspace.\n\nBrain never needed the provider for that answer. head and tree come from its\nown `git rev-parse HEAD` and `HEAD^{tree}`, which succeed in a partial clone.\nWhat makes stamping sound rather than a guess is verifySemanticWorktreeStable,\nwhich has already confirmed the tree did not move while the provider ran, so\nthe snapshot describes exactly that commit. The stamp is disclosed as a warning\nrather than applied silently.\n\nVerified end to end on a real `--filter=blob:none` clone: the index builds and\nresolves symbols. Two mistakes on the way, both pinned by tests:\n\n  - stamping only the in-memory header left the persisted snapshot blank, and\n    the two then disagreed (\"commit ... does not match snapshot \\\"\\\"\"). The\n    stamp belongs in the stream scanner, beside the repo_key normalisation that\n    exists for the same reason.\n  - the assignment first landed inside the already-current branch, which only\n    runs when a semantic source exists -- so a FIRST index, exactly the failing\n    case, left it empty. A test now asserts it precedes that guard.\n\nTHE INSTALL MESSAGE CONTRADICTED THE DOCS.\n\nIt named only `scripts/install.sh` from the entire-brain checkout -- the\ncontributor's path, assuming a sibling clone. The published guide says\n`entire plugin install graph`, so a user who followed the docs and hit this\nerror was handed a different, harder instruction they usually could not follow.\nBoth are kept, documented path first.\n\nAN UNKNOWN FLAG NOW ANSWERS ITSELF.\n\nThe guide documents `inspect impact --symbol`, which does not exist. The flag\nis deliberately not added -- `inspect context` and `inspect tests` take their\nsymbol positionally too, so accepting it on one would bend a consistent\ninterface around a typo. The error now names the right form.\n\nThat hint first vanished without a trace: wrapJSONErrorRendering walks every\nchild and REPLACED each one's flag-error handler. It now chains, so any command\nmay improve its own flag error. That was a latent trap for the next person as\nmuch as a bug for this one.\nMSGEOF\ngit add -A\ngit commit -q -F /Users/suhaan/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp/mprod.txt 2>&1|tail -2\ngit push -q origin HEAD:fix/agent-guide-directive-and-discovery 2>&1|tail -1\necho \"pushed: $(git rev-parse --short HEAD)\"","description":"Commit the three proactive fixes","timeout":1800000}},"serverClassifierRequest":"47046640-26fd-4593-9349-fad3612dfafe","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfhtTRZ4DvrFvk5GYT2Re","type":"assistant","uuid":"1338c8ea-6d18-4455-a27f-ec4f142abb53","timestamp":"2026-10-04T21:14:18.037Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/deve