{"parentUuid":"8d2d81c0-814b-41e3-89b0-9fae61960078","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"e7d5ff4e-b60f-475f-83f8-4b2d43603eb4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"ok so these are the only doc rpoblmes-\n\n<pasted_content id=\"3b25\">\n1. inspect impact --symbol does not exist\nUse Cases → Check What a Code Change Could Affect\nentire brain inspect impact --symbol ValidateToken   # unknown flag: --symbol\nFix — the symbol is positional:\nentire brain inspect impact ValidateToken\nThis is a docs error, not a product bug. I checked the siblings before concluding that: inspect context and inspect tests are positional too (Use: \"impact <symbol-or-text>\"). Adding a --symbol flag would make impact the odd one out, so the page should change rather than the CLI.\n2. init-agents is missing from setup\nOverview → Set Up Your Repository teaches setup then status, and never mentions the step that makes an agent actually use Brain.\nBrain's own setup output lists it first:\nNext\n  entire-brain init-agents   write AGENTS.md/CLAUDE.md so your agent uses this brain\n  entire-brain overview      what this project is\nWithout it, the user has a brain their agent never consults — and concludes the product does not work. The Agent Prompt tab includes it; the CLI path does not.\nFix — add to that code block:\nentire brain setup\nentire brain init-agents\nentire brain status\nand after it: \"init-agents writes AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md and the agent guide, so your coding agent knows this brain exists and how to use it. Your own text outside the managed blocks is preserved.\"\nFix this one first. A wrong flag produces an error the reader can see. A missing init-agents produces no error at all.\n\n\n5. --path must have three parts\nBoth pages use --path constraints.retry.policy — valid — but neither states the rule. A two-part path is rejected:\n--path \"project.deploy\" is not a valid taxonomy path (category.subcategory.type)\nFix — one clause after \"The path flag groups the fact under a topic\": \"Paths have three parts: category.subcategory.type.\"\n</pasted_content id=\"3b25\">\n\n?"},"uuid":"2269830d-651c-42fe-93ac-849779452170","timestamp":"2026-10-04T21:15:05.159Z","permissionMode":"auto","origin":{"kind":"human"},"promptSource":"typed","turnOrigin":"human","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
