{"parentUuid":"61e71cb0-c2ff-4786-872b-342207352a29","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14969936 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"79f4a25b-1189-42ad-8c25-9f9421449398","timestamp":"2026-10-04T21:24:44.597Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14969936 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"79f4a25b-1189-42ad-8c25-9f9421449398","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfhuH9L5T8eWMfwSMiP97","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01J2N6HJr62GSnLH6oBEMPmp","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide\ncat > /Users/suhaan/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp/mwired.txt <<'MSGEOF'\nfeat(status): say when no agent has been told this brain exists\n\nA brain nothing reads is the product's worst failure mode, and until now it was\nentirely silent: setup succeeds, every source reports healthy, and no agent ever\nconsults the brain because nothing told it the brain is there. The user\nconcludes the product does not work, and no output disagrees.\n\nThe published guide makes this the DEFAULT path, not an edge case. Overview ->\nSet Up Your Repository teaches `setup` then `status` and never mentions\n`init-agents`; only the Agent Prompt tab includes it. Anyone following the CLI\ninstructions ends up here.\n\n`status` now leads its Onboarding block with:\n\n  agents    x not wired — run `entire-brain init-agents` so your agent uses this brain\n              missing: .entire/agent-guide.md, AGENTS.md or CLAUDE.md\n\nand the line disappears once init-agents has run. It is first in the block on\npurpose: it decides whether any other line is ever acted on.\n\nAgentsWired is read-only and cheap -- the guide must exist, and at least one of\nAGENTS.md / CLAUDE.md must carry the managed pointer. One is enough: the two are\ndocumented aliases and a repository may keep only the one its agent reads. A\nfile carrying the user's own text but not the managed block does not count.\n\nAbsence is REPORTED, never repaired. Writing into someone's repository because\nthey ran a read-only status command would be a worse surprise than the one this\ndiagnoses.\n\nTwo wrong turns on the way, both worth recording. The line first went into\nrenderBrainOnboardingStatus, which is not the renderer `status` uses -- there\nare two, and the live one is in status_render.go. Then it still never fired,\nbecause the check read opts.Env.RepoRoot, which is empty on the ordinary status\npath; report.Repo.Root is the resolved root. Reverting to the empty one drops\nthe warning to zero occurrences on a repository that is demonstrably unwired,\nwhich is how that was confirmed rather than assumed.\n\nThe docs still need the `init-agents` step added. This makes the omission\nvisible instead of silent in the meantime.\nMSGEOF\ngit add -A\ngit commit -q -F /Users/suhaan/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp/mwired.txt 2>&1|tail -2\ngit push -q origin HEAD:fix/agent-guide-directive-and-discovery 2>&1|tail -1\necho \"pushed: $(git rev-parse --short HEAD)\"","description":"Commit the unwired-agents warning","timeout":1800000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":337,"cache_read_input_tokens":921888,"output_tokens":1008,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":337},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1008,"cache_read_input_tokens":921888,"cache_creation_input_tokens":337,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":337,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01J2N6HJr62GSnLH6oBEMPmp":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide\ncat > /Users/suhaan/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp/mwired.txt <<'MSGEOF'\nfeat(status): say when no agent has been told this brain exists\n\nA brain nothing reads is the product's worst failure mode, and until now it was\nentirely silent: setup succeeds, every source reports healthy, and no agent ever\nconsults the brain because nothing told it the brain is there. The user\nconcludes the product does not work, and no output disagrees.\n\nThe published guide makes this the DEFAULT path, not an edge case. Overview ->\nSet Up Your Repository teaches `setup` then `status` and never mentions\n`init-agents`; only the Agent Prompt tab includes it. Anyone following the CLI\ninstructions ends up here.\n\n`status` now leads its Onboarding block with:\n\n  agents    x not wired — run `entire-brain init-agents` so your agent uses this brain\n              missing: .entire/agent-guide.md, AGENTS.md or CLAUDE.md\n\nand the line disappears once init-agents has run. It is first in the block on\npurpose: it decides whether any other line is ever acted on.\n\nAgentsWired is read-only and cheap -- the guide must exist, and at least one of\nAGENTS.md / CLAUDE.md must carry the managed pointer. One is enough: the two are\ndocumented aliases and a repository may keep only the one its agent reads. A\nfile carrying the user's own text but not the managed block does not count.\n\nAbsence is REPORTED, never repaired. Writing into someone's repository because\nthey ran a read-only status command would be a worse surprise than the one this\ndiagnoses.\n\nTwo wrong turns on the way, both worth recording. The line first went into\nrenderBrainOnboardingStatus, which is not the renderer `status` uses -- there\nare two, and the live one is in status_render.go. Then it still never fired,\nbecause the check read opts.Env.RepoRoot, which is empty on the ordinary status\npath; report.Repo.Root is the resolved root. Reverting to the empty one drops\nthe warning to zero occurrences on a repository that is demonstrably unwired,\nwhich is how that was confirmed rather than assumed.\n\nThe docs still need the `init-agents` step added. This makes the omission\nvisible instead of silent in the meantime.\nMSGEOF\ngit add -A\ngit commit -q -F /Users/suhaan/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp/mwired.txt 2>&1|tail -2\ngit push -q origin HEAD:fix/agent-guide-directive-and-discovery 2>&1|tail -1\necho \"pushed: $(git rev-parse --short HEAD)\"","description":"Commit the unwired-agents warning","timeout":1800000}},"serverClassifierRequest":"7aaa4f45-62a2-453b-b3d9-ffcc7e864f64","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfhuH8iNkiE8iobYW1C6C","type":"assistant","uuid":"6c1ec7d0-4bcb-4b48-bb2c-86f162805162","timestamp":"2026-10-04T21:25:03.288Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
