{"parentUuid":"f84cb602-6c11-4b41-bad6-8f6c8870d28a","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"c71dbf21-2278-4694-a02b-5a0b5a0230e7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XYfxtQgu7P7s7BaZheGaJM","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Claude Code \"mods\" feature\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Mods overview - Claude Code Docs\",\"url\":\"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/plugins/mods/overview\"},{\"title\":\"Customize Claude Code with mods in TypeScript\",\"url\":\"https://claude.com/blog/claude-code-mods\"},{\"title\":\"\\\"No reason why everyone should have an identical Claude experience\\\": Anthropic's mods let you change Claude Code's look and behavior - The New Stack\",\"url\":\"https://thenewstack.io/anthropic-claude-code-mods-plugins/\"},{\"title\":\"Claude Code's new Mods system lets developers rewrite the AI coding tool from the inside\",\"url\":\"https://the-decoder.com/claude-codes-new-mods-system-lets-developers-rewrite-the-ai-coding-tool-from-the-inside/\"},{\"title\":\"How to Install and Build Claude Code Mods: A Setup Guide\",\"url\":\"https://www.mindstudio.ai/blog/claude-code-mods-how-to\"},{\"title\":\"Getting started with Claude Code mods / claude.dev Blog\",\"url\":\"https://claude.dev/blog/getting-started-with-claude-code-mods/\"},{\"title\":\"Claude Code mods: How to Install, Create, Differences from Hooks, and Supported Environments - SmartScope\",\"url\":\"https://smartscope.blog/en/blog/claude-code-mods-how-to-install-create-2026/\"},{\"title\":\"Claude Code Mods: What They Can Do and What They Can Reach\",\"url\":\"https://cellcog.ai/blog/claude-code-mods/\"},{\"title\":\"Claude Code mods: what they are and how to use them\",\"url\":\"https://newfacedesign.com/blog/claude-code-mods\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what the Claude Code \"mods\" feature is:\n\n## Overview\n\nA mod is a plugin that changes how Claude Code looks and behaves, made of JavaScript or TypeScript event handlers that Claude Code calls when an event happens, such as a tool call, a submitted prompt, or a part of the interface being drawn.\n\n## What Mods Can Do\n\nMods can draw an interface you can use (a pane beside the transcript or a band above the prompt with tabs, buttons, and text fields), redraw Claude Code's own interface by replacing or restyling parts Claude Code draws itself, step into a tool call or a request, and run your own code on a command (/command) that runs your function with no Claude turn.\n\n## How to Get Started\n\nYou can write a mod yourself, or ask Claude Code to write one for you, and mods ship inside plugins, so you install and share them like any plugin. They work in the Claude Code CLI and desktop app.\n\n## Built-in Examples\n\nSome built-in features of Claude Code now ship as mods, for example, the built-in /diff feature is now a mod, so you can turn it off or replace it with your own version.\n\n## Security Consideration\n\nMods run with the same access to your machine as Claude Code itself.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"cfbed428-4a48-40db-ada4-d997474dbbdb","timestamp":"2026-10-04T21:35:53.364Z","toolUseResult":{"query":"Claude Code \"mods\" feature","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01FjF25JSJbSSgd4hG3zAqnK","content":[{"title":"Mods overview - Claude Code Docs","url":"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/plugins/mods/overview"},{"title":"Customize Claude Code with mods in TypeScript","url":"https://claude.com/blog/claude-code-mods"},{"title":"\"No reason why everyone should have an identical Claude experience\": Anthropic's mods let you change Claude Code's look and behavior - The New Stack","url":"https://thenewstack.io/anthropic-claude-code-mods-plugins/"},{"title":"Claude Code's new Mods system lets developers rewrite the AI coding tool from the inside","url":"https://the-decoder.com/claude-codes-new-mods-system-lets-developers-rewrite-the-ai-coding-tool-from-the-inside/"},{"title":"How to Install and Build Claude Code Mods: A Setup Guide","url":"https://www.mindstudio.ai/blog/claude-code-mods-how-to"},{"title":"Getting started with Claude Code mods / claude.dev Blog","url":"https://claude.dev/blog/getting-started-with-claude-code-mods/"},{"title":"Claude Code mods: How to Install, Create, Differences from Hooks, and Supported Environments - SmartScope","url":"https://smartscope.blog/en/blog/claude-code-mods-how-to-install-create-2026/"},{"title":"Claude Code Mods: What They Can Do and What They Can Reach","url":"https://cellcog.ai/blog/claude-code-mods/"},{"title":"Claude Code mods: what they are and how to use them","url":"https://newfacedesign.com/blog/claude-code-mods"}]},"Based on the search results, here's what the Claude Code \"mods\" feature is:\n\n## Overview\n\nA mod is a plugin that changes how Claude Code looks and behaves, made of JavaScript or TypeScript event handlers that Claude Code calls when an event happens, such as a tool call, a submitted prompt, or a part of the interface being drawn.\n\n## What Mods Can Do\n\nMods can draw an interface you can use (a pane beside the transcript or a band above the prompt with tabs, buttons, and text fields), redraw Claude Code's own interface by replacing or restyling parts Claude Code draws itself, step into a tool call or a request, and run your own code on a command (/command) that runs your function with no Claude turn.\n\n## How to Get Started\n\nYou can write a mod yourself, or ask Claude Code to write one for you, and mods ship inside plugins, so you install and share them like any plugin. They work in the Claude Code CLI and desktop app.\n\n## Built-in Examples\n\nSome built-in features of Claude Code now ship as mods, for example, the built-in /diff feature is now a mod, so you can turn it off or replace it with your own version.\n\n## Security Consideration\n\nMods run with the same access to your machine as Claude Code itself."],"durationSeconds":6.