{"parentUuid":"ce0f5b11-c802-4e9c-bb91-7f9722e2a9b9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cfhv8vmvaWnFHBy715gkh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9097,"cache_read_input_tokens":934145,"output_tokens":1809,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":924},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":9097},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1809,"cache_read_input_tokens":934145,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9097,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":9097,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":12751,"serverClassifierRequest":"5b776c6e-3ee0-4d41-958a-80549314518e","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cfhv8vDvgB2PHfjGxBXnp","type":"assistant","uuid":"3b6dcead-e511-4707-aa1c-f6f5e348ece5","timestamp":"2026-10-04T21:36:14.336Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"3b6dcead-e511-4707-aa1c-f6f5e348ece5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cfhv8vmvaWnFHBy715gkh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I can give you real ones. Mods run *inside* Claude Code — they can draw a pane beside the transcript, a band above the prompt, intercept tool calls, and run `/commands` with **no Claude turn** (zero tokens).\n\n## 1. Memory pane — show what brain actually contributed\n\nRight now brain's value is invisible. Facts get injected, the agent uses them or doesn't, and you never see it. A pane beside the transcript listing *which facts and symbols were pulled this turn, and which ones Claude actually referenced*.\n\nThat's your roadmap's **\"memory tab — visualisation (v0)\"**, and it's the first time the product would show its own worth instead of asserting it.\n\n## 2. A band that makes today's three failure modes impossible to miss\n\nOne line above the prompt: freshness, **agents-unwired**, and **branch mismatch** (\"12 facts here, 0 on this branch\"). All three are things I fixed this session by adding text to `status` — which nobody runs. A band is always there.\n\n`$.ui.invalidate('ui.render')` on each turn keeps it live.\n\n## 3. `/why <symbol>` — instant, zero tokens\n\nMod commands run your function directly with **no Claude turn**. So `/why DeployWindow` returns brain's answer and history in a pane, costing nothing, even while Claude is working. Memory lookup stops competing with the model for context budget.\n\n## 4. The one I'd actually build: make grep *be* brain\n\nA mod can **hold a tool call and answer it without running the tool.** So intercept `Grep`/`Glob`, run brain's semantic search, and return that.\n\nThis matters because of something I measured: the graph is a ~1:1 substitute for grep, and the token win lives in the **42% of sessions that never substitute** — because the agent has to *choose* to. A mod removes the choice. \"Agents should use Brain\" becomes \"grep is Brain.\"\n\nSettings hooks can't do this; they can only block or log. A mod can answer.\n\n---\n\n**Caveat worth stating:** mods aren't sandboxed and run with your permissions, so a brain mod that intercepts tool calls is a real trust surface — fine for a first-party plugin, worth saying out loud before shipping one.\n\nIf you want one today, I'd build **#2** — it's small, it's the visible half of three fixes already in #331, and it needs no model calls.\n\n**Sources:** [Mods overview](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/plugins/mods/overview) · [Customize Claude Code with mods](https://claude.com/blog/claude-code-mods) · [sample mods](https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code-playground/tree/main/claude-code/mods)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9097,"cache_read_input_tokens":934145,"output_tokens":1809,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":924},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":9097},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1809,"cache_read_input_tokens":934145,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9097,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":9097,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"5b776c6e-3ee0-4d41-958a-80549314518e","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cfhv8vDvgB2PHfjGxBXnp","type":"assistant","uuid":"e8198a72-6fd5-43b3-8e66-1c0ad5e5a73f","timestamp":"2026-10-04T21:36:25.348Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionI