ONLY)\",\n      \"line\": 1,\n      \"text\": \"# Working-tree overlay seam: treating the semantic index as a stale baseline a coding agent patches at read time (DESIGN ONLY)\\n\\n## What this is\\n\\nThe semantic index is a batch artifact built at a commit (`semantic/generations/\\u003ccommit\\u003e-\\u003ctree\\u003e/semantic.sqlite`).\\nA coding agent's job is to *change code*, so the index is **always stale relative to the working tree** —\\non a live branch `entire brain status` reports `freshness: unsafe` the moment the agent edits a file, and\\na full reindex is too slow to run between tool calls. Today the read surfaces resolve symbols against the\\nindex (`semanticSymbolsForFiles` → `findSemanticSymbolsForFilesSQLite` in `internal/cli/semantic.go`), so a\\nfact's locus, an impact traversal, or `inspect changes` can be answered against code that no longer matches\\ndisk.\\n\\nTh","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"aa29ddd9-f98c-42d8-aba9-930d19de8906","timestamp":"2026-10-04T21:42:21.145Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"brain bin: /Users/suhaan/.local/share/entire/plugins/bin/entire-brain\n=== a query that should MISS ===\n{\n  \"branch\": \"main\",\n  \"query\": \"zzqq nonexistent topic that cannot match anything\",\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"source\": \"doc\",\n      \"id\": \"doc:13373c35a78f\",\n      \"path\": \"seed/docs/docs/release_readiness_audit.md\",\n      \"heading\": \"Release Narrative\",\n      \"line\": 343,\n      \"text\": \"Fixture-backed contract coverage: `TestQMDAliasesAcrossRetrievalVerbs` exercises\\nthe supported local surface across `search`, `query`, `vsearch`, `get`, and\\n`multi-get`, including `--format json`, `-n` / `--number`, JSON result shapes,\\nresolved-branch reporting, and missing-id reporting.\\n`TestQMDBranchOverrideAcrossRetrievalVerbs` pins branch override behavior across\\nall five verbs, including wrong-branch misses. `TestQMDLimitAliasesAndPrecedence`\\npins positive `--limit` handling plus mixed `--limit`/`-n` ordering.\\n`TestQMDHelpContractsForRetrievalVerbs` and\\n`TestQMDTopLevelHelpListsRetrievalVerbs` pin the help surface for supported\\nverbs and aliases, while\\n`TestQMDFormatCLIOverridesJSONAndReportsMissingIDs` pins human-readable output\\nand missing-id behavior. `TestQMDUnsupportedFormatRejectedAcrossRetrievalVerbs`\\nfails every supported retrieval verb on unsupported formats, so `csv`,\n=== a query that should HIT ===\n{\n  \"branch\": \"main\",\n  \"query\": \"semantic index\",\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"source\": \"doc\",\n      \"id\": \"doc:116ce0b55235\",\n      \"path\": \"seed/docs/docs/worktree_overlay_seam.md\",\n      \"heading\": \"Working-tree overlay seam: treating the semantic index as a stale baseline a coding agent patches at read time (DESIGN ONLY)\",\n      \"line\": 1,\n      \"text\": \"# Working-tree overlay seam: treating the semantic index as a stale baseline a coding agent patches at read time (DESIGN ONLY)\\n\\n## What this is\\n\\nThe semantic index is a batch artifact built at a commit (`semantic/generations/\\u003ccommit\\u003e-\\u003ctree\\u003e/semantic.sqlite`).\\nA coding agent's job is to *change code*, so the index is **always stale relative to the working tree** —\\non a live branch `entire brain status` reports `freshness: unsafe` the moment the agent edits a file, and\\na full reindex is too slow to run between tool calls. Today the read surfaces resolve symbols against the\\nindex (`semanticSymbolsForFiles` → `findSemanticSymbolsForFilesSQLite` in `internal/cli/semantic.go`), so a\\nfact's locus, an impact traversal, or `inspect changes` can be answered against code that no longer matches\\ndisk.\\n\\nTh","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"d291a88c-cfb6-4a9d-8f38-2f08b31b3637","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/mods/brain-memory","root":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":fa