\\\\nlonger have to arrange directories. These are still required, and `install.sh`\\\\\\\\nchecks all of them before it builds anything, reporting every missing one in a\\\\\\\\nsingle pass with the fix for each:\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- the Entire CLI, on `PATH` as `entire`\\\\\\\\n- Git\\\\\\\\n- a Go toolchain, 1.27 or newer, for `entire-brain`\\\\\\\\n- a cgo-capable C compiler for `entire-graph`, which uses tree-sitter native\\\\\\\\n  parser bindings — `xcode-select --install` on macOS, `build-essential` on\\\\\\\\n  Debian/Ubuntu. `entire-brain` itself is a pure-Go build and does not need cgo.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nNothing about a *repository* is a prerequisite of this install. What a repository\\\\\\\\nneeds before `entire brain setup` — and what it does not — is\\\\\\\\n[step 3a](#3a-what-setup-needs-first-and-what-it-does-not).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**What it does to your machine.** Four things, and nothing else:\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n1. builds `entire-graph` and registers it with the Entire CLI\\\\\\\\n   (`entire plugin install`),\\\\\\\\n2. builds `entire-brain` and registers it the same way,\\\\\\\\n3. writes the default `entire-brain` plugi\"\n}","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"d93207dc-881b-48dc-9107-3e4457dd1618","timestamp":"2026-10-04T21:47:37.570Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"  ❯ ./register.js calls: $.fs.write\n\n✔ Validation passed with warnings\nDONE\n=== captured shape ===\n{\n  \"tool\": \"Bash\",\n  \"eventKeys\": [\n    \"command\",\n    \"description\",\n    \"tool\",\n    \"tool_use_id\"\n  ],\n  \"resultKeys\": [\n    \"ref\",\n    \"result\",\n    \"text\"\n  ],\n  \"resultTypes\": {\n    \"ref\": \"number\",\n    \"result\": \"object\",\n    \"text\": \"string\"\n  },\n  \"innerKeys\": [\n    \"stdout\",\n    \"stderr\",\n    \"interrupted\",\n    \"isImage\",\n    \"returnCodeInterpretation\",\n    \"noOutputExpected\",\n    \"backgroundTaskId\",\n    \"backgroundedByUser\",\n    \"backgroundedByTurnAbort\",\n    \"backgroundedToDeliverMessage\",\n    \"time