{"parentUuid":"7cdb080a-b221-4d9c-b58d-9f6ed0e84421","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfhwSitfYhanKRZHD2kdg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1136,"cache_read_input_tokens":238026,"output_tokens":1481,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":159},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1136},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1481,"cache_read_input_tokens":238026,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1136,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1136,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":2234,"serverClassifierRequest":"149c0c5b-0487-4f51-921f-f3478bb44551","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfhwSiSPbG1dhXsVRTBaL","type":"assistant","uuid":"56551d91-fd66-4aeb-beb4-830355addf86","timestamp":"2026-10-04T21:53:11.683Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-installed","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"56551d91-fd66-4aeb-beb4-830355addf86","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfhwSitfYhanKRZHD2kdg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01H5p9g2U2yMgcK7WQkt4cGK","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/mods/brain-memory/README.md","content":"# brain-memory\n\nA Claude Code mod that shows what Entire Brain actually contributed to each turn —\nand, more usefully, when it came back **empty** and why.\n\nBrain's value is invisible today. Facts get retrieved, the agent uses them or doesn't,\nand nobody sees either. The expensive case is the empty answer: an empty result nobody\nnotices is how a brain quietly stops being consulted while everyone still believes it works.\n\n## Use it\n\n```\n/brain-memory      opens the pane\n```\n\nEach row is one brain call, grouped by turn:\n\n```\nBrain memory   3 answered   2 empty\n\nthis turn ─────────────────────────────────\n+ query    semantic index lock      (10 results)\n· search   zzqqxx                   (nothing matched)\n    note: facts last distilled 2026-10-03 and all captured sessions are distilled\nturn 4 ────────────────────────────────────\n· get      fact:0000000000000000    (1 not found)\n```\n\n`+` answered · `·` empty · `!` the call failed or was refused.\n\nThe yellow line under an empty row is brain's own `blind_spot` — brain already explains\nwhy it had nothing, and that explanation is otherwise buried in a JSON payload no human\nreads. Empty and failed calls are also announced in the transcript, so they're noticed\nwith the pane closed. The spinner carries a running count.\n\nBoth routes count: the MCP tools (`mcp__entire-brain__*`) and the CLI through Bash\n(`entire brain …`, `entire-brain …`). The mod only observes — a tool result reaches\nClaude exactly as the tool returned it, pinned by a test.\n\n## Install\n\nAlready wired via `env.CLAUDE_CODE_PLUGIN_DIRS` in `~/.claude/settings.json`. To remove it,\ndelete that key. For one session instead:\n\n```\nclaude --plugin-dir /Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/mods/brain-memory\n```\n\nThe bare `CLAUDE_CODE_PLUGIN_DIRS` process environment variable did **not** load the mod in\na `claude -p` run here; the `settings.json` entry did. Use the settings entry.\n\n## Develop\n\n```\nclaude plugin validate .\nclaude plugin test\n```\n\n## Two things that only showed up by running it\n\nA green suite and a passing `validate` both covered code that was broken in a live session.\nWorth knowing before changing `payloadTextOf` or `summarize`:\n\n1. **The payload is nested, differently per route.** The test kit documents a `tool.call`\n   stub of `{ result: '<text>' }`, and neither route produces that:\n\n   ```\n   Bash: { ref, result: { stdout: '<brain JSON>', stderr, persistedOutputPath, … }, text }\n   MCP:  { ref, result: [ { type: 'text', text: '<brain JSON>' } ], text }\n   ```\n\n   Reading `result.result` as the payload parses the *wrapper*, finds no `results` field,\n   and scores every empty answer as a hit — the exact failure this mod exists to surface.\n\n2. **Brain payloads get truncated.** One real `entire brain query` here is 39 KB over 103\n   lines; the hook saw 80. Truncated JSON doesn't parse, and falling back to a line count\n   turns every truncated answer into a hit. So the mod reads `persistedOutputPath` when\n   Claude Code kept the full output, and otherwise classifies from the array's opening\n   (`\"results\": [` followed by `]` or `{`), which truncation never reaches.\n\nTests cover both with the envelopes captured from a running session. Every guard in the\nsuite has been verified by weakening — patch it compile-clean, watch the test go red.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1136,"cache_read_input_tokens":238026,"output_tokens":1481,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":159},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1136},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1481,"cache_read_input_tokens":238026,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1136,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1136,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01H5p9g2U2yMgcK7WQkt4cGK":{"file_path":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/mods/brain-memory/README.md","content":"# brain-memory\n\nA Claude Code mod that shows what Entire Brain actually contributed to each turn —\nand, more usefully, when it came back **empty** and why.\n\nBrain's value is invisible today. Facts get retrieved, the agent uses them or doesn't,\nand nobody sees either. The expensive case is the empty answer: an empty result nobody\nnotices is how a brain quietly stops being consulted while everyone still believes it works.\n\n## Use it\n\n```\n/brain-memory      opens the pane\n```\n\nEach row is one brain call, grouped by turn:\n\n```\nBrain memory   3 answered   2 empty\n\nthis turn ─────────────────────────────────\n+ query    semantic index lock      (10 results)\n· search   zzqqxx                   (nothing matched)\n    note: facts last distilled 2026-10-03 and all captured sessions are distilled\nturn 4 ────────────────────────────────────\n· get      fact:0000000000000000    (1 not found)\n```\n\n`+` answered · `·` empty · `!` the call failed or was refused.\n\nThe yellow line under an empty row is brain's own `blind_spot` — brain already explains\nwhy it had nothing, and that explanation is otherwise buried in a JSON payload no human\nreads. Empty and failed calls are also announced in the transcript, so they're noticed\nwith the pane closed. The spinner carries a running count.\n\nBoth routes count: the MCP tools (`mcp__entire-brain__*`) and the CLI through Bash\n(`entire brain …`, `entire-brain …`). The mod only observes — a tool result reaches\nClaude exactly as the tool returned it, pinned by a test.\n\n## Install\n\nAlready wired via `env.CLAUDE_CODE_PLUGIN_DIRS` in `~/.claude/settings.json`. To remove it,\ndelete that key. For one session instead:\n\n```\nclaude --plugin-dir /Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/mods/brain-memory\n```\n\nThe bare `CLAUDE_CODE_PLUGIN_DIRS` process environment variable did **not** load the mod in\na `claude -p` run here; the `settings.json` entry did. Use the settings entry.\n\n## Develop\n\n```\nclaude plugin validate .\nclaude plugin test\n```\n\n## Two things that only showed up by running it\n\nA green suite and a passing `validate` both covered code that was broken in a live session.\nWorth knowing before changing `payloadTextOf` or `summarize`:\n\n1. **The payload is nested, differently per route.** The test kit documents a `tool.call`\n   stub of `{ result: '<text>' }`, and neither route produces that:\n\n   ```\n   Bash: { ref, result: { stdout: '<brain JSON>', stderr, persistedOutputPath, … }, text }\n   MCP:  { ref, result: [ { type: 'text', text: '<brain JSON>' } ], text }\n   ```\n\n   Reading `result.result` as the payload parses the *wrapper*, finds no `results` field,\n   and scores every empty answer as a hit — the exact failure this mod exists to surface.\n\n2. **Brain payloads get truncated.** One real `entire brain query` here is 39 KB over 103\n   lines; the hook saw 80. Truncated JSON doesn't parse, and falling back to a line count\n   turns every truncated answer into a hit. So the mod reads `persistedOutputPath` when\n   Claude Code kept the full output, and otherwise classifies from the array's opening\n   (`\"results\": [` followed by `]` or `{`), which truncation never reaches.\n\nTests cover both with the envelopes captured from a running session. Every guard in the\nsuite has been verified by weakening — patch it compile-clean, watch the test go red.\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"149c0c5b-0487-4f51-921f-f3478bb44551","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfhwSiSPbG1dhXsVRTBaL","type":"assistant","uuid":"819e26bf-0b98-43d3-b27a-82c2364dc0ac","timestamp":"2026-10-04T21:53:25.631Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-installed","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"819e26bf-0b98-43d3-b27a-82c2364dc0ac","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"5c5a12e9-b219-4b59-9c91-bf4367c8ecdf","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01H5p9g2U2yMgcK7WQkt4cGK","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/mods/brain-memory/README.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"ab968ec6-4a66-469a-99b0-34a168a8533b","timestamp":"2026-10-04T21:53:25.981Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/mods/brain-memory/README.md","content":"# brain-memory\n\nA Claude Code mod that shows what Entire Brain actually contributed to each turn —\nand, more usefully, when it came back **empty** and why.\n\nBrain's value is invisible today. Facts get retrieved, the agent uses them or doesn't,\nand nobody sees either. The expensive case is the empty answer: an empty result nobody\nnotices is how a brain quietly stops being consulted while everyone still believes it works.\n\n## Use it\n\n```\n/brain-memory      opens the pane\n```\n\nEach row is one brain call, grouped by turn:\n\n```\nBrain memory   3 answered   2 empty\n\nthis turn ─────────────────────────────────\n+ query    semantic index lock      (10 results)\n· search   zzqqxx                   (nothing matched)\n    note: facts last distilled 2026-10-03 and all captured sessions are distilled\nturn 4 ────────────────────────────────────\n· get      fact:0000000000000000    (1 not found)\n```\n\n`+` answered · `·` empty · `!` the call failed or was refused.\n\nThe yellow line under an empty row is brain's own `blind_spot` — brain already explains\nwhy it had nothing, and that explanation is otherwise buried in a JSON payload no human\nreads. Empty and failed calls are also announced in the transcript, so they're noticed\nwith the pane closed. The spinner carries a running count.\n\nBoth routes count: the MCP tools (`mcp__entire-brain__*`) and the CLI through Bash\n(`entire brain …`, `entire-brain …`). The mod only observes — a tool result reaches\nClaude exactly as the tool returned it, pinned by a test.\n\n## Install\n\nAlready wired via `env.CLAUDE_CODE_PLUGIN_DIRS` in `~/.claude/settings.json`. To remove it,\ndelete that key. For one session instead:\n\n```\nclaude --plugin-dir /Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/mods/brain-memory\n```\n\nThe bare `CLAUDE_CODE_PLUGIN_DIRS` process environment variable did **not** load the mod in\na `claude -p` run here; the `settings.json` entry did. Use the settings entry.\n\n## Develop\n\n```\nclaude plugin validate .\nclaude plugin test\n```\n\n## Two things that only showed up by running it\n\nA green suite and a passing `validate` both covered code that was broken in a live session.\nWorth knowing before changing `payloadTextOf` or `summarize`:\n\n1. **The payload is nested, differently per route.** The test kit documents a `tool.call`\n   stub of `{ result: '<text>' }`, and neither route produces that:\n\n   ```\n   Bash: { ref, result: { stdout: '<brain JSON>', stderr, persistedOutputPath, … }, text }\n   MCP:  { ref, result: [ { type: 'text', text: '<brain JSON>' } ], text }\n   ```\n\n   Reading `result.result` as the payload parses the *wrapper*, finds no `results` field,\n   and scores every empty answer as a hit — the exact failure this mod exists to surface.\n\n2. **Brain payloads get truncated.** One real `entire brain query` here is 39 KB over 103\n   lines; the hook saw 80. Truncated JSON doesn't parse, and falling back to a line count\n   turns every truncated answer into a hit. So the mod reads `persistedOutputPath` when\n   Claude Code kept the full output, and otherwise classifies from the array's opening\n   (`\"results\": [` followed by `]` or `{`), which truncation never reaches.\n\nTests cover both with the envelopes captured from a running session. Every guard in the\nsuite has been verified by weakening — patch it compile-clean, watch the test go red.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"149c0c5b-0487-4f51-921f-f3478bb44551","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-installed","root":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-installed","branch":"HEAD","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"entireio","host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"},{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-graph","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/entiredb","visibility":"private"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/cli","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/entire.io","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-installed","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"819e26bf-0b98-43d3-b27a-82c2364dc0ac","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-installed","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"ab968ec6-4a66-469a-99b0-34a168a8533b","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14735691 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"961f6457-a879-4c71-a200-fd225525284a","timestamp":"2026-10-04T21:53:26.006Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14735691 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-installed","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"961f6457-a879-4c71-a200-fd225525284a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfhwU2corD8x3f8fLhy2s","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The mod is built, verified live, and installed.\n\n**Activate it here: run `/reload-plugins`, then `/brain-memory`.** If the pane doesn't appear, a fresh `claude` session will definitely have it — the settings entry is in place.\n\n## What it does\n\nA pane listing every brain call grouped by turn — `+` answered, `·` empty, `!` failed — with the query, the row count, and, under each empty one, brain's own `blind_spot` note in yellow. That note already exists; it's just buried in a JSON payload nobody reads. Empty and failed calls also get a dim transcript line, so they're noticed with the pane closed, and the spinner carries a running count. Both routes count: MCP tools and `entire brain` through Bash.\n\nIt only observes — a test pins that the tool result reaches Claude byte-identical.\n\n## Two bugs that only appeared when I ran it\n\n`claude plugin validate` passed and 9/9 tests passed on code that was **broken in both real routes**. The test kit documents a `tool.call` stub of `{result: '<text>'}`; neither route produces that:\n\n```\nBash: { ref, result: { stdout: '<brain JSON>', stderr, persistedOutputPath, … }, text }\nMCP:  { ref, result: [ { type: 'text', text: '<brain JSON>' } ], text }\n```\n\nReading `result.result` as the payload parses the *wrapper*, finds no `results` field, and scores **every empty answer as a hit** — precisely the failure the mod exists to surface. Then a live run showed `query` scoring \"80 lines\" instead of \"10 results\": one real brain query here is 39 KB / 103 lines and Claude Code truncates Bash output, so the JSON never parses. It now reads `persistedOutputPath` for the full text, and otherwise classifies from the array's opening, which truncation never reaches.\n\nBoth are covered by tests using envelopes captured from a running session.\n\n## Verification\n\n16 tests pass, and all 12 guards proven by weakening — patched compile-clean, test shown red, restored. Two of my first six weakenings reported zero failures because `\\Q…\\E` made `\\n` literal and the edit never applied; redone in Python. Live, against a real brain:\n\n```\n[empty] search  zzqqxx                 (nothing matched)  note: facts last distilled 2026-10-03…\n[hit  ] query   semantic index         (10 results)\n[empty] get     fact:0000000000000000  (1 not found)\n```\n\n## Files and the one config change\n\n`/Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/mods/brain-memory/` — `hooks/register.js`, `tests/brain-memory.test.ts`, `README.md`.\n\nI added exactly one line to `~/.claude/settings.json` (backup at `~/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp/settings.json.bak`):\n\n```json\n\"CLAUDE_CODE_PLUGIN_DIRS\": \"/Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/mods/brain-memory\"\n```\n\nDelete that key to uninstall. Note the bare process env var did **not** load a mod in `claude -p` — only the settings entry did.\n\nStill untouched and waiting on you: the six brain PRs (#318, #320, #321, #329, #330, #331, with #331 last), and `devenv/GRAPH-PARTIAL-CLONE-ISSUE.md`, which I haven't filed since that's an outward action on `entireio/entire-graph`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1563,"cache_read_input_tokens":239162,"output_tokens":1154,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1563},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1154,"cache_read_input_tokens":239162,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1563,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1563,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"989b674e-90b2-4f50-9e0d-fc83335f983b","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfhwU2AWoCg2H687ssgxt","type":"assistant","uuid":"91840e8c-7d86-4166-aaf6-576b7a4f4db0","timestamp":"2026-10-04T21:53:40.519Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-installed","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
