served. Mode persists for the whole session until changed or stopped.\\n\\nSix intensity levels:\\n\\n| Level | What change |\\n|-------|-------------|\\n| `lite` | Drop filler/hedging. Sentences stay full. Professional but tight. |\\n| `full` | Default. Drop articles, fragments OK, short synonyms. |\\n| `ultra` | Bare fragments. Abbreviations (DB, auth, fn). Arrows for causality. |\\n| `wenyan-lite` | Classical Chinese register, light compression. |\\n| `wenyan-full` | Maximum 文言文. 80-90% character reduction. |\\n| `wenyan-ultra` | Extreme classical compression. |\\n\\nAuto-clarity rule: caveman drops to normal prose for security warnings, irreversible-action confirmations, multi-step sequences where fragment ambiguity risks misread, and when user repeats a question. Resumes after the clear part.\\n\\n## How to invoke\\n\\n```\\n/caveman              # full mode (default)\\n/caveman lite         # lighter compression\\n/caveman ultra        # extreme compression\\n/caveman wenyan       # classical Chinese\\nstop caveman          # back to normal prose\\n```\\n\\n## Example output\\n\\nQuestion: \\\"Why does my React component re-render?\\\"\\n\\nNormal prose:\\n\\u003e Your component re-renders because you create a new object reference each render. Wrapping it in `useMemo` will fix the issue.\\n\\nCaveman (full):\\n\\u003e New object ref each render. Inline object prop = new ref = re-render. Wrap in `useMemo`.\\n\\nCaveman (ultra):\\n\\u003e Inline obj prop → new ref → re-render. `useMemo`.\\n\\n## See also\\n\\n- [`SKILL.md`](./SKILL.md) — full LLM-facing instructions\\n- [Caveman README](../../README.md) — repo overview, install, benchmarks\",\n      \"excerpt\": \"# caveman Talk like smart caveman. Same brain, fewer tokens. ## What it does Compress every model response to caveman-style prose. Drops articles, filler, pleasantries, and hedging. Keeps every technical detail, code block, error string, and symbol exact. Cuts ~65-75% of output tokens with full accuracy preserved. Mode persists for the whole session until changed or stopped. Six intensity levels: | Level | What change | |-------|-------------| | `lite` | Drop filler/hedging. Sentences stay full. Professional but tight. | | `full` | Default. Drop articles, fragments OK, short synonyms. | | `ult...\",\n      \"score\": 0.016129032258064516\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"doc\",\n      \"id\": \"doc:c77cc7a43ba8\",\n      \"path\": \"seed/docs/experts-local-demo/README.md\",\n      \"heading\": \"`entire experts` Local Demo\",\n      \"line\": 1,\n      \"text\": \"# `entire experts` Local Demo\\n\\nEnd-to-end local demo for `entire experts` against a synthetic **entire-api**\\ncell with realistic multi-agent provenance — no production data required.\\n\\nWhat it does:\\n\\n- starts Postgres in Docker (`:5436`)\\n- migrates + seeds **5 agents** (codex, claude, cursor, gemini, copilot) with\\n  checkpoints, facets, and materialised sessions for `entireio/cli`\\n- runs `entire-api/cmd/experts-demo` (mock OAuth core + fake SpiceDB authz)\\n- runs `entire experts cmd/entire/cli/ --repo \\u003cdemo-ulid\\u003e` through the real CLI\\n  auth path (jurisdiction token exchange → cell identity bearer)\\n- writes text + JSON to `output/` and fails on privacy leaks or empty profiles\\n\\n## One-Shot Run\\n\\nRequires Docker, Go, and `entire login` (for the login JWT the mock core\\nexchanges).\\n\\n```bash\\ncd /Users/suhaan/devenv/experts-local-demo\\n./bin/demo.sh\\ncat output/experts.txt\\njq '.profiles | length' output/experts.json   # expect 5\\n```\\n\\n## Manual Run\\n\\nTerminal 1:\\n\\n```bash\\ncd /Users/suhaan/devenv/experts-local-demo\\n./bin/seed-demo-data.sh\\n./bin/start-api.sh\\n```\\n\\nTerminal 2:\\n\\n```bash\\ncd /Users/suhaan/devenv/experts-local-demo\\n./bin/run-cli.sh\\n```\\n\\n## Useful Overrides\\n\\n```bash\\nAPI_PORT=8790 API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8790 ./bin/demo.sh\\nDEMO_SCOPE=cmd/entire/cli/ ./bin/demo.sh\\nKEEP_API=1 KEEP_PG=1 ./bin/demo.sh   # leave API + Postgres running after demo\\n```\\n\\nDefaults:\\n\\n- `API_REPO=../entire-api`\\n- `CLI_REPO=../cli`\\n- `API_PORT=8799` (8787 is often taken by Cloudflare workerd locally)\\n- `DEMO_SCOPE=cmd/entire/cli/`\\n- `DEMO_REPO_ID=41YG9ZSVMMW659YEWTKM8X986W` (stable ULID for the seeded repo;\\n  use this instead of `entireio/cli` so cell routing stays on the local API)\\n\\n## What You Should See\\n\\nText output ranks five agent profiles (Claude, Codex, Cursor, Gemini, Copilot)\\nwith skills, tool mix, MCP servers, matched files under `cmd/entire/cli/`, and\\nsession evidence.\\n\\nJSON output has `\\\"source\\\":\\\"db\\\"` and a non-empty `\\\"profiles\\\"` array. It must not\\ncontain `DO_NOT_LEAK`, raw `\\\"prompt\\\"`, or human author fields.\\n\\n## Auth / Routing Notes\\n\\nThe demo API includes a **mock entire-core** at `/mock-core` that performs RFC\\n8693 token exchange locally. `run-cli.sh` sets:\\n\\n- `ENTIRE_API_BASE_URL` → local demo cell\\n- `ENTIRE_CORE_BASE_URL_TEMPLATE` → mock core (exchange stays local)\\n- `ENTIRE_API_AUDIENCE_TEMPLATE` → local cell URL (aud pin matches demo server)\\n\\nYou still need a real `entire login` session — the mock core reads your login\\nJWT and mints a cell identity token the demo API accepts.\\n\\n```bash\\ncd /Users/suhaan/devenv/cli\\ngo run ./cmd/entire auth status\\ngo run ./cmd/entire login   # if needed\\n```\\n\\nThe CLI uses `--insecure-http-auth` for plain-HTTP local URLs.\",\n      \"excerpt\": \"...tire experts` against a synthetic **entire-api** cell with realistic multi-agent provenance — no production data required. What it does: - starts Postgres in Docker (`:5436`) - migrates + seeds **5 agents** (codex, claude, cursor, gemini, copilot) with checkpoints, facets, and materialised sessions for `entireio/cli` - runs `entire-api/cmd/experts-demo` (mock OAuth core + fake SpiceDB authz) - runs `entire experts cmd/entire/cli/ --repo \\u003cdemo-ulid\\u003e` through the real CLI auth path (jurisdiction token exchange → cell identity bearer) - writes text + JSON to `output/` and fails on privacy lea...\",\n      \"score\": 0.015873015873015872\n    }\n  ]\n}\n"}],"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"099bfaf7-3f6a-4f42-a420-f4aad699c7c4","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","root":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":1,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":243},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-graph","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/entiredb","visibility":"private"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/cli","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/entire.io","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"fc21b699-1982-4e1d-8b0d-52bd6c44e5eb","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
