{"parentUuid":"9cae6781-a692-4f84-8d06-051cc514d6f3","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfhxWQxtL5gjEiB2V8jGW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01S5dbyWMMBYX8o4oYsiyTTf","name":"mcp__entire-brain__brain_search","input":{"query":"why agents do not use the brain tools; agent guide directive"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":850,"cache_read_input_tokens":327861,"output_tokens":917,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":791},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":850},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":917,"cache_read_input_tokens":327861,"cache_creation_input_tokens":850,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":850,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01S5dbyWMMBYX8o4oYsiyTTf":{"query":"why agents do not use the brain tools; agent guide directive"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"3f551b4f-ab3d-4dba-a17e-369eed0978ae","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CfhxWQVreUFmnEd3bYMuU","type":"assistant","uuid":"d82e51ad-ae45-4e44-964c-9a2290c49dbc","timestamp":"2026-10-04T22:07:18.002Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"d82e51ad-ae45-4e44-964c-9a2290c49dbc","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"fd25f374-f99e-4e2a-9ad4-41cb9376e77f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01S5dbyWMMBYX8o4oYsiyTTf","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"branch\": \"main\",\n  \"likely_edit_files\": [\n    \"README.md\"\n  ],\n  \"query\": \"why agents do not use the brain tools; agent guide directive\",\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"source\": \"doc\",\n      \"id\": \"doc:66d502a4957d\",\n      \"path\": \"seed/docs/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-10-entire-graph-opus-30pct-resolution-gateway.md\",\n      \"heading\": \"Anything surprising or fragile\",\n      \"line\": 38,\n      \"text\": \"- Use clean, dedicated worktrees for `entire-graph` and `graphmark`; never benchmark the current dirty GraphMark checkout.\\n- Before paid evaluation, require `go test ./...` in Entire Graph, GraphMark’s Go tests, and zero Python failures in a pinned Python 3.13 environment.\\n- Reconcile the divergent fidelity/fixed-answer artifacts, freeze one canonical manifest, and record every binary, repository, scorer, dataset, prompt, model, effort, and grading-container hash.\\n- Follow the installed graph doctrine: graph-search first, inspect only focused source, then run the nearest test and full compile once.\\n\\n### Anything surprising or fragile\\n\\n- **Observed:** the installed guide omits a search format, while search defaults to JSON; representative JSON was about 45% larger than agent/text output. [agents.go](/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph/internal/cli/agents.go:17)\\n- **Observed:** existing presearch blindly echoes bytes without validating query, tree, version, or options; session replay may return the first payload for a different query. Neither mechanism is acceptable for the gateway. [search.go](/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph/internal/cli/search.go:131)\\n- **Observed:** the GraphMark wrapper advertises `brief` and `show`, which the current canonical CLI does not expose.\\n- **Observed:** nearest predecessors—turn-zero predelivery, call-site packets, composed answers, broader ranking, and VERIFY advice—did not establish behavioral displacement. The new route survives only if source reads fall alongside true-locate work.\\n- **Open hypothesis:** a zero-turn packet must remove roughly half of the exclusive locate-plus-read pool after accounting for packet persistence. That hypothesis is tested before confirmation, not assumed.\\n\\n## Implementation changes\\n\\n### 1. Add a provenance-preserving semantic API\\n\\nIntroduce:\\n\\n`sem.ResolveRepository(ctx, repo, version, task, ResolveOptions) (ResolutionEnvelopeV1, error)`\\n\\nand the thin CLI:\\n\\n`entire graph resolve --repo \\u003cpath\\u003e (--task-file \\u003cpath\\u003e | --query \\u003ctext\\u003e) --format json|agent --max-context-bytes 8192`\\n\\nExisting commands and defaults remain backward-compatible.\\n\\n`ResolutionEnvelopeV1` contains:\\n\\n- `schema` and fingerprint-algorithm versions.\\n- Producer binary, provider, and search-algorithm versions.\\n- Repository key, tree/commit, and `clean | dirty | uncacheable` worktree state/digest.\\n- Normalized-query hash and every effective retrieval/output option.\\n- Orthogonal retrieval status (`ready | low_confidence | miss`) and coverage status (`complete | degraded | unknown`).\\n- Primary locator, true and emitted spans, focus line, source state (`complete | clipped | unavailable`), and body hash.\\n- Provenance-bearing locators: anchor, role, relation, direction, evidence kind/span, and confidence.\\n- Available/emitted counts, truncation reasons, serialized bytes, compact agent payload, and payload hash.\",\n      \"excerpt\": \"...le once. ### Anything surprising or fragile - **Observed:** the installed guide omits a search format, while search defaults to JSON; representative JSON was about 45% larger than agent/text output. [agents.go](/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph/internal/cli/agents.go:17) - **Observed:** existing presearch blindly echoes bytes without validating query, tree, version, or options; session replay may return the first payload for a different query. Neither mechanism is acceptable for the gateway. [search.go](/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph/internal/cli/search.go:131) - **Observed:** the GraphMark...\",\n      \"score\": 0.01639344262295082\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"doc\",\n      \"id\": \"doc:ced9964e8311\",\n      \"path\": \"seed/docs/CLAUDE.md\",\n      \"line\": 101,\n      \"text\": \"- `entire sem diff --base main --head HEAD`       what changed, entity-level\\n\\nKnowledge + context (entire-brain MCP tools, wired globally in `~/.claude.json`):\\n- `brain_search` / `brain_code`   find code + facts by intent\\n- `brain_impact`                  blast radius of a change\\n- `brain_context` / `brain_brief` task-scoped context packet\\n- `brain_query` / `brain_vsearch` hybrid + vector search\\n- `brain_status`                  which sources are live for this repo\\n\\nThis repo has the entire-graph code graph installed. Before exploring code with\\ngrep/find/whole-file reads, read .entire/graph-agent.md — the search-first, verify-once\\ndoctrine for coding agents.\\n@.entire/graph-agent.md\\n\\nIt also has an entire-brain. Graph answers *where the code is*; Brain answers *why it is\\nthat way* — prior decisions, earlier attempts, durable facts. Before asserting any\\nrationale or history, read .entire/agent-guide.md.\\n@.entire/agent-guide.md\",\n      \"excerpt\": \"...this repo This repo has the entire-graph code graph installed. Before exploring code with grep/find/whole-file reads, read .entire/graph-agent.md — the search-first, verify-once doctrine for coding agents. @.entire/graph-agent.md It also has an entire-brain. Graph answers *where the code is*; Brain answers *why it is that way* — prior decisions, earlier attempts, durable facts. Before asserting any rationale or history, read .entire/agent-guide.md. @.entire/agent-guide.md\",\n      \"score\": 0.016129032258064516\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"doc\",\n      \"id\": \"doc:0083dca3b44a\",\n      \"path\": \"seed/docs/.agents/skills/cavecrew/README.md\",\n      \"heading\": \"cavecrew\",\n      \"line\": 1,\n      \"text\": \"# cavecrew\\n\\nDecision guide. When to delegate to caveman subagents instead of doing the work inline.\\n\\n## What it does\\n\\nTells the main thread when to spawn a caveman-style subagent versus the vanilla equivalent. The win: subagent tool-results inject back into main context verbatim, and caveman output is roughly 1/3 the size of vanilla prose. Across 20 delegations in one session, that is the difference between context exhaustion and finishing the task.\\n\\nThree subagents:\\n\\n| Subagent | Job | Use when |\\n|----------|-----|----------|\\n| `cavecrew-investigator` | Locate code (read-only) | \\\"Where is X defined / what calls Y / list uses of Z\\\" |\\n| `cavecrew-builder` | Surgical edit, 1-2 files | Scope is obvious, ≤2 files. Refuses 3+ file scope. |\\n| `cavecrew-reviewer` | Diff/file review | One-line findings with severity emoji |\\n\\nUse vanilla `Explore` or `Code Reviewer` when you want prose, architecture commentary, or rationale. Use main thread directly for one-line answers and 3+ file refactors.\\n\\nThis skill is a decision guide, not a slash command. It activates when the conversation mentions delegation.\\n\\n## How to invoke\\n\\nTriggers on phrases like \\\"delegate to subagent\\\", \\\"use cavecrew\\\", \\\"spawn investigator\\\", \\\"save context\\\", \\\"compressed agent output\\\".\\n\\n## Example chaining\\n\\nLocate → fix → verify (most common):\\n\\n1. `cavecrew-investigator` returns site list (`path:line — symbol — note`)\\n2. Main thread picks 1-2 sites, hands paths to `cavecrew-builder`\\n3. `cavecrew-reviewer` audits the resulting diff\\n\\nParallel scout: spawn 2-3 `cavecrew-investigator` calls in one message with different angles (defs, callers, tests). Aggregate in main.\\n\\n## See also\\n\\n- [`SKILL.md`](./SKILL.md) — full decision matrix and output contracts\\n- [`agents/cavecrew-investigator.md`](../../agents/cavecrew-investigator.md)\\n- [`agents/cavecrew-builder.md`](../../agents/cavecrew-builder.md)\\n- [`agents/cavecrew-reviewer.md`](../../agents/cavecrew-reviewer.md)\\n- [Caveman README](../../README.md) — repo overview\",\n      \"excerpt\": \"# cavecrew Decision guide. When to delegate to caveman subagents instead of doing the work inline. ## What it does Tells the main thread when to spawn a caveman-style subagent versus the vanilla equivalent. The win: subagent tool-results inject back into main context verbatim, and caveman output is roughly 1/3 the size of vanilla prose. Across 20 delegations in one session, that is the difference between context exhaustion and finishing the task. Three subagents: | Subagent | Job | Use when | |----------|-----|----------| | `cavecrew-investigator` | Locate code (read-only) | \\\"Where is X define...\",\n      \"score\": 0.015873015873015872\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"doc\",\n      \"id\": \"doc:a1905a2fb7f3\",\n      \"path\": \"seed/docs/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-10-entire-graph-opus-30pct-resolution-gateway.md\",\n      \"heading\": \"Burned-corpus qualification\",\n      \"line\": 125,\n      \"text\": \"- Test preloader success, timeout/error fail-open, stale-worktree rejection, atomic handoff, and source prompt-injection framing.\\n- Run every pinned fidelity corpus with no symbol/call F1 regression.\\n- Reconcile the current 1,334-versus-1,498 fixed-answer corpus drift; freeze one manifest and require zero per-item regression.\\n\\n### Burned-corpus qualification\\n\\nUse exactly 60 previously exposed ML300 tasks, stratified by language and repository, three repetitions, and all four arms: 720 sessions.\\n\\nProceed only when:\\n\\n- Packet delivery and fingerprint match are 100%; leakage is zero.\\n- Chance-corrected offline addressability covers at least 52% of exclusive locate-plus-read mass.\\n- Both exclusive locate and source-read counts decline.\\n- The upper 95% confidence bound on combined locate-plus-read ratio is ≤0.48.\\n- Let `p` be the measured candidate-only persisted packet/guide token tax as a fraction of baseline tokens. Require the upper 95% API-message ratio to satisfy `M ≤ (0.70 − p)^(1/1.70)`.\\n- Post-edit test/build/verification activity has a lower 95% ratio ≥0.90, preventing savings through abandoned validation.\\n- Error, timeout, empty-patch, and turn-cap rates are each no worse than baseline by more than three points.\\n- Prospective hierarchical simulation predicts ≥90% joint power for the final token and resolution gates. Below 80% stops the route; 80–90% requires a larger untouched manifest before confirmation.\\n\\nPacket correctness or gold-line recall alone never qualifies the candidate.\\n\\n### Confirmatory corpus and scheduling\\n\\nStart with the 141 untouched ML300 tasks. Choose the smallest `N` from `{141, 200, 300, 400, 500, 600, 700, 800}` that reaches ≥90% simulated joint power using the less favorable qualification effect estimate and repository-level variance.\\n\\nIf `N\\u003e141`, fill the reserve from the official 2,294-task SWE-bench pool, excluding every instance ID appearing in local plans, logs, manifests, results, transcript analyses, or previous gold-patch work. Official dataset sizes and harness support are documented by [SWE-bench](https://www.swebench.com/SWE-bench/guides/datasets/).\\n\\nOrder eligible reserve tasks by SHA-256 of `2026-08-10-eg-opus30:\\u003cinstance_id\\u003e`, cap added tasks from any repository at 10%, and require reproducible base commits and grading images. If 800 tasks still provide \\u003c90% predicted power, stop: the chosen claim is not practically verifiable with this design.\\n\\nEach task receives all four arms and three repetitions: `12N` sessions. Use balanced Latin-square arm order inside each task/repetition and interleave sessions in wall-clock time. Operational waves contain at most 50 tasks, but no efficacy summaries are released until all waves finish.\\n\\nAfter the first untouched session, candidate code, prompts, scorer, retry policy, graphs, and manifests are immutable. A revised candidate requires unused replacement tasks and a new preregistration.\\n\\n### Final release gates\",\n      \"excerpt\": \"...mass. - Both exclusive locate and source-read counts decline. - The upper 95% confidence bound on combined locate-plus-read ratio is ≤0.48. - Let `p` be the measured candidate-only persisted packet/guide token tax as a fraction of baseline tokens. Require the upper 95% API-message ratio to satisfy `M ≤ (0.70 − p)^(1/1.70)`. - Post-edit test/build/verification activity has a lower 95% ratio ≥0.90, preventing savings through abandoned validation. - Error, timeout, empty-patch, and turn-cap rates are each no worse than baseline by more than three points. - Prospective hierarchical simulat...\",\n      \"score\": 0.015625\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"doc\",\n      \"id\": \"doc:96210a4e4dfb\",\n      \"path\": \"seed/docs/.claude/mods/brain-memory/README.md\",\n      \"heading\": \"brain-memory\",\n      \"line\": 1,\n      \"text\": \"# brain-memory\\n\\nA Claude Code mod that shows what Entire Brain actually contributed to each turn —\\nand, more usefully, when it came back **empty** and why.\\n\\nBrain's value is invisible today. Facts get retrieved, the agent uses them or doesn't,\\nand nobody sees either. The expensive case is the empty answer: an empty result nobody\\nnotices is how a brain quietly stops being consulted while everyone still believes it works.\\n\\n## Use it\\n\\n```\\n/brain-memory      opens the pane\\n```\\n\\nEach row is one brain call, grouped by turn:\\n\\n```\\nBrain memory   3 answered   2 empty\\n\\nthis turn ─────────────────────────────────\\n+ query    semantic index lock      (10 results)\\n· search   zzqqxx                   (nothing matched)\\n    note: facts last distilled 2026-10-03 and all captured sessions are distilled\\nturn 4 ────────────────────────────────────\\n· get      fact:0000000000000000    (1 not found)\\n```\\n\\n`+` answered · `·` empty · `!` the call failed or was refused.\\n\\nThe yellow line under an empty row is brain's own `blind_spot` — brain already explains\\nwhy it had nothing, and that explanation is otherwise buried in a JSON payload no human\\nreads. Empty and failed calls are also announced in the transcript, so they're noticed\\nwith the pane closed. The spinner carries a running count.\\n\\nBoth routes count: the MCP tools (`mcp__entire-brain__*`) and the CLI through Bash\\n(`entire brain …`, `entire-brain …`). The mod only observes — a tool result reaches\\nClaude exactly as the tool returned it, pinned by a test.\\n\\n## Install\\n\\nAlready wired via `env.CLAUDE_CODE_PLUGIN_DIRS` in `~/.claude/settings.json`. To remove it,\\ndelete that key. For one session instead:\\n\\n```\\nclaude --plugin-dir /Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/mods/brain-memory\\n```\\n\\nThe bare `CLAUDE_CODE_PLUGIN_DIRS` process environment variable did **not** load the mod in\\na `claude -p` run here; the `settings.json` entry did. Use the settings entry.\\n\\n## Develop\\n\\n```\\nclaude plugin validate .\\nclaude plugin test\\n```\\n\\n## Two things that only showed up by running it\\n\\nA green suite and a passing `validate` both covered code that was broken in a live session.\\nWorth knowing before changing `payloadTextOf` or `summarize`:\\n\\n1. **The payload is nested, differently per route.** The test kit documents a `tool.call`\\n   stub of `{ result: '\\u003ctext\\u003e' }`, and neither route produces that:\\n\\n   ```\\n   Bash: { ref, result: { stdout: '\\u003cbrain JSON\\u003e', stderr, persistedOutputPath, … }, text }\\n   MCP:  { ref, result: [ { type: 'text', text: '\\u003cbrain JSON\\u003e' } ], text }\\n   ```\\n\\n   Reading `result.result` as the payload parses the *wrapper*, finds no `results` field,\\n   and scores every empty answer as a hit — the exact failure this mod exists to surface.\\n\\n2. **Brain payloads get truncated.** One real `entire brain query` here is 39 KB over 103\",\n      \"excerpt\": \"# brain-memory A Claude Code mod that shows what Entire Brain actually contributed to each turn — and, more usefully, when it came back **empty** and why. Brain's value is invisible today. Facts get retrieved, the agent uses them or doesn't, and nobody sees either. The expensive case is the empty answer: an empty result nobody notices is how a brain quietly stops being consulted while everyone still believes it works. ## Use it ``` /brain-memory opens the pane ``` Each row is one brain call, grouped by turn: ``` Brain memory 3 answered 2 empty this turn ─────────────...\",\n      \"score\": 0.015384615384615385\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"doc\",\n      \"id\": \"doc:635720c285d6\",\n      \"path\": \"seed/docs/same-content/plug/data/repos/local/repo-fd8a8b5d2a78/README.md\",\n      \"heading\": \"Entire Brain\",\n      \"line\": 1,\n      \"text\": \"# Entire Brain\\n\\nThis brain combines seeded repository context with Entire session history when available.\\n\\n## Session History\\n\\n- Sessions: 0\\n- Checkpoints scanned: 0\\n- `main`: 0 sessions in `sessions/main`\\n\\n## History Index\\n\\n- Generated at: `2026-09-15T20:40:32Z`\\n- Index: `history/generations/aab0ba25dfcbccee5012bedbc223c9085622ff04/index.json`\\n- Records: 0\\n- Decisions: 0\\n- Learnings: 0\\n- Validations: 0\\n- Tool calls: 0\",\n      \"score\": 0.015151515151515152\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"doc\",\n      \"id\": \"doc:0772015f7301\",\n      \"path\": \"seed/docs/v031-probe/data/repos/local/repo-b09c6272e667/README.md\",\n      \"heading\": \"Entire Brain\",\n      \"line\": 1,\n      \"text\": \"# Entire Brain\\n\\nThis brain combines seeded repository context with Entire session history when available.\\n\\n## Seeded Baseline\\n\\n- Generated at: `2026-09-13T15:23:16Z`\\n- Summary: `seed/repo-overview.md`\\n- Documents: 0\\n- Entrypoints: 0\\n- Commands: 0\\n- Historical gap: no session history available (confidence: heuristic)\\n- Commit coverage: 1 total — 0 pre-session, 0 covered, 0 missing session coverage after oldest session, 1 with no session history (`seed/history-gaps.md`)\\n\\n## Session History\\n\\n- Sessions: 0\\n- Checkpoints scanned: 0\\n- `main`: 0 sessions in `sessions/main`\\n\\n## History Index\\n\\n- Generated at: `2026-09-13T15:23:16Z`\\n- Index: `history/generations/d8685a120af2d3e34dd2afd36ea3bab517e636a7/index.json`\\n- Records: 0\\n- Decisions: 0\\n- Learnings: 0\\n- Validations: 0\\n- Tool calls: 0\\n\\n## Semantic Index\\n\\n- Generated at: `2026-09-13T15:23:16Z`\\n- Provider: `entire-graph` `dev`\\n- Schema: `1.1`\\n- Snapshot: `semantic/snapshots/0d64c8fb6b80a40145002c44130f9316dc7e8db6-9c175ba1a9f5a61c/snapshot.ndjson`\\n- Symbols: 2\\n- Relations: 4\\n- Commit: `0d64c8fb6b80a40145002c44130f9316dc7e8db6`\\n- Branch: `main`\\n- Intake: run `entire brain inspect code \\u003csymbol\\u003e --json` then `entire brain inspect context \\u003csymbol\\u003e --json` for task-specific semantic context.\",\n      \"excerpt\": \"# Entire Brain This brain combines seeded repository context with Entire session history when available. ## Seeded Baseline - Generated at: `2026-09-13T15:23:16Z` - Summary: `seed/repo-overview.md` - Documents: 0 - Entrypoints: 0 - Commands: 0 - Historical gap: no session history available (confidence: heuristic) - Commit coverage: 1 total — 0 pre-session, 0 covered, 0 missing session coverage after oldest session, 1 with no session history (`seed/history-gaps.md`) ## Session History - Sessions: 0 - Checkpoints scanned: 0 - `main`: 0 sessions in `sessions/main` ## History Index - Generated a...\",\n      \"score\": 0.014925373134328358\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"doc\",\n      \"id\": \"doc:8b9b3d8433b8\",\n      \"path\": \"seed/docs/v030-probe2/data/repos/local/repo-e87087ab24bf/README.md\",\n      \"heading\": \"Entire Brain\",\n      \"line\": 1,\n      \"text\": \"# Entire Brain\\n\\nThis brain combines seeded repository context with Entire session history when available.\\n\\n## Seeded Baseline\\n\\n- Generated at: `2026-09-13T05:01:43Z`\\n- Summary: `seed/repo-overview.md`\\n- Documents: 0\\n- Entrypoints: 0\\n- Commands: 0\\n- Historical gap: no session history available (confidence: heuristic)\\n- Commit coverage: 1 total — 0 pre-session, 0 covered, 0 missing session coverage after oldest session, 1 with no session history (`seed/history-gaps.md`)\\n\\n## Session History\\n\\n- Sessions: 0\\n- Checkpoints scanned: 0\\n- `main`: 0 sessions in `sessions/main`\\n\\n## History Index\\n\\n- Generated at: `2026-09-13T05:01:43Z`\\n- Index: `history/generations/467c805851423ba518a7bb3309221f825eba1010/index.json`\\n- Records: 0\\n- Decisions: 0\\n- Learnings: 0\\n- Validations: 0\\n- Tool calls: 0\\n\\n## Semantic Index\\n\\n- Generated at: `2026-09-13T05:01:43Z`\\n- Provider: `entire-graph` `dev`\\n- Schema: `1.1`\\n- Snapshot: `semantic/snapshots/373cd6b52bdb5e87312760c5776aae1e3eb81f15-4cac7d85f6d7b7dc/snapshot.ndjson`\\n- Symbols: 1\\n- Relations: 1\\n- Commit: `373cd6b52bdb5e87312760c5776aae1e3eb81f15`\\n- Branch: `main`\\n- Intake: run `entire brain inspect code \\u003csymbol\\u003e --json` then `entire brain inspect context \\u003csymbol\\u003e --json` for task-specific semantic context.\",\n      \"excerpt\": \"# Entire Brain This brain combines seeded repository context with Entire session history when available. ## Seeded Baseline - Generated at: `2026-09-13T05:01:43Z` - Summary: `seed/repo-overview.md` - Documents: 0 - Entrypoints: 0 - Commands: 0 - Historical gap: no session history available (confidence: heuristic) - Commit coverage: 1 total — 0 pre-session, 0 covered, 0 missing session coverage after oldest session, 1 with no session history (`seed/history-gaps.md`) ## Session History - Sessions: 0 - Checkpoints scanned: 0 - `main`: 0 sessions in `sessions/main` ## History Index - Generated a...\",\n      \"score\": 0.014705882352941176\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"doc\",\n      \"id\": \"doc:a75d1bb5e858\",\n      \"path\": \"seed/docs/same-content2/plug/data/repos/local/repo-557e835e8835/README.md\",\n      \"heading\": \"Entire Brain\",\n      \"line\": 1,\n      \"text\": \"# Entire Brain\\n\\nThis brain combines seeded repository context with Entire session history when available.\\n\\n## Seeded Baseline\\n\\n- Generated at: `2026-09-15T20:41:50Z`\\n- Summary: `seed/repo-overview.md`\\n- Documents: 0\\n- Entrypoints: 0\\n- Commands: 0\\n- Historical gap: no session history available (confidence: heuristic)\\n- Commit coverage: 1 total — 0 pre-session, 0 covered, 0 missing session coverage after oldest session, 1 with no session history (`seed/history-gaps.md`)\\n\\n## Session History\\n\\n- Sessions: 0\\n- Checkpoints scanned: 0\\n- `main`: 0 sessions in `sessions/main`\\n\\n## History Index\\n\\n- Generated at: `2026-09-15T20:41:50Z`\\n- Index: `history/generations/d59752ff580f429a794853d908341e1df0bf8c44/index.json`\\n- Records: 0\\n- Decisions: 0\\n- Learnings: 0\\n- Validations: 0\\n- Tool calls: 0\\n\\n## Semantic Index\\n\\n- Generated at: `2026-09-15T20:41:50Z`\\n- Provider: `entire-graph` `dev`\\n- Schema: `1.1`\\n- Snapshot: `semantic/snapshots/641925aa048bd93dca5248cb6351a660fd2c0682-b155c9f90d699764/snapshot.ndjson`\\n- Symbols: 1\\n- Relations: 1\\n- Commit: `641925aa048bd93dca5248cb6351a660fd2c0682`\\n- Branch: `main`\\n- Intake: run `entire brain inspect code \\u003csymbol\\u003e --json` then `entire brain inspect context \\u003csymbol\\u003e --json` for task-specific semantic context.\",\n      \"excerpt\": \"# Entire Brain This brain combines seeded repository context with Entire session history when available. ## Seeded Baseline - Generated at: `2026-09-15T20:41:50Z` - Summary: `seed/repo-overview.md` - Documents: 0 - Entrypoints: 0 - Commands: 0 - Historical gap: no session history available (confidence: heuristic) - Commit coverage: 1 total — 0 pre-session, 0 covered, 0 missing session coverage after oldest session, 1 with no session history (`seed/history-gaps.md`) ## Session History - Sessions: 0 - Checkpoints scanned: 0 - `main`: 0 sessions in `sessions/main` ## History Index - Generated a...\",\n      \"score\": 0.014492753623188406\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"doc\",\n      \"id\": \"doc:71ae73841426\",\n      \"path\": \"seed/docs/CLAUDE.md\",\n      \"heading\": \"Two-agent split (current)\",\n      \"line\": 51,\n      \"text\": \"- **Live verification over assertion.** Run the thing. A claim without a command behind it is a\\n  hypothesis.\\n- **No AI attribution footers in commits.**\\n- **Reproduce-proven-results doctrine:** treat every task as already achieved by someone; \\\"no\\\" or\\n  \\\"impossible\\\" is never a terminal answer — go one layer deeper (transcripts, harness, source).\\n\\n## Two-agent split (current)\\n\\nTwo Claude Code agents run in parallel on this machine and must not collide.\\n\\n| agent | owns | notes file |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| **graph-bench** | entire-graph token benchmarks, graphmark harness, rep30/rep100/300 cells | `graph-bench-results/TokensNotes.md` |\\n| **memory-bench** | memory/recall benchmarks (LOCOMO, prose-memory, cmm parity) | `graph-bench-results/MemoryNotes.md` |\\n\\n**Coordinate through `AGENT-COMMS.md`** (repo root). Read it at the start of a session and before\\ntouching anything the other agent owns. Protocol and message format are defined in that file.\\n\\nShared, do not stomp:\\n- `graphmark/` (entirehq/graphmark; formerly `graphmark-bench/`, which no longer exists) — the benchmark harness. Announce in comms before editing its runner/scorer.\\n- GCP VMs `graphbench-a..d` — claim a VM in comms before launching cells on it.\\n- **Never `scp` a script onto a VM while sessions are running.** Bash reads scripts lazily;\\n  overwriting in place moves bytes under a running shell and corrupts live runs (this destroyed 22\\n  sessions). Deploy to a temp path and atomic `mv`.\\n\\n## Benchmark doctrine (read before quoting any number)\\n\\nFull ledger of what is live and what is struck: **`graph-bench-results/TokensNotes.md`**.\\nMethod drill: the `graph-bench-forensics` skill.\\n\\nNon-negotiables:\\n- **Fairness:** tool *output* differences are legitimate; arm-asymmetric *instructions* are not.\\n  Test — *would this sentence help an arm with no tool?* If yes, both arms or neither.\\n- **Gate:** a pair counts only if both arms `subtype==\\\"success\\\"` AND non-empty patch. Drop\\n  symmetrically.\\n- **Power:** MDE is ~25–26 points at n=30. Never read sub-groups of 3–7 inside one cell. Always\\n  report a bootstrap CI and the median beside the total.\\n- **Never replicate an instance; always add instances.** Run-level noise is ~87% of paired variance.\\n- **Audit the harness before blaming the tool.** Every withdrawn headline here died of a harness\\n  bug. See TokensNotes §5 for the ten silent-failure modes already found.\\n\\n## Code intelligence: query the brain + graph BEFORE grepping\\n\\nEvery main checkout has an Entire brain. Its **code graph** is built for all repos; **durable\\nfacts** where the brain reports them. One graph/brain call beats a grep+read sweep. For \\\"where is /\\nwho calls / what depends on / what does this change break\\\", ask FIRST; grep only as fallback.\\n\\nStructural, deterministic (CLI, any repo, no setup):\\n- `entire sem edges   --repo . --format ndjson`   callers / callees\\n- `entire sem symbols --repo . --format ndjson`   definitions (file:line)\",\n      \"excerpt\": \"...* treat every task as already achieved by someone; \\\"no\\\" or \\\"impossible\\\" is never a terminal answer — go one layer deeper (transcripts, harness, source). ## Two-agent split (current) Two Claude Code agents run in parallel on this machine and must not collide. | agent | owns | notes file | |---|---|---| | **graph-bench** | entire-graph token benchmarks, graphmark harness, rep30/rep100/300 cells | `graph-bench-results/TokensNotes.md` | | **memory-bench** | memory/recall benchmarks (LOCOMO, prose-memory, cmm parity) | `graph-bench-results/MemoryNotes.md` | **Coordinate through `AGENT-COMMS.md`**...\",\n      \"score\": 0.014285714285714285\n    }\n  ]\n}\n"}]}]},"uuid":"9504652a-d4bb-4b9b-9eff-939c084c4ce0","timestamp":"2026-10-04T22:07:18.426Z","toolUseResult":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"branch\": \"main\",\n  \"likely_edit_files\": [\n    \"README.md\"\n  ],\n  \"query\": \"why agents do not use the brain tools; agent guide directive\",\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"source\": \"doc\",\n      \"id\": \"doc:66d502a4957d\",\n      \"path\": \"seed/docs/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-10-entire-graph-opus-30pct-resolution-gateway.md\",\n      \"heading\": \"Anything surprising or fragile\",\n      \"line\": 38,\n      \"text\": \"- Use clean, dedicated worktrees for `entire-graph` and `graphmark`; never benchmark the current dirty GraphMark checkout.\\n- Before paid evaluation, require `go test ./...` in Entire Graph, GraphMark’s Go tests, and zero Python failures in a pinned Python 3.13 environment.\\n- Reconcile the divergent fidelity/fixed-answer artifacts, freeze one canonical manifest, and record every binary, repository, scorer, dataset, prompt, model, effort, and grading-container hash.\\n- Follow the installed graph doctrine: graph-search first, inspect only focused source, then run the nearest test and full compile once.\\n\\n### Anything surprising or fragile\\n\\n- **Observed:** the installed guide omits a search format, while search defaults to JSON; representative JSON was about 45% larger than agent/text output. [agents.go](/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph/internal/cli/agents.go:17)\\n- **Observed:** existing presearch blindly echoes bytes without validating query, tree, version, or options; session replay may return the first payload for a different query. Neither mechanism is acceptable for the gateway. [search.go](/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph/internal/cli/search.go:131)\\n- **Observed:** the GraphMark wrapper advertises `brief` and `show`, which the current canonical CLI does not expose.\\n- **Observed:** nearest predecessors—turn-zero predelivery, call-site packets, composed answers, broader ranking, and VERIFY advice—did not establish behavioral displacement. The new route survives only if source reads fall alongside true-locate work.\\n- **Open hypothesis:** a zero-turn packet must remove roughly half of the exclusive locate-plus-read pool after accounting for packet persistence. That hypothesis is tested before confirmation, not assumed.\\n\\n## Implementation changes\\n\\n### 1. Add a provenance-preserving semantic API\\n\\nIntroduce:\\n\\n`sem.ResolveRepository(ctx, repo, version, task, ResolveOptions) (ResolutionEnvelopeV1, error)`\\n\\nand the thin CLI:\\n\\n`entire graph resolve --repo \\u003cpath\\u003e (--task-file \\u003cpath\\u003e | --query \\u003ctext\\u003e) --format json|agent --max-context-bytes 8192`\\n\\nExisting commands and defaults remain backward-compatible.\\n\\n`ResolutionEnvelopeV1` contains:\\n\\n- `schema` and fingerprint-algorithm versions.\\n- Producer binary, provider, and search-algorithm versions.\\n- Repository key, tree/commit, and `clean | dirty | uncacheable` worktree state/digest.\\n- Normalized-query hash and every effective retrieval/output option.\\n- Orthogonal retrieval status (`ready | low_confidence | miss`) and coverage status (`complete | degraded | unknown`).\\n- Primary locator, true and emitted spans, focus line, source state (`complete | clipped | unavailable`), and body hash.\\n- Provenance-bearing locators: anchor, role, relation, direction, evidence kind/span, and confidence.\\n- Available/emitted counts, truncation reasons, serialized bytes, compact agent payload, and payload hash.\",\n      \"excerpt\": \"...le once. ### Anything surprising or fragile - **Observed:** the installed guide omits a search format, while search defaults to JSON; representative JSON was about 45% larger than agent/text output. [agents.go](/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph/internal/cli/agents.go:17) - **Observed:** existing presearch blindly echoes bytes without validating query, tree, version, or options; session replay may return the first payload for a different query. Neither mechanism is acceptable for the gateway. [search.go](/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph/internal/cli/search.go:131) - **Observed:** the GraphMark...\",\n      \"score\": 0.01639344262295082\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"doc\",\n      \"id\": \"doc:ced9964e8311\",\n      \"path\": \"seed/docs/CLAUDE.md\",\n      \"line\": 101,\n      \"text\": \"- `entire sem diff --base main --head HEAD`       what changed, entity-level\\n\\nKnowledge + context (entire-brain MCP tools, wired globally in `~/.claude.json`):\\n- `brain_search` / `brain_code`   find code + facts by intent\\n- `brain_impact`                  blast radius of a change\\n- `brain_context` / `brain_brief` task-scoped context packet\\n- `brain_query` / `brain_vsearch` hybrid + vector search\\n- `brain_status`                  which sources are live for this repo\\n\\nThis repo has the entire-graph code graph installed. Before exploring code with\\ngrep/find/whole-file reads, read .entire/graph-agent.md — the search-first, verify-once\\ndoctrine for coding agents.\\n@.entire/graph-agent.md\\n\\nIt also has an entire-brain. Graph answers *where the code is*; Brain answers *why it is\\nthat way* — prior decisions, earlier attempts, durable facts. Before asserting any\\nrationale or history, read .entire/agent-guide.md.\\n@.entire/agent-guide.md\",\n      \"excerpt\": \"...this repo This repo has the entire-graph code graph installed. Before exploring code with grep/find/whole-file reads, read .entire/graph-agent.md — the search-first, verify-once doctrine for coding agents. @.entire/graph-agent.md It also has an entire-brain. Graph answers *where the code is*; Brain answers *why it is that way* — prior decisions, earlier attempts, durable facts. Before asserting any rationale or history, read .entire/agent-guide.md. @.entire/agent-guide.md\",\n      \"score\": 0.016129032258064516\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"doc\",\n      \"id\": \"doc:0083dca3b44a\",\n      \"path\": \"seed/docs/.agents/skills/cavecrew/README.md\",\n      \"heading\": \"cavecrew\",\n      \"line\": 1,\n      \"text\": \"# cavecrew\\n\\nDecision guide. When to delegate to caveman subagents instead of doing the work inline.\\n\\n## What it does\\n\\nTells the main thread when to spawn a caveman-style subagent versus the vanilla equivalent. The win: subagent tool-results inject back into main context verbatim, and caveman output is roughly 1/3 the size of vanilla prose. Across 20 delegations in one session, that is the difference between context exhaustion and finishing the task.\\n\\nThree subagents:\\n\\n| Subagent | Job | Use when |\\n|----------|-----|----------|\\n| `cavecrew-investigator` | Locate code (read-only) | \\\"Where is X defined / what calls Y / list uses of Z\\\" |\\n| `cavecrew-builder` | Surgical edit, 1-2 files | Scope is obvious, ≤2 files. Refuses 3+ file scope. |\\n| `cavecrew-reviewer` | Diff/file review | One-line findings with severity emoji |\\n\\nUse vanilla `Explore` or `Code Reviewer` when you want prose, architecture commentary, or rationale. Use main thread directly for one-line answers and 3+ file refactors.\\n\\nThis skill is a decision guide, not a slash command. It activates when the conversation mentions delegation.\\n\\n## How to invoke\\n\\nTriggers on phrases like \\\"delegate to subagent\\\", \\\"use cavecrew\\\", \\\"spawn investigator\\\", \\\"save context\\\", \\\"compressed agent output\\\".\\n\\n## Example chaining\\n\\nLocate → fix → verify (most common):\\n\\n1. `cavecrew-investigator` returns site list (`path:line — symbol — note`)\\n2. Main thread picks 1-2 sites, hands paths to `cavecrew-builder`\\n3. `cavecrew-reviewer` audits the resulting diff\\n\\nParallel scout: spawn 2-3 `cavecrew-investigator` calls in one message with different angles (defs, callers, tests). Aggregate in main.\\n\\n## See also\\n\\n- [`SKILL.md`](./SKILL.md) — full decision matrix and output contracts\\n- [`agents/cavecrew-investigator.md`](../../agents/cavecrew-investigator.md)\\n- [`agents/cavecrew-builder.md`](../../agents/cavecrew-builder.md)\\n- [`agents/cavecrew-reviewer.md`](../../agents/cavecrew-reviewer.md)\\n- [Caveman README](../../README.md) — repo overview\",\n      \"excerpt\": \"# cavecrew Decision guide. When to delegate to caveman subagents instead of doing the work inline. ## What it does Tells the main thread when to spawn a caveman-style subagent versus the vanilla equivalent. The win: subagent tool-results inject back into main context verbatim, and caveman output is roughly 1/3 the size of vanilla prose. Across 20 delegations in one session, that is the difference between context exhaustion and finishing the task. Three subagents: | Subagent | Job | Use when | |----------|-----|----------| | `cavecrew-investigator` | Locate code (read-only) | \\\"Where is X define...\",\n      \"score\": 0.015873015873015872\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"doc\",\n      \"id\": \"doc:a1905a2fb7f3\",\n      \"path\": \"seed/docs/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-10-entire-graph-opus-30pct-resolution-gateway.md\",\n      \"heading\": \"Burned-corpus qualification\",\n      \"line\": 125,\n      \"text\": \"- Test preloader success, timeout/error fail-open, stale-worktree rejection, atomic handoff, and source prompt-injection framing.\\n- Run every pinned fidelity corpus with no symbol/call F1 regression.\\n- Reconcile the current 1,334-versus-1,498 fixed-answer corpus drift; freeze one manifest and require zero per-item regression.\\n\\n### Burned-corpus qualification\\n\\nUse exactly 60 previously exposed ML300 tasks, stratified by language and repository, three repetitions, and all four arms: 720 sessions.\\n\\nProceed only when:\\n\\n- Packet delivery and fingerprint match are 100%; leakage is zero.\\n- Chance-corrected offline addressability covers at least 52% of exclusive locate-plus-read mass.\\n- Both exclusive locate and source-read counts decline.\\n- The upper 95% confidence bound on combined locate-plus-read ratio is ≤0.48.\\n- Let `p` be the measured candidate-only persisted packet/guide token tax as a fraction of baseline tokens. Require the upper 95% API-message ratio to satisfy `M ≤ (0.70 − p)^(1/1.70)`.\\n- Post-edit test/build/verification activity has a lower 95% ratio ≥0.90, preventing savings through abandoned validation.\\n- Error, timeout, empty-patch, and turn-cap rates are each no worse than baseline by more than three points.\\n- Prospective hierarchical simulation predicts ≥90% joint power for the final token and resolution gates. Below 80% stops the route; 80–90% requires a larger untouched manifest before confirmation.\\n\\nPacket correctness or gold-line recall alone never qualifies the candidate.\\n\\n### Confirmatory corpus and scheduling\\n\\nStart with the 141 untouched ML300 tasks. Choose the smallest `N` from `{141, 200, 300, 400, 500, 600, 700, 800}` that reaches ≥90% simulated joint power using the less favorable qualification effect estimate and repository-level variance.\\n\\nIf `N\\u003e141`, fill the reserve from the official 2,294-task SWE-bench pool, excluding every instance ID appearing in local plans, logs, manifests, results, transcript analyses, or previous gold-patch work. Official dataset sizes and harness support are documented by [SWE-bench](https://www.swebench.com/SWE-bench/guides/datasets/).\\n\\nOrder eligible reserve tasks by SHA-256 of `2026-08-10-eg-opus30:\\u003cinstance_id\\u003e`, cap added tasks from any repository at 10%, and require reproducible base commits and grading images. If 800 tasks still provide \\u003c90% predicted power, stop: the chosen claim is not practically verifiable with this design.\\n\\nEach task receives all four arms and three repetitions: `12N` sessions. Use balanced Latin-square arm order inside each task/repetition and interleave sessions in wall-clock time. Operational waves contain at most 50 tasks, but no efficacy summaries are released until all waves finish.\\n\\nAfter the first untouched session, candidate code, prompts, scorer, retry policy, graphs, and manifests are immutable. A revised candidate requires unused replacement tasks and a new preregistration.\\n\\n### Final release gates\",\n      \"excerpt\": \"...mass. - Both exclusive locate and source-read counts decline. - The upper 95% confidence bound on combined locate-plus-read ratio is ≤0.48. - Let `p` be the measured candidate-only persisted packet/guide token tax as a fraction of baseline tokens. Require the upper 95% API-message ratio to satisfy `M ≤ (0.70 − p)^(1/1.70)`. - Post-edit test/build/verification activity has a lower 95% ratio ≥0.90, preventing savings through abandoned validation. - Error, timeout, empty-patch, and turn-cap rates are each no worse than baseline by more than three points. - Prospective hierarchical simulat...\",\n      \"score\": 0.015625\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"doc\",\n      \"id\": \"doc:96210a4e4dfb\",\n      \"path\": \"seed/docs/.claude/mods/brain-memory/README.md\",\n      \"heading\": \"brain-memory\",\n      \"line\": 1,\n      \"text\": \"# brain-memory\\n\\nA Claude Code mod that shows what Entire Brain actually contributed to each turn —\\nand, more usefully, when it came back **empty** and why.\\n\\nBrain's value is invisible today. Facts get retrieved, the agent uses them or doesn't,\\nand nobody sees either. The expensive case is the empty answer: an empty result nobody\\nnotices is how a brain quietly stops being consulted while everyone still believes it works.\\n\\n## Use it\\n\\n```\\n/brain-memory      opens the pane\\n```\\n\\nEach row is one brain call, grouped by turn:\\n\\n```\\nBrain memory   3 answered   2 empty\\n\\nthis turn ─────────────────────────────────\\n+ query    semantic index lock      (10 results)\\n· search   zzqqxx                   (nothing matched)\\n    note: facts last distilled 2026-10-03 and all captured sessions are distilled\\nturn 4 ────────────────────────────────────\\n· get      fact:0000000000000000    (1 not found)\\n```\\n\\n`+` answered · `·` empty · `!` the call failed or was refused.\\n\\nThe yellow line under an empty row is brain's own `blind_spot` — brain already explains\\nwhy it had nothing, and that explanation is otherwise buried in a JSON payload no human\\nreads. Empty and failed calls are also announced in the transcript, so they're noticed\\nwith the pane closed. The spinner carries a running count.\\n\\nBoth routes count: the MCP tools (`mcp__entire-brain__*`) and the CLI through Bash\\n(`entire brain …`, `entire-brain …`). The mod only observes — a tool result reaches\\nClaude exactly as the tool returned it, pinned by a test.\\n\\n## Install\\n\\nAlready wired via `env.CLAUDE_CODE_PLUGIN_DIRS` in `~/.claude/settings.json`. To remove it,\\ndelete that key. For one session instead:\\n\\n```\\nclaude --plugin-dir /Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/mods/brain-memory\\n```\\n\\nThe bare `CLAUDE_CODE_PLUGIN_DIRS` process environment variable did **not** load the mod in\\na `claude -p` run here; the `settings.json` entry did. Use the settings entry.\\n\\n## Develop\\n\\n```\\nclaude plugin validate .\\nclaude plugin test\\n```\\n\\n## Two things that only showed up by running it\\n\\nA green suite and a passing `validate` both covered code that was broken in a live session.\\nWorth knowing before changing `payloadTextOf` or `summarize`:\\n\\n1. **The payload is nested, differently per route.** The test kit documents a `tool.call`\\n   stub of `{ result: '\\u003ctext\\u003e' }`, and neither route produces that:\\n\\n   ```\\n   Bash: { ref, result: { stdout: '\\u003cbrain JSON\\u003e', stderr, persistedOutputPath, … }, text }\\n   MCP:  { ref, result: [ { type: 'text', text: '\\u003cbrain JSON\\u003e' } ], text }\\n   ```\\n\\n   Reading `result.result` as the payload parses the *wrapper*, finds no `results` field,\\n   and scores every empty answer as a hit — the exact failure this mod exists to surface.\\n\\n2. **Brain payloads get truncated.** One real `entire brain query` here is 39 KB over 103\",\n      \"excerpt\": \"# brain-memory A Claude Code mod that shows what Entire Brain actually contributed to each turn — and, more usefully, when it came back **empty** and why. Brain's value is invisible today. Facts get retrieved, the agent uses them or doesn't, and nobody sees either. The expensive case is the empty answer: an empty result nobody notices is how a brain quietly stops being consulted while everyone still believes it works. ## Use it ``` /brain-memory opens the pane ``` Each row is one brain call, grouped by turn: ``` Brain memory 3 answered 2 empty this turn ─────────────...\",\n      \"score\": 0.015384615384615385\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"doc\",\n      \"id\": \"doc:635720c285d6\",\n      \"path\": \"seed/docs/same-content/plug/data/repos/local/repo-fd8a8b5d2a78/README.md\",\n      \"heading\": \"Entire Brain\",\n      \"line\": 1,\n      \"text\": \"# Entire Brain\\n\\nThis brain combines seeded repository context with Entire session history when available.\\n\\n## Session History\\n\\n- Sessions: 0\\n- Checkpoints scanned: 0\\n- `main`: 0 sessions in `sessions/main`\\n\\n## History Index\\n\\n- Generated at: `2026-09-15T20:40:32Z`\\n- Index: `history/generations/aab0ba25dfcbccee5012bedbc223c9085622ff04/index.json`\\n- Records: 0\\n- Decisions: 0\\n- Learnings: 0\\n- Validations: 0\\n- Tool calls: 0\",\n      \"score\": 0.015151515151515152\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"doc\",\n      \"id\": \"doc:0772015f7301\",\n      \"path\": \"seed/docs/v031-probe/data/repos/local/repo-b09c6272e667/README.md\",\n      \"heading\": \"Entire Brain\",\n      \"line\": 1,\n      \"text\": \"# Entire Brain\\n\\nThis brain combines seeded repository context with Entire session history when available.\\n\\n## Seeded Baseline\\n\\n- Generated at: `2026-09-13T15:23:16Z`\\n- Summary: `seed/repo-overview.md`\\n- Documents: 0\\n- Entrypoints: 0\\n- Commands: 0\\n- Historical gap: no session history available (confidence: heuristic)\\n- Commit coverage: 1 total — 0 pre-session, 0 covered, 0 missing session coverage after oldest session, 1 with no session history (`seed/history-gaps.md`)\\n\\n## Session History\\n\\n- Sessions: 0\\n- Checkpoints scanned: 0\\n- `main`: 0 sessions in `sessions/main`\\n\\n## History Index\\n\\n- Generated at: `2026-09-13T15:23:16Z`\\n- Index: `history/generations/d8685a120af2d3e34dd2afd36ea3bab517e636a7/index.json`\\n- Records: 0\\n- Decisions: 0\\n- Learnings: 0\\n- Validations: 0\\n- Tool calls: 0\\n\\n## Semantic Index\\n\\n- Generated at: `2026-09-13T15:23:16Z`\\n- Provider: `entire-graph` `dev`\\n- Schema: `1.1`\\n- Snapshot: `semantic/snapshots/0d64c8fb6b80a40145002c44130f9316dc7e8db6-9c175ba1a9f5a61c/snapshot.ndjson`\\n- Symbols: 2\\n- Relations: 4\\n- Commit: `0d64c8fb6b80a40145002c44130f9316dc7e8db6`\\n- Branch: `main`\\n- Intake: run `entire brain inspect code \\u003csymbol\\u003e --json` then `entire brain inspect context \\u003csymbol\\u003e --json` for task-specific semantic context.\",\n      \"excerpt\": \"# Entire Brain This brain combines seeded repository context with Entire session history when available. ## Seeded Baseline - Generated at: `2026-09-13T15:23:16Z` - Summary: `seed/repo-overview.md` - Documents: 0 - Entrypoints: 0 - Commands: 0 - Historical gap: no session history available (confidence: heuristic) - Commit coverage: 1 total — 0 pre-session, 0 covered, 0 missing session coverage after oldest session, 1 with no session history (`seed/history-gaps.md`) ## Session History - Sessions: 0 - Checkpoints scanned: 0 - `main`: 0 sessions in `sessions/main` ## History Index - Generated a...\",\n      \"score\": 0.014925373134328358\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"doc\",\n      \"id\": \"doc:8b9b3d8433b8\",\n      \"path\": \"seed/docs/v030-probe2/data/repos/local/repo-e87087ab24bf/README.md\",\n      \"heading\": \"Entire Brain\",\n      \"line\": 1,\n      \"text\": \"# Entire Brain\\n\\nThis brain combines seeded repository context with Entire session history when available.\\n\\n## Seeded Baseline\\n\\n- Generated at: `2026-09-13T05:01:43Z`\\n- Summary: `seed/repo-overview.md`\\n- Documents: 0\\n- Entrypoints: 0\\n- Commands: 0\\n- Historical gap: no session history available (confidence: heuristic)\\n- Commit coverage: 1 total — 0 pre-session, 0 covered, 0 missing session coverage after oldest session, 1 with no session history (`seed/history-gaps.md`)\\n\\n## Session History\\n\\n- Sessions: 0\\n- Checkpoints scanned: 0\\n- `main`: 0 sessions in `sessions/main`\\n\\n## History Index\\n\\n- Generated at: `2026-09-13T05:01:43Z`\\n- Index: `history/generations/467c805851423ba518a7bb3309221f825eba1010/index.json`\\n- Records: 0\\n- Decisions: 0\\n- Learnings: 0\\n- Validations: 0\\n- Tool calls: 0\\n\\n## Semantic Index\\n\\n- Generated at: `2026-09-13T05:01:43Z`\\n- Provider: `entire-graph` `dev`\\n- Schema: `1.1`\\n- Snapshot: `semantic/snapshots/373cd6b52bdb5e87312760c5776aae1e3eb81f15-4cac7d85f6d7b7dc/snapshot.ndjson`\\n- Symbols: 1\\n- Relations: 1\\n- Commit: `373cd6b52bdb5e87312760c5776aae1e3eb81f15`\\n- Branch: `main`\\n- Intake: run `entire brain inspect code \\u003csymbol\\u003e --json` then `entire brain inspect context \\u003csymbol\\u003e --json` for task-specific semantic context.\",\n      \"excerpt\": \"# Entire Brain This brain combines seeded repository context with Entire session history when available. ## Seeded Baseline - Generated at: `2026-09-13T05:01:43Z` - Summary: `seed/repo-overview.md` - Documents: 0 - Entrypoints: 0 - Commands: 0 - Historical gap: no session history available (confidence: heuristic) - Commit coverage: 1 total — 0 pre-session, 0 covered, 0 missing session coverage after oldest session, 1 with no session history (`seed/history-gaps.md`) ## Session History - Sessions: 0 - Checkpoints scanned: 0 - `main`: 0 sessions in `sessions/main` ## History Index - Generated a...\",\n      \"score\": 0.014705882352941176\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"doc\",\n      \"id\": \"doc:a75d1bb5e858\",\n      \"path\": \"seed/docs/same-content2/plug/data/repos/local/repo-557e835e8835/README.md\",\n      \"heading\": \"Entire Brain\",\n      \"line\": 1,\n      \"text\": \"# Entire Brain\\n\\nThis brain combines seeded repository context with Entire session history when available.\\n\\n## Seeded Baseline\\n\\n- Generated at: `2026-09-15T20:41:50Z`\\n- Summary: `seed/repo-overview.md`\\n- Documents: 0\\n- Entrypoints: 0\\n- Commands: 0\\n- Historical gap: no session history available (confidence: heuristic)\\n- Commit coverage: 1 total — 0 pre-session, 0 covered, 0 missing session coverage after oldest session, 1 with no session history (`seed/history-gaps.md`)\\n\\n## Session History\\n\\n- Sessions: 0\\n- Checkpoints scanned: 0\\n- `main`: 0 sessions in `sessions/main`\\n\\n## History Index\\n\\n- Generated at: `2026-09-15T20:41:50Z`\\n- Index: `history/generations/d59752ff580f429a794853d908341e1df0bf8c44/index.json`\\n- Records: 0\\n- Decisions: 0\\n- Learnings: 0\\n- Validations: 0\\n- Tool calls: 0\\n\\n## Semantic Index\\n\\n- Generated at: `2026-09-15T20:41:50Z`\\n- Provider: `entire-graph` `dev`\\n- Schema: `1.1`\\n- Snapshot: `semantic/snapshots/641925aa048bd93dca5248cb6351a660fd2c0682-b155c9f90d699764/snapshot.ndjson`\\n- Symbols: 1\\n- Relations: 1\\n- Commit: `641925aa048bd93dca5248cb6351a660fd2c0682`\\n- Branch: `main`\\n- Intake: run `entire brain inspect code \\u003csymbol\\u003e --json` then `entire brain inspect context \\u003csymbol\\u003e --json` for task-specific semantic context.\",\n      \"excerpt\": \"# Entire Brain This brain combines seeded repository context with Entire session history when available. ## Seeded Baseline - Generated at: `2026-09-15T20:41:50Z` - Summary: `seed/repo-overview.md` - Documents: 0 - Entrypoints: 0 - Commands: 0 - Historical gap: no session history available (confidence: heuristic) - Commit coverage: 1 total — 0 pre-session, 0 covered, 0 missing session coverage after oldest session, 1 with no session history (`seed/history-gaps.md`) ## Session History - Sessions: 0 - Checkpoints scanned: 0 - `main`: 0 sessions in `sessions/main` ## History Index - Generated a...\",\n      \"score\": 0.014492753623188406\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"doc\",\n      \"id\": \"doc:71ae73841426\",\n      \"path\": \"seed/docs/CLAUDE.md\",\n      \"heading\": \"Two-agent split (current)\",\n      \"line\": 51,\n      \"text\": \"- **Live verification over assertion.** Run the thing. A claim without a command behind it is a\\n  hypothesis.\\n- **No AI attribution footers in commits.**\\n- **Reproduce-proven-results doctrine:** treat every task as already achieved by someone; \\\"no\\\" or\\n  \\\"impossible\\\" is never a terminal answer — go one layer deeper (transcripts, harness, source).\\n\\n## Two-agent split (current)\\n\\nTwo Claude Code agents run in parallel on this machine and must not collide.\\n\\n| agent | owns | notes file |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| **graph-bench** | entire-graph token benchmarks, graphmark harness, rep30/rep100/300 cells | `graph-bench-results/TokensNotes.md` |\\n| **memory-bench** | memory/recall benchmarks (LOCOMO, prose-memory, cmm parity) | `graph-bench-results/MemoryNotes.md` |\\n\\n**Coordinate through `AGENT-COMMS.md`** (repo root). Read it at the start of a session and before\\ntouching anything the other agent owns. Protocol and message format are defined in that file.\\n\\nShared, do not stomp:\\n- `graphmark/` (entirehq/graphmark; formerly `graphmark-bench/`, which no longer exists) — the benchmark harness. Announce in comms before editing its runner/scorer.\\n- GCP VMs `graphbench-a..d` — claim a VM in comms before launching cells on it.\\n- **Never `scp` a script onto a VM while sessions are running.** Bash reads scripts lazily;\\n  overwriting in place moves bytes under a running shell and corrupts live runs (this destroyed 22\\n  sessions). Deploy to a temp path and atomic `mv`.\\n\\n## Benchmark doctrine (read before quoting any number)\\n\\nFull ledger of what is live and what is struck: **`graph-bench-results/TokensNotes.md`**.\\nMethod drill: the `graph-bench-forensics` skill.\\n\\nNon-negotiables:\\n- **Fairness:** tool *output* differences are legitimate; arm-asymmetric *instructions* are not.\\n  Test — *would this sentence help an arm with no tool?* If yes, both arms or neither.\\n- **Gate:** a pair counts only if both arms `subtype==\\\"success\\\"` AND non-empty patch. Drop\\n  symmetrically.\\n- **Power:** MDE is ~25–26 points at n=30. Never read sub-groups of 3–7 inside one cell. Always\\n  report a bootstrap CI and the median beside the total.\\n- **Never replicate an instance; always add instances.** Run-level noise is ~87% of paired variance.\\n- **Audit the harness before blaming the tool.** Every withdrawn headline here died of a harness\\n  bug. See TokensNotes §5 for the ten silent-failure modes already found.\\n\\n## Code intelligence: query the brain + graph BEFORE grepping\\n\\nEvery main checkout has an Entire brain. Its **code graph** is built for all repos; **durable\\nfacts** where the brain reports them. One graph/brain call beats a grep+read sweep. For \\\"where is /\\nwho calls / what depends on / what does this change break\\\", ask FIRST; grep only as fallback.\\n\\nStructural, deterministic (CLI, any repo, no setup):\\n- `entire sem edges   --repo . --format ndjson`   callers / callees\\n- `entire sem symbols --repo . --format ndjson`   definitions (file:line)\",\n      \"excerpt\": \"...* treat every task as already achieved by someone; \\\"no\\\" or \\\"impossible\\\" is never a terminal answer — go one layer deeper (transcripts, harness, source). ## Two-agent split (current) Two Claude Code agents run in parallel on this machine and must not collide. | agent | owns | notes file | |---|---|---| | **graph-bench** | entire-graph token benchmarks, graphmark harness, rep30/rep100/300 cells | `graph-bench-results/TokensNotes.md` | | **memory-bench** | memory/recall benchmarks (LOCOMO, prose-memory, cmm parity) | `graph-bench-results/MemoryNotes.md` | **Coordinate through `AGENT-COMMS.md`**...\",\n      \"score\": 0.014285714285714285\n    }\n  ]\n}\n"}],"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"3f551b4f-ab3d-4dba-a17e-369eed0978ae","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","root":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":1,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":243},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-graph","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/entiredb","visibility":"private"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/cli","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/entire.io","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d82e51ad-ae45-4e44-964c-9a2290c49dbc","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","