{"parentUuid":"1100214b-d55d-4adc-8179-fd7cfd31b7f2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfhxXPDFdvtL1jLmpQNd7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Refresh took: 3 results → 10, now indexing the current tree. Saving the manifest finding, since it affects your merge decision:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12315,"cache_read_input_tokens":328711,"output_tokens":1576,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":502},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":12315},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1576,"cache_read_input_tokens":328711,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12315,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":12315,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"68e96804-40dd-40cd-b1d2-93b799576cca","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfhxXNmi9xerDHbST5bcH","attributionMcpServer":"entire-brain","attributionMcpTool":"brain_search","type":"assistant","uuid":"437a2f72-3db7-4250-af76-186a9b8447ad","timestamp":"2026-10-04T22:07:27.231Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"437a2f72-3db7-4250-af76-186a9b8447ad","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfhxXPDFdvtL1jLmpQNd7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TMZAszUimgC4AUcjXDwP79","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/brain-manifest-unknown-field-blackout.md","content":"---\nname: brain-manifest-unknown-field-blackout\ndescription: \"A manifest field added/retired without a schema bump makes an older strict brain reader report memory_state_corrupt and turn every source off; remedy is refresh --force\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2\n  modified: 2026-10-04\n---\n\ndevenv's brain was dark for months and nobody noticed. `entire brain refresh`\ndied with:\n\n    memory_state_corrupt: brain manifest cannot be parsed:\n    json: unknown field \"checkpointed_unexported_commits\"\n\n**Mechanism.** `decodeStrictVersionedJSON` (`internal/cli/versioned_state.go:28`)\ncalls `checkedVersionedJSONHeader` first, which errors only when\n`header.SchemaVersion > current`. The field at\n`sources.seed.history_coverage.checkpointed_unexported_commits` was retired\n**at** version 3 without bumping the version, so the gate designed to say\n\"schema version 4 is newer than supported 3\" waves it through, and\n`decoder.DisallowUnknownFields()` then fails with a raw JSON error that reads\nlike data corruption rather than version skew.\n\nConsequence is total, not partial: all sources off, `facts: false`,\n`semantic: false`, and the memory worker failing on its retry loop forever —\nfor state that is entirely readable.\n\n**Remedy that works:** `entire brain refresh --force --agent none --worktree`\n(`--worktree` is required on a dirty tree; devenv is permanently dirty). Took\ndevenv from `freshness: unsafe`, seed 3 months behind HEAD, 20 docs → `ok`,\nseed at HEAD, 55 docs, and search 3 results → 10.\n\n**The real fix is already written and unmerged**: `loadBrainManifest` on\n`fix/agent-guide-directive-and-discovery` (worktree `brain-v1-guide`) tolerates\nundeclared fields for readers while `loadBrainManifestForReplace` stays strict\nfor writers, so a writer never erases what another build recorded. Its own\ncomment describes this exact symptom. Only `brain-v1-guide` and `brain-stack2`\nknow the field; every other checkout does not.\n\n**Why it matters beyond devenv:** run a newer brain once, then an older one — or\nshare a repo with a teammate on an older build — and that repo's brain goes\nsilent with an error naming a JSON field. See\n[[brain-is-a-separate-plugin-binary]]: the binary `which entire` finds is not\nthe one running. Related: [[brain-facts-are-branch-scoped]].\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12315,"cache_read_input_tokens":328711,"output_tokens":1576,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":502},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":12315},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1576,"cache_read_input_tokens":328711,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12315,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":12315,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01TMZAszUimgC4AUcjXDwP79":{"file_path":"/Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/brain-manifest-unknown-field-blackout.md","content":"---\nname: brain-manifest-unknown-field-blackout\ndescription: \"A manifest field added/retired without a schema bump makes an older strict brain reader report memory_state_corrupt and turn every source off; remedy is refresh --force\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2\n  modified: 2026-10-04\n---\n\ndevenv's brain was dark for months and nobody noticed. `entire brain refresh`\ndied with:\n\n    memory_state_corrupt: brain manifest cannot be parsed:\n    json: unknown field \"checkpointed_unexported_commits\"\n\n**Mechanism.** `decodeStrictVersionedJSON` (`internal/cli/versioned_state.go:28`)\ncalls `checkedVersionedJSONHeader` first, which errors only when\n`header.SchemaVersion > current`. The field at\n`sources.seed.history_coverage.checkpointed_unexported_commits` was retired\n**at** version 3 without bumping the version, so the gate designed to say\n\"schema version 4 is newer than supported 3\" waves it through, and\n`decoder.DisallowUnknownFields()` then fails with a raw JSON error that reads\nlike data corruption rather than version skew.\n\nConsequence is total, not partial: all sources off, `facts: false`,\n`semantic: false`, and the memory worker failing on its retry loop forever —\nfor state that is entirely readable.\n\n**Remedy that works:** `entire brain refresh --force --agent none --worktree`\n(`--worktree` is required on a dirty tree; devenv is permanently dirty). Took\ndevenv from `freshness: unsafe`, seed 3 months behind HEAD, 20 docs → `ok`,\nseed at HEAD, 55 docs, and search 3 results → 10.\n\n**The real fix is already written and unmerged**: `loadBrainManifest` on\n`fix/agent-guide-directive-and-discovery` (worktree `brain-v1-guide`) tolerates\nundeclared fields for readers while `loadBrainManifestForReplace` stays strict\nfor writers, so a writer never erases what another build recorded. Its own\ncomment describes this exact symptom. Only `brain-v1-guide` and `brain-stack2`\nknow the field; every other checkout does not.\n\n**Why it matters beyond devenv:** run a newer brain once, then an older one — or\nshare a repo with a teammate on an older build — and that repo's brain goes\nsilent with an error naming a JSON field. See\n[[brain-is-a-separate-plugin-binary]]: the binary `which entire` finds is not\nthe one running. Related: [[brain-facts-are-branch-scoped]].\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"68e96804-40dd-40cd-b1d2-93b799576cca","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CfhxXNmi9xerDHbST5bcH","attributionMcpServer":"entire-brain","attributionMcpTool":"brain_search","type":"assistant","uuid":"5f0a170b-5809-419a-b616-a8e091c103c0","timestamp":"2026-10-04T22:07:38.984Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
