rain refresh --force --agent none --worktree`\n(`--worktree` is required on a dirty tree; devenv is permanently dirty). Took\ndevenv from `freshness: unsafe`, seed 3 months behind HEAD, 20 docs → `ok`,\nseed at HEAD, 55 docs, and search 3 results → 10.\n\n**The real fix is already written and unmerged**: `loadBrainManifest` on\n`fix/agent-guide-directive-and-discovery` (worktree `brain-v1-guide`) tolerates\nundeclared fields for readers while `loadBrainManifestForReplace` stays strict\nfor writers, so a writer never erases what another build recorded. Its own\ncomment describes this exact symptom. Only `brain-v1-guide` and `brain-stack2`\nknow the field; every other checkout does not.\n\n**Why it matters beyond devenv:** run a newer brain once, then an older one — or\nshare a repo with a teammate on an older build — and that repo's brain goes\nsilent with an error naming a JSON field. See\n[[brain-is-a-separate-plugin-binary]]: the binary `which entire` finds is not\nthe one running. Related: [[brain-facts-are-branch-scoped]].\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false,"memdirStamped":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"5f0a170b-5809-419a-b616-a8e091c103c0","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
