{"parentUuid":"37422a86-7f2a-4492-9a27-ea8b78a2bc87","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"/Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/brain-manifest-unknown-field-blackout.md","snippet":"1\t---\n2\tname: brain-manifest-unknown-field-blackout\n3\tdescription: \"A manifest field added/retired without a schema bump makes refresh (the strict writer path) fail, leaving the index silently stale; remedy is refresh --force --worktree\"\n4\tmetadata:\n5\t  node_type: memory\n6\t  type: project\n7\t  originSessionId: 6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2\n8\t  modified: 2026-10-04T22:07:39.018Z\n9\t---\n10\t\n11\tdevenv's brain was dark for months and nobody noticed. `entire brain refresh`\n...\n18\tcalls `checkedVersionedJSONHeader` first, which errors only when\n19\t`header.SchemaVersion > current`. The field at\n20\t`sources.seed.history_coverage.checkpointed_unexported_commits` was retired\n21\t**at** version 3 without bumping the version, so the gate designed to say\n22\t\"schema version 4 is newer than supported 3\" waves it through, and\n23\t`decoder.DisallowUnknownFields()` then fails with a raw JSON error that reads\n24\tlike data corruption rather than version skew.\n25\t\n26\t**What was actually observed here, as distinct from the branch comment:**\n27\t`status` and the query verbs kept working throughout — only `refresh` failed,\n28\tand it failed in the *writer* path (`loadBrainManifestForReplace`), which is\n29\tdeliberately strict so a writer never erases fields another build recorded.\n30\tThe damage was therefore silent staleness, not a blackout: devenv's index sat\n31\t3 months behind HEAD and returned noise. The branch comment describes a\n32\tharsher consequence (all sources off, worker retrying forever); that was not\n33\treproduced here and should not be quoted as if it were.\n34\t\n35\t**Remedy that works:** `entire brain refresh --force --agent none --worktree`\n36\t(`--worktree` is required on a dirty tree; devenv is permanently dirty). Took\n37\tdevenv from `freshness: unsafe`, seed 3 months behind HEAD, 20 docs → `ok`,\n38\tseed at HEAD, 55 docs, and search 3 results → 10.\n39\t\n40\t**The real fix is already written and unmerged**: `loadBrainManifest` on\n41\t`fix/agent-guide-directive-and-discovery` (worktree `brain-v1-guide`) tolerates"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"95b0a178-f4ef-4e71-a5b2-b9fec391d15b","timestamp":"2026-10-04T22:10:00.722Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nNote: /Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/brain-manifest-unknown-field-blackout.md changed on disk since you last read it. That's usually deliberate, so take it as the current state rather than reverting it; if the change looks wrong, say so rather than undoing it yourself — otherwise no need to call it out. Here are the relevant changes (shown with line numbers):\n1\t---\n2\tname: brain-manifest-unknown-field-blackout\n3\tdescription: \"A manifest field added/retired without a schema bump makes refresh (the strict writer path) fail, leaving the index silently stale; remedy is refresh --force --worktree\"\n4\tmetadata:\n5\t  node_type: memory\n6\t  type: project\n7\t  originSessionId: 6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2\n8\t  modified: 2026-10-04T22:07:39.018Z\n9\t---\n10\t\n11\tdevenv's brain was dark for months and nobody noticed. `entire brain refresh`\n...\n18\tcalls `checkedVersionedJSONHeader` first, which errors only when\n19\t`header.SchemaVersion > current`. The field at\n20\t`sources.seed.history_coverage.checkpointed_unexported_commits` was retired\n21\t**at** version 3 without bumping the version, so the gate designed to say\n22\t\"schema version 4 is newer than supported 3\" waves it through, and\n23\t`decoder.DisallowUnknownFields()` then fails with a raw JSON error that reads\n24\tlike data corruption rather than version skew.\n25\t\n26\t**What was actually observed here, as distinct from the branch comment:**\n27\t`status` and the query verbs kept working throughout — only `refresh` failed,\n28\tand it failed in the *writer* path (`loadBrainManifestForReplace`), which is\n29\tdeliberately strict so a writer never erases fields another build recorded.\n30\tThe damage was therefore silent staleness, not a blackout: devenv's index sat\n31\t3 months behind HEAD and returned noise. The branch comment describes a\n32\tharsher consequence (all sources off, worker retrying forever); that was not\n33\treproduced here and should not be quoted as if it were.\n34\t\n35\t**Remedy that works:** `entire brain refresh --force --agent none --worktree`\n36\t(`--worktree` is required on a dirty tree; devenv is permanently dirty). Took\n37\tdevenv from `freshness: unsafe`, seed 3 months behind HEAD, 20 docs → `ok`,\n38\tseed at HEAD, 55 docs, and search 3 results → 10.\n39\t\n40\t**The real fix is already written and unmerged**: `loadBrainManifest` on\n41\t`fix/agent-guide-directive-and-discovery` (worktree `brain-v1-guide`) tolerates\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
