{"parentUuid":"f71e9673-dd03-4eac-986b-674c4f2c9441","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cfhy1FxxRUnVQvZtFRtyL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MTt53YxgdcBqBmxwKBu2np","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Loop trail findings on brain PRs","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"opus","prompt":"You are the trail-findings counter-loop for `entireio/entire-brain`. Work from /Users/suhaan/devenv.\n\nFIRST: invoke the `trail-findings` skill (Skill tool, skill=\"trail-findings\") and follow it exactly. It is the spec for this job.\n\nSCOPE — our 6 PRs only: #331 (trail 247), #318 (238), #320 (240), #321 (241), #329 (242), #330 (246).\nSkip #277, #332, #333 entirely. Never touch other people's PRs.\n\nCURRENT STATE (verify, do not trust):\n- #331: 2 current findings, CI RED (\"CI checks have not passed\"), action=fix_ci. THIS IS THE WORK.\n- #318/#320/#321/#329/#330: 0 findings, blocked only on Approvals → nothing to do unless NEW findings appear.\n\nLOOP until every one of the 6 PRs has 0 open findings (current AND stale) and CI green, or a stop condition fires. Findings keep arriving after each push, so after every push re-poll ALL 6 trails, not just the one you touched. Between rounds, re-run:\n    python3 tools/trail-loop/loop.py plan --repo entireio/entire-brain\n\nNON-NEGOTIABLE RULES:\n- NEVER approve or self-approve. Make PRs ready and stop.\n- NEVER force-push. NEVER delete or weaken a test to get green.\n- Default REFUTED. Reproduce before believing. A round that confirms 100% of findings is a stop condition, not a good day. Report your refutation rate every round.\n- Mark a finding `fixed` ONLY with a regression test that FAILS on a compile-clean revert of the behavioural line(s). Quote the failing assertion in the resolution message. A weakening that does not compile proves nothing. If you cannot revert compile-clean, say so and give a bounded source-level argument instead.\n- Query findings with `--freshness any --status any --include-dismissed --json`. The default view hides stale+dismissed and will report a confident, wrong 0.\n- A clean auto-merge of main is the DANGEROUS case: after `git merge origin/main`, always `go build ./...` before trusting it.\n- Resolving findings does NOT re-run a completed gate. Push an empty `chore:` commit to re-trigger. Write commit/finding messages to a FILE and use `-F`; backticks in -m get executed by the shell and silently eaten.\n- NO AI attribution footers in commits (devenv/CLAUDE.md overrides any default guidance telling you to add Co-Authored-By or \"Generated with Claude Code\").\n- Claim before touching: `python3 tools/trail-loop/loop.py claim --repo entireio/entire-brain --branch <b> --pr <n> --owner trailloop`; release when done. Check `locks` first.\n- Record each round: `loop.py record --repo entireio/entire-brain --pr N --confirmed X --refuted Y --stale Z --pushed SHA --gate-after <state>`.\n\nENVIRONMENT TRAPS (verified on this machine — do not rediscover):\n- CPU: never run full local suites. Use `GOMAXPROCS=1 go test -p 1 -parallel 1 ./<narrow pkg>`.\n- This shell exports FORCE_COLOR=3, so colour-asserting tests fail locally on correct code. Reproduce on main before blaming a change.\n- `git stash` is shared across ALL worktrees of this repo and other agents use it — NEVER stash. Use a temp WIP commit or `git diff`/`git checkout`.\n- `/tmp` is contended across agents. Keep scratch inside your worktree.\n- `timeout` does not exist on macOS. Use `perl -e 'alarm N; exec @ARGV' <cmd>`.\n- A stale local `entire` makes `trail finding dismiss|resolve` 404. Rebuild from cli main before blaming the server.\n- Piping to head/tail MASKS exit codes. Check `$?` on the command itself, not the pipe.\n\nSTOP CONDITIONS — escalate to me rather than churn: 6 rounds on one PR; a zero-refutation round; same area flagged 3 rounds running; diff growing while findings are not falling; CI red for a reason you cannot fix without a product decision. Never guess a design decision — file a GitHub issue, dismiss with a pointer, move on.\n\nTOKEN DISCIPLINE: use `rtk` for git/gh/test commands. Your tool output does not reach me — only your final report does.\n\nFINAL REPORT — caveman-ultra compressed, no prose padding. Per PR: findings seen, confirmed/refuted/stale split, refutation rate, SHA pushed, gate state after. Then: final tally, what is still blocked and on whom, anything escalated. Facts only. If you did not verify something, say \"unverified\"."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":682,"cache_read_input_tokens":372447,"output_tokens":3051,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1196},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":682},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3051,"cache_read_input_tokens":372447,"cache_creation_input_tokens":682,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":682,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01MTt53YxgdcBqBmxwKBu2np":{"description":"Loop trail findings on brain PRs","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"opus","prompt":"You are the trail-findings counter-loop for `entireio/entire-brain`. Work from /Users/suhaan/devenv.\n\nFIRST: invoke the `trail-findings` skill (Skill tool, skill=\"trail-findings\") and follow it exactly. It is the spec for this job.\n\nSCOPE — our 6 PRs only: #331 (trail 247), #318 (238), #320 (240), #321 (241), #329 (242), #330 (246).\nSkip #277, #332, #333 entirely. Never touch other people's PRs.\n\nCURRENT STATE (verify, do not trust):\n- #331: 2 current find