{"parentUuid":"958d8389-9394-4e7b-bcc4-fd9f5eb2568c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfhzK7f1oWrAYJ9mesJsz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KssgkTyP8MXTyVZXzCHk8e","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/mods/brain-memory\npython3 - <<'PY'\np='README.md'; s=open(p).read()\nold = \"## Develop\"\nnew = \"\"\"## State\n\nThe pane's rows live in `$.state` (`types/index.d.ts` declares the contract), not in module\nvariables. `register` runs again on every reload, so module variables start over — a pane that\nforgot every call each time the file was saved would be useless during exactly the work it\nsupports, and its empty state would then read as \"brain was never called\", the false negative\nthis mod exists to prevent. Writing `$.state` also redraws its readers, so the mod calls no\n`$.ui.invalidate`.\n\n`/clear`, `/resume` and `/branch` reset `$.state` by design, and calls made before the mod first\nloaded are invisible to it — which is why the empty state says \"since this pane started\nwatching\" rather than claiming none happened.\n\n## Develop\"\"\"\nassert old in s\nopen(p,'w').write(s.replace(old,new,1))\nprint(\"README updated\")\nPY\nDEV=/Users/suhaan/.claude/dev-mods/6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2/brain-memory\nmkdir -p \"$DEV/types\"\ncp hooks/register.js \"$DEV/hooks/register.js\"\ncp tests/brain-memory.test.ts \"$DEV/tests/brain-memory.test.ts\"\ncp types/index.d.ts \"$DEV/types/index.d.ts\"\ncp README.md \"$DEV/README.md\"\ncp .claude-plugin/plugin.json \"$DEV/.claude-plugin/plugin.json\"\necho \"synced to dev-mods\"\nclaude plugin validate \"$DEV\" 2>&1 | tail -5","description":"Sync the state migration into the live mod"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1727,"cache_read_input_tokens":389374,"output_tokens"