{"parentUuid":"4f7bfbfe-0176-425e-903a-f73454851a1e","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/mods/brain-memory/README.md","snippet":"44\t\n45\t```\n46\tclaude --plugin-dir /Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/mods/brain-memory\n47\t```\n48\t\n49\tThe bare `CLAUDE_CODE_PLUGIN_DIRS` process environment variable did **not** load the mod in\n50\ta `claude -p` run here; the `settings.json` entry did. Use the settings entry.\n51\t\n52\t## State\n53\t\n54\tThe pane's rows live in `$.state` (`types/index.d.ts` declares the contract), not in module\n55\tvariables. `register` runs again on every reload, so module variables start over — a pane that\n56\tforgot every call each time the file was saved would be useless during exactly the work it\n57\tsupports, and its empty state would then read as \"brain was never called\", the false negative\n58\tthis mod exists to prevent. Writing `$.state` also redraws its readers, so the mod calls no\n59\t`$.ui.invalidate`.\n60\t\n61\t`/clear`, `/resume` and `/branch` reset `$.state` by design, and calls made before the mod first\n62\tloaded are invisible to it — which is why the empty state says \"since this pane started\n63\twatching\" rather than claiming none happened.\n64\t\n65\t## Develop\n66\t\n67\t```\n68\tclaude plugin validate .\n69\tclaude plugin test\n70\t```\n71\t\n72\t## Two things that only showed up by running it"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"368b87a5-9627-4b39-be13-8b2d65338061","timestamp":"2026-10-04T22:30:58.509Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nNote: /Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/mods/brain-memory/README.md changed on disk since you last read it. That's usually deliberate, so take it as the current state rather than reverting it; if the change looks wrong, say so rather than undoing it yourself — otherwise no need to call it out. Here are the relevant changes (shown with line numbers):\n44\t\n45\t```\n46\tclaude --plugin-dir /Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/mods/brain-memory\n47\t```\n48\t\n49\tThe bare `CLAUDE_CODE_PLUGIN_DIRS` process environment variable did **not** load the mod in\n50\ta `claude -p` run here; the `settings.json` entry did. Use the settings entry.\n51\t\n52\t## State\n53\t\n54\tThe pane's rows live in `$.state` (`types/index.d.ts` declares the contract), not in module\n55\tvariables. `register` runs again on every reload, so module variables start over — a pane that\n56\tforgot every call each time the file was saved would be useless during exactly the work it\n57\tsupports, and its empty state would then read as \"brain was never called\", the false negative\n58\tthis mod exists to prevent. Writing `$.state` also redraws its readers, so the mod calls no\n59\t`$.ui.invalidate`.\n60\t\n61\t`/clear`, `/resume` and `/branch` reset `$.state` by design, and calls made before the mod first\n62\tloaded are invisible to it — which is why the empty state says \"since this pane started\n63\twatching\" rather than claiming none happened.\n64\t\n65\t## Develop\n66\t\n67\t```\n68\tclaude plugin validate .\n69\tclaude plugin test\n70\t```\n71\t\n72\t## Two things that only showed up by running it\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/mods/brain-memory","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
