{"parentUuid":"d06d17d3-6baf-4471-a9e6-faece4bdd3ee","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfhzM4ovQKEAteP25bD3u","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":650,"cache_read_input_tokens":392814,"output_tokens":1169,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":431},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":650},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1169,"cache_read_input_tokens":392814,"cache_creation_input_tokens":650,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":650,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":6185,"serverClassifierRequest":"02ab0cec-5523-4ae5-9224-b7156f20e510","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfhzM4JQhEY77U9AFQP1n","attributionMcpServer":"entire-brain","attributionMcpTool":"brain_search","type":"assistant","uuid":"f82304e7-556f-42cb-82c9-b7d2998655d2","timestamp":"2026-10-04T22:31:19.531Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/mods/brain-memory","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"f82304e7-556f-42cb-82c9-b7d2998655d2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfhzM4ovQKEAteP25bD3u","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Brain returned 65 KB there — I won't read it; the point was to have a call recorded.\n\n## Where things stand\n\n**Trail loop** — the agent is still running. It stopped and handed back pending its own background work (CI on #331, most likely) and will report when that lands. I have no results yet and won't guess at them.\n\n**The mod's reload amnesia — fixed.** Its rows now live in `$.state` with a declared contract:\n\n```\nstate writes: brain-memory.calls, brain-memory.turn\nstate reads:  brain-memory.calls, brain-memory.turn   ✔ Validation passed\n```\n\nThat matters because `register` re-runs on every reload, so module variables start over. A pane that forgot every call each time I saved the file was useless during exactly the work it supports — and worse, its empty state then read as \"brain was never called\", the false negative the mod exists to catch. Writing state also redraws its readers, so `$.ui.invalidate` is gone.\n\n**Verification: 17 tests, 15 guards proven by weakening.** The new ones:\n\n| weakening | tests that went red |\n|---|---|\n| pane reads a fresh array instead of state | 13 |\n| the state write never lands | 13 |\n| turn counter never advances | **0 → 1** |\n\nThat third one is why I keep doing this. Neutering turn grouping left all 16 tests green — the feature that answers \"what did brain give me for *this* question\" had no guard at all. Added one, confirmed it fires.\n\nOne honest limit: reload survival itself isn't covered by the suite, because the kit hands each test a fresh module and resets `$.state`. What the suite proves is that the pane reads and writes through state; the reload behaviour follows from that plus the documented semantics, and you'll see it directly — this sync triggers a reload at the end of this turn, and the brain call I just made should still be in the pane afterwards. This one reload still loses anything recorded by the old module-variable build; from here on they persist.\n\nAlso worth flagging from that 65 KB result: the mod reads `persistedOutputPath` for Bash but an MCP result that the harness spills to a file takes a different shape. Likely a gap, unverified — I'd rather measure it than patch blind, and it's the same class of bug that only showed up by running the thing."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":650,"cache_read_input_tokens":392814,"output_tokens":1169,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":431},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":650},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1169,"cache_read_input_tokens":392814,"cache_creation_input_tokens":650,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":650,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"02ab0cec-5523-4ae5-9224-b7156f20e510","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfhzM4JQhEY77U9AFQP1n","attributionMcpServer":"entire-brain","attributionMcpTool":"brain_search","type":"assistant","uuid":"aef61e18-7740-466d-8e86-fa2e9f74cd6d","timestamp":"2026-10-04T22:31:28.667Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/mods/brain-memory","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
