that review posts, under the same rules as round 1: default REFUTED; `fixed` only with a regression test that fails on a compile-clean revert, with the failing assertion quoted; query with `--freshness any --status any --include-dismissed --json`; record each round with `loop.py record`.\n\nExpect new findings — that is the known cost of this sync and the user accepted it.\n\nKEEP USING the CLI you built at /Users/suhaan/devenv/cli-trailloop-build/entire-new. I independently confirmed the installed /Users/suhaan/.local/bin/entire is the stale build, so resolve/dismiss through it would 404.\n\nI verified your round-1 report independently before authorizing this: 0 open findings on all six trails with the current binary and splits matching yours exactly (247: 8res/4dis, 238: 2res, 240: 0, 241: 2res, 242: 3res, 246: 3res/1dis); `verifySemanticHeadStable` is wired in production at semantic.go:751, inside the stamped-header branch and before the disclosure at :758, not merely defined; both new tests pass. Good work — the second test guarding the call site was the right instinct.\n\nSTOP CONDITIONS unchanged: 6 rounds on one PR, a zero-refutation round, same area flagged 3 rounds running, diff growing while findings are not falling, or anything needing a product decision. Escalate instead of churning.\n\nReport caveman-ultra compressed: per PR, commits behind before/after, build+vet result, SHA pushed, findings seen with confirmed/refuted/stale split and refutation rate, gate state after. Flag explicitly any merge that was conflict-free but broke the build.","type":"message","recipient":"a385ce05501705175","content":"Round 2 authorized: sync main INTO the four behin…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":395199,"cache_read_input_tokens":26450,"output_tokens":1243,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_req