{"parentUuid":"cd7fbdc5-93ef-44dd-86dd-3a3f7f3e5b90","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfiFXbFmc7DZdSwcP7wYP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Real news on both fronts:\n\n## Five of six are CI-green\n\n| PR | CI | red |\n|---|---|---|\n| #331, #330, #329, #321, #320 | **30 pass, 0 pending, 0 real failures** | `Entire Gates` — Approvals only |\n| #318 | 11 pass, 18 pending | none yet |\n\n## The sync produced one new finding, as predicted\n\n**Trail 238 / #318** — `01M44VYF80GRZEC5HTQYSRG7GC`, medium:\n\n> The `os.Lstat` check silently skips file-type validation when the file doesn't exist. If the symlink check passed and `Lstat` fails for another reason (permissions, I/O error), the code proceeds to `parseFactsFile` without confirming the file is regular. This differs from `loadFacts` (facts.go:151)…\n\nThat's the cost of the sync, and it's a reasonable-looking finding rather than noise — it's adjacent to the CWE-59 symlink work already in your memory, and it cites a sibling call site that handles the same pattern differently. Whether it's *real* is the agent's job to establish, and the rule stands: default refuted, and `fixed` only with a test that fails on a compile-clean revert.\n\nThe agent is in its loop on it. I'm not touching that trail — it holds the lock.\n\nSo the picture is: five PRs sitting at zero findings and green CI, blocked on your approval alone; one PR with a single medium finding being worked. I'll pass on the agent's round-2 report, verified, when it hands back."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":950,"cache_read_input_tokens":439926,"output_tokens":511,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":950},"