in","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"b1302147-9496-4fae-97df-73bf78d666e3","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PreToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_01WqGAbwn71K7JyF2xqn3rax","hookEvent":"PreToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"hookSpecificOutput\":{\"hookEventName\":\"PreToolUse\",\"permissionDecisionReason\":\"RTK auto-rewrite\",\"updatedInput\":{\"command\":\"rtk read /Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/trail-finding-sweep-pitfalls.md\",\"description\":\"Read the existing trail pitfalls memory\"}}}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"rtk hook claude","durationMs":10},"type":"attachment","uuid":"35f4cb98-3390-4e32-b45a-169953e406ba","timestamp":"2026-10-05T02:16:34.818Z","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"b1302147-9496-4fae-97df-73bf78d666e3","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"dcfd6075-aaa2-465e-9d27-0c1beef6ac09","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WqGAbwn71K7JyF2xqn3rax","type":"tool_result","content":"---\nname: trail-finding-sweep-pitfalls\ndescription: \"Two ways a finding sweep silently reports zero: scoping to the trails you happen to be working, and grepping ^01M when the CLI indents its IDs — use --json\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: feedback\n  originSessionId: 27642e0f-a981-4143-aea0-6f4f8cb34d37\n  modified: 2026-09-04T06:00:35.108Z\n---\n\nReporting \"0 open findings\" twice in one session when the real count was **142** cost\ncredibility both times. Two independent causes, both silent:\n\n1. **Scope.** I swept only the ~15 trails I had been working. Findings live on *every*\n   trail, including ones whose PRs merged months ago — and those matter more, because they\n   describe defects already on `main`. Sweep the full trail-number range, both repos.\n2. **Parsing.** `entire trail finding list` **indents** its rows, so\n   `grep -cE \"^01M\"` matches nothing and prints a confident `0`. The correct filter is\n   `grep -cE \"^[[:space:]]+01M.*open\"`, and better still `--json` — the human table also\n   wraps long `LOCATION` values, which silently corrupts column-based `awk`.\n\nAlso: `--repo` requires an explicit trail selector, so `finding show <id>` alone fails —\nkeep the trail number paired with every id. Default `--freshness` is `current`; stale\nfindings are hidden unless asked for.\n\n**Why:** both failures produce a *plausible* clean result rather than an error, so nothing\nprompts a re-check. This is the [[mechanism-endpoint-caught-a-false-headline]] shape — the\nnumber moved the way I wanted, so I stopped looking.\n\n**How to apply:** derive counts from `--json`, sweep the whole range, and before reporting\na zero, verify the pipeline on a trail *known* to have findings. State the scope of any\ncount out loud (\"trails 1-210, both repos\"), so a scoped number can never read as a global\none. Related: [[per-loser-forensics-doctrine]], [[reproduce-proven-results-doctrine]].","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"aaeed433-9bed-4458-8401-df3aefb1a0af","timestamp":"2026-10-05T02:16:37.511Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"---\nname: trail-finding-sweep-pitfalls\ndescription: \"Two ways a finding sweep silently reports zero: scoping to the trails you happen to be working, and grepping ^01M when the CLI indents its IDs — use --json\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: feedback\n  originSessionId: 27642e0f-a981-4143-aea0-6f4f8cb34d37\n  modified: 2026-09-04T06:00:35.108Z\n---\n\nReporting \"0 open findings\" twice in one session when the real count was **142** cost\ncredibility both times. Two independent causes, both silent:\n\n1. **Scope.** I swept only the ~15 trails I had been working. Findings live on *every*\n   trail, including ones whose PRs merged months ago — and those matter more, because they\n   describe defects already on `main`. Sweep the full trail-number range, both repos.\n2. **Parsing.** `entire trail finding list` **indents** its rows, so\n   `grep -cE \"^01M\"` matches nothing and prints a confident `0`. The correct filter is\n   `grep -cE \"^[[:space:]]+01M.*open\"`, and better still `--json` — the human table also\n   wraps long `LOCATION` values, which silently corrupts column-based `awk`.\n\nAlso: `--repo` requires an explicit trail selector, so `finding show <id>` alone fails —\nkeep the trail number paired with every id. Default `--freshness` is `current`; stale\nfindings are hidden unless asked for.\n\n**Why:** both failures produce a *plausible* clean result rather than an error, so nothing\nprompts a re-check. This is the [[mechanism-endpoint-caught-a-false-headline]] shape — the\nnumber moved the way I wanted, so I stopped looking.\n\n**How to apply:** derive counts from `--json`, sweep the whole range, and before reporting\na zero, verify the pipeline on a trail *known* to have findings. State the scope of any\ncount out loud (\"trails 1-210, both repos\"), so a scoped number can never read as a global\none. Related: [[per-loser-forensics-doctrine]], [[reproduce-proven-results-doctrine]].","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"classifierBoundary":true,"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"61af608c-f166-4dfd-b790-acf08c8bd210","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","root":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":1,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":244},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-graph","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/entiredb","visibility":"private"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/cli","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/entire.io","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b1302147-9496-4fae-97df-73bf78d666e3","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
