{"parentUuid":"8e70a9ad-8f9e-425c-bfc1-694091464fb7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfiHY62NypE4BjZ9djHtS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VUVmj8yTCfWp6Q1SWRJwYx","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'PY'\np='/Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/trail-finding-sweep-pitfalls.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nold = \"**Why:** both failures produce a *plausible* clean result rather than an error, so nothing\\nprompts a re-check.\"\nassert old in s\nnew = \"\"\"**A third silent zero, found 2026-10-04:** the findings sub-gate can read zero because\n**no agent review has ever run for the current head** — its summary says so in words\n(`No agent review has run for the current head`), but the sub-gate still reads as not-failing,\nso a sweep sees a clean PR that was never reviewed. The driver's `action` field caught it\n(`retrigger_gate`). An empty `chore:` push made the review run; it posted a medium finding\nwithin 20 minutes. The inverse trap fired on the same PR immediately after: the new gate read\n`Findings: passed` while that finding was open, because the review posted *after* the check\ncompleted. **Both gate readings were wrong, in opposite directions, on one PR inside 20\nminutes. Only `trail finding list` was right.**\n\n**A fourth, worse one — stale local worktrees.** Before merging main forward, check the\nworktree against its OWN PR head, not just against main: one worktree here was **76 commits\nbehind `origin/<its-own-branch>`** (0 ahead). Merging main from that tree and pushing would\nhave silently reverted the PR's own work with no conflict and a green build.\n`git merge --ff-only origin/<branch>` first, every time.\n\n**Why:** all of these produce a *plausible* clean result rather than an error, so nothing\nprompts a re-check.\"\"\"\nopen(p,'w').write(s.replace(old,new,1))\nprint(\"extended\")\nPY\npython3 - <<'PY'\np='/Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/MEMORY.md'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"— a scoped sweep and a `^01M` grep both report a confident 0; real count was 142. Use --json, sweep all trails, state the scope\",\n            \"— FOUR silent zeros: scoped sweep, `^01M` grep, a gate zero meaning NO REVIEW RAN, and a worktree 76 commits behind its own PR head; use --json, ff-only first\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nprint(\"index updated\")\nPY","description":"Record the two new trail-loop traps"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1882,"cache_read_input_tokens":453352,"output_tokens":890,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1882},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":890,"cache_read_input_tokens":453352,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1882,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1882,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01VUVmj8yTCfWp6Q1SWRJwYx":{"command":"python3 - <<'PY'\np='/Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/trail-finding-sweep-pitfalls.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nold = \"**Why:** both failures produce a *plausible* clean result rather than an error, so nothing\\nprompts a re-check.\"\nassert old in s\nnew = \"\"\"**A third silent zero, found 2026-10-04:** the findings sub-gate can read zero because\n**no agent review has ever run for the current head** — its summary says so in words\n(`No agent review has run for the current head`), but the sub-gate still reads as not-failing,\nso a sweep sees a clean PR that was never reviewed. The driver's `action` field caught it\n(`retrigger_gate`). An empty `chore:` push made the review run; it posted a medium finding\nwithin 20 minutes. The inverse trap fired on the same PR immediately after: the new gate read\n`Findings: passed` while that finding was open, because the review posted *after* the check\ncompleted. **Both gate readings were wrong, in opposite directions, on one PR inside 20\nminutes. Only `trail finding list` was right.**\n\n**A fourth, worse one — stale local worktrees.** Before merging main forward, check the\nworktree against its OWN PR head, not just against main: one worktree here was **76 commits\nbehind `origin/<its-own-branch>`** (0 ahead). Merging main from that tree and pushing would\nhave silently reverted the PR's own work with no conflict and a green build.\n`git merge --ff-only origin/<branch>` first, every time.\n\n**Why:** all of these produce a *plausible* clean result rather than an error, so nothing\nprompts a re-check.\"\"\"\nopen(p,'w').write(s.replace(old,new,1))\nprint(\"extended\")\nPY\npython3 - <<'PY'\np='/Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/MEMORY.md'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"— a scoped sweep and a `^01M` grep both report a confident 0; real count was 142. Use --json, sweep all trails, state the scope\",\n            \"— FOUR silent zeros: scoped sweep, `^01M` grep, a gate zero meaning NO REVIEW RAN, and a worktree 76 commits behind its own PR head; use --json, ff-only first\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nprint(\"index updated\")\nPY","description":"Record the two new trail-loop traps"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"ab38bd65-a05f-42fd-a9e7-319180678c17","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfiHY5Y75Y9TGtyhe6y1H","type":"assistant","uuid":"f2372aa7-d91a-459f-a889-a9ae7bc30251","timestamp":"2026-10-05T02:16:48.721Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/de