{"parentUuid":"61f74e08-1302-4c56-95bf-9019bf427090","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cfjiuko1nFTb5DvV5aMLQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1801,"cache_read_input_tokens":552581,"output_tokens":1506,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":427},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1801,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1506,"cache_read_input_tokens":552581,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1801,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1801},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":5980,"serverClassifierRequest":"37e29d96-e33f-4060-947f-742d6aeb41f5","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfjiukFGPoFdf3TBcSMNn","type":"assistant","uuid":"1e0e814f-1b70-4b87-b93b-54d76ffc973b","timestamp":"2026-10-05T20:30:06.365Z","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.290","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"1e0e814f-1b70-4b87-b93b-54d76ffc973b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cfjiuko1nFTb5DvV5aMLQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Measured the whole thing. Here's what's true.\n\n## Capture: what I verified\n\n| launched from | agent worked in | session captured to |\n|---|---|---|\n| `devenv/` (disabled) | `entire-brain` | **nothing, anywhere** |\n| `entire-brain` (enabled) | `cli` | **entire-brain** (4 files), 0 in cli |\n\nSo the session binds to the **launch repo**, not the working repo. The hook's cwd *does* follow you — I proved that (`HOOK_PWD=/Users/suhaan/devenv` → `.../brain-installed` across two Bash calls) — but session *ownership* is fixed at SessionStart.\n\n**What I changed:** installed Entire's full hook set into `~/.claude/settings.json` — all 7 hooks, merged without touching your existing ones, verified valid and nothing lost. This is necessary for any fix (previously the hooks didn't run at all from devenv) and safe: outside an Entire repo every verb exits 0 silently, which I tested in a throwaway repo. Backup at `~/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp/settings.before-capture.json`.\n\n**But it isn't sufficient, and I won't claim it is.** devenv is `enabled: false`, so no session is ever created to attach anything to.\n\nashtom's \"mine works from another folder\" is explained: he launches from *an* enabled repo. The supported move after that is `entire session adopt --from <launch repo>` — its help says exactly *\"useful when an agent starts in one repository or worktree, then moves and makes changes in another.\"*\n\n**Your three options:**\n\n1. **Launch from any enabled repo**, then `entire session adopt` into the one you worked in. Works today, zero product change, one command.\n2. **Enable devenv** so a session always exists, then adopt. This contradicts your own CLAUDE.md warning about mis-attribution — checkpoints made while in devenv would still land on devenv. Your call, not mine.\n3. **The real fix (product):** lazy session creation — when a hook fires with cwd inside an enabled repo and no session exists, create one there. That makes launch location irrelevant and is the feature worth filing.\n\nI'd file 3 and use 1 meanwhile. Say the word and I'll open the issue.\n\n## MCP gaps — and a stale line in your own guide\n\nAgent-facing CLI verbs with **no MCP tool**: `recall`, `verify`, `overview`, `entities`, `show`, `guide`. `recall` is the worst, because the agent guide *mandates* it (\"Previous decisions… MUST be investigated with Brain first\") while an MCP-only agent cannot call it. The rest (`dash`, `viz`, `watch`, `workspace`, `add`, `distill`, `path`) are operational and fine as CLI-only.\n\nAnd a contradiction inside #331 itself:\n\n```\n.entire/agent-guide.md:54   \"No MCP tool writes a fact, so this is a CLI call;\n                             do not go looking for one.\"\nmcp.go:906                  \"name\": \"brain_remember\"\n```\n\nThe guide tells agents not to look for a tool that the same branch registers. That one is a two-line fix in the guide generator, and it ships with the PR you're about to merge."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1801,"cache_read_input_tokens":552581,"output_tokens":1506,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":427},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1801,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1506,"cache_read_input_tokens":552581,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1801,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1801},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"37