{"parentUuid":"3b7d0180-8103-4e4d-9d57-09b8e5e543e2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cfjj3kjmGoQUfPW9dRSq1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Can't check — **your GitHub token has expired** (`The token in default is invalid`). Run `gh auth login -h github.com` and I'll confirm.\n\nLast verified state, about an hour ago: **not merged.** All six sat at 0 open findings with CI green, blocked only on Approvals. Nothing I did could change that — I won't self-approve.\n\n## What we added and improved\n\n**Brain in devenv — was broken, now works**\n- Refresh had been failing for ~3 months. Fixed. Docs indexed: **20 → 55**. Search results for the same query: **3 → 10**. Freshness: `unsafe` → `ok`.\n- devenv had **no brain agent guide at all** — only graph's. Now wired, so brain is a mandatory step instead of an optional one.\n- Session capture from devenv: **0 files → 4**. Nothing was being recorded before; now it is.\n\n**New: the brain-memory pane**\n- Shows what brain gave you each turn, and — the point — when it gave you **nothing**, with brain's own reason why.\n- **22 tests, 19 guards proven** by breaking each one and watching the test fail.\n- Running it for real found **3 bugs that both the test suite and the validator missed**: wrong payload nesting (scored every empty answer as a hit), undercounting truncated replies (said 15 when brain found 20), and `facts: null` read as \"no data field\" instead of \"empty\".\n\n**PR cleanup**\n- **6 PRs → 0 open findings**, CI **30 pass / 0 fail** on every one.\n- **4 branches synced** from 35–56 commits behind main → **0 behind**. No merge broke the build.\n- **3 findings handled this session: 1 fixed, 2 refuted (67% refuted).** Across their full history those six trails now show 24 findings dispositioned — 18 resolved, 6 dismissed.\n- Found **2 new ways a gate lies**: it can report zero because *no review ever ran*, and it can report \"passed\" while a finding is open. Both now written down.\n\n## One number I don't have\n\n**I can't tell you brain usage went up by X%.** Nothing measured it. There's a written plan to measure exactly that (`~/.claude/plans/dynamic-petting-globe.md` — real `claude -p` sessions, pre-registered pass bar, ~32 sessions) and it was never run. Everything above is a count of things fixed, not proof that agents now use brain more. The honest claim is: brain in devenv went from unusable-and-unwired to working-and-mandatory. Whether that changes behaviour is untested.\n\n**One caveat on the devenv enable you just authorized:** sessions now land on the devenv repo. When you work inside a sub-repo, `entire session adopt --from /Users/suhaan/devenv` moves the session to the right repo. The real fix is still lazy session creation — say the word and I'll file it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":383,"cache_read_input_tokens":560800,"output_tokens":2113,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1162},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":383,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2113,"cache_read_input_tokens":560800,"cache_creation_input_tokens":383,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":383},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"5de43129-662e-4e93-b10d-0d58d79a1828","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cfjj3kFzrS9AnG6oLkHXm","type":"assistant","uuid":"dc2e4cdc-3011-4d39-808c-ff68b07a71bd","timestamp":"2026-10-05T20:32:15.860Z","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entr