{"parentUuid":"59327a94-cc92-4adc-8afa-52b65015b1b9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfjjRmfw6hv3BeG1eWQvx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Not a network error — an auth one: \"Not logged in.\" Same root cause though, since the sandbox has lost keychain/directory access, which is where that credential lives.\n\nI'm going to stop digging here rather than keep probing around a broken sandbox. Three different routes have now failed for the same underlying reason, and a fourth isn't likely to be different.\n\n**Where that leaves the one open question.** To find out whether the six PRs merged, open a real Terminal window (outside Claude Code) and run:\n\n```\ngh pr view 331 --repo entireio/entire-brain --json state,mergedAt\n```\n\nOr just open the PRs page. Paste me the result and I'll fold it into the summary.\n\n**The likely quickest fix for this session:** restart Claude Code. The sandbox had working network and directory access for most of today — every gh query behind the numbers I gave you ran fine — and lost them partway through. A fresh session should come back with them.\n\n**Nothing needs fixing on your machine.** To be explicit, since I sent you down a wrong path earlier: don't run `sudo killall mDNSResponder`, don't re-auth GitHub, don't touch DNS settings. My mDNSResponder diagnosis was wrong — I read \"curl can't resolve but dig can\" as a daemon problem on your Mac, when `whoami` returning `501` and `pgrep` failing should have told me immediately it was the sandbox. That cost you two commands.\n\nEverything else from today is delivered and unaffected: the bullet list of what we added, the three remaining doc fixes, the devenv enable (verified working — 0 session files → 4), and the lazy-session-creation request I'll draft whenever you want it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens"