{"parentUuid":"3cfbfba0-137f-443b-8ff6-65e83e05fd86","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfjjUk52dVmdj2MZCeDrz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1246,"cache_read_input_tokens":572378,"output_tokens":1924,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":844},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1246,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1924,"cache_read_input_tokens":572378,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1246,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1246},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":9632,"serverClassifierRequest":"a9991442-5d60-4c73-b6bd-4084fab58386","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfjjUjGAYJ8x2xtkqTSDJ","type":"assistant","uuid":"960caf71-07f8-4a8c-ac28-5b9fc489b534","timestamp":"2026-10-05T20:37:38.282Z","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.290","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"960caf71-07f8-4a8c-ac28-5b9fc489b534","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfjjUk52dVmdj2MZCeDrz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"No — GitHub Actions being down wouldn't stop `curl` resolving **anthropic.com**, and it wouldn't make `whoami` print `501` or `pgrep` say \"Cannot get process list\". Those are my sandbox losing name resolution and directory access. GitHub itself answered fine when I hit it by IP: HTTP 200 in 27ms.\n\nGood — docs done. Here's the list.\n\n## What we added and improved\n\n**Brain in devenv: was broken, now works**\n- Refresh had been failing for ~3 months. Fixed. Indexed docs **20 → 55**. Same search query returned **3 → 10** results. Freshness `unsafe` → `ok`.\n- devenv had **no brain guide at all** — only a graph one. Now wired, so consulting brain is a required step, not optional.\n- Session capture from devenv: **0 files → 4**. Sessions launched here recorded nothing before.\n\n**New: the brain-memory pane**\n- Shows what brain gave you each turn — and when it gave you **nothing**, with brain's own reason why. That silent-empty case was invisible before.\n- **22 tests, 19 guards proven** by breaking each one and watching it fail.\n- Running it for real found **3 bugs the tests and validator both missed**: empty answers scored as hits, truncated replies undercounted (said 15 when brain found 20), and `facts: null` misread as \"no data\".\n\n**Brain fixes shipped in the PRs**\n- Partial clones now index. Before, a fully parsed index was thrown away — on entiredb that was **2,526 files, 35,510 symbols, 196,448 relations**, discarded.\n- The `--symbol` error now tells you the correct command instead of just failing.\n- The install message matches the docs instead of contradicting them.\n- Refresh no longer wedges when a manifest field changes.\n\n**PR cleanup**\n- **6 PRs → 0 open findings.** CI **30 pass / 0 fail** on all six.\n- **4 branches synced** from 35–56 commits behind → **0**. No merge broke the build.\n- **3 findings handled this session: 1 fixed, 2 refuted (67% refuted).** Across those six trails, 24 findings now dispositioned — 18 resolved, 6 dismissed.\n\n**Traps found and written down**\n- **2 new ways the gate lies**: it reports zero when *no review ever ran*, and reports \"passed\" while a finding is open. Both hit the same PR within 20 minutes.\n- A worktree can sit **76 commits behind its own PR** — merging from it would silently revert the PR's work with no conflict and a green build.\n- **6 brain commands have no MCP tool** (`recall`, `verify`, `overview`, `entities`, `show`, `guide`) — and `recall` is one the guide *requires*.\n- The guide says \"no MCP tool writes a fact\" while the same branch ships `brain_remember`.\n\n## The number I can't give you\n\n**There is no usage figure.** Nothing measured whether agents now use brain more. Brain in devenv went from unusable-and-unwired to working-and-required — that's real — but the behaviour change is untested. The plan to measure it is written and unrun. If you want that number, that's the next piece of work, not something I can back-fill."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1246,"cache_read_input_tokens":572378,"output_tokens":1924,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":844},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1246,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1924,"cache_read_input_tokens":572378,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1246,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1246},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"a99