{"parentUuid":"0a096887-4da8-42ca-aa23-fa52d3c79aa1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfjyrcX6JtEePssajD7wK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here's what's actually broken and the three ways out, ranked.\n\n**What's lost:** name resolution via `getaddrinfo` (so `curl`/`gh` can't resolve any host), keychain reads (so no `gh` or `entire` token), directory lookups (`whoami` → `501`), and process listing. **What still works:** the filesystem, local git, builds, tests, brain, graph, and the mod — everything I did today except anything needing a network name or a stored credential. The handicap is narrow, just badly placed.\n\n**1. Restart Claude Code — best option, ~10 seconds.** The sandbox is per-session and had all of this working for most of today. A restart almost certainly restores it, and it fixes the other casualties too: the MCP servers that disconnected and context7 timing out are the same root cause, not separate faults.\n\n**2. If you'd rather not restart: give me a token through settings `env`.** I confirmed that path reaches my shell — `CLAUDE_CODE_PLUGIN_DIRS` is visible to me because it's set there. Add to `~/.claude/settings.json`:\n\n```json\n\"env\": { \"GH_TOKEN\": \"<token>\" }\n```\n\nThat beats *both* broken pieces: `GH_TOKEN` skips the keychain, and I'd call GitHub with `curl --resolve`, which I already proved works (HTTP 200 in 27ms by IP). Caveat worth stating: that token sits in plaintext on disk, so use a fine-grained read-only one scoped to that repo, and rotate it after. Same trick works for `ENTIRE_TOKEN` if you want the `entire` CLI back.\n\n**3. Don't bother with permission rules.** You already have `skipDangerousModePermissionPrompt: true` and a Bash allow rule, and the sandbox bypass was still refused — that came from the auto-mode classifier, not a permission gap. I'd rather not route around a safety flag for something a restart fixes anyway.\n\nMy recommendation is **1**. Option 2 only if you're mid-something you don't want to lose — and in that case a read-only token, not your main one."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3514,"cache_read_input_tokens":582062,"output_tokens":1612,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":917},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3514},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1612,"cache_read_input_tokens":582062,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3514,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3514,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"c9f9b9e1-df44-490b-aeb0-327e6a2b69ff","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfjyrbpfrpPNdsfWVpFkJ","type":"assistant","uuid":"a8b1f283-bf0b-4751-b99c-9a471d3c558b","timestamp":"2026-10-05T23:46:19.228Z","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.290","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
