e bottleneck, not retrieval"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"5ce25f5a-70a5-455b-92e5-ba74b13f30d3","timestamp":"2026-10-06T00:53:54.235Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nNote: /Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/MEMORY.md changed on disk since you last read it. That's usually deliberate, so take it as the current state rather than reverting it; if the change looks wrong, say so rather than undoing it yourself — otherwise no need to call it out. Here are the relevant changes (shown with line numbers):\n124\t- [Stale entire binary: finding 404](stale-entire-binary-finding-404.md) — dismiss/resolve 404 was a 2026-08-19 CLI decoding empty reviewId; rebuild from cli main before blaming the server\n125\t- [Agent wake mechanisms](agent-wake-mechanisms.md) — Claude: asyncRewake Stop hook (installed); Codex: `codex queue --thread <id>` after every actionable send\n126\t- [Pilot8 subscription A/B state](pilot8-subscription-ab-state.md) — claude -p on Max; config v3 paper-done, prep running; blocked on user notional-stop + overage statement\n127\t- [My verification harness false-passes](verification-harness-false-pass.md) — 3x in one session: `timeout` absent on macOS, `.git` is a file in worktrees, un-isolated trials; a false pass is silent and ends the search\n128\t- [--no-optional-locks is not enough](git-no-optional-locks-insufficient.md) — it stops `git status` but NOT `git diff <commit>`; plumbing changes the answer, GIT_INDEX_FILE=copy keeps both\n129\t- [SBPL sandbox precedence quirks](sbpl-sandbox-precedence-quirks.md) — wildcard deny loses to an earlier explicit allow (gold stayed readable); subpath \"/\" and allow file-read* break dyld; EPERM stops PATH searches\n130\t- [Guard never met the real thing](guard-never-met-the-real-thing.md) — the pilot8 auth check required a key the real CLI never prints; dry-run launch guards against the real binary\n131\t- [Brain manifest unknown-field blackout](brain-manifest-unknown-field-blackout.md) 