{"parentUuid":"bf3295a9-64a5-45d0-9ad0-f3b96ffa7f7a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cfk55XkJeWffBPQ714U4Q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1277,"cache_read_input_tokens":599224,"output_tokens":2969,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1416},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1277},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2969,"cache_read_input_tokens":599224,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1277,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1277,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":19683,"serverClassifierRequest":"b2caf8dc-a2fe-4f47-a7a8-e2f3f2312145","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cfk55XMET1GuMuyN8zTGB","type":"assistant","uuid":"e4efde47-4554-4ad0-821b-a1c8181b5625","timestamp":"2026-10-06T00:54:47.980Z","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.290","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"e4efde47-4554-4ad0-821b-a1c8181b5625","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cfk55XkJeWffBPQ714U4Q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Found the key thing: `loadBrainIgnore` reads **only** `.brainignore`. With no such file — which is every fresh repo — the ignore set is **empty**, so every file counts, including the ones Entire itself just wrote. The mechanism to fix this already exists and is simply unused.\n\n# Plan: two install-experience fixes\n\n## Fix A — Entire's own files must not block Entire's install\n\n**Root cause.** `seed.go:271` calls `worktreeDirty` → `loadBrainIgnore` (`semantic.go:2433`), which returns an empty pattern set unless the repo has a hand-written `.brainignore`. So `init-agents` writes `AGENTS.md` / `CLAUDE.md` / `.entire/*`, and the next command refuses because the tree is dirty — with files we authored seconds earlier.\n\n**Change 1 — a built-in ignore set.** Add Entire-managed paths to the ignore used *by the dirtiness gate*: `.entire/`, `.brainignore`, and the agent pointer files (`AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `.claude/settings.json`, `.codex/hooks.json`). Merged with any user `.brainignore`, never replacing it.\n\nThe justification matters, so it isn't a hack: the gate exists to stop us seeding uncommitted **source** into an index attributed to a commit. Config files Entire wrote are not source. Excluding them is the gate working as intended.\n\n**Change 2 — the refusal must be actionable.** Today: `dirty_worktree: refusing to seed uncommitted content without --worktree`. It names a flag, not an intent, and never says *which* files. Replace with the count and first few paths, plus \"pass `--worktree` to index your uncommitted work, or commit/stash first.\"\n\n**Change 3 — verify whether `setup` hits this at all.** `refresh.go:223` gates seeding behind `seedRefreshNeeded`. I have not confirmed the install path reaches the refusal; the reporter's experience says it does. That gets established before coding, not assumed.\n\n**Tests.** A repo dirty *only* with Entire-authored files seeds successfully; a repo with one dirty source file still refuses; a user `.brainignore` still applies. Each verified by weakening — drop the built-in set and watch the first test go red.\n\n## Fix B — stop silently choosing another vendor's model\n\n**Root cause.** `defaultRefreshAgent` (`refresh.go:881`) is `codex → claude → none`, hardcoded, unannounced.\n\n**The argument I'd lead with** is that the codebase already decided this, for ollama, in the same function:\n\n> *choosing one is a product decision, not a default worth guessing* … *so a privacy-motivated install does not quietly become a cloud call.*\n\nRouting a repo's content to codex while the user sits in Claude Code is the same class of surprise.\n\n**New order:**\n1. **The harness you're running under**, detected from env — `CLAUDE_CODE_ENTRYPOINT` is already referenced at `hook_cmd.go:425`, `CODEX_HOME` at `skill_form.go:114`. This is detection, not guessing.\n2. **Ask**, only when attached to a TTY. Setup UI here is already TTY-gated and must stay that way, or a piped install hangs forever.\n3. **Fall back** to the documented order, and **always print the choice** — mirroring the existing ollama fallthrough warning.\n\n**Tests.** Claude-harness env picks claude-code even with codex on PATH; no harness + no TTY picks deterministically and never prompts; the chosen agent is always announced. Weakening-verified.\n\n## Decisions I need from you\n\n- **Branch.** I'd open a **separate PR off main**, not stack on #331 — #331 is green and waiting on your approval, and touching it reopens agent review on work that's already clean. Risk: `defaultRefreshAgent` may live only on the #331 branch; I'll check, and if so it stacks and I'll tell you.\n- **Scope of the ignore set.** Including `AGENTS.md` / `CLAUDE.md` means a user's *own* edits to those files also stop blocking the gate. I think that's correct — they're agent config, not indexed source — but it is a judgement call and it's yours.\n\n## What I won't do\n\nMerge, approve, or push to any existing PR without you saying so. And I'll report the dirty-path check in Fix A Change 3 as a finding either way, including if it shows the install path *doesn't* hit the refusal and the reporter hit it somewhere else — that would change Fix A.\n\nSay go and I'll start with Change 3, since it can invalidate the rest."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1277,"cache_read_input_tokens":599224,"output_tokens":2969,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1416},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1277},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2969,"cache_read_input_tokens":599224,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1277,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1277,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"b2caf8dc-a2fe-4f47-a7a8-e2f3f2312145","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cfk55XMET1GuMuyN8zTGB","type":"assistant","uuid":"5674d39b-c32d-4247-a915-52cbefae36cf","timestamp":"2026-10-06T00:55:09.401Z","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.290","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
