nning to change the order to prefer the harness the user is CURRENTLY running under, then prompt on a TTY, then fall back.\n\nQUESTION 1 — branch provenance. Does `defaultRefreshAgent` exist in brain-installed (the older checkout) too, or only on the feature branch? Same for the ollama-removal comment block above it. I need to know whether a fix belongs on main or must stack on the feature branch.\n\nQUESTION 2 — callers. Who calls `defaultRefreshAgent`? Every call site, file:line. Which user-facing commands end up here (`refresh`, `distill`, `setup`, `watch`)? Is the chosen agent printed to the user anywhere today?\n\nQUESTION 3 — harness detection. What already exists to tell which coding agent is running?\n  - `CLAUDE_CODE_ENTRYPOINT` is referenced at internal/cli/hook_cmd.go:425 — in what capacity?\n  - `CODEX_HOME` at internal/cli/skill_form.go:114 and `harnessHomeRoot` — what does that do?\n  - Is there any existing \"which harness am I in\" helper to REUSE rather than write new? Search for env reads like CLAUDECODE, CLAUDE_CODE_*, CODEX_*, AGENT, ENTIRE_AGENT.\n  - Does the hooks layer already know the agent type (e.g. `resolveSessionAgentType`, types.AgentType)? Could that be reused here?\n\nQUESTION 4 — TTY gating + prompting. What helper decides interactive vs piped? (expect something like Caps.TTY, isTerminal, stdinIsTerminal). Give its file:line and an example call site. What prompt/select UI does the codebase already use (huh? survey? custom)? Name a representative existing interactive prompt I should copy the style of.\n\nQUESTION 5 — how is the ollama fallthrough warning surfaced? `ollamaModelMissingWarning` returns a string — who prints it, through what writer, and at what point in the flow? That is the pattern I want to mirror for announcing the chosen agent.\n\nUse `entire graph search --repo . --profile full --head --query \"...\"` first; grep only as fallback. Use rtk for shell.\n\nOUTPUT: caveman-ultra compressed. Bullets, file:line, no prose. M