{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-06T01:02:05.448Z","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a2811ed429f91e2cf</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_014xaL4F4xmj7gx1PmxwYJiX</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2/tasks/a2811ed429f91e2cf.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Map agent auto-selection and TTY gating\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Findings. All paths absolute.\n\n## Q1 — branch provenance\n\n- `defaultRefreshAgent` **exists in BOTH**. Not feature-branch-only.\n  - main/installed: `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-installed/internal/cli/refresh.go:741`\n  - feature: `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/refresh.go:851`\n- Body on main is **bare** — no comments, identical logic: no-egress → `codex` → `claude-code` → `none`. The codex-first bug is a **main bug**.\n- Ollama-removal comment block = **feature-branch only** (`refresh.go:836-850` + inline block 858-884).\n- `ollamaModelMissingWarning` = **feature-branch only**. Absent from brain-installed (grep: zero hits).\n- Introduced by commit `13e897d6` \"fix: close a secret-leak path and an agent default that cannot run\" (also `7711c04e` touched local-model handling).\n- Also feature-only: `watch.go:120` `distillAgent: \"auto\"`. Main has `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-installed/internal/cli/watch.go:108` → hardcoded `\"codex\"` (never even reaches `defaultRefreshAgent`).\n- **Verdict**: core reorder fix belongs on **main**. But if you want to touch the ollama comment/warning, or want `watch` to route through the function at all, you must **stack on the feature branch** — on main, watch bypasses it entirely.\n\n## Q2 — callers\n\n13 non-test call sites, **identical set in both checkouts** (only line numbers shift). Feature-branch lines:\n\n- `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/refresh.go:145` — `refresh`, gated `== \"auto\"`\n- `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/distill_cmd.go:710` — `distill`, gated `== \"auto\"`, resolved before dry-run branch (salt correctness)\n- `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/setup.go:1271` — `setup`, via injected `steps.detectAgent` seam\n- `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/skill_cmd.go:178`, `:204`, `:246`\n- `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/facts_write_cmd.go:256`\n- `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/facts_read_cmd.go:311`\n- `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/facts_admin_cmd.go:611`\n- `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/facts_eval.go:398`\n- `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/facts_eval_gen.go:133`\n- `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/workspace_patterns.go:106`, `:751`\n\n`setup` has a second indirection — `steps.detectAgent` consumed at `setup.go:581` (resolve-once before daemon plan is built) and `setup.go:951` (backfill phase).\n\n`watch`: reaches here only on the feature branch, via `distillAgent: \"auto\"` → `runDistill` → `distill_cmd.go:710`.\n\n**Is the chosen agent printed today?** Almost never:\n- **Only** user-visible surface: `setup.go:1021` `setupBackfillSpendLabel` → `\"agent \" + agent`, printed at `setup.go:974` via `progress.Skip(...)` (\"fact backfill will SPEND TOKENS now: agent codex over N session(s)…\"). Setup-only, backfill-only.\n- `refresh`, `distill`, `skill`, `facts *`, `workspace patterns`: **silent**. Agent only leaks into JSON/state structs — `setup.go:987` (`setupBackfillState.Agent`), `distill_cmd.go:1403`, `distill_cmd.go:2134` (cache salt).\n- `setup.go:954` is the one \"nothing found\" message: `\"fact backfill: no agent CLI on PATH (install codex or claude…)\"`.\n- This is the whole reported bug: codex gets picked and nothing says so.\n\n## Q3 — harness detection\n\n**Nothing exists. There is no \"which harness am I in\" helper to reuse.** Exhaustive repo-wide grep for `CLAUDECODE`, `CLAUDE_CODE_*`, `CODEX_*`, `ENTIRE_AGENT`, `AGENT_TYPE`:\n\n- `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/hook_cmd.go:425` — `CLAUDE_CODE_ENTRYPOINT` appears **only inside a doc comment**, listing env vars observed on a Claude Code PreToolUse hook (measured vs Claude Code 2.1.288). **Never read in code.** Zero `os.Getenv(\"CLAUDE_CODE_ENTRYPOINT\")` anywhere. Same for `CLAUDECODE` — zero hits, even in comments.\n- `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/skill_form.go:114` — `CODEX_HOME` is **write-destination resolution only**, not detection. Pairs with `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR` at `skill_form.go:113`.\n- `harnessHomeRoot` at `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/skill_form.go:291` — returns env value or documented default; rejects relative/whitespace values. **Returns a path, not an identity.** Returns the fallback when unset, so it cannot distinguish \"set\" from \"unset\" — unusable as-is for detection.\n- `resolveSessionAgentType` — **does not exist in this repo** (zero hits).\n- `types.AgentType` — **does not exist here**. Only reference is a comment at `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/export.go:3226` naming `cmd/entire/cli/agent/chunking.go DetectAgentTypeFromContent` — that lives in the **separate `cli` repo**, and it sniffs **transcript file content**, not the live process. Wrong layer; not reusable for \"am I running under X right now\".\n- Hooks layer does **not** know agent type. `hook_cmd.go` parses only `hook_event_name` / `tool_name` / `tool_input` (`agentHookPayload`, `hook_cmd.go:430`).\n\n**Implication**: you write harness detection new. Style precedent for env reads: `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/agent_policy.go:14-25` (`brainNoEgressMode`, `envBool`, `securityToggleEnabled`). Note `defaultRefreshAgent` returns `\"claude-code\"` (hyphenated) but probes binary `\"claude\"` — keep that mapping if you key off env.\n\n## Q4 — TTY gating + prompting\n\nTwo unrelated TTY mechanisms:\n\n- **CLI-side, stdin**: `stdinIsTerminal()` at `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/seed.go:1811` — `os.Stdin.Stat()` + `os.ModeCharDevice`. This is the one you want.\n  - call site A: `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/seed.go:1793` — `if opts.noInteractive || !stdinIsTerminal() { return fallback }`\n  - call site B: `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/hook_cmd.go:446` — `hookStdinWouldBlock`\n  - present on main too (`/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-installed/internal/cli/seed.go:1518`)\n- **TUI-side, stdout**: `Caps.TTY` via `tui.DetectCaps` / `DetectCapsWithEnv` at `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/tui/render.go:61-74` — uses `isatty`, plus `SupportsFullScreen` TERM check. This is for **rendering**, not for deciding whether to block on input. Also `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/dash.go:617`.\n\n**Prompt UI**: no `huh`, no `survey`, no `promptui` (checked go.mod). `bubbletea`/`lipgloss` are present but used **only** for the dashboard (`internal/tui/tui.go`, `internal/cli/dash.go`) — not for prompts.\n\n**The only interactive prompt in the entire CLI** — copy this style verbatim:\n- `promptSeedTimeoutAction`, `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/seed.go:1792-1809`\n- Pattern: guard on `opts.noInteractive || !stdinIsTerminal()` → return fallback; `fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"...\\n[k]eep quick / [c]ontinue / [f]ail: \")`; `fmt.Fscanln(os.Stdin, &amp;response)`; **any error → fallback**; `strings.ToLower(strings.TrimSpace(...))` switch with single-letter + full-word cases; `default:` is the safe option.\n- Prompt goes to **stderr**, answer read from stdin.\n\nCaveat: `defaultRefreshAgent` currently takes `(ctx, runner, repoDir)` and has **no access to `opts`/`cmd`**. To prompt or print you must thread a writer + a `noInteractive` flag through all 13 call sites, or add a wrapper and leave the pure function for tests. Tests call it directly with a 3-arg signature: `refresh_test.go:22`, `refresh_ollama_auto_test.go:34-48`, `local_agent_preference_test.go:63`.\n\n## Q5 — ollama fallthrough warning\n\n**It is never printed. Dead code.**\n\n- Defined `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/refresh.go:893` (doc comment `:890`).\n- Non-test callers: **zero**. Grep for both the symbol and its literal string (`\"cannot be chosen automatically\"`) returns only the definition.\n- Only referenced from tests: `refresh_ollama_auto_test.go:61,70,73,77` and a comment at `local_agent_preference_test.go:36`.\n- Its own doc comment says \"the line a caller prints\" and the inline block at `refresh.go:879` claims \"The caller warns when it falls through\" — **both statements are false in the current tree**. The privacy-regression guard the comments promise does not actually fire.\n\n**So there is no existing pattern to mirror here.** The nearest real precedent for announcing a chosen agent:\n- `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/setup.go:974` — `progress.Skip(fmt.Sprintf(\"fact backfill will SPEND TOKENS now: %s over %d session(s)...\", setupBackfillSpendLabel(agent, setupOpts), ...))`\n- Writer chain: `newRefreshProgress(cmd.ErrOrStderr())` → `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/progress.go:224` → `newProgress` `:231` → `newProgressWithRenderer(out, prefix, tui.NewRenderer(out), processLive)`. Spinner on a TTY, prefixed plain lines otherwise — so it degrades correctly when piped.\n- Timing precedent is explicitly documented at `setup.go:966-972`: cost/choice line must print **BEFORE** the spend, so the user can Ctrl-C. Same argument applies to announcing the agent.\n- `--json` suppression precedent: `setup.go:1257-1260` redirects out/err to `io.Discard`.\n\n**Suggested shape** (unverified, my read): announce via `progress`/`cmd.ErrOrStderr()` at each resolve site, and wire up `ollamaModelMissingWarning` at the same point — it is already written and tested, just never called.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>55908</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>27</tool_uses><duration_ms>156371</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
