{"parentUuid":"e0625bd8-cbc2-4e32-ae2d-9c0c40da316a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cfk5UuoVv2c6SY1byuQoM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WEAycY2oPuW3bR58MmPdD2","name":"AskUserQuestion","input":{"questions":[{"question":"Fix A stops Entire's own files from blocking Entire's install. But AGENTS.md and CLAUDE.md are files users also edit by hand. How wide should the built-in ignore be?","header":"Ignore scope","multiSelect":false,"options":[{"label":"Entire-authored paths only (Recommended)","description":"Ignore .entire/, .brainignore, .claude/settings.json, .codex/hooks.json, plus AGENTS.md and CLAUDE.md. Treats all of these as agent config rather than indexed source. Side effect: a user's own hand-edits to AGENTS.md/CLAUDE.md also stop blocking the gate — which I think is correct, since they aren't source either.","preview":"builtin ignore:\n  .entire/\n  .brainignore\n  .claude/settings.json\n  .codex/hooks.json\n  AGENTS.md\n  CLAUDE.md\n\ndirty src/foo.go  -> still refuses\ndirty AGENTS.md   -> proceeds"},{"label":"Only the managed block","description":"Ignore AGENTS.md/CLAUDE.md only when the diff is confined to Entire's own <!-- entire-agent:begin/end --> markers; any other edit still blocks. Most precise, but needs diff parsing and can misfire on a reformat or a merge that touches the block.","preview":"builtin ignore:\n  .entire/  .brainignore  (always)\n\nAGENTS.md dirty:\n  diff inside entire-agent markers -> proceeds\n  diff anywhere else               -> refuses"},{"label":"Narrow — dotfiles only","description":"Ignore .entire/, .brainignore, .claude/settings.json, .codex/hooks.json — but NOT AGENTS.md or CLAUDE.md. Safest, smallest change. Does NOT fully fix the reported bug: graph's init-agents writes AGENTS.md/CLAUDE.md, so install would still be blocked by them.","preview":"builtin ignore:\n  .entire/\n  .brainignore\n  .claude/settings.json\n  .codex/hooks.json\n\ndirty AGENTS.md -> STILL refuses\n(reported bug not fully fixed)"},{"label":"Install-time bypass instead","description":"Leave the ignore set alone. Instead, setup/install defaults to --worktree behaviour, on the grounds that at install time indexing what is on disk is the intent. Simpler, but means install indexes ALL uncommitted work, including unrelated source edits."}]}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1344,"cache_read_input_tokens":610416,"output_tokens":1024,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1344},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1024,"cache_read_input_tokens":610416,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1344,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1344,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01WEAycY2oPuW3bR58MmPdD2":{"questions":[{"question":"Fix A stops Entire's own files from blocking Entire's install. But AGENTS.md and CLAUDE.md are files users also edit by hand. How wide should the built-in ignore be?","header":"Ignore scope","multiSelect":false,"options":[{"label":"Entire-authored paths only (Recommended)","description":"Ignore .entire/, .brainignore, .claude/settings.json, .codex/hooks.json, plus AGENTS.md and CLAUDE.md. Treats all of these as agent config rather than indexed source. Side effect: a user's own hand-edits to AGENTS.md/CLAUDE.md also stop blocking the gate — which I think is correct, since they aren't source either.","preview":"builtin ignore:\n  .entire/\n  .brainignore\n  .claude/settings.json\n  .codex/hooks.json\n  AGENTS.md\n  C