ide/internal/cli/facts_eval_gen.go:133`\n- `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/workspace_patterns.go:106`, `:751`\n\n`setup` has a second indirection — `steps.detectAgent` consumed at `setup.go:581` (resolve-once before daemon plan is built) and `setup.go:951` (backfill phase).\n\n`watch`: reaches here only on the feature branch, via `distillAgent: \"auto\"` → `runDistill` → `distill_cmd.go:710`.\n\n**Is the chosen agent printed today?** Almost never:\n- **Only** user-visible surface: `setup.go:1021` `setupBackfillSpendLabel` → `\"agent \" + agent`, printed at `setup.go:974` via `progress.Skip(...)` (\"fact backfill will SPEND TOKENS now: agent codex over N session(s)…\"). Setup-only, backfill-only.\n- `refresh`, `distill`, `skill`, `facts *`, `workspace patterns`: **silent**. Agent only leaks into JSON/state structs — `setup.go:987` (`setupBackfillState.Agent`), `distill_cmd.go:1403`, `distill_cmd.go:2134` (cache salt).\n- `setup.go:954` is the one \"nothing found\" message: `\"fact backfill: no agent CLI on PATH (install codex or claude…)\"`.\n- This is the whole reported bug: codex gets picked and nothing says so.\n\n## Q3 — harness detection\n\n**Nothing exists. There is no \"which harness am I in\" helper to reuse.** Exhaustive repo-wide grep for `CLAUDECODE`, `CLAUDE_CODE_*`, `CODEX_*`, `ENTIRE_AGENT`, `AGENT_TYPE`:\n\n- `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/hook_cmd.go:425` — `CLAUDE_CODE_ENTRYPOINT` appears **only inside a doc comment**, listing env vars observed on a Claude Code PreToolUse hook (measured vs Claude Code 2.1.288). **Never read in code.** Zero `os.Getenv(\"CLAUDE_CODE_ENTRYPOINT\")` anywhere. Same for `CLAUDECODE` — zero hits, even in comments.\n- `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/skill_form.go:114` — `CODEX_HOME` is **write-destination resolution only**, not detection. Pairs with `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR` at `skill_form.go:113`.\n- `harnessHomeRoot` at `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/skill