is verified.** `CODEX_HOME` (`skill_form.go:114`) is write-destination\nresolution, not detection, and the `CODEX_COMPANION_*` vars present here come from a Claude Code\nplugin, not from Codex. So: detect Claude Code positively; leave Codex to the existing PATH probe\nuntil a signal is confirmed on a real Codex run. Inventing one would repeat a mistake already in\nmemory — a guard written against a key the real CLI never emits.\n\nNew order: **detected harness → PATH probe (unchanged order) → none.**\n\nStyle precedent for env reads: `agent_policy.go:14-25` (`brainNoEgressMode`, `envBool`). Keep the\nexisting name mapping — the function returns `\"claude-code\"` while probing the binary `\"claude\"`.\n\n**B2 — Announce the choice, and wire up the dead warning.**\n\nPrint the chosen agent before any token spend, mirroring the documented ordering rule at\n`setup.go:966-972` (the cost line must precede the spend so the user can Ctrl-C). Writer chain is\n`newRefreshProgress(cmd.ErrOrStderr())` (`progress.go:224`), which degrades to prefixed plain\nlines when piped. Suppress under `--json` as `setup.go:1257` already does.\n\nAt the same site, call `ollamaModelMissingWarning` — already written and already tested, just\nnever invoked. This makes two false source comments true.\n\n**B3 — Keep the signature change contained.**\n\n`defaultRefreshAgent(ctx, runner, repoDir)` has no access to `opts`/`cmd`, and three existing tests\ncall it with that 3-arg shape (`refresh_test.go:22`, `refresh_ollama_auto_test.go:34`,\n`local_agent_preference_test.go:63`). Threading a writer through all 13 call sites is invasive and\nwould churn the tests.\n\nInstead: **leave the pure function alone**, add a thin wrapper that resolves + announces, and use\nit at the three user-facing sites — `refresh.go:145`, `distill_cmd.go:710`, `setup.go:1271` (which\nalready has a `steps.detectAgent` seam). Internal/non-interactive callers keep the pure function.\n\n**B4 — `watch` on main never reaches the function at all.** `watch.go:108` hardcodes `\"codex\"`;\nthe feature branch changed it to `\"auto\"` (`watch.go:120`). On main this is a third codex default.\nFix with B1 or it survives the reorder.\n\n### Deferred: the interactive prompt\n\nThe reporter also asked for a CLI choice. Worth doing, but **after** B1–B4 land, because it is the\ninvasive part. When done, copy the only interactive prompt in the CLI verbatim —\n`promptSeedTimeoutAction` (`seed.go:1792-1809`): guard on `opts.noInteractive || !stdinIsTerminal()`\n(`seed.go:1811`) and return the fallback; prompt to **stderr**, read stdin, **any error falls back**.\nNo prompt library exists here — `bubbletea`/`lipgloss` are dashboard-only. A prompt that is not\nTTY-gated hangs every piped install forever.\n\n---\n\n## Files to modify\n\n| file | change |\n|---|---|\n| `internal/cli/semantic.go` | ignore list `:2473`, pathspec list `:2408`, refusal message `:594` |\n| `internal/cli/seed.go` | refusal message `:276` |\n| `internal/cli/refresh.go` | `defaultRefreshAgent` `:851`/`:741`, announce wrapper, call `ollamaModelMissingWarning` |\n| `internal/cli/distill_cmd.go` | use the announcing wrapper at `:710` |\n| `internal/cli/setup.go` | use it via the `steps.detectAgent` seam at `:1271` |\n| `internal/cli/watch.go` | `\"codex\"` → `\"auto\"` at `:108` (main only) |\n\n## Branching\n\nBoth defects are on **main**, so this is a **separate PR off main** — not stacked on #331, which is\ngreen and awaiting approval; touching it reopens agent review on clean work.\n\nOne exception: `ollamaModelMissingWarning` and the ollama comment block exist **only** on the\nfeature branch. If B2's wiring of that warning is wanted, that piece stacks. Confirm before\nstarting; the rest is main-safe either way.\n\n## Verification\n\nPer the repo's own doctrine, every guard is **verified by weakening**: patch it compile-clean,\nshow the test red, quote the failing assertion, restore.\n\n**Fix A**\n1. Repo dirty **only** with `AGENTS.md`/`CLAUDE.md`/`.claude/settings.json` → `setup` seeds and\n   indexes clean. Weaken by removing the new entries → test red.\n2. Repo with one dirty **source** file → both refusals still fire. This is the guard that stops\n   the fix becoming \"ignore everything\".\n3. A user `.brainignore` still applies, and built-ins do not replace it.\n4. Refusal message names the offending paths.\n\n**End-to-end, the actual reported bug:** fresh clone → `entire graph init-agents` →\n`entire brain setup`. Must succeed. It currently fails. This is the acceptance test.\n\n**Fix B**\n5. `CLAUDECODE` set + `codex` on PATH → picks `claude-code`. Weaken by dropping detection → red.\n6. No harness env, no TTY → deterministic, no prompt, never hangs.\n7. The chosen agent is announced on stderr; silent under `--json`.\n8. `ollamaModelMissingWarning` fires when ollama is present and something else is chosen —\n   currently unreachable, so this test fails before the fix.\n\n**Constraints:** no full local suites (CPU-bound) — `GOMAXPROCS=1 go test -p 1 -parallel 1` on\nnarrow packages. This shell exports `FORCE_COLOR=3`, so any colour-asserting test must be\nreproduced on main before being blamed on the change.\n\n## Not doing\n\nMerging, approving, or pushing to any existing PR without explicit approval. The `\" -> \"`\npath-splitting bug is filed separately, not folded in.\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"94086257-9f20-4df9-a6a8-880aa76e777c","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Cfk5iw9kawfgV7bvXmwJq","type":"assistant","uuid":"4d4a9dae-91e9-4b5d-ae23-de9eabd2015c","timestamp":"2026-10-06T01:04:16.118Z","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.290","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"4d4a9dae-91e9-4b5d-ae23-de9eabd2015c","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"e7c90eee-8619-470e-b4f1-6a320f51d5ac","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RrxM9dLwggWP1RRSmEzb57","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/dynamic-petting-globe.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"90a684fb-5f5a-49d3-85fe-54c88fe79aa1","timestamp":"2026-10-06T01:04:16.220Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"update","filePath":"/Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/dynamic-petting-globe.md","content":"# Fix two install-experience defects in entire-brain\n\n## Context\n\nEarly user feedback on brain, both reproduced in source:\n\n> *\"the brain install is really picky about there not being **ANY** changes in any files in git.\n> even the previous config file and agent file updates from the graph extension install.\n> it's not the easiest to figure that out, could be me 😅\"*\n\n> *\"the brain facts import defaults to Codex, idk what model. any chance we could default to\n> Sonnet or Opus? Or maybe ask the user for a choice in the cli flow?\"*\n\nThey are two unrelated defects that both land on a first-time user:\n\n**A. Entire's own installers create the dirt that blocks Entire's install.** `init-agents` writes\n`AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `.claude/settings.json`; the next command refuses because the tree is\ndirty. The reporter blamed themselves. It is not them.\n\n**B. Fact distillation silently routes repo content to Codex**, even for a user sitting inside\nClaude Code, and never says which agent it chose.\n\nBoth are on `main`, not just the unmerged stack. Everything below is `file:line` from source,\nestablished by three exploration passes.\n\n---\n\n## Fix A — Entire-authored config must not block the install\n\n### What is actually broken\n\n`brainIgnore.Ignored` (`internal/cli/semantic.go:2467`) hardcodes a segment list at `:2473`:\n`node_modules, vendor, dist, build, target, .entire`. **`.entire/*` is already exempt.** The gap\nis exactly the three paths outside it: **`AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `.claude/settings.json`**.\n\n`loadBrainIgnore` (`:2433`) otherwise reads only `.brainignore`, which does not exist in a fresh\nrepo — so for a new user the user-pattern set is empty and only the hardcoded list applies.\n\n**There are two refusals, not one.** A dirty install fails both components:\n\n| refusal | file:line | message |\n|---|---|---|\n| seed | `seed.go:276` | `dirty_worktree: refusing to seed uncommitted content without --worktree` |\n| semantic | `semantic.go:594` | `dirty_worktree: refusing to index uncommitted content without --worktree` |\n\nConfirmed call chain for `entire brain setup`: `setup.go:659` → `setup.go:1261` →\n`watch.go:647 runRefresh` (with `watch.go:609 watchDeterministicRefreshOptions`, which leaves\n**both** worktree flags false) → `refresh.go:223` → `refresh.go:274` → `refresh_phases.go:30` →\n`seed.go:271`. Semantic arrives via `refresh.go:401` → `:452` → `refresh_phases.go:36`.\n\nSetup already *recognises* this state — `setupIsDirtyWorktree` (`setup.go:196`), matched at\n`:211`, with a hint at `:133` naming `.entire/` and `.claude/` — but still fails the components.\nThe diagnosis exists; the fix does not.\n\n### Changes\n\n1. **Extend the hardcoded ignore** at `semantic.go:2473` with the three Entire-authored paths.\n   Decided with the user: ignore `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `.claude/settings.json`,\n   `.codex/hooks.json`, `.brainignore` — alongside the existing `.entire`. A user's own hand-edits\n   to `AGENTS.md`/`CLAUDE.md` also stop blocking, which is correct: they are agent config, not\n   indexed source.\n\n   *Justification, so this is not a hack:* the gate exists to stop seeding uncommitted **source**\n   into an index attributed to a commit. Config Entire wrote is not source.\n\n   Matching semantics are already settled (`brainIgnorePatternMatches`, `:2490`): patterns are\n   **anchored at repo root**, trailing `/` means directory-prefix. So `.claude/settings.json` must\n   be written in full — a bare `settings.json` would not match.\n\n2. **Mirror it into `gitPathspecExclusions`** (`semantic.go:2408`), which carries the same\n   built-ins for `git diff` pathspecs and likewise omits `.claude`. Leaving the two lists divergent\n   is how this class of bug recurs.\n\n3. **Make both refusals actionable.** Today they name a flag, not an intent, and never say which\n   files. Include the count and first few offending paths, and state the remedy in plain words:\n   pass `--worktree` to index uncommitted work, or commit/stash first. Apply to `seed.go:276` and\n   `semantic.go:594` together — a user who clears one hits the other.\n\n### Out of scope, but found and worth recording\n\n`worktreeStatusPaths` (`semantic.go:3094`) applies `strings.Cut(path, \" -> \")` to **every** status\nline, not only `R`/`C` rename entries, so a filename literally containing `\" -> \"` splits into two\nbogus paths. Latent, unproven against a live repo. File separately; do not fold in here.\n\n---\n\n## Fix B — stop silently choosing another vendor's agent\n\n### What is actually broken\n\n`defaultRefreshAgent` — `refresh.go:851` (feature branch), `refresh.go:741` (**main**) — is\n`no-egress → codex → claude-code → none`, hardcoded, with **no announcement anywhere**. 13 call\nsites; the only user-visible mention of the chosen agent is setup's backfill spend label\n(`setup.go:1021`, printed at `:974`). Every other path is silent.\n\nThe codebase already made this exact call once, for ollama, in the same function:\n\n> *choosing one is a product decision, not a default worth guessing* … *the caller warns when it\n> falls through, so a privacy-motivated install does not quietly become a cloud call.*\n\n**Both of those claims are presently false.** `ollamaModelMissingWarning` (`refresh.go:893`) has\n**zero non-test callers** — the privacy guard it promises never fires.\n\n### Changes\n\n**B1 — Detect the harness the user is running under, and prefer it.**\n\nVerified by reading this session's own environment: `CLAUDECODE` and `CLAUDE_CODE_ENTRYPOINT` are\ngenuinely set inside Claude Code. That is detection, not guessing.\n\n**No Codex signal is verified.** `CODEX_HOME` (`skill_form.go:114`) is write-destination\nresolution, not detection, and the `CODEX_COMPANION_*` vars present here come from a Claude Code\nplugin, not from Codex. So: detect Claude Code positively; leave Codex to the existing PATH probe\nuntil a signal is confirmed on a real Codex run. Inventing one would repeat a mistake already in\nmemory — a guard written against a key the real CLI never emits.\n\nNew order: **detected harness → PATH probe (unchanged order) → none.**\n\nStyle precedent for env reads: `agent_policy.go:14-25` (`brainNoEgressMode`, `envBool`). Keep the\nexisting name mapping — the function returns `\"claude-code\"` while probing the binary `\"claude\"`.\n\n**B2 — Announce the choice, and wire up the dead warning.**\n\nPrint the chosen agent before any token spend, mirroring the documented ordering rule at\n`setup.go:966-972` (the cost line must precede the spend so the user can Ctrl-C). Writer chain is\n`newRefreshProgress(cmd.ErrOrStderr())` (`progress.go:224`), which degrades to prefixed plain\nlines when piped. Suppress under `--json` as `setup.go:1257` already does.\n\nAt the same site, call `ollamaModelMissingWarning` — already written and already tested, just\nnever invoked. This makes two false source comments true.\n\n**B3 — Keep the signature change contained.**\n\n`defaultRefreshAgent(ctx, runner, repoDir)` has no access to `opts`/`cmd`, and three existing tests\ncall it with that 3-arg shape (`refresh_test.go:22`, `refresh_ollama_auto_test.go:34`,\n`local_agent_preference_test.go:63`). Threading a writer through all 13 call sites is invasive and\nwould churn the tests.\n\nInstead: **leave the pure function alone**, add a thin wrapper that resolves + announces, and use\nit at the three user-facing sites — `refresh.go:145`, `distill_cmd.go:710`, `setup.go:1271` (which\nalready has a `steps.detectAgent` seam). Internal/non-interactive callers keep the pure function.\n\n**B4 — `watch` on main never reaches the function at all.** `watch.go:108` hardcodes `\"codex\"`;\nthe feature branch changed it to `\"auto\"` (`watch.go:120`). On main this is a third codex default.\nFix with B1 or it survives the reorder.\n\n### Deferred: the interactive prompt\n\nThe reporter also asked for a CLI choice. Worth doing, but **after** B1–B4 land, because it is the\ninvasive part. When done, copy the only interactive prompt in the CLI verbatim —\n`promptSeedTimeoutAction` (`seed.go:1792-1809`): guard on `opts.noInteractive || !stdinIsTerminal()`\n(`seed.go:1811`) and return the fallback; prompt to **stderr**, read stdin, **any error falls back**.\nNo prompt library exists here — `bubbletea`/`lipgloss` are dashboard-only. A prompt that is not\nTTY-gated hangs every piped install forever.\n\n---\n\n## Files to modify\n\n| file | change |\n|---|---|\n| `internal/cli/semantic.go` | ignore list `:2473`, pathspec list `:2408`, refusal message `:594` |\n| `internal/cli/seed.go` | refusal message `:276` |\n| `internal/cli/refresh.go` | `defaultRefreshAgent` `:851`/`:741`, announce wrapper, call `ollamaModelMissingWarning` |\n| `internal/cli/distill_cmd.go` | use the announcing wrapper at `:710` |\n| `internal/cli/setup.go` | use it via the `steps.detectAgent` seam at `:1271` |\n| `internal/cli/watch.go` | `\"codex\"` → `\"auto\"` at `:108` (main only) |\n\n## Branching\n\nBoth defects are on **main**, so this is a **separate PR off main** — not stacked on #331, which is\ngreen and awaiting approval; touching it reopens agent review on clean work.\n\nOne exception: `ollamaModelMissingWarning` and the ollama comment block exist **only** on the\nfeature branch. If B2's wiring of that warning is wanted, that piece stacks. Confirm before\nstarting; the rest is main-safe either way.\n\n## Verification\n\nPer the repo's own doctrine, every guard is **verified by weakening**: patch it compile-clean,\nshow the test red, quote the failing assertion, restore.\n\n**Fix A**\n1. Repo dirty **only** with `AGENTS.md`/`CLAUDE.md`/`.claude/settings.json` → `setup` seeds and\n   indexes clean. Weaken by removing the new entries → test red.\n2. Repo with one dirty **source** file → both refusals still fire. This is the guard that stops\n   the fix becoming \"ignore everything\".\n3. A user `.brainignore` still applies, and built-ins do not replace it.\n4. Refusal message names the offending paths.\n\n**End-to-end, the actual reported bug:** fresh clone → `entire graph init-agents` →\n`entire brain setup`. Must succeed. It currently fails. This is the acceptance test.\n\n**Fix B**\n5. `CLAUDECODE` set + `codex` on PATH → picks `claude-code`. Weaken by dropping detection → red.\n6. No harness env, no TTY → deterministic, no prompt, never hangs.\n7. The chosen agent is announced on stderr; silent under `--json`.\n8. `ollamaModelMissingWarning` fires when ollama is present and something else is chosen —\n   currently unreachable, so this test fails before the fix.\n\n**Constraints:** no full local suites (CPU-bound) — `GOMAXPROCS=1 go test -p 1 -parallel 1` on\nnarrow packages. This shell exports `FORCE_COLOR=3`, so any colour-asserting test must be\nreproduced on main before being blamed on the change.\n\n## Not doing\n\nMerging, approving, or pushing to any existing PR without explicit approval. The `\" -> \"`\npath-splitting bug is filed separately, not folded in.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":223,"newStart":1,"newLines":208,"lines":["-# Fix agent usage of Brain + Graph, and verify it in a clean environment","+# Fix two install-experience defects in entire-brain"," "," ## Context"," ","-PRs #329–#331 (unmerged) fixed a text defect that plausibly suppressed tool usage: brain's","-shipped agent guide told agents they could skip the tools, and CI enforced that wording in both","-directions. **Whether fixing it actually raises usage is unmeasured.**","+Early user feedback on brain, both reproduced in source:"," ","-The one experiment run so far is invalid, and it is worth being precise about why: the guide text","-was injected into each agent's *prompt*. That tests whether the wording works once it is already","-in context — the thing nobody doubted. The real-world failure is that the guide *file* never","-changes behaviour. Both arms used the tools 100% of the time, so there was no headroom to detect","-an increase, and n was 2 per arm.","+> *\"the brain install is really picky about there not being **ANY** changes in any files in git.","+> even the previous config file and agent file updates from the graph extension install.","+> it's not the easiest to figure that out, could be me 😅\"*"," ","-This plan replaces that with a clean-environment measurement using real `claude -p` sessions, a","-pre-registered success bar, and a fix/re-measure loop. Three exploration passes established the","-mechanics below; everything cited is `file:line` from source.","+> *\"the brain facts import defaults to Codex, idk what model. any chance we could default to","+> Sonnet or Opus? Or maybe ask the user for a choice in the cli flow?\"*"," ","-### What is now established","+They are two unrelated defects that both land on a first-time user:"," ","-**Guide delivery (entire-brain).** `init-agents` writes `.entire/agent-guide.md`, root `AGENTS.md`,","-root `CLAUDE.md` (carrying `@.entire/agent-guide.md`), and — new in #331 — a `PreToolUse` entry in","-`.claude/settings.json` (`internal/agentsetup/files.go:19,221,249`; `claudehooks.go:46`). `setup`","-writes **none** of them (`setup.go` has no reference to any of those names), which confirms the","-reported \"AGENTS.md never appeared\" as intended behaviour, not a bug. There are almost no gates;","-the only hard one is root resolution (`agent_setup.go:47`).","+**A. Entire's own installers create the dirt that blocks Entire's install.** `init-agents` writes","+`AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `.claude/settings.json`; the next command refuses because the tree is","+dirty. The reporter blamed themselves. It is not them."," ","-**Two hazards in that path.** `ENTIRE_REPO_ROOT` outranks cwd (`env.go:23,73`), so a host that sets","-it can silently install into the outer repo; and the walk-up stops at the *innermost* `.git`","-(`migration.go:94-131`), so a nested clone captures the files. Also: the combined guide carrying","-the Graph directive ships **only when both products are enabled** (`guide.go:128`) — a brain-only","-install gets `BrainGuide()` with no Graph instruction at all (`guide.go:130`).","+**B. Fact distillation silently routes repo content to Codex**, even for a user sitting inside","+Claude Code, and never says which agent it chose."," ","-**Graph has no MCP server, by design.** No MCP/JSON-RPC dependency in `go.mod`, no server under","-`cmd/` or `internal/cli`, and `README.md:268` states it will not expose one. So Bash is the only","-route to Graph, and the guide is correct to name a shell command — but an MCP-first harness has no","-Graph tool at all. This is a constraint to measure around, not a bug to fix.","+Both are on `main`, not just the unmerged stack. Everything below is `file:line` from source,","+established by three exploration passes."," ","-**The measurement already exists and is usable.** `entire graph stats` computes","-`graph_first_rate = GraphFirstSessions / SessionsWithLocate`","-(`entire-graph/internal/cli/stats.go:1183-1189,1236`) from local Claude Code JSONL transcripts in","-`~/.claude/projects/<repo-slug>/` (`:374-386`), and `--sessions-dir` / `--transcript` override that","-path — which is what makes a clean-env arm measurable. Two caveats that change the design:","+---"," ","-- **MCP calls are invisible to it.** Only Bash `entire graph <verb>` / `entire-graph <verb>` count","-  as graph calls (`:1048-1055`); `mcp__entire-brain__*` matches neither bucket. Brain usage","-  therefore needs its own measure.","-- **Pin the binary.** The withdrawn \"82.9M tokens saved\" figure was binary-version drift","-  (`scripts/entire-graph-statusline.sh:115`), and the graph-first rate runs in the same binary.","+## Fix A — Entire-authored config must not block the install"," ","-The exploration could not find the provenance of the quoted `332 / 96,987 (0.34%)` baseline — it is","-only ever quoted, never derived. Treat it as context, not as this experiment's control.","+### What is actually broken"," ","-### The two unknowns that decide everything","+`brainIgnore.Ignored` (`internal/cli/semantic.go:2467`) hardcodes a segment list at `:2473`:","+`node_modules, vendor, dist, build, target, .entire`. **`.entire/*` is already exempt.** The gap","+is exactly the three paths outside it: **`AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `.claude/settings.json`**."," ","-Neither is answerable from source, and both are cheap to settle:","+`loadBrainIgnore` (`:2433`) otherwise reads only `.brainignore`, which does not exist in a fresh","+repo — so for a new user the user-pattern set is empty and only the hardcoded list applies."," ","-1. **Does the model actually receive the guide** through `CLAUDE.md`'s `@.entire/agent-guide.md`","-   import? If not, every wording fix in #331 is inert.","-2. **Is `$CLAUDE_FILE_PATH` populated** in a `PreToolUse` hook? #331's wiring passes","-   `--file \"$CLAUDE_FILE_PATH\"`; if that variable is not set, the hook runs with an empty path and","-   **my own hook is a no-op.**","+**There are two refusals, not one.** A dirty install fails both components:"," ","-These run first, as two single sessions, before any arm.","+| refusal | file:line | message |","+|---|---|---|","+| seed | `seed.go:276` | `dirty_worktree: refusing to seed uncommitted content without --worktree` |","+| semantic | `semantic.go:594` | `dirty_worktree: refusing to index uncommitted content without --worktree` |"," ","----","+Confirmed call chain for `entire brain setup`: `setup.go:659` → `setup.go:1261` →","+`watch.go:647 runRefresh` (with `watch.go:609 watchDeterministicRefreshOptions`, which leaves","+**both** worktree flags false) → `refresh.go:223` → `refresh.go:274` → `refresh_phases.go:30` →","+`seed.go:271`. Semantic arrives via `refresh.go:401` → `:452` → `refresh_phases.go:36`."," ","-## Scope: entire-graph is OUT, and that is now settled","+Setup already *recognises* this state — `setupIsDirtyWorktree` (`setup.go:196`), matched at","+`:211`, with a hint at `:133` naming `.entire/` and `.claude/` — but still fails the components.","+The diagnosis exists; the fix does not."," ","-The decoy/ranking problem is the half that makes usage *persist* — 3 of 4 sessions used the tool","-exactly as instructed, got a decoy, and succeeded with grep instead. The","-`redesign-graph-cost-reduction` session answered, and it changes the picture:","+### Changes"," ","-- **Sample-idf is already fixed, unmerged** — PR #291, also inside the launch-candidate stack","-  (#315 at `dd76b8fe`, and `0d92152d`). My earlier `internal/sem/search.go` citations were from a","-  stale build; the current code picks repo-wide DF when an exact corpus is known.","-- **I re-measured with their frozen binary and the decoy reproduces identically.**","-  `entire-graph-0d92152d` (sha256 `09f393fe…`): ranks 1–3 are","-  `brainBriefSemanticNeedsCurrentBoundary` 30.13 / `acquireSemanticIndexLock` 29.38 /","-  `runSemanticIngestTraces` 29.37 — the same scores to 2dp as the old binary, and **neither real","-  decider appears anywhere in the returned set.** So the idf fix does not move this case, which","-  isolates it to name-signal dominance rather than idf. Their follow-up sharpened it further: the","-  deciders being *absent from the returned set* makes this a **recall** failure, not merely an","-  ordering one — no reranking could rescue a candidate that was never returned.","-- **Name dominance is diagnosed, deliberately not patched ad hoc.** `searchNameCoverageWeight=10`","-  is intentionally not idf-weighted; their post-hoc study-6 found the name gap in 25/66 ranking","-  misses vs 16/123 hits, and a scoring emulator showed weight 0 rescuing 6 misses and losing 0","-  hits — emulator evidence only. The real test is a pre-registered \"study 7\" on 12 fresh repos","-  with a paraphrase stratum.","+1. **Extend the hardcoded ignore** at `semantic.go:2473` with the three Entire-authored paths.","+   Decided with the user: ignore `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `.claude/settings.json`,","+   `.codex/hooks.json`, `.brainignore` — alongside the existing `.entire`. A user's own hand-edits","+   to `AGENTS.md`/`CLAUDE.md` also stop blocking, which is correct: they are agent config, not","+   indexed source."," ","-**Codex holds the Go lease on entire-graph, and ranking changes go through that prereg.** So no","-entire-graph file gets touched here — tuning to my single case is exactly what the prereg exists to","-prevent, and they are right about that. Three commitments made to them and kept in this plan:","+   *Justification, so this is not a hack:* the gate exists to stop seeding uncommitted **source**","+   into an index attributed to a commit. Config Entire wrote is not source."," ","-1. The decoy query is **held out** — it goes into an evaluation set only, never a tuning set.","-2. The clean-env arms **pin graph to `0d92152d`**, so they measure their current state rather than","-   the stale installed symlink (which points at a dev checkout).","-3. The repro gets filed as a GitHub issue on `entireio/entire-graph` — recorded, no collision.","+   Matching semantics are already settled (`brainIgnorePatternMatches`, `:2490`): patterns are","+   **anchored at repo root**, trailing `/` means directory-prefix. So `.claude/settings.json` must","+   be written in full — a bare `settings.json` would not match."," ","-One finding handed back to them rather than acted on: `files_scanned=1855` but","-`files_content_read_during_preselection=1853`, with 12 `E_MINIFIED` partial failures in the same","-output. If a deliberate skip counts as \"unread\" and thereby revokes the exact-corpus idf path, that","-is a defect in its own right. They are passing it, plus a suggestion to expose `idf_source` in","-`stats` so it is checkable from outside, to Codex.","+2. **Mirror it into `gitPathspecExclusions`** (`semantic.go:2408`), which carries the same","+   built-ins for `git diff` pathspecs and likewise omits `.claude`. Leaving the two lists divergent","+   is how this class of bug recurs."," ","-**Consequence for the bar below:** Graph ranking will still return this class of decoy during the","-experiment. So the third pre-registered metric — used-then-abandoned — is measuring something this","-plan *cannot* fix. It is reported, not optimised, and if A1 clears rows 1–2 but fails row 3, the","-honest conclusion is \"brain-side fix works; sustained usage is gated on graph ranking\", not a","-failure of #331.","+3. **Make both refusals actionable.** Today they name a flag, not an intent, and never say which","+   files. Include the count and first few offending paths, and state the remedy in plain words:","+   pass `--worktree` to index uncommitted work, or commit/stash first. Apply to `seed.go:276` and","+   `semantic.go:594` together — a user who clears one hits the other."," ","+### Out of scope, but found and worth recording","+","+`worktreeStatusPaths` (`semantic.go:3094`) applies `strings.Cut(path, \" -> \")` to **every** status","+line, not only `R`/`C` rename entries, so a filename literally containing `\" -> \"` splits into two","+bogus paths. Latent, unproven against a live repo. File separately; do not fold in here.","+"," ---"," ","-## Phase 1 — Harness (no model cost)","+## Fix B — stop silently choosing another vendor's agent"," ","-Build under `~/.claude/jobs/<job>/tmp/cleanenv/`, nothing inside `devenv/`.","+### What is actually broken"," ","-- **Pinned binaries.** Build `entire-brain` from the stack tip (`fix/agent-guide-directive-and-discovery`)","-  and record the commit; use the installed `entire-graph` and record its version. Every arm uses","-  the same two binaries.","-- **One fresh clone per arm**, each with no `.entire/`, no `CLAUDE.md`, no `AGENTS.md`, so arms","-  cannot contaminate each other. `ENTIRE_REPO_ROOT` explicitly unset in every arm (it outranks cwd).","-- **Instrumentation, three independent channels** — because no single one sees everything:","-  | channel | catches | why needed |","-  |---|---|---|","-  | PATH shim logging every `entire` call with a run id | all Brain + Graph **CLI** calls, in order | the only ordered record of what the agent actually ran |","-  | `entire graph stats --sessions-dir <arm>` | `graph_first_rate`, graph calls, exploration calls | the project's own metric, so before/after is comparable |","-  | transcript grep for `mcp__entire-brain__` | Brain **MCP** usage | invisible to `graph stats` |","-- **Isolated transcript dir per arm** so `--sessions-dir` reads only that arm's sessions.","-- A fixed task set (6–8 locate/explain/change tasks) written once and reused verbatim across arms.","+`defaultRefreshAgent` — `refresh.go:851` (feature branch), `refresh.go:741` (**main**) — is","+`no-egress → codex → claude-code → none`, hardcoded, with **no announcement anywhere**. 13 call","+sites; the only user-visible mention of the chosen agent is setup's backfill spend label","+(`setup.go:1021`, printed at `:974`). Every other path is silent."," ","-## Phase 2 — Settle the two unknowns (2 sessions)","+The codebase already made this exact call once, for ollama, in the same function:"," ","-- **Probe A:** `claude -p \"quote the sentence in your instructions about your FIRST action\"` with cwd","-  in an `init-agents`-installed clone. Establishes whether the `@` import reaches the model.","-- **Probe B:** a session told to edit one file; check the shim log for a `hook pre-edit --file <path>`","-  call with a **non-empty** path. Establishes whether `$CLAUDE_FILE_PATH` works.","+> *choosing one is a product decision, not a default worth guessing* … *the caller warns when it","+> falls through, so a privacy-motivated install does not quietly become a cloud call.*"," ","-If Probe A fails, the fix is to inline the directive into `CLAUDE.md` rather than import it, and","-everything downstream re-runs. If Probe B fails, #331's hook wiring is corrected before the arms run.","+**Both of those claims are presently false.** `ollamaModelMissingWarning` (`refresh.go:893`) has","+**zero non-test callers** — the privacy guard it promises never fires."," ","-## Phase 3 — Arms, pre-registered","+### Changes"," ","-Three arms, **n ≥ 10 sessions each**, same tasks, same binaries, fresh clone per arm:","+**B1 — Detect the harness the user is running under, and prefer it.**"," ","-- **A0 — no guide.** `setup` only, no `init-agents`. The true baseline.","-- **A1 — guide only.** `init-agents`, hook entry removed from `.claude/settings.json`.","-- **A2 — guide + hook.** Full `init-agents`. Isolates whether wording alone sufficed.","+Verified by reading this session's own environment: `CLAUDECODE` and `CLAUDE_CODE_ENTRYPOINT` are","+genuinely set inside Claude Code. That is detection, not guessing."," ","-**Pre-registered bar, fixed before the first session runs:**","+**No Codex signal is verified.** `CODEX_HOME` (`skill_form.go:114`) is write-destination","+resolution, not detection, and the `CODEX_COMPANION_*` vars present here come from a Claude Code","+plugin, not from Codex. So: detect Claude Code positively; leave Codex to the existing PATH probe","+until a signal is confirmed on a real Codex run. Inventing one would repeat a mistake already in","+memory — a guard written against a key the real CLI never emits."," ","-| metric | A0 expectation | pass condition for A1 |","-|---|---|---|","-| sessions with ≥1 Graph or Brain call | low | **≥ 9/10** |","-| `graph_first_rate` | ~0 | **≥ 0.7** |","-| sessions that used a tool then abandoned it for grep | — | **≤ 3/10** |","+New order: **detected harness → PATH probe (unchanged order) → none.**"," ","-n=10 per arm is adequate *for an effect this large* — 0/10 vs 7/10 is Fisher exact p < 0.001 — and","-is not adequate for a small one. If the observed effect is small, the honest outcome is \"not","-established at this n\", not a wider search for a subgroup that worked.","+Style precedent for env reads: `agent_policy.go:14-25` (`brainNoEgressMode`, `envBool`). Keep the","+existing name mapping — the function returns `\"claude-code\"` while probing the binary `\"claude\"`."," ","-The third row is the one that matters most and the one the earlier run exposed: first-call","-compliance can rise while sustained usage stays flat.","+**B2 — Announce the choice, and wire up the dead warning.**"," ","-**Fairness rules, fixed in advance.** The graph session's warning is that their past A/Bs \"died of","-asymmetric prompts\", which matches this project's own benchmark doctrine, so these are not","-negotiable mid-run:","+Print the chosen agent before any token spend, mirroring the documented ordering rule at","+`setup.go:966-972` (the cost line must precede the spend so the user can Ctrl-C). Writer chain is","+`newRefreshProgress(cmd.ErrOrStderr())` (`progress.go:224`), which degrades to prefixed plain","+lines when piped. Suppress under `--json` as `setup.go:1257` already does."," ","-- **Symmetric instructions.** The task text is byte-identical across arms. The *only* difference is","-  the guide under test, which arrives through `init-agents` rather than the prompt. Test for any","-  sentence I am tempted to add: *would this help an arm that has no guide?* If yes, it goes in all","-  arms or none.","-- **Paired, symmetric gating.** A task counts only when every arm completed it; a task that fails","-  in one arm is dropped from all of them, not just the one that failed.","-- **Report the median and a bootstrap CI beside every rate**, with raw counts — not a mean alone.","+At the same site, call `ollamaModelMissingWarning` — already written and already tested, just","+never invoked. This makes two false source comments true."," ","-## Phase 4 — Ask every session what went wrong","+**B3 — Keep the signature change contained.**"," ","-After each task, a follow-up turn in the same session: what was your first action, did you reach","-for Brain or Graph, if not why not, what did the tool return, was it useful, what would have made","-you use it. Collected verbatim.","+`defaultRefreshAgent(ctx, runner, repoDir)` has no access to `opts`/`cmd`, and three existing tests","+call it with that 3-arg shape (`refresh_test.go:22`, `refresh_ollama_auto_test.go:34`,","+`local_agent_preference_test.go:63`). Threading a writer through all 13 call sites is invasive and","+would churn the tests."," ","-This is the highest-yield channel available — it is what exposed the root cause in the first place","-(\"The agent guide says to start substantive tasks with `entire brain brief`… I skipped that\"). It is","-also self-report, so it is used to *find* mechanisms, never to score the arms; scoring comes from","-the three instrumented channels only.","+Instead: **leave the pure function alone**, add a thin wrapper that resolves + announces, and use","+it at the three user-facing sites — `refresh.go:145`, `distill_cmd.go:710`, `setup.go:1271` (which","+already has a `steps.detectAgent` seam). Internal/non-interactive callers keep the pure function."," ","-## Phase 5 — Loop","+**B4 — `watch` on main never reaches the function at all.** `watch.go:108` hardcodes `\"codex\"`;","+the feature branch changed it to `\"auto\"` (`watch.go:120`). On main this is a third codex default.","+Fix with B1 or it survives the reorder."," ","-Each round: read the feedback, find the top blocker, fix it in the stack (brain side) or hand it to","-the graph session, re-run the affected arm, re-check against the same pre-registered bar. Stop when","-A1 or A2 clears the bar on a round where no new blocker class appeared, or when a round produces a","-blocker that is a product decision rather than a defect — which comes back to you rather than","-getting guessed.","+### Deferred: the interactive prompt"," ","-**Candidate blockers already identified**, to check rather than assume: the `@`-import path (Probe A);","-`$CLAUDE_FILE_PATH` (Probe B); brain-only installs getting no Graph directive (`guide.go:128,130`);","-`ENTIRE_REPO_ROOT` mis-targeting; and MCP-first sessions having no Graph route at all, which no","-wording can fix.","+The reporter also asked for a CLI choice. Worth doing, but **after** B1–B4 land, because it is the","+invasive part. When done, copy the only interactive prompt in the CLI verbatim —","+`promptSeedTimeoutAction` (`seed.go:1792-1809`): guard on `opts.noInteractive || !stdinIsTerminal()`","+(`seed.go:1811`) and return the fallback; prompt to **stderr**, read stdin, **any error falls back**.","+No prompt library exists here — `bubbletea`/`lipgloss` are dashboard-only. A prompt that is not","+TTY-gated hangs every piped install forever."," "," ---"," ","-## Cost, stated up front","+## Files to modify"," ","-Roughly 32+ real `claude -p` sessions (2 probes + 3 arms × 10) plus a feedback turn each, at a","-locate task's typical size. Order of a few million tokens per full round, and the loop may need more","-than one round. Sonnet, small tasks, and arms re-run individually rather than all three each time.","-Say the word if you want a smaller first round — 5 per arm would still separate 0 from 0.7.","+| file | change |","+|---|---|","+| `internal/cli/semantic.go` | ignore list `:2473`, pathspec list `:2408`, refusal message `:594` |","+| `internal/cli/seed.go` | refusal message `:276` |","+| `internal/cli/refresh.go` | `defaultRefreshAgent` `:851`/`:741`, announce wrapper, call `ollamaModelMissingWarning` |","+| `internal/cli/distill_cmd.go` | use the announcing wrapper at `:710` |","+| `internal/cli/setup.go` | use it via the `steps.detectAgent` seam at `:1271` |","+| `internal/cli/watch.go` | `\"codex\"` → `\"auto\"` at `:108` (main only) |"," ","+## Branching","+","+Both defects are on **main**, so this is a **separate PR off main** — not stacked on #331, which is","+green and awaiting approval; touching it reopens agent review on clean work.","+","+One exception: `ollamaModelMissingWarning` and the ollama comment block exist **only** on the","+feature branch. If B2's wiring of that warning is wanted, that piece stacks. Confirm before","+starting; the rest is main-safe either way.","+"," ## Verification"," ","-The deliverable is not \"the tests pass\" — it is a number against a bar fixed in advance:","+Per the repo's own doctrine, every guard is **verified by weakening**: patch it compile-clean,","+show the test red, quote the failing assertion, restore."," ","-1. Phase 2 probes answered yes/no with the evidence inline.","-2. A table of A0 / A1 / A2 on all three metrics, with counts and a median + bootstrap CI beside","-   every rate, and the exact commands and both pinned binary versions that produced them.","-3. Every fix made during the loop carries a regression test verified by weakening — guard patched","-   compile-clean, test shown red, assertion quoted.","-4. The verbatim feedback, including anything that contradicts the result.","-5. If the bar is not cleared, that is reported as the finding, with what remains unfixed. A result","-   that says \"usage did not improve\" is a successful execution of this plan.","+**Fix A**","+1. Repo dirty **only** with `AGENTS.md`/`CLAUDE.md`/`.claude/settings.json` → `setup` seeds and","+   indexes clean. Weaken by removing the new entries → test red.","+2. Repo with one dirty **source** file → both refusals still fire. This is the guard that stops","+   the fix becoming \"ignore everything\".","+3. A user `.brainignore` still applies, and built-ins do not replace it.","+4. Refusal message names the offending paths."," ","-Nothing merges without your approval; PRs #329–#331 stay unmerged and this work stacks on #331.","+**End-to-end, the actual reported bug:** fresh clone → `entire graph init-agents` →","+`entire brain setup`. Must succeed. It currently fails. This is the acceptance test.","+","+**Fix B**","+5. `CLAUDECODE` set + `codex` on PATH → picks `claude-code`. Weaken by dropping detection → red.","+6. No harness env, no TTY → deterministic, no prompt, never hangs.","+7. The chosen agent is announced on stderr; silent under `--json`.","+8. `ollamaModelMissingWarning` fires when ollama is present and something else is chosen —","+   currently unreachable, so this test fails before the fix.","+","+**Constraints:** no full local suites (CPU-bound) — `GOMAXPROCS=1 go test -p 1 -parallel 1` on","+narrow packages. This shell exports `FORCE_COLOR=3`, so any colour-asserting test must be","+reproduced on main before being blamed on the change.","+","+## Not doing","+","+Merging, approving, or pushing to any existing PR without explicit approval. The `\" -> \"`","+path-splitting bug is filed separately, not folded in."]}],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"94086257-9f20-4df9-a6a8-880aa76e777c","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","root":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","branch":"fix/agent-guide-directive-and-discovery","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"entireio","host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"},{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"unknown"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/cli","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"4d4a9dae-91e9-4b5d-ae23-de9eabd2015c","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.290","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
