{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-06T01:05:03.201Z","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a3f95551b258786b9</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2/tasks/a3f95551b258786b9.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Find test patterns for both areas\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Findings below. All paths absolute.\n\n## Q1 — dirty-worktree gate tests\n\nTwo fixture styles exist. **Fake `CommandRunner` with canned `git status --porcelain` is the dominant/house style.** Real-git-in-TempDir is used only by the security-hardening file (it must spawn real git to prove hook/config neutralisation).\n\nFake-runner tests (unit level):\n- `TestWorktreeDirtyKeepsRenameFromIgnoredToPublic` — `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/semantic_test.go:896` — bare `&amp;fakeCommandRunner{}`, canned porcelain, `brainIgnore{patterns: ...}` literal. **Most representative.**\n- `TestWorktreeDirtyUsesExpandedUntrackedStatus` — `.../internal/cli/semantic_test.go:919` — canned runner; scripts BOTH `--porcelain --untracked-files=all` and plain `--porcelain` (because `gitStatusPorcelainAll` tries the expanded form first), then asserts via `fakeRunnerCalled(...)`.\n- `TestSemanticIndexRejectsDirtyWorktreeWithoutWorktreeFlag` — `.../internal/cli/semantic_test.go:557` — `semanticFixtureRunner` + override porcelain to `\" M file.go\\n\"`; asserts `strings.Contains(err.Error(), \"dirty_worktree\")`.\n- `TestSemanticIndexFailsClosedWhenWorktreeStatusUnavailable` — `.../semantic_test.go:570` — same shape, `fakeCommandResponse{err: errors.New(\"status failed\")}`.\n- `TestSemanticIndexFailsIfCleanWorktreeChangesDuringSnapshot` / `...IfDirtyWorktree...` — `.../semantic_test.go:583`, `:598` — uses `runner.sequences[...]` to return clean-then-dirty across two calls.\n- `TestSemanticIndexAndStaleIgnoreBrainignoredDirtyFiles` — `.../semantic_test.go:872` — hybrid: real `.brainignore` file + real dir in `t.TempDir()`, fake runner for git.\n- `TestSeedRejectsDirtyWorktreeWithoutWorktreeFlag` — `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/seed_test.go:400` — command-level, `seedFixtureRepo(t)` (real files in TempDir, no `git init`) + `seedFixtureRunner(repoDir)`, overrides `git status --porcelain --untracked-files=all`, runs through `NewRootCommand` + `execute(t, cmd, \"refresh\",\"seed\",...)`.\n\nReal-git tests (`exec` + `ExecRunner{}`):\n- `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/git_harden_security_test.go:111,142,183,...` — `gitHardenRepo(t)` does a real `git init` in TempDir; uses `loadBrainIgnore(repo)` against the real dir; `gitHardenAssertCommandsRunNoHook` (`:566`) drives `{\"refresh\",\"--agent\",\"none\"}` with `wantErr: \"dirty_worktree\"` (line 574).\n- `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/degenerate_repo_test.go:166` `TestWorktreeRefreshNamesADegenerateRepository` — real `git init`, `Runner: ExecRunner{}`, `t.Skip` if git absent.\n\n`loadBrainIgnore` fixture helpers (write a real `.brainignore` into `t.TempDir()`):\n- `ignoreForTest(t, patterns...)` — `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/brainignore_disclosure_test.go:11` (returns ignore **and** repo dir)\n- `brainIgnoreForTest(t, patterns...)` — `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/semantic_coverage_test.go:209`\n\n`filterWorktreeStatus` — **no direct unit test** (`grep` over `*_test.go` returns zero hits). It is only covered transitively through `worktreeDirtyWithIgnore`. Gap worth filling.\n\nRepresentative fixture setup, quoted verbatim (`semantic_test.go:896-901`):\n\n```go\nfunc TestWorktreeDirtyKeepsRenameFromIgnoredToPublic(t *testing.T) {\n\trepoDir := t.TempDir()\n\tignore := brainIgnore{patterns: []string{\"ignored/\"}}\n\trunner := &amp;fakeCommandRunner{responses: map[string]fakeCommandResponse{\n\t\tfakeCommandKey(\"git\", \"status\", \"--porcelain\"): {stdout: \"R  ignored/file.go -&gt; public/file.go\\n\"},\n\t}}\n\tdirty, err := worktreeDirtyWithIgnore((&amp;cobra.Command{}).Context(), runner, repoDir, ignore)\n```\n\nNote the context idiom: `(&amp;cobra.Command{}).Context()`, not `context.Background()`, in `semantic_test.go`.\n\n## Q2 — agent-selection tests\n\nPATH is **never** manipulated for these. A stub runner answers the `&lt;name&gt; --version` probe. Three distinct local stubs exist (no shared one):\n\n- `availabilityRunner` — `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/local_agent_preference_test.go:9` — keys on `name`:\n```go\ntype availabilityRunner struct{ present map[string]bool }\n\nfunc (a *availabilityRunner) Run(ctx context.Context, dir, name string, args ...string) ([]byte, []byte, error) {\n\tif a.present[name] {\n\t\treturn []byte(name + \" 1.0.0\\n\"), nil, nil\n\t}\n\treturn nil, nil, context.Canceled\n}\n```\n  Used by `TestLocalModelIsPreferredOverACloudAgent` (`:42`, table-driven, `t.Parallel()`) and `TestWatchDefaultsToDetectionNotAHardcodedCloudAgent` (`:74`).\n- `fakeWhichRunner` — `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/refresh_ollama_auto_test.go:9` — same idea, value receiver, also matches `args[0]`. Used by `TestAutoNeverResolvesToOllama` (`:29`) and `TestFallingBackFromOllamaIsDisclosed` (`:55`) — the only `ollamaModelMissingWarning` tests.\n- `fakeCommandRunner` with explicit `--version` keys — `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/refresh_test.go:16` `TestDefaultRefreshAgentHonorsNoEgressMode`: `fakeCommandKey(\"codex\",\"--version\")`, `fakeCommandKey(\"claude\",\"--version\")`, plus `t.Setenv(\"ENTIRE_BRAIN_NO_EGRESS\",\"1\")` and a negative assert `len(runner.calls) != 0`. Note: this test has **no** `t.Parallel()` (it uses `t.Setenv`).\n\nImpl under test: `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/refresh.go:851` (`defaultRefreshAgent`), `:893` (`ollamaModelMissingWarning`), `:904` (`commandLooksAvailable`).\n\nReal PATH-prepending exists elsewhere but for *subprocess* fixtures, not availability probes: `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/seed_test.go:644`, `.../command_regression_test.go:116`, `.../git_harden_probe_test.go:41`, `.../git_no_optional_locks_test.go:102`, `.../doctor_honest_reporting_test.go:536` (`t.Setenv(\"PATH\",\"\")`).\n\n## Q3 — the CommandRunner seam\n\n- Interface: `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/runner.go:17` — single method `Run(ctx, dir, name string, args ...string) ([]byte, []byte, error)` → `(stdout, stderr, err)`.\n- Optional extras, same file: `EnvironmentCommandRunner` (`:26`, `RunWithEnv`), `CommandStreamer` (`:55`, `Stream`), `CommandStream` (`:60`). Production impl is `ExecRunner{}` (same file).\n- Standard test double: `fakeCommandRunner` — `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/export_test.go:15`. Implements `Run`, `RunWithEnv`, `Stream`. Fields: `responses map[string]fakeCommandResponse`, `sequences map[string][]fakeCommandResponse` (per-call-N answers), `fallback func(name, args) (resp, bool)`, `calls []fakeCommandCall` (records `dir/name/args/env/hasDeadline`).\n- Key func: `fakeCommandKey(name, args...)` — `export_test.go:170` (NUL-joined).\n- `fakeCommandResponse{stdout, stderr string; err error}` — `export_test.go:27`.\n- Unscripted-command behaviour matters: unknown key → `errors.New(\"unexpected command: \"+key)`, **except** auto-answers for `git --version`, `git symbolic-ref ... origin/HEAD`, `entire graph version --json` (`export_test.go:80-104`). So you do not need to script those.\n- Call assertion helper: `fakeRunnerCalled(runner, name, args...)` — `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/semantic_test.go:4799`.\n- `runOnlyCommandRunner` — `export_test.go:32` — wrapper that hides `RunWithEnv`/`Stream`, for fail-closed tests.\n\nUsage:\n```go\nrunner := &amp;fakeCommandRunner{responses: map[string]fakeCommandResponse{\n\tfakeCommandKey(\"git\", \"status\", \"--porcelain\"): {stdout: \" M a.go\\n\"},\n}}\ncmd := NewRootCommand(Options{Version: \"test-version\", Env: env, Runner: runner})\nout, err := execute(t, cmd, \"refresh\", \"--agent\", \"none\")\n```\n`execute(t, cmd, args...)` — `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/root_test.go:16` — wires stdout+stderr to ONE buffer, returns `(string, error)`.\n\nRepo-shaped fixtures to reuse rather than reinvent:\n- `seedFixtureRepo(t)` `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/seed_test.go:553` (real files, NO `git init`)\n- `seedFixtureRunner(repoDir)` `.../seed_test.go:581`\n- `semanticFixtureRunner(repoDir, snapshot)` `.../semantic_test.go:4777`\n- `semanticTestEnv(t, repoDir)` `.../semantic_test.go:4725` (four `t.TempDir()`s into `EntireEnv`)\n- `gitHardenBrainEnv(t, repo)` `.../git_harden_security_test.go:549` (same but one root)\n\n## Q4 — interactive / TTY-gated paths\n\n**There are NO interactive prompt tests, because there are no interactive prompts.** `grep` for `Scanln`, `bufio.NewReader(os.Stdin)`, `survey`, `promptui`, `huh.`, `Confirm(` over non-test `internal/cli/*.go` returns zero. The CLI is non-interactive by design.\n\nTTY-gated branches ARE tested. Mechanism = **inject capabilities, never fake a terminal**:\n- `tui.Caps` struct — `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/tui/render.go:31` — `{TTY, Color, Unicode bool; Width int}`. Doc comment at `render.go:20-28` states the rule explicitly: lipgloss's global profile bound to `os.Stdout` \"makes styled output untestable (it depends on how the TEST process was started)\", so `Caps` is \"an explicit, injectable answer\".\n- `tui.PlainCaps()` — `render.go:49` — the byte-stable assert-safe mode.\n- Test helpers: `ttyCaps()` — `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/progress_test.go:16` (`tui.Caps{TTY:true, Color:true, Unicode:true, Width:120}`); `newTestProgress(t, buf, caps)` — `progress_test.go:18`; `stripANSI` — `progress_test.go:43`; `visibleLines` — `progress_test.go:26`.\n- Env matrix is injected too, never `t.Setenv`: `DetectCapsWithEnv(w, lookup EnvLookup)` — `render.go:61`; tests pass `envFrom(map[string]string{...})` — `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/tui/render_test.go:22,47-53`. Same for `SupportsFullScreen(func(string) string)` — `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/tui/layout_test.go:202`.\n- Real-stdin TTY is handled honestly rather than faked: `TestStdinIsReadUnlessItWouldBlockOnAPerson` — `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/hook_payload_test.go:166` — comment says \"THE HANG ITSELF IS NOT REPRODUCIBLE IN-PROCESS... `go test` does not provide one\"; it tests the predicate `hookStdinWouldBlock` (`hook_cmd.go:445`) and compares `os.Stdin` against `stdinIsTerminal()` (`seed.go:1811`) rather than a constant. Paired with a source-level test that the call site consults the predicate (`hook_payload_test.go:198`).\n- Reader-injection for command stdin: `cmd.SetIn(strings.NewReader(...))` — `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/hook_payload_test.go:128,147`, `.../hook_cmd_test.go:104`.\n- Only real second process in the suite: `TestHelperHoldBrainWriteLock` — `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/facts_reclassify_lock_test.go:27` — re-exec'd child, gated on env var + `t.Skip`, reads stdin to hold an flock.\n\n## Q5 — conventions\n\n**`t.Parallel()`**\n- Rule (stated in a prior session note, repeated in `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/docs/testing-for-optimization.md:27`): parallel by default, **not** when mutating process-global state. docs line 27: \"Global publication-hook tests deliberately remain nonparallel.\" *(the \"`t.Parallel()` unless mutating process-global state\" phrasing itself is from a session transcript in `.entire/`, not a tracked doc — unverified as a written rule)*\n- Reality: 375 `t.Parallel()` calls across 76 of 460 test files. **New-style single-concern files are ~100% parallel; the big legacy files are 0%.**\n  - Parallel: `local_agent_preference_test.go` (2/2), `refresh_ollama_auto_test.go` (2/2), `dirty_worktree_stall_test.go` (2/2), `unrunnable_remedy_test.go`, `brainignore_disclosure_test.go` (6), `status_cause_ignore_regression_test.go`, `setup_invocation_test.go`, `progress_test.go`.\n  - **Must NOT**: `semantic_test.go` (0), `seed_test.go` (0), `git_harden_security_test.go` (0), `refresh_test.go` (0), `degenerate_repo_test.go` (0). These do `t.Setenv`, `t.Chdir`-ish work, real git, and shared brain-dir locks.\n  - Concrete trap: `t.Setenv` + `t.Parallel()` panics in Go. `refresh_test.go:16` uses `t.Setenv(\"ENTIRE_BRAIN_NO_EGRESS\",\"1\")` → must stay serial. **If you add a `t.Parallel()` to a new agent-selection test, do not put it in the same func as `t.Setenv`.**\n  - 9 files contain both calls in different funcs (e.g. `setup_test.go`, `mcp_test.go`) — legal, just not in the same test.\n\n**Error-string / code assertions**\n- No generic helper. House style is inline:\n  `if err == nil || !strings.Contains(err.Error(), \"dirty_worktree\") { t.Fatalf(\"... err = %v, want dirty_worktree\", err) }` — `seed_test.go:406`, `semantic_test.go:565`.\n- For the code itself, reference the **constant, not the literal**: `dirtyWorktreeErrorCode = \"dirty_worktree\"` at `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/export.go:967`. `dirty_worktree_stall_test.go:45` asserts on the *identifier name* appearing in source.\n- Table-driven multi-verb error assert pattern: `{argv: []string{...}, wantErr: \"dirty_worktree\"}` — `git_harden_security_test.go:570-592`.\n- Typed-code helpers exist for other domains and are the model if you want one: `requireSessionTombstoneError(t, err, code, state)` — `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/session_tombstone_fail_closed_test.go:28`; `assertCommandJSONContains` — `.../phase1_ci_test.go:69`.\n- JSON error envelope type for `--format json`: `commandJSONError{Code, Message}` — asserted in `root_test.go:27`.\n\n**Golden / snapshot convention — yes, but narrow**\n- Dir: `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/testdata/` and `.../testdata/render/`.\n- Two helpers, deliberately different:\n  - `assertGolden(t, name, got)` — `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/setup_daemon_test.go:30` — plain byte compare for launchd/systemd unit files. **No update env var.**\n  - `checkJSONContract(t, name, value)` — `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/render_json_contract_test.go:34` — round-trips the golden through the real `writeJSON`, not a reimplementation. Regenerate with `ENTIRE_BRAIN_UPDATE_GOLDEN=1` (const `goldenUpdateEnv`, `:32`). CRLF is normalised before compare.\n  - MCP tool surface: `mcp_test.go:2147` writes the golden back when the env var is set (`:2155`).\n- **Rule for goldens**: captured from a real run then **scrubbed** — home dirs → `/home/example/...`, temps → `/tmp/example`. `benchmarks/agent-brain/test_publication_safety.py` fails the build on a leaked contributor path (documented `render_json_contract_test.go:26-31`).\n- `.gitattributes` pins goldens to `eol=lf`.\n- **There is no golden convention for human-readable CLI output.** Rendered output is asserted with `strings.Contains` on specific lines (`setup_render_test.go:103`) or via `visibleLines`/`stripANSI`. Follow that for any new seed/refresh text, do not add a new golden.\n\n**FORCE_COLOR=3 in your shell — impact: essentially none, with one caveat**\n- `FORCE_COLOR` appears **nowhere** in the repo (`grep` over `*.go`/`*.toml`/`*.md`/`*.json`: zero hits). `terminalCaps` honours only `NO_COLOR` (presence-based, `render.go:88`), `TERM`, `LANG`/`LC_ALL`.\n- Every colour-asserting test injects `tui.Caps` explicitly and writes to a `bytes.Buffer`, and `DetectCapsWithEnv` returns `PlainCaps()` for any non-`*os.File` writer (`render.go:62-65`). So the process env cannot leak in.\n- Colour-asserting tests, for your awareness (all safe, all parallel, all injected):\n  - `TestSetupSummaryColoursEveryPhaseDistinctly` — `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/setup_render_test.go:110` — asserts literal `\"38;5;\"+color+\"m\"` substrings. Most brittle test in the repo w.r.t. colour; it builds `tui.Caps{TTY:true, Color:true,...}` itself.\n  - `TestProgressNoColorProducesNoEscapes` — `.../internal/cli/progress_test.go:378` — asserts **absence** of `\\x1b[3` / `\\x1b[1m`; sets `caps.Color = false` on a struct, does not touch env.\n  - `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/tui/render_test.go:115-125` — NO_COLOR matrix, env injected via `envFrom(...)`.\n- Caveat (unverified): `lipgloss` is imported directly in `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/tui/detail.go` and `render.go`. lipgloss/termenv consult a package-global profile derived from `os.Stdout` at init. If a future test asserts on `detail.go` output without going through `Caps`, your `FORCE_COLOR=3` could matter. No current test does.\n\n**Other house rules you should match**\n- CONTRIBUTING.md item 3: every fix needs a test that **fails without it**, and the PR must include the failure output from a reverted fix.\n- Tests carry long `//` comments naming the issue number and quoting the real broken output (see `local_agent_preference_test.go:21-38`, `unrunnable_remedy_test.go:11-31`). This is strongly enforced by convention — a bare test with no narrative will look foreign.\n- Source-level guard tests are an accepted pattern when behaviour needs infra you cannot build: `readSourceForTest(t, \"refresh.go\")` and `functionBodyForTest(t, src, \"fn\")` — `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/sourceread_testhelper_test.go:11,25`. Both fail loudly on missing/empty input to avoid vacuous passes. Used by `dirty_worktree_stall_test.go:26,43`.\n- Table tests use `map[string]struct{...}` with descriptive sentence-like keys + `t.Run(name, ...)`, not `[]struct` slices (see `local_agent_preference_test.go:45`, `unrunnable_remedy_test.go:41`).\n- Do not run full suites here; targeted `go test ./internal/cli -run '^TestX$' -count=1` is the convention in `docs/testing-for-optimization.md`.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>110304</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>50</tool_uses><duration_ms>319845</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"remove","timestamp":"2026-10-06T01:05:16.325Z","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a3f95551b258786b9</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2/tasks/a3f95551b258786b9.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Find test patterns for both areas\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Findings below. All paths absolute.\n\n## Q1 — dirty-worktree gate tests\n\nTwo fixture styles exist. **Fake `CommandRunner` with canned `git status --porcelain` is the dominant/house style.** Real-git-in-TempDir is used only by the security-hardening file (it must spawn real git to prove hook/config neutralisation).\n\nFake-runner tests (unit level):\n- `TestWorktreeDirtyKeepsRenameFromIgnoredToPublic` — `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/semantic_test.go:896` — bare `&amp;fakeCommandRunner{}`, canned porcelain, `brainIgnore{patterns: ...}` literal. **Most representative.**\n- `TestWorktreeDirtyUsesExpandedUntrackedStatus` — `.../internal/cli/semantic_test.go:919` — canned runner; scripts BOTH `--porcelain --untracked-files=all` and plain `--porcelain` (because `gitStatusPorcelainAll` tries the expanded form first), then asserts via `fakeRunnerCalled(...)`.\n- `TestSemanticIndexRejectsDirtyWorktreeWithoutWorktreeFlag` — `.../internal/cli/semantic_test.go:557` — `semanticFixtureRunner` + override porcelain to `\" M file.go\\n\"`; asserts `strings.Contains(err.Error(), \"dirty_worktree\")`.\n- `TestSemanticIndexFailsClosedWhenWorktreeStatusUnavailable` — `.../semantic_test.go:570` — same shape, `fakeCommandResponse{err: errors.New(\"status failed\")}`.\n- `TestSemanticIndexFailsIfCleanWorktreeChangesDuringSnapshot` / `...IfDirtyWorktree...` — `.../semantic_test.go:583`, `:598` — uses `runner.sequences[...]` to return clean-then-dirty across two calls.\n- `TestSemanticIndexAndStaleIgnoreBrainignoredDirtyFiles` — `.../semantic_test.go:872` — hybrid: real `.brainignore` file + real dir in `t.TempDir()`, fake runner for git.\n- `TestSeedRejectsDirtyWorktreeWithoutWorktreeFlag` — `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/seed_test.go:400` — command-level, `seedFixtureRepo(t)` (real files in TempDir, no `git init`) + `seedFixtureRunner(repoDir)`, overrides `git status --porcelain --untracked-files=all`, runs through `NewRootCommand` + `execute(t, cmd, \"refresh\",\"seed\",...)`.\n\nReal-git tests (`exec` + `ExecRunner{}`):\n- `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/git_harden_security_test.go:111,142,183,...` — `gitHardenRepo(t)` does a real `git init` in TempDir; uses `loadBrainIgnore(repo)` against the real dir; `gitHardenAssertCommandsRunNoHook` (`:566`) drives `{\"refresh\",\"--agent\",\"none\"}` with `wantErr: \"dirty_worktree\"` (line 574).\n- `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/degenerate_repo_test.go:166` `TestWorktreeRefreshNamesADegenerateRepository` — real `git init`, `Runner: ExecRunner{}`, `t.Skip` if git absent.\n\n`loadBrainIgnore` fixture helpers (write a real `.brainignore` into `t.TempDir()`):\n- `ignoreForTest(t, patterns...)` — `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/brainignore_disclosure_test.go:11` (returns ignore **and** repo dir)\n- `brainIgnoreForTest(t, patterns...)` — `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/semantic_coverage_test.go:209`\n\n`filterWorktreeStatus` — **no direct unit test** (`grep` over `*_test.go` returns zero hits). It is only covered transitively through `worktreeDirtyWithIgnore`. Gap worth filling.\n\nRepresentative fixture setup, quoted verbatim (`semantic_test.go:896-901`):\n\n```go\nfunc TestWorktreeDirtyKeepsRenameFromIgnoredToPublic(t *testing.T) {\n\trepoDir := t.TempDir()\n\tignore := brainIgnore{patterns: []string{\"ignored/\"}}\n\trunner := &amp;fakeCommandRunner{responses: map[string]fakeCommandResponse{\n\t\tfakeCommandKey(\"git\", \"status\", \"--porcelain\"): {stdout: \"R  ignored/file.go -&gt; public/file.go\\n\"},\n\t}}\n\tdirty, err := worktreeDirtyWithIgnore((&amp;cobra.Command{}).Context(), runner, repoDir, ignore)\n```\n\nNote the context idiom: `(&amp;cobra.Command{}).Context()`, not `context.Background()`, in `semantic_test.go`.\n\n## Q2 — agent-selection tests\n\nPATH is **never** manipulated for these. A stub runner answers the `&lt;name&gt; --version` probe. Three distinct local stubs exist (no shared one):\n\n- `availabilityRunner` — `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/local_agent_preference_test.go:9` — keys on `name`:\n```go\ntype availabilityRunner struct{ present map[string]bool }\n\nfunc (a *availabilityRunner) Run(ctx context.Context, dir, name string, args ...string) ([]byte, []byte, error) {\n\tif a.present[name] {\n\t\treturn []byte(name + \" 1.0.0\\n\"), nil, nil\n\t}\n\treturn nil, nil, context.Canceled\n}\n```\n  Used by `TestLocalModelIsPreferredOverACloudAgent` (`:42`, table-driven, `t.Parallel()`) and `TestWatchDefaultsToDetectionNotAHardcodedCloudAgent` (`:74`).\n- `fakeWhichRunner` — `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/refresh_ollama_auto_test.go:9` — same idea, value receiver, also matches `args[0]`. Used by `TestAutoNeverResolvesToOllama` (`:29`) and `TestFallingBackFromOllamaIsDisclosed` (`:55`) — the only `ollamaModelMissingWarning` tests.\n- `fakeCommandRunner` with explicit `--version` keys — `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/refresh_test.go:16` `TestDefaultRefreshAgentHonorsNoEgressMode`: `fakeCommandKey(\"codex\",\"--version\")`, `fakeCommandKey(\"claude\",\"--version\")`, plus `t.Setenv(\"ENTIRE_BRAIN_NO_EGRESS\",\"1\")` and a negative assert `len(runner.calls) != 0`. Note: this test has **no** `t.Parallel()` (it uses `t.Setenv`).\n\nImpl under test: `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/refresh.go:851` (`defaultRefreshAgent`), `:893` (`ollamaModelMissingWarning`), `:904` (`commandLooksAvailable`).\n\nReal PATH-prepending exists elsewhere but for *subprocess* fixtures, not availability probes: `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/seed_test.go:644`, `.../command_regression_test.go:116`, `.../git_harden_probe_test.go:41`, `.../git_no_optional_locks_test.go:102`, `.../doctor_honest_reporting_test.go:536` (`t.Setenv(\"PATH\",\"\")`).\n\n## Q3 — the CommandRunner seam\n\n- Interface: `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/runner.go:17` — single method `Run(ctx, dir, name string, args ...string) ([]byte, []byte, error)` → `(stdout, stderr, err)`.\n- Optional extras, same file: `EnvironmentCommandRunner` (`:26`, `RunWithEnv`), `CommandStreamer` (`:55`, `Stream`), `CommandStream` (`:60`). Production impl is `ExecRunner{}` (same file).\n- Standard test double: `fakeCommandRunner` — `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/export_test.go:15`. Implements `Run`, `RunWithEnv`, `Stream`. Fields: `responses map[string]fakeCommandResponse`, `sequences map[string][]fakeCommandResponse` (per-call-N answers), `fallback func(name, args) (resp, bool)`, `calls []fakeCommandCall` (records `dir/name/args/env/hasDeadline`).\n- Key func: `fakeCommandKey(name, args...)` — `export_test.go:170` (NUL-joined).\n- `fakeCommandResponse{stdout, stderr string; err error}` — `export_test.go:27`.\n- Unscripted-command behaviour matters: unknown key → `errors.New(\"unexpected command: \"+key)`, **except** auto-answers for `git --version`, `git symbolic-ref ... origin/HEAD`, `entire graph version --json` (`export_test.go:80-104`). So you do not need to script those.\n- Call assertion helper: `fakeRunnerCalled(runner, name, args...)` — `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/semantic_test.go:4799`.\n- `runOnlyCommandRunner` — `export_test.go:32` — wrapper that hides `RunWithEnv`/`Stream`, for fail-closed tests.\n\nUsage:\n```go\nrunner := &amp;fakeCommandRunner{responses: map[string]fakeCommandResponse{\n\tfakeCommandKey(\"git\", \"status\", \"--porcelain\"): {stdout: \" M a.go\\n\"},\n}}\ncmd := NewRootCommand(Options{Version: \"test-version\", Env: env, Runner: runner})\nout, err := execute(t, cmd, \"refresh\", \"--agent\", \"none\")\n```\n`execute(t, cmd, args...)` — `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/root_test.go:16` — wires stdout+stderr to ONE buffer, returns `(string, error)`.\n\nRepo-shaped fixtures to reuse rather than reinvent:\n- `seedFixtureRepo(t)` `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/seed_test.go:553` (real files, NO `git init`)\n- `seedFixtureRunner(repoDir)` `.../seed_test.go:581`\n- `semanticFixtureRunner(repoDir, snapshot)` `.../semantic_test.go:4777`\n- `semanticTestEnv(t, repoDir)` `.../semantic_test.go:4725` (four `t.TempDir()`s into `EntireEnv`)\n- `gitHardenBrainEnv(t, repo)` `.../git_harden_security_test.go:549` (same but one root)\n\n## Q4 — interactive / TTY-gated paths\n\n**There are NO interactive prompt tests, because there are no interactive prompts.** `grep` for `Scanln`, `bufio.NewReader(os.Stdin)`, `survey`, `promptui`, `huh.`, `Confirm(` over non-test `internal/cli/*.go` returns zero. The CLI is non-interactive by design.\n\nTTY-gated branches ARE tested. Mechanism = **inject capabilities, never fake a terminal**:\n- `tui.Caps` struct — `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/tui/render.go:31` — `{TTY, Color, Unicode bool; Width int}`. Doc comment at `render.go:20-28` states the rule explicitly: lipgloss's global profile bound to `os.Stdout` \"makes styled output untestable (it depends on how the TEST process was started)\", so `Caps` is \"an explicit, injectable answer\".\n- `tui.PlainCaps()` — `render.go:49` — the byte-stable assert-safe mode.\n- Test helpers: `ttyCaps()` — `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/progress_test.go:16` (`tui.Caps{TTY:true, Color:true, Unicode:true, Width:120}`); `newTestProgress(t, buf, caps)` — `progress_test.go:18`; `stripANSI` — `progress_test.go:43`; `visibleLines` — `progress_test.go:26`.\n- Env matrix is injected too, never `t.Setenv`: `DetectCapsWithEnv(w, lookup EnvLookup)` — `render.go:61`; tests pass `envFrom(map[string]string{...})` — `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/tui/render_test.go:22,47-53`. Same for `SupportsFullScreen(func(string) string)` — `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/tui/layout_test.go:202`.\n- Real-stdin TTY is handled honestly rather than faked: `TestStdinIsReadUnlessItWouldBlockOnAPerson` — `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/hook_payload_test.go:166` — comment says \"THE HANG ITSELF IS NOT REPRODUCIBLE IN-PROCESS... `go test` does not provide one\"; it tests the predicate `hookStdinWouldBlock` (`hook_cmd.go:445`) and compares `os.Stdin` against `stdinIsTerminal()` (`seed.go:1811`) rather than a constant. Paired with a source-level test that the call site consults the predicate (`hook_payload_test.go:198`).\n- Reader-injection for command stdin: `cmd.SetIn(strings.NewReader(...))` — `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/hook_payload_test.go:128,147`, `.../hook_cmd_test.go:104`.\n- Only real second process in the suite: `TestHelperHoldBrainWriteLock` — `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/facts_reclassify_lock_test.go:27` — re-exec'd child, gated on env var + `t.Skip`, reads stdin to hold an flock.\n\n## Q5 — conventions\n\n**`t.Parallel()`**\n- Rule (stated in a prior session note, repeated in `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/docs/testing-for-optimization.md:27`): parallel by default, **not** when mutating process-global state. docs line 27: \"Global publication-hook tests deliberately remain nonparallel.\" *(the \"`t.Parallel()` unless mutating process-global state\" phrasing itself is from a session transcript in `.entire/`, not a tracked doc — unverified as a written rule)*\n- Reality: 375 `t.Parallel()` calls across 76 of 460 test files. **New-style single-concern files are ~100% parallel; the big legacy files are 0%.**\n  - Parallel: `local_agent_preference_test.go` (2/2), `refresh_ollama_auto_test.go` (2/2), `dirty_worktree_stall_test.go` (2/2), `unrunnable_remedy_test.go`, `brainignore_disclosure_test.go` (6), `status_cause_ignore_regression_test.go`, `setup_invocation_test.go`, `progress_test.go`.\n  - **Must NOT**: `semantic_test.go` (0), `seed_test.go` (0), `git_harden_security_test.go` (0), `refresh_test.go` (0), `degenerate_repo_test.go` (0). These do `t.Setenv`, `t.Chdir`-ish work, real git, and shared brain-dir locks.\n  - Concrete trap: `t.Setenv` + `t.Parallel()` panics in Go. `refresh_test.go:16` uses `t.Setenv(\"ENTIRE_BRAIN_NO_EGRESS\",\"1\")` → must stay serial. **If you add a `t.Parallel()` to a new agent-selection test, do not put it in the same func as `t.Setenv`.**\n  - 9 files contain both calls in different funcs (e.g. `setup_test.go`, `mcp_test.go`) — legal, just not in the same test.\n\n**Error-string / code assertions**\n- No generic helper. House style is inline:\n  `if err == nil || !strings.Contains(err.Error(), \"dirty_worktree\") { t.Fatalf(\"... err = %v, want dirty_worktree\", err) }` — `seed_test.go:406`, `semantic_test.go:565`.\n- For the code itself, reference the **constant, not the literal**: `dirtyWorktreeErrorCode = \"dirty_worktree\"` at `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/export.go:967`. `dirty_worktree_stall_test.go:45` asserts on the *identifier name* appearing in source.\n- Table-driven multi-verb error assert pattern: `{argv: []string{...}, wantErr: \"dirty_worktree\"}` — `git_harden_security_test.go:570-592`.\n- Typed-code helpers exist for other domains and are the model if you want one: `requireSessionTombstoneError(t, err, code, state)` — `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/session_tombstone_fail_closed_test.go:28`; `assertCommandJSONContains` — `.../phase1_ci_test.go:69`.\n- JSON error envelope type for `--format json`: `commandJSONError{Code, Message}` — asserted in `root_test.go:27`.\n\n**Golden / snapshot convention — yes, but narrow**\n- Dir: `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/testdata/` and `.../testdata/render/`.\n- Two helpers, deliberately different:\n  - `assertGolden(t, name, got)` — `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/setup_daemon_test.go:30` — plain byte compare for launchd/systemd unit files. **No update env var.**\n  - `checkJSONContract(t, name, value)` — `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/render_json_contract_test.go:34` — round-trips the golden through the real `writeJSON`, not a reimplementation. Regenerate with `ENTIRE_BRAIN_UPDATE_GOLDEN=1` (const `goldenUpdateEnv`, `:32`). CRLF is normalised before compare.\n  - MCP tool surface: `mcp_test.go:2147` writes the golden back when the env var is set (`:2155`).\n- **Rule for goldens**: captured from a real run then **scrubbed** — home dirs → `/home/example/...`, temps → `/tmp/example`. `benchmarks/agent-brain/test_publication_safety.py` fails the build on a leaked contributor path (documented `render_json_contract_test.go:26-31`).\n- `.gitattributes` pins goldens to `eol=lf`.\n- **There is no golden convention for human-readable CLI output.** Rendered output is asserted with `strings.Contains` on specific lines (`setup_render_test.go:103`) or via `visibleLines`/`stripANSI`. Follow that for any new seed/refresh text, do not add a new golden.\n\n**FORCE_COLOR=3 in your shell — impact: essentially none, with one caveat**\n- `FORCE_COLOR` appears **nowhere** in the repo (`grep` over `*.go`/`*.toml`/`*.md`/`*.json`: zero hits). `terminalCaps` honours only `NO_COLOR` (presence-based, `render.go:88`), `TERM`, `LANG`/`LC_ALL`.\n- Every colour-asserting test injects `tui.Caps` explicitly and writes to a `bytes.Buffer`, and `DetectCapsWithEnv` returns `PlainCaps()` for any non-`*os.File` writer (`render.go:62-65`). So the process env cannot leak in.\n- Colour-asserting tests, for your awareness (all safe, all parallel, all injected):\n  - `TestSetupSummaryColoursEveryPhaseDistinctly` — `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/setup_render_test.go:110` — asserts literal `\"38;5;\"+color+\"m\"` substrings. Most brittle test in the repo w.r.t. colour; it builds `tui.Caps{TTY:true, Color:true,...}` itself.\n  - `TestProgressNoColorProducesNoEscapes` — `.../internal/cli/progress_test.go:378` — asserts **absence** of `\\x1b[3` / `\\x1b[1m`; sets `caps.Color = false` on a struct, does not touch env.\n  - `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/tui/render_test.go:115-125` — NO_COLOR matrix, env injected via `envFrom(...)`.\n- Caveat (unverified): `lipgloss` is imported directly in `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/tui/detail.go` and `render.go`. lipgloss/termenv consult a package-global profile derived from `os.Stdout` at init. If a future test asserts on `detail.go` output without going through `Caps`, your `FORCE_COLOR=3` could matter. No current test does.\n\n**Other house rules you should match**\n- CONTRIBUTING.md item 3: every fix needs a test that **fails without it**, and the PR must include the failure output from a reverted fix.\n- Tests carry long `//` comments naming the issue number and quoting the real broken output (see `local_agent_preference_test.go:21-38`, `unrunnable_remedy_test.go:11-31`). This is strongly enforced by convention — a bare test with no narrative will look foreign.\n- Source-level guard tests are an accepted pattern when behaviour needs infra you cannot build: `readSourceForTest(t, \"refresh.go\")` and `functionBodyForTest(t, src, \"fn\")` — `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide/internal/cli/sourceread_testhelper_test.go:11,25`. Both fail loudly on missing/empty input to avoid vacuous passes. Used by `dirty_worktree_stall_test.go:26,43`.\n- Table tests use `map[string]struct{...}` with descriptive sentence-like keys + `t.Run(name, ...)`, not `[]struct` slices (see `local_agent_preference_test.go:45`, `unrunnable_remedy_test.go:41`).\n- Do not run full suites here; targeted `go test ./internal/cli -run '^TestX$' -count=1` is the convention in `docs/testing-for-optimization.md`.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>110304</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>50</tool_uses><duration_ms>319845</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>","reason":"absorbed_mid_turn","commandUuid":"72f224cb-404e-4334-b045-ca9893310cb7","deliveryId":"73c80c3a-c7a9-45f5-8147-b20bd1ea727b"}
