{"parentUuid":"930ecd57-7cc0-459c-a5fb-ec8c8f65e902","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cfk5rwb1QcSzp2kbAiWqV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"That's the plan's biggest flaw, and I found it before the reviewer did. **`brainIgnore.Ignored` is not the dirty gate — it's the indexing filter**, used in 17 places including `filterSemanticSnapshot` (`:1610`), the snapshot stream (`semantic_stream.go:242`), the file walks (`:5692`), and coverage (`semantic_coverage.go:113`).\n\nAdding `AGENTS.md`/`CLAUDE.md` there would **delete them from the indexed corpus** — a regression dressed as a fix. Correcting the seam:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1752,"cache_read_input_tokens":633402,"output_tokens":2882,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1069},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1752},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2882,"cache_read_input_tokens":633402,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1752,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1752,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"ad1ea1d3-b941-451f-ae99-ee2d6ebcb93f","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cfk5rwCwUoVxqGkR1kT63","type":"assistant","uuid":"d0eda51d-1f95-48eb-a285-7069691444b0","timestamp":"2026-10-06T01:04:59.633Z","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.290","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"d0eda51d-1f95-48eb-a285-7069691444b0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cfk5rwb1QcSzp2kbAiWqV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Azory2UZyiyPqMdx9tNa3B","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/dynamic-petting-globe.md","old_string":"1. **Extend the hardcoded ignore** at `semantic.go:2473` with the three Entire-authored paths.\n   Decided with the user: ignore `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `.claude/settings.json`,\n   `.codex/hooks.json`, `.brainignore` — alongside the existing `.entire`. A user's own hand-edits\n   to `AGENTS.md`/`CLAUDE.md` also stop blocking, which is correct: they are agent config, not\n   indexed source.\n\n   *Justification, so this is not a hack:* the gate exists to stop seeding uncommitted **source**\n   into an index attributed to a commit. Config Entire wrote is not source.\n\n   Matching semantics are already settled (`brainIgnorePatternMatches`, `:2490`): patterns are\n   **anchored at repo root**, trailing `/` means directory-prefix. So `.claude/settings.json` must\n   be written in full — a bare `settings.json` would not match.\n\n2. **Mirror it into `gitPathspecExclusions`** (`semantic.go:2408`), which carries the same\n   built-ins for `git diff` pathspecs and likewise omits `.claude`. Leaving the two lists divergent\n   is how this class of bug recurs.","new_string":"1. **Add a GATE-ONLY ignore — do NOT touch the shared hardcoded list.**\n\n   ⚠️ **The obvious fix is wrong, and this is the most important decision in the plan.**\n   `brainIgnore.Ignored` (`semantic.go:2467`) is **not** the dirty gate — it is the *indexing*\n   filter, used at 17 non-test sites: `filterSemanticSnapshot` (`:1610`, `:1642`), the snapshot\n   stream (`semantic_stream.go:242`, `:244`, `:362`), the file walks (`:3136`, `:3166`, `:5531`,\n   `:5692`, `:5715`), and coverage (`semantic_coverage.go:113`).\n\n   Adding `AGENTS.md`/`CLAUDE.md` to that list would **remove them from the indexed doc corpus** —\n   a regression disguised as a fix. Brain indexes markdown; `AGENTS.md` and `CLAUDE.md` are exactly\n   the kind of repo doc a user expects it to know about.\n\n   **Correct seam:** enrich only the `brainIgnore` *instance* the gate uses. `brainIgnore.patterns`\n   is per-instance and is matched by `brainIgnorePatternMatches` (`:2490`), which is root-anchored\n   and handles exact paths — so `.claude/settings.json` matches as written. Add a\n   `worktreeGateIgnore(repoDir)` helper returning `loadBrainIgnore(repoDir)` with the\n   Entire-authored paths appended to `.patterns`, and use it in `worktreeDirty`\n   (`semantic.go:2924`). Indexing keeps the untouched `loadBrainIgnore`.\n\n   Paths to add, decided with the user: `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `.claude/settings.json`,\n   `.codex/hooks.json`, `.brainignore`. (`.entire/*` is already exempt via the segment rule at\n   `:2473` — no change needed.) A user's own hand-edits to `AGENTS.md`/`CLAUDE.md` also stop\n   blocking the gate, which is correct: they are agent config, not indexed source — and because\n   this is gate-only, they remain **indexed** as before.\n\n   *Justification:* the gate exists to stop seeding uncommitted **source** into an index attributed\n   to a commit. Config Entire wrote is not source. Indexing it is fine; blocking on it is not.\n\n2. **Check `worktreeDirty`'s other callers before landing.** It is also used by\n   `verifySemanticWorktreeStable` (`:2941`) and `semanticStaleReport` (`:3329`). The first is a\n   post-index stability check and the second is read-only reporting; both arguably *should* ignore\n   Entire config too, but that must be a decision, not a side effect. Confirm each, and say so.\n\n3. **Leave `gitPathspecExclusions` (`semantic.go:2408`) ALONE unless proven safe.** It feeds\n   `git diff` pathspecs for change detection; widening it could make brain miss real edits. Only\n   touch it if the adversarial check shows it is gate-only."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1752,"cache_read_input_tokens":633402,"output_tokens":2882,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1069},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1752},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2882,"cache_read_input_tokens":633402,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1752,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1752,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Azory2UZyiyPqMdx9tNa3B":{"file_path":"/Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/dynamic-petting-globe.md","old_string":"1. **Extend the hardcoded ignore** at `semantic.go:2473` with the three Entire-authored paths.\n   Decided with the user: ignore `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `.claude/settings.json`,\n   `.codex/hooks.json`, `.brainignore` — alongside the existing `.entire`. A user's own hand-edits\n   to `AGENTS.md`/`CLAUDE.md` also stop blocking, which is correct: they are agent config, not\n   indexed source.\n\n   *Justification, so this is not a hack:* the gate exists to stop seeding uncommitted **source**\n   into an index attributed to a commit. Config Entire wrote is not source.\n\n   Matching semantics are already settled (`brainIgnorePatternMatches`, `:2490`): patterns are\n   **anchored at repo root**, trailing `/` means directory-prefix. So `.claude/settings.json` must\n   be written in full — a bare `settings.json` would not match.\n\n2. **Mirror it into `gitPathspecExclusions`** (`semantic.go:2408`), which carries the same\n   built-ins for `git diff` pathspecs and likewise omits `.claude`. Leaving the two lists divergent\n   is how this class of bug recurs.","new_string":"1. **Add a GATE-ONLY ignore — do NOT touch the shared hardcoded list.**\n\n   ⚠️ **The obvious fix is wrong, and this is the most important decision in the plan.**\n   `brainIgnore.Ignored` (`semantic.go:2467`) is **not** the dirty gate — it is the *indexing*\n   filter, used at 17 non-test sites: `filterSemanticSnapshot` (`:1610`, `:1642`), the snapshot\n   stream (`semantic_stream.go:242`, `:244`, `:362`), the file walks (`:3136`, `:3166`, `:5531`,\n   `:5692`, `:5715`), and coverage (`semantic_coverage.go:113`).\n\n   Adding `AGENTS.md`/`CLAUDE.md` to that list would **remove them from the indexed doc corpus** —\n   a regression disguised as a fix. Brain indexes markdown; `AGENTS.md` and `CLAUDE.md` are exactly\n   the kind of repo doc a user expects it to know about.\n\n   **Correct seam:** enrich only the `brainIgnore` *instance* the gate uses. `brainIgnore.patterns`\n   is per-instance and is matched by `brainIgnorePatternMatches` (`:2490`), which is root-anchored\n   and handles exact paths — so `.claude/settings.json` matches as written. Add a\n   `worktreeGateIgnore(repoDir)` helper returning `loadBrainIgnore(repoDir)` with the\n   Entire-authored paths appended to `.patterns`, and use it in `worktreeDirty`\n   (`semantic.go:2924`). Indexing keeps the untouched `loadBrainIgnore`.\n\n   Paths to add, decided with the user: `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `.claude/settings.json`,\n   `.codex/hooks.json`, `.brainignore`. (`.entire/*` is already exempt via the segment rule at\n   `:2473` — no change needed.) A user's own hand-edits to `AGENTS.md`/`CLAUDE.md` also stop\n   blocking the gate, which is correct: they are agent config, not indexed source — and because\n   this is gate-only, they remain **indexed** as before.\n\n   *Justification:* the gate exists to stop seeding uncommitted **source** into an index attributed\n   to a commit. Config Entire wrote is not source. Indexing it is fine;