{"parentUuid":"e6a83c0e-7977-4d6e-9904-e0eb8a1d2b85","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cfk5vaNRxrcskMQAk6aCi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Resolved — `promptSeedTimeoutAction` does exist and does read stdin (`Fscanln`, `seed.go:1798`). One agent's grep was wrong. The prompt template is real. Folding in the test conventions and correcting my FORCE_COLOR caution:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1948,"cache_read_input_tokens":646697,"output_tokens":1765,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":587},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1948},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1765,"cache_read_input_tokens":646697,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1948,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1948,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"5e63fa69-1098-44b7-a89e-14e1d5eb318e","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cfk5vZwtA99QoxiiCR3Lj","type":"assistant","uuid":"da212f60-d4f2-4f47-b679-870998b681ce","timestamp":"2026-10-06T01:05:42.513Z","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.290","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"da212f60-d4f2-4f47-b679-870998b681ce","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cfk5vaNRxrcskMQAk6aCi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HSywFAZU8VfAPqsmoiucfB","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/dynamic-petting-globe.md","old_string":"## Verification\n\nPer the repo's own doctrine, every guard is **verified by weakening**: patch it compile-clean,\nshow the test red, quote the failing assertion, restore.","new_string":"## Verification\n\nThe repo already **requires** this: CONTRIBUTING.md item 3 says every fix needs a test that fails\nwithout it, and that the PR must include the failure output from a reverted fix. So weakening is\nnot an extra step here — it is the contribution standard. Patch each guard compile-clean, show the\ntest red, quote the failing assertion, restore.\n\n### Test seams to reuse (do not invent new ones)\n\n- **Command seam:** `CommandRunner` (`runner.go:17`), doubled by `fakeCommandRunner`\n  (`export_test.go:15`) keyed with `fakeCommandKey` (`:170`). It auto-answers `git --version` and\n  friends, so those need no scripting.\n- **Dirty-gate template:** `TestWorktreeDirtyKeepsRenameFromIgnoredToPublic`\n  (`semantic_test.go:896`) — `brainIgnore{patterns: ...}` literal + canned porcelain. This is\n  exactly the shape the gate-only ignore needs. Command-level equivalent:\n  `TestSeedRejectsDirtyWorktreeWithoutWorktreeFlag` (`seed_test.go:400`).\n- **Agent-availability template:** `availabilityRunner` (`local_agent_preference_test.go:9`) —\n  stubs the `<name> --version` probe. PATH is never manipulated for this.\n- Context idiom in these files is `(&cobra.Command{}).Context()`, not `context.Background()`.\n- Assert on the constant `dirtyWorktreeErrorCode` (`export.go:967`), never the bare literal.\n- Human-readable CLI output has **no golden convention** — assert with `strings.Contains` /\n  `visibleLines`. Do not add a golden for the new refusal text.\n\n### Two traps\n\n- **`t.Setenv` + `t.Parallel()` panics in Go.** The harness-detection tests set env, so they must\n  stay serial — and must not share a function with a parallel test. Precedent:\n  `refresh_test.go:16` sets `ENTIRE_BRAIN_NO_EGRESS` and is deliberately non-parallel.\n- **`filterWorktreeStatus` has no direct unit test** — it is only covered transitively. The\n  gate-only ignore runs straight through it, so add one rather than relying on that.\n\n~~FORCE_COLOR~~ — checked and withdrawn: colour tests inject `tui.Caps` explicitly and\n`DetectCapsWithEnv` returns `PlainCaps()` for any non-`*os.File` writer (`render.go:62`), so the\nshell's `FORCE_COLOR=3` cannot leak in. Not a risk for this work."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1948,"cache_read_input_tokens":646697,"output_tokens":1765,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":587},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1948},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1765,"cache_read_input_tokens":646697,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1948,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1948,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01HSywFAZU8VfAPqsmoiucfB":{"file_path":"/Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/dynamic-petting-globe.md","old_string":"## Verification\n\nPer the repo's own doctrine, every guard is **verified by weakening**: patch it compile-clean,\nshow the test red, quote the failing assertion, restore.","new_string":"## Verification\n\nThe repo already **requires** this: CONTRIBUTING.md item 3 says every fix needs a test that fails\nwithout it, and that the PR must include the failure output from a reverted fix. So weakening is\nnot an extra step here — it is the contribution standard. Patch each guard compile-clean, show the\ntest red, quote the failing assertion, restore.\n\n### Test seams to reuse (do not invent new ones)\n\n- **Command seam:** `CommandRunner` (`runner.go:17`), doubled by `fakeCommandRunner`\n  (`export_test.go:15`) keyed with `fakeCommandKey` (`:170`). It auto-answers `git --version` and\n  friends, so those need no scripting.\n- **Dirty-gate template:** `TestWorktreeDirtyKeepsRenameFromIgnoredToPublic`\n  (`semantic_test.go:896`) — `brainIgnore{patterns: ...}` literal + canned porcelain. This is\n  exactly the shape the gate-only ignore needs. Command-level equivalent:\n  `TestSeedRejectsDirtyWorktreeWithoutWorktreeFlag` (`seed_test.go:400`).\n- **Agent-availability template:** `availabilityRunner` (`local_agent_preference_test.go:9`) —\n  stubs the `<name> --version` probe. PATH is never manipulated for this.\n- Context idiom in these files is `(&cobra.Command{}).Context()`, not `context.Background()`.\n- Assert on the constant `dirtyWorktreeErrorCode` (`export.go:967`), never the bare literal.\n- Human-readable CLI output has **no golden convention** — assert with `strings.Contains` /\n  `visibleLines`. Do not add a golden for the new refusal text.\n\n### Two traps\n\n- **`t.Setenv` + `t.Parallel()` panics in Go.** The harness-detection tests set env, so they must\n  stay serial — and must not share a function with a parallel test. Precedent:\n  `refresh_test.go:16` sets `ENTIRE_BRAIN_NO_EGRESS` and is deliberately non-parallel.\n- **`filterWorktreeStatus` has no direct unit test** — it is only covered transitively. The\n  gate-only ignore runs straight through it, so add one rather than relying on that.\n\n~~FORCE_COLOR~~ — checked and withdrawn: colour tests inject `tui.Caps` explicitly and\n`DetectCapsWithEnv` returns `PlainCaps()` for any non-`*os.File` writer (`render.go:62`), so the\nshell's `FORCE_COLOR=3` cannot leak in. Not a risk for this work."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"5e63fa69-1098-44b7-a89e-14e1d5eb318e","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Cfk5vZwtA99QoxiiCR3Lj","type":"assistant","uuid":"943793e9-6793-4ff9-9b6b-8cbbdc1f7c55","timestamp":"2026-10-06T01:05:54.269Z","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.290","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
