{"parentUuid":"908dd1f0-2081-4f09-ab1c-5ec0f69b2cbd","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cfk5yAvNJbzifJgVUgz7R","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BiwYvWmsxJRDiDujjhtLhZ","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/dynamic-petting-globe.md","offset":1,"limit":60},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":755,"cache_read_input_tokens":650906,"output_tokens":677,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":557},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":755},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":677,"cache_read_input_tokens":650906,"cache_creation_input_tokens":755,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":755,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01BiwYvWmsxJRDiDujjhtLhZ":{"file_path":"/Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/dynamic-petting-globe.md","offset":1,"limit":60}},"serverClassifierRequest":"93dcf44c-48a4-4e85-a05c-32e81731e20d","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cfk5yAZnWznqN3YDh3vRM","type":"assistant","uuid":"7b6d8925-8557-456b-8c8e-1c39641261c0","timestamp":"2026-10-06T01:06:17.751Z","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.290","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"7b6d8925-8557-456b-8c8e-1c39641261c0","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"e7c90eee-8619-470e-b4f1-6a320f51d5ac","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BiwYvWmsxJRDiDujjhtLhZ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Fix two install-experience defects in entire-brain\n2\t\n3\t## Context\n4\t\n5\tEarly user feedback on brain, both reproduced in source:\n6\t\n7\t> *\"the brain install is really picky about there not being **ANY** changes in any files in git.\n8\t> even the previous config file and agent file updates from the graph extension install.\n9\t> it's not the easiest to figure that out, could be me 😅\"*\n10\t\n11\t> *\"the brain facts import defaults to Codex, idk what model. any chance we could default to\n12\t> Sonnet or Opus? Or maybe ask the user for a choice in the cli flow?\"*\n13\t\n14\tThey are two unrelated defects that both land on a first-time user:\n15\t\n16\t**A. Entire's own installers create the dirt that blocks Entire's install.** `init-agents` writes\n17\t`AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `.claude/settings.json`; the next command refuses because the tree is\n18\tdirty. The reporter blamed themselves. It is not them.\n19\t\n20\t**B. Fact distillation silently routes repo content to Codex**, even for a user sitting inside\n21\tClaude Code, and never says which agent it chose.\n22\t\n23\tBoth are on `main`, not just the unmerged stack. Everything below is `file:line` from source,\n24\testablished by three exploration passes.\n25\t\n26\t---\n27\t\n28\t## Fix A — Entire-authored config must not block the install\n29\t\n30\t### What is actually broken\n31\t\n32\t`brainIgnore.Ignored` (`internal/cli/semantic.go:2467`) hardcodes a segment list at `:2473`:\n33\t`node_modules, vendor, dist, build, target, .entire`. **`.entire/*` is already exempt.** The gap\n34\tis exactly the three paths outside it: **`AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `.claude/settings.json`**.\n35\t\n36\t`loadBrainIgnore` (`:2433`) otherwise reads only `.brainignore`, which does not exist in a fresh\n37\trepo — so for a new user the user-pattern set is empty and only the hardcoded list applies.\n38\t\n39\t**There are two refusals, not one.** A dirty install fails both components:\n40\t\n41\t| refusal | file:line | message |\n42\t|---|---|---|\n43\t| seed | `seed.go:276` | `dirty_worktree: refusing to seed uncommitted content without --worktree` |\n44\t| semantic | `semantic.go:594` | `dirty_worktree: refusing to index uncommitted content without --worktree` |\n45\t\n46\tConfirmed call chain for `entire brain setup`: `setup.go:659` → `setup.go:1261` →\n47\t`watch.go:647 runRefresh` (with `watch.go:609 watchDeterministicRefreshOptions`, which leaves\n48\t**both** worktree flags false) → `refresh.go:223` → `refresh.go:274` → `refresh_phases.go:30` →\n49\t`seed.go:271`. Semantic arrives via `refresh.go:401` → `:452` → `refresh_phases.go:36`.\n50\t\n51\tSetup already *recognises* this state — `setupIsDirtyWorktree` (`setup.go:196`), matched at\n52\t`:211`, with a hint at `:133` naming `.entire/` and `.claude/` — but still fails the components.\n53\tThe diagnosis exists; the fix does not.\n54\t\n55\t### Changes\n56\t\n57\t1. **Add a GATE-ONLY ignore — do NOT touch the shared hardcoded list.**\n58\t\n59\t   ⚠️ **The obvious fix is wrong, and this is the most important decision in the plan.**\n60\t   `brainIgnore.Ignored` (`semantic.go:2467`) is **not** the dirty gate — it is the *indexing*"}]},"uuid":"a50b88f8-48bb-4998-98f5-d89aa64dda24","timestamp":"2026-10-06T01:06:17.765Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/dynamic-petting-globe.md","content":"# Fix two install-experience defects in entire-brain\n\n## Context\n\nEarly user feedback on brain, both reproduced in source:\n\n> *\"the brain install is really picky about there not being **ANY** changes in any files in git.\n> even the previous config file and agent file updates from the graph extension install.\n> it's not the easiest to figure that out, could be me 😅\"*\n\n> *\"the brain facts import defaults to Codex, idk what model. any chance we could default to\n> Sonnet or Opus? Or maybe ask the user for a choice in the cli flow?\"*\n\nThey are two unrelated defects that both land on a first-time user:\n\n**A. Entire's own installers create the dirt that blocks Entire's install.** `init-agents` writes\n`AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `.claude/settings.json`; the next command refuses because the tree is\ndirty. The reporter blamed themselves. It is not them.\n\n**B. Fact distillation silently routes repo content to Codex**, even for a user sitting inside\nClaude Code, and never says which agent it chose.\n\nBoth are on `main`, not just the unmerged stack. Everything below is `file:line` from source,\nestablished by three exploration passes.\n\n---\n\n## Fix A — Entire-authored config must not block the install\n\n### What is actually broken\n\n`brainIgnore.Ignored` (`internal/cli/semantic.go:2467`) hardcodes a segment list at `:2473`:\n`node_modules, vendor, dist, build, target, .entire`. **`.entire/*` is already exempt.** The gap\nis exactly the three paths outside it: **`AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `.claude/settings.json`**.\n\n`loadBrainIgnore` (`:2433`) otherwise reads only `.brainignore`, which does not exist in a fresh\nrepo — so for a new user the user-pattern set is empty and only the hardcoded list applies.\n\n**There are two refusals, not one.** A dirty install fails both components:\n\n| refusal | file:line | message |\n|---|---|---|\n| seed | `seed.go:276` | `dirty_worktree: refusing to seed uncommitted content without --worktree` |\n| semantic | `semantic.go:594` | `dirty_worktree: refusing to index uncommitted content without --worktree` |\n\nConfirmed call chain for `entire brain setup`: `setup.go:659` → `setup.go:1261` →\n`watch.go:647 runRefresh` (with `watch.go:609 watchDeterministicRefreshOptions`, which leaves\n**both** worktree flags false) → `refresh.go:223` → `refresh.go:274` → `refresh_phases.go:30` →\n`seed.go:271`. Semantic arrives via `refresh.go:401` → `:452` → `refresh_phases.go:36`.\n\nSetup already *recognises* this state — `setupIsDirtyWorktree` (`setup.go:196`), matched at\n`:211`, with a hint at `:133` naming `.entire/` and `.claude/` — but still fails the components.\nThe diagnosis exists; the fix does not.\n\n### Changes\n\n1. **Add a GATE-ONLY ignore — do NOT touch the shared hardcoded list.**\n\n   ⚠️ **The obvious fix is wrong, and this is the most important decision in the plan.**\n   `brainIgnore.Ignored` (`semantic.go:2467`) is **not** the dirty gate — it is the *indexing*","numLines":60,"startLine":1,"totalLines":264}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"7b6d8925-8557-456b-8c8e-1c39641261c0","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.290","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
