{"parentUuid":"0d036570-e4e9-478a-b8f3-49ed3c178381","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14949713 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"9589d79f-89c2-44c8-b09c-5ae4043ca052","timestamp":"2026-10-06T01:06:19.759Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14949713 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.290","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"9589d79f-89c2-44c8-b09c-5ae4043ca052","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cfk5z6LorYN6go8XVZ9A1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013Eem7ZytU4ZvHoPCFGb5Ra","name":"ExitPlanMode","input":{"plan":"# Fix two install-experience defects in entire-brain\n\n## Context\n\nEarly user feedback on brain, both reproduced in source:\n\n> *\"the brain install is really picky about there not being **ANY** changes in any files in git.\n> even the previous config file and agent file updates from the graph extension install.\n> it's not the easiest to figure that out, could be me 😅\"*\n\n> *\"the brain facts import defaults to Codex, idk what model. any chance we could default to\n> Sonnet or Opus? Or maybe ask the user for a choice in the cli flow?\"*\n\nThey are two unrelated defects that both land on a first-time user:\n\n**A. Entire's own installers create the dirt that blocks Entire's install.** `init-agents` writes\n`AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `.claude/settings.json`; the next command refuses because the tree is\ndirty. The reporter blamed themselves. It is not them.\n\n**B. Fact distillation silently routes repo content to Codex**, even for a user sitting inside\nClaude Code, and never says which agent it chose.\n\nBoth are on `main`, not just the unmerged stack. Everything below is `file:line` from source,\nestablished by three exploration passes.\n\n---\n\n## Fix A — Entire-authored config must not block the install\n\n### What is actually broken\n\n`brainIgnore.Ignored` (`internal/cli/semantic.go:2467`) hardcodes a segment list at `:2473`:\n`node_modules, vendor, dist, build, target, .entire`. **`.entire/*` is already exempt.** The gap\nis exactly the three paths outside it: **`AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `.claude/settings.json`**.\n\n`loadBrainIgnore` (`:2433`) otherwise reads only `.brainignore`, which does not exist in a fresh\nrepo — so for a new user the user-pattern set is empty and only the hardcoded list applies.\n\n**There are two refusals, not one.** A dirty install fails both components:\n\n| refusal | file:line | message |\n|---|---|---|\n| seed | `seed.go:276` | `dirty_worktree: refusing to seed uncommitted content without --worktree` |\n| semantic | `semantic.go:594` | `dirty_worktree: refusing to index uncommitted content without --worktree` |\n\nConfirmed call chain for `entire brain setup`: `setup.go:659` → `setup.go:1261` →\n`watch.go:647 runRefresh` (with `watch.go:609 watchDeterministicRefreshOptions`, which leaves\n**both** worktree flags false) → `refresh.go:223` → `refresh.go:274` → `refresh_phases.go:30` →\n`seed.go:271`. Semantic arrives via `refresh.go:401` → `:452` → `refresh_phases.go:36`.\n\nSetup already *recognises* this state — `setupIsDirtyWorktree` (`setup.go:196`), matched at\n`:211`, with a hint at `:133` naming `.entire/` and `.claude/` — but still fails the components.\nThe diagnosis exists; the fix does not.\n\n### Changes\n\n1. **Add a GATE-ONLY ignore — do NOT touch the shared hardcoded list.**\n\n   ⚠️ **The obvious fix is wrong, and this is the most important decision in the plan.**\n   `brainIgnore.Ignored` (`semantic.go:2467`) is **not** the dirty gate — it is the *indexing*\n   filter, used at 17 non-test sites: `filterSemanticSnapshot` (`:1610`, `:1642`), the snapshot\n   stream (`semantic_stream.go:242`, `:244`, `:362`), the file walks (`:3136`, `:3166`, `:5531`,\n   `:5692`, `:5715`), and coverage (`semantic_coverage.go:113`).\n\n   Adding `AGENTS.md`/`CLAUDE.md` to that list would **remove them from the indexed doc corpus** —\n   a regression disguised as a fix. Brain indexes markdown; `AGENTS.md` and `CLAUDE.md` are exactly\n   the kind of repo doc a user expects it to know about.\n\n   **Correct seam:** enrich only the `brainIgnore` *instance* the gate uses. `brainIgnore.patterns`\n   is per-instance and is matched by `brainIgnorePatternMatches` (`:2490`), which is root-anchored\n   and handles exact paths — so `.claude/settings.json` matches as written. Add a\n   `worktreeGateIgnore(repoDir)` helper returning `loadBrainIgnore(repoDir)` with the\n   Entire-authored paths appended to `.patterns`, and use it in `worktreeDirty`\n   (`semantic.go:2924`). Indexing keeps the untouched `loadBrainIgnore`.\n\n   Paths to add, decided with the user: `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `.claude/settings.json`,\n   `.codex/hooks.json`, `.brainignore`. (`.entire/*` is already exempt via the segment rule at\n   `:2473` — no change needed.) A user's own hand-edits to `AGENTS.md`/`CLAUDE.md` also stop\n   blocking the gate, which is correct: they are agent config, not indexed source — and because\n   this is gate-only, they remain **indexed** as before.\n\n   *Justification:* the gate exists to stop seeding uncommitted **source** into an index attributed\n   to a commit. Config Entire wrote is not source. Indexing it is fine; blocking on it is not.\n\n2. **Check `worktreeDirty`'s other callers before landing.** It is also used by\n   `verifySemanticWorktreeStable` (`:2941`) and `semanticStaleReport` (`:3329`). The first is a\n   post-index stability check and the second is read-only reporting; both arguably *should* ignore\n   Entire config too, but that must be a decision, not a side effect. Confirm each, and say so.\n\n3. **Leave `gitPathspecExclusions` (`semantic.go:2408`) ALONE unless proven safe.** It feeds\n   `git diff` pathspecs for change detection; widening it could make brain miss real edits. Only\n   touch it if the adversarial check shows it is gate-only.\n\n3. **Make both refusals actionable.** Today they name a flag, not an intent, and never say which\n   files. Include the count and first few offending paths, and state the remedy in plain words:\n   pass `--worktree` to index uncommitted work, or commit/stash first. Apply to `seed.go:276` and\n   `semantic.go:594` together — a user who clears one hits the other.\n\n### Out of scope, but found and worth recording\n\n`worktreeStatusPaths` (`semantic.go:3094`) applies `strings.Cut(path, \" -> \")` to **every** status\nline, not only `R`/`C` rename entries, so a filename literally containing `\" -> \"` splits into two\nbogus paths. Latent, unproven against a live repo. File separately; do not fold in here.\n\n---\n\n## Fix B — stop silently choosing another vendor's agent\n\n### What is actually broken\n\n`defaultRefreshAgent` — `refresh.go:851` (feature branch), `refresh.go:741` (**main**) — is\n`no-egress → codex → claude-code → none`, hardcoded, with **no announcement anywhere**. 13 call\nsites; the only user-visible mention of the chosen agent is setup's backfill spend label\n(`setup.go:1021`, printed at `:974`). Every other path is silent.\n\nThe codebase already made this exact call once, for ollama, in the same function:\n\n> *choosing one is a product decision, not a default worth guessing* … *the caller warns when it\n> falls through, so a privacy-motivated install does not quietly become a cloud call.*\n\n**Both of those claims are presently false.** `ollamaModelMissingWarning` (`refresh.go:893`) has\n**zero non-test callers** — the privacy guard it promises never fires.\n\n### Changes\n\n**B1 — Detect the harness the user is running under, and prefer it.**\n\nVerified by reading this session's own environment: `CLAUDECODE` and `CLAUDE_CODE_ENTRYPOINT` are\ngenuinely set inside Claude Code. That is detection, not guessing.\n\n**No Codex signal is verified.** `CODEX_HOME` (`skill_form.go:114`) is write-destination\nresolution, not detection, and the `CODEX_COMPANION_*` vars present here come from a Claude Code\nplugin, not from Codex. So: detect Claude Code positively; leave Codex to the existing PATH probe\nuntil a signal is confirmed on a real Codex run. Inventing one would repeat a mistake already in\nmemory — a guard written against a key the real CLI never emits.\n\nNew order: **detected harness → PATH probe (unchanged order) → none.**\n\nStyle precedent for env reads: `agent_policy.go:14-25` (`brainNoEgressMode`, `envBool`). Keep the\nexisting name mapping — the function returns `\"claude-code\"` while probing the binary `\"claude\"`.\n\n**B2 — Announce the choice, and wire up the dead warning.**\n\nPrint the chosen agent before any token spend, mirroring the documented ordering rule at\n`setup.go:966-972` (the cost line must precede the spend so the user can Ctrl-C). Writer chain is\n`newRefreshProgress(cmd.ErrOrStderr())` (`progress.go:224`), which degrades to prefixed plain\nlines when piped. Suppress under `--json` as `setup.go:1257` already does.\n\nAt the same site, call `ollamaModelMissingWarning` — already written and already tested, just\nnever invoked. This makes two false source comments true.\n\n**B3 — Keep the signature change contained.**\n\n`defaultRefreshAgent(ctx, runner, repoDir)` has no access to `opts`/`cmd`, and three existing tests\ncall it with that 3-arg shape (`refresh_test.go:22`, `refresh_ollama_auto_test.go:34`,\n`local_agent_preference_test.go:63`). Threading a writer through all 13 call sites is invasive and\nwould churn the tests.\n\nInstead: **leave the pure function alone**, add a thin wrapper that resolves + announces, and use\nit at the three user-facing sites — `refresh.go:145`, `distill_cmd.go:710`, `setup.go:1271` (which\nalready has a `steps.detectAgent` seam). Internal/non-interactive callers keep the pure function.\n\n**B4 — `watch` on main never reaches the function at all.** `watch.go:108` hardcodes `\"codex\"`;\nthe feature branch changed it to `\"auto\"` (`watch.go:120`). On main this is a third codex default.\nFix with B1 or it survives the reorder.\n\n### Deferred: the interactive prompt\n\nThe reporter also asked for a CLI choice. Worth doing, but **after** B1–B4 land, because it is the\ninvasive part — and because B1 alone may satisfy the request: a user in Claude Code who gets\nClaude Code has nothing left to choose.\n\nWhen done, copy the **only** interactive prompt in the CLI verbatim — `promptSeedTimeoutAction`\n(`seed.go:1792-1806`, confirmed by direct read; one exploration pass wrongly reported the CLI has\nno prompts at all). Its shape: guard on `opts.noInteractive || !stdinIsTerminal()`\n(`seed.go:1811`) and return the fallback; prompt to **stderr**; `fmt.Fscanln(os.Stdin, &response)`;\n**any error falls back**; `default:` is the safe branch. No prompt library exists here —\n`bubbletea`/`lipgloss` are dashboard-only. A prompt that is not TTY-gated hangs every piped\ninstall forever.\n\n---\n\n## Files to modify\n\n| file | change |\n|---|---|\n| `internal/cli/semantic.go` | ignore list `:2473`, pathspec list `:2408`, refusal message `:594` |\n| `internal/cli/seed.go` | refusal message `:276` |\n| `internal/cli/refresh.go` | `defaultRefreshAgent` `:851`/`:741`, announce wrapper, call `ollamaModelMissingWarning` |\n| `internal/cli/distill_cmd.go` | use the announcing wrapper at `:710` |\n| `internal/cli/setup.go` | use it via the `steps.detectAgent` seam at `:1271` |\n| `internal/cli/watch.go` | `\"codex\"` → `\"auto\"` at `:108` (main only) |\n\n## Branching\n\nBoth defects are on **main**, so this is a **separate PR off main** — not stacked on #331, which is\ngreen and awaiting approval; touching it reopens agent review on clean work.\n\nOne exception: `ollamaModelMissingWarning` and the ollama comment block exist **only** on the\nfeature branch. If B2's wiring of that warning is wanted, that piece stacks. Confirm before\nstarting; the rest is main-safe either way.\n\n## Verification\n\nThe repo already **requires** this: CONTRIBUTING.md item 3 says every fix needs a test that fails\nwithout it, and that the PR must include the failure output from a reverted fix. So weakening is\nnot an extra step here — it is the contribution standard. Patch each guard compile-clean, show the\ntest red, quote the failing assertion, restore.\n\n### Test seams to reuse (do not invent new ones)\n\n- **Command seam:** `CommandRunner` (`runner.go:17`), doubled by `fakeCommandRunner`\n  (`export_test.go:15`) keyed with `fakeCommandKey` (`:170`). It auto-answers `git --version` and\n  friends, so those need no scripting.\n- **Dirty-gate template:** `TestWorktreeDirtyKeepsRenameFromIgnoredToPublic`\n  (`semantic_test.go:896`) — `brainIgnore{patterns: ...}` literal + canned porcelain. This is\n  exactly the shape the gate-only ignore needs. Command-level equivalent:\n  `TestSeedRejectsDirtyWorktreeWithoutWorktreeFlag` (`seed_test.go:400`).\n- **Agent-availability template:** `availabilityRunner` (`local_agent_preference_test.go:9`) —\n  stubs the `<name> --version` probe. PATH is never manipulated for this.\n- Context idiom in these files is `(&cobra.Command{}).Context()`, not `context.Background()`.\n- Assert on the constant `dirtyWorktreeErrorCode` (`export.go:967`), never the bare literal.\n- Human-readable CLI output has **no golden convention** — assert with `strings.Contains` /\n  `visibleLines`. Do not add a golden for the new refusal text.\n\n### Two traps\n\n- **`t.Setenv` + `t.Parallel()` panics in Go.** The harness-detection tests set env, so they must\n  stay serial — and must not share a function with a parallel test. Precedent:\n  `refresh_test.go:16` sets `ENTIRE_BRAIN_NO_EGRESS` and is deliberately non-parallel.\n- **`filterWorktreeStatus` has no direct unit test** — it is only covered transitively. The\n  gate-only ignore runs straight through it, so add one rather than relying on that.\n\n~~FORCE_COLOR~~ — checked and withdrawn: colour tests inject `tui.Caps` explicitly and\n`DetectCapsWithEnv` returns `PlainCaps()` for any non-`*os.File` writer (`render.go:62`), so the\nshell's `FORCE_COLOR=3` cannot leak in. Not a risk for this work.\n\n**Fix A**\n1. Repo dirty **only** with `AGENTS.md`/`CLAUDE.md`/`.claude/settings.json` → `setup` seeds and\n   indexes clean. Weaken by removing the new entries → test red.\n2. Repo with one dirty **source** file → both refusals still fire. This is the guard that stops\n   the fix becoming \"ignore everything\".\n3. A user `.brainignore` still applies, and built-ins do not replace it.\n4. Refusal message names the offending paths.\n\n**End-to-end, the actual reported bug:** fresh clone → `entire graph init-agents` →\n`entire brain setup`. Must succeed. It currently fails. This is the acceptance test.\n\n**Fix B**\n5. `CLAUDECODE` set + `codex` on PATH → picks `claude-code`. Weaken by dropping detection → red.\n6. No harness env, no TTY → deterministic, no prompt, never hangs.\n7. The chosen agent is announced on stderr; silent under `--json`.\n8. `ollamaModelMissingWarning` fires when ollama is present and something else is chosen —\n   currently unreachable, so this test fails before the fix.\n\n**Constraints:** no full local suites (CPU-bound). The repo's own convention is targeted:\n`go test ./internal/cli -run '^TestX$' -count=1` (`docs/testing-for-optimization.md`), with\n`GOMAXPROCS=1 -p 1 -parallel 1` on this machine.\n\n## Not doing\n\nMerging, approving, or pushing to any existing PR without explicit approval. The `\" -> \"`\npath-splitting bug is filed separately, not folded in.\n","planFilePath":"/Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/dynamic-petting-globe.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1161,"cache_read_input_tokens":653653,"output_tokens":31,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1161},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":31,"cache_read_input_tokens":653653,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1161,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1161,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_013Eem7ZytU4ZvHoPCFGb5Ra":{}},"serverClassifierRequest":"9df214e5-51b5-49ca-a312-d7ac78732e7b","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cfk5z5xjxn77TJPoMLNjo","type":"assistant","uuid":"5e779f2e-4243-4181-8dcf-0c28886062e7","timestamp":"2026-10-06T01:06:21.067Z","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.290","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"5e779f2e-4243-4181-8dcf-0c28886062e7","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"e7c90eee-8619-470e-b4f1-6a320f51d5ac","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","content":"User has approved your plan. You can now start coding. Start with updating your todo list if applicable\n\nYour plan has been saved to: /Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/dynamic-petting-globe.md\nYou can refer back to it if needed during implementation.\n\n## Approved Plan:\n# Fix two install-experience defects in entire-brain\n\n## Context\n\nEarly user feedback on brain, both reproduced in source:\n\n> *\"the brain install is really picky about there not being **ANY** changes in any files in git.\n> even the previous config file and agent file updates from the graph extension install.\n> it's not the easiest to figure that out, could be me 😅\"*\n\n> *\"the brain facts import defaults to Codex, idk what model. any chance we could default to\n> Sonnet or Opus? Or maybe ask the user for a choice in the cli flow?\"*\n\nThey are two unrelated defects that both land on a first-time user:\n\n**A. Entire's own installers create the dirt that blocks Entire's install.** `init-agents` writes\n`AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `.claude/settings.json`; the next command refuses because the tree is\ndirty. The reporter blamed themselves. It is not them.\n\n**B. Fact distillation silently routes repo content to Codex**, even for a user sitting inside\nClaude Code, and never says which agent it chose.\n\nBoth are on `main`, not just the unmerged stack. Everything below is `file:line` from source,\nestablished by three exploration passes.\n\n---\n\n## Fix A — Entire-authored config must not block the install\n\n### What is actually broken\n\n`brainIgnore.Ignored` (`internal/cli/semantic.go:2467`) hardcodes a segment list at `:2473`:\n`node_modules, vendor, dist, build, target, .entire`. **`.entire/*` is already exempt.** The gap\nis exactly the three paths outside it: **`AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `.claude/settings.json`**.\n\n`loadBrainIgnore` (`:2433`) otherwise reads only `.brainignore`, which does not exist in a fresh\nrepo — so for a new user the user-pattern set is empty and only the hardcoded list applies.\n\n**There are two refusals, not one.** A dirty install fails both components:\n\n| refusal | file:line | message |\n|---|---|---|\n| seed | `seed.go:276` | `dirty_worktree: refusing to seed uncommitted content without --worktree` |\n| semantic | `semantic.go:594` | `dirty_worktree: refusing to index uncommitted content without --worktree` |\n\nConfirmed call chain for `entire brain setup`: `setup.go:659` → `setup.go:1261` →\n`watch.go:647 runRefresh` (with `watch.go:609 watchDeterministicRefreshOptions`, which leaves\n**both** worktree flags false) → `refresh.go:223` → `refresh.go:274` → `refresh_phases.go:30` →\n`seed.go:271`. Semantic arrives via `refresh.go:401` → `:452` → `refresh_phases.go:36`.\n\nSetup already *recognises* this state — `setupIsDirtyWorktree` (`setup.go:196`), matched at\n`:211`, with a hint at `:133` naming `.entire/` and `.claude/` — but still fails the components.\nThe diagnosis exists; the fix does not.\n\n### Changes\n\n1. **Add a GATE-ONLY ignore — do NOT touch the shared hardcoded list.**\n\n   ⚠️ **The obvious fix is wrong, and this is the most important decision in the plan.**\n   `brainIgnore.Ignored` (`semantic.go:2467`) is **not** the dirty gate — it is the *indexing*\n   filter, used at 17 non-test sites: `filterSemanticSnapshot` (`:1610`, `:1642`), the snapshot\n   stream (`semantic_stream.go:242`, `:244`, `:362`), the file walks (`:3136`, `:3166`, `:5531`,\n   `:5692`, `:5715`), and coverage (`semantic_coverage.go:113`).\n\n   Adding `AGENTS.md`/`CLAUDE.md` to that list would **remove them from the indexed doc corpus** —\n   a regression disguised as a fix. Brain indexes markdown; `AGENTS.md` and `CLAUDE.md` are exactly\n   the kind of repo doc a user expects it to know about.\n\n   **Correct seam:** enrich only the `brainIgnore` *instance* the gate uses. `brainIgnore.patterns`\n   is per-instance and is matched by `brainIgnorePatternMatches` (`:2490`), which is root-anchored\n   and handles exact paths — so `.claude/settings.json` matches as written. Add a\n   `worktreeGateIgnore(repoDir)` helper returning `loadBrainIgnore(repoDir)` with the\n   Entire-authored paths appended to `.patterns`, and use it in `worktreeDirty`\n   (`semantic.go:2924`). Indexing keeps the untouched `loadBrainIgnore`.\n\n   Paths to add, decided with the user: `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `.claude/settings.json`,\n   `.codex/hooks.json`, `.brainignore`. (`.entire/*` is already exempt via the segment rule at\n   `:2473` — no change needed.) A user's own hand-edits to `AGENTS.md`/`CLAUDE.md` also stop\n   blocking the gate, which is correct: they are agent config, not indexed source — and because\n   this is gate-only, they remain **indexed** as before.\n\n   *Justification:* the gate exists to stop seeding uncommitted **source** into an index attributed\n   to a commit. Config Entire wrote is not source. Indexing it is fine; blocking on it is not.\n\n2. **Check `worktreeDirty`'s other callers before landing.** It is also used by\n   `verifySemanticWorktreeStable` (`:2941`) and `semanticStaleReport` (`:3329`). The first is a\n   post-index stability check and the second is read-only reporting; both arguably *should* ignore\n   Entire config too, but that must be a decision, not a side effect. Confirm each, and say so.\n\n3. **Leave `gitPathspecExclusions` (`semantic.go:2408`) ALONE unless proven safe.** It feeds\n   `git diff` pathspecs for change detection; widening it could make brain miss real edits. Only\n   touch it if the adversarial check shows it is gate-only.\n\n3. **Make both refusals actionable.** Today they name a flag, not an intent, and never say which\n   files. Include the count and first few offending paths, and state the remedy in plain words:\n   pass `--worktree` to index uncommitted work, or commit/stash first. Apply to `seed.go:276` and\n   `semantic.go:594` together — a user who clears one hits the other.\n\n### Out of scope, but found and worth recording\n\n`worktreeStatusPaths` (`semantic.go:3094`) applies `strings.Cut(path, \" -> \")` to **every** status\nline, not only `R`/`C` rename entries, so a filename literally containing `\" -> \"` splits into two\nbogus paths. Latent, unproven against a live repo. File separately; do not fold in here.\n\n---\n\n## Fix B — stop silently choosing another vendor's agent\n\n### What is actually broken\n\n`defaultRefreshAgent` — `refresh.go:851` (feature branch), `refresh.go:741` (**main**) — is\n`no-egress → codex → claude-code → none`, hardcoded, with **no announcement anywhere**. 13 call\nsites; the only user-visible mention of the chosen agent is setup's backfill spend label\n(`setup.go:1021`, printed at `:974`). Every other path is silent.\n\nThe codebase already made this exact call once, for ollama, in the same function:\n\n> *choosing one is a product decision, not a default worth guessing* … *the caller warns when it\n> falls through, so a privacy-motivated install does not quietly become a cloud call.*\n\n**Both of those claims are presently false.** `ollamaModelMissingWarning` (`refresh.go:893`) has\n**zero non-test callers** — the privacy guard it promises never fires.\n\n### Changes\n\n**B1 — Detect the harness the user is running under, and prefer it.**\n\nVerified by reading this session's own environment: `CLAUDECODE` and `CLAUDE_CODE_ENTRYPOINT` are\ngenuinely set inside Claude Code. That is detection, not guessing.\n\n**No Codex signal is verified.** `CODEX_HOME` (`skill_form.go:114`) is write-destination\nresolution, not detection, and the `CODEX_COMPANION_*` vars present here come from a Claude Code\nplugin, not from Codex. So: detect Claude Code positively; leave Codex to the existing PATH probe\nuntil a signal is confirmed on a real Codex run. Inventing one would repeat a mistake already in\nmemory — a guard written against a key the real CLI never emits.\n\nNew order: **detected harness → PATH probe (unchanged order) → none.**\n\nStyle precedent for env reads: `agent_policy.go:14-25` (`brainNoEgressMode`, `envBool`). Keep the\nexisting name mapping — the function returns `\"claude-code\"` while probing the binary `\"claude\"`.\n\n**B2 — Announce the choice, and wire up the dead warning.**\n\nPrint the chosen agent before any token spend, mirroring the documented ordering rule at\n`setup.go:966-972` (the cost line must precede the spend so the user can Ctrl-C). Writer chain is\n`newRefreshProgress(cmd.ErrOrStderr())` (`progress.go:224`), which degrades to prefixed plain\nlines when piped. Suppress under `--json` as `setup.go:1257` already does.\n\nAt the same site, call `ollamaModelMissingWarning` — already written and already tested, just\nnever invoked. This makes two false source comments true.\n\n**B3 — Keep the signature change contained.**\n\n`defaultRefreshAgent(ctx, runner, repoDir)` has no access to `opts`/`cmd`, and three existing tests\ncall it with that 3-arg shape (`refresh_test.go:22`, `refresh_ollama_auto_test.go:34`,\n`local_agent_preference_test.go:63`). Threading a writer through all 13 call sites is invasive and\nwould churn the tests.\n\nInstead: **leave the pure function alone**, add a thin wrapper that resolves + announces, and use\nit at the three user-facing sites — `refresh.go:145`, `distill_cmd.go:710`, `setup.go:1271` (which\nalready has a `steps.detectAgent` seam). Internal/non-interactive callers keep the pure function.\n\n**B4 — `watch` on main never reaches the function at all.** `watch.go:108` hardcodes `\"codex\"`;\nthe feature branch changed it to `\"auto\"` (`watch.go:120`). On main this is a third codex default.\nFix with B1 or it survives the reorder.\n\n### Deferred: the interactive prompt\n\nThe reporter also asked for a CLI choice. Worth doing, but **after** B1–B4 land, because it is the\ninvasive part — and because B1 alone may satisfy the request: a user in Claude Code who gets\nClaude Code has nothing left to choose.\n\nWhen done, copy the **only** interactive prompt in the CLI verbatim — `promptSeedTimeoutAction`\n(`seed.go:1792-1806`, confirmed by direct read; one exploration pass wrongly reported the CLI has\nno prompts at all). Its shape: guard on `opts.noInteractive || !stdinIsTerminal()`\n(`seed.go:1811`) and return the fallback; prompt to **stderr**; `fmt.Fscanln(os.Stdin, &response)`;\n**any error falls back**; `default:` is the safe branch. No prompt library exists here —\n`bubbletea`/`lipgloss` are dashboard-only. A prompt that is not TTY-gated hangs every piped\ninstall forever.\n\n---\n\n## Files to modify\n\n| file | change |\n|---|---|\n| `internal/cli/semantic.go` | ignore list `:2473`, pathspec list `:2408`, refusal message `:594` |\n| `internal/cli/seed.go` | refusal message `:276` |\n| `internal/cli/refresh.go` | `defaultRefreshAgent` `:851`/`:741`, announce wrapper, call `ollamaModelMissingWarning` |\n| `internal/cli/distill_cmd.go` | use the announcing wrapper at `:710` |\n| `internal/cli/setup.go` | use it via the `steps.detectAgent` seam at `:1271` |\n| `internal/cli/watch.go` | `\"codex\"` → `\"auto\"` at `:108` (main only) |\n\n## Branching\n\nBoth defects are on **main**, so this is a **separate PR off main** — not stacked on #331, which is\ngreen and awaiting approval; touching it reopens agent review on clean work.\n\nOne exception: `ollamaModelMissingWarning` and the ollama comment block exist **only** on the\nfeature branch. If B2's wiring of that warning is wanted, that piece stacks. Confirm before\nstarting; the rest is main-safe either way.\n\n## Verification\n\nThe repo already **requires** this: CONTRIBUTING.md item 3 says every fix needs a test that fails\nwithout it, and that the PR must include the failure output from a reverted fix. So weakening is\nnot an extra step here — it is the contribution standard. Patch each guard compile-clean, show the\ntest red, quote the failing assertion, restore.\n\n### Test seams to reuse (do not invent new ones)\n\n- **Command seam:** `CommandRunner` (`runner.go:17`), doubled by `fakeCommandRunner`\n  (`export_test.go:15`) keyed with `fakeCommandKey` (`:170`). It auto-answers `git --version` and\n  friends, so those need no scripting.\n- **Dirty-gate template:** `TestWorktreeDirtyKeepsRenameFromIgnoredToPublic`\n  (`semantic_test.go:896`) — `brainIgnore{patterns: ...}` literal + canned porcelain. This is\n  exactly the shape the gate-only ignore needs. Command-level equivalent:\n  `TestSeedRejectsDirtyWorktreeWithoutWorktreeFlag` (`seed_test.go:400`).\n- **Agent-availability template:** `availabilityRunner` (`local_agent_preference_test.go:9`) —\n  stubs the `<name> --version` probe. PATH is never manipulated for this.\n- Context idiom in these files is `(&cobra.Command{}).Context()`, not `context.Background()`.\n- Assert on the constant `dirtyWorktreeErrorCode` (`export.go:967`), never the bare literal.\n- Human-readable CLI output has **no golden convention** — assert with `strings.Contains` /\n  `visibleLines`. Do not add a golden for the new refusal text.\n\n### Two traps\n\n- **`t.Setenv` + `t.Parallel()` panics in Go.** The harness-detection tests set env, so they must\n  stay serial — and must not share a function with a parallel test. Precedent:\n  `refresh_test.go:16` sets `ENTIRE_BRAIN_NO_EGRESS` and is deliberately non-parallel.\n- **`filterWorktreeStatus` has no direct unit test** — it is only covered transitively. The\n  gate-only ignore runs straight through it, so add one rather than relying on that.\n\n~~FORCE_COLOR~~ — checked and withdrawn: colour tests inject `tui.Caps` explicitly and\n`DetectCapsWithEnv` returns `PlainCaps()` for any non-`*os.File` writer (`render.go:62`), so the\nshell's `FORCE_COLOR=3` cannot leak in. Not a risk for this work.\n\n**Fix A**\n1. Repo dirty **only** with `AGENTS.md`/`CLAUDE.md`/`.claude/settings.json` → `setup` seeds and\n   indexes clean. Weaken by removing the new entries → test red.\n2. Repo with one dirty **source** file → both refusals still fire. This is the guard that stops\n   the fix becoming \"ignore everything\".\n3. A user `.brainignore` still applies, and built-ins do not replace it.\n4. Refusal message names the offending paths.\n\n**End-to-end, the actual reported bug:** fresh clone → `entire graph init-agents` →\n`entire brain setup`. Must succeed. It currently fails. This is the acceptance test.\n\n**Fix B**\n5. `CLAUDECODE` set + `codex` on PATH → picks `claude-code`. Weaken by dropping detection → red.\n6. No harness env, no TTY → deterministic, no prompt, never hangs.\n7. The chosen agent is announced on stderr; silent under `--json`.\n8. `ollamaModelMissingWarning` fires when ollama is present and something else is chosen —\n   currently unreachable, so this test fails before the fix.\n\n**Constraints:** no full local suites (CPU-bound). The repo's own convention is targeted:\n`go test ./internal/cli -run '^TestX$' -count=1` (`docs/testing-for-optimization.md`), with\n`GOMAXPROCS=1 -p 1 -parallel 1` on this machine.\n\n## Not doing\n\nMerging, approving, or pushing to any existing PR without explicit approval. The `\" -> \"`\npath-splitting bug is filed separately, not folded in.\n","tool_use_id":"toolu_013Eem7ZytU4ZvHoPCFGb5Ra"}]},"uuid":"3de69a97-07ae-4510-899c-fa5d1654e417","timestamp":"2026-10-06T01:08:43.999Z","toolUseResult":{"plan":"# Fix two install-experience defects in entire-brain\n\n## Context\n\nEarly user feedback on brain, both reproduced in source:\n\n> *\"the brain install is really picky about there not being **ANY** changes in any files in git.\n> even the previous config file and agent file updates from the graph extension install.\n> it's not the easiest to figure that out, could be me 😅\"*\n\n> *\"the brain facts import defaults to Codex, idk what model. any chance we could default to\n> Sonnet or Opus? Or maybe ask the user for a choice in the cli flow?\"*\n\nThey are two unrelated defects that both land on a first-time user:\n\n**A. Entire's own installers create the dirt that blocks Entire's install.** `init-agents` writes\n`AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `.claude/settings.json`; the next command refuses because the tree is\ndirty. The reporter blamed themselves. It is not them.\n\n**B. Fact distillation silently routes repo content to Codex**, even for a user sitting inside\nClaude Code, and never says which agent it chose.\n\nBoth are on `main`, not just the unmerged stack. Everything below is `file:line` from source,\nestablished by three exploration passes.\n\n---\n\n## Fix A — Entire-authored config must not block the install\n\n### What is actually broken\n\n`brainIgnore.Ignored` (`internal/cli/semantic.go:2467`) hardcodes a segment list at `:2473`:\n`node_modules, vendor, dist, build, target, .entire`. **`.entire/*` is already exempt.** The gap\nis exactly the three paths outside it: **`AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `.claude/settings.json`**.\n\n`loadBrainIgnore` (`:2433`) otherwise reads only `.brainignore`, which does not exist in a fresh\nrepo — so for a new user the user-pattern set is empty and only the hardcoded list applies.\n\n**There are two refusals, not one.** A dirty install fails both components:\n\n| refusal | file:line | message |\n|---|---|---|\n| seed | `seed.go:276` | `dirty_worktree: refusing to seed uncommitted content without --worktree` |\n| semantic | `semantic.go:594` | `dirty_worktree: refusing to index uncommitted content without --worktree` |\n\nConfirmed call chain for `entire brain setup`: `setup.go:659` → `setup.go:1261` →\n`watch.go:647 runRefresh` (with `watch.go:609 watchDeterministicRefreshOptions`, which leaves\n**both** worktree flags false) → `refresh.go:223` → `refresh.go:274` → `refresh_phases.go:30` →\n`seed.go:271`. Semantic arrives via `refresh.go:401` → `:452` → `refresh_phases.go:36`.\n\nSetup already *recognises* this state — `setupIsDirtyWorktree` (`setup.go:196`), matched at\n`:211`, with a hint at `:133` naming `.entire/` and `.claude/` — but still fails the components.\nThe diagnosis exists; the fix does not.\n\n### Changes\n\n1. **Add a GATE-ONLY ignore — do NOT touch the shared hardcoded list.**\n\n   ⚠️ **The obvious fix is wrong, and this is the most important decision in the plan.**\n   `brainIgnore.Ignored` (`semantic.go:2467`) is **not** the dirty gate — it is the *indexing*\n   filter, used at 17 non-test sites: `filterSemanticSnapshot` (`:1610`, `:1642`), the snapshot\n   stream (`semantic_stream.go:242`, `:244`, `:362`), the file walks (`:3136`, `:3166`, `:5531`,\n   `:5692`, `:5715`), and coverage (`semantic_coverage.go:113`).\n\n   Adding `AGENTS.md`/`CLAUDE.md` to that list would **remove them from the indexed doc corpus** —\n   a regression disguised as a fix. Brain indexes markdown; `AGENTS.md` and `CLAUDE.md` are exactly\n   the kind of repo doc a user expects it to know about.\n\n   **Correct seam:** enrich only the `brainIgnore` *instance* the gate uses. `brainIgnore.patterns`\n   is per-instance and is matched by `brainIgnorePatternMatches` (`:2490`), which is root-anchored\n   and handles exact paths — so `.claude/settings.json` matches as written. Add a\n   `worktreeGateIgnore(repoDir)` helper returning `loadBrainIgnore(repoDir)` with the\n   Entire-authored paths appended to `.patterns`, and use it in `worktreeDirty`\n   (`semantic.go:2924`). Indexing keeps the untouched `loadBrainIgnore`.\n\n   Paths to add, decided with the user: `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `.claude/settings.json`,\n   `.codex/hooks.json`, `.brainignore`. (`.entire/*` is already exempt via the segment rule at\n   `:2473` — no change needed.) A user's own hand-edits to `AGENTS.md`/`CLAUDE.md` also stop\n   blocking the gate, which is correct: they are agent config, not indexed source — and because\n   this is gate-only, they remain **indexed** as before.\n\n   *Justification:* the gate exists to stop seeding uncommitted **source** into an index attributed\n   to a commit. Config Entire wrote is not source. Indexing it is fine; blocking on it is not.\n\n2. **Check `worktreeDirty`'s other callers before landing.** It is also used by\n   `verifySemanticWorktreeStable` (`:2941`) and `semanticStaleReport` (`:3329`). The first is a\n   post-index stability check and the second is read-only reporting; both arguably *should* ignore\n   Entire config too, but that must be a decision, not a side effect. Confirm each, and say so.\n\n3. **Leave `gitPathspecExclusions` (`semantic.go:2408`) ALONE unless proven safe.** It feeds\n   `git diff` pathspecs for change detection; widening it could make brain miss real edits. Only\n   touch it if the adversarial check shows it is gate-only.\n\n3. **Make both refusals actionable.** Today they name a flag, not an intent, and never say which\n   files. Include the count and first few offending paths, and state the remedy in plain words:\n   pass `--worktree` to index uncommitted work, or commit/stash first. Apply to `seed.go:276` and\n   `semantic.go:594` together — a user who clears one hits the other.\n\n### Out of scope, but found and worth recording\n\n`worktreeStatusPaths` (`semantic.go:3094`) applies `strings.Cut(path, \" -> \")` to **every** status\nline, not only `R`/`C` rename entries, so a filename literally containing `\" -> \"` splits into two\nbogus paths. Latent, unproven against a live repo. File separately; do not fold in here.\n\n---\n\n## Fix B — stop silently choosing another vendor's agent\n\n### What is actually broken\n\n`defaultRefreshAgent` — `refresh.go:851` (feature branch), `refresh.go:741` (**main**) — is\n`no-egress → codex → claude-code → none`, hardcoded, with **no announcement anywhere**. 13 call\nsites; the only user-visible mention of the chosen agent is setup's backfill spend label\n(`setup.go:1021`, printed at `:974`). Every other path is silent.\n\nThe codebase already made this exact call once, for ollama, in the same function:\n\n> *choosing one is a product decision, not a default worth guessing* … *the caller warns when it\n> falls through, so a privacy-motivated install does not quietly become a cloud call.*\n\n**Both of those claims are presently false.** `ollamaModelMissingWarning` (`refresh.go:893`) has\n**zero non-test callers** — the privacy guard it promises never fires.\n\n### Changes\n\n**B1 — Detect the harness the user is running under, and prefer it.**\n\nVerified by reading this session's own environment: `CLAUDECODE` and `CLAUDE_CODE_ENTRYPOINT` are\ngenuinely set inside Claude Code. That is detection, not guessing.\n\n**No Codex signal is verified.** `CODEX_HOME` (`skill_form.go:114`) is write-destination\nresolution, not detection, and the `CODEX_COMPANION_*` vars present here come from a Claude Code\nplugin, not from Codex. So: detect Claude Code positively; leave Codex to the existing PATH probe\nuntil a signal is confirmed on a real Codex run. Inventing one would repeat a mistake already in\nmemory — a guard written against a key the real CLI never emits.\n\nNew order: **detected harness → PATH probe (unchanged order) → none.**\n\nStyle precedent for env reads: `agent_policy.go:14-25` (`brainNoEgressMode`, `envBool`). Keep the\nexisting name mapping — the function returns `\"claude-code\"` while probing the binary `\"claude\"`.\n\n**B2 — Announce the choice, and wire up the dead warning.**\n\nPrint the chosen agent before any token spend, mirroring the documented ordering rule at\n`setup.go:966-972` (the cost line must precede the spend so the user can Ctrl-C). Writer chain is\n`newRefreshProgress(cmd.ErrOrStderr())` (`progress.go:224`), which degrades to prefixed plain\nlines when piped. Suppress under `--json` as `setup.go:1257` already does.\n\nAt the same site, call `ollamaModelMissingWarning` — already written and already tested, just\nnever invoked. This makes two false source comments true.\n\n**B3 — Keep the signature change contained.**\n\n`defaultRefreshAgent(ctx, runner, repoDir)` has no access to `opts`/`cmd`, and three existing tests\ncall it with that 3-arg shape (`refresh_test.go:22`, `refresh_ollama_auto_test.go:34`,\n`local_agent_preference_test.go:63`). Threading a writer through all 13 call sites is invasive and\nwould churn the tests.\n\nInstead: **leave the pure function alone**, add a thin wrapper that resolves + announces, and use\nit at the three user-facing sites — `refresh.go:145`, `distill_cmd.go:710`, `setup.go:1271` (which\nalready has a `steps.detectAgent` seam). Internal/non-interactive callers keep the pure function.\n\n**B4 — `watch` on main never reaches the function at all.** `watch.go:108` hardcodes `\"codex\"`;\nthe feature branch changed it to `\"auto\"` (`watch.go:120`). On main this is a third codex default.\nFix with B1 or it survives the reorder.\n\n### Deferred: the interactive prompt\n\nThe reporter also asked for a CLI choice. Worth doing, but **after** B1–B4 land, because it is the\ninvasive part — and because B1 alone may satisfy the request: a user in Claude Code who gets\nClaude Code has nothing left to choose.\n\nWhen done, copy the **only** interactive prompt in the CLI verbatim — `promptSeedTimeoutAction`\n(`seed.go:1792-1806`, confirmed by direct read; one exploration pass wrongly reported the CLI has\nno prompts at all). Its shape: guard on `opts.noInteractive || !stdinIsTerminal()`\n(`seed.go:1811`) and return the fallback; prompt to **stderr**; `fmt.Fscanln(os.Stdin, &response)`;\n**any error falls back**; `default:` is the safe branch. No prompt library exists here —\n`bubbletea`/`lipgloss` are dashboard-only. A prompt that is not TTY-gated hangs every piped\ninstall forever.\n\n---\n\n## Files to modify\n\n| file | change |\n|---|---|\n| `internal/cli/semantic.go` | ignore list `:2473`, pathspec list `:2408`, refusal message `:594` |\n| `internal/cli/seed.go` | refusal message `:276` |\n| `internal/cli/refresh.go` | `defaultRefreshAgent` `:851`/`:741`, announce wrapper, call `ollamaModelMissingWarning` |\n| `internal/cli/distill_cmd.go` | use the announcing wrapper at `:710` |\n| `internal/cli/setup.go` | use it via the `steps.detectAgent` seam at `:1271` |\n| `internal/cli/watch.go` | `\"codex\"` → `\"auto\"` at `:108` (main only) |\n\n## Branching\n\nBoth defects are on **main**, so this is a **separate PR off main** — not stacked on #331, which is\ngreen and awaiting approval; touching it reopens agent review on clean work.\n\nOne exception: `ollamaModelMissingWarning` and the ollama comment block exist **only** on the\nfeature branch. If B2's wiring of that warning is wanted, that piece stacks. Confirm before\nstarting; the rest is main-safe either way.\n\n## Verification\n\nThe repo already **requires** this: CONTRIBUTING.md item 3 says every fix needs a test that fails\nwithout it, and that the PR must include the failure output from a reverted fix. So weakening is\nnot an extra step here — it is the contribution standard. Patch each guard compile-clean, show the\ntest red, quote the failing assertion, restore.\n\n### Test seams to reuse (do not invent new ones)\n\n- **Command seam:** `CommandRunner` (`runner.go:17`), doubled by `fakeCommandRunner`\n  (`export_test.go:15`) keyed with `fakeCommandKey` (`:170`). It auto-answers `git --version` and\n  friends, so those need no scripting.\n- **Dirty-gate template:** `TestWorktreeDirtyKeepsRenameFromIgnoredToPublic`\n  (`semantic_test.go:896`) — `brainIgnore{patterns: ...}` literal + canned porcelain. This is\n  exactly the shape the gate-only ignore needs. Command-level equivalent:\n  `TestSeedRejectsDirtyWorktreeWithoutWorktreeFlag` (`seed_test.go:400`).\n- **Agent-availability template:** `availabilityRunner` (`local_agent_preference_test.go:9`) —\n  stubs the `<name> --version` probe. PATH is never manipulated for this.\n- Context idiom in these files is `(&cobra.Command{}).Context()`, not `context.Background()`.\n- Assert on the constant `dirtyWorktreeErrorCode` (`export.go:967`), never the bare literal.\n- Human-readable CLI output has **no golden convention** — assert with `strings.Contains` /\n  `visibleLines`. Do not add a golden for the new refusal text.\n\n### Two traps\n\n- **`t.Setenv` + `t.Parallel()` panics in Go.** The harness-detection tests set env, so they must\n  stay serial — and must not share a function with a parallel test. Precedent:\n  `refresh_test.go:16` sets `ENTIRE_BRAIN_NO_EGRESS` and is deliberately non-parallel.\n- **`filterWorktreeStatus` has no direct unit test** — it is only covered transitively. The\n  gate-only ignore runs straight through it, so add one rather than relying on that.\n\n~~FORCE_COLOR~~ — checked and withdrawn: colour tests inject `tui.Caps` explicitly and\n`DetectCapsWithEnv` returns `PlainCaps()` for any non-`*os.File` writer (`render.go:62`), so the\nshell's `FORCE_COLOR=3` cannot leak in. Not a risk for this work.\n\n**Fix A**\n1. Repo dirty **only** with `AGENTS.md`/`CLAUDE.md`/`.claude/settings.json` → `setup` seeds and\n   indexes clean. Weaken by removing the new entries → test red.\n2. Repo with one dirty **source** file → both refusals still fire. This is the guard that stops\n   the fix becoming \"ignore everything\".\n3. A user `.brainignore` still applies, and built-ins do not replace it.\n4. Refusal message names the offending paths.\n\n**End-to-end, the actual reported bug:** fresh clone → `entire graph init-agents` →\n`entire brain setup`. Must succeed. It currently fails. This is the acceptance test.\n\n**Fix B**\n5. `CLAUDECODE` set + `codex` on PATH → picks `claude-code`. Weaken by dropping detection → red.\n6. No harness env, no TTY → deterministic, no prompt, never hangs.\n7. The chosen agent is announced on stderr; silent under `--json`.\n8. `ollamaModelMissingWarning` fires when ollama is present and something else is chosen —\n   currently unreachable, so this test fails before the fix.\n\n**Constraints:** no full local suites (CPU-bound). The repo's own convention is targeted:\n`go test ./internal/cli -run '^TestX$' -count=1` (`docs/testing-for-optimization.md`), with\n`GOMAXPROCS=1 -p 1 -parallel 1` on this machine.\n\n## Not doing\n\nMerging, approving, or pushing to any existing PR without explicit approval. The `\" -> \"`\npath-splitting bug is filed separately, not folded in.\n","isAgent":false,"filePath":"/Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/dynamic-petting-globe.md"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"5e779f2e-4243-4181-8dcf-0c28886062e7","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-guide","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.290","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
