{"parentUuid":"96f9bd29-f848-428f-b840-0df518c84749","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cfk6EKGag71vyUAeFsT6e","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KogTpasz5XMhe6gP1EWAB3","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Implement install-UX fixes","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"opus","prompt":"Implement an approved plan in entire-brain. Work ONLY in /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-install-ux (a clean worktree, branch `fix/install-ux-dirty-gate-and-agent-default`, based on origin/main @6c8ebdab). Never touch other checkouts.\n\nREAD FIRST: /Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/dynamic-petting-globe.md — the full approved plan. Follow it. Line numbers in it are from the FEATURE branch (brain-v1-guide); you are on MAIN, where they differ. Main line numbers I verified:\n- semantic.go:575  \"refusing to index uncommitted content without --worktree\"\n- semantic.go:2269 loadBrainIgnore\n- semantic.go:2541 worktreeDirty\n- seed.go:276      \"refusing to seed uncommitted content without --worktree\"\n- refresh.go:829   defaultRefreshAgent\n- watch.go:110     distillAgent: \"codex\"   (hardcoded; plan item B4)\n\nSCOPE FOR THIS PR (main-safe only):\n- Fix A, changes 1, 2 and 4 (gate-only ignore; check worktreeDirty's other callers; actionable refusal messages).\n- Fix B: B1 (prefer detected harness), B3 (contained wrapper), B4 (watch.go \"codex\" -> \"auto\"), and the ANNOUNCE half of B2.\n- EXCLUDED: wiring `ollamaModelMissingWarning` — it has ZERO hits on main, it exists only on the feature branch. Do not port it. Do not invent it.\n- EXCLUDED: the deferred interactive prompt.\n- EXCLUDED: the `\" -> \"` path-splitting bug (separate issue).\n\nTHE ONE DECISION THAT MATTERS — do not get this wrong. `brainIgnore.Ignored` is the INDEXING filter (17 non-test call sites incl. filterSemanticSnapshot, the snapshot stream, the file walks, semantic_coverage). Adding AGENTS.md/CLAUDE.md there would DELETE them from the indexed doc corpus — a regression disguised as a fix. Add a NEW gate-only helper (`worktreeGateIgnore(repoDir)`) that returns loadBrainIgnore(repoDir) with the Entire-authored paths appended to `.patterns`, and use it in `worktreeDirty` ONLY. Paths: AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, .claude/settings.json, .codex/hooks.json, .brainignore. (.entire/* is already exempt via the segment rule — do not re-add it.) Do NOT modify the hardcoded segment list or gitPathspecExclusions.\n\nVERIFICATION IS THE DELIVERABLE, not the diff. CONTRIBUTING.md item 3 requires a test that fails without the fix, with the failure output quoted in the PR. For EVERY guard you add: patch it compile-clean, run the test, capture it RED, quote the failing assertion, restore, confirm green. A weakening that does not compile proves nothing — redo it. If a weakening produces 0 failures, SUSPECT YOUR TEST FIRST (a missing/empty fixture makes a guard look unholdable); grep to confirm the edit applied before concluding the guard is unnecessary.\n\nTEST CONVENTIONS (reuse, do not invent):\n- fakeCommandRunner (export_test.go) + fakeCommandKey; auto-answers `git --version` etc.\n- Dirty-gate template: TestWorktreeDirtyKeepsRenameFromIgnoredToPublic (semantic_test.go) — brainIgnore{patterns:...} + canned porcelain. Command-level: TestSeedRejectsDirtyWorktreeWithoutWorktreeFlag (seed_test.go).\n- Agent-availability: availabilityRunner (local_agent_preference_test.go). Never manipulate PATH for this.\n- Context idiom: `(&cobra.Command{}).Context()`.\n- Assert the constant dirtyWorktreeErrorCode, never the bare literal.\n- No golden for human-readable output — strings.Contains.\n- `t.Setenv` + `t.Parallel()` PANICS. Harness-detection tests set env, so keep them serial and not in a func with t.Parallel().\n- filterWorktreeStatus has no direct unit test; add one since the gate-only ignore runs through it.\n- House style: tests carry a narrative comment quoting the real broken behaviour. Match it.\n\nREQUIRED TESTS (plan's acceptance list): dirty ONLY with Entire config -> proceeds; one dirty SOURCE file -> both refusals still fire (this guard stops the fix becoming \"ignore everything\"); user .brainignore still applies; refusal names the offending paths; CLAUDECODE set + codex on PATH -> picks claude-code; no harness env + no TTY -> deterministic, never hangs; chosen agent announced on stderr and silent under --json.\n\nHARNESS DETECTION: I verified by reading a live Claude Code session env that CLAUDECODE and CLAUDE_CODE_ENTRYPOINT are genuinely set. Use those. There is NO verified Codex signal — CODEX_HOME is write-destination resolution, not detection. Do not invent one; leave codex to the existing PATH probe.\n\nENV TRAPS: no full suites (CPU-bound) — `GOMAXPROCS=1 go test ./internal/cli -run '^TestX$' -count=1 -p 1 -parallel 1`. `timeout` does not exist on macOS; use `perl -e 'alarm N; exec @ARGV' <cmd>`. Piping to head/tail MASKS exit codes — check $? on the command itself. NEVER `git stash` (shared across worktrees). Build AND vet before finishing: `go build ./...` and `go vet ./...`.\n\nDO NOT: commit? yes you may commit on this branch. DO NOT push, do not open a PR, do not merge, do not approve anything, no AI attribution footers in commit messages.\n\nOUTPUT: caveman-ultra compressed. Per change: what, file:line, why. Then a weakening table: guard | what you broke | test that went red | quoted assertion. Then build/vet result. Then anything you could NOT verify, labelled \"unverified\". Facts only, no prose padding. Your tool output does not reach me — only this report does."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1577,"cache_read_input_tokens":663116,"output_tokens":2375,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input