{"parentUuid":"478de7a0-534d-4f64-9fde-856513a03438","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cfk6NJYtM3AoRb5hHMsJA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CDW12aQUQvKtdpJkrYXmCf","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"ac4b585e3f8302c86","summary":"Four corrections from adversarial review","message":"STOP and read: an adversarial review of the plan found four defects. Apply these corrections before going further.\n\n1) KEEP THE AVAILABILITY PROBE — this one would ship a hard regression.\nB1 as written (\"detected harness → PATH probe\") can return \"claude-code\" on env alone. `distill.go` then builds argv starting with `claude`, and there is NO fallback. A Claude Code session where the `claude` binary is not on the child PATH would turn a WORKING codex run into a hard exec failure.\nCorrect rule: prefer the detected harness ONLY IF its binary is also available (reuse `commandLooksAvailable`). Detected-but-unavailable must fall through to the existing probe order, not win. Add a test for exactly that: CLAUDECODE set, `claude` NOT available, codex available → picks codex.\n\n2) THE ACCEPTANCE TEST IN THE PLAN IS INVALID — do not rely on it.\nPlan says \"fresh clone → graph init-agents → brain setup must succeed; it currently fails.\" That is WRONG. `watchDeterministicRefreshComponents` passes bestEffort=true, so `reportStageAndShouldAbort` returns false and seed/semantic failures are reported, not fatal; docs+history still succeed, and setup only hard-fails when NOTHING built. **`entire brain setup` already exits 0 (degraded) on a dirty tree**, so that test passes before AND after the fix and proves nothing — a false pass.\nAssert on the COMPONENT outcome instead: seed and semantic must go from failed/degraded to built. Exit code is not the signal. `entire brain refresh` (non-bestEffort, exits non-zero) is the better end-to-end surface.\n\n3) DROP `.codex/hooks.json` from the gate ignore list.\nNothing in this repo writes it — the only hook writer is `MergePreEditHook` → `.claude/settings.json` (claudehooks.go). Do not ignore a path nothing creates. Keep: AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, .claude/settings.json, .brainignore.\n\n4) B1 DOES NOT REACH THE WATCH DAEMON — the one unattended path that spends tokens.\n`daemonEnv` builds an EXPLICIT env map (plugin dirs + PATH only); CLAUDECODE is not inherited, so the daemon still resolves codex-first even after B1+B4. (`setupChildEnv` uses os.Environ() and DOES inherit — an inconsistency worth noting.) Either plumb the resolved agent/signal into the daemon env, or if that is out of scope, leave it alone and REPORT it explicitly as a known limitation. Do not silently ship a fix that misses the path it most matters on.\n\nLINE NUMBERS: trust the ones I gave you in the original prompt. They came from `git show origin/main:...` on the actual base commit 6c8ebdab. The review quoted brain-installed, which sits at 52a4bf81 — a different commit, hence different lines. Verify before editing either way.\n\nCONTEXT YOU SHOULD HAVE: this repo's own `.brainignore` already lists `.claude/settings.json` under \"Local agent/editor runtime state\" and deliberately does NOT list AGENTS.md or CLAUDE.md — maintainers drew that line on purpose, putting those two on the INDEXED side. Our gate-only approach is consistent with that (they stay indexed; only the dirty gate ignores them). If your implementation ever makes them stop being indexed, you have taken the wrong seam — stop and say so.\n\nAlso note: `watch.go` already swallows `dirty_worktree` and continues, and `setupIsDirtyWorktree` matches on the `dirty_worktree:` PREFIX. So rewording the refusal is safe only as long as the prefix is preserved. Keep the `dirtyWorktreeErrorCode + \":\"` prefix exactly, and add a test pinning that the prefix survives the rewording.\n\nEverything else in your brief stands.","type":"message","recipient":"ac4b585e3f8302c86","content":"STOP and read: an adversarial review of the plan …"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5651,"cache_read_input_tokens":667601,"output_tokens":3282,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1770},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5651},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3282,"cache_read_input_tokens":667601,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5651,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5651,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01CDW12aQUQvKtdpJkrYXmCf":{"to":"ac4b585e3f8302c86","summary":"Four corrections from adversarial review","message":"STOP and read: an adversarial review of the plan found four defects. Apply these corrections before going further.\n\n1) KEEP THE AVAILABILITY PROBE — this one would ship a hard regression.\nB1 as written (\"detected harness → PATH probe\") can return \"claude-code\" on env alone. `distill.go` then builds argv starting with `claude`, and there is NO fallback. A Claude Code session where the `claude` binary is not on the child PATH would turn a WORKING codex run into a hard exec failure.\nCorrect rule: prefer the detected harness ONLY IF its binary is also available (reuse `commandLooksAvailable`). Detected-but-unavailable must fall through to the existing probe order, not win. Add a test for exactly that: CLAUDECODE set, `claude` NOT available, codex available → picks codex.\n\n2) THE ACCEPTANCE TEST IN THE PLAN IS INVALID — do not rely on it.\nPlan says \"fresh clone → graph init-agents → brain setup must succeed; it currently fails.\" That is WRONG. `watchDeterministicRefreshComponents` passes bestEffort=true, so `reportStageAndShouldAbort` returns false and seed/semantic failures are reported, not fatal; docs+history still succeed, and setup only hard-fails when NOTHING built. **`entire brain setup` already exits 0 (degraded) on a dirty tree**, so that test passes before AND after the fix and proves nothing — a false pass.\nAssert on the COMPONENT outcome instead: seed and semantic must go from failed/degraded to built. Exit code is not the signal. `entire brain refresh` (non-bestEffort, exits non-zero) is the better end-to-end surface.\n\n3) DROP `.codex/hooks.json` from the gate ignore list.\nNothing in this repo writes it — the only hook writer is `MergePreEditHook` → `.claude/settings.json` (claudehooks.go). Do not ignore a path nothing creates. Keep: AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, .claude/settings.json, .brainignore.\n\n4) B1 DOES NOT REACH THE WATCH DAEMON — the one unattended path that spends tokens.\n`daemonEnv` builds an EXPLICIT env map (plugin dirs + PATH only); CLAUDECODE is not inherited, so the daemon still resolves codex-first even after B1+B4. (`setupChildEnv` uses os.Environ() and DOES inherit — an inconsistency worth noting.) Either plumb the resolved agent/signal into the daemon env, or if that is out of scope, leave it alone and REPORT it explicitly as a known limitation. Do not silently ship a fix that misses the path it most matters on.\n\nLINE NUMBERS: trust the ones I gave you in the original prompt. They came from `git show origin/main:...` on the actual base commit 6c8ebdab. The review quoted brain-installed, which sits at 52a4bf81 — a different commit, hence different lines. Verify before editing either way.\n\nCONTEXT YOU SHOULD HAVE: this repo's own `.brainignore` already lists `.claude/settings.json` under \"Local agent/editor runtime state\" and deliberately does NOT list AGENTS.md or CLAUDE.md — maintainers drew that line on purpose, putting those two on the INDEXED side. Our gate-only approach is consistent with that (they stay indexed; only the dirty gate ignores them). If your implementation ever makes them stop being indexed, you have taken the wrong seam — stop and say so.\n\nAlso note: `watch.go` already swallows `dirty_worktree` and continues, and `setupIsDirtyWorktree` matches on the `dirty_worktree:` PREFIX. So rewording the refusal is safe only as long as the prefix is preserved. Keep the `dirtyWorktreeErrorCode + \":\"` prefix exactly, and add a test pinning that the prefix survives the rewording.\n\nEverything else in your brief stands."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"1546cfd5-2bd5-4895-961e-62d9f515212f","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Cfk6NJBa1W91MKcH5enmg","type":"assistant","uuid":"2326754b-8c16-43ef-9519-056fd437bed4","timestamp":"2026-10-06T01:12:02.852Z","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-install-ux","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.290","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
