{"parentUuid":"aa9b03a2-1d60-4f8c-a138-cf8c3ff22673","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cfk6S7NJDGwckrEQznihK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017An4Z5ko22h9QRmDcWFCN1","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/dynamic-petting-globe.md","old_string":"New order: **detected harness → PATH probe (unchanged order) → none.**","new_string":"New order: **detected harness *if its binary is also available* → PATH probe (unchanged order) → none.**\n\n⚠️ **The availability check is not optional.** Returning `claude-code` on env alone would make\n`distill.go` build argv starting with `claude` with no fallback — turning a working codex run into\na hard exec failure whenever the `claude` binary is absent from the child PATH. Detected-but-\nunavailable must fall through, and a test must pin it: `CLAUDECODE` set, `claude` unavailable,\ncodex available → picks codex.\n\n⚠️ **B1 does not reach the watch daemon**, which is the one unattended path that spends tokens on\na timer. `daemonEnv` builds an *explicit* env map (plugin dirs + PATH only), so `CLAUDECODE` is not\ninherited and the daemon still resolves codex-first. (`setupChildEnv` uses `os.Environ()` and does\ninherit — an inconsistency in its own right.) Either plumb the resolved agent into the daemon env,\nor report it explicitly as a known limitation. Shipping silently would miss the path where the\ndefect costs most."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":789,"cache_read_input_tokens":676651,"output_tokens":521,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":789},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"inp