{"parentUuid":"8b27e44f-4abb-4e9a-b1e7-f8c40ad8241c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cfk6ScdwFXAVKHNnuVDaw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Frnh2umEoi5MEuycsXMkWw","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/dynamic-petting-globe.md","old_string":"   Paths to add, decided with the user: `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `.claude/settings.json`,\n   `.codex/hooks.json`, `.brainignore`. (`.entire/*` is already exempt via the segment rule at\n   `:2473` — no change needed.)","new_string":"   Paths to add, decided with the user: `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `.claude/settings.json`,\n   `.brainignore`. (`.entire/*` is already exempt via the segment rule — no change needed.\n   `.codex/hooks.json` was **dropped** after review: nothing in this repo writes it — the only\n   hook writer is `MergePreEditHook` → `.claude/settings.json`.)\n\n   **Why `.patterns` and not the segment list** — this is the whole point of the gate-only seam.\n   `pathHasSegment` does exact *segment* equality, so `.claude/settings.json` entered there would\n   be a silent **no-op** and the reporter's own file would still block; the only spelling that\n   works is bare `.claude`, which would swallow `.claude/` entirely at any depth. `.patterns` goes\n   through `brainIgnorePatternMatches`, which is root-anchored and matches the full path as\n   written. Segment entries would also match at **any** depth (`docs/AGENTS.md`), which\n   `TestBrainIgnoreDoesNotOvermatchDefaultDirectoryPrefixes` exists to prevent.\n\n   **Corroboration:** this repo's own `.brainignore` already lists `.claude/settings.json` under\n   *\"Local agent/editor runtime state\"* and deliberately does **not** list `AGENTS.md`/`CLAUDE.md` —\n   maintainers put those two on the indexed side on purpose, and `isHighSignalDoc` (`seed.go`)\n   ranks them top-signal. Gate-only keeps that intact. If an implementation ever makes them stop\n   being indexed, the seam is wrong — stop."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":588,"cache_read_input_tokens":677440,"output_tokens":791,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":588},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":791,"cache_read_input_tokens":677440,"cache_creation_input_tokens":588,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":588,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Frnh2umEoi5MEuycsXMkWw":{"file_path":"/Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/dynamic-petting-globe.md","old_string":"   Paths to add, decided with the user: `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `.claude/settings.json`,\n   `.codex/hooks.json`, `.brainignore`. (`.entire/*` is already exempt via the segment rule at\n   `:2473` — no change needed.)","new_string":"   Paths to add, decided with the user: `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `.claude/settings.json`,\n   `.brainignore`. (`.entire/*` is already exempt via the segment rule — no change needed.\n   `.codex/hooks.json` was **dropped** after review: nothing in this repo writes it — the only\n   hook writer is `MergePreEditHook` → `.claude/settings.json`.)\n\n   **Why `.patterns` and not the segment list** — this is the whole point of the gate-only seam.\n   `pathHasSegment` does exact *segment* equality, so `.claude/settings.json` entered there would\n   be a silent **no-op** and the reporter's own file would still block; the only spelling that\n   works is bare `.claude`, which would swallow `.claude/` entirely at any depth. `.patterns` goes\n   through `brainIgnoreP