thIgnore` delegates; existing tests unchanged.\n  - `worktreeStatusPathList` — semantic.go:2663.\n  - Semantic gate uses a SEPARATE gateIgnore from the indexer's `ignore` — semantic.go:574,583.\n  - Seed gate — seed.go:271,280.\n  - `dirtyWorktreeRefusal` / `describeDirtyWorktreePaths` — semantic.go:2697,2706 — names count + up to 5 paths + \"pass --worktree … or commit or stash these changes first\". `dirtyWorktreeErrorCode+\":\"` prefix preserved EXACTLY (setupIsDirtyWorktree + watch recovery match on it).\n  - docs/getting-started.md:276-302 — the doc DOCUMENTED this failure as expected behaviour (`entire enable` → two red x). Now stale; rewritten.\n  \n  **worktreeDirty's 3 other callers — decision, not side effect (plan item 2).** All three move WITH the gate, documented in-code at semantic.go:2633:\n  - `verifySemanticWorktreeStable` (semantic.go:2641): MUST match — it compares against a `dirtyBefore` captured by the gate; a mismatch would invent \"worktree dirtiness changed during semantic indexing\".\n  - `semanticStaleReport` (semantic.go:2995): must not print `worktree=dirty` about a tree the gate calls clean, or status_render names a remedy the state doesn't need.\n  - `semanticRefreshNeeded` (refresh.go:791): left on the indexing ignore it would queue a rebuild for a config edit and then have the rebuild refuse it — the reported bug one layer up.\n  `gitPathspecExclusions` and `worktreeFingerprint` deliberately NOT changed (worktree mode indexes that content, so it should change the hash).\n  \n  FIX B — agent default\n  - `defaultRefreshAgent` — refresh.go:843 — order: no-egress → detected harness (IF its binary probes OK) → codex → claude → none.\n  - `detectedAgentHarness` — refresh.go:874 — `envBool(\"CLAUDECODE\") || CLAUDE_CODE_ENTRYPOINT != \"\"`. No Codex signal invented.\n  - `agentProbeBinary` — refresh.go:885 — claude-code→claude. **Your correction #1 applied**: detected-but-unavailable falls through to the probe; test `TestDefaultRefreshAgentFallsBackWhenHarnessBinaryMissing` pins it.\n  - `resolveRefreshAgentAnnounced` wrapper + `announceResolvedAgent` — refresh.go:909,922. Pure fn + its 3 existing callers untouched (B3). Plain Fprintln not a progress task — bytes must not depend on TTY/elapsed time.\n  - Wired at 3 user-facing sites: refresh.go:145 (stderr), distill_cmd.go:665 (nil writer under --json), setup.go:1279 (nil writer under --json).\n  - watch.go:116 `\"codex\"` → `\"auto\"`.\n  - EXCLUDED as instructed: `ollamaModelMissingWarning` (confirmed 0 hits on main), interactive prompt, `\" -> \"` bug.\n  \n  One existing test edited: setup_pr89_test.go:415 pins `w.distillAgent = \"codex\"`. With \"auto\" + a fixture runner answering no `--version`, runDistill returns \"distillation requires an agent\" before reaching the pass lock, so the test would assert about a pass that never contended. Subject is contention, not selection. Commented in place.\n  \n  ## WEAKENING TABLE (every one applied compile-clean, sentinel grep-confirmed, built, run, restored)\n  \n  | guard | what I broke | test red | quoted assertion |\n  |---|---|---|---|\n  | gate exemption | `worktreeGateIgnore` returns plain `loadBrainIgnore` | 4 tests | `a tree dirty only with Entire-authored config was gated as dirty; this is the reported install failure` |\n  | gate exemption (e2e) | same | TestRefreshBuildsBothComponentsAfterInitAgents | `refresh after init-agents: dirty_worktree: refusing to seed uncommitted content without --worktree (3 uncommitted paths: AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, .claude/settings.json); …` |\n  | not \"ignore everything\" | gate paths + `\"**\"` | 4 tests | `one uncommitted source file was gated as clean; the fix became 'ignore everything'` |\n  | user .brainignore kept | `withGatePaths` drops `i.patterns` | TestWorktreeGateKeepsUserBrainIgnore | `a user .brainignore pattern stopped applying once the built-ins were added` |\n  | right seam (indexing intact) | gate paths added to `brainIgnore.Ignored` | TestWorktreeGateIgnoreKeepsIndexingIgnoreIntact | `AGENTS.md became ignored by the INDEXING filter; that deletes it from the indexed doc corpus, which is a regression disguised as a fix` |\n  | actionable refusal | back to bare message | 3 tests | `refusal does not mention \"2 uncommitted paths\": \"dirty_worktree: refusing to index uncommitted content without --worktree\"` |\n  | machine prefix | dropped `dirty_worktree:` | TestDirtyWorktreeRefusalKeepsMachinePrefix | `refusal lost its machine-readable prefix: \"refusing to seed uncommitted content without --worktree (1 uncommitted path: src/main.go); …\"` |\n  | filterWorktreeStatus all-vs-any | `allIgnored` → any-ignored | new test + existing TestWorktreeDirtyKeepsRenameFromIgnoredToPublic | `filterWorktreeStatus(\"R  AGENTS.md -> docs/AGENTS.md\\n\") = \"\", want \"R  AGENTS.md -> docs/AGENTS.md\\n\"` |\n  | harness preference | detection block removed | 3 tests | `defaultRefreshAgent inside Claude Code = \"codex\", want claude-code` |\n  | availability verified | return harness unverified | TestDefaultRefreshAgentFallsBackWhenHarnessBinaryMissing | `defaultRefreshAgent with CLAUDECODE set but no claude binary = \"claude-code\", want codex` |\n  | ENTRYPOINT signal | CLAUDECODE only | TestDefaultRefreshAgentDetectsEntrypointAlone | `defaultRefreshAgent with CLAUDE_CODE_ENTRYPOINT=cli = \"codex\", want claude-code` |\n  | announce | `announceResolvedAgent` no-op | 3 tests | `refresh did not announce the agent it chose on stderr: \"refresh: locate brain\\n…\"` |\n  | distill --json silence | always pass stderr | TestDistillJSONStaysSilentAboutTheAgent | `json: the agent announcement leaked into machine output: \"agent: auto-selected codex (SPENDS TOKENS) — override with --agent\\n{\\n  \\\"code\\\": \\\"command_failed\\\"…` |\n  | setup announce | setup never announces | TestSetupDetectAgentAnnouncesExceptUnderJSON | `human: setup chose an agent without saying which, so the json case above proves nothing: \"\"` |\n  | setup --json silence | always pass stderr | same | `json: setup announced the agent while a machine reader was parsing: \"agent: auto-selected codex …\"` |\n  | watch default | `\"auto\"` → `\"codex\"` | TestWatchDistillAgentDefaultsToAuto | `watch distill agent default = \"codex\", want auto (a hardcoded vendor here bypasses defaultRefreshAgent entirely)` |\n  \n  16 weakenings, 16 red. Zero \"0 failures\" outcomes. One patcher failed its anchor (gofmt had realigned the struct literal) — caught by the sentinel guard, re-anchored, re-run red.\n  \n  ## ACCEPTANCE TEST — your correction #2 applied\n  Plan's \"setup must succeed\" test discarded as invalid (bestEffort=true ⇒ setup exits 0 degraded before AND after). Replaced with `TestRefreshBuildsBothComponentsAfterInitAgents` on `refresh` (non-bestEffort) asserting COMPONENT outcomes: `refresh: seed baseline: 3 documents… done` and `refresh: semantic index: 1 symbol… done` both present, and no `dirty_worktree` anywhere in output.\n  \n  New file: internal/cli/install_ux_test.go, 18 test funcs, narrative comments quoting the real reports.\n  \n  ## BUILD / VET / TESTS\n  - `go build ./...` clean. `go vet ./...` clean. `gofmt -l -s internal/cli/` empty.\n  - Targeted sweeps (GOMAXPROCS=1, -p 1 -parallel 1): `Worktree|Dirty|Agent|Refresh|Seed|Semantic|Setup|Watch|Distill|Status|FilterWorktree|InitAgents` → 995 pass. `Skill|Facts|Workspace|Pattern|Memory|Export|Doctor|Brief|Query|Ignore|Index` → 1552 pass. New tests 27/27.\n  - **One failure, PROVEN pre-existing**: `TestOllamaDistillAgentEnvelopeAllowanceIsCeilinged`. Reverted all 7 source files to pristine main, removed my test file, ran 5x → 4 FAIL / 1 ok. Byte count differs each run (37.8M/39.8M/40.9M vs 33.5M ceiling). It is a load-sensitive race between the httptest writer goroutine and the client's stop; nothing I touched is on that path.\n  \n  ## KNOWN LIMITATION — your correction #4, reported not silently shipped\n  `daemonEnv` (setup.go:1204) builds an EXPLICIT env map (plugin dirs + PATH only), so CLAUDECODE does NOT reach the `workspace watch --distill` daemon; with B4's \"auto\" it resolves codex-first there. **Partially mitigated and I verified the mitigation path in source**: setup.go:580 resolves the agent ONCE, `setupWatchPlanEntryFor` (setup_watchplan.go:189) writes it to the plan, `applyWatchPlanEntry` (setup_watchplan.go:207) sets `w.distillAgent` from it — so a daemon installed by a `setup` run INSIDE Claude Code does get claude-code. The gap is only a daemon with no plan entry, or one installed from a non-Claude-Code shell. Inconsistency worth noting: `setupChildEnv` (setup.go:1087) uses `os.Environ()` and DOES inherit. Not plumbed — out of this PR's scope.\n  \n  ## UNVERIFIED\n  - No real `entire graph init-agents` → `entire brain setup` run against a live repo; the end-to-end is at command level with a fake CommandRunner.\n  - `.codex/hooks.json` dropped on your instruction, but note this repo's OWN `.brainignore` lists it under \"Local agent/editor runtime state\" — if some installer does write it, it will still block the gate.\n  - `rejectAgentForNoEgress(\"auto\")` fires BEFORE the auto resolution (distill_cmd.go:651 vs :658), so `watch --distill` under ENTIRE_BRAIN_NO_EGRESS now errors on \"auto\" where it previously errored on \"codex\" — same class, not a new regression, but not fixed either.\n  - No full `go test ./...` (CPU-bound, per your constraint). ~2350 of 3136 test funcs exercised across the two sweeps.\n  - Did not record an `entire brain remember` fact (would write brain state outside PR scope).\n  - Nothing pushed, no PR, no merge, no approvals. No AI attribution footer.\n  \n</agent-message>\n\nThat \"other Claude session\" is an agent working inside this same session — a subagent or teammate spawned on your user's behalf (by you, or alongside you) — so this was not typed by your user. Treat it as that agent's report or request and act on it within this session's own permission settings. Such 