{"parentUuid":"a91e49b1-9963-4f52-810a-39a51b86bf33","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cfk8vdZGamN5LpfXdf2pc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Found a real error — **mine**. My correction #3 was wrong:\n\n- `.codex/hooks.json` **is** written — by the `cli` repo (`agent/codex/hook_root.go`), a sibling in the same product, not by brain.\n- This repo's own `.brainignore` lists it at line 15, under the maintainers' own \"local agent/editor runtime state\" stanza.\n\nSo `entire enable --agent codex` would dirty the tree and hit exactly the bug we're fixing — for Codex users, which is ironic given fix B. Sending it back:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1924,"cache_read_input_tokens":691089,"output_tokens":2096,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":929},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1924},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2096,"cache_read_input_tokens":691089,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1924,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1924,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"0c7031be-385e-407d-8208-8e11fb833464","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cfk8vdBgcXZXYnjSKM93x","type":"assistant","uuid":"23bf0810-aab3-408b-bcc9-daafd60f3825","timestamp":"2026-10-06T01:45:09.123Z","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-install-ux","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.290","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"23bf0810-aab3-408b-bcc9-daafd60f3825","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cfk8vdZGamN5LpfXdf2pc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WcbhEbQh2qWFL5yUk6ohyM","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"ac4b585e3f8302c86","summary":"My correction #3 was wrong, restore codex paths","message":"One correction to reverse — my earlier instruction #3 was WRONG, and your \"unverified\" note caught it. Please fix.\n\nI told you to drop `.codex/hooks.json` because \"nothing in this repo writes it\". That reasoning was too narrow. It IS written — by the sibling `cli` repo at `cli/cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/hook_root.go`, via `entire enable --agent codex`. Same product, same install flow, same user. A Codex user hits precisely the bug this PR fixes, and we would have shipped the fix with their case still broken — which would be a poor result for a PR whose other half is about not disadvantaging Codex users.\n\nDecisive evidence, which also removes any arbitrariness from the list: this repo's OWN `.brainignore` lines 12-16 already define the set, under the comment \"Local agent/editor runtime state\":\n\n    .claude/settings.json\n    .claude/skills/\n    .codex/config.toml\n    .codex/hooks.json\n    .codex/skills/\n\nThat is the maintainers' own line between \"agent runtime state\" and \"source\". Align the gate built-ins with it exactly, rather than with my guess. So `entireAuthoredGatePaths` becomes those five plus `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `.brainignore`.\n\nAlso please fix the comment you added at semantic.go:2327 — it currently says `.codex/hooks.json` is \"deliberately absent — nothing in this codebase writes\" it. That is true of this repo and misleading about the product; it would have cemented my mistake for the next reader. Replace it with the real reason the list looks like it does: it mirrors the repo's own `.brainignore` \"local agent/editor runtime state\" stanza, and the writers live across brain, graph and cli.\n\nAdd one test pinning a Codex-shaped install: a tree dirty only with `.codex/hooks.json` (plus `AGENTS.md`/`CLAUDE.md`) must pass the gate. Weakening-verify it like the rest — drop `.codex/hooks.json` from the list, show it red, quote the assertion, restore.\n\nKeep everything else exactly as it is. Do not re-touch the indexing filter: I verified `brainIgnore.Ignored` and `gitPathspecExclusions` are untouched versus main and that must stay true. Build + vet + gofmt clean before you finish. Amend onto the existing commit rather than adding a second one. Still: no push, no PR, no merge, no approvals, no AI attribution footer.\n\nReport back just the delta: what changed, the new test, its weakening evidence, and build/vet status.","type":"message","recipient":"ac4b585e3f8302c86","content":"One correction to reverse — my earlier instructio…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1924,"cache_read_input_tokens":691089,"output_tokens":2096,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":929},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1924},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2096,"cache_read_input_tokens":691089,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1924,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1924,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01WcbhEbQh2qWFL5yUk6ohyM":{"to":"ac4b585e3f8302c86","summary":"My correction #3 was wrong, restore codex paths","message":"One correction to reverse — my earlier instruction #3 was WRONG, and your \"unverified\" note caught it. Please fix.\n\nI told you to drop `.codex/hooks.json` because \"nothing in this repo writes it\". That reasoning was too narrow. It IS written — by the sibling `cli` repo at `cli/cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/hook_root.go`, via `entire enable --agent codex`. Same product, same install flow, same user. A Codex user hits precisely the bug this PR fixes, and we would have shipped the fix with their case still broken — which would be a poor result for a PR whose other half is about not disadvantaging Codex users.\n\nDecisive evidence, which also removes any arbitrariness from the list: this repo's OWN `.brainignore` lines 12-16 already define the set, under the comment \"Local agent/editor runtime state\":\n\n    .claude/settings.json\n    .claude/skills/\n    .codex/config.toml\n    .codex/hooks.json\n    .codex/skills/\n\nThat is the maintainers' own line between \"agent runtime state\" and \"source\". Align the gate built-ins with it exactly, rather than with my guess. So `entireAuthoredGatePaths` becomes those five plus `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `.brainignore`.\n\nAlso please fix the comment you added at semantic.go:2327 — it currently says `.codex/hooks.json` is \"deliberately absent — nothing in this codebase writes\" it. That is true of this repo and misleading about the product; it would have cemented my mistake for the next reader. Replace it with the real reason the list looks like it does: it mirrors the repo's own `.brainignore` \"local agent/editor runtime state\" stanza, and the writers live across brain, graph and cli.\n\nAdd one test pinning a Codex-shaped install: a tree dirty only with `.codex/hooks.json` (plus `AGENTS.md`/`CLAUDE.md`) must pass the gate. Weakening-verify it like the rest — drop `.codex/hooks.json` from the list, show it red, quote the assertion, restore.\n\nKeep everything else exactly as it is. Do not re-touch the indexing filter: I verified `brainIgnore.Ignored` and `gitPathspecExclusions` are untouched versus main and that must stay true. Build + vet + gofmt clean before you finish. Amend onto the existing commit rather than adding a second one. Still: no push, no PR, no merge, no approvals, no AI attribution footer.\n\nReport back just the delta: what changed, the new test, its weakening evidence, and build/vet status."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"0c7031be-385e-407d-8208-8e11fb833464","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Cfk8vdBgcXZXYnjSKM93x","type":"assistant","uuid":"4f988165-6263-4d95-ae23-b21aeebcb576","timestamp":"2026-10-06T01:45:22.169Z","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-install-ux","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.290","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
