{"parentUuid":"40d80246-a537-4c40-a0fb-089e5af53961","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cfma9dzLqQ1dJKzxhss1V","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The plumbing is actually complete — `setupOpts.model` → watch plan → daemon, and `watch --model` exists. So the gap is purely that we never *say* it. Sending the final piece:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1930,"cache_read_input_tokens":706026,"output_tokens":1897,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":441},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1930},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1897,"cache_read_input_tokens":706026,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1930,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1930,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"9b89d396-ac43-48fe-9e70-fe4b0e3c4465","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cfma9dd1x5bF1nE86Sisc","type":"assistant","uuid":"8235b178-641a-44bb-a421-50ad1c7f2113","timestamp":"2026-10-06T19:56:24.556Z","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-install-ux","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.290","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"8235b178-641a-44bb-a421-50ad1c7f2113","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cfma9dzLqQ1dJKzxhss1V","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011fQL7cqpGDg6zgnzYXcZ58","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"ac4b585e3f8302c86","summary":"Close the model-visibility and daemon gaps","message":"Two final changes on the same branch, then we're done. Amend onto c24cf48b.\n\nCONTEXT — the reporter's second sentence was \"idk what model\", and we have not answered it. I checked whether we should pin Sonnet/Opus as a default: NO. `setup.go:47` already states the decision and the reason — \"Model is deliberately NOT defaulted to a hard-coded name — model ids age badly — so the agent's own default applies unless --model is given.\" That is sound and we respect it. Hardcoding a model id would be the same mistake as the codex-first default, in the other direction.\n\nSo the fix is VISIBILITY, not a default. The plumbing already exists end to end: `setupOpts.model` → `setup_watchplan.go:178` Model → `:212` → `w.model` → daemon, and `watch --model` / `distill --model` are both real flags. The only thing missing is that nothing ever tells the user which model is in play.\n\nCHANGE 1 — announce the model alongside the agent.\nExtend `announceResolvedAgent` (refresh.go:922) to take the model and say it. Required shapes:\n- model pinned: name it, e.g. `agent: auto-selected claude-code, model opus (SPENDS TOKENS) — override with --agent/--model`\n- model NOT pinned: say so EXPLICITLY rather than omitting it, e.g. `... model: the agent's own default — pin one with --model`. The whole point is that \"idk what model\" must stop being true; silence is what caused the complaint.\n- `agent: none` case keeps its current text (no model to name).\nThread the model from the same three user-facing sites already wired (refresh, distill, setup). Keep `--json` silent exactly as now. Keep it a plain Fprintln, not a progress task, so bytes don't depend on TTY or elapsed time.\n\nCHANGE 2 — close the daemon gap you reported.\nYou found `setup.go:580` resolves the agent once and `setupWatchPlanEntryFor` writes it to the plan, so a daemon installed from inside Claude Code inherits it; the hole is a plan entry with no agent, or a setup run from a non-Claude-Code shell. Make the resolved agent ALWAYS be written into the watch plan entry, so the daemon never falls back to its own codex-first resolution with a different env. If the plan entry already carries an explicit user choice, do not overwrite it — only fill the blank. Do the same for model if it is set. If after investigating you conclude this cannot be done safely in this PR, say so plainly with the reason and leave it — do not half-do it.\n\nVERIFICATION — same bar as before, no exceptions:\n- A test that the announcement names the model when pinned.\n- A test that it explicitly says \"agent's own default\" when unpinned. This is the one that answers the report; weaken it by dropping the unpinned branch and show it red.\n- A test that `--json` stays silent about both agent and model.\n- A test that a watch plan entry written by setup carries the resolved agent, and that an explicit user choice is NOT overwritten.\n- Every guard weakening-verified, compile-clean, red output quoted, restored. If a weakening yields 0 failures, suspect your test first and grep to confirm the edit applied.\n\nUnchanged constraints: do NOT touch the indexing filter (`brainIgnore.Ignored`, `gitPathspecExclusions`, the segment list) — I verified it is untouched and that must hold. `go build ./...`, `go vet ./...`, `gofmt -l -s internal/cli/` all clean. GOMAXPROCS=1 -p 1 -parallel 1, targeted -run only. No push, no PR, no merge, no approvals, no AI attribution footer.\n\nREPORT: just the delta — what changed, new tests, weakening evidence with quoted red assertions, build/vet, and anything you could not verify.","type":"message","recipient":"ac4b585e3f8302c86","content":"Two final changes on the same branch, then we're …"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1930,"cache_read_input_tokens":706026,"output_tokens":1897,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":441},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1930},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1897,"cache_read_input_tokens":706026,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1930,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1930,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_011fQL7cqpGDg6zgnzYXcZ58":{"to":"ac4b585e3f8302c86","summary":"Close the model-visibility and daemon gaps","message":"Two final changes on the same branch, then we're done. Amend onto c24cf48b.\n\nCONTEXT — the reporter's second sentence was \"idk what model\", and we have not answered it. I checked whether we should pin Sonnet/Opus as a default: NO. `setup.go:47` already states the decision and the reason — \"Model is deliberately NOT defaulted to a hard-coded name — model ids age badly — so the agent's own default applies unless --model is given.\" That is sound and we respect it. Hardcoding a model id would be the same mistake as the codex-first default, in the other direction.\n\nSo the fix is VISIBILITY, not a default. The plumbing already exists end to end: `setupOpts.model` → `setup_watchplan.go:178` Model → `:212` → `w.model` → daemon, and `watch --model` / `distill --model` are both real flags. The only thing missing is that nothing ever tells the user which model is in play.\n\nCHANGE 1 — announce the model alongside the agent.\nExtend `announceResolvedAgent` (refresh.go:922) to take the model and say it. Required shapes:\n- model pinned: name it, e.g. `agent: auto-selected claude-code, model opus (SPENDS TOKENS) — override with --agent/--model`\n- model NOT pinned: say so EXPLICITLY rather than omitting it, e.g. `... model: the agent's own default — pin one with --model`. The whole point is that \"idk what model\" must stop being true; silence is what caused the complaint.\n- `agent: none` case keeps its current text (no model to name).\nThread the model from the same three user-facing sites already wired (refresh, distill, setup). Keep `--json` silent exactly as now. Keep it a plain Fprintln, not a progress task, so bytes don't depend on TTY or elapsed time.\n\nCHANGE 2 — close the daemon gap you reported.\nYou found `setup.go:580` resolves the agent once and `setupWatchPlanEntryFor` writes it to the plan, so a daemon installed from inside Claude Code inherits it; the hole is a plan entry with no agent, or a setup run from a non-Claude-Code shell. Make the resolved agent ALWAYS be written into the watch plan entry, so the daemon never falls back to its own codex-first resolution with a different env. If the plan entry already carries an explicit user choice, do not overwrite it — only fill the blank. Do the same for model if it is set. If after investigating you conclude this cannot be done safely in this PR, say so plainly with the reason and leave it — do not half-do it.\n\nVERIFICATION — same bar as before, no exceptions:\n- A test that the announcement names the model when pinned.\n- A test that it explicitly says \"agent's own default\" when unpinned. This is the one that answers the report; weaken it by dropping the unpinned branch and show it red.\n- A test that `--json` stays silent about both agent and model.\n- A test that a watch plan entry written by setup carries the resolved agent, and that an explicit user choice is NOT overwritten.\n- Every guard weakening-verified, compile-clean, red output quoted, restored. If a weakening yields 0 failures, suspect your test first and grep to confirm the edit applied.\n\nUnchanged constraints: do NOT touch the indexing filter (`brainIgnore.Ignored`, `gitPathspecExclusions`, the segment list) — I verified it is untouched and that must hold. `go build ./...`, `go vet ./...`, `gofmt -l -s internal/cli/` all clean. GOMAXPROCS=1 -p 1 -parallel 1, targeted -run only. No push, no PR, no merge, no approvals, no AI attribution footer.\n\nREPORT: just the delta — what changed, new tests, weakening evidence with quoted red assertions, build/vet, and anything you could not verify."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"9b89d396-ac43-48fe-9e70-fe4b0e3c4465","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Cfma9dd1x5bF1nE86Sisc","type":"assistant","uuid":"7f115c2d-35cd-4711-8279-f904ae23ec2d","timestamp":"2026-10-06T19:56:42.268Z","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-install-ux","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.290","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
