{"parentUuid":"4609dc33-bd89-4853-8d40-476de743d4ad","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14991959 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"5877ed5b-bef0-4a69-a278-fab228d339be","timestamp":"2026-10-06T19:56:42.957Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14991959 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-install-ux","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.290","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"5877ed5b-bef0-4a69-a278-fab228d339be","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfmaBdvB7jU3FjWHXiJcd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Fair hit — I kept handing back a \"product decision\" that the reporter had already made. But the answer turned out not to be the one either of us assumed.\n\n## I was about to default to Sonnet/Opus. That would have been wrong.\n\n`setup.go:47` already records the decision and the reason:\n\n> *\"Model is deliberately NOT defaulted to a hard-coded name — **model ids age badly** — so the agent's own default applies unless `--model` is given.\"*\n\nHardcoding a model id is the same error as the codex-first default, pointed the other way: a guess baked into source that rots. So I'm not doing it.\n\n## The real gap is that we never *say* the model\n\nThe plumbing is already complete end to end — `setupOpts.model` → watch plan → `w.model` → daemon, with `--model` on both `watch` and `distill`. A user can already pin Opus today.\n\nWhat's missing is that **nothing ever tells them what's running**. That's precisely the reporter's words: *\"idk what model\"* — a visibility complaint, not a default complaint. So the fix now in flight:\n\n- When a model is pinned: name it.\n- When it isn't: say **\"the agent's own default — pin one with `--model`\"** explicitly, rather than staying silent. Silence is what produced the complaint.\n\nCombined with fix B, a Claude Code user now gets the Claude CLI, is told so, and is told how to pin Opus — which answers the request as filed without inventing a default that ages.\n\nAlso closing the daemon gap I'd flagged and left open: the resolved agent will always be written into the watch plan entry, so the daemon can't fall back to its own codex-first resolution under a different env — without overwriting an explicit user choice.\n\nBoth pieces carry the same bar as the rest: every guard weakening-verified, red output quoted, indexing filter untouched. I'll report the delta once it lands, verified myself rather than relayed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2018,"cache_read_input_tokens":707956,"output_tokens":614,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2018},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":614,"cache_read_input_tokens":707956,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2018,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2018,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"855025b9-dc90-4e3a-a7f0-e3c96e5ec5f7","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfmaBdXs9mb4GEtcuoQA2","type":"assistant","uuid":"7e3d4969-dc29-4d4c-90ae-e7a836596741","timestamp":"2026-10-06T19:56:52.380Z","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-install-ux","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.290","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
