{"parentUuid":"89848d30-b10c-4481-8379-ef0179cf9912","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfmhcxUekcRzFFCbChTbd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes — and it says I got it wrong.\n\n**I told you six PRs were sitting blocked on your approval. At least three of them merged yesterday:** #318, #320 and #331. Plus #332 and #334 from khaong, and #319 was closed.\n\nMy last fetch was **Oct 4 21:25**. Everything in your paste happened after that. I did caveat it, but a caveat doesn't make a wrong answer right — I reported a week's merge activity as \"only 3 merged\" when the real number was much higher.\n\n## The bell that actually rings\n\n**#332 — khaong, merged 2 days ago — carries #331's exact title:** *\"fix(guide): make shipped guidance directive, name only commands graph exposes, and wire the pre-edit hook.\"*\n\nThat's the branch I had an agent clearing findings on all session. If khaong landed that work as #332, then today's trail-loop rounds on #331 were cleaning a PR that was already being superseded — and #331 showing as \"merged yesterday\" alongside it suggests both went in, or one absorbed the other.\n\nWorth you checking which, because it decides whether today's two rounds on #331 were useful or redundant.\n\n## The consequence that matters right now\n\n**My new fix branch is based on a stale main.** I branched `fix/install-ux-dirty-gate-and-agent-default` off `6c8ebdab` — the tip *as of Oct 4*. Since then #318, #320, #331, #332 and #334 have merged. So:\n\n- The branch is now several PRs behind.\n- #332 touched the **agent guide and the pre-edit hook** — adjacent to my Fix B (`defaultRefreshAgent`, announcements). Real conflict risk.\n- Worse, the zero-conflict case: main may now call functions I changed the signature of. That's silently broken a build in this repo three times before.\n\nIt needs `git merge origin/main` plus `go build ./...` **and** `go vet ./...` before it's PR-ready. I can't do that from here — no network to fetch.\n\n## Also worth noting\n\nThe titles in your paste appear offset by one row from their numbers — e.g. the line under #317 is `perf(semantic): verify a generation once per file version`, which is #316's branch (`perf/verify-once-per-generation`). So I'd treat the number↔title pairing as unreliable, and some of #311–#315 read like entire-graph work rather than brain. Don't let me build a story on that until it's confirmed.\n\n**What unblocks me:** `GH_TOKEN` in `~/.claude/settings.json` env. Then I can fetch, rebase the branch onto real main, re-run build/vet and the live before/after, and tell you exactly what merged and whether #332 overlaps our work."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1678,"cache_read_input_tokens":739902,"output_tokens":4608,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":3717},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1678},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4608,"cache_read_input_tokens":739902,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1678,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1678,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"51db007d-714f-43f4-8539-f1dfc33bd705","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cfmhcx5b2EMSk79XzBnXj","type":"assistant","uuid":"e6acc6df-8cc3-4c64-a48e-6aea5156e8cd","timestamp":"2026-10-06T21:35:14.241Z","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.290","gitB