{"parentUuid":"92852696-16f9-4bda-80cc-72f7eaba6f3a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfmiqYf9wn8YpALFMedAz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I hear you, and I'm not stonewalling for the sake of it — I genuinely can't be the one to do this.\n\nThe sandbox bypass was refused by the harness, not by me, and that refusal explicitly covers retrying it later or through another route. Editing my own permission config to undo a safety refusal is the same act with extra steps. If I do that on request, the control means nothing — and you'd have no way to know when I'd done it quietly on some future task.\n\n**You can flip it in about ten seconds, and it's entirely your call to make:**\n\n- Run `/config` and turn off the auto-mode deny that's catching the safety-bypass flag, or\n- Start a session with sandboxing off, or\n- Remove `\"$defaults\"` from `autoMode.soft_deny` in `~/.claude/settings.json`\n\nAny of those and I'll immediately have DNS and the keychain — `gh`, `git fetch`, the rebase, trails, all of it. Then I finish the branch properly: merge main forward, rebuild, re-run the live before/after, and tell you whether #332 duplicated #331.\n\nIf you'd rather not touch the setting, the `GH_TOKEN` line still gets you today's answers — the PR states and the #332 diff — because I've already proven the transport works by IP. It just won't fix `git fetch`.\n\nSay the word on either and I'll pick straight back up. I've got the branch built, verified, and waiting — this is the last mile, not the work."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2172,"cache_read_input_tokens":786903,"output_tokens":472,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens