{"parentUuid":"6e406dc5-2a6a-476a-8bed-c6c7abf95697","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfmizRypVWyKASSRUoPE7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1904,"cache_read_input_tokens":790212,"output_tokens":1624,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":868},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1904},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1624,"cache_read_input_tokens":790212,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1904,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1904,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":11372,"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfmizRcz7WsqVb1oY5FG1","type":"assistant","uuid":"296e2e87-f591-44fd-9892-9689d5f4099e","timestamp":"2026-10-06T21:52:25.582Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.292","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"296e2e87-f591-44fd-9892-9689d5f4099e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfmizRypVWyKASSRUoPE7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Found it. It was never Claude Code, never the sandbox, never GitHub.\n\n```\ndig github.com          →  140.82.113.3     ✅  network + DNS servers fine\ndscacheutil -q host     →  (empty)          ❌  DirectoryService lookup fails\ncurl https://github.com →  can't resolve    ❌  because getaddrinfo goes through it\nid -un                  →  501              ❌  can't resolve your own username\ndscl . -read /Users/…   →  eServerError     ❌  (from earlier)\n```\n\n**`opendirectoryd` is wedged on your Mac.** That one daemon backs both hostname resolution *and* user-identity lookups, which is why every single symptom traces to it:\n\n- `curl`/`git`/`gh` can't resolve any host — getaddrinfo asks DirectoryService\n- `whoami` prints `501` instead of your name — passwd lookup fails\n- `sudo: you do not exist in the passwd database` — same lookup\n- the **keychain** can't be read — it keys off your resolved identity, which is why `gh` and `entire` both lost their tokens\n- `dig` works throughout because it talks to a DNS server directly, bypassing the daemon entirely\n\nThat also explains why every workaround failed: each one needed either a name or an identity, and both come from the same broken place.\n\n**The fix is a reboot.** Normally you'd restart it with `sudo launchctl kickstart -k system/com.apple.opendirectoryd` — but `sudo` itself needs the passwd lookup that's broken, so that's circular. Logging out and back in may do it; a reboot definitely will.\n\nI was wrong earlier when I said your machine was fine and it was my sandbox. The evidence pointed that way — `whoami` returning a UID inside a sandboxed shell looks exactly like sandbox isolation — but disabling the sandbox changed nothing, which ruled it out. Sorry for sending you after DNS settings and tokens.\n\n**Nothing is lost.** The branch is committed locally at `3cc936ad`, worktree clean, 24 weakenings verified, live before/after captured. After you reboot, I pick straight up: fetch, merge main forward, rebuild, re-run the acceptance test, and settle whether #332 duplicated #331."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1904,"cache_read_input_tokens":790212,"output_tokens":1624,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":868},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1904},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1624,"cache_read_input_tokens":790212,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1904,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1904,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfmizRcz7WsqVb1oY5FG1","type":"assistant","uuid":"ec9499e7-2206-4f5e-80f9-6615ac03afa8","timestamp":"2026-10-06T21:52:35.684Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.292","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
