{"parentUuid":"644e86d7-77c3-44b9-b9b1-fb05d8b515a5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cfmj39d9VMoc9v2VAzB9P","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Your browser resolved github.com fine — you pasted PR lists from it. So DNS works **system-wide**; it's only this process tree that's lost its connection to the daemon. That changes the fix.\n\n**Run this in a fresh Terminal.app window** (a brand-new window, not a tab in the one that launched Claude Code):\n\n```\nwhoami && dscacheutil -q host -a name github.com | head -2\n```\n\n**If it prints `suhaan` and an IP** — your system is healthy and only Claude Code's process tree is broken. Quit Claude Code completely (not `/clear`, actually exit), then relaunch from that same fresh window:\n\n```\ncd ~/devenv/entire-brain && claude\n```\n\nThe reason your earlier restarts didn't help: relaunching from the *same* terminal inherits the same broken bootstrap context. It has to be a new window.\n\n**If it prints `501` and nothing** — then it is system-wide, and this is the command:\n\n```\nsudo launchctl kickstart -k system/com.apple.opendirectoryd\n```\n\nThat restarts the daemon in place, no reboot. It'll only work from a shell where `sudo` can look you up — which is the same test above, so run that first.\n\nTell me which one you got and I'll take it from there. Everything's committed at `3cc936ad` and waiting."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1663,"cache_read_input_tokens":792116,"output_tokens":1579,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1149},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1663},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1579,"cache_read_input_tokens":792116,"cache_creation_i