{"parentUuid":"9142e25a-dad7-475c-87f9-a2f2f2aaef16","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfmjGRhesDygJmGcu8UtF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1622,"cache_read_input_tokens":793779,"output_tokens":3307,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2468},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1622},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3307,"cache_read_input_tokens":793779,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1622,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1622,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":27827,"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfmjGQkMBP6SmMJ2iQnMu","type":"assistant","uuid":"9ef9d0ef-47b0-47e5-b49b-2de1e00137c7","timestamp":"2026-10-06T21:56:23.158Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.292","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"9ef9d0ef-47b0-47e5-b49b-2de1e00137c7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfmjGRhesDygJmGcu8UtF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here it is — titles reconciled against the branch names I'd verified locally (GitHub's list puts each title above its number, which is why my earlier read was off by one).\n\n## Brain PRs — last week\n\n**Merged: 13**\n\n*Facts*\n- **#311** — remember things that are not about one repository\n- **#318** — name the branches holding facts when a query finds none\n- **#320** — return the persisted merged fact in JSON\n- **#306** — facts import *(merged in this session)*\n\n*Agent guidance*\n- **#331** — make shipped guidance directive, name only commands graph exposes, wire the pre-edit hook\n- **#332** — same area, merged by **khaong**\n\n*Performance & distill*\n- **#316** — verify a semantic generation once per file version, not once per query\n- **#317** — make the ollama chunk-size limits real, and correct the advice that broke them\n\n*Measurement*\n- **#312** — measure index size and query latency against codebase size\n\n*Docs*\n- **#313** — publish what we measure, what we found, and what we do not claim\n- **#314** — say what the install script does, not what it is not\n- **#315** — re-score the twelve gap rows against what shipped\n- **#334** — contributor concepts guide *(khaong)*\n\n**Closed without merging: 1** — #319\n\n**Still open: 3**\n- **#321** — make the distill timeout configurable and name the nested-repo trap\n- **#329** — return output an agent can accept, and disclose what was dropped\n- **#330** — multi-agent safety / indexing on Windows\n\n## What the week was actually about\n\n**Nearly every PR makes brain honest about itself.** Say which branches hold the facts when a query looks empty. Return what was really saved. Publish what we *don't* claim. Correct advice that broke the thing it advised. Make guidance directive instead of optional.\n\nThat's the same defect class as today's work — empty answers that read as success, and tools that never say what they chose.\n\n**Docs were a third of it** — four PRs. Unusual, and it tracks: a tool whose value is invisible needs documentation as much as code.\n\n**#332 is the one to check.** Merged by khaong in the same area as your #331, a day apart. Either it duplicated that work or landed a different cut. Worth two minutes of your time, because my install-UX branch touches the same guide and hook code.\n\n**One pattern worth naming:** brain merged 13 PRs while entire-graph did 378 commits next door. Brain's constraint is review throughput, not authorship — which is why four of the six we cleared today merged within a day of being unblocked."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1622,"cache_read_input_tokens":793779,"output_tokens":3307,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2468},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1622},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3307,"cache_read_input_tokens":793779,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1622,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1622,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfmjGQkMBP6SmMJ2iQnMu","type":"assistant","uuid":"b9f79df0-ba69-41d9-b353-ccddeb198397","timestamp":"2026-10-06T21:56:33.380Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e