{"parentUuid":"3d7c4577-fad7-4c4f-8cea-0616438e2fbe","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfmjbpkG44ejQYeuqYWSF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"- **Brain stops lying when it has nothing.** It now names the branches holding your facts instead of a bare empty result, returns the fact it actually saved, and remembers things that aren't tied to one repo. Facts import landed too.\n\n- **Agents are now told to use brain, not invited to.** The shipped guidance became directive, names only commands that really exist, and wires a pre-edit hook — so an agent has a reason to consult the brain instead of grepping past it.\n\n- **Two speed and correctness fixes.** Semantic generations verify once per file version rather than once per query, and the ollama chunk-size limits became real — along with the advice that had been telling people to break them.\n\n- **The claims got published with their limits attached** — what we measure, what we found, and explicitly what we do *not* claim, plus index size and query latency measured against codebase size. Four doc PRs in one week, which is a lot, and right for a tool whose value is otherwise invisible.\n\n- **Still open: the three that bite new users** — configurable distill timeout and the nested-repo trap (#321), retrieval output an agent can actually accept (#329), and multi-agent safety on Windows (#330). Plus the branch I built today for the two install complaints, which is done and verified but needs a rebase before it can ship."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3474,"cache_read_input_tokens":795401,"output_tokens":411,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3474},"inference_geo":"not