{"parentUuid":"6cb6a579-f638-41f1-8bf7-d1a3096974f5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfmmP9xnbZqVGeb4G9J5w","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Hard numbers already: **43 top-level verbs**, doctor emits **35 lines** of internal schema names with 5 warns + 1 error on a *healthy* brain, and a first run ends \"degraded\" with a hint that was wrong for your case. Launching three parallel audits to get the complete list:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1704,"cache_read_input_tokens":816875,"output_tokens":1994,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":506},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1704},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1994,"cache_read_input_tokens":816875,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1704,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1704,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"63d86017-5ff6-4d85-9e4e-1b8b0f18377a","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfmmP9ZUdxQ1LjWdqTUtG","type":"assistant","uuid":"86b1f544-ac59-476b-8119-1b46f6280df2","timestamp":"2026-10-06T22:23:43.352Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.292","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"86b1f544-ac59-476b-8119-1b46f6280df2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfmmP9xnbZqVGeb4G9J5w","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017QUzJjXpAhnH2PZWYnBkmu","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Audit the first-run user flow","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"opus","prompt":"Audit entire-brain's FIRST-TIME USER FLOW and return a complete, prioritised defect list. Repo: /Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain (read origin/main; also /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-install-ux for an unmerged fix). Read-only: change nothing, commit nothing.\n\nGOAL: zero → first useful answer, with no dead ends and no misleading advice.\n\nREAL EVIDENCE — a live first run on a real research repo, today:\n- `entire brain setup` ended \"Brain ready (degraded)\" with seed AND semantic both FAILED on `dirty_worktree`.\n- The hint said: \"commit or stash the working tree … `entire enable` writes .entire/ and .claude/ without committing them, which is what a first run usually trips over.\"\n- That hint was WRONG for this user. Their dirt was ~250 real staged files (notebooks, models, figures, results). `.entire/`, `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md` were not in `git status` at all.\n- Re-running setup produced the identical degraded result. There is no forward path from inside `setup`.\n- `refresh --worktree` exists and would have worked. **`setup` exposes no such flag** — I verified: zero worktree/dirty flags on setup.\n- Result: a user mid-work is permanently degraded and told to do something irrelevant.\n\nINVESTIGATE AND LIST, each with file:line, severity (blocker/major/minor), and a concrete fix:\n1. Every path from `setup` that ends degraded or failed, and whether a forward path exists from inside setup. Is a `--worktree`/`--include-uncommitted` escape the right fix, or should setup auto-fall-back and say so?\n2. Every hint/remedy string in the setup + refresh + seed + semantic paths. For each: is it ALWAYS true, or only true in one case? The one above is wrong whenever dirt is not Entire's own files. Find the others. A confidently wrong remedy is worse than none.\n3. What does a brand-new user actually get? On a fresh repo with no sessions: facts 0/0, history 0 records, docs maybe 0. Is the first `brain query`/`overview`/`brief` useful, or empty? If empty, does it SAY why, or does it look broken? Trace what a first query returns with an empty brain.\n4. The daemon. Setup installs a persistent launchd service and announces it. Is that the right default for a first run? What does a user do who does not want it? Is removal discoverable?\n5. Idempotency and progress. Re-running setup repeated the same failures with no new information and no suggestion of what changed. Should it detect \"same failure twice\" and escalate the advice?\n6. `doctor`: 35 lines, mostly internal schema names (memory_overlay, memory_fts, memory_jobs, write_lock, memory_schema_capabilities), with 5 warn + 1 error on a brain that works. Which lines does a USER need? Which are implementer-only? Propose the user-facing subset and what the rest should hide behind (e.g. --verbose).\n\nUse `entire graph search --repo . --profile full --head --query \"...\"` before grepping; grep as fallback. Use rtk. Do NOT run full test suites (CPU-bound). Do NOT run `entire brain setup` against any real repo — use source reading plus, if needed, a throwaway git repo under /Users/suhaan/.claude/jobs/6ca2c8fb/tmp.\n\nOUTPUT: caveman-ultra compressed. A numbered list, each row: severity | what is wrong | file:line | concrete fix. Then \"TOP 5 TO FIX FIRST\" with one line of reasoning each. No prose padding, no preamble. Mark anything you could not confirm from source as \"unverified\"."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1704,"cache_read_input_tokens":816875,"output_tokens":1994,"output_to