{"parentUuid":"3c7fa06d-33c6-40aa-849b-4a9d49f31c2d","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14993913 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"a34804e0-1c7d-4de7-9661-ddffe353b27d","timestamp":"2026-10-06T22:24:15.491Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14993913 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.292","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"a34804e0-1c7d-4de7-9661-ddffe353b27d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfmmSCNxy9DSxP7eFBRAy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017qkhyEKpsBge4Sh81mf5so","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Audit agent usage of brain","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"opus","prompt":"Audit why CODING AGENTS do or don't use entire-brain, and return a complete prioritised defect list. Repos: /Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain (main) and /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-install-ux (unmerged fixes). Read-only.\n\nGOAL: an agent in a session reaches for brain at the right moments, gets a usable answer, and is never silently misled.\n\nEVIDENCE ALREADY ESTABLISHED (verify, then build on — do not redo):\n- The MCP surface is MISSING six CLI verbs agents need: `recall`, `verify`, `overview`, `entities`, `show`, `guide`. `recall` is the worst: the shipped agent guide MANDATES retrieving prior decisions, but an MCP-only agent cannot call it.\n- The shipped guide says \"No MCP tool writes a fact, so this is a CLI call; do not go looking for one\" — yet `brain_remember` IS registered in mcp.go. The guide contradicts the binary that ships it.\n- Facts are BRANCH-SCOPED: `recall` on main returns empty while facts live on the session's branch. The blind_spot line says so, but only if the agent reads it.\n- `init-agents` writes the guide; `setup` does not. A user who only runs `setup` gets a brain no agent is told about.\n- A session launched from a parent directory captures nothing, silently.\n\nINVESTIGATE AND LIST, each with file:line, severity, concrete fix:\n1. MCP vs CLI parity. Enumerate EVERY CLI verb and every MCP tool. For each gap, judge: does an agent need it? Is the gap deliberate (interactive/operational) or an oversight? Propose the minimal set to add.\n2. Does any MCP tool's OUTPUT mislead? Check empty-result shapes across tools: does each say WHY it is empty (blind_spot or equivalent), or can an agent read \"no results\" as \"no such thing exists\"? That false negative is the core risk. Name every tool whose empty answer is bare.\n3. Truncation. Tool results are capped at 32768 bytes; oversize replies drop tail rows and set `response_truncated` with a `dropped_from` record. Is that discoverable to an agent reading the result, or buried? Does every truncating surface declare it, or only some?\n4. The guide text itself (`.entire/agent-guide.md` generator). List every claim in it that is false, stale, or unverifiable against the shipped binary — the brain_remember one is a known example. Each with the generator's file:line.\n5. Discoverability. If an agent has brain available but no guide, is there anything that would lead it to use brain? (tool descriptions, `--help`, MCP tool descriptions.) Are the MCP tool descriptions good enough to be self-selecting without the guide?\n6. The pre-edit hook (`hook pre-edit`, in the unmerged branch). What does it actually serve an agent, and when? Is it wired by setup or only init-agents?\n\nUse `entire graph search --repo . --profile full --head --query \"...\"` first; grep as fallback. Use rtk. No full test suites. Do not modify anything.\n\nOUTPUT: caveman-ultra compressed. Numbered list: severity | defect | file:line | fix. Then \"TOP 5 TO FIX FIRST\" with one line each. Mark unconfirmed items \"unverified\". No preamble, no prose padding."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2396,"cache_read_input_tokens":818579,"output_tokens":1270,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2396},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1270,"cache_read_input_tokens":818579,"cache_crea