{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-06T22:28:01.875Z","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a6b60705e8b507ebf</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01Ayk4L4tVoNh7ZMkprzs4LS</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2/tasks/a6b60705e8b507ebf.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Audit MCP empty-result shapes\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Source: `/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-install-ux/internal/cli`. Static read only, nothing executed.\n\n**blind_spot contract.** `emptyResultBlindSpot` (`blind_spot.go:34`) returns one `note:` string. It says no brain built, brain unreadable, fact store lossy, distillation coverage unknown, or last distilled and N sessions since. It never mentions branch, embedder, conversation source or backfill. It is attached at only 3 call sites:\n- `retrieve_cmd.go:283` and `:303`\n- `retrieval_transport.go:333`, set by `retrieve_cmd.go:375`\n- `facts_read_cmd.go:412` and `:430`\n\n**Per tool**\n\n1. brain_query | `{query,branch,results:[]}` + `blind_spot` | Y | `retrieval_transport.go:333`, `retrieve_cmd.go:375` | LOW. Echoes `branch`, but the note does not say facts are branch-scoped.\n2. brain_search | same as brain_query | Y | same | LOW\n3. brain_vsearch | same as brain_query | Y | same | LOW-MED. Per the comment at `mcp.go:~1228`, a missing or stale conversation vector store returns a structured error, not an empty result. Missing embedder for the other sources: unverified.\n4. brain_get | `{branch,results:[],missing:[ids]}` | N in JSON | `retrieve_cmd.go:760` | MED. The text path adds \"not found is NOT evidence of absence\" (`:85`) only when the fact store is lossy. JSON `missing` carries no note.\n5. brain_multi_get | same as brain_get | N in JSON | `retrieve_cmd.go:760` | MED\n6. brain_entity_history | `{matches:[],note?,warnings?,index:{entities:0}}` | partial: `note` field | `entities_cmd.go:357` | LOW. When the index is empty the RESULT says \"the entity index is empty; run `entire brain entities backfill`\". Warnings go to stderr, which MCP discards (`cmd.SetErr(io.Discard)`), so only `note` and `truncated` reach the agent. A branch filter that empties the matches carries no note: unverified.\n7. brain_code / brain_search_code | `{freshness,trust,completeness_level,pagination,results:[]}` | N (equivalent: `freshness`) | `semantic.go:3389-3430` | LOW-MED. No semantic index returns an error (\"semantic index missing; run `entire brain index`\", `semantic.go:3413`). A stale index returns empty plus `freshness.severity`, with no sentence saying so.\n8. brain_search_graph | delegates to runSemanticQuery, same shape | N (`freshness`) | `semantic_graph.go:409` | LOW-MED\n9. brain_context | `{freshness,…,context:{symbols:[],relations:[]}}` | N (`freshness`) | `semantic.go:3484` | LOW-MED\n10. brain_impact | `{freshness,impact:{roots:[],symbols:[],relations:[]}}` | N (`freshness`) | `semantic.go:3570` | MED. This is the \"no callers\" false negative: empty means \"unindexed or unresolved\", not \"none\".\n11. brain_tests | `{freshness,tests:{roots:[],suggestions:[]}}` | N (`freshness`) | `semantic.go:3798` | MED\n12. brain_boundaries | `{freshness,boundary:{boundaries:[],handlers:[],relations:[]}}` | N (`freshness`) | `semantic.go:3732` | MED. An empty list reads as \"no routes or tools\".\n13. brain_changes / brain_detect_changes | `{freshness,changes:{clean:true,files:[],symbols:[]}}` | N | `semantic.go:3640` | LOW. `clean` is explicit.\n14. brain_query_graph | `{symbols:[],relations:[]}` | N, no freshness either | `semantic_graph.go:456` | HIGH. Bare empties on JSON.\n15. brain_dead_code | `{symbols:[]}` | N, no freshness either | `semantic_graph.go:936` | MED. Empty reads as \"no dead code\".\n16. brain_trace_path | `{found:false,path:[]}` | N | `semantic_graph.go:735` (`result.Found`) | MED. Reads as \"no path exists\"; depth defaults to 4, which silently limits it. `found:false` is explicit but says nothing about depth or unindexed symbols.\n17. brain_get_code_snippet | error \"source snippet unavailable for X\" | n/a (error, not empty) | `semantic_graph.go:~905` | LOW\n18. brain_get_graph_schema / brain_get_architecture | counts and metadata | N | `semantic_graph.go` | LOW. Counts of 0 are self-describing. Unverified in detail.\n19. brain_regressions | `{anomalies:[],scanned_files:N,warnings?}` | N (equivalent: `warnings` + `scanned_files`) | `regression.go:1173`, `:392`, `:445` | LOW-MED. Warnings are explicit: \"no code identifiers found in query\", \"history holds no precise code assertions for these identifiers\", \"history scan unavailable\". There is no warning for a missing brain or session history: unverified.\n20. brain_review | same as brain_regressions | N (`warnings`) | `regression.go:1388`, `:1414` | LOW-MED\n21. brain_workspace_regressions | aggregated by repo, with `skipped` repos reported | partial | `workspace.go:3680` | LOW-MED. Exact JSON shape unverified.\n22. brain_workspace_review | same as brain_workspace_regressions | partial | `workspace.go:3806` | LOW-MED\n23. brain_workspace_graph | `skipped` members reported (`workspace.go:1018`) | partial | `workspace.go:1010` | LOW\n24. brain_patterns | `[]` | N | `patterns_cmd.go:124` | HIGH. JSON mode returns a bare `[]` (`writeJSON(cmd, filtered)`). Only text mode separates \"not built (run `entire brain patterns refresh`)\" from \"none detected yet\".\n25. brain_patterns_status | `{present:false,…}` | Y, `present` flag | `patterns_cmd.go:551` | LOW\n26. brain_status / brain_index_status | status report with `sources`, `semantic.blind_spots` and freshness | Y | `agent_surface.go:1104` | LOW. This is the preflight tool; it is not empty-prone.\n27. brain_brief | packet with `blind_spot` records from semantic (`brain_brief_compact.go:171`) | partial | n/a | MED. The shape of a brief with nothing found, and whether it carries the facts or branch note, is unverified.\n28. brain_list_projects | `{projects:[]}` | N | `mcp.go:~1770` | LOW-MED. Cross-repo scope is refused with an explicit error (`mcp.go:1712`, `mcpCrossRepoRefusal`) when the repo is unresolved, but a legitimately empty list is bare.\n29. brain_index_repository, brain_refresh, brain_delete_project, brain_remember, brain_ingest_traces | write or action tools | n/a | n/a | n/a\n\n**BARE EMPTIES (the false-negative set)**\n- brain_query_graph: `{symbols:[],relations:[]}`, no freshness and no note. HIGH.\n- brain_patterns JSON: a bare `[]`. The \"not built\" vs \"none\" distinction exists only in text mode. HIGH.\n- brain_dead_code: `{symbols:[]}`, no freshness. MED.\n- brain_get / brain_multi_get JSON `missing`: no integrity or branch note in JSON. The text path has one, and only for a lossy store. MED.\n- brain_impact, brain_tests, brain_boundaries, brain_trace_path: empty arrays or `found:false` with `freshness` only (trace_path has none). Nothing says \"unindexed or unresolved is not the same as none\". MED.\n- brain_code, brain_search_code, brain_search_graph, brain_context: `freshness` only. LOW-MED.\n- brain_list_projects: `{projects:[]}`. LOW-MED.\n\n**Known traps**\n- **Branch scoping:** `branch` is echoed in the result JSON of query, search, vsearch and get (`retrieve_cmd.go:264`, `:760`; `retrieval_transport.go:307`). No `blind_spot` text anywhere explains that facts are branch-scoped, so recall on the wrong branch returns the generic \"distillation coverage unknown\" note. Unverified for brain_brief.\n- **Entity history backfill:** the RESULT does say so, via `note` (`entities_cmd.go:357`). It is the only tool that does.\n- **Embedder / brain_cgo missing:** no empty-result explanation found in `retrieve_cmd.go` or `retrieval_transport.go`. vsearch on conversation errors, so it is not a silent empty. For the other sources: unverified.\n- **Conversation source experimental and off by default:** I found only the flag help text (`retrieve_cmd.go:128`). I could not find a runtime message for a disabled source: unverified.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>105505</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>23</tool_uses><duration_ms>92582</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
