_render.go:268, status_render.go:~560). Label map `setupComponentLabels` (setup.go:93) is used only for failure lines, so the same component has two names in one run.\n- `repo ... (&lt;RepoKey&gt;)` (setup_render.go:145) and `locate brain: &lt;key&gt;` (refresh.go:168).\n- Hashed daemon label `io.entire.brain-watch.1a2b3c4d` (setup.go:913, 890; setup_render.go:179).\n- `refresh:` stage names (`reclassify facts`, `pattern layer`, `branch overlays`, `history vectors`, `conversation vectors`) and counts (`412 embedded, 17 pruned (3050 total)`, `40781 symbols, 131529 relations`).\n- Messages `skipped` appended to non-skips (`fact backfill will SPEND TOKENS now ... skipped`; `daemon already running ... skipped`).\n\nCut (3 bullets)\n- Setup: delete nested refresh stderr lines and the `setup: instant core: &lt;x&gt;` / `ready in` / backfill-begin / workspace / daemon begin/done lines (~35-45 of ~65). Keep one preflight/consent line, any failure+hint, the SPEND TOKENS line, the summary, Next. Pass `io.Discard` as the nested refresh's stderr/stdout (setup.go:1254-1257) when not `--json`, and drop its `refreshed brain:` line.\n- Summary: remove `instant` tick row, `repo (key)`, `brain` path (keep one), per-row timings, coverage line, duplicate persistent-service text; show facts + daemon + Next only. Use user labels (`setupComponentLabel`) wherever a component appears.\n- Refresh: default `statusAfter` false (refresh.go:108); print one `refreshed brain` line (+ degraded/warn) and collapse the per-stage pairs to skipped/done only when slow or failed; if status stays, drop the `Brain`/identity/instant/coverage lines.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>124495</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>19</tool_uses><duration_ms>108796</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>","reason":"absorbed_mid_turn","commandUuid":"adbb1c58-c839-4008-bdb8-de4e86fabafd","deliveryId":"c3e80635-d035-4ec5-b664-41a3d1feaf30"}
{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-06T22:30:20.961Z","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a9171ae15c9bbdc26</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01BSV4wZSwLwaRxewZteA6xt</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2/tasks/a9171ae15c9bbdc26.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Trace empty-brain first query\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Findings. Caveman-compressed.\n\n## 1. `brain query \"...\"` (also `search`, `vsearch` — all one code path)\n\n| # | user sees | file:line | explains WHY? |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1.1 | `no results for \"&lt;q&gt;\"` | `/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain/internal/cli/retrieve_cmd.go:283` (single-concept text) | no |\n| 1.2 | same string, multi-concept/bounded path | `/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain/internal/cli/retrieval_transport.go:455` | no |\n| 1.3 | JSON: `\"blind_spot\": \"&lt;note&gt;\"` | `/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain/internal/cli/retrieve_cmd.go:264-266`, `:356` | yes-ish |\n| 1.4 | text: note printed on line after \"no results\" | `/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain/internal/cli/retrieve_cmd.go:284-286` | yes-ish |\n| 1.5 | note for brand-new built brain, facts source NOT yet declared (0 distills): `note: the brain has no distilled facts; run \\`entire brain refresh\\`, then \\`distill\\`` | `/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain/internal/cli/blind_spot.go:66` | PARTIAL — says no facts, does NOT say 0 sessions captured, does NOT say sessions source is empty |\n| 1.6 | note if sessions declared &gt;0 but never distilled: `note: N captured session(s) have never been distilled; run \\`entire brain distill\\`` | `/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain/internal/cli/blind_spot.go:64` | yes |\n| 1.7 | note if NO manifest at all: `note: no brain has been built for this repository, so nothing is indexed here and this empty result is not evidence of absence; run \\`entire brain setup\\`` | `/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain/internal/cli/blind_spot.go:98` | yes — best message in codebase |\n| 1.8 | note if manifest unreadable: `note: this repository's brain could not be read, so this empty result is not evidence of absence; run \\`entire brain status\\`` | `/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain/internal/cli/blind_spot.go:96` | yes |\n| 1.9 | note if fact store lossy: `note: this empty result is NOT evidence of absence — &lt;integrity warning&gt;` | `/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain/internal/cli/blind_spot.go:59` | yes |\n\nThere IS an \"empty brain, here is why\" layer (`blind_spot.go`), always non-empty, always appended on 0 results. It is a 1-line `note:` only — no \"here is what to do to populate it beyond distill/refresh/setup\".\n\n## 2. MISLEADING string on empty corpus (answer to your item 5)\n\n| # | user sees | file:line | explains WHY? |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 2.1 | `note: facts last distilled &lt;date&gt; and all captured sessions are distilled — the answer may genuinely not be in the brain` | `/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain/internal/cli/blind_spot.go:71` | NO — actively WRONG on empty corpus |\n\nTrigger condition: `distillCoverage` returns `ok=true` whenever `manifest.Sources.Facts != nil` (`/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain/internal/cli/blind_spot.go:18-31`). It never checks `source.Facts == 0` and never checks `len(Sessions.Sessions) == 0`. So a brain where distill ran once over ZERO sessions (facts source written with 0 facts, 0 sessions) gets \"all captured sessions are distilled — the answer may genuinely not be in the brain\". That is the exact sentence the file's own comment at `blind_spot.go:51-54` calls \"the most damaging thing this tool can say\", and the guard they wrote only covers lossy stores, not empty ones.\n\nNo \"corpus exhausted\" / \"no more results\" wording exists anywhere in `internal/cli/`. Only truncation wording: `response_truncated` at `/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain/internal/cli/retrieval_transport.go:309`, `:691`, and `abstract previews truncated` at `:487`.\n\n## 3. `brain overview` on empty-but-built brain\n\n| # | user sees | file:line | explains WHY? |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 3.1 | `repo: &lt;root&gt; (&lt;key&gt;)` | `/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain/internal/cli/agent_surface.go:612` | n/a |\n| 3.2 | `freshness: unknown (no semantic index to check)` | `/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain/internal/cli/agent_surface.go:617` | yes (semantic only) |\n| 3.3 | `semantic: 0 files, 0 symbols, 0 relations` | `/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain/internal/cli/agent_surface.go:623` | NO — bare zeros |\n| 3.4 | boundaries/commands/entrypoints/documents/recent decisions/patterns/consolidations/themes sections: SILENTLY OMITTED, each gated on `len(...) &gt; 0` | `agent_surface.go:624,626,643,646,649,659,665,671` | NO — section vanishes, zero text |\n| 3.5 | `warnings:` + `brain not built yet — run \\`entire brain refresh\\`; every count in this report is absence of data, not absence of findings` | `/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain/internal/cli/agent_surface.go:500` (guard), printed at `:678-683` | yes — BUT only fires when `!anySource(...) &amp;&amp; manifest.GeneratedAt.IsZero()` |\n\n3.5 is the gap: a brain that was *just built* has a manifest with `GeneratedAt` set and at least seed/semantic sources, so `anySource` is true → this warning does NOT fire. A freshly-built zero-session brain prints `semantic: N files...` + nothing else, with ZERO explanation that history/facts/docs are empty. `anySource` at `/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain/internal/cli/dash.go:663-665`. Text renderer never prints `report.Sources` at all (JSON-only field).\n\n## 4. `brain brief \"&lt;task&gt;\"` on empty brain\n\n| # | user sees | file:line | explains WHY? |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 4.1 | `task: &lt;task&gt;` | `/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain/internal/cli/agent_surface.go:1854` | n/a |\n| 4.2 | `freshness: &lt;sev&gt;` (omitted if empty) | `:1855-1857` | no |\n| 4.3 | `live: dirty=false changed_files=0` | `:1858` | n/a |\n| 4.4 | every section (`edit_file`/`test_file`/`file`/`symbol`/`runtime_trace`/`test`/`history`/`fact`/`action`/`consolidation`/`theme`/`conversation`) is a bare `for` loop → emits NOTHING, no header, no placeholder | `:1859-1925` | NO |\n| 4.5 | `warning: semantic index missing; run \\`entire brain refresh\\`` | `/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain/internal/cli/agent_surface.go:1470` | yes — only if semantic source nil |\n| 4.6 | `warning: history index missing; run \\`entire brain refresh\\`` | `/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain/internal/cli/agent_surface.go:1611` | yes — BUT gated at `:1610` on `Sources.Sessions != nil` |\n\n4.6 is the critical gap. Guard: `} else if status.Manifest != nil &amp;&amp; status.Manifest.Sources != nil &amp;&amp; status.Manifest.Sources.Sessions != nil {` at `agent_surface.go:1610`. Zero captured sessions → sessions source nil → NO warning at all. And if the history source exists with 0 records, the `if` branch is taken, produces 0 matches, and appends no warning either. Facts: gated on `status.Sources.Facts` at `:1613`; false on an undistilled brain → silently skipped, no warning.\n\nNet: `brain brief \"anything\"` on a freshly-built zero-session brain prints 3 lines (`task:`, `live:`, maybe `freshness:`) and NOTHING ELSE. It does NOT say why. `brief` has no equivalent of `blind_spot.go` — the choke point is never called from the brief path (`emptyResultBlindSpot` callers are only `facts_read_cmd.go:375,393` and `retrieve_cmd.go:264,284,356`).\n\n## 5. `brain recall` empty text\n\n| # | user sees | file:line | explains WHY? |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 5.1 | `no facts for \"&lt;q&gt;\" on &lt;branch&gt;` | `/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain/internal/cli/facts_read_cmd.go:389` | no |\n| 5.2 | `warning: &lt;storeWarning&gt;` when store declared-vs-actual mismatch | `:390-392` | yes |\n| 5.3 | blind-spot note, SUPPRESSED when `storeWarning != \"\"` | `:393-395` (text), `:375-377` (JSON) | inherits §1.5-1.9 |\n\n## 6. MISSING vs BUILT-BUT-EMPTY — where the code draws (and fails to draw) the line\n\n| # | mechanism | file:line | verdict |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 6.1 | `declaredIndexDefect.Warning()` — explicitly separates absent-file from unreadable-file: `\"&lt;label&gt; is declared in the manifest but &lt;path&gt; is not on disk — run \\`entire brain refresh\\`\"` vs `\"&lt;label&gt; declared in the manifest cannot be read: &lt;err&gt; — ...\"` | `/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain/internal/cli/declared_indexes.go:92-96` | DECLARED-vs-ON-DISK only. Says nothing about record COUNT. |\n| 6.2 | design rule: \"A source the manifest does not declare is healthy, full stop. That is what keeps a brand-new brain reading as 'not built' instead of 'corrupt'\" | `/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain/internal/cli/declared_indexes.go:36-37` | undeclared == healthy == silent. Brand-new brain is therefore SILENT, not explained. |\n| 6.3 | `inspectDeclaredIndex` returns healthy `declaredIndexDefect{}` for undeclared source | `/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain/internal/cli/declared_indexes.go:140-142` | silent |\n| 6.4 | `inspectFactStore` returns zero-value (healthy) on `source == nil` | `/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain/internal/cli/facts_integrity.go:262-264` | silent |\n| 6.5 | `distillCoverage` ok=false iff facts source nil — count never consulted | `/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain/internal/cli/blind_spot.go:18-21` | ROOT CAUSE of §2.1 |\n| 6.6 | component state: `present[name]` → `\"built\"` purely from `sources.X != nil`; never from a count | `/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain/internal/cli/setup_status.go:185-189`, `:222` | 0-record source renders as `+ built` on the instant line (`status_render.go:589`) |\n| 6.7 | `errHistorySessionsRootMissing` — the one place an absent `sessions/` root is distinguished from a degraded walk: \"An absent sessions/ ROOT is an empty Brain, not a degraded inventory.\" | `/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain/internal/cli/history_input.go:143-151` | distinction exists internally, never reaches query/brief/overview output |\n| 6.8 | `sessionSourceFingerprintAbsent = \"absent\"` — provable \"this brain has no sessions\" fingerprint | `/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain/internal/cli/history.go:1705-1717` | exists, not surfaced in any empty-result text |\n| 6.9 | ONLY user-facing string in the repo that names an empty-but-built corpus: `facts: 0/0 sessions distilled (no captured sessions yet)` | `/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain/internal/cli/setup_status.go:339` + `:343-344` | yes — but lives ONLY in `status`'s Onboarding block, not in query/brief/overview/recall |\n\n## 7. Bottom line for a brand-new user\n\n1. `brain query \"x\"` → `no results for \"x\"` + one `note:` line. Best-case explains. Worst-case (facts source written over 0 sessions) tells them \"the answer may genuinely not be in the brain\" — a lie. `blind_spot.go:71`.\n2. `brain overview` → `repo:`, `freshness:`, `semantic: N files...`. No mention that facts/history/docs are empty. The \"brain not built yet\" warning at `agent_surface.go:500` cannot fire on a built brain.\n3. `brain brief \"x\"` → 3 lines, total silence about why. No blind-spot machinery wired in. `agent_surface.go:1610` gates the one applicable warning behind a sessions source that does not exist on a zero-session brain.\n4. `brain recall \"x\"` → `no facts for \"x\" on main` + same note as query.\n5. The only honest empty-corpus sentence in the product (`no captured sessions yet`) is stranded in `entire brain status`.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>94357</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>50</tool_uses><duration_ms>267374</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"remove","timestamp":"2026-10-06T22:30:32.348Z","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a9171ae15c9bbdc26</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01BSV4wZSwLwaRxewZteA6xt</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2/tasks/a9171ae15c9bbdc26.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Trace empty-brain first query\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Findings. Caveman-compressed.\n\n## 1. `brain query \"...\"` (also `search`, `vsearch` — all one code path)\n\n| # | user sees | file:line | explains WHY? |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1.1 | `no results for \"&lt;q&gt;\"` | `/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain/internal/cli/retrieve_cmd.go:283` (single-concept text) | no |\n| 1.2 | same string, multi-concept/bounded path | `/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain/internal/cli/retrieval_transport.go:455` | no |\n| 1.3 | JSON: `\"blind_spot\": \"&lt;note&gt;\"` | `/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain/internal/cli/retrieve_cmd.go:264-266`, `:356` | yes-ish |\n| 1.4 | text: note printed on line after \"no results\" | `/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain/internal/cli/retrieve_cmd.go:284-286` | yes-ish |\n| 1.5 | note for brand-new built brain, facts source NOT yet declared (0 distills): `note: the brain has no distilled facts; run \\`entire brain refresh\\`, then \\`distill\\`` | `/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain/internal/cli/blind_spot.go:66` | PARTIAL — says no facts, does NOT say 0 sessions captured, does NOT say sessions source is empty |\n| 1.6 | note if sessions declared &gt;0 but never distilled: `note: N captured session(s) have never been distilled; run \\`entire brain distill\\`` | `/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain/internal/cli/blind_spot.go:64` | yes |\n| 1.7 | note if NO manifest at all: `note: no brain has been built for this repository, so nothing is indexed here and this empty result is not evidence of absence; run \\`entire brain setup\\`` | `/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain/internal/cli/blind_spot.go:98` | yes — best message in codebase |\n| 1.8 | note if manifest unreadable: `note: this repository's brain could not be read, so this empty result is not evidence of absence; run \\`entire brain status\\`` | `/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain/internal/cli/blind_spot.go:96` | yes |\n| 1.9 | note if fact store lossy: `note: this empty result is NOT evidence of absence — &lt;integrity warning&gt;` | `/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain/internal/cli/blind_spot.go:59` | yes |\n\nThere IS an \"empty brain, here is why\" layer (`blind_spot.go`), always non-empty, always appended on 0 results. It is a 1-line `note:` only — no \"here is what to do to populate it beyond distill/refresh/setup\".\n\n## 2. MISLEADING string on empty corpus (answer to your item 5)\n\n| # | user sees | file:line | explains WHY? |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 2.1 | `note: facts last distilled &lt;date&gt; and all captured sessions are distilled — the answer may genuinely not be in the brain` | `/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain/internal/cli/blind_spot.go:71` | NO — actively WRONG on empty corpus |\n\nTrigger condition: `distillCoverage` returns `ok=true` whenever `manifest.Sources.Facts != nil` (`/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain/internal/cli/blind_spot.go:18-31`). It never checks `source.Facts == 0` and never checks `len(Sessions.Sessions) == 0`. So a brain where distill ran once over ZERO sessions (facts source written with 0 facts, 0 sessions) gets \"all captured sessions are distilled — the answer may genuinely not be in the brain\". That is the exact sentence the file's own comment at `blind_spot.go:51-54` calls \"the most damaging thing this tool can say\", and the guard they wrote only covers lossy stores, not empty ones.\n\nNo \"corpus exhausted\" / \"no more results\" wording exists anywhere in `internal/cli/`. Only truncation wording: `response_truncated` at `/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain/internal/cli/retrieval_transport.go:309`, `:691`, and `abstract previews truncated` at `:487`.\n\n## 3. `brain overview` on empty-but-built brain\n\n| # | user sees | file:line | explains WHY? |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 3.1 | `repo: &lt;root&gt; (&lt;key&gt;)` | `/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain/internal/cli/agent_surface.go:612` | n/a |\n| 3.2 | `freshness: unknown (no semantic index to check)` | `/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain/internal/cli/agent_surface.go:617` | yes (semantic only) |\n| 3.3 | `semantic: 0 files, 0 symbols, 0 relations` | `/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain/internal/cli/agent_surface.go:623` | NO — bare zeros |\n| 3.4 | boundaries/commands/entrypoints/documents/recent decisions/patterns/consolidations/themes sections: SILENTLY OMITTED, each gated on `len(...) &gt; 0` | `agent_surface.go:624,626,643,646,649,659,665,671` | NO — section vanishes, zero text |\n| 3.5 | `warnings:` + `brain not built yet — run \\`entire brain refresh\\`; every count in this report is absence of data, not absence of findings` | `/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain/internal/cli/agent_surface.go:500` (guard), printed at `:678-683` | yes — BUT only fires when `!anySource(...) &amp;&amp; manifest.GeneratedAt.IsZero()` |\n\n3.5 is the gap: a brain that was *just built* has a manifest with `GeneratedAt` set and at least seed/semantic sources, so `anySource` is true → this warning does NOT fire. A freshly-built zero-session brain prints `semantic: N files...` + nothing else, with ZERO explanation that history/facts/docs are empty. `anySource` at `/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain/internal/cli/dash.go:663-665`. Text renderer never prints `report.Sources` at all (JSON-only field).\n\n## 4. `brain brief \"&lt;task&gt;\"` on empty brain\n\n| # | user sees | file:line | explains WHY? |\n|---|---|--