{"parentUuid":"342e66a7-1add-4929-8dd7-2fcc75abffc3","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfmmwNgAEk4Nvo4KZTJtu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both decisions logged. Writing the plan — the deliverable here is the *system* (list + loop + fresh-env proof), which the audit rows then populate:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2076,"cache_read_input_tokens":828408,"output_tokens":4717,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1408},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2076},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4717,"cache_read_input_tokens":828408,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2076,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2076,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"0787f168-5882-49df-aa96-b624e3b4fd32","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfmmwNGr3G2wCBXCsDTPj","type":"assistant","uuid":"afb4b226-dad7-496f-b88f-4a156abfc714","timestamp":"2026-10-06T22:31:13.716Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.292","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"afb4b226-dad7-496f-b88f-4a156abfc714","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfmmwNgAEk4Nvo4KZTJtu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KMc7xMcWBtLj2WN8USUYwA","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/dynamic-petting-globe.md","content":"# Make brain solid for a first-time external user — a tracked, verified loop\n\n## Context\n\nTwo complaints from a real early user, both reproduced in source and live:\n\n> *\"the brain install is really picky about there not being **ANY** changes in any files in git …\n> it's not the easiest to figure that out, could be me 😅\"*\n\n> *\"the brain facts import defaults to Codex, idk what model.\"*\n\nThen, today, a live first run on a real research repo ended:\n\n```\nBrain ready (degraded) in 7.7s\n  ✗ seed baseline: dirty_worktree: refusing to seed uncommitted content without --worktree\n  ✗ semantic index: dirty_worktree: refusing to index uncommitted content without --worktree\n  hint: commit or stash the working tree … `entire enable` writes .entire/ and .claude/\n        without committing them, which is what a first run usually trips over\n```\n\n**The hint was wrong.** That repo's dirt was ~250 real staged files — notebooks, models, figures,\nresults. `.entire/`, `AGENTS.md` and `CLAUDE.md` were not in `git status` at all. Re-running\n`setup` produced the identical result, and `setup` exposes no `--worktree` escape, so a user\nmid-work is permanently degraded and told to do something irrelevant to their problem.\n\n**Target user: someone outside the team installing fresh.** The bar is that they get a working\nbrain their agent actually uses, without reading source.\n\n**This is a standing loop, not a one-off PR.** Fix everything, keep a live list, verify each fix,\nand re-verify old ones later — in fresh sessions — so regressions surface instead of accumulating.\n\n---\n\n## The system (the real deliverable)\n\n### 1. A committed backlog — `docs/install-ux-backlog.md`\n\nOne row per defect, in the entire-brain repo so the team sees it and a fix PR can tick its own row:\n\n| field | meaning |\n|---|---|\n| `id` | stable (`UX-07`), referenced by commits and tests |\n| `severity` | blocker / major / minor, judged by *first-run* impact |\n| `symptom` | what the user sees, in their words — not the internal cause |\n| `anchor` | `file:line` |\n| `fix` | one line |\n| `status` | `open` → `fixed` → `verified` → (`regressed`) |\n| `check` | the exact command that proves it, re-runnable by anyone |\n| `last_verified` | date + how (weakening / fresh-env / both) |\n\n`symptom` is phrased from the outside on purpose: a list written in internal vocabulary\n(`memory_overlay`, `dirty_worktree`) re-creates the very problem we are fixing.\n\n### 2. The loop\n\nPick highest-severity `open` → fix → **weakening-verify** → **fresh-env verify** → set `verified`\nwith date and command. One PR per small batch; brain's constraint is review throughput, not\nauthorship (13 merged last week while 6 finished PRs queued), so batches stay reviewable.\n\n### 3. Fresh-env harness — `scripts/freshenv-check.sh`, committed\n\nEach check runs in a throwaway git repo with its own `XDG_DATA_HOME`/config, so no existing brain,\nplugin registry or cache leaks in. Committed so any session or subagent can run it unchanged.\n\n**Stated limit, up front:** this cannot catch \"the install instructions are wrong\", because the\nbinaries are already on the machine. Install-step defects need a real cold start and are marked\n`unverifiable-here` rather than silently passed. A harness that cannot fail the case it is\npointed at reports success — that failure mode has already bitten this work three times today.\n\n### 4. Regression sweep\n\nPeriodically, in a **fresh session**, a subagent re-runs the whole harness and flips any failing\nrow to `regressed`. Fresh matters: a session that made a fix is the worst judge of whether it\nholds.\n\n---\n\n## Verification bar (per row, no exceptions)\n\n1. **A test that fails on a compile-clean revert**, with the failing assertion quoted. Not an extra\n   step — CONTRIBUTING.md item 3 already requires it, and the PR must carry the red output.\n2. **A fresh-env check** that reproduces the user-visible symptom and shows it gone.\n3. **A negative control** wherever the fix could over-apply. The dirty-gate fix is the archetype:\n   without \"a dirty *source* file is still refused\", a passing check is indistinguishable from\n   having switched the safety off.\n4. If a weakening produces **zero** failures, suspect the test first and grep to confirm the edit\n   applied. Two \"unholdable guards\" today were missing fixtures, not missing bugs.\n\n---\n\n## Rows already established (seed the backlog with these)\n\n**Blockers — a first-run user is stuck**\n- `setup` has no `--worktree` escape; a user with legitimate WIP is degraded forever with no\n  forward path from inside `setup`.\n- The dirty-tree hint is wrong whenever the dirt is not Entire's own files — the live case above.\n- Entire's own installers (`init-agents`, `entire enable`) write files that then block the install.\n  **Fix built and verified: branch `fix/install-ux-dirty-gate-and-agent-default` @ `3cc936ad`.**\n\n**Major — silent wrong behaviour**\n- Agent default silently picks codex over the harness the user is in, and never says which. *Fixed\n  on the same branch.*\n- The model is never named — *\"idk what model\"* stays literally true. *Fixed on the same branch\n  by stating it, without hardcoding an id that ages.*\n- `daemonEnv` carries no harness signal, so the unattended daemon still resolves codex-first.\n- Facts are branch-scoped: `recall` on `main` reads empty while the facts sit on another branch.\n- Six CLI verbs have no MCP tool — `recall`, `verify`, `overview`, `entities`, `show`, `guide`.\n  `recall` is the worst: the shipped guide *mandates* it and an MCP-only agent cannot call it.\n- The shipped guide says *\"No MCP tool writes a fact\"* while the same build registers\n  `brain_remember`.\n\n**Major — the product talks to itself, not the user**\n- `doctor` prints 35 lines, mostly internal schema names, returning 5 warn + 1 error on a brain\n  that works. A diagnostic that cries wolf on a healthy system trains people to ignore it.\n- 43 top-level verbs, including **seven** ways to ask a question (`query`, `search`, `vsearch`,\n  `get`, `multi-get`, `show`, `recall`).\n- `setup` 12 flags, `distill` 15.\n- `init-agents` — the step that makes an agent use brain at all — is absent from the setup flow\n  and from Overview → Set Up Your Repository.\n\nThree audits (first-run flow, agent usage, surface simplification) are running and will append\ntheir findings with `file:line` and severity. The list above is the floor, not the total.\n\n---\n\n## First increment\n\nThe branch is **already built and verified**: 24 weakenings all red-then-green, indexing filter\nuntouched, and a live before/after on a real repo —\n\n```\nBEFORE  exit=1  seed baseline failed / dirty_worktree\nAFTER   exit=0  seed baseline done · semantic index: 2 symbols, 2 relations, 2 files\nCONTROL dirty source file → still refused\n```\n\n**It needs a rebase before it ships.** It sits on `6c8ebdab` while #318, #320, #331, #332 and #334\nhave merged since — and #332 touched the same guide and hook code. **Blocked on `git fetch`**,\nwhich needs working DNS (see below).\n\n## Files\n\n| path | change |\n|---|---|\n| `docs/install-ux-backlog.md` | new — the live list |\n| `scripts/freshenv-check.sh` | new — throwaway repo + isolated dirs, one check per row |\n| `internal/cli/semantic.go`, `seed.go`, `refresh.go`, `setup.go`, `watch.go`, `distill_cmd.go` | the fixes, in small batches |\n| `internal/cli/mcp.go` | MCP parity for the missing verbs |\n| `internal/cli/doctor*.go` | user-facing subset; internals behind `--verbose` |\n\n## Verification\n\n1. `scripts/freshenv-check.sh` green for every `verified` row.\n2. Each fix's weakening evidence quoted in its PR.\n3. A fresh-session regression sweep re-runs the harness and flips failures to `regressed`.\n4. The end-to-end that matters: a throwaway repo → `entire graph init-agents` →\n   `entire brain setup` → first `brain query` returns something useful, with **no** degraded\n   components and **no** advice that does not apply.\n\n## Known blocker, stated plainly\n\n`opendirectoryd` is unreachable from this process tree: no DNS, no keychain, `whoami` → `501`.\nSo `git fetch`, `gh` and the trail CLI all fail, and the rebase cannot happen from here. Disabling\nthe Claude Code sandbox did **not** fix it, which ruled out the sandbox as the cause. Everything\nelse in this plan proceeds offline; the rebase waits for a shell with a working bootstrap context.\n\n## Not doing\n\nMerging, approving or pushing without explicit approval. No model id hardcoded — `setup.go` already\nrecords why (\"model ids age badly\"), and that reasoning stands.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2076,"cache_read_input_tokens":828408,"output_tokens":4717,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1408},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2076},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4717,"cache_read_input_tokens":828408,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2076,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2076,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01KMc7xMcWBtLj2WN8USUYwA":{"file_path":"/Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/dynamic-petting-globe.md","content":"# Make brain solid for