no** advice that does not apply.\n\n## Known blocker, stated plainly\n\n`opendirectoryd` is unreachable from this process tree: no DNS, no keychain, `whoami` → `501`.\nSo `git fetch`, `gh` and the trail CLI all fail, and the rebase cannot happen from here. Disabling\nthe Claude Code sandbox did **not** fix it, which ruled out the sandbox as the cause. Everything\nelse in this plan proceeds offline; the rebase waits for a shell with a working bootstrap context.\n\n## Not doing\n\nMerging, approving or pushing without explicit approval. No model id hardcoded — `setup.go` already\nrecords why (\"model ids age badly\"), and that reasoning stands.\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"0787f168-5882-49df-aa96-b624e3b4fd32","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CfmmwNGr3G2wCBXCsDTPj","type":"assistant","uuid":"8ab873a3-dd59-4820-a1bd-93554e7ea424","timestamp":"2026-10-06T22:31:56.106Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.292","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"8ab873a3-dd59-4820-a1bd-93554e7ea424","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_non_blocking_error","hookName":"PreToolUse:Write","toolUseID":"toolu_01KMc7xMcWBtLj2WN8USUYwA","hookEvent":"PreToolUse","stderr":"Failed with non-blocking status code: --file is required","stdout":"","exitCode":1,"command":"entire brain hook pre-edit","durationMs":47},"type":"attachment","uuid":"097d923e-2cc9-4f69-baf5-836e90ccd715","timestamp":"2026-10-06T22:31:56.179Z","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.292","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"8ab873a3-dd59-4820-a1bd-93554e7ea424","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"3cfdb7de-816c-439b-a19a-fa4c2def69a9","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KMc7xMcWBtLj2WN8USUYwA","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/dynamic-petting-globe.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"a0b56617-c8b9-4de1-b3ee-1d624e557678","timestamp":"2026-10-06T22:31:56.196Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"update","filePath":"/Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/dynamic-petting-globe.md","content":"# Make brain solid for a first-time external user — a tracked, verified loop\n\n## Context\n\nTwo complaints from a real early user, both reproduced in source and live:\n\n> *\"the brain install is really picky about there not being **ANY** changes in any files in git …\n> it's not the easiest to figure that out, could be me 😅\"*\n\n> *\"the brain facts import defaults to Codex, idk what model.\"*\n\nThen, today, a live first run on a real research repo ended:\n\n```\nBrain ready (degraded) in 7.7s\n  ✗ seed baseline: dirty_worktree: refusing to seed uncommitted content without --worktree\n  ✗ semantic index: dirty_worktree: refusing to index uncommitted content without --worktree\n  hint: commit or stash the working tree … `entire enable` writes .entire/ and .claude/\n        without committing them, which is what a first run usually trips over\n```\n\n**The hint was wrong.** That repo's dirt was ~250 real staged files — notebooks, models, figures,\nresults. `.entire/`, `AGENTS.md` and `CLAUDE.md` were not in `git status` at all. Re-running\n`setup` produced the identical result, and `setup` exposes no `--worktree` escape, so a user\nmid-work is permanently degraded and told to do something irrelevant to their problem.\n\n**Target user: someone outside the team installing fresh.** The bar is that they get a working\nbrain their agent actually uses, without reading source.\n\n**This is a standing loop, not a one-off PR.** Fix everything, keep a live list, verify each fix,\nand re-verify old ones later — in fresh sessions — so regressions surface instead of accumulating.\n\n---\n\n## The system (the real deliverable)\n\n### 1. A committed backlog — `docs/install-ux-backlog.md`\n\nOne row per defect, in the entire-brain repo so the team sees it and a fix PR can tick its own row:\n\n| field | meaning |\n|---|---|\n| `id` | stable (`UX-07`), referenced by commits and tests |\n| `severity` | blocker / major / minor, judged by *first-run* impact |\n| `symptom` | what the user sees, in their words — not the internal cause |\n| `anchor` | `file:line` |\n| `fix` | one line |\n| `status` | `open` → `fixed` → `verified` → (`regressed`) |\n| `check` | the exact command that proves it, re-runnable by anyone |\n| `last_verified` | date + how (weakening / fresh-env / both) |\n\n`symptom` is phrased from the outside on purpose: a list written in internal vocabulary\n(`memory_overlay`, `dirty_worktree`) re-creates the very problem we are fixing.\n\n### 2. The loop\n\nPick highest-severity `open` → fix → **weakening-verify** → **fresh-env verify** → set `verified`\nwith date and command. One PR per small batch; brain's constraint is review throughput, not\nauthorship (13 merged last week while 6 finished PRs queued), so batches stay reviewable.\n\n### 3. Fresh-env harness — `scripts/freshenv-check.sh`, committed\n\nEach check runs in a throwaway git repo with its own `XDG_DATA_HOME`/config, so no existing brain,\nplugin registry or cache leaks in. Committed so any session or subagent can run it unchanged.\n\n**Stated limit, up front:** this cannot catch \"the install instructions are wrong\", because the\nbinaries are already on the machine. Install-step defects need a real cold start and are marked\n`unverifiable-here` rather than silently passed. A harness that cannot fail the case it is\npointed at reports success — that failure mode has already bitten this work three times today.\n\n### 4. Regression sweep\n\nPeriodically, in a **fresh session**, a subagent re-runs the whole harness and flips any failing\nrow to `regressed`. Fresh matters: a session that made a fix is the worst judge of whether it\nholds.\n\n---\n\n## Verification bar (per row, no exceptions)\n\n1. **A test that fails on a compile-clean revert**, with the failing assertion quoted. Not an extra\n   step — CONTRIBUTING.md item 3 already requires it, and the PR must carry the red output.\n2. **A fresh-env check** that reproduces the user-visible symptom and shows it gone.\n3. **A negative control** wherever the fix could over-apply. The dirty-gate fix is the archetype:\n   without \"a dirty *source* file is still refused\", a passing check is indistinguishable from\n   having switched the safety off.\n4. If a weakening produces **zero** failures, suspect the test first and grep to confirm the edit\n   applied. Two \"unholdable guards\" today were missing fixtures, not missing bugs.\n\n---\n\n## Rows already established (seed the backlog with these)\n\n**Blockers — a first-run user is stuck**\n- `setup` has no `--worktree` escape; a user with legitimate WIP is degraded forever with no\n  forward path from inside `setup`.\n- The dirty-tree hint is wrong whenever the dirt is not Entire's own files — the live case above.\n- Entire's own installers (`init-agents`, `entire enable`) write files that then block the install.\n  **Fix built and verified: branch `fix/install-ux-dirty-gate-and-agent-default` @ `3cc936ad`.**\n\n**Major — silent wrong behaviour**\n- Agent default silently picks codex over the harness the user is in, and never says which. *Fixed\n  on the same branch.*\n- The model is never named — *\"idk what model\"* stays literally true. *Fixed on the same branch\n  by stating it, without hardcoding an id that ages.*\n- `daemonEnv` carries no harness signal, so the unattended daemon still resolves codex-first.\n- Facts are branch-scoped: `recall` on `main` reads empty while the facts sit on another branch.\n- Six CLI verbs have no MCP tool — `recall`, `verify`, `overview`, `entities`, `show`, `guide`.\n  `recall` is the worst: the shipped guide *mandates* it and an MCP-only agent cannot call it.\n- The shipped guide says *\"No MCP tool writes a fact\"* while the same build registers\n  `brain_remember`.\n\n**Major — the product talks to itself, not the user**\n- `doctor` prints 35 lines, mostly internal schema names, returning 5 warn + 1 error on a brain\n  that works. A diagnostic that cries wolf on a healthy system trains people to ignore it.\n- 43 top-level verbs, including **seven** ways to ask a question (`query`, `search`, `vsearch`,\n  `get`, `multi-get`, `show`, `recall`).\n- `setup` 12 flags, `distill` 15.\n- `init-agents` — the step that makes an agent use brain at all — is absent from the setup flow\n  and from Overview → Set Up Your Repository.\n\nThree audits (first-run flow, agent usage, surface simplification) are running and will append\ntheir findings with `file:line` and severity. The list above is the floor, not the total.\n\n---\n\n## First increment\n\nThe branch is **already built and verified**: 24 weakenings all red-then-green, indexing filter\nuntouched, and a live before/after on a real repo —\n\n```\nBEFORE  exit=1  seed baseline failed / dirty_worktree\nAFTER   exit=0  seed baseline done · semantic index: 2 symbols, 2 relations, 2 files\nCONTROL dirty source file → still refused\n```\n\n**It needs a rebase before it ships.** It sits on `6c8ebdab` while #318, #320, #331, #332 and #334\nhave merged since — and #332 touched the same guide and hook code. **Blocked on `git fetch`**,\nwhich needs working DNS (see below).\n\n## Files\n\n| path | change |\n|---|---|\n| `docs/install-ux-backlog.md` | new — the live list |\n| `scripts/freshenv-check.sh` | new — throwaway repo + isolated dirs, one check per row |\n| `internal/cli/semantic.go`, `seed.go`, `refresh.go`, `setup.go`, `watch.go`, `distill_cmd.go` | the fixes, in small batches |\n| `internal/cli/mcp.go` | MCP parity for the missing verbs |\n| `internal/cli/doctor*.go` | user-facing subset; internals behind `--verbose` |\n\n## Verification\n\n1. `scripts/freshenv-check.sh` green for every `verified` row.\n2. Each fix's weakening evidence quoted in its PR.\n3. A fresh-session regression sweep re-runs the harness and flips failures to `regressed`.\n4. The end-to-end that matters: a throwaway repo → `entire graph init-agents` →\n   `entire brain setup` → first `brain query` returns something useful, with **no** degraded\n   components and **no** advice that does not apply.\n\n## Known blocker, stated plainly\n\n`opendirectoryd` is unreachable from this process tree: no DNS, no keychain, `whoami` → `501`.\nSo `git fetch`, `gh` and the trail CLI all fail, and the rebase cannot happen from here. Disabling\nthe Claude Code sandbox did **not** fix it, which ruled out the sandbox as the cause. Everything\nelse in this plan proceeds offline; the rebase waits for a shell with a working bootstrap context.\n\n## Not doing\n\nMerging, approving or pushing without explicit approval. No model id hardcoded — `setup.go` already\nrecords why (\"model ids age badly\"), and that reasoning stands.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":314,"newStart":1,"newLines":171,"lines":["-# Fix two install-experience defects in entire-brain","+# Make brain solid for a first-time external user — a tracked, verified loop"," "," ## Context"," ","-Early user feedback on brain, both reproduced in source:","+Two complaints from a real early user, both reproduced in source and live:"," ","-> *\"the brain install is really picky about there not being **ANY** changes in any files in git.","-> even the previous config file and agent file updates from the graph extension install.","+> *\"the brain install is really picky about there not being **ANY** changes in any files in git …"," > it's not the easiest to figure that out, could be me 😅\"*"," ","-> *\"the brain facts import defaults to Codex, idk what model. any chance we could default to","-> Sonnet or Opus? Or maybe ask the user for a choice in the cli flow?\"*","+> *\"the brain facts import defaults to Codex, idk what model.\"*"," ","-They are two unrelated defects that both land on a first-time user:","+Then, today, a live first run on a real research repo ended:"," ","-**A. Entire's own installers create the dirt that blocks Entire's install.** `init-agents` writes","-`AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `.claude/settings.json`; the next command refuses because the tree is","-dirty. The reporter blamed themselves. It is not them.","+```","+Brain ready (degraded) in 7.7s","+  ✗ seed baseline: dirty_worktree: refusing to seed uncommitted content without --worktree","+  ✗ semantic index: dirty_worktree: refusing to index uncommitted content without --worktree","+  hint: commit or stash the working tree … `entire enable` writes .entire/ and .claude/","+        without committing them, which is what a first run usually trips over","+```"," ","-**B. Fact distillation silently routes repo content to Codex**, even for a user sitting inside","-Claude Code, and never says which agent it chose.","+**The hint was wrong.** That repo's dirt was ~250 real staged files — notebooks, models, figures,","+results. `.entire/`, `AGENTS.md` and `CLAUDE.md` were not in `git status` at all. Re-running","+`setup` produced the identical result, and `setup` exposes no `--worktree` escape, so a user","+mid-work is permanently degraded and told to do something irrelevant to their problem."," ","-Both are on `main`, not just the unmerged stack. Everything below is `file:line` from source,","-established by three exploration passes.","+**Target user: someone outside the team installing fresh.** The bar is that they get a working","+brain their agent actually uses, without reading source."," ","+**This is a standing loop, not a one-off PR.** Fix everything, keep a live list, verify each fix,","+and re-verify old ones later — in fresh sessions — so regressions surface instead of accumulating.","+"," ---"," ","-## Fix A — Entire-authored config must not block the install","+## The system (the real deliverable)"," ","-### What is actually broken","+### 1. A committed backlog — `docs/install-ux-backlog.md`"," ","-`brainIgnore.Ignored` (`internal/cli/semantic.go:2467`) hardcodes a segment list at `:2473`:","-`node_modules, vendor, dist, build, target, .entire`. **`.entire/*` is already exempt.** The gap","-is exactly the three paths outside it: **`AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `.claude/settings.json`**.","+One row per defect, in the entire-brain repo so the team sees it and a fix PR can tick its own row:"," ","-`loadBrainIgnore` (`:2433`) otherwise reads only `.brainignore`, which does not exist in a fresh","-repo — so for a new user the user-pattern set is empty and only the hardcoded list applies.","+| field | meaning |","+|---|---|","+| `id` | stable (`UX-07`), referenced by commits and tests |","+| `severity` | blocker / major / minor, judged by *first-run* impact |","+| `symptom` | what the user sees, in their words — not the internal cause |","+| `anchor` | `file:line` |","+| `fix` | one line |","+| `status` | `open` → `fixed` → `verified` → (`regressed`) |","+| `check` | the exact command that proves it, re-runnable by anyone |","+| `last_verified` | date + how (weakening / fresh-env / both) |"," ","-**There are two refusals, not one.** A dirty install fails both components:","+`symptom` is phrased from the outside on purpose: a list written in internal vocabulary","+(`memory_overlay`, `dirty_worktree`) re-creates the very problem we are fixing."," ","-| refusal | file:line | message |","-|---|---|---|","-| seed | `seed.go:276` | `dirty_worktree: refusing to seed uncommitted content without --worktree` |","-| semantic | `semantic.go:594` | `dirty_worktree: refusing to index uncommitted content without --worktree` |","+### 2. The loop"," ","-Confirmed call chain for `entire brain setup`: `setup.go:659` → `setup.go:1261` →","-`watch.go:647 runRefresh` (with `watch.go:609 watchDeterministicRefreshOptions`, which leaves","-**both** worktree flags false) → `refresh.go:223` → `refresh.go:274` → `refresh_phases.go:30` →","-`seed.go:271`. Semantic arrives via `refresh.go:401` → `:452` → `refresh_phases.go:36`.","+Pick highest-severity `open` → fix → **weakening-verify** → **fresh-env verify** → set `verified`","+with date and command. One PR per small batch; brain's constraint is review throughput, not","+authorship (13 merged last week while 6 finished PRs queued), so batches stay reviewable."," ","-Setup already *recognises* this state — `setupIsDirtyWorktree` (`setup.go:196`), matched at","-`:211`, with a hint at `:133` naming `.entire/` and `.claude/` — but still fails the components.","-The diagnosis exists; the fix does not.","+### 3. Fresh-env harness — `scripts/freshenv-check.sh`, committed"," ","-### Changes","+Each check runs in a throwaway git repo with its own `XDG_DATA_HOME`/config, so no existing brain,","+plugin registry or cache leaks in. Committed so any session or subagent can run it unchanged."," ","-1. **Add a GATE-ONLY ignore — do NOT touch the shared hardcoded list.**","+**Stated limit, up front:** this cannot catch \"the install instructions are wrong\", because the","+binaries are already on the machine. Install-step defects need a real cold start and are marked","+`unverifiable-here` rather than silently passed. A harness that cannot fail the case it is","+pointed at reports success — that failure mode has already bitten this work three times today."," ","-   ⚠️ **The obvious fix is wrong, and this is the most important decision in the plan.**","-   `brainIgnore.Ignored` (`semantic.go:2467`) is **not** the dirty gate — it is the *indexing*","-   filter, used at 17 non-test sites: `filterSemanticSnapshot` (`:1610`, `:1642`), the snapshot","-   stream (`semantic_stream.go:242`, `:244`, `:362`), the file walks (`:3136`, `:3166`, `:5531`,","-   `:5692`, `:5715`), and coverage (`semantic_coverage.go:113`).","+### 4. Regression sweep"," ","-   Adding `AGENTS.md`/`CLAUDE.md` to that list would **remove them from the indexed doc corpus** —","-   a regression disguised as a fix. Brain indexes markdown; `AGENTS.md` and `CLAUDE.md` are exactly","-   the kind of repo doc a user expects it to know about.","+Periodically, in a **fresh session**, a subagent re-runs the whole harness and flips any failing","+row to `regressed`. Fresh matters: a session that made a fix is the worst judge of whether it","+holds."," ","-   **Correct seam:** enrich only the `brainIgnore` *instance* the gate uses. `brainIgnore.patterns`","-   is per-instance and is matched by `brainIgnorePatternMatches` (`:2490`), which is root-anchored","-   and handles exact paths — so `.claude/settings.json` matches as written. Add a","-   `worktreeGateIgnore(repoDir)` helper returning `loadBrainIgnore(repoDir)` with the","-   Entire-authored paths appended to `.patterns`, and use it in `worktreeDirty`","-   (`semantic.go:2924`). Indexing keeps the untouched `loadBrainIgnore`.","+---"," ","-   Paths to add, decided with the user: `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `.claude/settings.json`,","-   `.brainignore`. (`.entire/*` is already exempt via the segment rule — no change needed.","-   `.codex/hooks.json` was **dropped** after review: nothing in this repo writes it — the only","-   hook writer is `MergePreEditHook` → `.claude/settings.json`.)","+## Verification bar (per row, no exceptions)"," ","-   **Why `.patterns` and not the segment list** — this is the whole point of the gate-only seam.","-   `pathHasSegment` does exact *segment* equality, so `.claude/settings.json` entered there would","-   be a silent **no-op** and the reporter's own file would still block; the only spelling that","-   works is bare `.claude`, which would swallow `.claude/` entirely at any depth. `.patterns` goes","-   through `brainIgnorePatternMatches`, which is root-anchored and matches the full path as","-   written. Segment entries would also match at **any** depth (`docs/AGENTS.md`), which","-   `TestBrainIgnoreDoesNotOvermatchDefaultDirectoryPrefixes` exists to prevent.","+1. **A test that fails on a compile-clean revert**, with the failing assertion quoted. Not an extra","+   step — CONTRIBUTING.md item 3 already requires it, and the PR must carry the red output.","+2. **A fresh-env check** that reproduces the user-visible symptom and shows it gone.","+3. **A negative control** wherever the fix could over-apply. The dirty-gate fix is the archetype:","+   without \"a dirty *source* file is still refused\", a passing check is indistinguishable from","+   having switched the safety off.","+4. If a weakening produces **zero** failures, suspect the test first and grep to confirm the edit","+   applied. Two \"unholdable guards\" today were missing fixtures, not missing bugs."," ","-   **Corroboration:** this repo's own `.brainignore` already lists `.claude/settings.json` under","-   *\"Local agent/editor runtime state\"* and deliberately does **not** list `AGENTS.md`/`CLAUDE.md` —","-   maintainers put those two on the indexed side on purpose, and `isHighSignalDoc` (`seed.go`)","-   ranks them top-signal. Gate-only keeps that intact. If an implementation ever makes them stop","-   being indexed, the seam is wrong — stop. A user's own hand-edits to `AGENTS.md`/`CLAUDE.md` also stop","-   blocking the gate, which is correct: they are agent config, not indexed source — and because","-   this is gate-only, they remain **indexed** as before.","+---"," ","-   *Justification:* the gate exists to stop seeding uncommitted **source** into an index attributed","-   to a commit. Config Entire wrote is not source. Indexing it is fine; blocking on it is not.","+## Rows already established (seed the backlog with these)"," ","-2. **Check `worktreeDirty`'s other callers before landing.** It is also used by","-   `verifySemanticWorktreeStable` (`:2941`) and `semanticStaleReport` (`:3329`). The first is a","-   post-index stability check and the second is read-only reporting; both arguably *should* ignore","-   Entire config too, but that must be a decision, not a side effect. Confirm each, and say so.","+**Blockers — a first-run user is stuck**","+- `setup` has no `--worktree` escape; a user with legitimate WIP is degraded forever with no","+  forward path from inside `setup`.","+- The dirty-tree hint is wrong whenever the dirt is not Entire's own files — the live case above.","+- Entire's own installers (`init-agents`, `entire enable`) write files that then block the install.","+  **Fix built and verified: branch `fix/install-ux-dirty-gate-and-agent-default` @ `3cc936ad`.**"," ","-3. **Leave `gitPathspecExclusions` (`semantic.go:2408`) ALONE unless proven safe.** It feeds","-   `git diff` pathspecs for change detection; widening it could make brain miss real edits. Only","-   touch it if the adversarial check shows it is gate-only.","+**Major — silent wrong behaviour**","+- Agent default silently picks codex over the harness the user is in, and never says which. *Fixed","+  on the same branch.*","+- The model is never named — *\"idk what model\"* stays literally true. *Fixed on the same branch","+  by stating it, without hardcoding an id that ages.*","+- `daemonEnv` carries no harness signal, so the unattended daemon still resolves codex-first.","+- Facts are branch-scoped: `recall` on `main` reads empty while the facts sit on another branch.","+- Six CLI verbs have no MCP tool — `recall`, `verify`, `overview`, `entities`, `show`, `guide`.","+  `recall` is the worst: the shipped guide *mandates* it and an MCP-only agent cannot call it.","+- The shipped guide says *\"No MCP tool writes a fact\"* while the same build registers","+  `brain_remember`."," ","-4. **Make both refusals actionable.** Today they name a flag, not an intent, and never say which","-   files. Include the count and first few offending paths, and state the remedy in plain words:","-   pass `--worktree` to index uncommitted work, or commit/stash first. Apply to `seed.go:276` and","-   `semantic.go:594` together — a user who clears one hits the other.","+**Major — the product talks to itself, not the user**","+- `doctor` prints 35 lines, mostly internal schema names, returning 5 warn + 1 error on a brain","+  that works. A diagnostic that cries wolf on a healthy system trains people to ignore it.","+- 43 top-level verbs, including **seven** ways to ask a question (`query`, `search`, `vsearch`,","+  `get`, `multi-get`, `show`, `recall`).","+- `setup` 12 flags, `distill` 15.","+- `init-agents` — the step that makes an agent use brain at all — is absent from the setup flow","+  and from Overview → Set Up Your Repository."," ","-### Out of scope, but found and worth recording","+Three audits (first-run flow, agent usage, surface simplification) are running and will append","+their findings with `file:line` and severity. The list above is the floor, not the total."," ","-`worktreeStatusPaths` (`semantic.go:3094`) applies `strings.Cut(path, \" -> \")` to **every** status","-line, not only `R`/`C` rename entries, so a filename literally containing `\" -> \"` splits into two","-bogus paths. Latent, unproven against a live repo. File separately; do not fold in here.","-"," ---"," ","-## Fix B — stop silently choosing another vendor's agent","+## First increment"," ","-### What is actually broken","+The branch is **already built and verified**: 24 weakenings all red-then-green, indexing filter","+untouched, and a live before/after on a real repo —"," ","-`defaultRefreshAgent` — `refresh.go:851` (feature branch), `refresh.go:741` (**main**) — is","-`no-egress → codex → claude-code → none`, hardcoded, with **no announcement anywhere**. 13 call","-sites; the only user-visible mention of the chosen agent is setup's backfill spend label","-(`setup.go:1021`, printed at `:974`). Every other path is silent.","+```","+BEFORE  exit=1  seed baseline failed / dirty_worktree","+AFTER   exit=0  seed baseline done · semantic index: 2 symbols, 2 relations, 2 files","+CONTROL dirty source file → still refused","+```"," ","-The codebase already made this exact call once, for ollama, in the same function:","+**It needs a rebase before it ships.** It sits on `6c8ebdab` while #318, #320, #331, #332 and #334","+have merged since — and #332 touched the same guide and hook code. **Blocked on `git fetch`**,","+which needs working DNS (see below)."," ","-> *choosing one is a product decision, not a default worth guessing* … *the caller warns when it","-> falls through, so a privacy-motivated install does not quietly become a cloud call.*","+## Files"," ","-**Both of those claims are presently false.** `ollamaModelMissingWarning` (`refresh.go:893`) has","-**zero non-test callers** — the privacy guard it promises never fires.","-","-### Changes","-","-**B1 — Detect the harness the user is running under, and prefer it.**","-","-Verified by reading this session's own environment: `CLAUDECODE` and `CLAUDE_CODE_ENTRYPOINT` are","-genuinely set inside Claude Code. That is detection, not guessing.","-","-**No Codex signal is verified.** `CODEX_HOME` (`skill_form.go:114`) is write-destination","-resolution, not detection, and the `CODEX_COMPANION_*` vars present here come from a Claude Code","-plugin, not from Codex. So: detect Claude Code positively; leave Codex to the existing PATH probe","-until a signal is confirmed on a real Codex run. Inventing one would repeat a mistake already in","-memory — a guard written against a key the real CLI never emits.","-","-New order: **detected harness *if its binary is also available* → PATH probe (unchanged order) → none.**","-","-⚠️ **The availability check is not optional.** Returning `claude-code` on env alone would make","-`distill.go` build argv starting with `claude` with no fallback — turning a working codex run into","-a hard exec failure whenever the `claude` binary is absent from the child PATH. Detected-but-","-unavailable must fall through, and a test must pin it: `CLAUDECODE` set, `claude` unavailable,","-codex available → picks codex.","-","-⚠️ **B1 does not reach the watch daemon**, which is the one unattended path that spends tokens on","-a timer. `daemonEnv` builds an *explicit* env map (plugin dirs + PATH only), so `CLAUDECODE` is not","-inherited and the daemon still resolves codex-first. (`setupChildEnv` uses `os.Environ()` and does","-inherit — an inconsistency in its own right.) Either plumb the resolved agent into the daemon env,","-or report it explicitly as a known limitation. Shipping silently would miss the path where the","-defect costs most.","-","-Style precedent for env reads: `agent_policy.go:14-25` (`brainNoEgressMode`, `envBool`). Keep the","-existing name mapping — the function returns `\"claude-code\"` while probing the binary `\"claude\"`.","-","-**B2 — Announce the choice, and wire up the dead warning.**","-","-Print the chosen agent before any token spend, mirroring the documented ordering rule at","-`setup.go:966-972` (the cost line must precede the spend so the user can Ctrl-C). Writer chain is","-`newRefreshProgress(cmd.ErrOrStderr())` (`progress.go:224`), which degrades to prefixed plain","-lines when piped. Suppress under `--json` as `setup.go:1257` already does.","-","-At the same site, call `ollamaModelMissingWarning` — already written and already tested, just","-never invoked. This makes two false source comments true.","-","-**B3 — Keep the signature change contained.**","-","-`defaultRefreshAgent(ctx, runner, repoDir)` has no access to `opts`/`cmd`, and three existing tests","-call it with that 3-arg shape (`refresh_test.go:22`, `refresh_ollama_auto_test.go:34`,","-`local_agent_preference_test.go:63`). Threading a writer through all 13 call sites is invasive and","-would churn the tests.","-","-Instead: **leave the pure function alone**, add a thin wrapper that resolves + announces, and use","-it at the three user-facing sites — `refresh.go:145`, `distill_cmd.go:710`, `setup.go:1271` (which","-already has a `steps.detectAgent` seam). Internal/non-interactive callers keep the pure function.","-","-**B4 — `watch` on main never reaches the function at all.** `watch.go:108` hardcodes `\"codex\"`;","-the feature branch changed it to `\"auto\"` (`watch.go:120`). On main this is a third codex default.","-Fix with B1 or it survives the reorder.","-","-### ⚠️ Open gap: the reporter asked for a MODEL, and B1–B4 deliver a CLI","-","-*\"any chance we could default to Sonnet or Opus?\"* — Sonnet and Opus are **models**.","-`--agent claude-code` selects a **CLI**; the model is a separate axis, set via `--model` and","-`injectAgentModel` (`setup.go`). So B1–B4 fix the surprise (\"why Codex?\") and the silence (\"idk","-what model\") only halfway: after them, a Claude Code user gets the Claude CLI — on whatever model","-that CLI happens to default to, still unstated.","-","-Fully answering the request needs either a brain-side `--model` default/passthrough for the","-distill step, or at minimum **printing the model alongside the agent** so \"idk what model\" stops","-being true. Needs a product decision; not folded into this PR.","-","-### Deferred: the interactive prompt","-","-The reporter also asked for a CLI choice. Worth doing, but **after** B1–B4 land, because it is the","-invasive part — and because B1 alone may satisfy the request: a user in Claude Code who gets","-Claude Code has nothing left to choose.","-","-When done, copy the **only** interactive prompt in the CLI verbatim — `promptSeedTimeoutAction`","-(`seed.go:1792-1806`, confirmed by direct read; one exploration pass wrongly reported the CLI has","-no prompts at all). Its shape: guard on `opts.noInteractive || !stdinIsTerminal()`","-(`seed.go:1811`) and return the fallback; prompt to **stderr**; `fmt.Fscanln(os.Stdin, &response)`;","-**any error falls back**; `default:` is the safe branch. No prompt library exists here —","-`bubbletea`/`lipgloss` are dashboard-only. A prompt that is not TTY-gated hangs every piped","-install forever.","-","----","-","-## Files to modify","-","-| file | change |","+| path | change |"," |---|---|","-| `internal/cli/semantic.go` | **new** `worktreeGateIgnore` helper + use it in `worktreeDirty` `:2924`; refusal message `:594`. **Do NOT touch** the shared ignore list `:2473` or `gitPathspecExclusions` `:2408` — see Change 1 |","-| `internal/cli/seed.go` | refusal message `:276` |","-| `internal/cli/refresh.go` | `defaultRefreshAgent` `:851`/`:741`, announce wrapper, call `ollamaModelMissingWarning` |","-| `internal/cli/distill_cmd.go` | use the announcing wrapper at `:710` |","-| `internal/cli/setup.go` | use it via the `steps.detectAgent` seam at `:1271` |","-| `internal/cli/watch.go` | `\"codex\"` → `\"auto\"` at `:108` (main only) |","+| `docs/install-ux-backlog.md` | new — the live list |","+| `scripts/freshenv-check.sh` | new — throwaway repo + isolated dirs, one check per row |","+| `internal/cli/semantic.go`, `seed.go`, `refresh.go`, `setup.go`, `watch.go`, `distill_cmd.go` | the fixes, in small batches |","+| `internal/cli/mcp.go` | MCP parity for the missing verbs |","+| `internal/cli/doctor*.go` | user-facing subset; internals behind `--verbose` |"," ","-## Branching","-","-Both defects are on **main**, so this is a **separate PR off main** — not stacked on #331, which is","-green and awaiting approval; touching it reopens agent review on clean work.","-","-One exception: `ollamaModelMissingWarning` and the ollama comment block exist **only** on the","-feature branch. If B2's wiring of that warning is wanted, that piece stacks. Confirm before","-starting; the rest is main-safe either way.","-"," ## Verification"," ","-The repo already **requires** this: CONTRIBUTING.md item 3 says every fix needs a test that fails","-without it, and that the PR must include the failure output from a reverted fix. So weakening is","-not an extra step here — it is the contribution standard. Patch each guard compile-clean, show the","-test red, quote the failing assertion, restore.","+1. `scripts/freshenv-check.sh` green for every `verified` row.","+2. Each fix's weakening evidence quoted in its PR.","+3. A fresh-session regression sweep re-runs the harness and flips failures to `regressed`.","+4. The end-to-end that matters: a throwaway repo → `entire graph init-agents` →","+   `entire brain setup` → first `brain query` returns something useful, with **no** degraded","+   components and **no** advice that does not apply."," ","-### Test seams to reuse (do not invent new ones)","+## Known blocker, stated plainly"," ","-- **Command seam:** `CommandRunner` (`runner.go:17`), doubled by `fakeCommandRunner`","-  (`export_test.go:15`) keyed with `fakeCommandKey` (`:170`). It auto-answers `git --version` and","-  friends, so those need no scripting.","-- **Dirty-gate template:** `TestWorktreeDirtyKeepsRenameFromIgnoredToPublic`","-  (`semantic_test.go:896`) — `brainIgnore{patterns: ...}` literal + canned porcelain. This is","-  exactly the shape the gate-only ignore needs. Command-level equivalent:","-  `TestSeedRejectsDirtyWorktreeWithoutWorktreeFlag` (`seed_test.go:400`).","-- **Agent-availability template:** `availabilityRunner` (`local_agent_preference_test.go:9`) —","-  stubs the `<name> --version` probe. PATH is never manipulated for this.","-- Context idiom in these files is `(&cobra.Command{}).Context()`, not `context.Background()`.","-- Assert on the constant `dirtyWorktreeErrorCode` (`export.go:967`), never the bare literal.","-- Human-readable CLI output has **no golden convention** — assert with `strings.Contains` /","-  `visibleLines`. Do not add a golden for the new refusal text.","+`opendirectoryd` is unreachable from this process tree: no DNS, no keychain, `whoami` → `501`.","+So `git fetch`, `gh` and the trail CLI all fail, and the rebase cannot happen from here. Disabling","+the Claude Code sandbox did **not** fix it, which ruled out the sandbox as the cause. Everything","+else in this plan proceeds offline; the rebase waits for a shell with a working bootstrap context."," ","-### Two traps","-","-- **`t.Setenv` + `t.Parallel()` panics in Go.** The harness-detection tests set env, so they must","-  stay serial — and must not share a function with a parallel test. Precedent:","-  `refresh_test.go:16` sets `ENTIRE_BRAIN_NO_EGRESS` and is deliberately non-parallel.","-- **`filterWorktreeStatus` has no direct unit test** — it is only covered transitively. The","-  gate-only ignore runs straight through it, so add one rather than relying on that.","-","-~~FORCE_COLOR~~ — checked and withdrawn: colour tests inject `tui.Caps` explicitly and","-`DetectCapsWithEnv` returns `PlainCaps()` for any non-`*os.File` writer (`render.go:62`), so the","-shell's `FORCE_COLOR=3` cannot leak in. Not a risk for this work.","-","-**Fix A**","-1. Repo dirty **only** with `AGENTS.md`/`CLAUDE.md`/`.claude/settings.json` → `setup` seeds and","-   indexes clean. Weaken by removing the new entries → test red.","-2. Repo with one dirty **source** file → both refusals still fire. This is the guard that stops","-   the fix becoming \"ignore everything\".","-3. A user `.brainignore` still applies, and built-ins do not replace it.","-4. Refusal message names the offending paths.","-","-**End-to-end, the actual reported bug:** fresh clone → `entire graph init-agents` → then","-`entire brain refresh`.","-","-⚠️ **Corrected after adversarial review — the original acceptance test was invalid.** It read","-\"`entire brain setup` must succeed; it currently fails.\" That is false: `watchDeterministicRefreshComponents`","-passes `bestEffort=true`, so seed/semantic failures are *reported, not fatal*, docs and history","-still build, and setup only hard-fails when nothing builds at all. **`setup` already exits 0","-(degraded) on a dirty tree**, so that test would have passed before and after — a false pass","-dressed as an acceptance gate.","-","-Assert on the **component outcome** (seed and semantic go from failed/degraded to built), not the","-exit code. Use `entire brain refresh`, which is not best-effort and does exit non-zero, as the","-end-to-end surface.","-","-**Fix B**","-5. `CLAUDECODE` set + `codex` on PATH → picks `claude-code`. Weaken by dropping detection → red.","-6. No harness env, no TTY → deterministic, no prompt, never hangs.","-7. The chosen agent is announced on stderr; silent under `--json`.","-8. `ollamaModelMissingWarning` fires when ollama is present and something else is chosen —","-   currently unreachable, so this test fails before the fix.","-","-**Constraints:** no full local suites (CPU-bound). The repo's own convention is targeted:","-`go test ./internal/cli -run '^TestX$' -count=1` (`docs/testing-for-optimization.md`), with","-`GOMAXPROCS=1 -p 1 -parallel 1` on this machine.","-"," ## Not doing"," ","-Merging, approving, or pushing to any existing PR without explicit approval. The `\" -> \"`","-path-splitting bug is filed separately, not folded in.","+Merging, approving or pushing without explicit approval. No model id hardcoded — `setup.go` already","+records why (\"model ids age badly\"), and that reasoning stands."]}],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8ab873a3-dd59-4820-a1bd-93554e7ea424","session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.292","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
