{"parentUuid":"f94085e9-1c24-421f-9ddf-cbd680aec7e7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfmnP4KaY5PtAdqoynnbE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now the backlog with everything the three audits found:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1124,"cache_read_input_tokens":875686,"output_tokens":5224,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1124},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5224,"cache_read_input_tokens":875686,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1124,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1124,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"8b0d6be7-5429-44d8-a49c-e8cb069f73be","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfmnP3v1MabuZ7tr8of5i","type":"assistant","uuid":"99b31a41-b192-4919-a45c-5cfcb20639d0","timestamp":"2026-10-06T22:36:41.847Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-ux-backlog","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.292","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"99b31a41-b192-4919-a45c-5cfcb20639d0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfmnP4KaY5PtAdqoynnbE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VJvyCfUSdCdwuB15sKJtKE","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-ux-backlog/docs/install-ux-backlog.md","content":"# Install & agent-usage backlog\n\nLive list. One row per defect, worked top-down, each verified before it is closed.\nTarget user: **someone outside the team installing fresh**, who must get a working brain their\nagent actually uses without reading source.\n\n`symptom` is written from outside on purpose. A backlog phrased in `memory_overlay` /\n`dirty_worktree` vocabulary recreates the problem it is trying to fix.\n\n**Status:** `open` → `fixed` → `verified` → (`regressed`)\n**Verified means:** a test that fails on a compile-clean revert, **and** a fresh-env check that\nreproduces the user-visible symptom and shows it gone, **and** a negative control wherever the fix\ncould over-apply.\n\nBaseline: `origin/main` @ `6c8ebdab`. Reproduce any row with `scripts/try-first-run.sh`.\n\n---\n\n## P0 — a first-run user is stuck or misled\n\n| id | symptom | anchor | fix | status |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| UX-01 | A throwaway `setup` **overwrites the real launchd daemon**, repointing it at a temp dir that then disappears. Trying brain in a scratch repo breaks your actual install. Observed while writing the harness. | daemon name derivation; `setup.go:838-857` | Derive the daemon identity per workspace+repo so a scratch repo cannot claim an existing name; refuse to rewrite a plist owned by another root. | open |\n| UX-02 | Ten error messages tell you to run **`entire brain index`**, which does not exist. Verified: `unknown command \"index\"`. It is the first thing a degraded user reaches for. | `semantic.go:890,3233,3324,3410,3477,3569,3635,5901`; `semantic_graph.go:154`; `refresh.go:78` | Replace all ten with `refresh index` via `setupCommandPrefix`, or register `index` as an alias. Add a test that every backticked `entire brain <verb>` resolves against the command tree. | open |\n| UX-03 | Uncommitted work ⇒ seed **and** semantic both fail, and `setup` has **no** `--worktree`, `--include-uncommitted` or `--force`. There is no forward path from inside `setup`. | `setup.go:470-482` | Add `--worktree`; better, auto-fall-back on `dirty_worktree` and say \"indexed the working tree as it stands, not attributed to HEAD\". Provenance is already recorded, so the fallback is safe and labelled. | open |\n| UX-04 | The dirty hint blames `entire enable`'s files. For anyone whose dirt is their own work it is **confidently wrong** — a live case had ~250 staged notebooks/models/figures and none of Entire's files. It reaches the user three times. | hint `setup.go:133-136`; matcher `setup.go:211-213`; reused `status_render.go:320` | Build the hint from the actual dirty paths. Mention `entire enable` only when the dirty set is a subset of Entire-authored paths. | open |\n| UX-05 | **`.brainignore` is the real escape hatch and is named nowhere** — 0 mentions in errors, 0 in README. It is already loaded by the gate and would have cleared the live case instantly. | gate `semantic.go:2537-2551`; loader `semantic.go:2271` | Name it in both refusals and the setup hint; print the top dirty directories as a paste-ready stanza; document in the quickstart. | open |\n| UX-06 | `refresh --worktree` **cannot repair a degraded brain** — it turns the semantic stage off unconditionally. The note then recommends the one command that will fail again. | skip `refresh.go:55-59`; note `refresh.go:648-650` | Pass `--worktree` through to semantic, or name `refresh index --worktree` in the note. | open |\n| UX-07 | `setup` writes **no guide, no pointer, no MCP registration, no hook**, and prints no next step. A setup-only repo is invisible to every agent. `setup.go` has zero references to `agentsetup`. | `setup.go` (whole); `agent_setup.go:13` | End `setup` by running `init-agents`, or at minimum print it as the next step. | open |\n| UX-08 | Our own installers write files that then block our own install. | `entireAuthoredGatePaths` | **Built and verified** on `fix/install-ux-dirty-gate-and-agent-default` @ `3cc936ad`. ⚠️ Does **not** fix UX-03/04 — a user whose dirt is real work is still stuck, and the wrong hint ships with it. Land UX-03+04+05 alongside. | fixed |\n\n## P1 — silently wrong, or reads as broken\n\n| id | symptom | anchor | fix | status |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| UX-09 | The guide tells agents *\"No MCP tool writes a fact; do not go looking for one\"* while the same build registers `brain_remember`. | `agentsetup/strict.go:155-156`; `guide.go:57`; tool at `mcp.go:905` | Correct the text; add a generator test asserting guide claims against the live tool list. A test already guards tool *descriptions* from naming absent tools — nothing guards the guide. | open |\n| UX-10 | The guide **mandates** `recall` and `verify`, and a once-per-session `version` + `capabilities` preflight. **None of those four are MCP tools.** The mandate is unfollowable for an MCP-only agent. | `strict.go:108-109,137-146` | Add `brain_recall`, `brain_verify`, `brain_guide`, `brain_overview`; fold capabilities/version into `brain_status`. `brain_guide` matters most — an MCP-only agent currently cannot read its own instructions. | open |\n| UX-11 | Empty `recall` on `main` blames distillation coverage. The real cause — facts live on another branch — is in **none** of the five blind-spot branches. The agent concludes the decision never existed. | `blind_spot.go:34-66` | Add a branch arm naming the branch read and that facts exist elsewhere. | open |\n| UX-12 | Bare empty results with no explanation: `brain_patterns` `[]` (the \"not built vs none found\" distinction exists only in text mode), `brain_query_graph` (no blind spot, no freshness), `brain_impact`/`tests`/`boundaries` (empty reads as \"no callers\"), `brain_trace_path` (never says depth defaulted to 4), `brain_dead_code`, `brain_get` `missing[]`. | `patterns_cmd.go:124`; `semantic_graph.go:456,735,936`; `semantic.go:3570,3732,3798`; `retrieve_cmd.go:760` | Every empty answer states why it is empty. | open |\n| UX-13 | Truncation is declared **only** for the byte-budget trim. Per-tool `limit` defaults (10/5/3/20), SQL `LIMIT`s and slice cuts are all silent, and `brain_code`/`brain_context` paginate with no `total`/`has_more`. | `mcp.go:1062-1073`; `semantic_graph.go:340-352,635-636`; `semantic.go:4456-4460` | Fetch limit+1, emit `has_more`; hoist snippet truncation to the root. | open |\n| UX-14 | Installed binary renders a **32768**-byte budget; the repo constant is **131072**. Live truncation bites 4× sooner than source implies. Installed build is Sep 21. | `mcp_response_budget.go:16` | Reinstall; the text is generated from the constant and self-heals. Record the drift. | open |\n| UX-15 | `brief` on an empty brain prints three lines and never says why. Its one applicable warning is gated behind `Sources.Sessions != nil`, which is nil on a zero-session repo — so it **cannot fire**. | guard `agent_surface.go:1636` | Drop the gate; wire `brief` to the blind-spot choke point. | open |\n| UX-16 | `overview` on a built-but-empty brain omits every section; its \"not built yet\" warning needs `GeneratedAt.IsZero()`, false the moment setup writes a manifest, so it **can never fire after a first run**. Reads as broken. | `agent_surface.go:514,624-700` | Second guard: manifest present but all counts zero ⇒ say the zeros are absence of data. | open |\n| UX-17 | MCP server `instructions` carry only the byte-budget contract — nothing says what brain is or when to call it. Tool descriptions are mechanism (\"Return/List/Search X\"), never trigger. `brain_brief` never says \"call first\". | `mcp.go:664-668`, `:806-990` | Lead each description with a trigger clause; put 2–3 trigger sentences in `instructions`. | open |\n| UX-18 | `hook pre-edit` is wired by **neither** `setup` nor `init-agents`; the docs admit it has \"no effect\" until a harness wires it. It also takes `--file` while PreToolUse delivers JSON on stdin. | `hook_cmd.go:15-17,183-196` | Have `init-agents` merge a PreToolUse entry; accept stdin; emit the hook JSON envelope. | open |\n| UX-19 | `--no-daemon` and `--no-backfill` are **not persisted**. A user who declined the daemon, then follows \"re-run setup\", silently gets a persistent login service and a token spend. | `setup.go:1308-1321,1360-1389` | Persist both. | open |\n| UX-20 | Re-running `setup` cannot learn: identical output, no comparison with the previous record, no escalation. | write `setup.go:668`; readers `setup_status.go:159` | Read the prior record; on a repeated identical failure escalate the advice. | open |\n| UX-21 | ~28 remedies hardcode `entire brain …` instead of `setupCommandPrefix`, so on one install shape the printed command is unrunnable. | `agent_surface.go`, `lifecycle_ops.go`, `memory_admin.go`, `semantic.go` (28 sites) | Route through `setupBrainCommand`; add a lint banning the literal. | open |\n\n## P2 — the product talks to itself\n\n| id | symptom | anchor | fix | status |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| UX-22 | `doctor` prints **40 lines / 6.4 KB**, 34 ok + 5 warn, on a healthy brain. **Of 6 non-ok lines, 1 names a remedy.** Three checks are constant `\"ok\"` literals that can never fail. No `--verbose` exists. | `lifecycle_ops.go:109-320`; constants `:123,:161,:181`; `doctor.go:113-114` | Cut to ≤8 actionable lines; everything else behind `--verbose`; `--json` unchanged. Delete the three checks that cannot fail. | open |\n| UX-23 | **46 verbs / ~127 invocable commands**, incl. **seven** ways to ask a question (`query`, `search`, `vsearch`, `get`, `multi-get`, `show`, `recall`). `search`/`vsearch` are literally `query --keyword` / `--semantic`, same constructor. | `root.go:98-185`; `retrieve_cmd.go:71-81` | Collapse retrieval to `query` + `get`; hide `memory`/`facts`-eval/`watch`/`distill` subtrees. Top-level 40 → ~16. | open |\n| UX-24 | A first `setup` prints **~65 lines**, ~24 of them the inner `refresh` leaking through. Duplicate consent text; two different names for the same component in one run; a hashed daemon id surfaced. | `setup.go:1254-1257,634,913`; `setup_render.go:197,268` | Pass `io.Discard` to the nested refresh when not `--json`. | open |\n| UX-25 | \"Brain ready (degraded) … the brain is queryable now\" prints even when seed **and** semantic both failed — i.e. no code index and no baseline. Exit 0. | `setup_render.go:149-158` | Say what is unavailable; keep exit 0 but stop asserting queryability it lacks. | open |\n| UX-26 | `status` has the Detail and Hint for each failed component but prints only the names. | `status_render.go:472-490` | Print Detail under each failure. | open |\n| UX-27 | A dirty tree prints **two contradictory remedies at once** — \"commit or stash\" in the verdict, \"refresh with `--worktree`\" in the cause underneath. | `status_render.go:320`; `agent_surface.go:4634` | One remedy resolver. | open |\n| UX-28 | Dead surface a user can trip over: `refresh seed --interactive` is registered and **never read**; `distill --jobs` is a self-conflicting alias; 9 verbs have zero README mentions; the docs contract test is one-directional. | `seed.go:238`; `distill_cmd.go:606`; `documented_commands_test.go:14` | Delete the dead flag; make the docs test bidirectional. | open |\n| UX-29 | Misleading names: `path` is a print verb that **builds** via `--ensure`; `add` means clone but collides with `workspace add`; `dash`/`viz`/`inspect graph-ui` are three visualizers; `repair`/`reset`/`memory repair`/`memory rebuild` are four names for one job; `stats` is one character from `status`. | `path.go:29`; `add.go:21`; `dash.go:38`; `viz.go:62`; `semantic.go:353,372` | Rename/merge per audit; weigh doc churn (`patterns` ×42, `path` ×11). | open |\n| UX-30 | Remedies that cannot be followed: `--graph-binary` is named but is not a `setup` flag; \"install with `scripts/install.sh` from the checkout\" is false for plugin installs; \"delete the setup record\" is destructive advice on a transient read error. | `semantic.go:1228,1302`; `setup.go:533` | Name runnable commands; distinguish parse from I/O failure. | open |\n\n---\n\n## How to reproduce\n\n```sh\nsh scripts/try-first-run.sh dirty    # uncommitted real work — UX-03/04/05/25\nsh scripts/try-first-run.sh clean    # the happy path — UX-07/15/16\n```\n\nRuns in a throwaway repo with isolated `XDG_*`. Passes `--no-daemon`: the daemon is **not**\nisolated by XDG (UX-01), and dropping that flag rewrites your real plist.\n\n**What this harness cannot catch:** anything about the install itself, because the binaries are\nalready present. Install-step defects are marked `unverifiable-here` rather than quietly passed.\n\n## Corrections already folded in\n\n- The local `entire-brain` checkout was **329 commits stale**; audit against `origin/main`.\n- `hook pre-edit` is already on main (`ab488d2c`), not unmerged.\n- `ollamaModelMissingWarning` is **not** on main — it exists only on a feature branch.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1124,"cache_read_input_tokens":875686,"output_tokens":5224,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1124},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5224,"cache_read_input_tokens":875686,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1124,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1124,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01VJvyCfUSdCdwuB15sKJtKE":{"file_path":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-ux-backlog/docs/install-ux-backlog.md","content":"# Install & agent-usage backlog\n\nLive list. One row per defect, worked top-down, each verified before it is closed.\nTarget user: **someone outside the team installing fresh**, who must get a working brain their\nagent actually uses without reading source.\n\n`symptom` is written from outside on purpose. A backlog phrased in `memory_overlay` /\n`dirty_worktree` vocabulary recreates the problem it is trying to fix.\n\n**Status:** `open` → `fixed` → `verified` → (`regressed`)\n**Verified means:** a test that fails on a compile-clean revert, **and** a fresh-env check that\nreproduces the user-visible symptom and shows it gone, **and** a negative control wherever the fix\ncould over-apply.\n\nBaseline: `origin/main` @ `6c8ebdab`. Reproduce any row with `scripts/try-first-run.sh`.\n\n---\n\n## P0 — a first-run user is stuck or misled\n\n| id | symptom | anchor | fix | status |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| UX-01 | A throwaway `setup` **overwrites the real launchd daemon**, repointing it at a temp dir that then disappears. Trying brain in a scratch repo breaks your actual install. Observed while writing the harness. | daemon name derivation; `setup.go:838-857` | Derive the daemon identity per workspace+repo so a scratch repo cannot claim an existing name; refuse to rewrite a plist owned by another root. | open |\n| UX-02 | Ten error messages tell you to run **`entire brain index`**, which does not exist. Verified: `unknown command \"index\"`. It is the first thing a degraded user reaches for. | `semantic.go:890,3233,3324,3410,3477,3569,3635,5901`; `semantic_graph.go:154`; `refresh.go:78` | Replace all ten with `refresh index` via `setupCommandPrefix`, or register `index` as an alias. Add a test that every backticked `entire brain <verb>` resolves against the command tree. | open |\n| UX-03 | Uncommitted work ⇒ seed **and** semantic both fail, and `setup` has **no** `--worktree`, `--include-uncommitted` or `--force`. There is no forward path from inside `setup`. | `setup.go:470-482` | Add `--worktree`; better, auto-fall-back on `dirty_worktree` and say \"indexed the working tree as it stands, not attributed to HEAD\". Provenance is already recorded, so the fallback is safe and labelled. | open |\n| UX-04 | The dirty hint blames `entire enable`'s files. For anyone whose dirt is their own work it is **confidently wrong** — a live case had ~250 staged notebooks/models/figures and none of Entire's files. It reaches the user three times. | hint `setup.go:133-136`; matcher `setup.go:211-213`; reused `status_render.go:320` | Build the hint from the actual dirty paths. Mention `entire enable` only when the dirty set is a subset of Entire-authored paths. | open |\n| UX-05 | **`.brainignore` is the real escape hatch and is named nowhere** — 0 mentions in errors, 0 in README. It is already loaded by the gate and would have cleared the live case instantly. | gate `semantic.go:2537-2551`; loader `semantic.go:2271` | Name it in both refusals and the setup hint; print the top dirty directories as a paste-ready stanza; document in the quickstart. | open |\n| UX-06 | `refresh --worktree` **cannot repair a degraded brain** — it turns the semantic stage off unconditionally. The note then recommends the one command that will fail again. | skip `refresh.go:55-59`; note `refresh.go:648-650` | Pass `--worktree` through to semantic, or name `refresh index --worktree` in the note. | open |\n| UX-07 | `setup` writes **no guide, no pointer, no MCP registration, no hook**, and prints no next step. A setup-only repo is invisible to every agent. `setup.go` has zero references to `agentsetup`. | `setup.go` (whole); `agent_setup.go:13` | End `setup` by running `init-agents`, or at minimum print it as the next step. | open |\n| UX-08 | Our own installers write files that then block our own install. | `entireAuthoredGatePaths` | **Built and verified** on `fix/install-ux-dirty-gate-and-agent-default` @ `3cc936ad`. ⚠️ Does **not** fix UX-03/04 — a user whose dirt is real work is still stuck, and the wrong hint ships with it. Land UX-03+04+05 alongside. | fixed |\n\n## P1 — silently wrong, or reads as broken\n\n| id | symptom | anchor | fix | status |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| UX-09 | The guide tells agents *\"No MCP tool writes a fact; do not go looking for one\"* while the same build registers `brain_remember`. | `agentsetup/strict.go:155-156`; `guide.go:57`; tool at `mcp.go:905` | Correct the text; add a generator test asserting guide claims against the live tool list. A test already guards tool *descriptions* from naming absent tools — nothing guards the guide. | open |\n| UX-10 | The guide **mandates** `recall` and `verify`, and a once-per-session `version` + `capabilities` preflight. **None of those four are MCP tools.** The mandate is unfollowable for an MCP-only agent. | `strict.go:108-109,137-146` | Add `brain_recall`, `brain_verify`, `brain_guide`, `brain_overview`; fold capabilities/version into `brain_status`. `brain_guide` matters most — an MCP-only agent currently cannot read its own instructions. | open |\n| UX-11 | Empty `recall` on `main` blames distillation coverage. The real cause — facts live on another branch — is in **none** of the five blind-spot branches. The agent concludes the decision never existed. | `blind_spot.go:34-66` | Add a branch arm naming the branch read and that facts exist elsewhere. | open |\n| UX-12 | Bare empty results with no explanation: `brain_patterns` `[]` (the \"not built vs none found\" distinction exists only in text mode), `brain_query_graph` (no blind spot, no freshness), `brain_impact`/`tests`/`boundaries` (empty reads as \"no callers\"), `brain_trace_path` (never says depth defaulted to 4), `brain_dead_code`, `brain_get` `missing[]`. | `patterns_cmd.go:124`; `semantic_graph.go:456,735,936`; `semantic.go:3570,3732,3798`; `retrieve_cmd.go:760` | Every empty answer states why it is empty. | open |\n| UX-13 | Truncation is declared **only** for the byte-budget trim. Per-tool `limit` defaults (10/5/3/20), SQL `LIMIT`s and slice cuts are all silent, and `brain_code`/`brain_context` paginate with no `total`/`has_more`. | `mcp.go:1062-1073`; `semantic_graph.go:340-352,635-636`; `semantic.go:4456-4460` | Fetch limit+1, emit `has_more`; hoist snippet truncation to the root. | open |\n| UX-14 | Installed binary renders a **32768**-byte budget; the repo constant is **131072**. Live truncation bites 4× sooner than source implies. Installed build is Sep 21. | `mcp_response_budget.go:16` | Reinstall; the text is generated from the constant and self-heals. Record the drift. | open |\n| UX-15 | `brief` on an empty brain prints three lines and never says why. Its one applicable warning is gated behind `Sources.Sessions != nil`, which is nil on a zero-session repo — so it **cannot fire**. | guard `agent_surface.go:1636` | Drop the gate; wire `brief` to the blind-spot choke point. | open |\n| UX-16 | `overview` on a built-but-empty brain omits every section; its \"not built yet\" warning needs `GeneratedAt.IsZero()`, false the moment setup writes a manifest, so it **can never fire after a first run**. Reads as broken. | `agent_surface.go:514,624-700` | Second guard: manifest present but all counts zero ⇒ say the zeros are absence of data. | open |\n| UX-17 | MCP server `instructions` carry only the byte-budget contract — nothing says what brain is or when to call it. Tool descriptions are mechanism (\"Return/List/Search X\"), never trigger. `brain_brief` never says \"call first\". | `mcp.go:664-668`, `:806-990` | Lead each description with a trigger clause; put 2–3 trigger sentences in `instructions`. | open |\n| UX-18 | `hook pre-edit` is wired by **neither** `setup` nor `init-agents`; the docs admit it has \"no effect\" until a harness wires it. It also takes `--file` while PreToolUse delivers JSON on stdin. | `hook_cmd.go:15-17,183-196` | Have `init-agents` merge a PreToolUse entry; accept stdin; emit the hook JSON envelope. | open |\n| UX-19 | `--no-daemon` and `--no-backfill` are **not persisted**. A user who declined the daemon, then follows \"re-run setup\", silently gets a persistent login service and a token spend. | `setup.go:1308-1321,1360-1389` | Persist both. | open |\n| UX-20 | Re-running `setup` cannot learn: identical output, no comparison with the previous record, no escalation. | write `setup.go:668`; readers `setup_status.go:159` | Read the prior record; on a repeated identical failure escalate the advice. | open |\n| UX-21 | ~28 remedies hardcode `entire brain …` instead of `setupCommandPrefix`, so on one install shape the printed command is unrunnable. | `agent_surface.go`, `lifecycle_ops.go`, `memory_admin.go`, `semantic.go` (28 sites) | Route through `setupBrainCommand`; add a lint banning the literal. | open |\n\n## P2 — the product talks to itself\n\n| id | symptom | anchor | fix | status |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| UX-22 | `doctor` prints **40 lines / 6.4 KB**, 34 ok + 5 warn, on a healthy brain. **Of 6 non-ok lines, 1 names a remedy.** Three checks are constant `\"ok\"` literals that can never fail. No `--verbose` exists. | `lifecycle_ops.go:109-320`; constants `:123,:161,:181`; `doctor.go:113-114` | Cut to ≤8 actionable lines; everything else behind `--verbose`; `--json` unchanged. Delete the three checks that cannot fail. | open |\n| UX-23 | **46 verbs / ~127 invocable commands**, incl. **seven** ways to ask a question (`query`, `search`, `vsearch`, `get`, `multi-get`, `show`, `recall`). `search`/`vsearch` are literally `query --keyword` / `--semantic`, same constructor. | `root.go:98-185`; `retrieve_cmd.go:71-81` | Collapse retrieval to `query` + `get`; hide `memory`/`facts`-eval/`watch`/`distill` subtrees. Top-level 40 → ~16. | open |\n| UX-24 | A first `setup` prints **~65 lines**, ~24 of them the inner `refresh` leaking through. Duplicate consent text; two different names for the same component in one run; a hashed daemon id surfaced. | `setup.go:1254-1257,634,913`; `setup_render.go:197,268` | Pass `io.Discard` to the nested refresh when not `--json`. | open |\n| UX-25 | \"Brain ready (degraded) … the brain is queryable now\" prints even when seed **and** semantic both failed — i.e. no code index and no baseline. Exit 0. | `setup_render.go:149-158` | Say what is unavailable; keep exit 0 but stop asserting queryability it lacks. | open |\n| UX-26 | `status` has the Detail and Hint for each failed component but prints only the names. | `status_render.go:472-490` | Print Detail under each failure. | open |\n| UX-27 | A dirty tree prints **two contradictory remedies at once** — \"commit or stash\" in the verdict, \"refresh with `--worktree`\" in the cause underneath. | `status_render.go:320`; `agent_surface.go:4634` | One remedy resolver. | open |\n| UX-28 | Dead surface a user can trip over: `refresh seed --interactive` is registered and **never read**; `distill --jobs` is a self-conflicting alias; 9 verbs have zero README mentions; the docs contract test is one-directional. | `seed.go:238`; `distill_cmd.go:606`; `documented_commands_test.go:14` | Delete the dead flag; make the docs test bidirectional. | open |\n| UX-29 | Misleading names: `path` is a print verb that **builds** via `--ensure`; `add` means clone but collides with `workspace add`; `dash`/`viz`/`inspect graph-ui` are three visualizers; `repair`/`reset`/`memory repair`/`memory rebuild` are four names for one job; `stats` is one character from `status`. | `path.go:29`; `add.go:21`; `dash.go:38`; `viz.go:62`; `semantic.go:353,372` | Rename/merge per audit; weigh doc churn (`patterns` ×42, `path` ×11). | open |\n| UX-30 | Remedies that cannot be followed: `--graph-binary` is named but is not a `setup` flag; \"install with `scripts/install.sh` from the checkout\" is false for plugin installs; \"delete the setup record\" is destructive advice on a transient read error. | `semantic.go:1228,1302`; `setup.go:533` | Name runnable commands; distinguish parse from I/O failure. | open |\n\n---\n\n## How to reproduce\n\n```sh\nsh scripts/try-first-run.sh dirty    # uncommitted real work — UX-03/04/05/25\nsh scripts/try-first-run.sh clean    # the happy path — UX-07/15/16\n```\n\nRuns in a throwaway repo with isolated `XDG_*`. Passes `--no-daemon`: the daemon is **not**\nisolated by XDG (UX-01), and dropping that flag rewrites your real plist.\n\n**What this harness cannot catch:** anything about the install itself, because the binaries are\nalready present. Install-step defects are marked `unverifiable-here` rather than quietly passed.\n\n## Corrections already folded in\n\n- The local `entire-brain` checkout was **329 commits stale**; audit against `origin/main`.\n- `hook pre-edit` is already on main (`ab488d2c`), not unmerged.\n- `ollamaModelMissingWarning` is **not** on main — it exists only on a feature branch.\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"8b0d6be7-5429-44d8-a49c-e8cb069f73be","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfmnP3v1MabuZ7tr8of5i","type":"assistant","uuid":"47957099-5b10-4d90-a54d-8c7d3bc62afe","timestamp":"2026-10-06T22:37:40.897Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-ux-backlog","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.292","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
