{"parentUuid":"6f0bf6a3-94b5-4344-a855-910a5b45cd68","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14973623 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"9e0ac7bd-104d-4aee-8354-7a4ac6a3e2e9","timestamp":"2026-10-11T20:10:25.931Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14973623 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"1eac9040-9610-45f1-aa43-df0931455a37","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"9e0ac7bd-104d-4aee-8354-7a4ac6a3e2e9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cfw4GsuEV2meHvC62TvCT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Status, and it's a lot better than when we stopped.\n\n## Unblocked\n\nDNS, keychain and `gh` all work. `whoami` is `suhaan` again — the `opendirectoryd` problem cleared itself.\n\n## Your PRs: 4 of 6 merged\n\n| merged | still open |\n|---|---|\n| **#318, #320, #330, #331** (+ #332, #333, #334) | **#321** distill timeout + nested-repo trap · **#329** retrieval output |\n\nMain moved from `6c8ebdab` → `e6bb5c42`, with **#336–#339** landing on top.\n\n## Your goal 4 is already built\n\n**`brain connect` exists on main — you just don't have it installed** (you're on 0.1.0; the command is `unknown` locally). From the source, `hostedFactsSyncAndPull` does exactly what you asked for:\n\n> *\"publish the branch's local facts … then merge the settled head — with server-stamped authors — back into the local branch store **so teammates' facts become** [visible]\"*\n\nIt even degrades sensibly: if publish is denied but pull is granted, it falls back to pull-only so you still receive the team's facts. **brainstore** is the service side — `factmerge` is exported for it in #338, and #339 is the client.\n\nSo: shared hosted brain = done and merged. The gap is distribution, not capability.\n\n## What this does to the backlog\n\nI have to flag this rather than hand you a stale list. **The 30-defect backlog was written against `6c8ebdab`**, and at least two items have since shipped:\n\n- **#333 \"Hide developer commands from default Brain CLI help\"** — that's my UX-23 surface item\n- **#337 \"put facts and history before status in `brief --json`; name recall in guides\"** — overlaps UX-10 and UX-15\n\nSo some rows are already dead. Presenting the list as current would be exactly the stale-evidence mistake I made earlier today with the PR states.\n\n## What I'd do next\n\n1. **Re-validate all 30 rows against `e6bb5c42`** and mark what shipped — an hour of agent work, and it stops us fixing things twice.\n2. **Rebase `fix/install-ux-dirty-gate-and-agent-default`** (still sitting on `6c8ebdab`, 24 weakenings verified) and check it against #331/#333, which touched the same guide and hook code.\n3. **Reinstall brain from main** so you actually have `connect`, `stop`/`start`, and the hidden-command cleanup.\n\nYour four goals map onto this cleanly: first-run flow and docs simplification are most of the backlog, efficiency is unmeasured so far, and hosted sharing needs an install plus a real two-person test. Say which to start and I'll go."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":993,"cache_read_input_tokens":908900,"output_tokens":900,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":993,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":900,"cache_read_input_tokens":908900,"cache_creation_input_tokens":993,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":993},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"20702977-9484-464a-8653-6586ee341c88","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cfw4GsBKvee3mSMH8dhdK","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"5d048e1b-16f6-4652-ab17-3c52e3fc222d","timestamp":"2026-10-11T20:10:39.641Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"1eac9040-9610-45f1-aa43-df0931455a37","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.