{"parentUuid":"29389ac5-e54b-4ce1-9c63-a40f84e0e89c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cfw6TbW3eD4JvtWYVpL7C","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017WmcjpppeC2QpmcywTfCCS","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Re-validate backlog against current main","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"opus","prompt":"Re-validate a 30-row defect backlog against CURRENT main. Several rows have probably shipped since it was written; presenting a stale list would make us fix things twice.\n\nBACKLOG: /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-ux-backlog/docs/install-ux-backlog.md — read it first. Rows are UX-01 … UX-30.\nBASELINE IT WAS WRITTEN AGAINST: entire-brain `6c8ebdab`.\nCURRENT MAIN: `e6bb5c42` (76 commits later). Read current main, not any stale worktree.\nUse /Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain (fetched; `git show origin/main:<file>`). Read-only — change nothing.\n\nKNOWN LANDINGS that likely kill or alter rows — verify each, do not assume:\n- #333 \"Hide developer commands from default Brain CLI help\" → likely affects UX-23 (46 verbs / 7 retrieval verbs) and UX-28 (undocumented surface).\n- #337 \"put facts and history before status in brief --json; name recall in guides\" → likely affects UX-10 (guide mandates unfollowable verbs), UX-15 (brief on empty brain).\n- #330 (merged) \"stop brain colliding with concurrent git, stalling on a dirty tree, and ignoring local models\" → **may partly or wholly fix UX-03/UX-04/UX-06** (the dirty-tree blockers). Check this one hardest — it is the core of the backlog.\n- #318 (merged) \"name the branches holding facts when a query finds none\" → likely fixes UX-11 (blind spot has no branch arm).\n- #320, #331, #332, #334, #336, #338, #339 also merged — check for incidental fixes.\n\nFOR EVERY ROW UX-01..UX-30 return exactly one verdict:\n  FIXED      — no longer reproduces on main. Give the commit/PR and the file:line proving it.\n  PARTIAL    — some of it fixed. Say precisely what remains, with file:line.\n  STILL OPEN — reproduces on main. Re-confirm the anchor still exists at a current file:line (line numbers WILL have moved).\n  INVALID    — was wrong when written. Say why.\n\nRe-confirm these specific claims against current main, since they are the backlog's load-bearing facts:\n1. Does `entire brain index` still not exist? (UX-02 — 10 error strings name it.)\n2. Does `setup` still have no `--worktree`/`--include-uncommitted`/`--force`? (UX-03)\n3. Is the `entire enable` dirty hint still unconditional? (UX-04)\n4. Is `.brainignore` still named in zero error strings and zero README lines? (UX-05)\n5. Does `refresh --worktree` still disable the semantic stage? (UX-06)\n6. Does `setup` still write no agent guide / print no next step? (UX-07)\n7. Does the guide still say \"No MCP tool writes a fact\"? (UX-09)\n8. Count `doctor` lines and non-ok lines on main; are the three constant-\"ok\" checks still there? (UX-22)\n9. Count top-level verbs on main after #333. (UX-23)\n10. Is `refresh seed --interactive` still registered-and-never-read? (UX-28)\n\nAlso flag any NEW defect the recent merges introduced, especially around the hosted-sync surface (`hosted_sync.go`, `hosted_token.go`, `pause.go`, `brain connect`) — it is new code aimed at first-time users, so it is the most likely place for fresh first-run defects.\n\nUse `entire graph search --repo . --profile full --head --query \"...\"` before grepping. Use rtk. Do NOT run full test suites (CPU-bound). You may run read-only `--help`/`doctor`/`status`, but do NOT run `entire brain setup` anywhere, and never without `--no-daemon` (a scratch run rewrites the real launchd plist — that happened once today).\n\nOUTPUT: caveman-ultra compressed. One line per row: `UX-nn | VERDICT | evidence file:line or PR | what remains`. Then \"NEW DEFECTS\" with the same shape. Then a 3-line summary: how many fixed / partial / open. No prose padding, no preamble. Mark anything unconfirmed \"unverified\"."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":383,"cache_read_input_tokens":912140,"output_tokens":1586,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":383,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1586,"cache_read_input_tokens":912140,"cache_creation_input_tokens":383,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":383},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_017WmcjpppeC2QpmcywTfCCS":{"description":"Re-validate backlog against current main","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"opus","prompt":"Re-validate a 30-row defect backlog against CURRENT main. Several rows have probably shipped since it was written; presenting a stale list would make us fix things twice.\n\nBACKLOG: /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-ux-backlog/docs/install-ux-backlog.md — read it first. Rows are UX-01 … UX-30.\nBASELINE IT WAS WRITTEN AGAINST: entire-brain `6c8ebdab`.\nCURRENT MAIN: `e6bb5c42` (76 commits later). Read current main, not any stale worktree.\nUse /Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain (fetched; `git show origin/main:<file>`). Read-only — change nothing.\n\nKNOWN LANDINGS that likely kill or alter rows — verify each, do not assume:\n- #333 \"Hide developer commands from default Brain CLI help\" → likely affects UX-23 (46 verbs / 7 retrieval verbs) and UX-28 (undocumented surface).\n- #337 \"put facts and history before status in brief --json; name recall in guides\" → likely affects UX-10 (guide mandates unfollowable verbs), UX-15 (brief on empty brain).\n- #330 (merged) \"stop brain colliding with concurrent git,