{"parentUuid":"9cd2ee65-cec6-494e-b155-2ac838113bbd","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14998394 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"8174b185-10bf-483b-abae-0167d5106fc8","timestamp":"2026-10-11T20:47:14.389Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14998394 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"1eac9040-9610-45f1-aa43-df0931455a37","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-ux-backlog","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"8174b185-10bf-483b-abae-0167d5106fc8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cfw75gDoxmd2XVHqRyLTU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LXNJv8GwhgP8aXmU8FogwH","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-ux-backlog\npython3 - <<'PY'\np='CHANGELOG.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nold = \"## [Unreleased]\\n\"\nassert old in s, \"anchor missing\"\nnew = \"\"\"## [Unreleased]\n\nTwenty days and 24 merged pull requests since 0.1.0. The theme is reach: the\nbrain is no longer confined to one machine, one repository, or one file format,\nand it says more about what it does and does not know.\n\n### Added\n\n- **Hosted memory.** `brain connect` binds a repository to its hosted store,\n  publishes the branch's facts, and merges the settled head back with\n  server-stamped authors, so a teammate's facts appear in your local brain. If\n  the publish grant is missing but the pull grant is not, it falls back to\n  pull-only rather than failing: you still receive the team's work.\n- **MCP over HTTP**, opt-in and authenticated, alongside the existing stdio\n  transport.\n- **A REST API with Python and TypeScript clients**, so services that are not\n  coding agents can read the brain.\n- **Webhooks**: notify another service when the brain changes.\n- **PDF, Word, Excel and PowerPoint** are read into the brain, not just\n  plain-text and Markdown.\n- **Facts that are not about one repository** — knowledge that spans a\n  workspace instead of being pinned to a single checkout.\n- **Durable facts written out as plain Markdown**, readable without the CLI.\n- **`brain remember` from MCP**, so an agent can record a fact without shelling\n  out.\n- **Importing memory from another tool**, for people arriving with an existing\n  corpus.\n- **`brain stop` / `brain start`** pause and resume background work\n  machine-wide — one switch instead of hunting daemons per repository.\n- **Benchmarks**: index size and query latency against codebase size, and\n  `memory-ladder`, a five-condition probe of agent memory surfaces.\n\n### Changed\n\n- **Developer commands are hidden from default `--help`.** The everyday surface\n  is what a new user sees; the maintenance tree is still there when needed.\n- **`brief --json` puts facts and history before status**, so the first thing an\n  agent reads is the recalled knowledge rather than the health report. The\n  shipped guides now name `recall` explicitly.\n- **Time-weighted ranking** in retrieval: recent evidence outranks stale\n  evidence of equal relevance.\n- **Semantic generations verify once per file version**, not once per query.\n\n### Fixed\n\n- **An empty fact query now names the branches that do hold facts.** Facts are\n  branch-scoped, and an empty answer on `main` used to read as \"this was never\n  decided\" when the evidence simply lived on another branch.\n- **`remember` returns the persisted merged fact in its JSON**, so a caller sees\n  what was actually stored rather than what it sent.\n- **The ollama chunk-size limits are real**, and the advice that told users to\n  exceed them is corrected.\n\n### Documentation\n\n- A contributor concepts guide.\n- What we measure, what we found, and — explicitly — what we do not claim.\n- The install script is described by what it does rather than what it is not.\n- The twelve gap rows are re-scored against what actually shipped.\n\n\"\"\"\nopen(p,'w').write(s.replace(old,new,1))\nprint(\"drafted\")\nPY\necho \"  [Unreleased] now spans: $(awk '/^## \\[Unreleased\\]/{f=1} f&&/^## \\[0\\.1\\.0\\]/{print NR-start; exit} /^## \\[Unreleased\\]/{start=NR}' CHANGELOG.md) lines\"","description":"Draft the Unreleased changelog section"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":912,"cache_read_input_tokens":928411,"output_tokens":1302,"output_tokens_de