{"parentUuid":"0675e1de-ba73-4102-9c0a-2133db9fe8a6","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"89adaa3b-9317-4fc6-bc49-2439ccc56343","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UopnHKHfzs5vnf3MnSbEvA","type":"tool_result","content":"=== what does benchmarks_doc_test.go guard? ===\n  // docs/benchmarks.md is a page outsiders are invited to act on: it tells people\n  // evaluating Brain to stop trusting our numbers and run the commands\n  // themselves. A command on that page that does not exist, or a flag that was\n  // renamed, turns the invitation into an embarrassment at exactly the moment\n  // somebody took us up on it — and nothing else in the build would notice,\n  // because documentation does not compile.\n  // Writing this page was itself the proof: the first draft listed `facts eval`\n  // as a zero-configuration command (it requires --tasks) and invoked\n  // `eval-compare` with positional arguments (it takes --a and --b). Both were\n  // caught by running them, which is what this test now does every build.\n  // documentedBrainCommands pulls every `entire brain ...` invocation out of the\n  // fenced shell blocks.\n\n=== what does feature_matrix_test.go guard? ===\n  func TestFeatureMatrixProseMatchesTheData(t *testing.T) {\n  func TestFeatureMatrixLabelCountsAreCorrect(t *testing.T) {\n  func TestClosedGapRowsSayWhatShipped(t *testing.T) {\n  func TestFeatureMatrixMovedToYesCountMatchesTheData(t *testing.T) {\n  func TestPartialGapDetectionCoversBothProductColumns(t *testing.T) {\n  func TestFeatureMatrixDocumentationLinksResolve(t *testing.T) {\n  func TestFeatureMatrixShippedBrainCommandsExist(t *testing.T) {","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"35a1c2a0-6871-437e-aaf8-b9c9db460a38","timestamp":"2026-10-11T20:47:49.403Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"=== what does benchmarks_doc_test.go guard? ===\n  // docs/benchmarks.md is a page outsiders are invited to act on: it tells people\n  // evaluating Brain to stop trusting our numbers and run the commands\n  // themselves. A command on that page that does not exist, or a flag that was\n  // renamed, turns the invitation into an embarrassment at exactly the moment\n  // somebody took us up on it — and nothing else in the build would notice,\n  // because documentation does not compile.\n  // Writing this page was itself the proof: the first draft listed `facts eval`\n  // as a zero-configuration command (it requires --tasks) and invoked\n  // `eval-compare` with positional arguments (it takes --a and --b). Both were\n  // caught by running them, which is what this test now does every build.\n  // documentedBrainCommands pulls every `entire brain ...` invocation out of the\n  // fenced shell blocks.\n\n=== what does feature_matrix_test.go guard? ===\n  func TestFeatureMatrixProseMatchesTheData(t *testing.T) {\n  func TestFeatureMatrixLabelCountsAreCorrect(t *testing.T) {\n  func TestClosedGapRowsSayWhatShipped(t *testing.T) {\n  func TestFeatureMatrixMovedToYesCountMatchesTheData(t *testing.T) {\n  func TestPartialGapDetectionCoversBothProductColumns(t *testing.T) {\n  func TestFeatureMatrixDocumentationLinksResolve(t *testing.T) {\n  func TestFeatureMatrixShippedBrainCommandsExist(t *testing.T) {","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"45994a8e-c691-42d8-aa31-c9c3864f563e","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain","root":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain","branch":"HEAD","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"entireio","host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"},{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0675e1de-ba73-4102-9c0a-2133db9fe8a6","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"1eac9040-9610-45f1-aa43-df0931455a37","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"35a1c2a0-6871-437e-aaf8-b9c9db460a38","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14994919 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"b27ab49d-70be-4c19-9efe-6fd064169f58","timestamp":"2026-10-11T20:47:49.431Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14994919 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"1eac9040-9610-45f1-aa43-df0931455a37","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"b27ab49d-70be-4c19-9efe-6fd064169f58","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cfw78FizaMMNBvpaz5KJT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here's what the four docs PRs actually did — and two of them are more interesting than \"docs\".\n\n## #313 — benchmarks page that tests itself\n\n`docs/benchmarks.md` (+177) publishes what we measure, what we found, and **explicitly what we don't claim**. But it also shipped `benchmarks_doc_test.go` (+272), which extracts every `entire brain …` command from the page's fenced blocks and runs them each build. Its own comment explains why:\n\n> *\"A command on that page that does not exist, or a flag that was renamed, turns the invitation into an embarrassment at exactly the moment somebody took us up on it — and nothing else in the build would notice, because documentation does not compile.\"*\n\nAnd it earned its keep immediately: the first draft listed `facts eval` as zero-config (it needs `--tasks`) and called `eval-compare` with positional args (it takes `--a`/`--b`). Both caught by running them.\n\n**That's the fix for a whole defect class** — my backlog has `entire brain index` named in 10 error strings while the verb doesn't exist. Same disease, and #313 built the vaccine for the docs half of it.\n\n## #315 — feature matrix held to the data\n\nRe-scored the twelve gap rows against what shipped: `feature-matrix.csv` (52 rows rewritten), `feature-matrix.md`, plus `feature_matrix_test.go` (+305) asserting seven things, including:\n\n- the prose matches the CSV\n- the label counts are arithmetically right\n- **closed rows say what actually shipped**\n- documentation links resolve\n- **commands claimed as shipped actually exist**\n\nSo the matrix can't drift from reality, and \"we closed this gap\" can't be asserted without naming the thing that closed it.\n\n## #314 — one small, honest edit\n\nREADME +5/−3: describe what the install script *does*, rather than what it isn't. Tiny, and squarely in your \"simplify docs\" goal — a sentence defined by negation makes a reader work to extract the positive claim.\n\n## #332 — contributor concepts guide\n\n`docs/concepts.md` (+98) and `CONTRIBUTING.md` (+23): the vocabulary — brain, seed, facts, semantic index, history — in one place, so a new contributor isn't inferring terms from code.\n\n## Why this matters for your goals\n\nTwo of your four goals are \"simplify docs\" and \"easy first-run\". **#313 and #315 establish the pattern worth extending: documentation with an executable guard.** Most of my backlog's worst rows are exactly this failure — a string promising something untrue (`entire brain index`, the `entire enable` dirty hint, \"no MCP tool writes a fact\"). The docs now have a test for that; the *error strings and guides don't yet*.\n\nThat's the single highest-leverage thing to add before the release: extend the `benchmarks_doc_test.go` idea to every backticked command in `internal/cli` and in the generated agent guide.\n\nThe `[Unreleased]` draft is written — 61 lines covering all 24 PRs. The backlog re-validation is still running."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1055,"cache_read_input_tokens":931659,"output_tokens":1008,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1055,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1008,"cache_read_input_tokens":931659,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1055,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1055},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"6b434ea8-f777-492c-9665-5