{"parentUuid":"b4b045c7-1afa-4c77-8a32-8cadce26bbf5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cfw7XC2eXzLswsSt4Vb3Z","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FsKZtPtY8fTsdNrguNa2CQ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-ux-backlog\npython3 - <<'PY'\np='CHANGELOG.md'; s=open(p).read()\nold = \"\"\"- **Hosted memory.** `brain connect` binds a repository to its hosted store,\n  publishes the branch's facts, and merges the settled head back with\n  server-stamped authors, so a teammate's facts appear in your local brain. If\n  the publish grant is missing but the pull grant is not, it falls back to\n  pull-only rather than failing: you still receive the team's work.\"\"\"\nnew = \"\"\"- **Hosted memory (not yet usable — see below).** `brain connect` binds a\n  repository to its hosted store, publishes the branch's facts, and merges the\n  settled head back with server-stamped authors, so a teammate's facts appear in\n  your local brain. If the publish grant is missing but the pull grant is not, it\n  falls back to pull-only rather than failing.\n\n  **This must not ship in 0.2.0 as written.** Automatic binding shells out to\n  `entire repo whereami`, which the host CLI does not provide, so `brain connect`\n  with no flags cannot succeed on a first run and the error names a command that\n  does not exist. The auto-connect path then returns silently — alone among its\n  sibling gates, which all report — so the loop never engages and never says so.\n  The session-end hook calls it for two branches at a 30s timeout each, with no\n  negative cache. Fix, or hold the feature, before tagging.\"\"\"\nassert old in s, \"anchor missing\"\nopen(p,'w').write(s.replace(old,new,1))\nprint(\"  changelog corrected\")\nPY\ngit diff --stat CHANGELOG.md | sed 's/^/  /'","description":"Correct the changelog hosted-memory claim"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1232,"cache_read_input_tokens":941330,"output_tokens":1007,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":337},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1232,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1007,"cache_read_input_tokens":941330,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1232,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1232},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01FsKZtPtY8fTsdNrguNa2CQ":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-ux-backlog\npython3 - <<'PY'\np='CHANGELOG.md'; s=open(p).read()\nold = \"\"\"- **Hosted memory.** `brain connect` binds a repository to its hosted store,\n  publishes the branch's facts, and merges the settled head back with\n  server-stamped authors, so a teammate's facts appear in your local brain. If\n  the publish grant is missing but the pull grant is not, it falls back to\n  pull-only rather than failing: you still receive the team's work.\"\"\"\nnew = \"\"\"- **Hosted memory (not yet usable — see below).** `brain connect` binds a\n  repository to its hosted store, publishes the branch's facts, and merges the\n  settled head back with server-stamped authors, so a teammate's facts appear in\n  your local brain. If the publish grant is missing but the pull grant is not, it\n  falls back to pull-only rather than failing.\n\n  **This must not ship in 0.2.0 as written.** Automatic binding shells out to\n  `entire repo whereami`, which the host CLI does not provide, so `brain connect`\n  with no flags cannot succeed on a first run and the error names a command that\n  does not exist. The auto-connect path then returns silently — alone among