{"parentUuid":"09a385c9-a424-4b06-92c5-1de0a7e55d10","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cfw7bTWffYbMhrUErQEpG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0187T8M1EVvsQ8GAS7wztmJz","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Fix the inert hosted connect path","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"opus","prompt":"Fix three confirmed first-run defects in entire-brain's new hosted-sync surface. Work ONLY in /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-connect-fix (clean worktree, branch `fix/hosted-connect-fails-loudly`, based on origin/main @ e6bb5c42).\n\nESTABLISHED BY LIVE VERIFICATION — do not re-litigate, but do re-confirm anchors (line numbers may differ):\n- `brain connect` auto-resolution shells out to `entire repo whereami --json` (`connect_cmd.go:114-123`). **That command does not exist** in the host CLI: `entire repo` offers clone/create/delete/get/list/mirror/visibility. Confirmed live — it prints root usage. It is tagged COR-2029 and exists nowhere in the cli repo, not on main and not on any branch. So the host dependency is UNSHIPPED, not merely missing locally.\n- Consequence 1 (ND-1): `brain connect` with no flags cannot succeed on a first run, and its error names a command that does not exist (`connect_cmd.go:74`).\n- Consequence 2 (ND-2): the auto-connect path in `hosted_sync.go:~50-53` does `return nil` on that failure with NO stderr line — alone among its sibling gates (~:40,:57,:62,:67,:73), which all report. The team-memory loop silently never engages.\n- Consequence 3 (ND-3): the session-end hook (`hook_cmd.go:~148-161`) runs this for the current AND default branch, each at a 30s timeout (`hosted_token.go:15 hostedShellOutTimeout`), with no negative cache — up to 60s of shelling out to a missing command per session end. The code itself flags this: \"cache a negative result if that ever gets expensive\".\n\nWHAT TO BUILD — do NOT reimplement repo resolution. The right fix is honesty plus cost control:\n1. **Report instead of returning silently.** The auto-connect failure must print one stderr line like its siblings, saying hosted sync stayed local and why. The local brain is unaffected — say that too, so it does not read as data loss.\n2. **Negative cache.** Once resolution has failed, do not shell out again for the rest of the process (and ideally not for a short TTL across the session-end pair). The 60s-per-session-end stall is the user-visible cost. Keep it simple and obviously correct over clever.\n3. **Make the `connect` error actionable.** Today it names `entire repo whereami`, which does not exist. It must say that automatic binding needs a host CLI that provides it (COR-2029), and that the user can bind now with `--repo-id` and `--api-url`. Name the runnable path first.\n4. **Doc comments** that claim whereami exists as a host contract should say it is not shipped yet, so the next reader does not repeat my mistake of assuming it was merely missing locally.\n\nVERIFICATION — this is the deliverable, not the diff. CONTRIBUTING.md item 3 requires a test that fails without the fix, with the red output quoted. For EVERY guard: patch it compile-clean, run the test, capture it RED, quote the failing assertion, restore, confirm green. If a weakening yields zero failures, suspect your test first and grep to confirm the edit applied.\n\nRequired tests:\n- auto-connect failure prints a line naming the repo/branch and that the local brain is unaffected (weaken: restore `return nil` ⇒ red).\n- the resolver is invoked at most once per process after a failure (weaken: drop the cache ⇒ red, by counting runner invocations).\n- `connect` with no flags produces an error naming `--repo-id`/`--api-url` and NOT naming only a nonexistent command (weaken: restore the old message ⇒ red).\n\nCONVENTIONS (reuse, do not invent): `fakeCommandRunner` + `fakeCommandKey` (`export_test.go`); context idiom `(&cobra.Command{}).Context()`; assert error codes via their constants; `strings.Contains` for human output — there is no golden convention for it. `t.Setenv` + `t.Parallel()` PANICS, so keep env-setting tests serial.\n\nENV: no full suites — `GOMAXPROCS=1 go test ./internal/cli -run '^TestX$' -count=1 -p 1 -parallel 1`. `timeout` is absent on macOS; use `perl -e 'alarm N; exec @ARGV' <cmd>`. Piping to head/tail MASKS exit codes. NEVER `git stash`. NEVER run `entire brain setup` without `--no-daemon` — a scratch run rewrites the real launchd plist. `go build ./...` AND `go vet ./...` before finishing.\n\nYou may commit on this branch. Do NOT push, open a PR, merge, or approve anything. No AI attribution footers.\n\nOUTPUT: caveman-ultra compressed. What changed with file:line; a weakening table (guard | what you broke | test red | quoted assertion); build/vet; anything unverified. Facts only."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1907,"cache_read_input_tokens":947609,"output_tokens":1830,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1907,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1830,"cache_read_input_tokens":947609,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1907,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1907},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_0187T8M1EVvsQ8GAS7wztmJz":{"description":"Fix the inert hosted connect path","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"opus","prompt":"Fix three confirmed first-run defects in entire-brain's new hosted-sync surface. Work ONLY in /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-connect-fix (clean worktree, branch `fix/hosted-connect-fails-loudly`, 