{"parentUuid":"8e69ebc0-694b-4bd0-969a-8f2d7a1140cb","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cfw7fBpDMrN69uV3Uh87S","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Good news on that front — the structure is a deliberate stack, not orphaned work.\n\n## How #330/#331 actually reach main\n\nI had this backwards. They're **stacked**, not stranded:\n\n```\n#331 → merged into fix/multiagent-safety-indexing-windows\n#330 → that branch merged into fix/retrieval-output-correctness\n#329 → OPEN, fix/retrieval-output-correctness → main, 55 commits\n```\n\nSo **#329 is the ship vehicle for all three.** It carries #330's merge commit, which carries #331. One approval lands the lot — including the dirty-tree fixes behind UX-03/04/06.\n\nAnd it's mergeable right now: **55 ahead, 19 behind, zero conflicts** against current main.\n\nThat changes the plan for the better. I don't need to rewrite those backlog rows or construct new PRs — **#329 just needs review and a merge-forward.** Same for `fix/setup-traps` (#321), also open and clean.\n\n## Where that leaves the release path\n\n| what | state |\n|---|---|\n| **#329** (carries #330, #331) | open, 0 conflicts — needs your approval |\n| **#321** setup traps | open — needs your approval |\n| **`brain connect` blocker** | agent fixing now on `fix/hosted-connect-fails-loudly` |\n| **install-UX branch** | merged forward, verified, 0 behind, unpushed |\n| **changelog** | drafted, and corrected to flag hosted memory as not-shippable |\n\nI won't approve or merge any of those — that's yours. But **#329 is the single highest-value action available**, because one merge closes three of the backlog's worst rows.\n\nThe connect fix is still running; I'll report it verified, with its weakening evidence, when it lands."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1145,"cache_read_input_tokens":952724,"o