{"parentUuid":"a40c607a-931c-47b6-b666-59d3a91d0a54","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cfw8PfE9kUU5f9NiZomjh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EqDDPFRVAJAhFWiy5BzmTP","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Make the product's own advice runnable","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"opus","prompt":"Fix three confirmed defects in entire-brain that share one theme: **a string telling the user something untrue**. Work ONLY in /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-truthful-advice (clean worktree, branch `fix/runnable-advice`, based on origin/main @ e6bb5c42). Do not touch other worktrees — two other agents are working in them.\n\n### UX-02 — `entire brain index` does not exist, and 12 strings tell users to run it\nVerified live: `entire brain index` → `unknown command \"index\"`. The registered verb is `refresh index` (`semantic.go:~331`). Sites found in non-test code: `semantic.go` (890, 3233, 3324, 3410, 3477, 3569, 3635, 5901), `semantic_graph.go:154`, `bench_scale.go:270`, and `refresh.go:78` names an unrunnable `entire brain index --worktree` in a MarkDeprecated string. Re-confirm every site yourself; line numbers may differ.\nFix: point them all at `refresh index`, built through `setupCommandPrefix` / `setupBrainCommand` rather than a hardcoded literal (see UX-21 note below).\n**Also add the guard**, because this class will recur: a test that extracts every backticked `entire brain <verb>` / `entire-brain <verb>` from non-test source in `internal/cli` and asserts each resolves against the registered command tree. Precedent to copy, it already exists and works: `internal/cli/benchmarks_doc_test.go` does exactly this for `docs/benchmarks.md` — read it first and follow its shape. Its own comment explains the rationale (\"documentation does not compile\"); the same is true of error strings.\n\n### UX-05 — `.brainignore` is the real escape hatch and is named nowhere\nThe dirty-tree refusals (`seed.go:~276`, `semantic.go:~575`) say only \"without --worktree\". `.brainignore` is already loaded by the gate (`loadBrainIgnore`, `semantic.go:~2270`; gate `semantic.go:~2549`) and would clear a blocked user instantly — a real user with ~250 dirty research files was stuck for exactly this reason. It appears in **0** README lines and **0** error strings.\nFix: name `.brainignore` in both refusals alongside `--worktree`, and list the offending paths so the user can act. If the refusal already lists paths on this branch, reuse that; do not duplicate the logic.\n\n### UX-09 — the shipped guide contradicts the shipped binary\nBoth guide generators say *\"No MCP tool writes a fact, so this is a CLI call; do not go looking for one.\"* — `internal/agentsetup/guide.go:~67` and `strict.go:~160`. But `brain_remember` IS registered (`mcp.go:~906`, dispatch `~1166`).\nFix the text. **Then add the generator test**: assert that no guide claim contradicts the live MCP tool list. Note the irony to avoid repeating it — `mcp_remember_test.go` already guards *tool descriptions* from naming non-existent tools, but nothing guards the *guide* against denying tools that exist. Build the guard in the direction that is missing.\n\n### Constraint that applies to all three\nPrefer `setupCommandPrefix`/`setupBrainCommand` over hardcoded `entire brain ` literals — there are 101 such literals and no lint; do not add more. If a cheap lint/test banning new literals outside the invocation helper is natural while you are here, add it; if it would balloon the diff, skip it and say so.\n\n### VERIFICATION — the deliverable, not the diff\nCONTRIBUTING.md item 3 requires a test that fails without the fix, with the red output quoted. For EVERY guard: patch it compile-clean, run, capture RED, quote the failing assertion, restore, confirm green. A weakening that yields zero failures means suspect your test first — grep to confirm the edit applied before concluding the guard is unnecessary. Two \"unholdable guards\" in this codebase today turned out to be missing fixtures.\nRequired reds: (a) restore one `entire brain index` string ⇒ the new command-resolution test goes red; (b) remove `.brainignore` from a refusal ⇒ red; (c) restore the \"No MCP tool writes a fact\" sentence ⇒ the new generator test goes red.\n\n### CONVENTIONS — reuse, do not invent\n`fakeCommandRunner` + `fakeCommandKey` (`export_test.go`); context idiom `(&cobra.Command{}).Context()`; assert the error-code constant `dirtyWorktreeErrorCode`, never the bare literal; `strings.Contains` for human output (no golden convention for it); `t.Setenv` + `t.Parallel()` PANICS so keep env tests serial; narrative comments on tests quoting the real broken behaviour are house style.\n\n### ENV TRAPS\nNo full suites — `GOMAXPROCS=1 go test ./internal/cli -run '^TestX$' -count=1 -p 1 -parallel 1`. `timeout` absent on macOS: `perl -e 'alarm N; exec @ARGV' <cmd>`. Piping to head/tail MASKS exit codes. NEVER `git stash` (shared across worktrees). NEVER run `entire brain setup` without `--no-daemon` — a scratch run rewrites the real launchd plist. `go build ./...` AND `go vet ./...` before finishing.\n\nYou may commit on this branch. Do NOT push, open a PR, merge, or approve. No AI attribution footers.\n\nOUTPUT: caveman-ultra compressed. Per row: what changed, file:line. Then a weakening table (guard | what you broke | test red | quoted assertion). Then build/vet. Then anything unverified. Facts only, no preamble."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1622,"cache_read_input_tokens":954490,"output_tokens":2087,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1622},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2