{"parentUuid":"69cbac24-2801-46c9-8fe8-471ab94a332e","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"compact_file_reference","filename":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-ux-backlog/docs/install-ux-backlog.md","displayPath":"../brain-ux-backlog/docs/install-ux-backlog.md"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"cef6ab0f-1331-4c2b-a82a-ed3b452386b4","timestamp":"2026-10-11T21:09:26.000Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nNote: /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-ux-backlog/docs/install-ux-backlog.md was read before the last conversation was summarized, but the contents are too large to include. Use Read tool if you need to access it.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"1eac9040-9610-45f1-aa43-df0931455a37","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-connect-fix","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"cef6ab0f-1331-4c2b-a82a-ed3b452386b4","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-ux-backlog/scripts/try-first-run.sh","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-ux-backlog/scripts/try-first-run.sh","content":"#!/bin/sh\n# try-first-run.sh — walk the first-run flow in a THROWAWAY repo with isolated\n# state, so you can see what an external user sees without touching real work.\n#\n#   sh scripts/try-first-run.sh            # clean repo (the happy path)\n#   sh scripts/try-first-run.sh dirty      # repo with real uncommitted work\n#   sh scripts/try-first-run.sh empty      # repo with no sessions, no facts\n#\n# Everything lands under a temp dir and is isolated via XDG_*, so your real\n# brain, plugin registry and caches are untouched. Nothing here writes to a\n# repo you care about. Delete the temp dir and it never happened.\nset -u\n\nMODE=\"${1:-clean}\"\nROOT=\"$(mktemp -d)\"\nREPO=\"$ROOT/demo-repo\"\nexport XDG_DATA_HOME=\"$ROOT/xdg-data\"\nexport XDG_CONFIG_HOME=\"$ROOT/xdg-config\"\nexport XDG_STATE_HOME=\"$ROOT/xdg-state\"\nexport XDG_CACHE_HOME=\"$ROOT/xdg-cache\"\nmkdir -p \"$XDG_DATA_HOME/entire\" \"$REPO\"\n\n# The plugin registry lives under XDG_DATA_HOME. Isolating it entirely would\n# hide `entire graph` from brain and produce a provider error that looks like a\n# product bug but is an artefact of the harness — that exact false failure cost\n# an hour once. Link the real registry so the tools resolve; brain's per-repo\n# store still lands in the temp dir.\nln -s \"$HOME/.local/share/entire/plugins\" \"$XDG_DATA_HOME/entire/plugins\" 2>/dev/null\n\nsay() { printf '\\n\\033[1m=== %s\\033[0m\\n' \"$1\"; }\n\ncd \"$REPO\" || exit 1\ngit init -q .\ngit config user.email you@example.com\ngit config user.name You\nmkdir -p src docs\nprintf 'package main\\n\\nfunc main() {}\\n'            > src/main.go\nprintf '# Demo\\n\\nA small project.\\n'                 > README.md\nprintf '# Notes\\n\\nWhy we chose X over Y.\\n'          > docs/notes.md\ngit add -A && git commit -qm \"initial commit\"\n\ncase \"$MODE\" in\n  dirty)\n    # Real work in progress — the case that degraded a live install today.\n    printf '\\n// work in progress\\n' >> src/main.go\n    printf 'draft results\\n'          > docs/RESULTS.md\n    ;;\nesac\n\nsay \"0. where you are\"\necho \"repo:  $REPO\"\necho \"state: $(git status --porcelain | wc -l | tr -d ' ') uncommitted path(s)\"\n\nsay \"1. what a user is told to run first\"\n# --no-daemon is NOT cosmetic. The launchd daemon is NOT isolated by XDG: its\n# plist name is derived such that a throwaway repo REWRITES the real one in\n# ~/Library/LaunchAgents, repointing it at a temp dir that is about to be\n# deleted. That happened once while writing this script. Never drop this flag.\necho '$ entire brain setup --no-daemon'\nentire brain setup --no-daemon 2>&1\n\nsay \"2. did it actually work? (read the component row, not the headline)\"\necho '$ entire brain status'\nentire brain status 2>&1\n\nsay \"3. the first real question a user asks\"\necho '$ entire brain brief \"add retry logic to the client\"'\nentire brain brief \"add retry logic to the client\" 2>&1\n\necho\necho '$ entire brain overview'\nentire brain overview 2>&1\n\necho\necho '$ entire brain query \"why was X chosen\"'\nentire brain query \"why was X chosen\" 2>&1 | head -30\n\nsay \"4. the command the errors tell you to run next\"\necho '$ entire brain index        # 10 error strings name this verb'\nentire brain index 2>&1 | head -3\n\nsay \"5. the repair loop setup points you at\"\necho '$ entire brain doctor       # count the lines; count the ones you can act on'\nentire brain doctor 2>&1 | tee \"$ROOT/doctor.out\" | head -45\necho \"...\"\necho \"doctor printed $(wc -l < \"$ROOT/doctor.out\" | tr -d ' ') lines\"\n\nsay \"6. does an agent know this brain exists?\"\nfor f in AGENTS.md CLAUDE.md .entire/agent-guide.md .claude/settings.json; do\n  [ -e \"$f\" ] && echo \"  present: $f\" || echo \"  MISSING: $f\"\ndone\necho \"  (setup writes none of them; only \\`entire brain init-agents\\` does)\"\n\nsay \"7. how many commands is a new user facing?\"\necho \"  top-level verbs: $(entire brain --help 2>&1 | grep -cE '^  [a-z][a-z-]+ ')\"\necho \"  ways to ask a question: query, search, vsearch, get, multi-get, show, recall\"\n\ncat <<EOF\n\n────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nScratch dir: $ROOT\nDelete with: rm -rf \"$ROOT\"\n\nTry the other modes:\n  sh scripts/try-first-run.sh dirty    # uncommitted real work\n  sh scripts/try-first-run.sh clean    # nothing uncommitted\n────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nEOF\n","numLines":109,"startLine":1,"totalLines":109}},"displayPath":"../brain-ux-backlog/scripts/try-first-run.sh"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"92f3d20e-b376-48e6-9f2a-6cdfee1302ec","timestamp":"2026-10-11T21:09:26.000Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-ux-backlog/scripts/try-first-run.sh\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\t#!/bin/sh\n2\t# try-first-run.sh — walk the first-run flow in a THROWAWAY repo with isolated\n3\t# state, so you can see what an external user sees without touching real work.\n4\t#\n5\t#   sh scripts/try-first-run.sh            # clean repo (the happy path)\n6\t#   sh scripts/try-first-run.sh dirty      # repo with real uncommitted work\n7\t#   sh scripts/try-first-run.sh empty      # repo with no sessions, no facts\n8\t#\n9\t# Everything lands under a temp dir and is isolated via XDG_*, so your real\n10\t# brain, plugin registry and caches are untouched. Nothing here writes to a\n11\t# repo you care about. Delete the temp dir and it never happened.\n12\tset -u\n13\t\n14\tMODE=\"${1:-clean}\"\n15\tROOT=\"$(mktemp -d)\"\n16\tREPO=\"$ROOT/demo-repo\"\n17\texport XDG_DATA_HOME=\"$ROOT/xdg-data\"\n18\texport XDG_CONFIG_HOME=\"$ROOT/xdg-config\"\n19\texport XDG_STATE_HOME=\"$ROOT/xdg-state\"\n20\texport XDG_CACHE_HOME=\"$ROOT/xdg-cache\"\n21\tmkdir -p \"$XDG_DATA_HOME/entire\" \"$REPO\"\n22\t\n23\t# The plugin registry lives under XDG_DATA_HOME. Isolating it entirely would\n24\t# hide `entire graph` from brain and produce a provider error that looks like a\n25\t# product bug but is an artefact of the harness — that exact false failure cost\n26\t# an hour once. Link the real registry so the tools resolve; brain's per-repo\n27\t# store still lands in the temp dir.\n28\tln -s \"$HOME/.local/share/entire/plugins\" \"$XDG_DATA_HOME/entire/plugins\" 2>/dev/null\n29\t\n30\tsay() { printf '\\n\\033[1m=== %s\\033[0m\\n' \"$1\"; }\n31\t\n32\tcd \"$REPO\" || exit 1\n33\tgit init -q .\n34\tgit config user.email you@example.com\n35\tgit config user.name You\n36\tmkdir -p src docs\n37\tprintf 'package main\\n\\nfunc main() {}\\n'            > src/main.go\n38\tprintf '# Demo\\n\\nA small project.\\n'                 > README.md\n39\tprintf '# Notes\\n\\nWhy we chose X over Y.\\n'          > docs/notes.md\n40\tgit add -A && git commit -qm \"initial commit\"\n41\t\n42\tcase \"$MODE\" in\n43\t  dirty)\n44\t    # Real work in progress — the case that degraded a live install today.\n45\t    printf '\\n// work in progress\\n' >> src/main.go\n46\t    printf 'draft results\\n'          > docs/RESULTS.md\n47\t    ;;\n48\tesac\n49\t\n50\tsay \"0. where you are\"\n51\techo \"repo:  $REPO\"\n52\techo \"state: $(git status --porcelain | wc -l | tr -d ' ') uncommitted path(s)\"\n53\t\n54\tsay \"1. what a user is told to run first\"\n55\t# --no-daemon is NOT cosmetic. The launchd daemon is NOT isolated by XDG: its\n56\t# plist name is derived such that a throwaway repo REWRITES the real one in\n57\t# ~/Library/LaunchAgents, repointing it at a temp dir that is about to be\n58\t# deleted. That happened once while writing this script. Never drop this flag.\n59\techo '$ entire brain setup --no-daemon'\n60\tentire brain setup --no-daemon 2>&1\n61\t\n62\tsay \"2. did it actually work? (read the component row, not the headline)\"\n63\techo '$ entire brain status'\n64\tentire brain status 2>&1\n65\t\n66\tsay \"3. the first real question a user asks\"\n67\techo '$ entire brain brief \"add retry logic to the client\"'\n68\tentire brain brief \"add retry logic to the client\" 2>&1\n69\t\n70\techo\n71\techo '$ entire brain overview'\n72\tentire brain overview 2>&1\n73\t\n74\techo\n75\techo '$ entire brain query \"why was X chosen\"'\n76\tentire brain query \"why was X chosen\" 2>&1 | head -30\n77\t\n78\tsay \"4. the command the errors tell you to run next\"\n79\techo '$ entire brain index        # 10 error strings name this verb'\n80\tentire brain index 2>&1 | head -3\n81\t\n82\tsay \"5. the repair loop setup points you at\"\n83\techo '$ entire brain doctor       # count the lines; count the ones you can act on'\n84\tentire brain doctor 2>&1 | tee \"$ROOT/doctor.out\" | head -45\n85\techo \"...\"\n86\techo \"doctor printed $(wc -l < \"$ROOT/doctor.out\" | tr -d ' ') lines\"\n87\t\n88\tsay \"6. does an agent know this brain exists?\"\n89\tfor f in AGENTS.md CLAUDE.md .entire/agent-guide.md .claude/settings.json; do\n90\t  [ -e \"$f\" ] && echo \"  present: $f\" || echo \"  MISSING: $f\"\n91\tdone\n92\techo \"  (setup writes none of them; only \\`entire brain init-agents\\` does)\"\n93\t\n94\tsay \"7. how many commands is a new user facing?\"\n95\techo \"  top-level verbs: $(entire brain --help 2>&1 | grep -cE '^  [a-z][a-z-]+ ')\"\n96\techo \"  ways to ask a question: query, search, vsearch, get, multi-get, show, recall\"\n97\t\n98\tcat <<EOF\n99\t\n100\t────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n101\tScratch dir: $ROOT\n102\tDelete with: rm -rf \"$ROOT\"\n103\t\n104\tTry the other modes:\n105\t  sh scripts/try-first-run.sh dirty    # uncommitted real work\n106\t  sh scripts/try-first-run.sh clean    # nothing uncommitted\n107\t────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n108\tEOF\n109\t\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"1eac9040-9610-45f1-aa43-df0931455a37","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-connect-fix","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"92f3d20e-b376-48e6-9f2a-6cdfee1302ec","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"compact_file_reference","filename":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/mods/brain-memory/hooks/register.js","displayPath":"../.claude/mods/brain-memory/hooks/register.js"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"56b5923a-6566-4415-9da4-035af5fee40d","timestamp":"2026-10-11T21:09:26.000Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nNote: /Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/mods/brain-memory/hooks/register.js was read before the last conversation was summarized, but the contents are too large to include. Use Read tool if you need to access it.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"1eac9040-9610-45f1-aa43-df0931455a37","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-connect-fix","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"56b5923a-6566-4415-9da4-035af5fee40d","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"compact_file_reference","filename":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/mods/brain-memory/tests/brain-memory.test.ts","displayPath":"../.claude/mods/brain-memory/tests/brain-memory.test.ts"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"deaf88ed-1631-472a-9877-6d73d008d6a5","timestamp":"2026-10-11T21:09:26.000Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nNote: /Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/mods/brain-memory/tests/brain-memory.test.ts was read before the last conversation was summarized, but the contents are too large to include. Use Read tool if you need to access it.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"1eac9040-9610-45f1-aa43-df0931455a37","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-connect-fix","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"deaf88ed-1631-472a-9877-6d73d008d6a5","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/mods/brain-memory/README.md","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/mods/brain-memory/README.md","content":"# brain-memory\n\nA Claude Code mod that shows what Entire Brain actually contributed to each turn —\nand, more usefully, when it came back **empty** and why.\n\nBrain's value is invisible today. Facts get retrieved, the agent uses them or doesn't,\nand nobody sees either. The expensive case is the empty answer: an empty result nobody\nnotices is how a brain quietly stops being consulted while everyone still believes it works.\n\n## Use it\n\n```\n/brain-memory      opens the pane\n```\n\nEach row is one brain call, grouped by turn:\n\n```\nBrain memory   3 answered   2 empty\n\nthis turn ─────────────────────────────────\n+ query    semantic index lock      (10 results)\n· search   zzqqxx                   (nothing matched)\n    note: facts last distilled 2026-10-03 and all captured sessions are distilled\nturn 4 ────────────────────────────────────\n· get      fact:0000000000000000    (1 not found)\n```\n\n`+` answered · `·` empty · `!` the call failed or was refused.\n\nThe yellow line under an empty row is brain's own `blind_spot` — brain already explains\nwhy it had nothing, and that explanation is otherwise buried in a JSON payload no human\nreads. Empty and failed calls are also announced in the transcript, so they're noticed\nwith the pane closed. The spinner carries a running count.\n\nBoth routes count: the MCP tools (`mcp__entire-brain__*`) and the CLI through Bash\n(`entire brain …`, `entire-brain …`). The mod only observes — a tool result reaches\nClaude exactly as the tool returned it, pinned by a test.\n\n## Install\n\nAlready wired via `env.CLAUDE_CODE_PLUGIN_DIRS` in `~/.claude/settings.json`. To remove it,\ndelete that key. For one session instead:\n\n```\nclaude --plugin-dir /Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/mods/brain-memory\n```\n\nThe bare `CLAUDE_CODE_PLUGIN_DIRS` process environment variable did **not** load the mod in\na `claude -p` run here; the `settings.json` entry did. Use the settings entry.\n\n## State\n\nThe pane's rows live in `$.state` (`types/index.d.ts` declares the contract), not in module\nvariables. `register` runs again on every reload, so module variables start over — a pane that\nforgot every call each time the file was saved would be useless during exactly the work it\nsupports, and its empty state would then read as \"brain was never called\", the false negative\nthis mod exists to prevent. Writing `$.state` also redraws its readers, so the mod calls no\n`$.ui.invalidate`.\n\n`/clear`, `/resume` and `/branch` reset `$.state` by design, and calls made before the mod first\nloaded are invisible to it — which is why the empty state says \"since this pane started\nwatching\" rather than claiming none happened.\n\n## Develop\n\n```\nclaude plugin validate .\nclaude plugin test\n```\n\n## Two things that only showed up by running it\n\nA green suite and a passing `validate` both covered code that was broken in a live session.\nWorth knowing before changing `payloadTextOf` or `summarize`:\n\n1. **The payload is nested, differently per route.** The test kit documents a `tool.call`\n   stub of `{ result: '<text>' }`, and neither route produces that:\n\n   ```\n   Bash: { ref, result: { stdout: '<brain JSON>', stderr, persistedOutputPath, … }, text }\n   MCP:  { ref, result: [ { type: 'text', text: '<brain JSON>' } ], text }\n   ```\n\n   Reading `result.result` as the payload parses the *wrapper*, finds no `results` field,\n   and scores every empty answer as a hit — the exact failure this mod exists to surface.\n\n2. **Brain truncates its own replies and declares it.** A reply that does not fit a byte\n   budget drops TAIL ROWS, not characters, so the JSON stays valid and nothing looks wrong:\n\n   ```json\n   \"response_truncated\": true,\n   \"response_truncation\": { \"budget_bytes\": 32768,\n     \"dropped_from\": [ { \"path\": \"results\", \"returned\": 15, \"total\": 20 } ] }\n   ```\n\n   Counting the rows that arrived reports 15 where brain found 20, understating the\n   contribution this pane exists to show. The pane reads `dropped_from` and renders\n   `15 of 20 results` — matched by `path`, because a total borrowed from another field\n   would be a number brain never reported.\n\n3. **Bash payloads get truncated too, differently.** One real `entire brain query` here is 39 KB over 103\n   lines; the hook saw 80. Truncated JSON doesn't parse, and falling back to a line count\n   turns every truncated answer into a hit. So the mod reads `persistedOutputPath` when\n   Claude Code kept the full output, and otherwise classifies from the array's opening\n   (`\"results\": [` followed by `]` or `{`), which truncation never reaches.\n\nTests cover both with the envelopes captured from a running session. Every guard in the\nsuite has been verified by weakening — patch it compile-clean, watch the test go red.\n","numLines":110,"startLine":1,"totalLines":110}},"displayPath":"../.claude/mods/brain-memory/README.md"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"18921f56-bf18-42bb-b7d7-37f1bf1d9830","timestamp":"2026-10-11T21:09:26.000Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"/Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/mods/brain-memory/README.md\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\t# brain-memory\n2\t\n3\tA Claude Code mod that shows what Entire Brain actually contributed to each turn —\n4\tand, more usefully, when it came back **empty** and why.\n5\t\n6\tBrain's value is invisible today. Facts get retrieved, the agent uses them or doesn't,\n7\tand nobody sees either. The expensive case is the empty answer: an empty result nobody\n8\tnotices is how a brain quietly stops being consulted while everyone still believes it works.\n9\t\n10\t## Use it\n11\t\n12\t```\n13\t/brain-memory      opens the pane\n14\t```\n15\t\n16\tEach row is one brain call, grouped by turn:\n17\t\n18\t```\n19\tBrain memory   3 answered   2 empty\n20\t\n21\tthis turn ─────────────────────────────────\n22\t+ query    semantic index lock      (10 results)\n23\t· search   zzqqxx                   (nothing matched)\n24\t    note: facts last distilled 2026-10-03 and all captured sessions are distilled\n25\tturn 4 ────────────────────────────────────\n26\t· get      fact:0000000000000000    (1 not found)\n27\t```\n28\t\n29\t`+` answered · `·` empty · `!` the call failed or was refused.\n30\t\n31\tThe yellow line under an empty row is brain's own `blind_spot` — brain already explains\n32\twhy it had nothing, and that explanation is otherwise buried in a JSON payload no human\n33\treads. Empty and failed calls are also announced in the transcript, so they're noticed\n34\twith the pane closed. The spinner carries a running count.\n35\t\n36\tBoth routes count: the MCP tools (`mcp__entire-brain__*`) and the CLI through Bash\n37\t(`entire brain …`, `entire-brain …`). The mod only observes — a tool result reaches\n38\tClaude exactly as the tool returned it, pinned by a test.\n39\t\n40\t## Install\n41\t\n42\tAlready wired via `env.CLAUDE_CODE_PLUGIN_DIRS` in `~/.claude/settings.json`. To remove it,\n43\tdelete that key. For one session instead:\n44\t\n45\t```\n46\tclaude --plugin-dir /Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/mods/brain-memory\n47\t```\n48\t\n49\tThe bare `CLAUDE_CODE_PLUGIN_DIRS` process environment variable did **not** load the mod in\n50\ta `claude -p` run here; the `settings.json` entry did. Use the settings entry.\n51\t\n52\t## State\n53\t\n54\tThe pane's rows live in `$.state` (`types/index.d.ts` declares the contract), not in module\n55\tvariables. `register` runs again on every reload, so module variables start over — a pane that\n56\tforgot every call each time the file was saved would be useless during exactly the work it\n57\tsupports, and its empty state would then read as \"brain was never called\", the false negative\n58\tthis mod exists to prevent. Writing `$.state` also redraws its readers, so the mod calls no\n59\t`$.ui.invalidate`.\n60\t\n61\t`/clear`, `/resume` and `/branch` reset `$.state` by design, and calls made before the mod first\n62\tloaded are invisible to it — which is why the empty state says \"since this pane started\n63\twatching\" rather than claiming none happened.\n64\t\n65\t## Develop\n66\t\n67\t```\n68\tclaude plugin validate .\n69\tclaude plugin test\n70\t```\n71\t\n72\t## Two things that only showed up by running it\n73\t\n74\tA green suite and a passing `validate` both covered code that was broken in a live session.\n75\tWorth knowing before changing `payloadTextOf` or `summarize`:\n76\t\n77\t1. **The payload is nested, differently per route.** The test kit documents a `tool.call`\n78\t   stub of `{ result: '<text>' }`, and neither route produces that:\n79\t\n80\t   ```\n81\t   Bash: { ref, result: { stdout: '<brain JSON>', stderr, persistedOutputPath, … }, text }\n82\t   MCP:  { ref, result: [ { type: 'text', text: '<brain JSON>' } ], text }\n83\t   ```\n84\t\n85\t   Reading `result.result` as the payload parses the *wrapper*, finds no `results` field,\n86\t   and scores every empty answer as a hit — the exact failure this mod exists to surface.\n87\t\n88\t2. **Brain truncates its own replies and declares it.** A reply that does not fit a byte\n89\t   budget drops TAIL ROWS, not characters, so the JSON stays valid and nothing looks wrong:\n90\t\n91\t   ```json\n92\t   \"response_truncated\": true,\n93\t   \"response_truncation\": { \"budget_bytes\": 32768,\n94\t     \"dropped_from\": [ { \"path\": \"results\", \"returned\": 15, \"total\": 20 } ] }\n95\t   ```\n96\t\n97\t   Counting the rows that arrived reports 15 where brain found 20, understating the\n98\t   contribution this pane exists to show. The pane reads `dropped_from` and renders\n99\t   `15 of 20 results` — matched by `path`, because a total borrowed from another field\n100\t   would be a number brain never reported.\n101\t\n102\t3. **Bash payloads get truncated too, differently.** One real `entire brain query` here is 39 KB over 103\n103\t   lines; the hook saw 80. Truncated JSON doesn't parse, and falling back to a line count\n104\t   turns every truncated answer into a hit. So the mod reads `persistedOutputPath` when\n105\t   Claude Code kept the full output, and otherwise classifies from the array's opening\n106\t   (`\"results\": [` followed by `]` or `{`), which truncation never reaches.\n107\t\n108\tTests cover both with the envelopes captured from a running session. Every guard in the\n109\tsuite has been verified by weakening — patch it compile-clean, watch the test go red.\n110\t\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"1eac9040-9610-45f1-aa43-df0931455a37","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-connect-fix","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"18921f56-bf18-42bb-b7d7-37f1bf1d9830","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"task_status","taskId":"a8293cf1559e5a7b0","taskType":"local_agent","description":"Make the product's own advice runnable","status":"running","deltaSummary":"Inspecting bench_scale.go index-missing error","outputFilePath":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/1eac9040-9610-45f1-aa43-df0931455a37/tasks/a8293cf1559e5a7b0.output","canContinueAgent":true},"type":"attachment","uuid":"28d1be32-b884-4dcc-9ec4-a86c1d955b7d","timestamp":"2026-10-11T21:09:26.000Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nBackground agent \"Make the product's own advice runnable\" (a8293cf1559e5a7b0) is still running. Progress: Inspecting bench_scale.go index-missing error Do NOT spawn a duplicate. You will be notified when it completes. You can read partial output at /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/1eac9040-9610-45f1-aa43-df0931455a37/tasks/a8293cf1559e5a7b0.output or send it a message with SendMessage.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"1eac9040-9610-45f1-aa43-df0931455a37","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-connect-fix","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"28d1be32-b884-4dcc-9ec4-a86c1d955b7d","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"plan_file_reference","planFilePath":"/Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/dynamic-petting-globe.md","planContent":"# Make brain solid for a first-time external user — a tracked, verified loop\n\n## Context\n\nTwo complaints from a real early user, both reproduced in source and live:\n\n> *\"the brain install is really picky about there not being **ANY** changes in any files in git …\n> it's not the easiest to figure that out, could be me 😅\"*\n\n> *\"the brain facts import defaults to Codex, idk what model.\"*\n\nThen, today, a live first run on a real research repo ended:\n\n```\nBrain ready (degraded) in 7.7s\n  ✗ seed baseline: dirty_worktree: refusing to seed uncommitted content without --worktree\n  ✗ semantic index: dirty_worktree: refusing to index uncommitted content without --worktree\n  hint: commit or stash the working tree … `entire enable` writes .entire/ and .claude/\n        without committing them, which is what a first run usually trips over\n```\n\n**The hint was wrong.** That repo's dirt was ~250 real staged files — notebooks, models, figures,\nresults. `.entire/`, `AGENTS.md` and `CLAUDE.md` were not in `git status` at all. Re-running\n`setup` produced the identical result, and `setup` exposes no `--worktree` escape, so a user\nmid-work is permanently degraded and told to do something irrelevant to their problem.\n\n**Target user: someone outside the team installing fresh.** The bar is that they get a working\nbrain their agent actually uses, without reading source.\n\n**This is a standing loop, not a one-off PR.** Fix everything, keep a live list, verify each fix,\nand re-verify old ones later — in fresh sessions — so regressions surface instead of accumulating.\n\n---\n\n## The system (the real deliverable)\n\n### 1. A committed backlog — `docs/install-ux-backlog.md`\n\nOne row per defect, in the entire-brain repo so the team sees it and a fix PR can tick its own row:\n\n| field | meaning |\n|---|---|\n| `id` | stable (`UX-07`), referenced by commits and tests |\n| `severity` | blocker / major / minor, judged by *first-run* impact |\n| `symptom` | what the user sees, in their words — not the internal cause |\n| `anchor` | `file:line` |\n| `fix` | one line |\n| `status` | `open` → `fixed` → `verified` → (`regressed`) |\n| `check` | the exact command that proves it, re-runnable by anyone |\n| `last_verified` | date + how (weakening / fresh-env / both) |\n\n`symptom` is phrased from the outside on purpose: a list written in internal vocabulary\n(`memory_overlay`, `dirty_worktree`) re-creates the very problem we are fixing.\n\n### 2. The loop\n\nPick highest-severity `open` → fix → **weakening-verify** → **fresh-env verify** → set `verified`\nwith date and command. One PR per small batch; brain's constraint is review throughput, not\nauthorship (13 merged last week while 6 finished PRs queued), so batches stay reviewable.\n\n### 3. Fresh-env harness — `scripts/freshenv-check.sh`, committed\n\nEach check runs in a throwaway git repo with its own `XDG_DATA_HOME`/config, so no existing brain,\nplugin registry or cache leaks in. Committed so any session or subagent can run it unchanged.\n\n**Stated limit, up front:** this cannot catch \"the install instructions are wrong\", because the\nbinaries are already on the machine. Install-step defects need a real cold start and are marked\n`unverifiable-here` rather than silently passed. A harness that cannot fail the case it is\npointed at reports success — that failure mode has already bitten this work three times today.\n\n### 4. Regression sweep\n\nPeriodically, in a **fresh session**, a subagent re-runs the whole harness and flips any failing\nrow to `regressed`. Fresh matters: a session that made a fix is the worst judge of whether it\nholds.\n\n---\n\n## Verification bar (per row, no exceptions)\n\n1. **A test that fails on a compile-clean revert**, with the failing assertion quoted. Not an extra\n   step — CONTRIBUTING.md item 3 already requires it, and the PR must carry the red output.\n2. **A fresh-env check** that reproduces the user-visible symptom and shows it gone.\n3. **A negative control** wherever the fix could over-apply. The dirty-gate fix is the archetype:\n   without \"a dirty *source* file is still refused\", a passing check is indistinguishable from\n   having switched the safety off.\n4. If a weakening produces **zero** failures, suspect the test first and grep to confirm the edit\n   applied. Two \"unholdable guards\" today were missing fixtures, not missing bugs.\n\n---\n\n## Rows already established (seed the backlog with these)\n\n**Blockers — a first-run user is stuck**\n- `setup` has no `--worktree` escape; a user with legitimate WIP is degraded forever with no\n  forward path from inside `setup`.\n- The dirty-tree hint is wrong whenever the dirt is not Entire's own files — the live case above.\n- Entire's own installers (`init-agents`, `entire enable`) write files that then block the install.\n  **Fix built and verified: branch `fix/install-ux-dirty-gate-and-agent-default` @ `3cc936ad`.**\n\n**Major — silent wrong behaviour**\n- Agent default silently picks codex over the harness the user is in, and never says which. *Fixed\n  on the same branch.*\n- The model is never named — *\"idk what model\"* stays literally true. *Fixed on the same branch\n  by stating it, without hardcoding an id that ages.*\n- `daemonEnv` carries no harness signal, so the unattended daemon still resolves codex-first.\n- Facts are branch-scoped: `recall` on `main` reads empty while the facts sit on another branch.\n- Six CLI verbs have no MCP tool — `recall`, `verify`, `overview`, `entities`, `show`, `guide`.\n  `recall` is the worst: the shipped guide *mandates* it and an MCP-only agent cannot call it.\n- The shipped guide says *\"No MCP tool writes a fact\"* while the same build registers\n  `brain_remember`.\n\n**Major — the product talks to itself, not the user**\n- `doctor` prints 35 lines, mostly internal schema names, returning 5 warn + 1 error on a brain\n  that works. A diagnostic that cries wolf on a healthy system trains people to ignore it.\n- 43 top-level verbs, including **seven** ways to ask a question (`query`, `search`, `vsearch`,\n  `get`, `multi-get`, `show`, `recall`).\n- `setup` 12 flags, `distill` 15.\n- `init-agents` — the step that makes an agent use brain at all — is absent from the setup flow\n  and from Overview → Set Up Your Repository.\n\nThree audits (first-run flow, agent usage, surface simplification) are running and will append\ntheir findings with `file:line` and severity. The list above is the floor, not the total.\n\n---\n\n## First increment\n\nThe branch is **already built and verified**: 24 weakenings all red-then-green, indexing filter\nuntouched, and a live before/after on a real repo —\n\n```\nBEFORE  exit=1  seed baseline failed / dirty_worktree\nAFTER   exit=0  seed baseline done · semantic index: 2 symbols, 2 relations, 2 files\nCONTROL dirty source file → still refused\n```\n\n**It needs a rebase before it ships.** It sits on `6c8ebdab` while #318, #320, #331, #332 and #334\nhave merged since — and #332 touched the same guide and hook code. **Blocked on `git fetch`**,\nwhich needs working DNS (see below).\n\n## Files\n\n| path | change |\n|---|---|\n| `docs/install-ux-backlog.md` | new — the live list |\n| `scripts/freshenv-check.sh` | new — throwaway repo + isolated dirs, one check per row |\n| `internal/cli/semantic.go`, `seed.go`, `refresh.go`, `setup.go`, `watch.go`, `distill_cmd.go` | the fixes, in small batches |\n| `internal/cli/mcp.go` | MCP parity for the missing verbs |\n| `internal/cli/doctor*.go` | user-facing subset; internals behind `--verbose` |\n\n## Verification\n\n1. `scripts/freshenv-check.sh` green for every `verified` row.\n2. Each fix's weakening evidence quoted in its PR.\n3. A fresh-session regression sweep re-runs the harness and flips failures to `regressed`.\n4. The end-to-end that matters: a throwaway repo → `entire graph init-agents` →\n   `entire brain setup` → first `brain query` returns something useful, with **no** degraded\n   components and **no** advice that does not apply.\n\n## Known blocker, stated plainly\n\n`opendirectoryd` is unreachable from this process tree: no DNS, no keychain, `whoami` → `501`.\nSo `git fetch`, `gh` and the trail CLI all fail, and the rebase cannot happen from here. Disabling\nthe Claude Code sandbox did **not** fix it, which ruled out the sandbox as the cause. Everything\nelse in this plan proceeds offline; the rebase waits for a shell with a working bootstrap context.\n\n## Not doing\n\nMerging, approving or pushing without explicit approval. No model id hardcoded — `setup.go` already\nrecords why (\"model ids age badly\"), and that reasoning stands.\n"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"b9cb7981-4763-4462-bec6-41cdbe974ba3","timestamp":"2026-10-11T21:09:26.001Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nA plan file exists from plan mode at: /Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/dynamic-petting-globe.md\n\nPlan contents:\n\n# Make brain solid for a first-time external user — a tracked, verified loop\n\n## Context\n\nTwo complaints from a real early user, both reproduced in source and live:\n\n> *\"the brain install is really picky about there not being **ANY** changes in any files in git …\n> it's not the easiest to figure that out, could be me 😅\"*\n\n> *\"the brain facts import defaults to Codex, idk what model.\"*\n\nThen, today, a live first run on a real research repo ended:\n\n```\nBrain ready (degraded) in 7.7s\n  ✗ seed baseline: dirty_worktree: refusing to seed uncommitted content without --worktree\n  ✗ semantic index: dirty_worktree: refusing to index uncommitted content without --worktree\n  hint: commit or stash the working tree … `entire enable` writes .entire/ and .claude/\n        without committing them, which is what a first run usually trips over\n```\n\n**The hint was wrong.** That repo's dirt was ~250 real staged files — notebooks, models, figures,\nresults. `.entire/`, `AGENTS.md` and `CLAUDE.md` were not in `git status` at all. Re-running\n`setup` produced the identical result, and `setup` exposes no `--worktree` escape, so a user\nmid-work is permanently degraded and told to do something irrelevant to their problem.\n\n**Target user: someone outside the team installing fresh.** The bar is that they get a working\nbrain their agent actually uses, without reading source.\n\n**This is a standing loop, not a one-off PR.** Fix everything, keep a live list, verify each fix,\nand re-verify old ones later — in fresh sessions — so regressions surface instead of accumulating.\n\n---\n\n## The system (the real deliverable)\n\n### 1. A committed backlog — `docs/install-ux-backlog.md`\n\nOne row per defect, in the entire-brain repo so the team sees it and a fix PR can tick its own row:\n\n| field | meaning |\n|---|---|\n| `id` | stable (`UX-07`), referenced by commits and tests |\n| `severity` | blocker / major / minor, judged by *first-run* impact |\n| `symptom` | what the user sees, in their words — not the internal cause |\n| `anchor` | `file:line` |\n| `fix` | one line |\n| `status` | `open` → `fixed` → `verified` → (`regressed`) |\n| `check` | the exact command that proves it, re-runnable by anyone |\n| `last_verified` | date + how (weakening / fresh-env / both) |\n\n`symptom` is phrased from the outside on purpose: a list written in internal vocabulary\n(`memory_overlay`, `dirty_worktree`) re-creates the very problem we are fixing.\n\n### 2. The loop\n\nPick highest-severity `open` → fix → **weakening-verify** → **fresh-env verify** → set `verified`\nwith date and command. One PR per small batch; brain's constraint is review throughput, not\nauthorship (13 merged last week while 6 finished PRs queued), so batches stay reviewable.\n\n### 3. Fresh-env harness — `scripts/freshenv-check.sh`, committed\n\nEach check runs in a throwaway git repo with its own `XDG_DATA_HOME`/config, so no existing brain,\nplugin registry or cache leaks in. Committed so any session or subagent can run it unchanged.\n\n**Stated limit, up front:** this cannot catch \"the install instructions are wrong\", because the\nbinaries are already on the machine. Install-step defects need a real cold start and are marked\n`unverifiable-here` rather than silently passed. A harness that cannot fail the case it is\npointed at reports success — that failure mode has already bitten this work three times today.\n\n### 4. Regression sweep\n\nPeriodically, in a **fresh session**, a subagent re-runs the whole harness and flips any failing\nrow to `regressed`. Fresh matters: a session that made a fix is the worst judge of whether it\nholds.\n\n---\n\n## Verification bar (per row, no exceptions)\n\n1. **A test that fails on a compile-clean revert**, with the failing assertion quoted. Not an extra\n   step — CONTRIBUTING.md item 3 already requires it, and the PR must carry the red output.\n2. **A fresh-env check** that reproduces the user-visible symptom and shows it gone.\n3. **A negative control** wherever the fix could over-apply. The dirty-gate fix is the archetype:\n   without \"a dirty *source* file is still refused\", a passing check is indistinguishable from\n   having switched the safety off.\n4. If a weakening produces **zero** failures, suspect the test first and grep to confirm the edit\n   applied. Two \"unholdable guards\" today were missing fixtures, not missing bugs.\n\n---\n\n## Rows already established (seed the backlog with these)\n\n**Blockers — a first-run user is stuck**\n- `setup` has no `--worktree` escape; a user with legitimate WIP is degraded forever with no\n  forward path from inside `setup`.\n- The dirty-tree hint is wrong whenever the dirt is not Entire's own files — the live case above.\n- Entire's own installers (`init-agents`, `entire enable`) write files that then block the install.\n  **Fix built and verified: branch `fix/install-ux-dirty-gate-and-agent-default` @ `3cc936ad`.**\n\n**Major — silent wrong behaviour**\n- Agent default silently picks codex over the harness the user is in, and never says which. *Fixed\n  on the same branch.*\n- The model is never named — *\"idk what model\"* stays literally true. *Fixed on the same branch\n  by stating it, without hardcoding an id that ages.*\n- `daemonEnv` carries no harness signal, so the unattended daemon still resolves codex-first.\n- Facts are branch-scoped: `recall` on `main` reads empty while the facts sit on another branch.\n- Six CLI verbs have no MCP tool — `recall`, `verify`, `overview`, `entities`, `show`, `guide`.\n  `recall` is the worst: the shipped guide *mandates* it and an MCP-only agent cannot call it.\n- The shipped guide says *\"No MCP tool writes a fact\"* while the same build registers\n  `brain_remember`.\n\n**Major — the product talks to itself, not the user**\n- `doctor` prints 35 lines, mostly internal schema names, returning 5 warn + 1 error on a brain\n  that works. A diagnostic that cries wolf on a healthy system trains people to ignore it.\n- 43 top-level verbs, including **seven** ways to ask a question (`query`, `search`, `vsearch`,\n  `get`, `multi-get`, `show`, `recall`).\n- `setup` 12 flags, `distill` 15.\n- `init-agents` — the step that makes an agent use brain at all — is absent from the setup flow\n  and from Overview → Set Up Your Repository.\n\nThree audits (first-run flow, agent usage, surface simplification) are running and will append\ntheir findings with `file:line` and severity. The list above is the floor, not the total.\n\n---\n\n## First increment\n\nThe branch is **already built and verified**: 24 weakenings all red-then-green, indexing filter\nuntouched, and a live before/after on a real repo —\n\n```\nBEFORE  exit=1  seed baseline failed / dirty_worktree\nAFTER   exit=0  seed baseline done · semantic index: 2 symbols, 2 relations, 2 files\nCONTROL dirty source file → still refused\n```\n\n**It needs a rebase before it ships.** It sits on `6c8ebdab` while #318, #320, #331, #332 and #334\nhave merged since — and #332 touched the same guide and hook code. **Blocked on `git fetch`**,\nwhich needs working DNS (see below).\n\n## Files\n\n| path | change |\n|---|---|\n| `docs/install-ux-backlog.md` | new — the live list |\n| `scripts/freshenv-check.sh` | new — throwaway repo + isolated dirs, one check per row |\n| `internal/cli/semantic.go`, `seed.go`, `refresh.go`, `setup.go`, `watch.go`, `distill_cmd.go` | the fixes, in small batches |\n| `internal/cli/mcp.go` | MCP parity for the missing verbs |\n| `internal/cli/doctor*.go` | user-facing subset; internals behind `--verbose` |\n\n## Verification\n\n1. `scripts/freshenv-check.sh` green for every `verified` row.\n2. Each fix's weakening evidence quoted in its PR.\n3. A fresh-session regression sweep re-runs the harness and flips failures to `regressed`.\n4. The end-to-end that matters: a throwaway repo → `entire graph init-agents` →\n   `entire brain setup` → first `brain query` returns something useful, with **no** degraded\n   components and **no** advice that does not apply.\n\n## Known blocker, stated plainly\n\n`opendirectoryd` is unreachable from this process tree: no DNS, no keychain, `whoami` → `501`.\nSo `git fetch`, `gh` and the trail CLI all fail, and the rebase cannot happen from here. Disabling\nthe Claude Code sandbox did **not** fix it, which ruled out the sandbox as the cause. Everything\nelse in this plan proceeds offline; the rebase waits for a shell with a working bootstrap context.\n\n## Not doing\n\nMerging, approving or pushing without explicit approval. No model id hardcoded — `setup.go` already\nrecords why (\"model ids age badly\"), and that reasoning stands.\n\n\nIf this plan is relevant to the current work and not already complete, continue working on it.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"1eac9040-9610-45f1-aa43-df0931455a37","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-connect-fix","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
