-8d83-772b3e7d7ef8","timestamp":"2026-10-11T21:09:45.608Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"1eac9040-9610-45f1-aa43-df0931455a37","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-truthful-advice","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"575d62b8-944e-4228-8d83-772b3e7d7ef8","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"b1331e42-5b90-45b6-9c58-e0c78213a423","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011XD3WxyN5oUXc4AVQr79fU","type":"tool_result","content":"UX-01   A throwaway `setup` **overwrites the real launchd daemon**, repointing it at a temp dir that then disappears. Trying brain in a scratch repo breaks your actual install. Observed while writing the harness.            daemon name derivation; `setup.go:838-857`\nUX-02   Ten error messages tell you to run **`entire brain index`**, which does not exist. Verified: `unknown command \"index\"`. It is the first thing a degraded user reaches for.            `semantic.go:890,3233,3324,3410,3477,3569,3635,5901`; `semantic_graph.go\nUX-03   Uncommitted work ⇒ seed **and** semantic both fail, and `setup` has **no** `--worktree`, `--include-uncommitted` or `--force`. There is no forward path from inside `setup`.            `setup.go:470-482`\nUX-04   The dirty hint blames `entire enable`'s files. For anyone whose dirt is their own work it is **confidently wrong** — a live case had ~250 staged notebooks/models/figures and none of Entire's files. It reaches the user three times.            hint `setup.go:133-136`; matcher `setup.go:211-213`; reused `status_rend\nUX-05   **`.brainignore` is the real escape hatch and is named nowhere** — 0 mentions in errors, 0 in README. It is already loaded by the gate and would have cleared the live case instantly.            gate `semantic.go:2537-2551`; loader `semantic.go:2271`\nUX-06   `refresh --worktree` **cannot repair a degraded brain** — it turns the semantic stage off unconditionally. The note then recommends the one command that will fail again.            skip `refresh.go:55-59`; note `refresh.go:648-650`\nUX-07   `setup` writes **no guide, no pointer, no MCP registration, no hook**, and prints no next step. A setup-only repo is invisible to every agent. `setup.go` has zero references to `agentsetup`.            `setup.go` (whole); `agent_setup.go:13`\nUX-08   Our own installers write files that then block our own install.            `entireAuthoredGatePaths`\nUX-09   The guide tells agents *\"No MCP tool writes a fact; do not go looking for one\"* while the same build registers `brain_remember`.            `agentsetup/strict.go:155-156`; `guide.go:57`; tool at `mcp.go:905`\nUX-10   The guide **mandates** `recall` and `verify`, and a once-per-session `version` + `capabilities` preflight. **None of those four are MCP tools.** The mandate is unfollowable for an MCP-only agent.            `strict.go:108-109,137-146`\nUX-11   Empty `recall` on `main` blames distillation coverage. The real cause — facts live on another branch — is in **none** of the five blind-spot branches. The agent concludes the decision never existed.            `blind_spot.go:34-66`\nUX-12   Bare empty results with no explanation: `brain_patterns` `[]` (the \"not built vs none found\" distinction exists only in text mode), `brain_query_graph` (no blind spot, no freshness), `brain_impact`/`tests`/`boundaries` (empty reads as \"no callers\"), `brain_trace_path` (never says depth defaulted to 4), `brain_dead_code`, `brain_get` `missing[]`.            `patterns_cmd.go:124`; `semantic_graph.go:456,735,936`; `semantic.go:357\nUX-13   Truncation is declared **only** for the byte-budget trim. Per-tool `limit` defaults (10/5/3/20), SQL `LIMIT`s and slice cuts are all silent, and `brain_code`/`brain_context` paginate with no `total`/`has_more`.            `mcp.go:1062-1073`; `semantic_graph.go:340-352,635-636`; `semantic.go:44\nUX-14   Installed binary renders a **32768**-byte budget; the repo constant is **131072**. Live truncation bites 4× sooner than source implies. Installed build is Sep 21.            `mcp_response_budget.go:16`\nUX-15   `brief` on an empty brain prints three lines and never says why. Its one applicable warning is gated behind `Sources.Sessions != nil`, which is nil on a zero-session repo — so it **cannot fire**.            guard `agent_surface.go:1636`\nUX-16   `overview` on a built-but-empty brain omits every section; its \"not built yet\" warning needs `GeneratedAt.IsZero()`, false the moment setup writes a manifest, so it **can never fire after a first run**. Reads as broken.            `agent_surface.go:514,624-700`\nUX-17   MCP server `instructions` carry only the byte-budget contract — nothing says what brain is or when to call it. Tool descriptions are mechanism (\"Return/List/Search X\"), never trigger. `brain_brief` never says \"call first\".            `mcp.go:664-668`, `:806-990`\nUX-18   `hook pre-edit` is wired by **neither** `setup` nor `init-agents`; the docs admit it has \"no effect\" until a harness wires it. It also takes `--file` while PreToolUse delivers JSON on stdin.            `hook_cmd.go:15-17,183-196`\nUX-19   `--no-daemon` and `--no-backfill` are **not persisted**. A user who declined the daemon, then follows \"re-run setup\", silently gets a persistent login service and a token spend.            `setup.go:1308-1321,1360-1389`\nUX-20   Re-running `setup` cannot learn: identical output, no comparison with the previous record, no escalation.            write `setup.go:668`; readers `setup_status.go:159`\nUX-21   ~28 remedies hardcode `entire brain …` instead of `setupCommandPrefix`, so on one install shape the printed command is unrunnable.            `agent_surface.go`, `lifecycle_ops.go`, `memory_admin.go`, `semantic.go`\nUX-22   `doctor` prints **40 lines / 6.4 KB**, 34 ok + 5 warn, on a healthy brain. **Of 6 non-ok lines, 1 names a remedy.** Three checks are constant `\"ok\"` literals that can never fail. No `--verbose` exists.            `lifecycle_ops.go:109-320`; constants `:123,:161,:181`; `doctor.go:113-1\nUX-23   **46 verbs / ~127 invocable commands**, incl. **seven** ways to ask a question (`query`, `search`, `vsearch`, `get`, `multi-get`, `show`, `recall`). `search`/`vsearch` are literally `query --keyword` / `--semantic`, same constructor.            `root.go:98-185`; `retrieve_cmd.go:71-81`\nUX-24   A first `setup` prints **~65 lines**, ~24 of them the inner `refresh` leaking through. Duplicate consent text; two different names for the same component in one run; a hashed daemon id surfaced.            `setup.go:1254-1257,634,913`; `setup_render.go:197,268`\nUX-25   \"Brain ready (degraded) … the brain is queryable now\" prints even when seed **and** semantic both failed — i.e. no code index and no baseline. Exit 0.            `setup_render.go:149-158`\nUX-26   `status` has the Detail and Hint for each failed component but prints only the names.            `status_render.go:472-490`\nUX-27   A dirty tree prints **two contradictory remedies at once** — \"commit or stash\" in the verdict, \"refresh with `--worktree`\" in the cause underneath.            `status_render.go:320`; `agent_surface.go:4634`\nUX-28   Dead surface a user can trip over: `refresh seed --interactive` is registered and **never read**; `distill --jobs` is a self-conflicting alias; 9 verbs have zero README mentions; the docs contract test is one-directional.            `seed.go:238`; `distill_cmd.go:606`; `documented_commands_test.go:14`\nUX-29   Misleading names: `path` is a print verb that **builds** via `--ensure`; `add` means clone but collides with `workspace add`; `dash`/`viz`/`inspect graph-ui` are three visualizers; `repair`/`reset`/`memory repair`/`memory rebuild` are four names for one job; `stats` is one character from `status`.            `path.go:29`; `add.go:21`; `dash.go:38`; `viz.go:62`; `semantic.go:353,3\nUX-30   Remedies that cannot be followed: `--graph-binary` is named but is not a `setup` flag; \"install with `scripts/install.sh` from the checkout\" is false for plugin installs; \"delete the setup record\" is destructive advice on a transient read error.            `semantic.go:1228,1302`; `setup.go:533`","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"5ac523ff-fc6b-41ae-9141-3