{"parentUuid":"bc2a7fde-1c0b-4c9b-b1dd-029dff5fd026","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"b1331e42-5b90-45b6-9c58-e0c78213a423","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SmwAGN23UBKV5cJ6uEEnj1","type":"tool_result","content":"────── UX-07\nSYMPTOM: `setup` writes **no guide, no pointer, no MCP registration, no hook**, and prints no next step. A setup-only repo is invisible to every agent. `setup.go` has zero references to `agentsetup`.\nANCHOR:  `setup.go` (whole); `agent_setup.go:13`\nFIX:     End `setup` by running `init-agents`, or at minimum print it as the next step.\n────── UX-18\nSYMPTOM: `hook pre-edit` is wired by **neither** `setup` nor `init-agents`; the docs admit it has \"no effect\" until a harness wires it. It also takes `--file` while PreToolUse delivers JSON on stdin.\nANCHOR:  `hook_cmd.go:15-17,183-196`\nFIX:     Have `init-agents` merge a PreToolUse entry; accept stdin; emit the hook JSON envelope.\n────── UX-19\nSYMPTOM: `--no-daemon` and `--no-backfill` are **not persisted**. A user who declined the daemon, then follows \"re-run setup\", silently gets a persistent login service and a token spend.\nANCHOR:  `setup.go:1308-1321,1360-1389`\nFIX:     Persist both.\n────── UX-22\nSYMPTOM: `doctor` prints **40 lines / 6.4 KB**, 34 ok + 5 warn, on a healthy brain. **Of 6 non-ok lines, 1 names a remedy.** Three checks are constant `\"ok\"` literals that can never fail. No `--verbose` exists.\nANCHOR:  `lifecycle_ops.go:109-320`; constants `:123,:161,:181`; `doctor.go:113-114`\nFIX:     Cut to ≤8 actionable lines; everything else behind `--verbose`; `--json` unchanged. Delete the three checks that cannot fail.\n────── UX-24\nSYMPTOM: A first `setup` prints **~65 lines**, ~24 of them the inner `refresh` leaking through. Duplicate consent text; two different names for the same component in one run; a hashed daemon id surfaced.\nANCHOR:  `setup.go:1254-1257,634,913`; `setup_render.go:197,268`\nFIX:     Pass `io.Discard` to the nested refresh when not `--json`.\n────── UX-25\nSYMPTOM: \"Brain ready (degraded) … the brain is queryable now\" prints even when seed **and** semantic both failed — i.e. no code index and no baseline. Exit 0.\nANCHOR:  `setup_render.go:149-158`\nFIX:     Say what is unavailable; keep exit 0 but stop asserting queryability it lacks.\n────── UX-26\nSYMPTOM: `status` has the Detail and Hint for each failed component but prints only the names.\nANCHOR:  `status_render.go:472-490`\nFIX:     Print Detail under each failure.\n────── UX-27\nSYMPTOM: A dirty tree prints **two contradictory remedies at once** — \"commit or stash\" in the verdict, \"refresh with `--worktree`\" in the cause underneath.\nANCHOR:  `status_render.go:320`; `agent_surface.go:4634`\nFIX:     One remedy resolver.\n────── UX-28\nSYMPTOM: Dead surface a user can trip over: `refresh seed --interactive` is registered and **never read**; `distill --jobs` is a self-conflicting alias; 9 verbs have zero README mentions; the docs contract test is one-directional.\nANCHOR:  `seed.go:238`; `distill_cmd.go:606`; `documented_commands_test.go:14`\nFIX:     Delete the dead flag; make the docs test bidirectional.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"40860909-9b9a-4a4c-8905-c87489ad1789","timestamp":"2026-10-11T21:10:47.800Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"────── UX-07\nSYMPTOM: `setup` writes **no guide, no pointer, no MCP registration, no hook**, and prints no next step. A setup-only repo is invisible to every agent. `setup.go` has zero references to `agentsetup`.\nANCHOR:  `setup.go` (whole); `agent_setup.go:13`\nFIX:     End `setup` by running `init-agents`, or at minimum print it as the next step.\n────── UX-18\nSYMPTOM: `hook pre-edit` is wired by **neither** `setup` nor `init-agents`; the docs admit it has \"no effect\" until a harness wires it. It also takes `--file` while PreToolUse delivers JSON on stdin.\nANCHOR:  `hook_cmd.go:15-17,183-196`\nFIX:     Have `init-agents` merge a PreToolUse entry; accept stdin; emit the 