{"parentUuid":"897b315c-14a2-460e-8d95-337a84ffd6dd","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cfw8srY5JVYsqKRZf7CYD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WfMJC5krXkTF2Lj2C7Et1p","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Setup/status output truth","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"opus","prompt":"WORKTREE: /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-ux-a-output  (branch fix/setup-status-output-truth, off origin/main e6bb5c42). Work ONLY there. Never cd to another checkout.\n\nRepo: entireio/entire-brain (Go). You are fixing four rows of docs/install-ux-backlog.md so a FIRST-TIME EXTERNAL USER is not misled by what setup/status print.\n\nUX-24 — a first `setup` prints ~65 lines, ~24 of them the inner `refresh` leaking through: duplicate consent text, two different names for the same component in one run, a hashed daemon id surfaced.\n  anchors: setup.go:1254-1257, :634, :913; setup_render.go:197, :268\n  fix: pass io.Discard to the nested refresh when NOT --json. Also kill the duplicate consent text, unify the component name, stop surfacing the hashed daemon id.\n\nUX-25 — \"Brain ready (degraded) … the brain is queryable now\" prints even when seed AND semantic both failed (no code index, no baseline). Exit 0.\n  anchor: setup_render.go:149-158\n  fix: say what is unavailable; KEEP exit 0; stop asserting queryability it does not have.\n\nUX-26 — `status` holds Detail and Hint for each failed component but prints only the names.\n  anchor: status_render.go:472-490\n  fix: print Detail under each failure.\n\nUX-27 — a dirty tree prints two contradictory remedies at once: \"commit or stash\" in the verdict and \"refresh with --worktree\" in the cause underneath.\n  anchors: status_render.go:320; agent_surface.go:4634\n  fix: one remedy resolver, used by both sites.\n\nRULES (non-negotiable):\n1. NEVER push, open a PR, merge, or approve anything. Commit to the local branch only. No AI attribution footer in commit messages.\n2. Every behaviour you claim to fix needs a TEST, and every test must be WEAKENING-VERIFIED: patch the production guard compile-clean, run the test, capture the RED assertion text, restore, confirm green. A green suite is not evidence. If a weakening produces ZERO failures, suspect your test first — grep to confirm the edit actually applied and that the fixture is non-empty.\n3. Negative controls where a fix could over-apply (e.g. --json output must stay byte-identical after the io.Discard change — prove it).\n4. CPU discipline: this machine runs other agents. Build/test ONLY the focused package. Use `GOMAXPROCS=1 go test ./internal/cli -run '<focused regex>' -count=1 -p 1 -parallel 1`. Never run the full suite.\n5. Use `rtk` for git/ls/grep (token-optimized proxy) wherever it works.\n6. Prefer `entire graph`/`entire brain` queries over grep sweeps for \"who calls this / what breaks\" — run `entire graph impact` before editing any exported symbol.\n7. Note: FORCE_COLOR=3 is set in this shell and breaks colour-assert tests on CORRECT code. If a colour test fails, reproduce it on unmodified main before blaming your change.\n\nBefore finishing: `go build ./... && go vet ./...` both clean, focused tests green, and update the `status` column of the four rows in docs/install-ux-backlog.md ONLY IF that file exists in your worktree (it is on a different branch — if absent, skip, do not create it).\n\nREPORT BACK IN CAVEMAN-ULTRA COMPRESSED FORM. Dense, no prose padding, no restating the task. Your tool output does not reach me — only your report. Must contain: branch SHA; per-row what changed (file:line); for EACH weakening, the one-line RED assertion text; build/vet exit codes; before/after line counts for setup and status output; anything you could NOT fix and why."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2172,"cache_read_input_token