a temp dir. This already destroyed the user's real install once today. Any live run you do must pass --no-daemon and use an isolated XDG_DATA_HOME/XDG_CONFIG_HOME/XDG_STATE_HOME/XDG_CACHE_HOME in a mktemp dir.\n3. Every behaviour you claim to fix needs a TEST, WEAKENING-VERIFIED: patch the production guard compile-clean, run the test, capture the RED assertion text, restore, confirm green. If a weakening yields ZERO failures, suspect your test — grep that the edit applied and the fixture is non-empty.\n4. Negative control for UX-19: an EXPLICIT `--daemon` on re-run must still override the persisted decline. Prove it.\n5. CPU discipline: other agents are running. Focused package only: `GOMAXPROCS=1 go test ./internal/cli -run '<focused regex>' -count=1 -p 1 -parallel 1`. Never the full suite.\n6. Use `rtk` for git/ls/grep. Use `entire graph impact` before editing exported symbols, not a grep sweep.\n7. FORCE_COLOR=3 is set here and breaks colour-assert tests on correct code — reproduce any colour failure on unmodified main before blaming your change.\n\nFinish with `go build ./... && go vet ./...` clean plus a LIVE end-to-end acceptance in an isolated throwaway repo: git init, a couple of files, `entire brain setup --no-daemon`, then show that an agent-visible pointer now exists (list the files written) and that a second run is idempotent.\n\nREPORT BACK IN CAVEMAN-ULTRA COMPRESSED FORM. Dense, no padding, no restating the task. Your tool output does not reach me — only your report. Must contain: branch SHA; per-row what changed (file:line); the decision on run-vs-print for UX-07 WITH its evidence; for EACH weakening the one-line RED assertion text; build/vet exit codes; the live acceptance transcript trimmed to the lines that prove it; anything you could NOT fix and why."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"b67225cd-10f1-4961-8b4e-dd3a6ccf9120","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Cfw8sr9WhtJr6cS6vcRam","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"1f9f93bf-747e-497d-a2ba-4e4fd7372545","timestamp":"2026-10-11T21:11:26.040Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"1eac9040-9610-45f1-aa43-df0931455a37","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-ux-backlog","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"1f9f93bf-747e-497d-a2ba-4e4fd7372545","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cfw8srY5JVYsqKRZf7CYD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01K5HNoL2imw7XKEQDKqunze","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Doctor actionable + dead surface","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"opus","prompt":"WORKTREE: /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-ux-c-doctor  (branch fix/doctor-actionable, off origin/main e6bb5c42). Work ONLY there. Never cd to another checkout.\n\nRepo: entireio/entire-brain (Go). Two rows about a product that talks to itself instead of to the user.\n\nUX-22 — `doctor` prints 40 lines / 6.4 KB on a HEALTHY brain: 34 ok + 5 warn + 1 error. Of the 6 non-ok lines, exactly ONE names a remedy. Three checks are constant \"ok\" literals that can never fail. There is no --verbose.\n  anchors: lifecycle_ops.go:109-320; the three unfailable constants at :123, :161, :181; doctor.go:113-114\n  fix: cut the default to <=8 ACTIONABLE lines; everything else behind `--verbose`; `--json` output unchanged (that is a contract — prove it byte-identical); DELETE the three checks that cannot fail.\n  A diagnostic that cries wolf on a healthy system trains people to ignore it. The bar: on a healthy brain, `doctor` should say so in a couple of lines. Every non-ok line it does print must name a command the user can actually run.\n\nUX-28 — dead surface a user can trip over: `refresh seed --interactive` is registered and NEVER read; `distill --jobs` is a self-conflicting alias; 9 verbs have zero README mentions; the docs contract test is ONE-directional (it checks documented->exists but not exists->documented).\n  anchors: seed.go:238; distill_cmd.go:606; documented_commands_test.go:14\n  fix: delete the dead flag; fix or remove the self-conflicting alias; make the docs test BIDIRECTIONAL so an undocumented verb fails CI. Then make it pass — either document the 9 verbs briefly in the README or hide the ones that are genuinely internal.\n\nThere is strong prior art in this repo for the bidirectional docs test: PR #313 shipped `benchmarks_doc_test.go` (runs every command appearing in docs/benchmarks.md) and PR #315 shipped `feature_matrix_test.go` (asserts the matrix matches the data and that claimed commands exist). READ BOTH before writing yours and follow their pattern rather than inventing one.\n\nRULES (non-negotiable):\n1. NEVER push, open a PR, merge, or approve. Commit to the local branch only. No AI attribution footer in commit messages.\n2. Every behaviour you claim to fix needs a TEST, WEAKENING-VERIFIED: patch the production guard compile-clean, run the test, capture the RED assertion text, restore, confirm green. A green suite is not evidence — a mutation sweep here once found 8 of 15 guards unheld. If a weakening yields ZERO failures, suspect your TEST first: grep that the edit applied and that the fixture is non-empty.\n3. Negative controls: (a) an UNHEALTHY brain must still produce its full actionable output at default verbosity — prove doctor did not just go quiet; (b) `doctor --json` byte-identical before/after; (c) your bidirectional docs test must actually go RED when you add a throwaway undocumented verb — demonstrate that, then remove the throwaway.\n4. Deleting the three unfailable checks: before deleting, confirm with `entire graph impact` (not grep) that nothing consumes their output, and that they are genuinely constant and not reachable-but-currently-true. \"I have not seen it fail\" is NOT the same as \"it cannot fail\" — quote the code that makes it constant.\n5. CPU discipline: other agents are running. Focused package only: `GOMAXPROCS=1 go test ./internal/cli -run '<focused regex>' -count=1 -p 1 -parallel 1`. Never the full suite.\n6. Use `rtk` for git/ls/grep.\n7. FORCE_COLOR=3 is set in this shell and breaks colour-assert tests on CORRECT code — reproduce any colour failure on unmodified main before blaming your change.\n\nFinish with `