{"parentUuid":"dc3cfffa-ca1b-489b-b473-42dc885ddfeb","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PreToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_01HGCpa2PN6hh9yyxVQGaNPt","hookEvent":"PreToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"hookSpecificOutput\":{\"hookEventName\":\"PreToolUse\",\"permissionDecisionReason\":\"RTK auto-rewrite\",\"updatedInput\":{\"command\":\"rtk read /Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/brain-not-on-api-main.md\",\"description\":\"Read existing memory on brain server state\"}}}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"rtk hook claude","durationMs":18},"type":"attachment","uuid":"03eabd57-4662-46ed-967f-3a80242c043a","timestamp":"2026-10-11T21:14:21.381Z","session_id":"1eac9040-9610-45f1-aa43-df0931455a37","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-api","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"dc3cfffa-ca1b-489b-b473-42dc885ddfeb","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"b1331e42-5b90-45b6-9c58-e0c78213a423","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HGCpa2PN6hh9yyxVQGaNPt","type":"tool_result","content":"---\nname: brain-not-on-api-main\ndescription: \"The brain subsystem is NOT on entire-api main — zero brain files; it lives only in the unmerged 10-part stack #744-#752 + #242, ~599 commits behind, so brain server defects are not live risks\"\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\nVerified directly 2026-08-29: `git ls-tree -r --name-only origin/main | grep -ci brain` → **0**.\n\nEvery brain server-side defect found in this campaign lives exclusively in the unmerged 10-part\nstack **#744–#752 + #242** (top branch `m4-brain-auth`), which is **~599 commits behind main** and\nunreviewed end to end. **Brain is not deployed anywhere, so none of them is a live production risk.**\n\nTwo consequences that repeatedly mislead audits:\n1. **Auditing `entire-api` main for brain code finds nothing** — check out the stack instead.\n2. **`internal/store/repo_purge.go` + `repoPurgeTables` exist on main but NOT on the brain branch**\n   (brain forked 2026-08-19; the purge-queue migration is `20260824181936`, five days later).\n   Writing a purge into the brain branch's inline `DeleteRepo` tx guarantees a rebase conflict.\n\n**Correction to an earlier claim of mine:** DEK shred on repo deletion does NOT need \"post-rebase\npurge machinery\" to snapshot the slug. `brainbuild.RepoKeyFor(slug, repoID) = slug + \"@\" + repoID`\n(`internal/brainbuild/fact_sync.go:43`) — **the repo ULID is already embedded in every `repo_key`**,\nso a purge finds every row by exact suffix match. ~1 migration + ~15 lines, not a re-keying project.\n\n**The real blocker is policy, not engineering:** `brain_fact_advances` is append-only *by grant*,\nwith an explicit `REVOKE UPDATE, DELETE` as its stated tamper-evidence mechanism\n(`20260819120300_brain_fact_advances.sql:18-19,68-69`). GDPR erasure vs. a tamper-evident audit\nchain is a human decision. **Useful out: deleting `brain_deks` alone suffices for crypto-shred** (the\nS3 ciphertext becomes undecryptable), so the audit chain can stay append-only.\n\nRelated: [[keystone-3-prs-open]], [[p1-client-server-interop-fork]], [[brain-ci-gate-split-trust]].","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"0ba1cff3-b060-4a68-8608-79bd045ba083","timestamp":"2026-10-11T21:14:22.632Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"---\nname: brain-not-on-api-main\ndescription: \"The brain subsystem is NOT on entire-api main — zero brain files; it lives only in the unmerged 10-part stack #744-#752 + #242, ~599 commits behind, so brain server defects are not live risks\"\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\nVerified directly 2026-08-29: `git ls-tree -r --name-only origin/main | grep -ci brain` → **0**.\n\nEvery brain server-side defect found in this campaign lives exclusively in the unmerged 10-part\nstack **#744–#752 + #242** (top branch `m4-brain-auth`), which is **~599 commits behind main** and\nunreviewed end to end. **Brain is not deployed anywhere, so none of them is a live production risk.**\n\nTwo consequences that repeatedly mislead audits:\n1. **Auditing `entire-api` main for brain code finds nothing** — check out the stack instead.\n2. **`internal/store/repo_purge.go` + `repoPurgeTables` exist on main but NOT on the brain branch**\n   (brain forked 2026-08-19; the purge-queue migration is `20260824181936`, five days later).\n   Writing a purge into the brain branch's inline `DeleteRepo` tx guarantees a rebase conflict.\n\n**Correction to an earlier claim of mine:** DEK shred on repo deletion does NOT need \"post-rebase\npurge machinery\" to snapshot the slug. `brainbuild.RepoKeyFor(slug, repoID) = slug + \"@\" + repoID`\n(`internal/brainbuild/fact_sync.go:43`) — **the repo ULID is already embedded in every `repo_key`**,\nso a purge finds every row by exact suffix match. ~1 migration + ~15 lines, not a re-keying project.\n\n**The real blocker is policy, not engineering:** `brain_fact_advances` is append-only *by grant*,\nwith an explicit `REVOKE UPDATE, DELETE` as its stated tamper-evidence mechanism\n(`20260819120300_brain_fact_advances.sql:18-19,68-69`). GDPR erasure vs. a tamper-evident audit\nchain is a human decision. **Useful out: deleting `brain_deks` alone suffices for crypto-shred** (the\nS3 ciphertext becomes undecryptable), so the audit chain can stay append-only.\n\nRelated: [[keystone-3-prs-open]], [[p1-client-server-interop-fork]], [[brain-ci-gate-split-trust]].","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"classifierBoundary":true,"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"fc627a67-ed8c-475d-b465-8f99dc46ba0c","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-api","root":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-api","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":1,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":11},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/entire-api","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/entire-api","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/entire-api","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-api","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"dc3cfffa-ca1b-489b-b473-42dc885ddfeb","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"1eac9040-9610-45f1-aa43-df0931455a37","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-api","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
