{"parentUuid":"4ff0d050-613c-4f8d-a48e-4c36ed2ed406","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14835947 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"0c948192-13ec-4b30-9fcf-78ab8408b6d5","timestamp":"2026-10-11T21:17:57.436Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14835947 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"1eac9040-9610-45f1-aa43-df0931455a37","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"0c948192-13ec-4b30-9fcf-78ab8408b6d5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cfw9RXKKYXTYRjKYiC9u9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AfGYD2dpLPb5xu8FoGyUgr","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"ac39578cdbbe4464d","summary":"Warn agent B: XDG isolation does not isolate brain store","message":"HAZARD you are hitting right now: setting XDG_* does NOT isolate the brain store, and your acceptance repo is writing into the user's REAL brain data.\n\nEvidence: I just ran the same pattern. `entire brain path` resolved to\n  $XDG_DATA_HOME/entire/plugins/data/brain/repos/<key>\nThe brain store lives UNDER the plugins directory. Any harness that symlinks the plugin registry into the isolated XDG_DATA_HOME (which you must do, or `entire graph` fails to resolve and you get a false provider error) thereby routes the brain store straight back through the symlink into ~/.local/share/entire/plugins/data/brain/repos/.\n\nI found YOUR artifact there: local/acc-repo-0de9394544d4 (17:16... created 16:40). I deleted only my own three (gh/example-org, local/alice-*) and LEFT yours alone in case you still need it. That directory now holds 121 accumulated throwaway repos from past sessions — this leaks every time anyone tests.\n\nWhat to do:\n1. Keep the symlink (you need the plugin binaries), but note in your report that store isolation is NOT achieved by XDG alone.\n2. Delete your own acc-repo-* under ~/.local/share/entire/plugins/data/brain/repos/local/ when your acceptance is done. Delete ONLY directories you created; others belong to other agents and to the user.\n3. Record this as a NEW backlog row in your report (do not edit docs/install-ux-backlog.md — it is on another branch): \"testing brain in a throwaway repo permanently pollutes the real brain store; XDG isolation is insufficient because the store lives inside the plugin dir; 121 orphaned repos already accumulated; there is no documented way to test brain without touching real data.\" This is the same family as UX-01 (the throwaway setup that overwrote the real launchd plist) and is worth fixing as part of your batch if cheap — e.g. an env var or flag that relocates the store root.\n\nAlso, two things I observed live that bear on YOUR rows, use them rather than re-deriving:\n- `entire brain setup --no-daemon` DOES already print a \"Next\" block:\n      Next\n        entire brain overview        what this project is\n        entire brain brief \"<task>\"  task-shaped context\n        entire brain status          backfill progress and daemon health\n  So UX-07's \"prints no next step\" is STALE as written. The surviving defect is the real one: it writes no guide/pointer/MCP registration/hook, and the Next block never mentions init-agents. Correct the row's premise in your report instead of repeating it.\n- `entire brain status` in a brand-new throwaway repo prints:\n      daemon + running, but the installed unit is stale and not current (io.entire.brain-watch.a2d3fd66); re-run `entire brain setup`\n  i.e. it reads the user's REAL global launchd unit even under isolated XDG, and advises re-running setup — which is exactly the advice that destroyed the user's real install today. That is UX-01 biting from a second direction. Worth a row/fix if it is in reach of your batch.","type":"message","recipient":"ac39578cdbbe4464d","recipient_kind":"agent","content":"HAZARD you are hitting right now: setting XDG_* d…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2322,"cache_read_input_tokens":151348,"output_tokens":1158,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2322},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1158,"cache_read_input_tokens":151348,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2322,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2322,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01AfGYD2dpLPb5xu8FoGyUgr":{"to":"ac39578cdbbe4464d","summary":"Warn agent B: XDG isolation does not isolate brain store","message":"HAZARD you are hitting right now: setting XDG_* does NOT isolate the brain store, and your acceptance repo is writing into the user's REAL brain data.\n\nEvidence: I just ran the same pattern. `entire brain path` resolved to\n  $XDG_DATA_HOME/entire/plugins/data/brain/repos/<key>\nThe brain store lives UNDER the plugins directory. Any harness that symlinks the plugin registry into the isolated XDG_DATA_HOME (which you must do, or `entire graph` fails to resolve and you get a false provider error) thereby routes the brain store straight back through the symlink into ~/.local/share/entire/plugins/data/brain/repos/.\n\nI found YOUR artifact there: local/acc-repo-0de9394544d4 (17:16... created 16:40). I deleted only my own three (gh/example-org, local/alice-*) and LEFT yours alone in case you still need it. That directory now holds 121 accumulated throwaway repos from past sessions — this leaks every time anyone tests.\n\nWhat to do:\n1. Keep the symlink (you need the plugin binaries), but note in your report that store isolation is NOT achieved by XDG alone.\n2. Delete your own acc-repo-* under ~/.local/share/entire/plugins/data/brain/repos/local/ when your acceptance is done. Delete ONLY directories you created; others belong to other agents and to the user.\n3. Record this as a NEW backlog row in your report (do not edit docs/install-ux-backlog.md — it is on another branch): \"testing brain in a throwaway repo permanently pollutes the real brain store; XDG isolation is insufficient because the store lives inside the plugin dir; 121 orphaned repos already accumulated; there is no documented way to test brain without touching real data.\" This is the same family as UX-01 (the throwaway setup that overwrote the real launchd plist) and is worth fixing as part of your batch if cheap — e.g. an env var or flag that relocates the store root.\n\nAlso, two things I observed live that bear on YOUR rows, use them rather than re-deriving:\n- `entire brain setup --no-daemon` DOES already print a \"Next\" block:\n      Next\n        entire brain overview        what this project is\n        entire brain brief \"<task>\"  task-shaped context\n        entire brain status          backfill progress and daemon health\n  So UX-07's \"prints no next step\" is STALE as written. The surviving defect is the real one: it writes no guide/pointer/MCP registration/hook, and the Next block never mentions init-agents. Correct the row's premise in your report instead of repeating it.\n- `entire brain status` in a brand-new throwaway repo prints:\n      daemon + running, but the installed unit is stale and not current (io.entire.brain-watch.a2d3fd66); re-run `entire brain setup`\n  i.e. it reads the user's REAL global launchd unit even under isolated XDG, and advises re-running setup — which is exactly the advice that destroyed the user's real install today. That is UX-01 biting from a second direction. Worth a row/fix if it is in reach of your batch."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"053e4295-b83a-45d9-a4cd-5dc885afdeac","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cfw9RWsnFX14DHTcj45i6","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"df5f3eab-a5ae-4968-b840-d3b08b6b6084","timestamp":"2026-10-11T21:18:13.939Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"1eac9040-9610-45f1-aa43-df0931455a37","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slu