{"parentUuid":"735ace50-53ae-4a53-9ec8-2a41183bc1cb","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cfw9gqQvKx3uJMU68xqbx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Decisive: **32 of 37 are from the real install**, all at **0.0% CPU / ~0.1s total CPU**, ages 11–25 min — idle and lingering, not working. Let me record both findings:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1390,"cache_read_input_tokens":173484,"output_tokens":2029,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":625},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1390},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2029,"cache_read_input_tokens":173484,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1390,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1390,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"6b7c2c53-cbda-478b-a766-aba01397c392","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cfw9gpydNtQms61W1g9Rf","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"bd94ead9-759a-4b81-a9de-0b53c64b9c9a","timestamp":"2026-10-11T21:21:35.727Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"1eac9040-9610-45f1-aa43-df0931455a37","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"bd94ead9-759a-4b81-a9de-0b53c64b9c9a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cfw9gqQvKx3uJMU68xqbx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KBJgdLiUPxSJizvmCagqnm","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"M=\"/Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory\"\ncat > \"$M/brain-test-isolation-is-impossible.md\" <<'EOF'\n---\nname: brain-test-isolation-is-impossible\ndescription: \"XDG_* does NOT isolate the brain store (it lives under plugins/data), so every throwaway test writes permanently into the real store; the memory worker leaks there even when XDG is isolated, and workers accumulate (37 procs / ~1GB)\"\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\nVerified live 2026-10-11 while testing the first-run flow.\n\n**The store lives inside the plugin dir.** `entire brain path` resolves to\n`$XDG_DATA_HOME/entire/plugins/data/brain/repos/<key>`. Any harness that symlinks the real plugin\nregistry into an isolated `XDG_DATA_HOME` — which you MUST do, or `entire graph` fails to resolve\nand you get a provider error that looks like a product bug — thereby routes the brain store straight\nback into `~/.local/share/entire/plugins/data/brain/repos/`. **Setting XDG_* is not a containment\nboundary for brain data.** `scripts/try-first-run.sh` carried a comment asserting the opposite\n(\"brain's per-repo store still lands in the temp dir\"); that claim was FALSE and is now corrected\nin place. 121 orphaned throwaway repos had already accumulated in the real store.\n\n**Partial fix:** symlink only `plugins/bin` (156 MB, just symlinks to binaries) and let\n`plugins/data` (96 GB on this machine) be local per test. Foreground commands then isolate\ncorrectly — proven: Alice's facts landed in her store and Bob's recall was genuinely empty.\n\n**But it is only partial.** Even with that fix, `entire brain setup` left\n`locks/{memory-worker,write}.lock` and `history/work/v1/{worker.log,coordinator.json}` in the\n**real** store for the fake repo. The worker's own log: `worker_started` → `prepass_failed` →\n`worker_degraded`. `memoryWorkerChildEnvironment` (`internal/cli/memory_cmd.go:153`) does preserve\n`os.Environ()`, so the leak comes from a different launch path — mechanism not yet pinned down.\nTwo processes disagreeing about where the brain lives is a correctness hazard, not just test noise.\n\n**Workers accumulate.** 37 `entire-brain memory worker` processes alive at once, **32 from the real\ninstall**, ~997 MB RSS total (~23 MB each, one at 255 MB), ages 11–25 min, **all at 0.0% CPU with\n~0.1s total CPU time** — parked, not working, long after their work finished. 14 distinct repos held\nrecent worker locks. Caveat: this machine was running four agents hammering brain across worktrees,\nso normal single-user use would be fewer; but idle processes surviving 25 minutes is still a leak.\n\n**Daemon is global too:** `entire brain status` in a brand-new throwaway repo reads the REAL launchd\nunit and prints \"the installed unit is stale and not current (io.entire.brain-watch.<hash>); re-run\n`entire brain setup`\". Following that advice from inside a scratch repo is exactly what overwrote\nthe real plist (backlog UX-01). Always pass `--no-daemon` in scratch repos.\n\nRelated: [[verification-harness-false-pass]], [[shared-tmp-contended-across-agents]],\n[[brain-is-a-separate-plugin-binary]], [[reclaim-disk-before-heavy-runs]].\nEOF\necho \"written: brain-test-isolation-is-impossible.md\"","description":"Record brain test isolation finding"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1390,"cache_read_input_tokens":173484,"output_tokens":2029,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":625},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1390},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2029,"cache_read_input_tokens":173484,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1390,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1390,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01KBJgdLiUPxSJizvmCagqnm":{"command":"M=\"/Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory\"\ncat > \"$M/brain-test-isolation-is-impossible.md\" <<'EOF'\n---\nname: brain-test-isolation-is-impossible\ndescription: \"XDG_* does NOT isolate the brain store (it lives under plugins/data), so every throwaway test writes permanently into the real store; the memory worker leaks there even when XDG is isolated, and workers accumulate (37 procs / ~1GB)\"\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\nVerified live 2026-10-11 while testing the first-run flow.\n\n**The store lives inside the plugin dir.** `entire brain path` resolves to\n`$XDG_DATA_HOME/entire/plugins/data/brain/repos/<key>`. Any harness that symlinks the real plugin\nregistry into an isolated `XDG_DATA_HOME` — which you MUST do, or `entire graph` fails to resolve\nand you get a provider error that looks like a product bug — thereby routes the brain store straight\nback into `~/.local/share/entire/plugins/data/brain/repos/`. **Setting XDG_* is not a containment\nboundary for brain data.** `scripts/try-first-run.sh` carried a comment asserting the opposite\n(\"brain's per-repo store still lands in the temp dir\"); that claim was FALSE and is now corrected\nin place. 121 orphaned throwaway repos had already accumulated in the real store.\n\n**Partial fix:** symlink only `plugins/bin` (156 MB, just symlinks to binaries) and let\n`plugins/data` (96 GB on this machine) be local per test. Foreground commands then isolate\ncorrectly — proven: Alice's facts landed in her store and Bob's recall was genuinely empty.\n\n**But it is only partial.** Even with that fix, `entire brain setup` left\n`locks/{memory-worker,write}.lock` and `history/work/v1/{worker.log,coordinator.json}` in the\n**real** store for the fake repo. The worker's own log: `worker_started` → `prepass_failed` →\n`worker_degraded`. `memoryWorkerChildEnvironment` (`internal/cli/memory_cmd.go:153`) does preserve\n`os.Environ()`, so the leak comes from a different launch path — mechanism not yet pinned down.\nTwo processes disagreeing about where the brain lives is a correctness hazard, not just test noise.\n\n**Workers accumulate.** 37 `entire-brain memory worker` processes alive at once, **32 from the real\ninstall**, ~997 MB RSS total (~23 MB each, one at 255 MB), ages 11–25 min, **all at 0.0% CPU with\n~0.1s total CPU time** — parked, not working, long after their work finished. 14 distinct repos held\nrecent worker locks. Caveat: this machine was running four agents hammering brain across worktrees,\nso normal single-user use would be fewer; but idle processes surviving 25 minutes is still a leak.\n\n**Daemon is global too:** `entire brain status` in a brand-new throwaway repo reads the REAL launchd\nunit and prints \"the installed unit is stale and not current (io.entire.brain-watch.<hash>); re-run\n`entire brain setup`\". Following that advice from inside a scratch repo is exactly what overwrote\nthe real plist (backlog UX-01). Always pass `--no-daemon` in scratch repos.\n\nRelated: [[verification-harness-false-pass]], [[shared-tmp-contended-across-agents]],\n[[brain-is-a-separate-plugin-binary]], [[reclaim-disk-before-heavy-runs]].\nEOF\necho \"written: brain-test-isolation-is-impossible.md\"","description":"Record brain test isolation finding"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"6b7c2c53-cbda-478b-a766-aba01397c392","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Cfw9gpydNtQms61W1g9Rf","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"c23f4c2a-5222-4434-b8ef-1346bbd3f2ac","timestamp":"2026-10-11T21:21:50.898Z"