{"parentUuid":"44c15339-c63b-40fd-bc76-586cd2ecd706","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cfw9oDyty4EdNnc8mJUVm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TMYdZCeCHsQbZm362Cnb8A","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-ux-backlog\npython3 - <<'PY'\np='docs/install-ux-backlog.md'; s=open(p).read()\n\n# 1. correct UX-07's stale premise (setup DOES print a Next block)\nold7_key='| UX-07 |'\ni=s.index(old7_key); j=s.index('\\n', i)\nold7=s[i:j]\nnew7=('| UX-07 | `setup` writes **no guide, no pointer, no MCP registration, no hook**. A setup-only repo is '\n      'invisible to every agent; `setup.go` has zero references to `agentsetup`. '\n      '**Premise corrected 2026-10-11:** setup *does* print a `Next` block (`overview` / `brief` / `status`) — '\n      'the earlier \"prints no next step\" was wrong. The surviving defect is that `Next` never names `init-agents`, '\n      'the one step that makes an agent use the brain at all. | `setup.go` (whole); `agent_setup.go:13` | '\n      'End `setup` by running `init-agents`, or name it in the `Next` block. | open |')\ns=s[:i]+new7+s[j:]\n\n# 2. append new rows after UX-30\nanchor=s.index('| UX-30 |'); end=s.index('\\n', anchor)\nrows = [\n ('UX-31',\n  'Brain data **cannot be isolated for testing**. The store lives under the plugin dir '\n  '(`$XDG_DATA_HOME/entire/plugins/data/brain/repos/<key>`), and a harness must symlink the real plugin '\n  'registry or `entire graph` fails to resolve — so XDG isolation routes the store straight back into the '\n  'real one. **121 orphaned throwaway repos** had accumulated there. Even after linking only `plugins/bin`, '\n  '`setup` still leaked `locks/*` and `history/work/v1/{worker.log,coordinator.json}` for the fake repo into '\n  'the **real** store (`worker_started` → `prepass_failed` → `worker_degraded`).',\n  '`memory_cmd.go:153` preserves `os.Environ()`, so the leak is a different launch path',\n  'Give the store an explicit root override (env var or flag) independent of the plugin dir.'),\n ('UX-32',\n  '`bundle import --sha256` is **required** but `--help` lists it as an ordinary optional flag; the user only '\n  'learns on failure. And `--overwrite` is required *in practice always*, because a fresh `setup` already '\n  'creates `seed, docs, facts` — so the refusal\\'s advice \"or import into a brain without them\" names a state '\n  'a real receiver is never in.',\n  'bundle import help text; the import refusal message',\n  'Mark `--sha256` required; have `export` print the exact import command; drop the impossible branch.'),\n ('UX-33',\n  'After `bundle import --overwrite` replaces the receiver\\'s facts, `recall` reports '\n  '\"no facts … no distillation timestamp is recorded; run `entire brain refresh`, then `distill`\" — it blames '\n  'distillation instead of naming the import that destroyed them. The user is sent to re-distill.',\n  'blind-spot branches reached by `recall`',\n  'Record that an import replaced the fact layer and say so in the empty-result note.'),\n ('UX-34',\n  '`memory worker` processes accumulate idle: **37 alive at once, 32 of them from the real install, ~997 MB RSS '\n  '(~23 MB each, one at 255 MB), ages 11–25 min, all at 0.0% CPU / ~0.1s total CPU time** — parked long after '\n  'their work finished, across 14 repos. (Measured on a machine running four agents, so normal use would be '\n  'fewer — but surviving 25 min idle is still a leak.)',\n  '`memory_cmd.go:123` spawn path; worker exit/TTL',\n  'Exit when idle, or reuse one worker per repo.'),\n ('UX-35',\n  '`status` in a brand-new throwaway repo reads the **real global** launchd unit and prints \"the installed unit '\n  'is stale and not current (io.entire.brain-watch.<hash>); re-run `entire brain setup`\". Following that advice '\n  'from a scratch repo is precisely what overwrote the real plist (UX-01), so the product advises the action '\n  'that breaks it.',\n  'daemon check in the status path; same derivation as UX-01',\n  'Scope the daemon check to the repo under inspection, or say which repo the unit belongs to.'),\n]\nadd=''.join(f\"\\n| {i} | {sym} | {anc} | {fix} | open |\" for i,sym,anc,fix in rows)\ns=s[:end]+add+s[end:]\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nprint('rows now:', s.count('\\n| UX-'))\nPY\nawk -F'|' '/^\\| *UX-3[1-5]/ {for(i=1;i<=NF;i++) gsub(/^ +| +$/,\"\",$i); printf \"%-7s %-6s %s\\n\",$2,$6,substr($3,1,70)}' docs/install-ux-backlog.md","description":"Add five new backlog rows and correct UX-07"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1480,"cache_read_input_tokens":180841,"output_tokens":1840,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1480},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1840,"cache_read_input_tokens":180841,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1480,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1480,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01TMYdZCeCHsQbZm362Cnb8A":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-ux-backlog\npython3 - <<'PY'\np='docs/install-ux-backlog.md'; s=open(p).read()\n\n# 1. correct UX-07's stale premise (setup DOES print a Next block)\nold7_key='| UX-07 |'\ni=s.index(old7_key); j=s.index('\\n', i)\nold7=s[i:j]\nnew7=('| UX-07 | `setup` writes **no guide, no pointer, no MCP registration, no hook**. A setup-only repo is '\n      'invisible to every agent; `setup.go` has zero references to `agentsetup`. '\n      '**Premise corrected 2026-10-11:** setup *does* print a `Next` block (`overview` / `brief` / `status`)