|"," | UX-05 | **`.brainignore` is the real escape hatch and is named nowhere** — 0 mentions in errors, 0 in README. It is already loaded by the gate and would have cleared the live case instantly. | gate `semantic.go:2537-2551`; loader `semantic.go:2271` | Name it in both refusals and the setup hint; print the top dirty directories as a paste-ready stanza; document in the quickstart. | open |"," | UX-06 | `refresh --worktree` **cannot repair a degraded brain** — it turns the semantic stage off unconditionally. The note then recommends the one command that will fail again. | skip `refresh.go:55-59`; note `refresh.go:648-650` | Pass `--worktree` through to semantic, or name `refresh index --worktree` in the note. | open |","-| UX-07 | `setup` writes **no guide, no pointer, no MCP registration, no hook**, and prints no next step. A setup-only repo is invisible to every agent. `setup.go` has zero references to `agentsetup`. | `setup.go` (whole); `agent_setup.go:13` | End `setup` by running `init-agents`, or at minimum print it as the next step. | open |","+| UX-07 | `setup` writes **no guide, no pointer, no MCP registration, no hook**. A setup-only repo is invisible to every agent; `setup.go` has zero references to `agentsetup`. **Premise corrected 2026-10-11:** setup *does* print a `Next` block (`overview` / `brief` / `status`) — the earlier \"prints no next step\" was wrong. The surviving defect is that `Next` never names `init-agents`, the one step that makes an agent use the brain at all. | `setup.go` (whole); `agent_setup.go:13` | End `setup` by running `init-agents`, or name it in the `Next` block. | open |"," | UX-08 | Our own installers write files that then block our own install. | `entireAuthoredGatePaths` | **Built and verified** on `fix/install-ux-dirty-gate-and-agent-default` @ `3cc936ad`. ⚠️ Does **not** fix UX-03/04 — a user whose dirt is real work is still stuck, and the wrong hint ships with it. Land UX-03+04+05 alongside. | fixed |"," "," ## P1 — silently wrong, or reads as broken"]},{"oldStart":97,"oldLines":6,"newStart":97,"newLines":11,"lines":[" | UX-28 | Dead surface a user can trip over: `refresh seed --interactive` is registered and **never read**; `distill --jobs` is a self-conflicting alias; 9 verbs have zero README mentions; the docs contract test is one-directional. | `seed.go:238`; `distill_cmd.go:606`; `documented_commands_test.go:14` | Delete the dead flag; make the docs test bidirectional. | open |"," | UX-29 | Misleading names: `path` is a print verb that **builds** via `--ensure`; `add` means clone but collides with `workspace add`; `dash`/`viz`/`inspect graph-ui` are three visualizers; `repair`/`reset`/`memory repair`/`memory rebuild` are four names for one job; `stats` is one character from `status`. | `path.go:29`; `add.go:21`; `dash.go:38`; `viz.go:62`; `semantic.go:353,372` | Rename/merge per audit; weigh doc churn (`patterns` ×42, `path` ×11). | open |"," | UX-30 | Remedies that cannot be followed: `--graph-binary` is named but is not a `setup` flag; \"install with `scripts/install.sh` from the checkout\" is false for plugin installs; \"delete the setup record\" is destructive advice on a transient read error. | `semantic.go:1228,1302`; `setup.go:533` | Name runnable commands; distinguish parse from I/O failure. | open |","+| UX-31 | Brain data **cannot be isolated for testing**. The store lives under the plugin dir (`$XDG_DATA_HOME/entire/plugins/data/brain/repos/<key>`), and a harness must symlink the real plugin registry or `entire graph` fails to resolve — so XDG isolation routes the store straight back into the real one. **121 orphaned throwaway repos** had accumulated there. Even after linking only `plugins/bin`, `setup` still leaked `locks/*` and `history/work/v1/{worker.log,coordinator.json}` for the fake repo into the **real** store (`worker_started` → `prepass_failed` → `worker_degraded`). | `memory_cmd.go:153` preserves `os.Environ()`, so the leak is a different launch path | Give the store an explicit root override (env var or flag) independent of the plugin dir. | open |","+| UX-32 | `bundle import --sha256` is **required** but `--help` lists it as an ordinary optional flag; the user only learns on failure. And `--overwrite` is required *in practice always*, because a fresh `setup` already creates `seed, docs, facts` — so the refusal's advice \"or import into a brain without them\" names a state a real receiver is never in. | bundle import help text; the import refusal message | Mark `--sha256` required; have `export` print the exact import command; drop the impossible branch. | open |","+| UX-33 | After `bundle import --overwrite` replaces the receiver's facts, `recall` reports \"no facts … no distillation timestamp is recorded; run `entire brain refresh`, then `distill`\" — it blames distillation instead of naming the import that destroyed them. The user is sent to re-distill. | blind-spot branches reached by `recall` | Record that an import replaced the fact layer and say so in the empty-result note. | open |","+| UX-34 | `memory worker` processes accumulate idle: **37 alive at once, 32 of them from the real install, ~997 MB RSS (~23 MB each, one at 255 MB), ages 11–25 min, all at 0.0% CPU / ~0.1s total CPU time** — parked long after their work finished, across 14 repos. (Measured on a machine running four agents, so normal use would be fewer — but surviving 25 min idle is still a leak.) | `memory_cmd.go:123` spawn path; worker exit/TTL | Exit when idle, or reuse one worker per repo. | open |","+| UX-35 | `status` in a brand-new throwaway repo reads the **real global** launchd unit and prints \"the installed unit is stale and not current (io.entire.brain-watch.<hash>); re-run `entire brain setup`\". Following that advice from a scratch repo is precisely what overwrote the real plist (UX-01), so the product advises the action that breaks it. | daemon check in the status path; same derivation as UX-01 | Scope the daemon check to the repo under inspection, or say which repo the unit belongs to. | open |"," "," ---"," "]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-ux-backlog/docs/install-ux-backlog.md"],"shared":true}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"0fed0928-8172-40b9-a5cb-8097f8df18ff","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-ux-backlog","root":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-ux-backlog","branch":"docs/install-ux-backlog","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":1,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":2},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"entireio","host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"},{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/entire-api","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-ux-backlog","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"959c175f-dace-4076-8c44-daabc8d9fbb6","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"1eac9040-9610-45f1-aa43-df0931455a37","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-ux-backlog","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
