{"parentUuid":"b36b80ec-9cf5-4ad7-92fa-b730ddb4b1cc","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cfw9prHykxsjsDaNeShhw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013jPjaWgTcUnv96pPDBnHcL","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-ux-backlog\ngit add docs/install-ux-backlog.md scripts/try-first-run.sh\ngit -c commit.gpgsign=false commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\ndocs: five rows from a live teammate-sharing run; correct two false claims\n\nAdds UX-31..UX-35, all reproduced live rather than read out of source:\n\n  UX-31  brain data cannot be isolated for testing — the store lives under\n         the plugin dir, so a harness that links the real plugin registry\n         (required, or `entire graph` fails to resolve) routes the store\n         back into the real one. 121 orphaned repos had accumulated.\n  UX-32  `bundle import --sha256` is required but documented as optional;\n         `--overwrite` is required in practice always.\n  UX-33  after an import replaces the receiver's facts, `recall` blames\n         distillation instead of naming the import.\n  UX-34  37 idle `memory worker` processes, ~997 MB RSS, 0.0% CPU.\n  UX-35  `status` in a scratch repo reads the real global launchd unit and\n         advises the re-run that overwrites it (UX-01 from a second angle).\n\nCorrects two claims that were wrong:\n\n  UX-07  said setup \"prints no next step\". It does print a Next block\n         (overview / brief / status). The real defect is narrower and\n         still true: Next never names init-agents.\n  try-first-run.sh asserted \"brain's per-repo store still lands in the\n         temp dir\". False — verified by `entire brain path`. The comment\n         now records the measurement and the partial fix (link only\n         plugins/bin), including that the fix does not stop the memory\n         worker leaking into the real store.\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -1\ngit status --porcelain | head","descri