{"parentUuid":"dbc7f069-0a5b-4d63-9667-ab2d7ad71194","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfwCnaj9Fq2sNmqwEvvHY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now the README, then I'll verify the doctor agent's branch:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1784,"cache_read_input_tokens":272307,"output_tokens":1358,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1784},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1358,"cache_read_input_tokens":272307,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1784,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1784,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"773a4a60-b257-437d-9cf6-ba56badb0e79","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfwCnaLpYeohaYtQePUwC","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"82e8eb4e-42bc-4852-980f-c230e4da48be","timestamp":"2026-10-11T22:02:05.034Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"1eac9040-9610-45f1-aa43-df0931455a37","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/mods/brain-memory","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
{"parentUuid":"82e8eb4e-42bc-4852-980f-c230e4da48be","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfwCnaj9Fq2sNmqwEvvHY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MkwoAxckMSJU5e2RaqftZF","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/mods/brain-memory\npython3 - <<'PY'\np='README.md'; s=open(p).read()\nanchor = \"## Install\"\nassert anchor in s\nnew = '''## `/brainusage` — is the habit forming?\n\nThe pane above answers \"what did brain give me just now\". It cannot answer \"is the\nagent reaching for brain at all, and is it getting anything back\", because `$.state`\nresets on `/clear` and `/resume`. That question needs history, and the only record of\nit is the transcript corpus.\n\n```\n/brainusage          the last month (the default)\n/brainusage 7        narrow the window\n```\n\n```\nBrain usage  last 31d  255 calls  236 answered  9 empty (4%)  10 failed\n\n·▁▃··▁▁▁▃▅▅▁▇▁▁▁▁▁▁·▁▁██▂▂···▁▅\n2026-09-11  →  2026-10-11   24 of 31 days active\n\nmonth ──────────────────────────────────\nMon    ·· ██ ██ ██\nTue    ·· ██ ██ ██\n...\nquiet ·· ██ ██ ██ ██ ██ busy (max 43/day)\n\nday by day, newest first ────────────────\n10-11 ███████████████ 20 · 3 empty\n10-04 ████████████████████████████████ 43 · 1 empty\n\nwhat it was asked for ───────────────────\nrefresh      ██████████████████ 25\nremember     █████████████████ 23\n```\n\nOne glyph per day, then the same month as a calendar, then the days that had traffic,\nthen which verbs were actually used. The ramp runs cool → warm as usage rises, because\nreaching for brain is the good case here. A day with nothing is a dim dot, never a\ncolour: a zero given a colour reads as a value, which is the mistake this mod is about.\n\n`scripts/collect-usage.py` does the scanning in a child process (the corpus here is\n2.0 GB across 2,996 files; the month window is ~1.5 s). Two things it gets right only\nbecause they were found by running it:\n\n- **`entire-brain` is also a directory.** `cd ~/devenv/entire-brain` followed by a\n  newline puts the next shell word exactly where a verb goes, so a naive match reports\n  `echo` and `git` as brain usage. A verb allowlist catches most of it, but not when\n  that word *is* a verb (`status=$(git status)`), so the match also refuses a preceding\n  `/`. It took three attempts to write a test that actually held — the first two passed\n  with the guard removed.\n- **A file's mtime bounds the scan, but not its contents.** A file last written before\n  the window cannot hold events inside it, so mtime is a sound filter — but a file\n  written today may carry months, so every matching line is date-checked on its own.\n\n```\npython3 scripts/collect-usage.py 31 > /tmp/u.json   # the data\nnode scripts/preview.mjs /tmp/u.json                # the pane, rendered outside Claude Code\npython3 scripts/test_collect_usage.py               # the collector's own guards\n```\n\n`preview.mjs` imports `hooks/register.js` unmodified, so it cannot drift from what the\npane really draws.\n\n'''\ns = s.replace(anchor, new + anchor)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nprint('README updated')\nPY\necho \"=== final: both suites ===\"\npython3 scripts/test_collect_usage.py 2>&1 | tail -1\nperl -e 'alarm 420; exec @ARGV' claude plugin test 2>&1 | tail -3\nperl -e 'alarm 200; exec @ARGV' claude plugin validate . 2>&1 | tail -3","description":"Document brainusage and run full verification","timeout":600000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1784,"cache_read_input_tokens":272307,"output_tokens":1358,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1784},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"outp