). Two things it gets right only\nbecause they were found by running it:\n\n- **`entire-brain` is also a directory.** `cd ~/devenv/entire-brain` followed by a\n  newline puts the next shell word exactly where a verb goes, so a naive match reports\n  `echo` and `git` as brain usage. A verb allowlist catches most of it, but not when\n  that word *is* a verb (`status=$(git status)`), so the match also refuses a preceding\n  `/`. It took three attempts to write a test that actually held — the first two passed\n  with the guard removed.\n- **A file's mtime bounds the scan, but not its contents.** A file last written before\n  the window cannot hold events inside it, so mtime is a sound filter — but a file\n  written today may carry months, so every matching line is date-checked on its own.\n\n```\npython3 scripts/collect-usage.py 31 > /tmp/u.json   # the data\nnode scripts/preview.mjs /tmp/u.json                # the pane, rendered outside Claude Code\npython3 scripts/test_collect_usage.py               # the collector's own guards\n```\n\n`preview.mjs` imports `hooks/register.js` unmodified, so it cannot drift from what the\npane really draws.\n\n'''\ns = s.replace(anchor, new + anchor)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nprint('README updated')\nPY\necho \"=== final: both suites ===\"\npython3 scripts/test_collect_usage.py 2>&1 | tail -1\nperl -e 'alarm 420; exec @ARGV' claude plugin test 2>&1 | tail -3\nperl -e 'alarm 200; exec @ARGV' claude plugin validate . 2>&1 | tail -3","description":"Document brainusage and run full verification","timeout":600000}},"serverClassifierRequest":"773a4a60-b257-437d-9cf6-ba56badb0e79","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfwCnaLpYeohaYtQePUwC","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"d4d7b8ee-21f4-4844-b14d-abe902d39ac6","timestamp":"2026-10-11T22:02:20.122Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"1eac9040-9610-45f1-aa43-df0931455a37","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cw