{"parentUuid":"6131bef7-76c6-48a1-bcd5-2b6386e08975","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfwDKddsQfTcWDeqj7WQw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Agent B is still actively writing (5 seconds ago). Here's where things stand.\n\n## `/brainusage` — done\n\n```\nBrain usage  last 31d  255 calls  236 answered  9 empty (4%)  10 failed\n\n·▁▃··▁▁▁▃▅▅▁▇▁▁▁▁▁▁·▁▁██▂▂···▁▅\n2026-09-11 → 2026-10-11   24 of 31 days active\n\nmonth ──────────────────\nMon  ·· ██ ██ ██          quiet ·· ██ ██ ██ ██ ██ busy (max 43/day)\nSat  ██ ██ ██ ██ ██\n\nday by day, newest first ──\n10-04 ████████████████████████ 43 · 1 empty\n10-11 ███████████████ 20 · 3 empty\n\nwhat it was asked for ──\nrefresh   ██████████████████ 25\nremember  █████████████████ 23\n```\n\nMonth window by default, `/brainusage 7` to narrow. One glyph per day, the same month as a calendar heatmap, then per-day bars and which verbs were actually used. Cool→warm as usage rises; a zero day is a dim dot, never coloured.\n\nData comes from the transcript corpus (2.0 GB / 2,996 files) via a collector script — ~1.5s for a month. 26 JS tests + 7 Python tests, **all 12 weakenings verified red**, `claude plugin validate` passes.\n\nTwo things worth flagging honestly:\n\n- **The directory-vs-command guard took three attempts to make real.** `entire-brain` is also a directory, and `cd ~/devenv/entire-brain` + newline puts the next shell word exactly where a verb goes — that's how the first version reported `echo` and `git` as brain usage. My first two tests passed *with the guard removed*; only a fixture where the next word is itself a real verb (`status=$(git status)`) actually holds it.\n- **The live slash command is unverified.** `$.process.run` dispatches correctly in the test harness, and `preview.mjs` renders the real `register.js`, but the mod needs a reload before `/brainusage` runs for real. Worth you trying it.\n\n## Branches — four now, all verified by me, none pushed\n\n| branch | what | my independent check |\n|---|---|---|\n| `fix/runnable-advice` | `entire brain index` → `refresh index` (10 sites), `.brainignore` named in refusals, guide stops denying `brain_remember` | build/vet clean |\n| `fix/doctor-actionable` | doctor **40 → 7 lines**, `--verbose` restores full, 2 unfailable checks deleted | ran it live: 7 lines/1137 bytes, every line ends in a runnable command; weakening red |\n| `fix/setup-status-output-truth` | nested refresh silenced (**52 → 34 lines**), stops claiming queryable when seed+semantic both failed, status prints failure reasons | build/vet clean; weakening red |\n| `fix/install-ux-dirty-gate-and-agent-default` | gate-only `.brainignore` exemption, agent default | from earlier |\n\nTwo agents caught their own bad work, which I'd rather see than not: one found its W7 test was vacuous (truncation hid the string under test) and deleted two more vacuous tests; the other **refused** one of my backlog anchors — `write_lock` isn't a constant, so deleting it would have removed a reachable error path. My anchor was wrong, not its analysis.\n\n## Goal 4 is the one that needs your decision\n\nThe client half ships. The server half does not exist: `entire-api` main has **zero** brain files and zero brain routes, and the 10-PR stack is **1,824 commits and 97 migrations** behind — which is exactly why `migration-check` fails on every PR from #745 on. #744 is code-green; its only red is the trail gate.\n\nBundles *do* work as an interim path — I verified two isolated machines, Bob's recall empty before and Alice's fact after. But **import replaces rather than merges**: Bob's own fact was destroyed, and `recall` then blames distillation instead of naming the import. So \"share my brain\" ships today; \"a team brain everyone contributes to\" is a server project.\n\nAlso found while testing: XDG doesn't isolate the brain store (it lives under the plugin dir), so every throwaway test writes permanently into your real store — **121 orphaned repos** had piled up. I corrected the harness, cleaned up my own leavings, and logged 5 new backlog rows (UX-31..35), including 37 idle `memory worker` processes holding ~1 GB at 0.0% CPU.\n\n**Nothing pushed, merged, or opened as a PR.** #329 and #321 remain green and mergeable whenever you say."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":791,"cache_read_input_tokens":291153,"output_tokens":2142,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":555},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":791},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2142,"cache_read_input_tokens":291153,"cache_creation_input_tokens":791,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":791,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"371613e5-159e-4700-b433-806e254d1aff","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfwDKdCphG9F9p9N7F5LZ","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"ef289c77-ca84-409b-8896-b2ebc7697d9a","timestamp":"2026-10-11T22:09:34.153Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"1eac9040-9610-45f1-aa43-df0931455a37","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-ux-b-agentwiring","sessionId":"6ca2c8fb-c97b-4bf3-a992-0e3c6d1967e2","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"dynamic-petting-globe"}
